es until copies of this spell were unearthed among the affairs of a misanthropic hermit who'd finally made the wrong noble's hair fall out. Several well-funded expeditions were launched in the wake of the discovery, but despite (or perhaps because of) the sometimes-violent competitiveness these naturalists had for each other, the location of the lizards' nesting grounds remains unknown to this day.":"动物学家们曾普遍认为这种动物已经灭绝了数个世纪，直到在一名厌世隐士的遗物中 发掘出了这个法术的抄本——这位隐士终于让某位不该得罪的贵族掉光了头发。 在这一发现之后，多支资金雄厚的考察队被派了出去，但尽管（或许正是由于）这些 博物学家彼此之间有时充满暴力的竞争，这些巨蜥巢穴的位置至今仍然是个谜。","“JUST WALK OUT you can leave!!! work social thing movies home class dentist clothes shoppi too fancy weed store cops if your quick friend ships IF IT SUCKS... HIT DA BRICKS!! real winners quit” [sic] -Admin, @dasharez0ne Twitter. March 30, 2018":"「直接走人 你可以走人！！！ 工作 社交场合 电影 家 课堂 牙医 买衣服 太潮的大麻店 条子发现前快溜 友谊小船 如果没意思……直接开溜！！ 真正的赢家会放弃」 -Admin，@dasharez0ne Twitter。2018年3月30日","“With a bit of a mind flip You're into the time slip And nothing can ever be the same” -Richard O'Brien, “Time Warp”. 1975.":"「一个轻微的思维倒转 你便进入了时间滑移 一切再也无法回到从前」 -理查德·奥布莱恩，《时空扭曲》。1975。","“Water dissolving And water removing There is water At the bottom of the ocean Under the water Carry the water Remove the water At the bottom of the ocean” -Talking Heads, “Once in a Lifetime”. 1980.":"「水在溶解 水在带走 有水存在 在海底 水面之下 承载着水 带走水 在海底」 -传声头乐队，《一生一次》。1980。","<steam dragon scales>":"<steam dragon scales>","“Gringoire put out his hand for the little bag, but she drew back. ‘Do not touch it! It is an amulet, and either you will do mischief to the charm, or it will hurt you.’” -Victor Marie Hugo, _Notre Dame de Paris_, Book II, chapter VII “A Wedding Night”. 1831.":"\"格兰古瓦伸手去取那小袋子，她却缩了回去。'别碰！这是护身符，要么你会毁掉它的法力，要么它会伤害你。'\" ——维克多·雨果，《巴黎圣母院》，第二卷第七章\"新婚之夜\"。1831年。","<amulet>":"<amulet>","“He killed the noble Mudjokivis. Of the skin he made him mittens, Made them with the fur side inside, Made them with the skin side outside. He, to get the warm side inside, Put the inside skin side outside; He, to get the cold side outside, Put the warm side fur side inside. That's why he put the fur side inside, Why he put the skin side outside, Why he turned them inside outside.” -Anonymous, in Wells' _A Parody Anthology_, p. 120. 1904.":"\"他杀了高贵的穆乔基维斯， 用它的皮做了手套， 毛面朝里做内衬， 皮面朝外做外层。 他为了把暖面放里面， 就把内层皮面翻外面； 他为了把凉面放外面， 就把暖面毛面翻里面。 这就是为什么他把毛面放里面， 为什么他把皮面放外面， 为什么他把里外翻了个遍。\" ——佚名，载于威尔斯编《戏仿诗选》，第120页。1904年。","“(Tell enters with his crossbow) W. TELL: My precious jewel now, —my chiefest treasure— A mark I'll set thee, which the cry of grief Could never penetrate,—but thou shalt pierce it,— And thou, my trusty bowstring, that so oft For sport has served me faithfully and well, Desert me not in this dread hour of need,— Only be true this once, my own good cord, That hast so often wing'd the biting shaft:— For shouldst thou fly successless from my hand, I have no second to send after thee.” -Friedrich Schiller, _Wilhelm Tell_, IV, iii. 1804. trans. Sir Theodore Martin, 1898.":"\"（退尔持弩登场） 威廉·退尔： 我珍贵的宝贝——我最贵重的财富—— 我要给你立一个标记，悲痛的哀泣 永远无法穿透——但你却要刺穿它—— 而你，我忠实的弩弦，多少次 在游戏中忠实地为我效劳， 在这危急万分的时刻，不要抛弃我—— 只这一次别辜负我，我的好弦， 你曾多少次为利箭插上翅膀：—— 因为倘若你这次从我手中徒劳飞去， 我便没有第二支可继你之后。\" ——弗里德里希·席勒，《威廉·退尔》，第四幕第三场。1804年。 西奥多·马丁爵士英译，1898年。","“The republic always maintains seven or eight thousand regular troops on the frontiers, to prevent the incursions of the Tartars. The King does not maintain these troops; he only pays the Heydukes, the Semelles, and the Janizaries. The first-mentioned are dressed in blue, with large buttons and plates of tin, and have bonnets made of felt upon their heads. They have firelocks, and the bardiche, which they say is a very good weapon.” -John Pinkerton, _A General Collection of the Best and Most Interesting Voyages and Travels in all parts of the World, many of which are now first translated into English. Digested on a New Plan_. 1808.":"\"共和国总是在边境维持七八千正规军，以防备鞑靼人的入侵。国王并不供养这些军队，他只支付海杜克兵、塞梅尔兵和耶尼切里兵的薪饷。前述第一种士兵身着蓝衣，缀有大纽扣和锡片，头戴毡帽。他们配备火枪和长柄斧，据说那是一种极好的武器。\" ——约翰·平克顿，《世界最佳最有趣航海与旅行记总汇，其中多篇首次译为英文。以新体例编纂》。1808年。","“On Carian coins, indeed of quite late date, the labrys, set up on its long pillar-like handle, with two dependent fillets, has much the appearance of a cult image.” -Sir Arthur John Evans, “Mycenaean tree and pillar cult and its Mediterranean relations,” _Journal of Hellenic Studies_ XXI, p. 109. 1901.":"\"在卡里亚的钱币上——确实是相当晚期的——双刃斧竖立在其长柱状手柄上，挂着两条垂带，极像一尊崇拜偶像的模样。\" ——阿瑟·约翰·埃文斯爵士，\"迈锡尼的树与柱崇拜及其地中海关联\"，《希腊研究杂志》第二十一卷，第109页。1901年。","“On leaf of palm, on sedge-wrought roll; On plastic clay and leathern scroll, Man wrote his thoughts; the ages passed, And lo! the Press was found at last!” -John Greenleaf Whittier, _The Library_, st. 4.":"\"棕榈叶上，莎草卷中； 可塑黏土与皮革卷轴， 人记录了他的思想；岁月流逝， 看哪！印刷机终于问世！\" ——约翰·格林利夫·惠蒂埃，《图书馆》，第四节。","“The weapon, thrown at 20 or 30 yards distance, twirled round in the air with astonishing velocity, and alighting on the right arm of one of his opponents, actually rebounded to a distance not less than 70 or 80 yards, leaving a horrible contusion behind, and exciting universal admiration.” -The Sydney Gazette and New South Wales Advertiser, 23 December 1804":"\"那武器从二三十码外掷出，以惊人的速度在空中旋转，击中对手右臂后，竟反弹至不下七八十码之外，留下一道可怖的瘀伤，激起全场赞叹。\" ——《悉尼公报与新南威尔士广告人报》，1804年12月23日。","“Weapon, shapely, naked, wan! Head from the mother's bowels drawn! Wooded flesh and metal bone! limb only one, and lip only one! Gray-blue leaf by red-heat grown! helve produced from a little seed sown! Resting the grass amid and upon, To be lean'd, and to lean on.” -Walt Whitman, _Song of the Broad-Axe_, l. 1-6. 1867.":"\"武器啊，形体优美，赤裸而苍白！ 从母腹中拔出的头颅！ 木质的肉与金属的骨！只有独肢，只有独唇！ 烈火锻成的灰蓝叶片！从一粒小种子生出的柄！ 栖息于草丛中与草叶上， 为人所倚，亦为人倚靠。\" ——沃尔特·惠特曼，《阔刃斧之歌》，第1-6行。1867年。","“Let who will boast their courage in the field, I find but little safety from my shield. Nature's, not honour's, law we must obey: This made me cast my useless shield away, And by a prudent flight and cunning save A life, which valour could not, from the grave. A better buckler I can soon regain; But who can get another life again?” -Archilochos. 7th cent. B.C. trans. William H. Goodwin, 1878.":"\"任谁去夸耀战场上的勇气吧， 我从盾牌中寻得的庇护却少得可怜。 自然之法则，非荣誉之法则，我们必须遵从： 正因如此，我扔掉了无用的盾牌， 凭借谨慎的逃跑和机敏，从坟墓中 保住了勇敢无法保全的生命。 更好的小圆盾，我很快就能再得； 可谁又能再得一条性命？\" ——阿尔基洛科斯，公元前7世纪。 威廉·H·古德温英译，1878年。","“so long suckers! i rev up my motorcylce and create a huge cloud of smoke. when the cloud dissipates im lying completely dead on the pavement” -wint, @dril Twitter. July 26, 2016":"\"再见了傻瓜们！我发动摩托车掀起一阵浓烟。 当烟雾散去时，我已经完全死在了人行道上\" ——wint，@dril 推特。2016年7月26日。","<leather armour>":"<leather armour>","“O Bell my wife, why dost thou flyte? Now is now, and then was then: Seek now all the world throughout, Thou kens not clowns from gentlemen: They are clad in black, green, yellow and blue, So far above their own degree. Once in my life I'll take a view; For I'll have a new cloak about me.” -Anonymous, “The Old Cloak”. 16th Century.":"\"贝尔吾妻，你为何争吵不休？ 今是今，昔是昔： 纵寻遍天涯海角， 你也分不清村夫与绅士： 他们身着黑、绿、黄与蓝， 远超出自己的身份。 此生我定要试上一回； 因为我定要为自己添一件新斗篷。\" ——佚名，\"旧斗篷\"。16世纪。","“I have always been fond of the West African proverb: ‘Speak softly and carry a big stick; you will go far.’ If I had not carried the big stick, the organization would not have gotten behind me, and if I had yelled and blustered, as Pankhurst and the similar dishonest lunatics desired, I would not have had ten votes.” -Theodore Roosevelt, in a letter to Henry L. Sprague. January 26, 1900.":"\"我一直喜欢这则西非谚语：'言语温和，手持大棒，你必将走远。'倘若我没有手握大棒，组织便不会支持我；倘若我像潘克赫斯特之流那些不诚实的疯子所期望的那样大喊大叫、虚张声势，我连十票都得不到。\" ——西奥多·罗斯福，致亨利·L·斯普拉格的信。1900年1月26日。","“He drew his dagger, that was sae sharp, That was sae sharp and meet, And drave it into the nut-browne bride, That fell deid at his feit.":"\"他拔出匕首，如此锋利， 如此锋利而精巧， 刺入那棕发新娘的胸膛， 她倒地死在他脚边。","‘Now stay for me, dear Annet,’ he sed, ‘Now stay, my dear,’ he cry'd; Then strake the dagger untill his heart, And fell deid by her side.” -English traditional ballad, “Lord Thomas and Fair Annet”, circa 1650.":"'等等我，亲爱的安妮特，'他说， '等等，吾爱，'他喊道； 然后将匕首刺入自己的心脏， 倒在她身旁死去。\" ——英格兰传统民谣，\"托马斯勋爵与美丽的安妮特\"，约1650年。","“He drew his dagger, that was sae sharp, That was sae sharp and meet, And drave it into the nut-browne bride, That fell deid at his feit. ‘Now stay for me, dear Annet,’ he sed, ‘Now stay, my dear,’ he cry'd; Then strake the dagger untill his heart, And fell deid by her side.” -English traditional ballad, “Lord Thomas and Fair Annet”, circa 1650.":"\"他拔出匕首，如此锋利， 如此锋利而精巧， 刺入那棕发新娘的胸膛， 她倒地死在他脚边。 '等等我，亲爱的安妮特，'他说， '等等，吾爱，'他喊道； 然后将匕首刺入自己的心脏， 倒在她身旁死去。\" ——英格兰传统民谣，\"托马斯勋爵与美丽的安妮特\"，约1650年。","“This caliber should be appropriate.” -prince Dajmiech, “Kajko and Kokosz: The Battle with Dajmiech”, Janusz Christa":"\"这个口径应该够用了。\" ——达伊米耶赫王子，《卡伊科与科科什：与达伊米耶赫之战》，雅努什·克里斯塔。","“Quemadmodum gladius neminem occidit: occidentis telum est.” “A sword by itself does not slay; it is merely the weapon used by the slayer.” -Lucius Annaeus Seneca, _Epistulae Morales ad Lucilium_, Letter LXXXVII: Some arguments in favor of the simple life, l. 30. ca. 65 A.D. trans. Richard Mott Gummere, 1917.":"\"Quemadmodum gladius neminem occidit: occidentis telum est.\" \"剑本身不杀任何人，它不过是杀人者所用的工具。\" ——卢修斯·安奈乌斯·塞内卡，《致卢基利乌斯的道德书简》，第八十七封信：为简朴生活辩护的几个论据，第30行。约公元65年。 理查德·莫特·古默尔英译，1917年。","“At these words he started up, and beheld—not his Sophia—no, nor a Circassian maid richly and elegantly attired for the grand Signior's seraglio. No; without a gown, in a shift that was somewhat of the coarsest, and none of the cleanest, bedewed likewise with some odoriferous effluvia, the produce of the day's labour, with a pitchfork in her hand, Molly Seagrim approached.” -Henry Fielding, _The History of Tom Jones, a Foundling_, Book V, ch. X. 1749.":"\"听到这话，他惊跳起来，看到的——不是他的索菲亚——不，也不是为苏丹后宫精心打扮的切尔克斯美人。不；没穿长裙，只穿着一件颇为粗糙、也不甚干净的衬衣，上面还沾着些许当日劳作产生的芬芳气味，手里握着一把干草叉——莫莉·西格里姆走了过来。\" ——亨利·菲尔丁，《弃儿汤姆·琼斯的历史》，第五卷第十章。1749年。","“With a terrible cry the Balrog fell forward, and its shadow plunged down and vanished. But even as it fell it swung its whip, and the thongs lashed and curled about the wizard's knees, dragging him to the brink. He staggered, and fell, grasped vainly at the stone, and slid into the abyss.” -J.R.R. Tolkien, _The Fellowship of the Ring_. II, 5, “The Bridge of Khazad-dûm”. 1954.":"\"伴随着一声可怕的嚎叫，炎魔向前倒下，它的阴影坠入深渊，消失了。但就在坠落之际，它挥动了鞭子，鞭梢抽打着缠绕住巫师的膝盖，将他拖向边缘。他踉跄着坠落，徒劳地抓向石头，滑入了深渊。\" ——J.R.R.托尔金，《魔戒同盟》，第二卷第五章\"卡扎督姆之桥\"。1954年。","“‘Ah! ah! ah!’ laughed his two men, ‘how the Norman villains will be humbled when they see their doughty knight's skull beaten in by our brave countryman.’” -_Tales of Chivalry; or, Perils by Flood and Field_. 1830.":"\"'哈！哈！哈！'他的两个手下笑道，'看那些诺曼恶棍看到他们勇猛的骑士被我们勇敢的同胞用连枷砸碎脑壳时，该有多么屈辱。'\" ——《骑士传奇；或，洪水与战场之危》。1830年。","<dreamshard necklace>":"<dreamshard necklace>","“I never knew, I never thought, Such bliss as this could fill me with a love divine, I'm afraid I'll wake and find it was only in my mind, Was it a dream, or are you really mine?” -Dick Powell, \"Was It a Dream?\". 1928.":"\"我从未知晓，从未想过， 如此至福竟能以神圣之爱充溢我心， 我怕醒来发现一切不过是梦中幻影， 这是梦吗，还是你真正属于我？\" ——迪克·鲍威尔，《这是梦吗？》。1928年。","<demon blade>":"<demon blade>","“It is said to have been the favourite weapon of the Norman priest, who, objecting to the shedding of blood, had no scruple about the dashing out of brains.” -T. M. Allison, “The Flail and Kindred Tools (from a historical and literary standpoint)”, _Archaeologia Aeliana_, Third Series, vol. IV. 1908.":"\"据说这是那位诺曼神父最喜爱的武器，他反对流血，却对敲碎脑浆毫无顾忌。\" ——T.M.阿利森，\"连枷及其同类工具（从历史与文学的角度看）\"，《阿利安娜考古》，第三辑，第四卷。1908年。","“‘But I am frightened of what is dark, urZah.’":"\"'可是我害怕黑暗中的东西，乌尔扎。'","‘With reason,’ the urRu replied. ‘Darkness imprisons the light. Darkness destroys all beings, covets all energy. It is evil.’":"'有理由的，'乌尔鲁答道。'黑暗囚禁了光明。黑暗摧毁一切生灵，觊觎一切能量。它是邪恶的。'","‘What is evil?’ Jen asked.":"'什么是邪恶？'詹问道。","‘Evil does not exist,’ urZah answered. ‘Evil is disharmony between existences. Now go, Gelfling, with your questions.’” -A. C. H. Smith, _Jim Henson’s “The Dark Crystal”: The Novelization_. 1982.":"'邪恶并不存在，'乌尔扎回答。'邪恶是存在之间的不和谐。现在去吧，格尔夫林，带着你的问题。'\" ——A.C.H.史密斯，《吉姆·亨森的\"魔水晶\"：小说版》。1982年。","“‘But I am frightened of what is dark, urZah.’ ‘With reason,’ the urRu replied. ‘Darkness imprisons the light. Darkness destroys all beings, covets all energy. It is evil.’ ‘What is evil?’ Jen asked. ‘Evil does not exist,’ urZah answered. ‘Evil is disharmony between existences. Now go, Gelfling, with your questions.’” -A. C. H. Smith, _Jim Henson’s “The Dark Crystal”: The Novelization_. 1982.":"\"'可是我害怕黑暗中的东西，乌尔扎。' '有理由的，'乌尔鲁答道。'黑暗囚禁了光明。黑暗摧毁一切生灵，觊觎一切能量。它是邪恶的。' '什么是邪恶？'詹问道。 '邪恶并不存在，'乌尔扎回答。'邪恶是存在之间的不和谐。现在去吧，格尔夫林，带着你的问题。'\" ——A.C.H.史密斯，《吉姆·亨森的\"魔水晶\"：小说版》。1982年。","“She danced, and was compelled to dance—to dance in the dark night. The shoes carried her on over thorn and brier; she scratched herself till she bled; she danced away across the heath to a little lonely house. Here she knew the executioner dwelt; and she tapped with her fingers on the panes, and called,—‘Come out, come out! I cannot come in, for I must dance!’":"\"她跳着，被迫跳着——在黑夜中跳着。鞋子带着她越过荆棘和灌木；她把自己刮得鲜血淋漓；她跳过荒野，来到一座孤独的小屋前。她知道刽子手住在这里；她用指节敲着窗格，喊道——'出来，出来！我进不去，因为我必须跳舞！'","And the Executioner said,—‘You probably don't know who I am? I cut off the bad people's heads with my axe, and mark how my axe rings!’":"刽子手说——'你大概不知道我是谁吧？我用斧头砍掉坏人的脑袋，你听听我的斧头如何作响！'","‘Do not strike off my head,’ said Karen, ‘for if you do I cannot repent of my sin. But strike off my feet with the red shoes?’":"'不要砍我的头，'卡伦说，'因为那样我就无法为我的罪忏悔了。但请砍掉我穿着红鞋的脚吧？'","And then she confessed all her sin, and the Executioner cut off her feet with the red shoes; but the shoes danced away with the little feet over the fields and into the deep forest.":"于是她忏悔了自己所有的罪，刽子手连同红鞋一起砍掉了她的双脚；但鞋子带着那双小脚跳走了，越过田野，跳进了幽深的森林。","And he cut her a pair of wooden feet, with crutches, and taught her a psalm, which the criminals always sing; and she kissed the hand that had held the axe, and went away across the heath.” -Hans Christian Andersen, “The Red Shoes”, _Nye Eventyr. Første Bind. Tredie Samling._. 1845.":"他给她削了一双木脚和一对拐杖，教她一首罪人们常唱的圣诗；她亲吻了那只握过斧头的手，然后穿过荒野离去了。\" ——汉斯·克里斯蒂安·安徒生，\"红鞋\"，《新童话·第一卷·第三辑》。1845年。","“She danced, and was compelled to dance—to dance in the dark night. The shoes carried her on over thorn and brier; she scratched herself till she bled; she danced away across the heath to a little lonely house. Here she knew the executioner dwelt; and she tapped with her fingers on the panes, and called,—‘Come out, come out! I cannot come in, for I must dance!’ And the Executioner said,—‘You probably don't know who I am? I cut off the bad people's heads with my axe, and mark how my axe rings!’ ‘Do not strike off my head,’ said Karen, ‘for if you do I cannot repent of my sin. But strike off my feet with the red shoes?’ And then she confessed all her sin, and the Executioner cut off her feet with the red shoes; but the shoes danced away with the little feet over the fields and into the deep forest. And he cut her a pair of wooden feet, with crutches, and taught her a psalm, which the criminals always sing; and she kissed the hand that had held the axe, and went away across the heath.” -Hans Christian Andersen, “The Red Shoes”, _Nye Eventyr. Første Bind. Tredie Samling._. 1845.":"\"她跳着，被迫跳着——在黑夜中跳着。鞋子带着她越过荆棘和灌木；她把自己刮得鲜血淋漓；她跳过荒野，来到一座孤独的小屋前。她知道刽子手住在这里；她用指节敲着窗格，喊道——'出来，出来！我进不去，因为我必须跳舞！' 刽子手说——'你大概不知道我是谁吧？我用斧头砍掉坏人的脑袋，你听听我的斧头如何作响！' '不要砍我的头，'卡伦说，'因为那样我就无法为我的罪忏悔了。但请砍掉我穿着红鞋的脚吧？' 于是她忏悔了自己所有的罪，刽子手连同红鞋一起砍掉了她的双脚；但鞋子带着那双小脚跳走了，越过田野，跳进了幽深的森林。 他给她削了一双木脚和一对拐杖，教她一首罪人们常唱的圣诗；她亲吻了那只握过斧头的手，然后穿过荒野离去了。\" ——汉斯·克里斯蒂安·安徒生，\"红鞋\"，《新童话·第一卷·第三辑》。1845年。","“I have seen the day, with my good biting falchion I would have made them skip: I am old now, And these same crosses spoil me.” -William Shakespeare, _King Lear_, V, iii. 1608.":"\"我见过那样的日子，用我锋利的弯刀 我能让他们跳起来：可如今我老了， 这些磨难把我毁了。\" ——威廉·莎士比亚，《李尔王》，第五幕第三场。1608年。","“Even after forcing their way, with great effort and loss, through this double defence, [the Germans] still found themselves at a disadvantage; for their armour scarce enabled them to contend on equal terms with the uncouth but formidable weapons of their adversaries. The Bohemians were armed with long iron flails, which they swung with prodigious force. They seldom failed to hit, and when they did so, the flail crashed through brazen helmet, skull and all.” -James A. Wylie, _The History of Protestantism_, vol. I, book 3, ch. 15 “John Huss and the Hussite Wars”. 1878.":"\"即使付出了巨大的努力和惨重的损失，突破了这双重防御之后，[德意志人]仍然发现自己处于劣势；因为他们的盔甲几乎不足以与敌人那粗陋却可怕的武器平等对抗。波希米亚人装备着长柄铁连枷，以惊人的力量挥舞着。他们极少失手，而一旦命中，连枷便击穿铜盔、头颅与一切。\" ——詹姆斯·A·怀利，《新教史》，第一卷第三册第十五章\"约翰·胡斯与胡斯战争\"。1878年。","“Revenge is a dish best served cold.” -Klingon proverb, _Star Trek II: The Wrath of Khan_. 1982":"\"复仇是一道冷却后更美味的菜。\" ——克林贡谚语，《星际迷航II：可汗之怒》。1982年。","“Therewith the gyant buckled him to fight, Inflamd with scornefull wrath and high disdaine, And lifting up his dreadful club on hight, All armed with ragged snubbes and knottie graine, Him thought at first encounter to have slaine.” -Edmund Spenser, _The Faerie Queene_, Book I, “The Legend of the Knight of the Red Crosse”, Canto VIII, stanza vii, l. 55-9. 1590.":"\"于是那巨人开始蓄势战斗， 燃着轻蔑的愤怒与高傲的鄙夷， 将他那可怕的巨棒高高举起， 上面布满粗糙的节疤与多瘤的木纹， 他以为第一击便能将对手杀死。\" ——埃德蒙·斯宾塞，《仙后》，第一卷\"红十字骑士的传说\"，第八章第七节，第55-59行。1590年。","oni-ni-kanabō “oni with a spiked iron club” -Japanese proverb indicating overwhelming power":"鬼に金棒 \"鬼持铁棒\" ——表示力量压倒性的日本谚语","“To know the perfect length of your ſhort ſtaffe, or half Pike, Forreſt bil, Partiſan or Gleue, or ſuch like weapons of vantage and perfect lengths, you ſhall ſtand vpright, holding the ſtaffe vpright cloſe by your body, with your left hãd, reaching with your right hand your ſtaffe as high as you can, and then allow to that length a ſpace to ſet both your hands, when you come to fight, wherein you may conueniently ſtrike, thruſt and ward, & that is the iuſt length according to you ſtature. And this note, that theſe lengths will commonly fall out to be eight or nine foot long, and will fit, although not iuſt, the ſtatures of all men, without any hindrance at all vnto them in their fight, becauſe in any weapon wherin the hands may be remoued, and at libertie, to make the weapon lõger or ſhorter in fight at his pleaſure, a foot of the ſtaffe behind the backmoſt hand doth no harme.” -George Silver,_Paradoxes of Defence_.1599.":"\"欲知你短杖或半长矛、林地钩镰、花钺或长刃戟等有利且完美长度之武器的精确尺寸，你当直立，将杖竖直紧贴身侧，以左手握之，右手尽力向上伸展握住杖身，然后在此长度之上再留出双手握持之余地，以利实战中刺、击、格挡之便，此即合你身形之恰好长度。且注意，此等长度通常为八九英尺，虽不甚精准，却适用于一切人之身形而于实战中毫无妨碍，盖因在任何可移动双手、于战斗中随意伸缩武器之兵器上，最后方之手后多出一尺杖身亦无妨碍也。\" ——乔治·西尔弗，《防御悖论》。1599年。","“Here it was that the ambassadors of the Samnites, finding him boiling turnips in the chimney corner, offered him a present of gold; but he sent them away with this saying; that he, who was content with such a supper, had no need of gold; and that he thought it more honourable to conquer those who possessed the gold, than to possess the gold itself.” -Plutarch, “Marcus Cato”, _Lives_. 75 AD. trans. John Dryden, 1683.":"\"正是在这里，萨莫奈人的使者们发现他正在灶角煮萝卜，便献给他一份黄金作礼物；但他将他们打发走了，并留下了这样的话：一个满足于这样一顿晚餐的人，不需要黄金；他认为征服那些拥有黄金的人，比拥有黄金本身更光荣。\" ——普鲁塔克，\"马库斯·加图\"，《希腊罗马名人传》。公元75年。 约翰·德莱顿英译，1683年。","“There will arise one named Feridoun, who shall inherit thy throne and reverse thy fortunes, and strike thee down with a cow-headed mace.” -Firdausi, _Shahnameh_. ca. 1000 A.D. trans. Helen Zimmern, 1883.":"\"将有一人名曰费里敦崛起，他将继承你的王位， 扭转你的命运，以牛头权杖将你击倒。\" ——菲尔多西，《列王纪》。约公元1000年。 海伦·齐默恩英译，1883年。","“And Diarmid oh, Diarmid he perished in the strife; His head it was spiked upon a halberd high; His colours they were trampled: he had no chance of life If the Lord God Himself stood by!— Och, ochone!” -James Clarence Mangan , _A Farewell to Patrick Sarsfield, Earl of Lucan_. ca. 1840.":"\"而迪尔米德啊，迪尔米德，他在战斗中丧生； 他的头颅被挑在高高的戟上； 他的旗帜被践踏：他毫无生还之机， 即便主上帝亲自站在一旁！—— 哦，哀哉！\" ——詹姆斯·克拉伦斯·曼根，《告别帕特里克·萨斯菲尔德，卢坎伯爵》。约1840年。","“The hammah that John Henry swung, It weighed over nine poun', He broke a rib in his left han' side, And his intrels fell on the groun', And his intrels fell on the groun'.” -Onah L. Spencer, _John Henry_. Early 20th cent.":"\"约翰·亨利挥的那把锤， 重过九磅不止， 他左边身侧断了一根肋骨， 肠子掉到了地上， 肠子掉到了地上。\" ——奥纳·L·斯宾塞，《约翰·亨利》。20世纪初。","“Lizzie Borden took an axe And gave her mother forty whacks. When she saw what she had done She gave her father forty-one.” -A popular skipping-rope rhyme, after 1893.":"\"丽兹·波登拿起一把斧头， 给了她母亲四十下。 当她看到自己的所作所为， 又给了她父亲四十一下。\" ——流行跳绳童谣，1893年后。","“I do not aim with my hand; he who aims with his hand has forgotten the face of his father. I aim with my eye. I do not shoot with my hand; he who shoots with his hand has forgotten the face of his father. I shoot with my mind. I do not kill with my gun; he who kills with his gun has forgotten the face of his father. I kill with my heart.” —Stephen King, “The Dark Tower III: The Waste Lands”":"\"我不以手瞄准；以手瞄准的人已忘记了他父亲的面容。 我以眼瞄准。 我不以手射击；以手射击的人已忘记了他父亲的面容。 我以意志射击。 我不以枪杀人；以枪杀人的人已忘记了他父亲的面容。 我以心杀人。\" ——斯蒂芬·金，《黑暗塔III：荒原》。","“So Joshua called together the priests and said, “Take up the Ark of the Lord's Covenant, and assign seven priests to walk in front of it, each carrying a ram's horn.":"\"于是约书亚召集祭司，说：'抬起主之约柜，并指派七名祭司走在前面，每人手持一只公羊角。'","When the people heard the sound of the rams’ horns, they shouted as loud as they could. Suddenly, the walls of Jericho collapsed, and the Israelites charged straight into the town and captured it. They completely destroyed everything in it with their swords—men and women, young and old, cattle, sheep, goats, and donkeys.” -Joshua 6:6,20-21, New Living Translation":"当民众听到羊角的声音，他们尽力大声呼喊。突然，耶利哥的城墙倒塌了，以色列人径直冲入城中，夺取了它。他们用刀剑彻底毁灭了城中一切——男女老幼、牛羊驴畜。\" ——《约书亚记》6:6,20-21，新生活译本。","“So Joshua called together the priests and said, “Take up the Ark of the Lord's Covenant, and assign seven priests to walk in front of it, each carrying a ram's horn. When the people heard the sound of the rams’ horns, they shouted as loud as they could. Suddenly, the walls of Jericho collapsed, and the Israelites charged straight into the town and captured it. They completely destroyed everything in it with their swords—men and women, young and old, cattle, sheep, goats, and donkeys.” -Joshua 6:6,20-21, New Living Translation":"\"于是约书亚召集祭司，说：'抬起主之约柜，并指派七名祭司走在前面，每人手持一只公羊角。' 当民众听到羊角的声音，他们尽力大声呼喊。突然，耶利哥的城墙倒塌了，以色列人径直冲入城中，夺取了它。他们用刀剑彻底毁灭了城中一切——男女老幼、牛羊驴畜。\" ——《约书亚记》6:6,20-21，新生活译本。","\"You're made of metal, but you have feelings, and you think about things, and that means you have a soul. And souls don't die.\" -_The Iron Giant_. 1999":"\"你是金属做的，但你拥有感情，你会思考事物， 这意味着你拥有灵魂。而灵魂是不会死的。\" ——《钢铁巨人》。1999年。","“Suppose you found your brother in bed with your wife, and put a javelin through both of them, you would be justified, and they would atone for their sins, and be received into the kingdom of God.” -Brigham Young, _Journal of Discourses_, 3:247. 1856.":"\"假设你发现你的兄弟和你的妻子在床上，用一支标枪刺穿两人，你将是正当的，他们将为他们的罪赎罪，并被接纳进入上帝的国度。\" ——杨百翰，《讲道集》，3:247。1856年。","“...for the shield may be as important for victory, as the sword or spear.” -Charles Darwin, “The Origin of Species”. 1859.":"\"……因为盾牌对于胜利来说，可能与剑或矛同等重要。\" ——查尔斯·达尔文，《物种起源》。1859年。","“A weapon that comes down as still As snowflakes fall upon the sod; But executes a freeman's will, As lightning does the will of God.” -John Pierpont, “The Ballot”. ca. 1850.":"\"一件武器，落下时如 雪花飘落草地的静谧； 却执行自由人的意志， 如闪电执行上帝的旨意。\" ——约翰·皮尔庞特，\"选票\"。约1850年。","“Well, I run to the rock and I hide my face The rock cried out, No hiding place There's no hiding place down here.” -Negro spiritual. 19th cent.":"\"我奔向岩石，藏起我的脸 岩石喊道，没有藏身之处 这里没有藏身之处。\" ——黑人灵歌。19世纪。","<buckler>":"<buckler>","“Nought can Deform the Human race Like to the Armours iron brace” -William Blake, “Auguries of Innocence”, 99-100. 1803.":"\"没有任何东西能使人形堕落 如那铁甲的铁箍一般\" ——威廉·布莱克，\"天真之预言\"，第99-100行。1803年。","“While we were at grips with this great army and their dreadful broadswords (maquahuitl [made of obsidian]), many of the most powerful among the enemy seem to have decided to capture a horse. They began with a furious attack, and laid hands on a good mare well trained both for sport and battle. Her rider, Pedro de Moron, was a fine horseman; and as he charged with three other horsemen into the enemy ranks—they had been instructed to charge together for mutual support—some of them seized his lance so he could not use it, and others slashed at him with their broadswords (maquahuitl), wounding him severely. Then they slashed at his mare, cutting her head at the neck so that it only hung by the skin. The mare fell dead, and if his mounted comrades had not come to Moron's rescue, he would probably have been killed also.” -Bernal Díaz del Castillo, _The Conquest of New Spain_. 1623. trans. J.M.Cohen, 1963.":"\"当我们与这支大军及其可怕的阔剑（马夸维特尔，以黑曜石制成）搏斗时，许多最强大的敌人似乎决定要俘获一匹马。他们发起猛攻，将手伸向一匹训练有素、既善游戏又善战斗的好母马。她的骑手佩德罗·德·莫隆是一位优秀的骑手；当他与另外三名骑手一同冲入敌阵时——他们受命一同冲锋以互相支援——有些人抓住了他的长矛使他无法使用，另一些人则用他们的阔剑（马夸维特尔）向他砍去，使他身负重伤。然后他们砍向他的母马，将马头从脖颈处砍下，仅剩皮肤相连。母马倒地而死，若非他的骑兵同伴们赶来救援，莫隆恐怕也会被杀。\" ——贝尔纳尔·迪亚斯·德尔·卡斯蒂略，《征服新西班牙信史》。1623年。 J.M.科恩英译，1963年。","“Robyn bent a full goode bowe, An arrowe he drowe at wyll; He hit so the proud sherife Upon the grounde he lay full still.” -_A Gest of Robyn Hode_ Sixth Fytte, l. 120-123. ca. 1450.":"\"罗宾拉开一张好弓， 随心射出一箭； 正中那傲慢的郡长， 他静静躺在尘土间。\" ——《罗宾汉事迹》，第六歌，第120-123行。约1450年。","“[My plan] does not propose to fill your lobby with squabbling colony agents, who will require the interposition of your mace at every instant to keep the peace among them.” -Edmund Burke, “On Conciliation with America”, speech in Parliament. 1775.":"\"[我的方案]并不打算让你的大厅挤满争吵不休的殖民地代理人，他们每时每刻都需要你的权杖来维持彼此之间的和平。\" ——埃德蒙·伯克，\"论与美洲和解\"，议会演讲。1775年。","“Manuals have their uses... but they are not to be confused with living.” -Robert Fulghum":"\"手册有它的用处……但不能把它和真正的生活混为一谈。\" ——罗伯特·富尔格姆。","“Little did then his pomp of plumes bestead The Azteca, or glittering pride of gold. Against the tempered sword; little his casque, Cay with its feathery coronal, or drest In graven terrors, when the Briton's hand Drove in through helm and head the spiked mace; Or swung its iron weights with shattering sway. Which, where they fell, destroyed.” -Robert Southey, _Madoc_. 1805.":"\"他那羽毛的华饰与闪耀的 黄金之傲，在淬炼的剑锋前 毫无用处；他的头盔—— 饰以羽冠，或雕满恐怖图案—— 也无济于事，当不列颠人的手 将带刺的钉头锤刺入盔与颅； 或以摧枯拉朽之势挥舞其铁质重球， 所落之处，尽皆毁灭。\" ——罗伯特·骚塞，《马多克》。1805年。","“But soon as early Dawn appeared, the rosy-fingered, then gathered the folk about the pyre of glorious Hector.” -Homer, _The Iliad_, XXIV, 776. trans. A. T. Murray, 1857.":"\"但当玫瑰指的黎明女神初现时，人们便聚集在光荣的赫克托尔的火葬堆旁。\" ——荷马，《伊利亚特》，第廿四卷，第776行。 A.T.默里英译，1857年。","“Down at that far end of the hallway, the mirror hovered, shadowing us. We discovered (very late at night such a discovery is inevitable) that there is something monstrous about mirrors. That was when Bioy remembered a saying by one of the heresiarchs of Uqbar: ‘Mirrors and copulation are abominable, for they multiply the number of mankind.’” -Jorge Luis Borges, _Tlön, Uqbar, Orbis Tertius_. 1947 trans. Andrew Hurley, 1998.":"\"在走廊的那一头，那面镜子悬浮着，隐隐笼罩着我们。我们发现（在深夜，这样的发现是不可避免的）镜子有一种可怕之处。就在这时比奥伊想起了乌克巴尔的一位异端领袖的话：'镜子和性交都是可憎的，因为它们都使人类的数目倍增。'\" ——豪尔赫·路易斯·博尔赫斯，《特隆、乌克巴尔、奥比斯·特蒂乌斯》。1947年。 安德鲁·赫尔利英译，1998年。","“Then gave I her, — so tutor'd by my art, — A sleeping potion; which so took effect As I intended, for it wrought on her The form of death: meantime I writ to Romeo That he should hither come as this dire night, To help to take her from her borrow'd grave, Being the time the potion's force should cease.” -William Shakespeare, _Romeo and Juliet_":"\"于是我依计给了她—— 一瓶安眠之药；那药果然 如我所愿起了作用，因为它在她身上 造成了死亡的假象：同时我写信给罗密欧 让他赶在这可怕之夜来此， 帮她离开这座借来的坟墓， 因为那时药力应当正好消失。\" ——威廉·莎士比亚，《罗密欧与朱丽叶》。","“But if when you say ‘whiskey’ you mean the oil of conversation, the philosophic wine, the ale that is consumed when good fellows get together, that puts a song in their hearts and laughter on their lips, and the warm glow of contentment in their eyes... then certainly I am for it.” -Noah S. Sweat, Jr. “If By Whiskey”. 1952":"\"但如果你说'威士忌'时指的是交谈的润滑油、哲思的美酒、 好伙伴们相聚时饮下的麦芽酒，那能在他们心中放歌、 唇边挂笑、眼中洋溢温暖知足光芒的佳酿…… 那么我当然赞成。\" ——诺亚·S·斯威特二世，\"如果我说威士忌\"。1952年。","“Let go your earthly tether. Enter the void. Empty, and become wind.” -_The Legend of Korra_. 2014":"\"放开你的尘世羁绊。遁入虚空。放空，化为风。\" ——《科拉传奇》。2014年。","“I shall never forget that dawn, and the strange horror of seeing that my hands had become as clouded glass, and watching them grow clearer and thinner as the day went by, until at last I could see the sickly disorder of my room through them, though I closed my transparent eyelids. My limbs became glassy, the bones and arteries faded, vanished, and the little white nerves went last. I gritted my teeth and stayed there to the end. At last only the dead tips of the fingernails remained, pallid and white, and the brown stain of some acid, upon my fingers.” -H.G. Wells, _The Invisible Man_, Chapter 20. 1897":"\"我永远不会忘记那个黎明，以及看到我双手变得如磨砂玻璃一般的奇异恐怖，看着它们随着白日推移变得越来越清晰、越来越薄，直到最后我能透过它们看到我房间里的病态混乱，尽管我闭着透明的眼睑。我的四肢变得玻璃般透明，骨骼和动脉逐渐消隐、消失，最后消失的是那些白色的小神经。我咬紧牙关，在那里坚持到了最后。最终只剩下指甲末端，死气沉沉、苍白无色，还有我手指上某种酸液留下的褐色污渍。\" ——H.G.威尔斯，《隐形人》，第二十章。1897年。","“Before her prayer was ended, torpor seized on all her body, and a thin bark closed around her gentle bosom, and her hair became as moving leaves; her arms were changed to waving branches, and her active feet as clinging roots were fastened to the ground— her face was hidden with encircling leaves.” -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, Book I:253-259, trans. Brookes More. 1922":"\"她的祈祷尚未结束，麻木便攫住了 她整个身躯，一层薄树皮包裹住 她温柔的胸膛，她的头发 化作摇曳的叶片；她的手臂变成 摆动的枝条，她灵活的双脚 如紧抓的根须牢牢扎入地面—— 她的面容被环绕的叶子遮掩。\" ——奥维德，《变形记》，第一卷：253-259行，布鲁克斯·莫尔英译。1922年。","“If when you say ‘whiskey’ you mean the devil's brew, the poison scourge, the bloody monster, that defiles innocence, dethrones reason, destroys the home, creates misery and poverty, yea, literally takes the bread from the mouths of little children... then certainly I am against it.” -Noah S. Sweat, Jr. “If By Whiskey”. 1952":"\"但如果你说'威士忌'时指的是魔鬼的酿造、剧毒的 祸害、血腥的怪物，它玷污纯真、废黜 理智、摧毁家庭、制造苦难与贫穷，甚至 从幼小孩童的口中夺走面包…… 那么我当然反对。\" ——诺亚·S·斯威特二世，\"如果我说威士忌\"。1952年。","“Aha! will fate play tricks upon me? Will the elements lay plots against me? Shall fire, air, and water make a combined attack against me? Well, they shall know what a determined man can do. I will not yield. I will not stir a single foot backwards, and it will be seen whether man or nature is to have the upper hand!” -Jules Verne, _Journey into the Interior of the Earth_. 1864 trans. F.A. Malleson, 1877":"\"啊哈！命运要捉弄我吗？自然元素要密谋害我吗？ 火焰、空气和水要联合攻击我吗？好吧，它们 会知道一个意志坚定的人能做什么。我不会屈服。我不会 后退一步，且看看是人还是自然 能够占据上风！\" ——儒勒·凡尔纳，《地心游记》。1864年。 F.A.马勒森英译，1877年。","“Then Robin he unbuckled his belt, And laid down his bow so long; He took up a staff of another oak graff, That was both stiff and strong. ‘But let me measure,’ said jolly Robin, ‘Before we begin our fray; For I'll not have mine to be longer than thine, For that will be counted foul play.’ ‘I pass not for length,’ bold Arthur replied, ‘My staff is of oak so free; Eight foot and a half it will knock down a calf, And I hope it will knock down thee.’ Then Robin could no longer forbear, He gave him such a knock, Quickly and soon the blood came down, Before it was ten o'clock. About and about and about they went, Like two wild boars in a chase, Striving to aim each other to maim, Leg, arm, or any other place. And knock for knock they hastily dealt, Which held for two hours and more; That all the wood rang at every bang, They plied their work so sore.” -Anonymous, “Robin Hood and the Tanner”.":"\"于是罗宾解开他的腰带， 放下他那把长弓； 他拿起一根橡木棍， 又硬又强又结实。 '但让我量一量，'快活的罗宾说， '在我们动手之前； 因为我不愿我的比你的长， 那会被算作不公平。' '我不在乎长短，'勇敢的亚瑟答道， '我的棍是上好的橡木； 八尺半长，能打倒一头小牛， 我希望它也能打倒你。' 于是罗宾再也按捺不住， 他给了他一记重击， 迅疾之间，血就淌了下来， 还没到十点钟。 他们转来转去，转来转去， 像两头追逐的野猪， 竭力想打残对方， 大腿、手臂，或任何地方。 一击换一击，他们急促地对打， 持续了两小时有余； 每次撞击，整座树林都回响， 他们打得如此猛烈。\" ——佚名，\"罗宾汉与制革匠\"。","“He hath loosed the fateful lightning of His terrible swift sword...” -Julia Ward Howe, “The Battle Hymn of the Republic”. 1861.":"\"祂可怖的迅剑已经挥出宿命的闪电……\" ——朱莉娅·沃德·豪，《共和国战歌》。1861年。","“Who was the first that forged the deadly blade? Of rugged steel his savage soul was made...” -Albius Tibullus, _Elegies_ I, xi. ca. 25 B.C. trans. James Grainger, 1822.":"\"是谁最先铸造了那致命的利刃？ 他的野蛮灵魂必是粗砺钢铁铸成……\" ——阿尔比乌斯·提布鲁斯，《哀歌》第一卷第十一首。约公元前25年。 詹姆斯·格兰杰英译，1822年。","“A ring of gold and a milk-white dove Are goodly gifts for thee, And a hempen rope for your own love To hang upon a tree.” -Oscar Wilde, “Chanson”. 1881.":"\"一枚金戒指和一只乳白鸽 是给你的好礼物， 还有一根麻绳给你的爱人 挂在树上。\" ——奥斯卡·王尔德，\"香颂\"。1881年。","“A mermaid who fancied to sing, Roused lust in the Octopus King. Her squiggly suitor, Tried hard to woo her, But she couldn't wear all his rings.”":"\"有一条美人鱼想唱歌， 唤起了章鱼王的欲火。 她那蜿蜒的追求者， 使劲想把她俘获， 但她戴不下他所有的戒指。\"","<ring>":"<ring>","“Love is a burning thing And it makes a fiery ring” -June Carter and Merle Kilgore, “Ring of Fire”. 1963.":"\"爱是一团燃烧之物 它铸成一枚烈火之戒\" ——琼·卡特与梅尔·基尔戈，\"火之戒\"。1963年。","“What surprised him the most, however, was the logic of his wings. They seemed so natural on that completely human organism that he couldn't understand why other men didn't have them too.” -Gabriel Garcia Marquez, _A Very Old Man with Enormous Wings_. 1955. trans. Gregory Rabassa. 1972":"\"然而最让他惊讶的，是他那对翅膀的逻辑。它们在那完全人类的机体上显得如此自然，以至于他无法理解为什么其他人类没有翅膀。\" ——加夫列尔·加西亚·马尔克斯，《巨翅老人》。1955年。 格雷戈里·拉巴萨英译。1972年。","“Some say the world will end in fire; Some say in ice. From what I've tasted of desire I hold with those who favor fire. But if it had to perish twice, I think I know enough of hate To say that for destruction ice Is also great And would suffice.” -Robert Frost, “Fire and Ice”. 1920.":"\"有人说世界将毁于火； 有人说毁于冰。 从我尝过的欲望滋味来看 我赞同那些倾向于火的人。 但倘若它必须毁灭两次， 我想我对仇恨了解得足够多 以至于可以说，就毁灭而言，冰 也同样出色 且足矣。\" ——罗伯特·弗罗斯特，\"火与冰\"。1920年。","“Hobbes: Did it work? Calvin: I think so. I feel smarter already.” -Bill Watterson, _Calvin and Hobbes_. November 19, 1993.":"\"霍布斯：管用吗？ 卡尔文：我觉得管用。 我已经感觉自己更聪明了。\" ——比尔·沃特森，《卡尔文与霍布斯》。1993年11月19日。","Buttercup: “And to think, all that time it was your cup that was poisoned.” Man in Black: “They were both poisoned. I spent the last few years building up an immunity to iocane powder.” -_The Princess Bride_. 1987":"金凤花： \"想想看，这一直以来都是你的杯子被下了毒。\" 黑衣人： \"两个杯子都下了毒。我花了好几年时间 建立起了对伊奥卡因粉的免疫力。\" ——《公主新娘》。1987年。","“And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, fell down bound into the midst of the burning fiery furnace.":"\"这三个人，沙得拉、米煞和亚伯尼歌，被捆着落入烈火燃烧的窑中。","Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonished, and rose up in haste, and spake, and said unto his counsellors, Did not we cast three men bound into the midst of the fire? They answered and said unto the king, True, O king.":"那时尼布甲尼撒王惊奇，急忙起来，对谋士说：我们捆起来扔在火里的不是三个人吗？他们回答王说：王啊，是的。","He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.":"王说：看哪，我见有四个人，并没有捆绑，在火中行走，也没有受伤；那第四个的相貌好像神子。","Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace, and spake, and said, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come hither. Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, came forth of the midst of the fire.":"于是尼布甲尼撒走近烈火燃烧的窑门，说：至高神的仆人沙得拉、米煞、亚伯尼歌，出来，上这里来吧。沙得拉、米煞、亚伯尼歌就从火中出来了。","And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king’s counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them.” -KJV Bible, Daniel 3:23-27.":"那些总督、巡抚、首领和王的谋士一同聚集来看这三个人，见火无力伤他们的身体，头发也没有烧焦，衣裳也没有变色，并没有火燎的气味。\" ——圣经和合本，《但以理书》3:23-27。","“And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, fell down bound into the midst of the burning fiery furnace. Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonished, and rose up in haste, and spake, and said unto his counsellors, Did not we cast three men bound into the midst of the fire? They answered and said unto the king, True, O king. He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God. Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace, and spake, and said, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come hither. Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, came forth of the midst of the fire. And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king’s counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them.” -KJV Bible, Daniel 3:23-27.":"\"这三个人，沙得拉、米煞和亚伯尼歌，被捆着落入烈火燃烧的窑中。 那时尼布甲尼撒王惊奇，急忙起来，对谋士说：我们捆起来扔在火里的不是三个人吗？他们回答王说：王啊，是的。 王说：看哪，我见有四个人，并没有捆绑，在火中行走，也没有受伤；那第四个的相貌好像神子。 于是尼布甲尼撒走近烈火燃烧的窑门，说：至高神的仆人沙得拉、米煞、亚伯尼歌，出来，上这里来吧。沙得拉、米煞、亚伯尼歌就从火中出来了。 那些总督、巡抚、首领和王的谋士一同聚集来看这三个人，见火无力伤他们的身体，头发也没有烧焦，衣裳也没有变色，并没有火燎的气味。\" ——圣经和合本，《但以理书》3:23-27。","“Here is my secret. It is very simple: It is only with the heart that one can see rightly; what is essential is invisible to the eye.” -Antoine de Saint Exupéry, _The Little Prince_. 1943.":"\"这是我的秘密。它很简单：只有用心才能看得清楚；本质的东西，用眼睛是看不见的。\" ——安托万·德·圣-埃克苏佩里，《小王子》。1943年。","“Life is too short to occupy oneself with the slaying of the slain more than once.” -Thomas Huxley":"\"生命太短暂，不可将已被杀者反复杀戮。\" ——托马斯·赫胥黎。","“Then as part of the game She completely forgot where she'd hidden herself And she spent the rest of her time Trying to find the parts” -Howard Jones, “Hide and Seek”. 1984.":"\"然后作为游戏的一部分 她完全忘了把自己藏在了哪里 于是她花了余下的时间 试图找到那些碎片\" ——霍华德·琼斯，\"捉迷藏\"。1984年。","“That which does not kill us makes us stronger.” -Friedrich Nietzsche":"\"那不能杀死我的，必使我更强大。\" ——弗里德里希·尼采。","“I am, indeed, a king, because I know how to rule myself.” -Pietro Aretino, letter to Mr. Agostino Ricchi, May 10th, 1537. from _The Works of Aretino, Translated into English from the original Italian_, trans. Samuel Putnam. 1926":"\"我确实是一位君王，因为我知道如何统治自己。\" ——彼得罗·阿雷蒂诺，致阿戈斯蒂诺·里奇先生的信，1537年5月10日。引自 《阿雷蒂诺作品集，自意大利原文译为英文》， 萨缪尔·帕特南英译。1926年。","“CLEOPATRA: Give me my robe, put on my crown; I have Immortal longings in me” -William Shakespeare, _Anthony & Cleopatra_, V, ii. ca. 1605.":"\"克莉奥佩特拉：给我拿袍子来，替我戴上王冠；我心中 怀有不朽的渴望\" ——威廉·莎士比亚，《安东尼与克莉奥佩特拉》，第五幕第二场。约1605年。","“The museum-cabinet and huge library arrogated to themselves the entire lower floor — there were the controversial and incompatible books that are somehow the history of the nineteenth century; there were scimitars from Nishapur, in whose frozen crescents the wind and violence of battle seemed to be living on.” -Jorge Luis Borges, _The Form of the Sword_. 1953. trans. Andrew Hurley.":"\"博物馆和庞大的藏书室占据了整个底层——那里陈列着那些彼此矛盾、不可调和的书，它们不知怎地就是十九世纪的历史；那里还有来自尼沙普尔的弯刀，在其冰冷的弧形刀刃中，战斗的风与暴力似乎仍然生生不息。\" ——豪尔赫·路易斯·博尔赫斯，《剑之形》。1953年。 安德鲁·赫尔利英译。","“To drift with every passion till my soul Is a stringed lute on which all winds can play, Is it for this that I have given away Mine ancient wisdom, and austere control? Methinks my life is a twice-written scroll Scrawled over on some boyish holiday.” -Oscar Wilde, _Helas_. 1881.":"\"随每一阵激情飘荡，直到我的灵魂 变成一面弦琴，任一切风来弹拨， 难道就是为了这个，我才放弃了 我那古老的智慧与严厉的自律？ 我想，我的生命是一张重写过的卷轴 在某次稚气的假日里被胡乱涂鸦。\" ——奥斯卡·王尔德，《唉》。1881年。","He had stopped trying to think. He just repeated his litany over and over: “I am an animal, you see that. I don’t have the words, they didn’t teach me the words. I don’t know how to think, the bastards didn’t let me learn how to think. But if you really are... all-powerful... all-knowing... then you figure it out! Look into my heart. I know that everything you need is in there. It has to be. I never sold my soul to anyone! It’s mine, it’s human! You take from me what it is I want... it just can’t be that I would want something bad! Damn it all, I can’t think of anything, except those words of his... ‘HAPPINESS FOR EVERYBODY, FREE, AND NO ONE WILL GO AWAY UNSATISFIED!’” -Arkady and Boris Strugatsky, “Roadside Picnic”. 1972. trans. Antonina W. Bouis, 1977.":"他已停止尝试思考。他只是反复念诵着他的祷文： \"我是一只动物，你看得出来。我不懂那些词，他们没教 我那些词。我不知道怎么思考，那些混蛋不让我学 怎么思考。但如果你真的是……全能的……全知的……那你自己 想明白！看看我的心。我知道你需要的一切都在里面。 一定在。我从来没有把我的灵魂出卖给任何人！它是我的，它是人的！你 从我这里找出我想要的究竟是什么……我不可能想要什么 坏东西！该死，我什么都想不出来，除了他的那些话…… '人人幸福，免费，而且没有人会不满地离去！'\" ——阿尔卡季和鲍里斯·斯特鲁加茨基，《路边野餐》。1972年。 安东尼娜·W·布伊斯英译，1977年。","“But revenge is hollow. I'd prefer amnesia.” -Tera Lynn Childs":"\"但复仇是空洞的。我更愿意失忆。\" ——特拉·琳恩·柴尔兹。","<scroll>":"<scroll>","“It used to be thought that the events that changed the world were things like big bombs, maniac politicians, huge earthquakes, or vast population movements, but it has now been realized that this is a very old-fashioned view held by people totally out of touch with modern thought. The things that really change the world, according to Chaos theory, are the tiny things. A butterfly flaps its wings in the Amazonian jungle, and subsequently a storm ravages half of Europe...” -Neil Gaiman and Terry Pratchett, _Good Omens: The Nice And Accurate Prophecies of Agnes Nutter, Witch_. 1990.":"\"过去人们认为，改变世界的事件是像大型炸弹、疯子政客、巨大地震或大规模人口迁徙之类的东西，但现在人们已经认识到，这是一种非常过时的观点，持有这种观点的人完全与现代思想脱节。根据混沌理论，真正改变世界的，是那些微小的事物。一只蝴蝶在亚马逊丛林中扇动翅膀，随后一场风暴便肆虐了半个欧洲……\" ——尼尔·盖曼与特里·普拉切特，《好兆头：女巫阿格妮丝·纳特精雅准确的预言》。1990年。","“I will revenge my injuries: if I cannot inspire love, I will cause fear.” -Mary Shelley, _Frankenstein, or the Modern Prometheus_, Vol. II, Chapter 9. 1818 (1st Ed.)":"\"我要报复我的创伤：如果我无法唤起爱，我就要制造恐惧。\" ——玛丽·雪莱，《弗兰肯斯坦，或现代普罗米修斯》， 第二卷第九章。1818年（第一版）。","“Calvin: I used to hate writing assignments, but now I enjoy them. I realized that the purpose of writing is to inflate weak ideas, obscure poor reasoning, and inhibit clarity. With a little practice, writing can be an intimidating and impenetrable fog!” -Bill Watterson, _Calvin and Hobbes_. February 11th, 1993.":"\"卡尔文：我过去讨厌写作作业，但现在我喜欢了。我意识到 写作的目的就是给贫乏的想法充气，让糟糕的推理更模糊， 并阻碍表达的清晰。稍加练习，写作就能变成一道 令人生畏、难以穿透的浓雾！\" ——比尔·沃特森，《卡尔文与霍布斯》。1993年2月11日。","“This, what is it in itself, and by itself, according to its proper constitution? What is the substance of it? What is the matter, or proper use? What is the form or efficient cause? What is it for in this world, and how long will it abide? Thus must thou examine all things, that present themselves unto thee.” -Marcus Aurelius, _Marcus Aurelius Antoninus - His Meditations concerning himselfe_, Book VIII, X. trans. Meric Casaubon, 1634.":"\"这个事物，就其本身，按它自身的构造，它究竟是什么？它的实质是什么？它的材料或功用是什么？它的形式或动力因是什么？它在这个世界上是为了什么，又能存在多久？你必须这样审察一切呈现在你面前的事物。\" ——马可·奥勒留，《沉思录》，第八卷第十章。梅里克·卡索邦英译，1634年。","“‘What a useful thing a pocket-map is!’ I remarked. ‘That’s another thing we’ve learned from your Nation,’ said Mein Herr, ‘map-making. But we’ve carried it much further than you. What do you consider the largest map that would be really useful?’ ‘About six inches to the mile.’ ‘Only six inches!’ exclaimed Mein Herr. ‘We very soon got to six yards to the mile. Then we tried a hundred yards to the mile. And then came the grandest idea of all! We actually made a map of the country, on the scale of a mile to the mile!’ ‘Have you used it much?’ I enquired. ‘It has never been spread out, yet,’ said Mein Herr: ‘the farmers objected: they said it would cover the whole country, and shut out the sunlight! So we now use the country itself, as its own map, and I assure you it does nearly as well.’” -Lewis Carroll, _Sylvie and Bruno Concluded_, Chapter XI. 1895":"\"'口袋地图是多么有用的东西啊！'我说道。 '这是我们向贵国学到的另一件事，'迈因·赫尔说，'地图制作。不过我们比你们走得远得多。 你认为真正有用的最大的地图是多大比例尺？' '大约六英寸兑一英里吧。' '才六英寸！'迈因·赫尔叫道。'我们很快就做到了六码兑一英里。然后我们尝试了一百码兑一英里。 接着，最伟大的想法诞生了！我们真的制作了一幅国家的地图，比例尺为一英里兑一英里！' '你们用得很多吗？'我问道。 '它还没有被展开过，'迈因·赫尔说：'农民们反对：他们说它会覆盖 整个国家，遮住阳光！所以我们现在把国家本身当作自己的地图， 我向你保证，效果也差不多。'\" ——刘易斯·卡罗尔，《西尔维与布鲁诺终结篇》，第十一章。1895年。","“The nature of the place where the Library was founded—a sanatorium rumored to harbor the pitiably deformed—had proven a lure to people with no desire at all for ‘regular human communication.’ I remember the case of a man who was normal in every respect, in words, in reasoning, in the practice of his profession, but strayed from this ‘normalcy’ in only one way: his inexplicable need to fill thousands of sheets of foolscap paper with seemingly meaningless words, phonemes close to wailing sounds, cries of fury and pain in relentless successions, fragments of sentences and pleas addressed to God-knows-whom.” -Giorgio de Maria, _The Twenty Days of Turin_, 1975. trans. Ramon Glazov, 2016":"\"图书馆所在地的性质——一所谣传收容着可怜畸形者的疗养院——对毫无'正常人际交流'欲望的人成了一种诱惑。我记得有一个案例，一个在各方面都正常的男人，在言辞、推理和职业实践上，都无从挑剔，但唯有一点偏离了这种'正常'：他不可解释地需要将成千上万张大页纸上写满看似毫无意义的词语、近乎哀嚎之音的音节、无休无止的愤怒与痛苦的呼喊、残缺的句段，以及写给天知道是谁的哀求。\" ——乔尔乔·德·马里亚，《都灵二十日》。1975年。 拉蒙·格拉佐夫英译，2016年。","“And in the naked light I saw Ten thousand people, maybe more. People talking without speaking, People hearing without listening; People writing songs That voices never shared: No one dared Disturb the sound Of silence.” -Simon & Garfunkel, _The Sound of Silence_. 1964.":"\"在赤裸的光中我看见 一万人，或许更多。 人们在交谈却不说话， 人们在聆听却不倾听； 人们写着歌 那些从未被声音分享的歌： 没有人敢 打扰那寂静 之声。\" ——西蒙与加芬克尔，《寂静之声》。1964年。","“When thou attended gloriously from heaven, Shalt in the sky appear, and from thee send Thy summoning archangels to proclaim Thy dread tribunal.” -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book III, 1667.":"\"当你荣耀地从天降临，在天空显现，从你那里派遣 传召众生的大天使，宣告你威严的审判庭。\" ——约翰·弥尔顿，《失乐园》，第三卷。1667年。","“Eiris sazun idisi sazun hera duoder suma hapt heptidun suma heri lezidun suma clubodun umbi cuoniouuidi insprinc haptbandun inuar uigandun":"\"Eiris sazun idisi sazun hera duoder suma hapt heptidun suma heri lezidun suma clubodun umbi cuoniouuidi insprinc haptbandun inuar uigandun","[Once sat women, they sat here then there. some fastened bonds, some impeded an army, some unraveled fetters: Escape the bonds, flee the enemy!]” -First Merseburg incantation, trans. Patricia Giangrosso, 2001":"[曾有女人们坐在一起， 她们坐在这里，又坐在那里。 有的系紧了绳索， 有的阻拦了军队， 有的解开了桎梏： 挣脱束缚， 逃离敌人！]\" ——第一则梅泽堡咒语，帕特里夏·吉安格罗索英译，2001年。","“Eiris sazun idisi sazun hera duoder suma hapt heptidun suma heri lezidun suma clubodun umbi cuoniouuidi insprinc haptbandun inuar uigandun [Once sat women, they sat here then there. some fastened bonds, some impeded an army, some unraveled fetters: Escape the bonds, flee the enemy!]” -First Merseburg incantation, trans. Patricia Giangrosso, 2001":"\"Eiris sazun idisi sazun hera duoder suma hapt heptidun suma heri lezidun suma clubodun umbi cuoniouuidi insprinc haptbandun inuar uigandun [曾有女人们坐在一起， 她们坐在这里，又坐在那里。 有的系紧了绳索， 有的阻拦了军队， 有的解开了桎梏： 挣脱束缚， 逃离敌人！]\" ——第一则梅泽堡咒语，帕特里夏·吉安格罗索英译，2001年。","“It was instinct. Illogical as lightning striking and not hurting. Each day the grain must be cut. It had to be cut. Why? Well, it just did, that was all. He laughed at the scythe in his big hands. Then, whistling, he took it out to the ripe and waiting field and did the work. He thought himself a little mad. Hell, it was an ordinary-enough wheat field, really, wasn't it?” -Ray Bradbury, _The Scythe_. 1943.":"\"这是本能。如闪电击而不伤一般不合逻辑。每日谷物都必须收割。必须收割。为什么？嗯，就是必须，就是这样。他对着大手中的镰刀笑了笑。然后，吹着口哨，他把它带到那片成熟而等待的麦田，干了起来。他觉得自己有点疯了。见鬼，这本来就是一片很普通的麦田，不是吗？\" ——雷·布拉德伯里，《镰刀》。1943年。","“‘Hurrah! my boys,’ says I, my shillelagh I let fly. Some Galway boys were by, they saw I was a hobbling; Then with a loud ‘hurrah!’ they joined me in the fray. Faugh-a-ballagh! Clear the way! for the rocky road to Dublin!” -D.K. Gavan, _Rocky Road to Dublin_. 19th Century.":"\"'好哇！兄弟们，'我说，我挥起我的橡木棍。 几个戈尔韦小子在旁边，他们看出我一瘸一拐； 然后随着一声响亮的'好哇！'他们加入了我的战斗。 Faugh-a-ballagh！让路！踏上通往都柏林的崎岖之路！\" ——D.K.加文，《通往都柏林的崎岖之路》。19世纪。","“You are the bows from which your children as living arrows are sent forth.” -Khalil Ghibran, _The Prophet_, “On Children”. 1923.":"\"你们是弓，你们的孩子是射出的活箭。\" ——哈利勒·纪伯伦，《先知》，\"论孩子\"。1923年。","“Who was the first that forged the deadly blade? Of rugged steel his savage soul was made” -Albius Tibullus, _Elegies_ I, xi. ca. 25 B.C. trans. James Grainger, 1822.":"\"是谁最先铸造了那致命的利刃？ 他的野蛮灵魂必是粗砺钢铁铸成\" ——阿尔比乌斯·提布鲁斯，《哀歌》第一卷第十一首。约公元前25年。 詹姆斯·格兰杰英译，1822年。","“And David put his hand in his bag, and took thence a stone, and slang it, and smote the Philistine in his forehead, that the stone sunk into his forehead; and he fell upon his face to the earth.” -KJV Bible, 1 Samuel 17:49.":"\"大卫伸手进他的囊中，掏出一块石子，用机弦甩去，打中非利士人的前额，石子陷入额内，他就仆倒，面伏于地。\" ——圣经和合本，《撒母耳记上》17:49。","“Thrice whirling round his head The whistling thong, Mezentius took his aim. Clean through his temples hissed the molten lead, And prostrate in the dust, the gallant youth lay dead.” -Virgil, Aeneid 9 trans. E. Fairfax Taylor":"\"三次在头顶旋转 那呼啸的皮条，墨曾提乌斯瞄准了目标。 熔化的铅弹嘶嘶穿过他的太阳穴， 那英勇的少年倒在尘土中，死了。\" ——维吉尔，《埃涅阿斯纪》第九卷。 E.费尔法克斯·泰勒英译。","“Or burst the vanish’d Hero’s lofty mound; Far on the solitary shore he sleeps: He fell, and falling nations mourn’d around; But now not one of saddening thousands weeps, Nor warlike worshipper his vigil keeps Where demi-gods appear’d, as records tell. Remove yon skull from out the scatter’d heaps: Is that a temple where a God may dwell? Why ev’n the worm at last disdains her shatter’d cell!":"\"或炸开那消逝英雄的高耸坟丘； 在那遥远的孤寂海岸上他安眠着： 他倒下了，倒下时万民哀悼； 但如今，千千万万悲恸者中无人哭泣， 也无人如传说所载，为那显圣的 半神守夜。从那散乱的骸骨堆中 移开那颗颅骨：那便是 神灵曾居的庙堂吗？ 为何连蛆虫最终都鄙弃这破碎的居所！","Look on its broken arch, its ruin’d wall, Its chambers desolate, and portals foul: Yes, this was once Ambition’s airy hall, The dome of Thought, the palace of the Soul: Behold through each lack-lustre, eyeless hole, The gay recess of Wisdom and of Wit And Passion’s host, that never brook’d control: Can all saint, sage, or sophist ever writ, People this lonely tower, this tenement refit?” -Lord Byron, _Childe Harold's Pilgrimage_, Canto the Second, Stanzas V-VI":"看那断裂的拱门，那残破的墙壁， 那荒废的厅堂，那污秽的门廊： 是的，这曾是野心的空中殿堂， 思想的穹顶，灵魂的宫殿： 透过每一对暗淡无光的空洞眼窝， 看那智慧与才思的欢快密室， 与那从不甘受控制的激情之群： 一切圣贤哲人术士写就的篇章， 可能住满这孤寂的高塔，修缮这座寓所？\" ——拜伦勋爵，《恰尔德·哈罗德游记》，第二歌，第五节至第六节。","“Or burst the vanish’d Hero’s lofty mound; Far on the solitary shore he sleeps: He fell, and falling nations mourn’d around; But now not one of saddening thousands weeps, Nor warlike worshipper his vigil keeps Where demi-gods appear’d, as records tell. Remove yon skull from out the scatter’d heaps: Is that a temple where a God may dwell? Why ev’n the worm at last disdains her shatter’d cell! Look on its broken arch, its ruin’d wall, Its chambers desolate, and portals foul: Yes, this was once Ambition’s airy hall, The dome of Thought, the palace of the Soul: Behold through each lack-lustre, eyeless hole, The gay recess of Wisdom and of Wit And Passion’s host, that never brook’d control: Can all saint, sage, or sophist ever writ, People this lonely tower, this tenement refit?” -Lord Byron, _Childe Harold's Pilgrimage_, Canto the Second, Stanzas V-VI":"\"或炸开那消逝英雄的高耸坟丘； 在那遥远的孤寂海岸上他安眠着： 他倒下了，倒下时万民哀悼； 但如今，千千万万悲恸者中无人哭泣， 也无人如传说所载，为那显圣的 半神守夜。从那散乱的骸骨堆中 移开那颗颅骨：那便是 神灵曾居的庙堂吗？ 为何连蛆虫最终都鄙弃这破碎的居所！ 看那断裂的拱门，那残破的墙壁， 那荒废的厅堂，那污秽的门廊： 是的，这曾是野心的空中殿堂， 思想的穹顶，灵魂的宫殿： 透过每一对暗淡无光的空洞眼窝， 看那智慧与才思的欢快密室， 与那从不甘受控制的激情之群： 一切圣贤哲人术士写就的篇章， 可能住满这孤寂的高塔，修缮这座寓所？\" ——拜伦勋爵，《恰尔德·哈罗德游记》，第二歌，第五节至第六节。","“The halberd is inferior to the spear on the battlefield. With the spear you can take the initiative; the halberd is defensive. In the hands of one of two men of equal ability, the spear gives a little extra strength.” -Miyamoto Musashi, _The Book of Five Rings_. 1645.":"\"战场上戟不如矛。用矛你可以掌握主动；戟则是防御性的。在两名能力相当的人手中，矛能给出一丝额外的力量。\" ——宫本武藏，《五轮书》。1645年。","“Bashō Osho said to his disciples, ‘If you have a staff, I will give you a staff. If you have no staff, I will take it from you.’":"\"芭蕉和尚示众云：'你有拄杖子，我与你拄杖子；你无拄杖子，我夺你拄杖子。'","Mumon's Comment":"无门评曰：","It helps me wade across a river when the bridge is down. It accompanies me to the village on a moonless night. If you call it a staff, you will enter hell like an arrow.” -Mumon Ekai, _The Gateless Gate_, case 44. 1228. trans. Katsuki Sekida":"扶过断桥水，伴归无月村。若唤作拄杖，入地狱如箭。\" ——无门慧开，《无门关》，第四十四则。1228年。 关毅峰英译。","“Bashō Osho said to his disciples, ‘If you have a staff, I will give you a staff. If you have no staff, I will take it from you.’ Mumon's Comment It helps me wade across a river when the bridge is down. It accompanies me to the village on a moonless night. If you call it a staff, you will enter hell like an arrow.” -Mumon Ekai, _The Gateless Gate_, case 44. 1228. trans. Katsuki Sekida":"\"芭蕉和尚示众云：'你有拄杖子，我与你拄杖子；你无拄杖子，我夺你拄杖子。' 无门评曰： 扶过断桥水，伴归无月村。若唤作拄杖，入地狱如箭。\" ——无门慧开，《无门关》，第四十四则。1228年。 关毅峰英译。","<staff>":"<staff>","“'I am Aed Abaid of Ess Rúaid, that is, the good god of wizardry of the Tuatha Dé Danann, and the Rúad Rofhessa, and Eochaid Ollathair are my three names.’":"\"'我是埃斯鲁艾德的埃德·阿拜德，即达努神族的善巫术之神，我又名鲁阿德·罗费萨和埃奥凯德·奥拉泰尔，这是我的三个名字。'","And thus he was, with Cermait Milbél, one of his sons, on his back, who had fallen in fight and combat by Lug, son of Cian, High King of Ireland. The Dagda betook himself to his knowledge and learning, and therefore frankincense and myrrh and herbs were put around the body of Cermait, and he lifted Cermait on his back, and bearing Cermait he searched the world, and came to the great eastern world.":"他如此自报，背上背着他在与爱尔兰至尊王、基安之子卢格的战斗与格斗中倒下的儿子之一，克尔迈特·米尔贝尔。达格达求助于他的知识与学问，于是在克尔迈特的遗体周围放上了乳香、没药和药草，然后他背起克尔迈特，扛着他周游世界，来到了大东方世界。","He met three men going the road and the way with their father's treasures. The Dagda asked news of them, and they said ‘We are three sons of one father and mother, and we are sharing our father's treasures.’ ‘What have ye?’ said the Dagda. ‘A shirt and a staff and a cloak,’ said they. ‘What virtues have these?’ said the Dagda. ‘This great staff that thou seest,’ said he, ‘has a smooth end and a rough end. One end slays the living, and the other end brings the dead to life.’” -Osborn Bergin, “How the Dagda Got His Magic Staff”, _Medieval Studies in Memory of Gertrude Schoepperle Loomis_. 1927.":"他遇到三个正带着父亲财宝赶路的男子。达格达向他们打听消息，他们说：'我们是同父同母的三兄弟，正在分配父亲的财宝。' '你们有什么？'达格达问。 '一件衬衣、一根杖和一件斗篷，'他们说。 '这些东西有什么功效？'达格达问。 '你看到的这根大杖，'他说，'有一端光滑，一端粗糙。一端杀生，另一端使死者复生。'\" ——奥斯本·伯金，\"达格达如何获得他的魔法杖\"，《纪念格特鲁德·舍珀尔·卢米斯的中世纪研究》。1927年。","“'I am Aed Abaid of Ess Rúaid, that is, the good god of wizardry of the Tuatha Dé Danann, and the Rúad Rofhessa, and Eochaid Ollathair are my three names.’ And thus he was, with Cermait Milbél, one of his sons, on his back, who had fallen in fight and combat by Lug, son of Cian, High King of Ireland. The Dagda betook himself to his knowledge and learning, and therefore frankincense and myrrh and herbs were put around the body of Cermait, and he lifted Cermait on his back, and bearing Cermait he searched the world, and came to the great eastern world. He met three men going the road and the way with their father's treasures. The Dagda asked news of them, and they said ‘We are three sons of one father and mother, and we are sharing our father's treasures.’ ‘What have ye?’ said the Dagda. ‘A shirt and a staff and a cloak,’ said they. ‘What virtues have these?’ said the Dagda. ‘This great staff that thou seest,’ said he, ‘has a smooth end and a rough end. One end slays the living, and the other end brings the dead to life.’” -Osborn Bergin, “How the Dagda Got His Magic Staff”, _Medieval Studies in Memory of Gertrude Schoepperle Loomis_. 1927.":"\"'我是埃斯鲁艾德的埃德·阿拜德，即达努神族的善巫术之神，我又名鲁阿德·罗费萨和埃奥凯德·奥拉泰尔，这是我的三个名字。' 他如此自报，背上背着他在与爱尔兰至尊王、基安之子卢格的战斗与格斗中倒下的儿子之一，克尔迈特·米尔贝尔。达格达求助于他的知识与学问，于是在克尔迈特的遗体周围放上了乳香、没药和药草，然后他背起克尔迈特，扛着他周游世界，来到了大东方世界。 他遇到三个正带着父亲财宝赶路的男子。达格达向他们打听消息，他们说：'我们是同父同母的三兄弟，正在分配父亲的财宝。' '你们有什么？'达格达问。 '一件衬衣、一根杖和一件斗篷，'他们说。 '这些东西有什么功效？'达格达问。 '你看到的这根大杖，'他说，'有一端光滑，一端粗糙。一端杀生，另一端使死者复生。'\" ——奥斯本·伯金，\"达格达如何获得他的魔法杖\"，《纪念格特鲁德·舍珀尔·卢米斯的中世纪研究》。1927年。","“The wizard suddenly remembered the words of the god. He remembered that of all the creatures that people the earth, Fire was the only one who knew his son to be a phantom. This memory, which at first calmed him, ended by tormenting him. He feared lest his son should meditate on this abnormal privilege and by some means find out he was a mere simulacrum. Not to be a man, to be a projection of another man's dreams—what an incomparable humiliation, what madness!” -Jorge Luis Borges, _The Circular Ruins_. 1940. trans. Anthony Bonner, 1962.":"\"巫师忽然想起了神明的话。他想起，在遍布大地的万物之中，唯有火知道他的儿子不过是一个幻影。这记忆起初使他平静，最后却折磨着他。他担心他的儿子会思索这反常的特权，并以某种方式发现自己仅是一个仿像。不是一个人，只是另一个人梦境的投射——这是何等无法比拟的屈辱，何等疯狂！\" ——豪尔赫·路易斯·博尔赫斯，《环形废墟》。1940年。 安东尼·邦纳英译，1962年。","“His scales are his pride, shut up together as with a close seal. One is so near to another, that no air can come between them. They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.” -KJV Bible, Job 41:15-17.":"\"它以骄傲的鳞甲为甲胄，紧紧闭合，如严密封印。鳞片片片相连，连空气也无法透入其间。它们彼此联结，互相胶结，不能分离。\" ——圣经和合本，《约伯记》41:15-17。","“How happy is the little Stone That rambles in the Road alone, And doesn't care about Careers And Exigencies never fears — Whose Coat of elemental Brown A passing Universe put on, And independent as the Sun Associates or glows alone, Fulfilling absolute Decree In casual simplicity —” -Emily Dickinson, “How happy is the little Stone”. ca. 1865.":"\"那小石子多么快乐 独自在路上漫步徜徉， 不在乎什么前程事业 也不畏惧什么急难困厄—— 披着质朴的棕色外套 那外套是路过的宇宙所披上， 像太阳一样独立不倚 或与万物为伴，或独自发光， 以漫不经心的淳朴 践行着绝对的谕旨——\" ——艾米莉·狄金森，\"那小石子多么快乐\"。约1865年。","“Stormform is said to cause A tempest of winds and showers, Beware its powers, beware its powers. Though its coming brings the gods their night, It obliges a bloodred spren. Beware its end, beware its end.” -Brandon Sanderson, “Words of Radiance”. 2014.":"\"据说风暴形态会带来 风雨交加的暴烈， 当心它的力量，当心它的力量。 虽然它的到来为诸神带来黑夜， 它却召唤出血红的灵。 当心它的结局，当心它的结局。\" ——布兰登·桑德森，《光辉之语》。2014年。","“Don’t sing if you want to live long They have no use for your song You’re dead, you’re dead, you’re dead You’re dead and outta this world":"\"想活得长久就别唱歌 他们不需要你的歌 你死了，你死了，你死了 你死了，已离开这个世界","You’ll never get a second chance Plan all your moves in advance Stay dead, stay dead, stay dead Stay dead and outta this world” -Norma Tanega, “You’re Dead”. 1966":"你永远不会有第二次机会 提前规划好你所有的举动 保持死亡，保持死亡，保持死亡 保持死亡，离开这个世界\" ——诺玛·塔内加，\"你死了\"。1966年。","“Don’t sing if you want to live long They have no use for your song You’re dead, you’re dead, you’re dead You’re dead and outta this world You’ll never get a second chance Plan all your moves in advance Stay dead, stay dead, stay dead Stay dead and outta this world” -Norma Tanega, “You’re Dead”. 1966":"\"想活得长久就别唱歌 他们不需要你的歌 你死了，你死了，你死了 你死了，已离开这个世界 你永远不会有第二次机会 提前规划好你所有的举动 保持死亡，保持死亡，保持死亡 保持死亡，离开这个世界\" ——诺玛·塔内加，\"你死了\"。1966年。","“The look of a scared thing Sitting in a net!” -Edna St. Vincent Millay, “When the Year Grows Old”. 1917.":"\"一张受惊之物 困在网中的神情！\" ——埃德娜·圣文森特·米莱，\"当年岁渐老\"。1917年。","“Don't try to rise above it, it's better below When life is going by you, you'll never know When everything is simple, it's really sublime Don't try to rise above it, below it is fine” -Daryl Hall & John Oates, “No Brain, No Pain”. 1979.":"\"不要试图超越它，下面更好 当生活从你身边流逝，你永远不会知道 当一切都很简单时，真是美妙至极 不要试图超越它，下面就很好\" ——达里尔·霍尔与约翰·奥茨，\"没有脑子，没有痛苦\"。1979年。","“Without noticing the occupations of an intervening day or two, which, as they consisted of the ordinary sylvan amusements of shooting and coursing, have nothing sufficiently interesting to detain the reader, we pass to one in some degree peculiar to Scotland, which may be called a sort of salmon-hunting. This chase, in which the fish is pursued and struck with barbed spears, or a sort of long shafted trident, called a waster, is much practised at the mouth of the Esk, and in the other salmon rivers of Scotland.” -Sir Walter Scott, _Guy Mannering_, ch. XXVI. 1815.":"\"其间一两日的活动无需赘述，因为它们不过是一些寻常的林间娱乐，如射猎与追猎之类，并无足够有趣之事以留住读者，我们便直接跳到一种在某种程度上为苏格兰所特有的活动，可称之为一种猎鲑。这种追逐，用带倒刺的长矛或一种名为'沃斯特'的长柄三叉戟来追捕和刺击鱼类，在埃斯克河口及苏格兰其他鲑鱼河流中极为盛行。\" ——沃尔特·司各特爵士，《盖伊·曼纳林》，第二十六章。1815年。","“Energy may be likened to the bending of a crossbow; decision, to the releasing of a trigger.” -Sun Tzu":"\"势如彍弩，节如发机。\" ——孙子。","“THE TROLL KING: Now, listen, Prince Peer, and give way to reason! You're cut out for a Troll. Why, look, already You bear yourself quite in a Troll-like fashion! And you want to become one, don't you? PEER GYNT: Of course. In return for a bride and a well-found kingdom I'm not unwilling to sacrifice something; But all things have their natural limit. I have taken a tail, it is true; but, then, I can undo the knots that our friend has tied And take the thing off. I have shed my breeches; They were old and patched; but that won't prevent me From putting them on if I have a mind to. I shall probably find it just as easy To deal with your Trollish way of living. I can easily swear that a cow's a maiden; An oath's not a difficult thing to swallow. But to know that one never can get one's freedom — Not even to die as a human being — To end one's days as a Troll of the mountains — Never go back, as you tell me plainly — That is a thing that I'll not submit to.” -Henrik Ibsen, _Peer Gynt_ . 1867.":"\"巨魔王：听着，皮尔王子，听从理性吧！ 你天生就是当巨魔的料。你看，你早已 摆出一副十足的巨魔作风了！ 而你也想变成巨魔，不是吗？ 皮尔·金特：当然。 换一个新娘和一个殷实的王国 我不介意牺牲点什么； 但万事都有其自然限度。 我确实装了条尾巴；可是， 我可以解开我们朋友系上的结 把它取下来。我脱掉了马裤； 它们又旧又破；但这不妨碍我 想穿的时候就穿上。 我大概会发现，适应 你们巨魔的生活方式也一样容易。 我可以轻易发誓说母牛是少女； 誓言不是什么难以下咽的东西。 但知道自己永远无法重获自由—— 连作为人死去都不行—— 作为山中巨魔了此一生—— 永远回不去，正如你明白告诉我的—— 那是我绝不会屈从的事。\" ——亨利克·易卜生，《培尔·金特》。1867年。","“[The principle of selection] is the magician's wand, by means of which he may summon into life whatever form and mould he pleases.” -William Youatt, _Sheep: their breeds, management, and diseases; to which is added the Mountain Shepherd's Manual_, ch. III. 1837.":"\"[选择的原则]是魔术师的法杖，凭借它，他可以从虚空中召唤出任何他喜爱的形态和模样。\" ——威廉·尤厄特，《绵羊：品种、管理与疾病；附山区牧羊人手册》，第三章。1837年。","<wand>":"<wand>","“But it isn't charm as veneer, as facilitating ooze or unguent, but charm that identifies and goes out to meet itself in others wherever it may be met with.” -Michael Hofmann, “Hell, he'll be frozen stiff!”, London Review of Books, 2022.":"\"但这不是作为装饰贴面的魅力，不是作为润滑剂或软膏的魅力， 而是那种辨识出自己、并在任何遇见之处走出去迎接 他人身上那个自己的魅力。\" ——迈克尔·霍夫曼，\"天啊，他会冻僵的！\"，《伦敦书评》，2022年。","“But it isn't charm as veneer, as facilitating ooze or unguent, but charm that identifies and goes out to meet itself in others wherever it may be met with.” -Michael Hofmann, “Hell, he'll be frozen stiff!”, London Review of Books, 2022. “He held up his hand, and they all stopped, and I thought he seemed to be saying, ‘All these lives will I give you, ay, and many more and greater, through countless ages, if you will fall down and worship me!’ And then a red cloud, like the colour of blood, seemed to close over my eyes, and before I knew what I was doing, I found myself opening the sash and saying to Him, ‘Come in, Lord and Master!’” -Bram Stoker, _Dracula_. 1897.":"\"但这不是作为装饰贴面的魅力，不是作为润滑剂或软膏的魅力， 而是那种辨识出自己、并在任何遇见之处走出去迎接 他人身上那个自己的魅力。\" ——迈克尔·霍夫曼，\"天啊，他会冻僵的！\"，《伦敦书评》，2022年。 \"他举起手，他们都停了下来，我觉得他似乎是在说：'所有这些生命我都要给你，是的，还有更多更伟大的生命，跨越无数世代，只要你肯俯伏敬拜我！'然后一团红色的云，如血的颜色，似乎笼罩了我的眼睛，在我还没意识到自己在做什么的时候，我发现自己已经打开了窗扇，对他说：'进来吧，主与主人！'\" ——布拉姆·斯托克，《德古拉》。1897年。","“Great holes secretly are digged where earth’s pores ought to suffice, and things have learnt to walk that ought to crawl.” -H.P. Lovecraft, “The Festival”. 1925":"\"大地毛孔本应足够之处，秘密地掘出了巨大的洞穴，本应爬行的东西学会了行走。\" ——H.P.洛夫克拉夫特，\"节日\"。1925年。","“Als Gregor Samsa eines Morgens aus unruhigen Träumen erwachte, fand er sich in seinem Bett zu einem ungeheueren Ungeziefer verwandelt.” -Franz Kafka, _Die Verwandlung_. 1915":"\"Als Gregor Samsa eines Morgens aus unruhigen Träumen erwachte, fand er sich in seinem Bett zu einem ungeheueren Ungeziefer verwandelt.\" 一天早晨，格里高尔·萨姆沙从不安的睡梦中醒来，发现自己躺在床上变成了一只巨大的甲虫。 ——弗朗茨·卡夫卡，《变形记》。1915年。","“‘God speed the kiss,’ said Max, and Katie sigh'd, With pray'rful palms close seal'd, ‘God speed the axe!’” -Isabella Valancey Crawford, “Malcolm's Katie: A Love Story”, Part I, _Old Spookses' Pass, Malcolm's Katie and Other Poems_. 1884.":"\"'愿上帝助这一吻成真，'马克斯说，凯蒂叹息着， 双手紧合如祈祷的封缄，'愿上帝助这一斧成功！'\" ——伊莎贝拉·瓦朗西·克劳福德，\"马尔科姆的凯蒂：一个爱情故事\"，第一部分，《老斯普克斯关口、马尔科姆的凯蒂及其他诗篇》。1884年。","“Not with a Club, the Heart is broken Nor with a Stone — A Whip so small you could not see it I've known To lash the Magic Creature Till it fell, Yet that Whip's Name Too noble then to tell.” -Emily Dickinson, “Not with a Club, the Heart is broken”. ca. 1865.":"\"心碎，不靠棍棒 也不靠石头—— 我曾知道一条小得 看不见的鞭子 抽打着那神奇的造物 直到它倒下， 然而那鞭子的名 太过高贵，不该说出。\" ——艾米莉·狄金森，\"心碎，不靠棍棒\"。约1865年。","Wasn't it beautiful running wild 'til you fell asleep Before the monsters caught up to you? -Taylor Swift, _Innocent_, 2010.":"\"难道不美吗——肆意奔跑，直到沉入梦乡， 在怪物追上来之前？\" -Taylor Swift, _Innocent_, 2010.","“The fact is that I am unique. What a man can pass unto others does not interest me; like the philosopher, I think nothing is communicated by the art of writing. Annoying and trivial minutiae have no place in my spirit, a spirit which is receptive only to whatsoever is grand.” -Jorge Luis Borges, “The House of Asterion”. 1947. trans. Antonios Sarhanis, 2008.":"\"事实是，我是独一无二的。一个人能传递给别人的东西，我毫无兴趣；如同那位哲人，我认为书写这种技艺无法传达任何东西。恼人而琐碎的细枝末节在我的精神中没有立足之地——这精神只接纳一切宏大的事物。\" -Jorge Luis Borges, \"阿斯忒里翁之家\". 1947. trans. Antonios Sarhanis, 2008.","“That country was then ruled by Antaeus, son of Poseidon, who used to kill strangers by forcing them to wrestle. Being forced to wrestle with him, Hercules hugged him, lifted him aloft, broke and killed him; for when he touched earth so it was that he waxed stronger, wherefore some said that he was a son of Earth.” -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 2.5.11. ca. 150 BC. trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913.":"\"那时统治那地方的是安泰俄斯，波塞冬之子。他惯于强迫陌生人与其角力，然后将他们杀死。赫拉克勒斯被迫与他角力，将他紧紧抱住，举到空中，折断了他的身体并将他杀死；因为安泰俄斯每当触及大地就会变得更强，因此有人说他是大地之子。\" -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 2.5.11. ca. 150 BC. trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913.","“The head foreman in the mine, called Antaeus, was an obese giant with a thick black beard who actually seemed to draw his strength from Mother Earth.” -Primo Levi, “The Periodic Table”. 1975.":"\"矿场里的工头，人称安泰俄斯， 是个肥胖的巨人，留着浓密的黑胡子， 他似乎真的从大地母亲那里汲取力量。\" -Primo Levi, \"The Periodic Table\". 1975.","“That country was then ruled by Antaeus, son of Poseidon, who used to kill strangers by forcing them to wrestle. Being forced to wrestle with him, Hercules hugged him, lifted him aloft, broke and killed him; for when he touched earth so it was that he waxed stronger, wherefore some said that he was a son of Earth.” -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 2.5.11. ca. 150 BC. trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913. “The head foreman in the mine, called Antaeus, was an obese giant with a thick black beard who actually seemed to draw his strength from Mother Earth.” -Primo Levi, “The Periodic Table”. 1975.":"\"那时统治那地方的是安泰俄斯，波塞冬之子。他惯于强迫陌生人与其角力，然后将他们杀死。赫拉克勒斯被迫与他角力，将他紧紧抱住，举到空中，折断了他的身体并将他杀死；因为安泰俄斯每当触及大地就会变得更强，因此有人说他是大地之子。\" -Pseudo-Apollodorus , _Library and Epitome_, 2.5.11. ca. 150 BC. trans. Sir James George Frazer, 1913. \"矿场里的工头，人称安泰俄斯， 是个肥胖的巨人，留着浓密的黑胡子， 他似乎真的从大地母亲那里汲取力量。\" -Primo Levi, \"The Periodic Table\". 1975.","“For myself, I have other occupations: I make absurd matches; I marry greybeards with minors, masters with servants, girls with small fortunes with tender lovers who have none. It is I who introduced into this world luxury, debauchery, games of chance, and chemistry. I am the author of the first cookery book, the inventor of festivals, of dancing, music, plays, and of the newest fashions; in a word, I am ASMODEUS, surnamed The Devil on Two Sticks.” -Alain René Le Sage, _Asmodeus: Or, The Devil on Two Sticks_. 1707.":"\"至于我自己，我另有营生：我撮合荒唐的婚姻；我让白发老翁娶少女，让主人娶仆役，让略有薄产的姑娘嫁给身无分文的多情郎。是我将奢侈、放荡、赌博和化学引入这个世界。我是第一本烹饪书的作者，是节庆、舞蹈、音乐、戏剧和最新时尚的发明者；总而言之，我就是阿斯摩蒂斯，绰号'双拐魔鬼'。\" -Alain René Le Sage, _Asmodeus: Or, The Devil on Two Sticks_. 1707.","“And Allah said, ‘As thou the deed hast done, so now the office shall be thine, O Azrael, to gather up for me the souls of men and women when their time has come; the souls of saints and sinners, of beggars and of princes, of the old or young, whate'er befall; and even though friends weep, and hearts of loved ones ache with sorrow and with anguish, when bereft of those they love.’ So Azrael became the messenger of Death.” -J. E. Hanauer, _Folk-lore of the Holy Land, Moslem, Christian and Jewish_. 1907.":"\"真主说， '既然你已行此事，如今这职分便归于你，阿兹瑞尔啊， 当时辰到来时，为我去收集世人的灵魂； 圣徒与罪人的灵魂，乞丐与王侯的灵魂， 老者与青年的灵魂，无论发生什么； 即便友人为之哭泣， 所爱之人因失去至亲而心碎，悲痛难抑。' 于是阿兹瑞尔成了死亡的信使。\" -J. E. Hanauer, _Folk-lore of the Holy Land, Moslem, Christian and Jewish_. 1907.","“There was an Old Man with a beard, Who said, ‘It is just as I feared! Two Owls and a Hen, Four Larks and a Wren, Have all built their nests in my beard!’” -Edward Lear, _A Book of Nonsense [No. 1]_. 1846.":"\"从前有个长须老翁， 他说：'果然不出我所料！ 两只猫头鹰加一只母鸡， 四只云雀和一只鹪鹩， 全在我的胡子里筑了巢！'\" -Edward Lear, _A Book of Nonsense [No. 1]_. 1846.","“Hoc idem magis ostendit antiquius Iovis nomen: nam olim Diovis et Diespiter dictus, id est dies pater; a quo dei dicti qui inde, et dius et divum, unde sub divo, Dius Fidius. Itaque inde eius perforatum tectum, ut ea videatur divum, id est caelum. Quidam negant sub tecto per hunc deierare oportere. Aelius Dium Fidium dicebat Diovis filium, ut Graeci Dioskopon Castorem, et putabat hunc esse Sancum ab Sabina lingua et Herculem a Graeca. Idem hic Dis pater dicitur infimus, qui est coniunctus terrae, ubi omnia ut oriuntur ita aboriuntur; quorum quod finis ortuum, Orcus dictus.” -Marcus Terentius Varro, _De Lingua Latina_, Liber V, circa 40 BC.":"\"这同一件事，朱庇特更古老的名称更能说明：因为最初他被称为迪奥维斯和迪耶斯匹特，也就是'日父'；由此衍生出'神'（dei）一词，以及'dius'和'divum'，由此有'sub divo'（在天空下）和狄乌斯·菲狄乌斯。因此他的庙宇屋顶开有天窗，以便从中望见天穹（divum），也就是天空。有人认为不应在有屋顶的地方向此神发誓。埃利乌斯说狄乌斯·菲狄乌斯是迪奥维斯之子，正如希腊人称卡斯托尔为狄奥斯库波；他还认为此神就是萨宾语中的桑库斯，希腊语中的赫拉克勒斯。同样，这位迪斯帕特被称为最低者，他与大地相连，万物在那里诞生又消亡；事物消亡的终点，被称为奥库斯。\" -Marcus Terentius Varro, _De Lingua Latina_, Liber V, circa 40 BC.","“Skill and grace, the twin brother and sister, are dancing playfully on your finger tips.” -Rabindranath Tagore, _Chitra_, Act I, Scene iv. 1914.":"\"技艺与优雅，这对孪生兄妹，正在你的指尖上欢快地舞蹈。\" -Rabindranath Tagore, _Chitra_, Act I, Scene iv. 1914.","“Twin children: the Girl, she was plain; The Brother was handsome & vain; ‘Let him brag of his looks,’ Father said; ‘mind your books! The best beauty is bred in the brain.’” -Aesop & Walter Crane, _The Baby's Own Aesop_, 36: “Brother & Sister”. 1887.":"\"一对孪生子：女孩相貌平平； 哥哥生得俊美又虚荣； 父亲说：'让他去夸耀他的容貌， 你只管专心读书！ 最美的美貌孕育在头脑之中。'\" -Aesop & Walter Crane, _The Baby's Own Aesop_, 36: \"Brother & Sister\". 1887.","“And my invention thrive, Edmund the base Shall top the legitimate. I grow; I prosper.— Now, gods, stand up for bastards!” -William Shakespeare, _King Lear_, I, ii. 1606.":"\"既然我的计谋得逞，庶子埃德蒙 必将凌驾嫡出之上。我蒸蒸日上，步步高升—— 如今，众神啊，为私生子撑腰吧！\" -William Shakespeare, _King Lear_, I, ii. 1606.","“When the forces stood in array Edmund proposed to decide their claims by single combat; but Canute saying that he, a man of small stature, would have little chance against the tall athletic Edmund, proposed, on the contrary, for them to divide the realm as their fathers had done.” -Thomas Keightley, _The History of England_. 1839.":"\"当两军列阵之际，埃德蒙提议以单挑决胜负；但克努特说，他身材矮小，与高大健壮的埃德蒙决斗，毫无胜算，于是反过来提议，不如像他们的父辈那样平分王国。\" -Thomas Keightley, _The History of England_. 1839.","“And my invention thrive, Edmund the base Shall top the legitimate. I grow; I prosper.— Now, gods, stand up for bastards!” -William Shakespeare, _King Lear_, I, ii. 1606. “When the forces stood in array Edmund proposed to decide their claims by single combat; but Canute saying that he, a man of small stature, would have little chance against the tall athletic Edmund, proposed, on the contrary, for them to divide the realm as their fathers had done.” -Thomas Keightley, _The History of England_. 1839.":"\"既然我的计谋得逞，庶子埃德蒙 必将凌驾嫡出之上。我蒸蒸日上，步步高升—— 如今，众神啊，为私生子撑腰吧！\" -William Shakespeare, _King Lear_, I, ii. 1606. \"当两军列阵之际，埃德蒙提议以单挑决胜负；但克努特说，他身材矮小，与高大健壮的埃德蒙决斗，毫无胜算，于是反过来提议，不如像他们的父辈那样平分王国。\" -Thomas Keightley, _The History of England_. 1839.","“I thoroughly disapprove of duels. I consider them unwise and I know they are dangerous. Also, sinful. If a man should challenge me, I would take him kindly and forgivingly by the hand and lead him to a quiet retired spot and kill him.” -Mark Twain, _Autobiography of Mark Twain_. 1924.":"\"我坚决反对决斗。我认为这既不明智，又很危险。而且，还有罪。如果有人向我挑战，我会友善而宽容地握住他的手，带他到一个安静隐蔽的地方，然后杀了他。\" -Mark Twain, _Autobiography of Mark Twain_. 1924.","“Khrysaor, married to Kallirhoe, daughter of glorious Okeanos, was father to the triple-headed Geryon, but Geryon was killed by the great strength of Herakles at sea-circled Erytheis beside his own shambling cattle on that day when Herakles drove those broad-faced cattle toward holy Tiryns, when he crossed the stream of Okeanos and had killed Orthos and the oxherd Eurytion out in the gloomy meadow beyond fabulous Okeanos.” -Hesiod, _Theogony_, circa 700 BCE.":"\"克律萨俄耳娶了光荣的俄刻阿诺斯之女卡利洛厄，生下了三首的格律翁。但格律翁被赫拉克勒斯以巨大的力量杀死在海环绕的厄律忒亚岛，就在他自己的蹒跚牛群旁。那一天，赫拉克勒斯驱赶着那些宽额的牛群前往神圣的梯林斯，渡过了俄刻阿诺斯的洪流，并在传说中俄刻阿诺斯彼岸那幽暗的草原上杀了奥尔索斯和牧牛人欧律提翁。\" -Hesiod, _Theogony_, circa 700 BCE.","“One, you lock the target Two, you bait the line Three, you slowly spread the net And four, you catch the man":"\"一，你锁定目标 二，你布下诱饵 三，你慢慢撒开网 四，你抓住了那个人","You catch the man You catch the man I’m looking for this man to sell him to other men To sell him to other men at ten times the price at least” —Front 242, “Headhunter”":"你抓住了那个人 你抓住了那个人 我要找到这个人，把他卖给别的人 把他卖给别的人，至少十倍的价钱\" -Front 242, \"Headhunter\"","“One, you lock the target Two, you bait the line Three, you slowly spread the net And four, you catch the man You catch the man You catch the man I’m looking for this man to sell him to other men To sell him to other men at ten times the price at least” —Front 242, “Headhunter”":"\"一，你锁定目标 二，你布下诱饵 三，你慢慢撒开网 四，你抓住了那个人 你抓住了那个人 你抓住了那个人 我要找到这个人，把他卖给别的人 把他卖给别的人，至少十倍的价钱\" -Front 242, \"Headhunter\"","“We have lingered in the chambers of the sea By sea-girls wreathed with seaweed red and brown Till human voices wake us, and we drown.” -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. lines 129-131. 1915.":"\"我们在大海的厅堂里徘徊流连， 有海之少女编着红褐海藻的花环， 直到人声将我们唤醒，我们便溺死。\" -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. lines 129-131. 1915.","“And then I looked farther, beyond the pallid line of the sands, and I saw a Pyramid of gold, the wonder Khufu had built. As a golden wonder it saluted me, as a golden thing it greeted me, as a golden miracle I shall remember it.” -Robert Hichens, _The Spell of Egypt_. 1910.":"\"然后我望向更远处，越过沙丘苍白的轮廓，我看见了一座黄金金字塔，那是胡夫建造的奇迹。它如金色的奇观向我致敬，如金色的造物向我致意，如金色的神迹，我将永远铭记。\" -Robert Hichens, _The Spell of Egypt_. 1910.","“Lo, thy comrades yonder in the house of Kirke are penned like swine in close-barred sties. And art thou come to release them? Nay, I tell thee, thou shalt not thyself return, but shalt remain there with the others.” -Homer, Odysseia":"\"看哪，你那些同伴正在喀耳刻的宅邸里，像猪一样被关在栅栏紧密的圈中。你是来解救他们的吗？不，我告诉你，你自己也不能回去，反倒得留在那里，与他们为伍。\" -Homer, Odysseia","“The second Labour which he undertook was the slaying of the Lernaian Hydra, springing from whose single body were fashioned a hundred necks, each bearing the head of a serpent. And when one head was cut off, the place where it was severed put forth two others; for this reason it was considered to be invincible, and with good reason, since the part of it which was subdued sent forth a two-fold assistance in its place. Against a thing so difficult to manage as this Herakles devised an ingenious scheme and commanded Iolaos to sear with a burning brand the part which had been severed, in order to check the flow of the blood.” -Diodorus Siculus, _Bibliotheca Historica_. [4. 11. 5.]. c. 100.":"\"他承担的第二件功业是杀死勒尔奈亚的许德拉。从她那单一体躯中长出百条脖颈，每条颈上各生一颗蛇头。每当一颗头被砍下，断处便生出两颗来；因此这怪物被视为不可战胜——这并非没有道理，因为被制服的那一部分反而送来了双倍的助力。面对如此棘手之物，赫拉克勒斯想出了一个巧妙的计策，命令伊俄拉俄斯用燃烧的火把灼烧被砍断的部位，以阻止鲜血流淌。\" -Diodorus Siculus, _Bibliotheca Historica_. [4. 11. 5.]. c. 100.","“Cat: But who can say what a thing is worth. Girl: The free market, supposedly. Cat: What _price_ do we put on a _soul_? Girl: $7.25 an hour.” -Dorothy Gambrell, _Cat and Girl_, 2010.":"\"猫：但谁能说清一件东西的价值呢。 女孩：大概是自由市场吧。 猫：一颗_灵魂_标什么_价_？ 女孩：时薪七块两毛五。\" -Dorothy Gambrell, _Cat and Girl_, 2010.","“This night the Lord of Illusion passed among you, Mara, mighty among dreamers, mighty for ill. He did come upon another who may work with the stuff of dreams in a different way. He did meet with Dharma, who may expel a dreamer from his dream. They did struggle, and the Lord Mara is no more. Why did they struggle, deathgod against illusionist? You say their ways are incomprehensible, being the ways of gods. This is not the answer.” -Roger Zelazny, “Lord of Light”. 1967.":"\"今夜，幻象之主从你们中间经过，玛拉，梦者中的强者，为恶的强者。他遇到了另一个能以不同方式运用梦境之质的人。他与法相遇——法能将梦者逐出梦境。他们交战了，玛拉主已不复存在。他们为何交战，死神对幻术师？你说，他们的方式深不可测，因为那是神祇的方式。这不是答案。\" -Roger Zelazny, \"Lord of Light\". 1967.","“He who lives looking for pleasures only, his senses uncontrolled, immoderate in his food, idle, and weak, Mara will certainly overthrow him, as the wind throws down a weak tree.” -The Buddha, _Dhammapada_, 1:7. trans. F. Max Muller":"\"若人唯求欢愉， 放纵感官，饮食无度， 怠惰，懦弱，玛拉必将倾覆他， 正如狂风摧折弱树。\" -The Buddha, _Dhammapada_, 1:7. trans. F. Max Muller","“This night the Lord of Illusion passed among you, Mara, mighty among dreamers, mighty for ill. He did come upon another who may work with the stuff of dreams in a different way. He did meet with Dharma, who may expel a dreamer from his dream. They did struggle, and the Lord Mara is no more. Why did they struggle, deathgod against illusionist? You say their ways are incomprehensible, being the ways of gods. This is not the answer.” -Roger Zelazny, “Lord of Light”. 1967. “He who lives looking for pleasures only, his senses uncontrolled, immoderate in his food, idle, and weak, Mara will certainly overthrow him, as the wind throws down a weak tree.” -The Buddha, _Dhammapada_, 1:7. trans. F. Max Muller":"\"今夜，幻象之主从你们中间经过，玛拉，梦者中的强者，为恶的强者。他遇到了另一个能以不同方式运用梦境之质的人。他与法相遇——法能将梦者逐出梦境。他们交战了，玛拉主已不复存在。他们为何交战，死神对幻术师？你说，他们的方式深不可测，因为那是神祇的方式。这不是答案。\" -Roger Zelazny, \"Lord of Light\". 1967. \"若人唯求欢愉， 放纵感官，饮食无度， 怠惰，懦弱，玛拉必将倾覆他， 正如狂风摧折弱树。\" -The Buddha, _Dhammapada_, 1:7. trans. F. Max Muller","“‘Stop thief! Stop thief!’ There is a magic in the sound. The tradesman leaves his counter, and the car-man his waggon; the butcher throws down his tray; the baker his basket; the milkman his pail; the errand-boy his parcels; the school-boy his marbles; the paviour his pickaxe; the child his battledore. Away they run, pell-mell, helter-skelter, slap-dash: tearing, yelling, screaming, knocking down the passengers as they turn the corners, rousing up the dogs, and astonishing the fowls: and streets, squares, and courts, re-echo with the sound.” -Charles Dickens, _Oliver Twist_. 1838.":"\"'抓贼！抓贼！'这喊声中有一种魔力。店主离开柜台，车夫抛下货车；屠夫扔下托盘，面包师丢下篮子；送奶工撇下奶桶，跑腿的小厮丢开包裹；学童扔掉弹珠，铺路工抛开铁镐；孩子扔下球拍。他们一路狂奔，乱作一团，横冲直撞，跌跌撞撞：拉扯着，吼叫着，尖声喊叫着，拐弯时撞倒行人，惊起群狗，吓坏家禽：于是整条街、整个广场、整片院落，都回荡着这喊声。\" -Charles Dickens, _Oliver Twist_. 1838.","“Ye men of Egypt, ye have heard your king! I go, and I return not. But the will Of the great Gods is plain; and ye must bring Ill deeds, ill passions, zealous to fulfil Their pleasure, to their feet; and reap their praise, The praise of Gods, rich boon! and length of days.” -Matthew Arnold, _Mycerinus_":"\"埃及的子民啊，你们听到了君王的宣告！ 我将离去，不再归来。然而伟大诸神 的旨意已然分明；你们必须怀着 恶行、恶念，热切地奔赴 他们脚下，以遂其意；并收获他们的赞美， 诸神的赞美，丰厚的恩赐！以及长久的寿命。\" -Matthew Arnold, _Mycerinus_","“Look behind you! A three-headed monkey!” -Guybrush Threepwood, _The Secret of Monkey Island_":"\"看你的背后！一只三头猴子！\" -Guybrush Threepwood, _The Secret of Monkey Island_","“It dooth appéere that there is in Cats as in all other kindes of beasts, a certaine reason and language wherby they vnderstand one another. But as touching this Grimmalkin: I take rather to be an Hagat or a VVitch then a Cat. For witches haue gone often in that likenes, And therof hath come the prouerb as trew as common, that a Cat hath nine liues, that is to say, a witch may take on her a Cats body nine times.” -William Baldwin, “Beware the Cat”, 1584":"\"看来，猫与所有其他种类的走兽一样，确实有某种理性与语言，使它们能够彼此理解。但说到这只格里马尔金：我宁愿视其为巫婆或女巫，而非一只猫。因为女巫常常化作那副模样，由此便产生了那句既真实又普遍的谚语：猫有九条命。也就是说，一个女巫可以九次化为猫形。\" -William Baldwin, \"Beware the Cat\", 1584","“One can prophesy with a Daniel's confidence that skilled electricians will settle the battles of the near future.” -Nikola Tesla, “The Transmission of Electrical Energy Without Wires As a Means for Furthering Peace”, _Electrical World and Engineer_. January 7, 1905.":"\"我们可以用但以理般的信心预言，熟练的电学家将决定近未来的战争胜负。\" -尼古拉·特斯拉, \"The Transmission of Electrical Energy Without Wires As a Means for Furthering Peace\", _Electrical World and Engineer_. January 7, 1905.","“Death and death alone gives meaning to life and this meaning is entirely negative.” -Georges Poulet":"\"死亡，唯有死亡赋予生命以意义，而这意义完全是负面的。\" -Georges Poulet","“What are you going to do with that big bat? Gonna hit me? Better make it count. Better make it hurt. Better kill me in one shot.” -Mr. Baseball, @MisterBaseball5 Twitter. 2017":"\"你拿那根大棒子想干嘛？想打我？最好一击命中。最好让我痛。最好一棒子打死我。\" -Mr. Baseball, @MisterBaseball5 Twitter. 2017","“...as soon as he had got through with all his work, he clutched up two more of my men, and began eating them for his morning's meal. Presently, with the utmost ease, he rolled the stone away from the door and drove out his sheep, but he at once put it back again—as easily as though he were merely clapping the lid on to a quiver full of arrows.” -Homer, _The Odyssey_, Book IX. trans. Samuel Butler, 1900.":"\"……他刚忙完所有的活儿，便又抓了我两个同伴，开始把他们当早饭吃。随后，他轻而易举地滚开门口的大石，把羊群赶出去，又马上把石头搬回去——轻松得就像给箭袋盖上盖子似的。\" -Homer, _The Odyssey_, Book IX. trans. Samuel Butler, 1900.","“Princess! youngest princess! Open the door for me! Dost thou not know what thou saidst to me Yesterday by the cool waters of the fountain? Princess, youngest princess! Open the door for me!” -Brothers Grimm (Margaret Hunt), _The Frog King, or Iron Henry_":"\"公主！最年轻的公主！ 为我开门！ 你难道忘了，昨日 在清凉的喷泉边你对我说的话？ 公主！最年轻的公主！ 为我开门！\" -Brothers Grimm (Margaret Hunt), _The Frog King, or Iron Henry_","“But Sigmund turned him about, and he said: ‘What aileth thee, son? Shall our life-days never be merry, and our labour never be done?’":"\"但西格蒙德转过身来，说：'你怎么了，孩子？ 难道我们的岁月永远不能欢乐，我们的劳苦永远不能终结？'","But Sinfiotli said: ‘I have looked, and lo, there is death in the cup.’":"辛菲奥特利说：'我看见了，看哪，杯中乃是死亡。'","And the song, and the tinkling of harp-strings to the roof-tree winded up; And Sigmund was dreamy with wine and the wearing of many a year; And the noise and the glee of the people as the sound of the wild woods were And the blossoming boughs of the Branstock were the wild trees waving about;":"于是歌声与竖琴的铮铮之音绕梁而上； 西格蒙德因酒意与经年劳顿而恍惚； 人群的喧哗与欢腾，在他听来犹如荒野林莽的声响； 而布兰斯托克的繁花枝干，恍若四周摇曳的野树；","So he said: ‘Well seen, my fosterling; let the lip then strain it out.’” -William Morris, _The Story of Sigurd the Volsung and the Fall of the Niblungs_. 1891.":"于是他说：'看得好，我的养子；那就用嘴唇将它滤去吧。'\" -William Morris, _The Story of Sigurd the Volsung and the Fall of the Niblungs_. 1891.","“But Sigmund turned him about, and he said: ‘What aileth thee, son? Shall our life-days never be merry, and our labour never be done?’ But Sinfiotli said: ‘I have looked, and lo, there is death in the cup.’ And the song, and the tinkling of harp-strings to the roof-tree winded up; And Sigmund was dreamy with wine and the wearing of many a year; And the noise and the glee of the people as the sound of the wild woods were And the blossoming boughs of the Branstock were the wild trees waving about; So he said: ‘Well seen, my fosterling; let the lip then strain it out.’” -William Morris, _The Story of Sigurd the Volsung and the Fall of the Niblungs_. 1891.":"\"但西格蒙德转过身来，说：'你怎么了，孩子？ 难道我们的岁月永远不能欢乐，我们的劳苦永远不能终结？' 辛菲奥特利说：'我看见了，看哪，杯中乃是死亡。' 于是歌声与竖琴的铮铮之音绕梁而上； 西格蒙德因酒意与经年劳顿而恍惚； 人群的喧哗与欢腾，在他听来犹如荒野林莽的声响； 而布兰斯托克的繁花枝干，恍若四周摇曳的野树； 于是他说：'看得好，我的养子；那就用嘴唇将它滤去吧。'\" -William Morris, _The Story of Sigurd the Volsung and the Fall of the Niblungs_. 1891.","“He saith that Tiamat our mother hath conceived a hatred for us, With all her force she rageth, full of wrath. All the gods have turned to her, With those, whom ye created, they go at her side. They are banded together, and at the side of Tiamat they advance; They are furious, they devise mischief without resting night and day. They prepare for battle, fuming and raging; They have joined their forces and are making war. Tiamat who formed all things, Made in addition weapons invincible; she spawned monster-serpents, Sharp of tooth, and merciless of fang; With poison, instead of blood, she filled their bodies. Fierce monster-vipers she clothed with terror, With splendor she decked them, she made them of lofty stature. Whoever beheld them, terror overcame him, Their bodies reared up and none could withstand their attack.” -Enuma Elish, Third Tablet. circa 668 BCE.":"\"他说，我们的母亲提亚马特对我们怀了憎恨， 她倾尽全力的狂怒，满腔怒火。 所有的神祇都转向了她， 与你们所造之众一道，随她而行。 他们结为一体，在提亚马特身侧前进； 他们狂怒不休，日夜谋划祸端。 他们为战斗准备，咆哮沸腾； 他们纠集兵力，正挑起战争。 提亚马特，创造万物的她， 更造了无敌的兵器；她产下了巨蛇怪物， 齿牙锋利，毒牙无情； 她以毒液代替鲜血，充塞它们的躯体。 凶猛的巨蛇怪物，她以恐怖包裹之， 以辉煌装饰之，使它们体型巍然。 谁见了它们，恐惧便攫住谁， 它们昂起身躯，谁也无法抵御它们的攻击。\" -Enuma Elish, Third Tablet. circa 668 BCE.","“_Urug_, tumbled down, fallen by crumbling down. Slipped down, as earth from a hill-side, stones which have been piled up or the like. To fall as water at a cascade. To fill up a hollow by putting earth into it. To lay gravel or materials on a road. A landslip.":"\" _乌鲁格_，翻滚而下，因崩裂而坠落。如山侧滚落的泥土，堆积之石之类。如瀑布之水般落下。以填土填入坑洼。在路上铺设砾石或材料。山体滑坡。","_Ururugan_, apparently a plural form of 'Urug'. To go with a number of men to any work. To make war, to attack with an army. To set upon in numbers, as it were to tumble upon in masses.” -Jonathan Rigg, A dictionary of the Sunda language of Java. 1862.":"_Ururugan_，显然是'Urug'的复数形式。指带一群人去从事某项工作。发动战争，以军队攻击。以人数优势围攻，仿佛蜂拥而至、成团坠落。\" -Jonathan Rigg, A dictionary of the Sunda language of Java. 1862.","“_Urug_, tumbled down, fallen by crumbling down. Slipped down, as earth from a hill-side, stones which have been piled up or the like. To fall as water at a cascade. To fill up a hollow by putting earth into it. To lay gravel or materials on a road. A landslip. _Ururugan_, apparently a plural form of 'Urug'. To go with a number of men to any work. To make war, to attack with an army. To set upon in numbers, as it were to tumble upon in masses.” -Jonathan Rigg, A dictionary of the Sunda language of Java. 1862.":"\" _乌鲁格_，翻滚而下，因崩裂而坠落。如山侧滚落的泥土，堆积之石之类。如瀑布之水般落下。以填土填入坑洼。在路上铺设砾石或材料。山体滑坡。 _Ururugan_，显然是'Urug'的复数形式。指带一群人去从事某项工作。发动战争，以军队攻击。以人数优势围攻，仿佛蜂拥而至、成团坠落。\" -Jonathan Rigg, A dictionary of the Sunda language of Java. 1862.","“Beside the man stands a woman - of sorts. Her emulation of the human gender is only superficial, a courtesy. Likewise the loose drapelike dress she wears is not cloth. She has simply shaped a portion of her stiff substance to suit the preferences of the fragile, mortal creatures among whom she currently moves. From a distance the illusion would work to pass her off as a woman standing still...":"\"男人身旁站着一个女人——勉强算是。她对人类性别的模仿只是表面的，一种礼节。同样，她穿的那身宽松垂坠的衣袍也并非布料。她不过是将自己那坚硬物质的一部分塑造成了符合那些脆弱的、终有一死的造物的偏好——在她当下与之交往的这群生灵面前。从远处看，这幻象足以让她蒙混过关，看起来就像一个静立不动的女人……","When she turns to the man - slowly; stone eaters are slow aboveground, except when they aren't - this movement pushes her beyond artful beauty into something altogether different. The man has grown used to it, but even so, he does not look at her. He does not want revulsion to spoil the moment.” -N.K. Jemisin, “The Fifth Season”. 2015.":"当她转向那男人时——缓慢地；噬石者在地面上很慢，除了例外之时——这动作将她从精巧的美推向了某种截然不同的东西。男人已经习惯了，但即便如此，他也不看她。他不想让厌恶毁掉这一刻。\" -N.K. Jemisin, \"The Fifth Season\". 2015.","“Beside the man stands a woman - of sorts. Her emulation of the human gender is only superficial, a courtesy. Likewise the loose drapelike dress she wears is not cloth. She has simply shaped a portion of her stiff substance to suit the preferences of the fragile, mortal creatures among whom she currently moves. From a distance the illusion would work to pass her off as a woman standing still... When she turns to the man - slowly; stone eaters are slow aboveground, except when they aren't - this movement pushes her beyond artful beauty into something altogether different. The man has grown used to it, but even so, he does not look at her. He does not want revulsion to spoil the moment.” -N.K. Jemisin, “The Fifth Season”. 2015.":"\"男人身旁站着一个女人——勉强算是。她对人类性别的模仿只是表面的，一种礼节。同样，她穿的那身宽松垂坠的衣袍也并非布料。她不过是将自己那坚硬物质的一部分塑造成了符合那些脆弱的、终有一死的造物的偏好——在她当下与之交往的这群生灵面前。从远处看，这幻象足以让她蒙混过关，看起来就像一个静立不动的女人…… 当她转向那男人时——缓慢地；噬石者在地面上很慢，除了例外之时——这动作将她从精巧的美推向了某种截然不同的东西。男人已经习惯了，但即便如此，他也不看她。他不想让厌恶毁掉这一刻。\" -N.K. Jemisin, \"The Fifth Season\". 2015.","“I beheld the wretch — the miserable monster whom I had created. He held up the curtain of the bed; and his eyes, if eyes they may be called, were fixed on me. His jaws opened, and he muttered some inarticulate sounds, while a grin wrinkled his cheeks.” -Mary Shelley, _Frankenstein_. 1818.":"\"我看见了那个可怜虫——那个我亲手创造的悲惨怪物。他撩起了床帘；他的眼睛，如果那也能叫作眼睛的话，死死地盯着我。他的下颌张开着，嘴里嘟囔着一些含混不清的声音，一抹笑纹爬上了他的脸颊。\" -Mary Shelley, _Frankenstein_. 1818.","“And when His master plan is unfurled There stands a handsome bid On the weather systems of the world” -Andrew Bird, “Banking on a Myth”. 2005.":"\"而当他 宏伟的计划展开时 便有一个漂亮的出价 押在世界的气象系统之上\" -Andrew Bird, \"Banking on a Myth\". 2005.","<bat>":"<bat>","“And when you look long into an abyss, the abyss also looks into you.” -Friedrich Nietzche, “Beyond Good and Evil”. 1886.":"\"当你久久地凝视深渊时，深渊也在凝视你。\" -Friedrich Nietzsche, \"Beyond Good and Evil\". 1886.","“Blood, sweat, and tea, sister! That's what it takes to achieve all great and terrible things.” -Emory R. Frie, _Wonderland_. 2016.":"\"血、汗和茶，姐妹！成就一切伟大而可怕之事，靠的就是这些。\" -Emory R. Frie, _Wonderland_. 2016.","“Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live.” -KJV Bible, Exodus 22:18.":"\"行邪术的女人，不可容她存活。\" -KJV Bible, Exodus 22:18.（和合本）","ADDER, n. A species of snake. So called from its habit of adding funeral outlays to the other expenses of living. -Ambrose Bierce, _The Devil's Dictionary_, 1906.":"加法蝰蛇，名词。蛇的一种。得名于其在生活其他开销之外，还习惯性地增加（add）一笔丧葬费用。 -Ambrose Bierce, _The Devil's Dictionary_, 1906.","““My father, my father, he seizes me fast, Full sorely the Erl-King has hurt me at last.”":"\"'父亲啊，父亲，他紧紧抓住了我， 桤木王他弄痛了我啊，好痛。'","The father now gallops, with terror half wild, He grasps in his arms the poor shuddering child; He reaches his courtyard with toil and with dread, The child in his arms finds he motionless, dead.” -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782. trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.":"父亲策马狂奔，惊恐几近癫狂， 他紧抱着怀中的孩子，可怜瑟瑟发抖； 他精疲力竭、满怀恐惧地赶到了庭院， 怀中的孩子，已然一动不动，死了。\" -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782. trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.","““My father, my father, he seizes me fast, Full sorely the Erl-King has hurt me at last.” The father now gallops, with terror half wild, He grasps in his arms the poor shuddering child; He reaches his courtyard with toil and with dread, The child in his arms finds he motionless, dead.” -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782. trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.":"\"'父亲啊，父亲，他紧紧抓住了我， 桤木王他弄痛了我啊，好痛。' 父亲策马狂奔，惊恐几近癫狂， 他紧抱着怀中的孩子，可怜瑟瑟发抖； 他精疲力竭、满怀恐惧地赶到了庭院， 怀中的孩子，已然一动不动，死了。\" -Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, _Erlkönig_, 1782. trans. Edgar Alfred Bowring, 1853.","“Alligators commit errors of diet.” -Bennet Bowler, M.D., _Contributions to the Natural History of the Alligator, (Crocodilus Mississipiensis), with a Microscopic Addendum_, p. 17. 1846.":"\"短吻鳄在饮食上会犯错误。\" -Bennet Bowler, M.D., _Contributions to the Natural History of the Alligator, (Crocodilus Mississipiensis), with a Microscopic Addendum_, p. 17. 1846.","“I should have been a pair of ragged claws scuttling across the floors of silent seas.” -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. 1915.":"\"我本该是一对参差不齐的利爪 在寂静海底的沙地上匆匆横行。\" -T.S. Eliot, _The Love Song of J. Alfred Prufrock_. 1915.","<occultist>":"<occultist>","“Be thou like the imperial Basilisk Killing thy foe with unapparent wounds! Gaze on Oppression, till at that dread risk Aghast she pass from the Earth's disk: Fear not, but gaze—for freemen mightier grow, And slaves more feeble, gazing on their foe:— If Hope, and Truth, and Justice may avail, Thou shalt be great—All hail!” -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Posthumous Poems”. 1824.":"\"愿你如那威严的蛇怪之王， 以无痕之伤杀死你的仇敌！ 凝视压迫吧，直到在那骇人的风险下， 她惊恐地从大地的圆盘上逃逸： 别怕，只需凝视——因为自由人会越发强大， 而奴隶们凝视着敌人时越发虚弱：—— 如果希望、真理与正义能够奏效， 你必伟大——万万岁！\" -Percy Bysshe Shelley, \"Posthumous Poems\". 1824.","“The sun was set; the night came on apace, And falling dews bewet around the place; The bat takes airy rounds on leathern wings, And the hoarse owl his woeful dirges sings.” -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps.":"\"太阳西沉；黑夜迅速降临， 降露濡湿了四周之地； 蝙蝠以革质的翅膀在空中盘旋， 嘶哑的猫头鹰唱起它悲哀的挽歌。\" -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps.","“Ere the bat hath flown His cloister'd flight.” -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.":"\"在蝙蝠完成它 廊下的巡礼之前。\" -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.","“The sun was set; the night came on apace, And falling dews bewet around the place; The bat takes airy rounds on leathern wings, And the hoarse owl his woeful dirges sings.” -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps. “Ere the bat hath flown His cloister'd flight.” -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.":"\"太阳西沉；黑夜迅速降临， 降露濡湿了四周之地； 蝙蝠以革质的翅膀在空中盘旋， 嘶哑的猫头鹰唱起它悲哀的挽歌。\" -John Gay, Shepherd's Week, Wednesday; or, The Dumps. \"在蝙蝠完成它 廊下的巡礼之前。\" -William Shakespeare, _Macbeth_, III, 2, line 40. 1605.","“I'm your only friend I'm not your only friend But I'm a little glowing friend But really I'm not actually your friend But I am” -They Might Be Giants, “Birdhouse in Your Soul”. 1989.":"\"我是你唯一的朋友 我不是你唯一的朋友 但我是个微微发光的朋友 但其实我不是你真正的朋友 但我是\" -They Might Be Giants, \"Birdhouse in Your Soul\". 1989.","“The Bès Kěmwar, “maggot spirit”, is one of the many _bès_ or disease spirits known to the Jah Hut of Malaysia. A polyvalent spirit, it is depicted as a maggot or caterpillar, with variants distinguished by hair, thorns, wings, and other details. It eats rice, vegetables, and other crops. It is responsible for aches in bones, joints, and muscles. If its caterpillar hair falls into water and that water is drunk, it causes coughing and bleeding in the throat. Maggot spirits are also known to live in rotten tree trunks and feed in them. Anyone who approaches the fallen tree will be bitten in the leg by the spirit, causing redness, swelling, and itching. All the toenails fall off but the swelling will be gone by two or three months.” - _A Book of Creatures_, 2020.":"\"贝斯·肯瓦尔（Bès Kěmwar），'蛆灵'，是马来西亚贾胡特人所知的众多_bès_或疾病精灵之一。作为一种多价精灵，它被描绘为蛆虫或毛虫，其变体以毛发、刺、翅膀及其他细节加以区分。它以稻米、蔬菜和其他作物为食。可导致骨骼、关节和肌肉的疼痛。若其毛虫的毛发落入水中，饮者将引发咳嗽和咽喉出血。蛆灵也居住在腐烂的树干中并以此为食。任何靠近这棵倒树的人都会被精灵咬伤腿部，引起红肿、瘙痒及肿胀。所有脚指甲都会脱落，但肿胀将在两三个月内消退。\" - _A Book of Creatures_, 2020.","“He thinks every bush a boggart.” -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768.":"\"他看每一丛灌木都像博加特（妖怪）。\" -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768.","“A BOGGART intruded himself, upon what pretext or by what authority is unknown, into the house of a quiet, inoffensive, and laborious farmer; and, when once it had taken possession it disputed the right of domicile with the legal mortal tenant, in a very unneighbourly and arbitrary manner. In particular, it seemed to have a great aversion to children. As there is no point on which a parent feels more acutely than that of the maltreatment of his offspring, the feelings of the father and more particularly of his good dame, were daily, ay, and nightly, harrowed up by the malice of this malignant and invisible boggart.” -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_ 1890.":"\"一个博加特侵入了某位安静守法、勤劳耕作之农夫的家；无人知晓它凭什么借口或何种权威。一旦占据那屋子，它便以一种极不友善、专横霸道的方式，与合法的凡人居住者争夺居住权。它尤其对孩童怀有极大敌意。对于父母而言，没有什么比子女遭受虐待更令人痛彻心扉的了，因此那位父亲，尤其是他的好妻子，日日夜夜被这恶毒而隐形的博加特之恶意所折磨。\" -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_ 1890.","“He thinks every bush a boggart.” -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768. “A BOGGART intruded himself, upon what pretext or by what authority is unknown, into the house of a quiet, inoffensive, and laborious farmer; and, when once it had taken possession it disputed the right of domicile with the legal mortal tenant, in a very unneighbourly and arbitrary manner. In particular, it seemed to have a great aversion to children. As there is no point on which a parent feels more acutely than that of the maltreatment of his offspring, the feelings of the father and more particularly of his good dame, were daily, ay, and nightly, harrowed up by the malice of this malignant and invisible boggart.” -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_ 1890.":"\"他看每一丛灌木都像博加特（妖怪）。\" -John Ray, _A Compleat Collection of English Proverbs_. 1768. \"一个博加特侵入了某位安静守法、勤劳耕作之农夫的家；无人知晓它凭什么借口或何种权威。一旦占据那屋子，它便以一种极不友善、专横霸道的方式，与合法的凡人居住者争夺居住权。它尤其对孩童怀有极大敌意。对于父母而言，没有什么比子女遭受虐待更令人痛彻心扉的了，因此那位父亲，尤其是他的好妻子，日日夜夜被这恶毒而隐形的博加特之恶意所折磨。\" -C.J.T., _Folk-lore and Legends: English_ 1890.","“Hello, my baby Hello, my honey Hello, my ragtime gal":"\"哈喽，我的宝贝 哈喽，我的甜心 哈喽，我的狂热姑娘","Send me a kiss by wire Baby, my hearts on fire":"给我发个电报吻吧 宝贝，我的心在燃烧","If you refuse me Honey, you'll lose me Then you'll be left alone":"如果你拒绝我 甜心，你就会失去我 然后你将孤身一人","Oh baby, telephone And tell me I'm your own.” -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, “Hello My Baby!”":"哦宝贝，打个电话 说我是你的人。\" -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, \"Hello My Baby!\"","“Hello, my baby Hello, my honey Hello, my ragtime gal Send me a kiss by wire Baby, my hearts on fire If you refuse me Honey, you'll lose me Then you'll be left alone Oh baby, telephone And tell me I'm your own.” -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, “Hello My Baby!”":"\"哈喽，我的宝贝 哈喽，我的甜心 哈喽，我的狂热姑娘 给我发个电报吻吧 宝贝，我的心在燃烧 如果你拒绝我 甜心，你就会失去我 然后你将孤身一人 哦宝贝，打个电话 说我是你的人。\" -Ida Emerson and Joseph E. Howard, \"Hello My Baby!\"","“And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.” -KJV Bible, Exodus 3:2.":"\"耶和华的使者从荆棘里火焰中向摩西显现。摩西观看，不料，荆棘被火烧着，却没有烧毁。\" -KJV Bible, Exodus 3:2.（和合本）","“Happiness is a butterfly, which when pursued, is always just beyond your grasp, but which, if you will sit down quietly, may alight upon you.” -Nathaniel Hawthorne":"\"幸福是一只蝴蝶，你若追逐它，它永远在你够不到的地方；但你若静静坐下，它也许就会落在你身上。\" -Nathaniel Hawthorne","“We'll call him Cacodemon, with his black Gib there, his Succuba, his Devil's Seed, his Spawn of Phlegethon, that o’ my Consience was bred o’ the Spume of Cocytus.” -John Fletcher, _The Knight of Malta_. 1647.":"\"我们就叫他卡科德蒙，带着他那黑猫吉布，他的苏库芭，他的魔鬼之种，他的弗莱格松后裔——我敢说，那可是用科塞特斯河的泡沫喂养出来的。\" -John Fletcher, _The Knight of Malta_. 1647.","“So passed he over into the island, taking with him the two brothers of Anaxius; where he found the forsaken knight attired in his own livery, as black as sorrow itself could see itself in the blackest glass: his ornaments of the same hue, but formd into the figures of ravens which seemed to gape for carrion: only his reins were snakes, which finely wrapping themselves one within the other, their heads came together to the cheeks and bosses of the bit, where they might seem to bite at the horse, and the horse, as he champed the bit, to bite at them, and that the white foam was engendered by the poisonous fury of the combat. His impresa was a Catoblepta, which so long lies dead as the moon (whereto it hath so natural a sympathy) wants her light. The word signified, that the moon wanted not the light, but the poor beast wanted the moon's light.” -Sir Philip Sidney":"\"于是他渡海登岛，携着阿纳克西乌斯的两位兄弟；在那里，他找到了那位被弃的骑士，身穿他自己的制服，色如悲伤本身在至暗的镜中照见自身时那般漆黑：他的饰物亦同此色，却铸成乌鸦的形状，仿佛在张口等待腐肉；唯有他的缰绳是蛇，它们彼此精巧地盘绕，蛇头汇聚于马衔的两颊与饰钉之处，仿佛要咬那马，而那马在嚼咬衔铁时，又仿佛要回咬它们；白色的泡沫便是这场毒烈的搏斗所生。他的纹章乃是一只卡托布莱帕，此兽在月亮（它与月亮有种天然的共感）失去光芒时，便长久地僵卧如死。铭词意为：月亮并非缺少光芒，而是那可怜的野兽缺少了月光。\" -Sir Philip Sidney","“The glory of Yahweh mounted up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of Yahweh's glory.":"\"耶和华的荣耀从基路伯那里上升，停在门坎以上；殿内满了云彩，院宇也被耶和华荣耀的光辉充满。","The sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard even to the outer court, as the voice of God Almighty when he speaks.” -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5":"基路伯翅膀的响声听到外院，好像全能神说话的声音。\" -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5（和合本）","“The glory of Yahweh mounted up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of Yahweh's glory. The sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard even to the outer court, as the voice of God Almighty when he speaks.” -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5":"\"耶和华的荣耀从基路伯那里上升，停在门坎以上；殿内满了云彩，院宇也被耶和华荣耀的光辉充满。 基路伯翅膀的响声听到外院，好像全能神说话的声音。\" -WEB Bible, Ezekiel 10:4-5（和合本）","“In its simplest form it is a bird of the night, an owl (_Strix rufipes_) that flies on silent wings during the night to announce illness, death, or some other unwelcome event. When its croaking is heard it is advised to throw ash into the air and utter a few prayers in the hopes of turning away its evil.":"\"其最基本的形式是一种夜鸟，一种猫头鹰（_Strix rufipes_），在夜间以无声的翅膀飞行，宣告疾病、死亡或其他不幸之事。当听到它的嘶哑叫声时，人们应当向空中撒灰并念诵几句祈祷，以期驱散它的邪恶。","The chonchón is also said to be a _calcu_ or evil sorcerer in disguise. It resemble a human head, with oversized wing-like ears that allow it to fly. During the night, these sorcerers’ heads detach themselves from their bodies and fly around to cause mischief, invisible to most, their ominous _tué, tué, tué_ call announcing misfortune. They have the same powers as sorcerers do, and have been known to suck the blood of sleepers.” - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.":"据说琼琼也是一种_calcu_，即伪装的邪恶巫师。它形似一颗人头，长着一对巨大的、翅膀般的耳朵，使其能够飞行。夜间，这些巫师的头颅从身体上分离，四处飞行作恶，对大多数人而言不可见，而它们那不祥的_tué, tué, tué_叫声宣告着不幸。它们拥有与巫师相同的能力，且据说会吸食沉睡者的鲜血。\" - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.","“In its simplest form it is a bird of the night, an owl (_Strix rufipes_) that flies on silent wings during the night to announce illness, death, or some other unwelcome event. When its croaking is heard it is advised to throw ash into the air and utter a few prayers in the hopes of turning away its evil. The chonchón is also said to be a _calcu_ or evil sorcerer in disguise. It resemble a human head, with oversized wing-like ears that allow it to fly. During the night, these sorcerers’ heads detach themselves from their bodies and fly around to cause mischief, invisible to most, their ominous _tué, tué, tué_ call announcing misfortune. They have the same powers as sorcerers do, and have been known to suck the blood of sleepers.” - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.":"\"其最基本的形式是一种夜鸟，一种猫头鹰（_Strix rufipes_），在夜间以无声的翅膀飞行，宣告疾病、死亡或其他不幸之事。当听到它的嘶哑叫声时，人们应当向空中撒灰并念诵几句祈祷，以期驱散它的邪恶。 据说琼琼也是一种_calcu_，即伪装的邪恶巫师。它形似一颗人头，长着一对巨大的、翅膀般的耳朵，使其能够飞行。夜间，这些巫师的头颅从身体上分离，四处飞行作恶，对大多数人而言不可见，而它们那不祥的_tué, tué, tué_叫声宣告着不幸。它们拥有与巫师相同的能力，且据说会吸食沉睡者的鲜血。\" - _A Book of Creatures_, 2015.","“The Devil, too, sometimes steals human children; it is not infrequent for him to carry away infants within the first six weeks after birth, and to substitute in their place imps.” -Martin Luther":"\"魔鬼有时也偷人类的孩子；他常常在婴儿出生后头六周内将其掳走，并用小鬼取而代之。\" -Martin Luther","“How doth the little crocodile Improve his shining tail, And pour the waters of the Nile On every golden scale!":"\"小小鳄鱼怎么样 把他闪亮的尾巴来改良， 把尼罗河水来浇漾， 浇在片片金鳞上！","How cheerfully he seems to grin, How neatly spreads his claws, And welcomes little fishes in With gently smiling jaws!” -Lewis Carroll, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.":"看他笑得多么欢畅， 爪子张得多齐整， 欢迎小鱼游进来， 那微笑的嘴巴多温存！\" -Lewis Carroll（赵元任译）, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.","“How doth the little crocodile Improve his shining tail, And pour the waters of the Nile On every golden scale! How cheerfully he seems to grin, How neatly spreads his claws, And welcomes little fishes in With gently smiling jaws!” -Lewis Carroll, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.":"\"小小鳄鱼怎么样 把他闪亮的尾巴来改良， 把尼罗河水来浇漾， 浇在片片金鳞上！ 看他笑得多么欢畅， 爪子张得多齐整， 欢迎小鱼游进来， 那微笑的嘴巴多温存！\" -Lewis Carroll（赵元任译）, _Alice's Adventures in Wonderland_, 1865.","“Good friend for Jesus’ sake forbear, To dig the dust enclosed here. Blessed be the man that spares these stones, And cursed be he that moves my bones.” -Epitaph on William Shakespeare's grave":"\"好朋友，看在耶稣的份上， 莫要挖掘此处封存的尘土。 容我安息者，必蒙赐福； 动我骸骨者，必受咒诅。\" -Epitaph on William Shakespeare's grave","“Between these twain the Daevas also chose not aright, for infatuation came upon them as they took counsel together, so that they chose the Worst Thought. Then they rushed together to Violence, that they might enfeeble the world of men.” -the Avesta, Yasna XXX, 6, Ahunavaiti Gatha. trans. Christian Bartholomae, 1951.":"\"在这两者之间，德弗们也未能正确选择，因为当它们一起商议时，迷惘降临在它们身上，于是它们选择了最恶之思。然后它们冲向了暴力，欲以此削弱凡人之界。\" -the Avesta, Yasna XXX, 6, Ahunavaiti Gatha. trans. Christian Bartholomae, 1951.","“Xinchub: At least you're conceding that I've got a soul. Petey: Yes, but it is battered, twisted, and drenched in the blood of the innocent. Xinchub: Mmm... yeah. Petey: When you stop being pleased by that we'll know you're making progress.” -Howard Tayler, _Schlock Mercenary_. February 8, 2008.":"\"辛丘布：至少你承认我有灵魂了。 皮蒂：是的，但它伤痕累累、面目扭曲，浸透了无辜者的鲜血。 辛丘布：嗯……是啊。 皮蒂：当有一天你对此不再沾沾自喜时，我们就知道你有所进步了。\" -Howard Tayler, _Schlock Mercenary_. February 8, 2008.","“As one example of the meanings inherent in a form, let us examine a particular form of vertical stone marker, variously called stele, obelisk, standing-stone, and memorial column. These have been historically and commonly used to commemorate honored phenomena. So, when a people wish to remember an important relationship, event or personage, a location is dedicated to it and often marked with an enduring and aspiring vertical form or sets of them. In natural language, a vertical stone means: an aspiring connector between us (on earth) and an ideal (up there); that we ‘stand up’ with pride about this honored phenomenon. The marker is a symbolic inhabitation of the place it occupies. Its size and workmanship is a sacrifice of much work and resources to a memory. It is a strong suggestion (because we left it to them and it is of durable material) that future people also give honor to the memorialized phenomenon. When we use this particular physical form of the vertical marker, both its historic use as an honorific and its meanings in natural language may well send a message that this is an honored place, a place about a ‘good’ both in our culture and in the culture of future observers.” -“Expert Judgment on Markers to Deter Inadvertent Human Intrusion into the Waste Isolation Pilot Plant”, Sandia National Laboratories report. 1993":"\"作为形式固有含义的一个例证，让我们考察一种特定的垂直石碑形式，它被不同地称为石碑、方尖碑、立石和纪念柱。历史上，这些碑柱一直被普遍用于纪念被尊崇的现象。因此，当一群人希望铭记某个重要的关系、事件或人物时，他们会为此选定一个地点，并通常以经久耐用、昂然向上的垂直形式或一组这样的形式来标记它。在自然语言中，一块垂直的石头意味着：我们（在地上）与一个理想（在天上）之间昂然向上的连接器；我们为这被尊崇的现象而自豪地'站立起来'。这块标记是对其所占据空间的象征性栖居。其规模和工艺是将大量劳动和资源奉献给一段记忆的牺牲行为。它（因为我们把它留给了后人，且它是由耐久材料制成的）是一个强有力的提示，希望未来的人们也能向这被铭记的现象致以敬意。当我们使用这种特定的垂直标记的物理形式时，其作为荣耀象征的历史用途，以及其在自然语言中的含义，很可能发送出一条信息：这是一个荣耀之地，一个关于'善'的地方——无论是在我们的文化中，还是在未来观察者的文化中。\" -\"Expert Judgment on Markers to Deter Inadvertent Human Intrusion into the Waste Isolation Pilot Plant\", Sandia National Laboratories report. 1993","“Standing over Hugo, and plucking at his throat, there stood a foul thing, a great, black beast, shaped like a hound, yet larger than any hound that ever mortal eye has rested upon. And even as they looked the thing tore the throat out of Hugo Baskerville...” -Arthur Conan Doyle, _The Hound of the Baskervilles_. 1902.":"\"站在雨果身旁，咬住他喉咙的，是一个肮脏的东西，一头巨大的黑色野兽，形如猎犬，却比凡人肉眼见过的任何猎犬都要庞大。就在他们眼睁睁看着的时候，那东西将雨果·巴斯克维尔的喉咙撕开了……\" -Arthur Conan Doyle, _The Hound of the Baskervilles_. 1902.","“How undisturbed, the sleep of the foolish.” -Philip K. Dick":"\"愚人的睡眠何其安稳。\" -Philip K. Dick","• Roy Quixote: Wait, what's my beef with clean energy again? — Durkon Pansa: Dunno, but if'n ye prefer, I know a grove o'peach trees tha've been gettin' fresh wit tha locals. -Rich Burlew, “Haleo and Julean”":"• 罗伊·吉诃德：等等，我跟清洁能源有什么仇来着？ — 杜尔康·潘萨：不知道，不过嘞，你要是想换个玩法，我知道有一片桃树林呗，那群桃树老对本地人放肆无礼嘞。 -Rich Burlew, \"Haleo and Julean\"","“When the hoopoe returned to Solomon (he told him the news), and he responded (to Sheba's people): “Are you giving me money? What GOD has given me is far better than what He has given you. You are the ones to rejoice in such gifts.” (To the hoopoe, he said), “Go back to them (and let them know that) we will come to them with forces they cannot imagine. We will evict them, humiliated and debased.” He said, “O you elders, which of you can bring me her mansion, before they arrive here as submitters?” One afrit from the jinns said, “I can bring it to you before you stand up. I am powerful enough to do this.” -The Quran, Sura 27 Al-Naml":"\"当戴胜鸟回到所罗门那里（向他报告了消息），他回应道（对示巴人）：'你们拿钱财来给我吗？真主赐予我的，远胜过他赐予你们的。你们才是应为这样的恩赐而欢喜的人。'（他对戴胜鸟说，）'回到他们那里去，（让他们知道）我们将以他们无法想象的兵力来到他们那里。我们将驱逐他们，使他们受辱蒙羞。'他说：'诸位长老啊，你们谁能在她来归顺之前，把她的宝座搬到我跟前来？'精灵中的一个伊弗利特说：'在你从座位上起身之前，我就能把它搬来。我有足够的力量做到此事。'\" -The Quran, Sura 27 Al-Naml","“No sooner had sleep caught him, dissolving all his grief as mists of refreshing slumber poured around him there— his powerful frame was bone-weary from charging Hector straight and hard to the walls of windswept Troy— than the ghost of stricken Patroclus drifted up... He was like the man to the life, every feature, the same tall build and the fine eyes and voice and the very robes that used to clothe his body. Hovering at his head the phantom rose and spoke: ‘Sleeping, Achilles? You’ve forgotten me, my friend. You never neglected me in life, only now in death. Bury me, quickly—let me pass the Gates of Hades. They hold me off at a distance, all the souls, the shades of the burnt-out, breathless dead, never to let me cross the river, mingle with them... They leave me to wander up and down, abandoned, lost at the House of Death with the all-embracing gates.’” -Homer, _The Iliad_, XXIII, 72-88. trans. Robert Fagles, 1990.":"\"睡意刚将他攫住，消解了所有悲愁—— 清爽的睡意如迷雾般围绕他倾泻而下—— 他那强健的躯体因直冲赫克托耳、 奋力杀到狂风呼啸的特洛伊城墙边而疲惫不堪—— 就在此刻，殒命的帕特罗克洛斯的魂影飘然而至…… 他形貌如生，每一处特征分毫不差， 同样的高大身躯，同样美好的眼睛和嗓音， 身披的衣袍正是生前所穿。 魂影悬浮在他头顶，开口说道： '你在沉睡吗，阿喀琉斯？你已将我遗忘，我的朋友。 生前你从不怠慢我，如今只在死后。 快将我埋葬——让我通过哈迪斯之门。 那些灵魂全将我远远挡开， 那些燃尽的、没有呼吸的死者的幽冥， 永不让我渡过冥河，与它们共处…… 它们任我徘徊游荡，被遗弃、迷失 在有深深重门的死亡之殿。'\" -Homer, _The Iliad_, XXIII, 72-88. trans. Robert Fagles, 1990.","“I sing the Body electric” -Walt Whitman, “I Sing the Body Electric”, _Leaves of Grass_. 1867.":"\"我歌唱那带电的躯体\" -Walt Whitman, \"I Sing the Body Electric\", _Leaves of Grass_. 1867.","“And the King went to where the blind men were, and drawing near said to them: ‘Do you now know what an elephant is like?’ ‘Assuredly, Lord: we now know what an elephant is like.’ ‘Tell me then, O blind men, what an elephant is like.’ And those blind men, O Bhikkhus, who had felt the head of the elephant, said: ‘An elephant, Sir, is like a large round jar. Those who had felt its ears, said: 'it is like a winnowing basket.’ Those who had felt its tusks, said: ‘it is like a plough-share.’ Those who had felt its trunk, said: ‘it is like a plough.’ Those who had felt its body, said: ‘it is like a granary.’ Those who had felt its feet, said: ‘it is like a pillar.’ Those who had felt its back, said: ‘it is like a mortar.’ Those who had felt its tail, said: ‘it is a like a pestle.’ Those who had felt the tuft of its tail, said: ‘it is like a broom.’ And they all fought amongst themselves with their fists, declaring, ‘such is an elephant, such is not elephant, an elephant is not like that, it is like this.’” And the King, O Bhikkhus, was highly delighted. -_Udāna_, VI “Jaccandhavagga”. ca. 5th cent. B.C. trans. Dawsonne Melanchthon Strong, 1902.":"\"于是国王来到盲人们所在之处，走近他们说道： '你们现在知道大象是什么样了吗？' '当然，尊主：我们现在知道大象是什么样了。' '那么告诉我，盲人们啊，大象是什么样？' 那些摸过大象头的盲人说：'尊主啊，大象像一个巨大的圆罐。' 那些摸过耳朵的说：'它像一个簸谷的竹篮。' 那些摸过象牙的说：'它像一个犁铧。' 那些摸过象鼻的说：'它像一把犁。' 那些摸过身躯的说：'它像一座谷仓。' 那些摸过脚的说：'它像一根柱子。' 那些摸过背的说：'它像一个石臼。' 那些摸过尾巴的说：'它像一根杵。' 那些摸过尾梢毛的说：'它像一把扫帚。' 于是他们纷纷举起拳头互相争吵，声称：'大象就是这样，大象不是这样，大象不像那样，它就像这样。'\" 国王，比丘们啊，感到十分欣慰。 -_Udāna_, VI \"Jaccandhavagga\". ca. 5th cent. B.C. trans. Dawsonne Melanchthon Strong, 1902.","“Portents had occurred indicating [Titus Flavius Vespasianus'] approaching end, such as the comet which was visible for a long time and the opening of the mausoleum of Augustus of its own accord. When his physicians chided him for continuing his usual course of living during his illness and attending to all the duties that belonged to his office, he answered: ‘The emperor ought to die on his feet.’” -Cassius Dio, _Roman History_, LXVI, xvii, 2. 222 A.D. trans. Earnest Cary, 1925.":"\"出现了预示[提图斯·弗拉维乌斯·维斯帕西亚努斯]大限将至的征兆，比如一颗长时间可见的彗星，以及奥古斯都陵墓自行裂开。当他的御医责备他在病中仍继续惯常的生活方式、处理所有属于其职位的公务时，他答道：'皇帝应当站着死。'\" -Cassius Dio, _Roman History_, LXVI, xvii, 2. 222 A.D. trans. Earnest Cary, 1925.","“Sea horses floundering in the slimy mud, Tossed up their heads, and dashed the ooze about them.” -John Dryden. _All For Love_, I, i, 15-17. 1678.":"\"海马在黏滑的淤泥中挣扎， 昂起它们的头，将污泥溅得四处都是。\" -John Dryden. _All For Love_, I, i, 15-17. 1678.","“SEE! warp is stretched For warrior’s fall; Lo, weft in loom, ’Tis wet with blood; Now, fight foreboding, ’Neath friends’ swift fingers Our gray woof waxeth With war’s alarms, Our warp blood-red, Our weft corse-blue.":"\"看哪！经线已绷紧， 为战士的陨落； 看，织机中的纬线， 已被鲜血浸湿； 如今，战斗的预感， 在友人迅捷的手指下， 我们的灰色织物 因战争的警讯而增长， 我们的经线血红， 我们的纬线尸蓝。","This woof is y-woven With entrails of men; This warp is hard weighted With heads of the slain; Spears blood-besprinkled For spindles we use, Our loom iron-bound, And arrows our reels; With swords for our shuttles This war-woof we work; So weave we, weird sisters, Our war-winning woof.":"这幅织物是以 人类的内脏织就； 这经线沉重地压着 被杀戮者的头颅； 沾满鲜血的长矛 充当我们的纺锤， 我们的织机镶着铁， 箭矢是我们的纱轴； 以刀剑为梭子， 我们编织这战争之纬； 如此我们纺织，怪诞的姐妹， 我们得胜的织品。","Now war-winner walketh To weave in her turn, Now Sword-swinger steppeth, Now Swift-stroke, now Storm; When they speed the shuttle How spear-heads shall flash! Shields crash, and helm-gnawer On harness bite hard!” -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861":"如今战争之胜者走来 轮到她来编织， 如今挥剑者踏入， 如今疾击者，如今风暴； 当她们加速梭子时 矛头将如何闪耀！ 盾牌碎裂，盔甲吞噬者 在铠甲上狠狠撕咬！\" -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861","“SEE! warp is stretched For warrior’s fall; Lo, weft in loom, ’Tis wet with blood; Now, fight foreboding, ’Neath friends’ swift fingers Our gray woof waxeth With war’s alarms, Our warp blood-red, Our weft corse-blue. This woof is y-woven With entrails of men; This warp is hard weighted With heads of the slain; Spears blood-besprinkled For spindles we use, Our loom iron-bound, And arrows our reels; With swords for our shuttles This war-woof we work; So weave we, weird sisters, Our war-winning woof. Now war-winner walketh To weave in her turn, Now Sword-swinger steppeth, Now Swift-stroke, now Storm; When they speed the shuttle How spear-heads shall flash! Shields crash, and helm-gnawer On harness bite hard!” -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861":"\"看哪！经线已绷紧， 为战士的陨落； 看，织机中的纬线， 已被鲜血浸湿； 如今，战斗的预感， 在友人迅捷的手指下， 我们的灰色织物 因战争的警讯而增长， 我们的经线血红， 我们的纬线尸蓝。 这幅织物是以 人类的内脏织就； 这经线沉重地压着 被杀戮者的头颅； 沾满鲜血的长矛 充当我们的纺锤， 我们的织机镶着铁， 箭矢是我们的纱轴； 以刀剑为梭子， 我们编织这战争之纬； 如此我们纺织，怪诞的姐妹， 我们得胜的织品。 如今战争之胜者走来 轮到她来编织， 如今挥剑者踏入， 如今疾击者，如今风暴； 当她们加速梭子时 矛头将如何闪耀！ 盾牌碎裂，盔甲吞噬者 在铠甲上狠狠撕咬！\" -_The Story of Burnt Njal_, trans. George Dasent. 1861","“But he had not been long in his hiding-hole, before the awful Ettin came in; and no sooner was he in, than he was heard crying: ‘Snouk but and snouk ben, I find the smell of an earthly man, Be he living, or be he dead, His heart this night shall kitchen my bread.’” -Joseph Jacobs, _The Red Ettin_":"\"但他刚在藏身之处躲了不久，那可怕的厄丁便走了进来；他才进门，就听到他喊道： '四处嗅啊四处探， 我闻到了凡人气味， 管他是活还是死， 今夜他心脏要给我的面包当馅料。'\" -Joseph Jacobs, _The Red Ettin_","“Behold the Lord High Executioner A personage of noble rank and title — A dignified and potent officer Whose functions are particularly vital! Defer, defer To the Lord High Executioner! Defer, defer To the noble Lord, to the noble Lord To the Lord High Executioner!” -Gilbert and Sullivan, “Behold the Lord High Executioner”, _The Mikado_. 1885":"\"看哪，至高刑法官 一位出身高贵、头衔显赫的人物—— 一位威严而有权的官员 他的职责格外至关重要！ 敬礼，敬礼 向着至高刑法官！ 敬礼，敬礼 向着高贵的法官，向着高贵的法官 向着至高刑法官！\" -Gilbert and Sullivan, \"Behold the Lord High Executioner\", _The Mikado_. 1885","“All the infections that sun sucks up From bogs, fens, flats, on Prosper fall and make him By inch-meal a disease! His spirits hear me And yet I needs must curse.” -William Shakespeare, _The Tempest_, II, 2. 1611.":"\"愿太阳从沼泽、泥塘、洼地中吸起的一切疫疠， 都降临在普洛斯彼罗身上，让他的身体 一寸一寸地溃烂！他的精灵们听见我的话， 但我还是要诅咒。\" -William Shakespeare, _The Tempest_, II, 2. 1611.","“The planet brought forth scintillating jewelled scuttling crabs, which the Vogons ate, smashing their shells with iron mallets; tall aspiring trees with breathtaking slenderness and colour which the Vogons cut down and burned the crab meat with; elegant gazellelike creatures with silken coats and dewy eyes which the Vogons would catch and sit on.” -Douglas Adams, _The Hitch-hiker's Guide to the Galaxy_. 1979.":"\"这颗行星产生了闪烁的、宝石般的、爬来爬去的螃蟹，沃贡人把它们吃掉，用铁锤砸开它们的壳；高大挺拔的树木，有着令人叹为观止的纤细和色彩，沃贡人把它们砍倒，用来烧螃蟹肉；优雅的、瞪羚般的动物，长着丝缎般的皮毛和水汪汪的眼睛，沃贡人把它们捉来当椅子坐。\" -Douglas Adams, _The Hitch-hiker's Guide to the Galaxy_. 1979.","“Solamen miseris socios habuisse doloris.” -Christopher Marlowe, _Doctor Faustus_. 1604":"\"患难之人有同病相怜的慰藉。\" -Christopher Marlowe, _Doctor Faustus_. 1604","“From this story it is evident that in former times the jellyfish once had a shell and bones something like a tortoise, but, ever since the Dragon King's sentence was carried out on the ancestor of the jelly fishes, his descendants have all been soft and boneless just as you see them to-day thrown up by the waves high upon the shores of Japan.” -“The Jellyfish and the Monkey”, adapted by Yei Theodora Ozaki, _Young Folk's Treasury_, vol. II. 1909.":"\"从这个故事可以看出，从前水母也曾像乌龟一样有着壳和骨头，但是自从龙王对水母的祖先施加了刑罚之后，他的后代便都如你今天在日本海岸边被海浪冲上来的那些一样，柔软而无骨了。\" -\"The Jellyfish and the Monkey\", adapted by Yei Theodora Ozaki, _Young Folk's Treasury_, vol. II. 1909.","“Always in focus You can't feel my stare. I zoom into you You don't know I'm there.” -Judas Priest, “Electric Eye”. 1982.":"\"始终聚焦 你感知不到我的凝视。 我向你拉近镜头 你却不知我在此处。\" -Judas Priest, \"Electric Eye\". 1982.","“In the desert I saw a creature, naked, bestial, Who, squatting upon the ground, Held his heart in his hands, And ate of it. I said, ‘Is it good, friend?’ ‘It is bitter — bitter’, he answered, ‘But I like it Because it is bitter, And because it is my heart.’” -Stephen Crane, _The Black Riders and Other Lines_. 1895.":"\"在沙漠中 我见到了一个生灵，赤裸，兽性， 蹲坐在地上， 双手捧着自己的心脏， 一口一口地吃着。 我说：'好吃吗，朋友？' '很苦——苦极了'，他答道， '但我喜欢它 正因为它苦， 也因为它是我的心。'\" -Stephen Crane, _The Black Riders and Other Lines_. 1895.","“El ojo que ves no es ojo porque tú lo veas, es ojo porque te ve.” -Antonio Machado, Campos de Castilla. 1912-1917.":"\"你所见的眼睛 并非因你看见它才是眼睛， 它之所以是眼睛，是因为它在看着你。\" -Antonio Machado, Campos de Castilla. 1912-1917.","“Then he descended softly and beckoned to Nuth. But the gnoles had watched him through knavish holes that they bore in trunks of the trees, and the unearthly silence gave way, as it were with a grace, to the rapid screams of Tonker as they picked him up from behind — screams that came faster and faster until they were incoherent. And where they took him it is not good to ask, and what they did with him I shall not say.” -Lord Dunsany, “How Nuth Would Have Practised His Art Upon the Gnoles”. 1912.":"\"于是他悄悄降下，向努斯示意。但那些格诺尔早已透过他们在树干上凿出的狡诈孔洞监视着他，于是那诡异的寂静，仿佛带着几分优雅地，被通克被他们从身后擒住时发出的急促尖叫所打破——尖叫声越来越快，越来越快，直到语无伦次。至于他们把他带到了哪里，这不是一个好问的问题，而他们对他做了什么，我也不会说。\" -Lord Dunsany, \"How Nuth Would Have Practised His Art Upon the Gnoles\". 1912.","“Swish, smack! Whip crack! Batter and beat! Yammer and bleat! Work, work! Nor dare to shirk, While Goblins quaff, and Goblins laugh, Round and round far underground Below, my lad!” -J.R.R. Tolkien, _The Hobbit_":"\"嗖嗖，啪啪！鞭子噼啪响！ 捶打又抽打！哀嚎又啼哭！ 干活，干活！休想偷懒， 当哥布林畅饮，哥布林欢笑， 在地底深处转着圈跑 往下，小伙子！\" -J.R.R. Tolkien, _The Hobbit_","“You do not come dramatically, with dragons That rear up with my life between their paws And dash me butchered down beside the wagons” -Philip Larkin, “To Failure”. 1949.":"\"你不会戏剧性地降临，带着巨龙 它们昂然立起，双爪挟持着我的性命， 把遭到屠戮的我摔在货车旁边\" -Philip Larkin, \"To Failure\". 1949.","“No coveting nor envy burns In thy bright golden eye, That calm and innocently turns On all below the sky.” -Hannah Flagg Gould, _The Youth's Coronal_":"\"没有贪恋，没有嫉妒燃烧 在你明亮的金色眼睛里， 那平静而无辜的目光， 投向天空下的一切万物。\" -Hannah Flagg Gould, _The Youth's Coronal_","“‘Listen Reb _Golem_,’ the old man said, wagging his finger. ‘Pay attention to what I say—you understand?’ ‘Understand...’ ‘If you want to stay here, you got to do like Mr. Gumbeiner says.’ ‘Do-like-Mr.-Gumbeiner-says...’ ‘_That's_ the way I like to hear a golem talk. Malka, give here the mirror from the pocketbook. Look, you see your face? You see on the forehead, what's written? If you don't do like Mr. Gumbeiner says, he'll wipe out what's written and you'll be no more alive.’ ‘No-more-alive...’ ‘_That's_ right. Now, listen. Under the porch you'll find a lawnmower. Take it. And cut the lawn. Then come back. Go.’” -Avram Davidson, “The Golem”, 1955.":"\"'听着，雷布_戈仑_，'老人说，摇晃着手指。'注意听我说——你明白吗？' '明白……' '你要是想留下来，就得照古姆拜纳先生说的做。' '照-古姆拜纳-先生-说的-做……' '这才是我要听的戈仑说话的样子。马尔卡，把钱包里的小镜子给我。看，你看见你的脸了吗？你看见额头上写的是什么了吗？你要是不照古姆拜纳先生说的做，他就会擦掉写的东西，你就活不成了。' '活-不成……' '这就对了。现在，听着。门廊下面你会找到一台割草机。把它拿来。去割草坪。然后回来。去吧。'\" -Avram Davidson, \"The Golem\", 1955.","“The Second Coming! Hardly are those words out When a vast image out of Spiritus Mundi Troubles my sight: somewhere in sands of the desert A shape with lion body and the head of a man, A gaze blank and pitiless as the sun, Is moving its slow thighs, while all about it Reel shadows of the indignant desert birds.” -W. B. Yeats, \"The Second Coming\". 1920.":"\"第二次降临！这几个字还没说完， 一个从宇宙之灵中涌出的巨大影像 便扰乱了我的视线：在沙漠的沙中某处， 一具狮身人面的形体， 目光空洞而冷酷，如烈日一般， 正缓缓移动着它的大腿，而它周围 盘旋着愤慨的沙漠之鸟的阴影。\" -W. B. Yeats, \"The Second Coming\". 1920.","“Bird-bodied, girl-faced things they are; abominable their droppings, their hands are talons, their faces haggard with hunger insatiable.” -Virgil, Aeneid 3":"\"她们是鸟身、少女面孔的东西；她们的排泄物令人作呕，她们的双手是利爪，她们的面孔因永不满足的饥饿而枯槁憔悴。\" -Virgil, Aeneid 3","“And Phineus had scarcely taken the first morsel up when, with as little warning as a whirlwind or a lightning flash, they dropped from the clouds proclaiming their desire for food with raucous cries. The young lords saw them coming and raised the alarm. Yet they had hardly done so before the Harpyiai had devoured the whole meal and were on the wing once more, far out at sea. All they left was an intolerable stench.” -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434":"\"菲纽斯还未来得及拿起第一口食物，她们便如旋风或闪电一般，毫无预兆地从云中坠落，发出沙哑的叫声宣告着对食物的渴望。年轻的贵族们看见她们来了，发出了警报。然而他们还未来得及行动，哈尔庇厄们便已吞尽了整餐食物，再度展开翅膀，远远地飞到了海上。她们留下的一切，只是一股无法忍受的恶臭。\" -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434","“Bird-bodied, girl-faced things they are; abominable their droppings, their hands are talons, their faces haggard with hunger insatiable.” -Virgil, Aeneid 3 “And Phineus had scarcely taken the first morsel up when, with as little warning as a whirlwind or a lightning flash, they dropped from the clouds proclaiming their desire for food with raucous cries. The young lords saw them coming and raised the alarm. Yet they had hardly done so before the Harpyiai had devoured the whole meal and were on the wing once more, far out at sea. All they left was an intolerable stench.” -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434":"\"她们是鸟身、少女面孔的东西；她们的排泄物令人作呕，她们的双手是利爪，她们的面孔因永不满足的饥饿而枯槁憔悴。\" -Virgil, Aeneid 3 \"菲纽斯还未来得及拿起第一口食物，她们便如旋风或闪电一般，毫无预兆地从云中坠落，发出沙哑的叫声宣告着对食物的渴望。年轻的贵族们看见她们来了，发出了警报。然而他们还未来得及行动，哈尔庇厄们便已吞尽了整餐食物，再度展开翅膀，远远地飞到了海上。她们留下的一切，只是一股无法忍受的恶臭。\" -Apollonius Rhodius, Argonautica 2. 179 — 434","“About her middle round A cry of Hell-hounds never-ceasing barked With wide Cerberean mouths full loud, and rung A hideous peal; yet, when they list, would creep, If aught disturbed their noise, into her womb, And kennel there; yet there still barked and howled Within unseen.” -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book II, 1667.":"\"在她腰间 一群地狱犬的嚎叫从不停止地吠着， 张着宽阔的刻耳柏洛斯般的巨口，震响着 一阵可怖的狂鸣；然而，它们高兴时，若有什么扰了 它们的喧嚣，便会爬进她的子宫， 蜷伏在那里；但在那里，看不见的地方， 却仍然吠着，嚎叫着。\" -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book II, 1667.","“Ok, let's review. It's up to the fair young maiden to rescue the dragon from the fire breathing knights in shining armour.” -Exiern":"\"好吧，让我们回顾一下。现在轮到那位美丽的少女，从那些身披闪亮铠甲、口吐火焰的骑士手中，去拯救巨龙了。\" -Exiern","“A foolish consistency is the hobgoblin of little minds, adored by little statesmen and philosophers and divines.” -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay II: Self-Reliance. 1841.":"\"愚蠢的一致性是渺小心灵的妖怪，备受渺小的政治家、哲学家和神学家的崇拜。\" -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay II: Self-Reliance. 1841.","“Fern came slowly down the stairs. Her eyes were red from crying. As she approached her chair, the carton wobbled, and there was a scratching noise. Fern looked at her father. Then she lifted the lid of the carton. There, inside, looking up at her, was the newborn pig. It was a white one. The morning light shone through its ears, turning them pink. “He's yours,” said Mr. Arable. “Saved from an untimely death. And may the good Lord forgive me for this foolishness.” -E.B. White, _Charlotte's Web_":"\"芬慢慢地走下楼梯。她的眼睛因为哭泣而红红的。当她走近她的椅子时，纸盒晃动了一下，传来一阵抓挠的声音。芬看着她的父亲。然后她掀起了纸盒的盖子。里面，一头新生的小猪正仰头望着她。那是一头白色的小猪。晨光透过它的耳朵，把它们映成了粉红色。'它是你的了，'阿拉布尔先生说。'从早夭的命运中救下来了。愿主宽恕我这番愚蠢。'\" -E.B. White, _Charlotte's Web_","“A traveller, by the faithful hound, Half-buried in the snow was found, Still grasping in his hand of ice That banner with the strange device, Excelsior!” -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “Excelsior”":"\"一位旅人，被忠实的猎犬发现，半埋在雪中，结冰的手里仍然握着那面旗帜，上面写着那奇特的铭言：精益求精！\" -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, \"Excelsior\"","“Do you know Do I know What's this thing called ‘man’? God only knows what a man is! I only know his price.” -Bertolt Brecht, “The Measures Taken”. 1930.":"\"你知道吗 我知道吗 这叫作'人'的东西是什么？ 只有上帝知道人是什么！ 我只知道他的价钱。\" -Bertolt Brecht, \"The Measures Taken\". 1930.","“Once on a time when Brahmadatta was reigning in Benares, the Bodhisatta was born an iguana. When he grew up he dwelt in a big burrow in the river bank with a following of many hundreds of other iguanas. Now the Bodhisatta had a son, a young iguana, who was great friends with a chameleon, whom he used to clip and embrace. This intimacy being reported to the iguana king, he sent for his young son and said that such friendship was misplaced, for chameleons were low creatures, and that if the intimacy was persisted in, calamity would befall the whole of the tribe of iguanas. And he enjoined his son to have no more to do with the chameleon. But the son continued in his intimacy.” -_Khuddaka Nikāya_, Jātaka 141 “Godha-jātaka”. ca. 4th cent. B.C. trans. Robert Chalmers, 1895.":"\"从前，当梵授王在波罗奈为王时，菩萨转生为一只鬣蜥。长大后，他住在大河岸边的一个大洞穴里，有数百只鬣蜥追随他。菩萨有一个儿子，一只年轻的鬣蜥，他与一只变色龙交情甚好，常常拥抱亲近。有人将这种亲密关系禀告了鬣蜥王，他便召来自己的小儿子，说这样的友谊是不适当的，因为变色龙是低等生物，如果继续这种亲密关系，灾祸将降临在整个鬣蜥族群身上。他命令儿子不要再与变色龙来往。但儿子仍继续这种亲密。\" -_Khuddaka Nikāya_, Jātaka 141 \"Godha-jātaka\". ca. 4th cent. B.C. trans. Robert Chalmers, 1895.","“Always ready to take advantage of every favourable opportunity, the Jackal is a sad parasite, and hangs on the skirts of the larger carnivora as they roam the country for prey, in the hope of securing some share of the creatures which they destroy or wound.” -John George Wood, _The Illustrated Natural History: Mammalia_. 1865.":"\"总是随时准备利用每一个有利机会，胡狼是可怜的寄生者，跟随在大型食肉兽的足边，跟随着它们巡游觅食的足迹，希望能分得它们杀死或击伤的猎物的一份。\" -John George Wood, _The Illustrated Natural History: Mammalia_. 1865.","“Beware of the Blob! It creeps And leaps and glides and slides Across the floor Right through the door And all around the wall, A splotch, a blotch...” -Burt Bacharach and Mack David, “Beware of the Blob”. 1958.":"\"当心那团泥浆怪！ 它爬行 跳跃 滑行蠕动 穿过地板 直穿大门 爬满墙壁， 一滩污迹，一团斑渍……\" -Burt Bacharach and Mack David, \"Beware of the Blob\". 1958.","“All the world loves a clown.” -Cole Porter, “Be a Clown”. 1948.":"\"全世界都爱小丑。\" -Cole Porter, \"Be a Clown\". 1948.","“Kobolds are harmless.” -Bearand the Bold, epitaph (Magic: the Gathering)":"\"狗头人并无危险。\" -Bearand the Bold, epitaph (Magic: the Gathering)","“The three of us were sitting ashen faced as if we had just witnessed a foul and malignant murder. At least if we had been watching a murder the murderer wouldn't have been looking us impassively in the eye as he did it. Maybe it was the feeling of cold unflinching arrogance that so disturbed us. But whatever malign emotions we tried to pin on to the lizard, we knew that they weren't the lizard's emotions at all, only ours. The lizard was simply going about its lizardly business in a simple, straightforward lizardly way. It didn't know anything about the horror, the guilt, the shame, the ugliness that we, uniquely guilty and ashamed animals, were trying to foist on it. So we got it all straight back at us, as if reflected in the mirror of its single unwavering and disinterested eye.” -Douglas Adams, “Last Chance to See”. 1990.":"\"我们三个面色惨白地坐着，仿佛刚刚目睹了一场肮脏而恶毒的谋杀。至少如果我们看的是谋杀，那个凶手也不会像眼下这样面无表情地直视着我们的眼睛。或许是那种冷酷而不为所动的傲慢感让我们如此不安。但无论我们试图将什么恶毒的情感强加到那只蜥蜴身上，我们都知道那根本不是蜥蜴的情感，而只是我们自己的。蜥蜴只不过在以简单直接的蜥蜴方式做它蜥蜴该做的事。它对那种恐惧、那种愧疚、那种羞耻、那种丑陋——我们这些唯一懂得愧疚和羞耻的动物试图强加给它的东西——一无所知。于是这一切都反弹回到我们身上，仿佛反射在它那只目光坚定而超然的眼睛的镜面中。\" -Douglas Adams, \"Last Chance to See\". 1990.","“... Kraken, also called the Crab-fish, which [according to the pilots of Norway] is not that huge, for heads and tails counted, he is no larger than our Öland is wide [i.e. less than 16 km] ... He stays at the sea floor, constantly surrounded by innumerable small fishes, who serve as his food and are fed by him in return: for his meal, if I remember correctly what E. Pontoppidan writes, lasts no longer than three months, and another three are then needed to digest it. His excrements nurture in the following an army of lesser fish, and for this reason, fishermen plumb after his resting place ... Gradually, Kraken ascends to the surface, and when he is at ten to twelve fathoms, the boats had better move out of his vicinity, as he will shortly thereafter burst up, like a floating island, spurting water from his dreadful nostrils and making ring waves around him, which can reach many miles. Could one doubt that this is the Leviathan of Job?” -Jacob Wallenberg, “Min son på galejan”. 1781.":"\"……克拉肯，亦称蟹鱼，据挪威的引水人说，并没有那么大，因为头和尾巴加在一起，也不比我们的厄兰岛宽多少（即不足16公里）……它栖息在海底，周身始终环绕着无数小鱼，这些小鱼既是它的食物，也反过来受它喂养：因为它的进食——如果我记得E. 蓬托皮丹的记载没错的话——持续时间不超过三个月，之后又需要三个月来消化。它的排泄物随后滋养了一大群小鱼，因此渔夫们会探测它的栖息之处……渐渐地，克拉肯升到海面，当它在十到十二英寻深时，船只最好撤离其附近，因为不久之后它便会破水而出，像一座浮动的岛屿，从它那可怕的鼻孔中喷出水流，掀起环状的巨浪，能够波及数英里之远。谁能怀疑这就是约伯记中的利维坦呢？\" -Jacob Wallenberg, \"Min son på galejan\". 1781.","<small abomination>":"<small abomination>","“Freilich verbürgt uns keine Silbe die Existenz von solcherlei Thieren, wenn wir uns den Drachen oder Lindwurm als ein Ungeheuer vorstellen, dessen langer Hals in einen Adler-, Löwen- oder Delphinenkopf endigt; das auf dem breiten Rücken Greifs- oder Nachisittige trägt; und am vielfach gerollten Schweif einen Stachel mit Widerhaken hat; Feuer speit; sich in Mädchen verliebt und diese entführt; bald diese bald jene Gestalt annimmt; auf sauer erworbenen Schatzen ruht — kurz, als ein Ungeheuer, das alle Eigenschaften besitzt, welche die Fabel ihm andichtet; dann wäre es Wahnsinn, an Drachen und Lindwürmer glauben zu wollen. Nehmen wir aber dafür bloß ein furchtbares Ungeheuer überhaupt, welches nun aus unserem Welttheile vertilgt ist, so hat der Glaube daran nichts Lächerliches.” -Leopold Ziegelhauſer, _Schattenbilder der Vorzeit: Ein Kranz von Geschichten, Sagen, Legenden, Märchen, Skizzen und Heldenmahlen, Aus allen Gegenden Deutschlands und des österreichischen Kaiserstaates_. 1844.":"\"当然，若我们将龙或林德虫想象为这样一种怪兽——它长长的脖颈末端长着鹰头、狮头或海豚头；宽阔的背上长着狮鹫或纳希翼；在层层盘卷的尾巴上长着带倒钩的毒刺；口吐火焰；爱上少女并将她们掳走；时而化作这种形态，时而变作那种；盘踞在辛苦积攒的财宝之上——简而言之，若将其想象为一头拥有寓言赋予它的一切特征的怪兽，那么相信龙和林德虫便是疯狂的。但若我们仅仅将它视为一种可怕的、如今已从我们大陆上灭绝的怪兽，那么对它存在的信念便毫无可笑之处。\" -Leopold Ziegelhauſer, _Schattenbilder der Vorzeit: Ein Kranz von Geschichten, Sagen, Legenden, Märchen, Skizzen und Heldenmahlen, Aus allen Gegenden Deutschlands und des österreichischen Kaiserstaates_. 1844.","“She walks in the twilight, her steps make no sound, Her feet leave no tracks on the dew-covered ground. Her hand gently beckons, she whispers your name— But those who go with her are never the same.” -Magic: the Gathering":"\"她在暮光中行走，脚步悄无声息， 她的脚在露水覆盖的地上不留痕迹。 她轻轻招手，低唤你的名字—— 但那些跟她而去的人从此不再一样。\" -Magic: the Gathering","“Ctesias writeth, that in Aethiopia likewise there is a beast which he calleth Mantichora, having three rankes of teeth, which when they meet togither are let in one within another like the teeth of combes: with the face and eares of a man, with red eyes; of colour sanguine, bodied like a lyon, and having a taile armed with a sting like a scorpion: his voice resembleth the noise of a flute and trumpet sounded together: very swift he is, and mans flesh of all others hee most desireth.” -Pliny the Elder, _Natural History_, Book 8, Chapter XXI":"\"克特西亚斯记载说，在埃塞俄比亚还有一种野兽，他称之为曼提科拉，生有三排牙齿，合拢时彼此相错如同梳齿；长着人的脸和耳朵，眼睛赤红；肤色血红；身躯似狮；尾巴上长着一根蝎子般的毒刺；其声音如同笛与号同时吹奏；它极为敏捷，而一切肉食中它最渴望人肉。\" -Pliny the Elder, _Natural History_, Book 8, Chapter XXI","“And Heaven came, bringing on night and longing for love, and he lay about Earth spreading himself full upon her. Then the son from his ambush stretched forth his left hand and in his right took the great long sickle with jagged teeth, and swiftly lopped off his own father's members and cast them away to fall behind him. And not vainly did they fall from his hand; for all the bloody drops that gushed forth Earth received, and as the seasons moved round she bare the strong Erinyes and the great Giants with gleaming armour, holding long spears in their hands, and the Nymphs whom they call Meliae all over the boundless earth.” -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 182-187, trans. H.G. Evelyn-White. 1920":"\"天神来了，带来了黑夜，渴望着爱情，他躺在大地身上，将自己完全铺展在她身上。于是那儿子从埋伏之处伸出了左手，右手拿起那把带有锯齿的巨大的长镰刀，迅速割下了他父亲的下体，将它们扔在身后。它们没有徒然地从他手中落下；大地承接了所有喷涌而出的血滴，随着季节流转，她生下了强大的厄里倪厄斯，和穿着闪亮铠甲、手持长矛的巨大巨人，以及那些在整个无边大地上被称作墨利埃的宁芙们。\" -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 182-187, trans. H.G. Evelyn-White. 1920","“Again at length my thought reviving came, When I no longer found my self the same; Then first this sea-green beard I felt to grow, And these large honours on my spreading brow; My long-descending locks the billows sweep, And my broad shoulders cleave the yielding deep; My fishy tail, my arms of azure hue, And ev'ry part divinely chang'd, I view.” -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XIII, 546-7. 8 A.D. trans. Garth, Dryden, et al.":"\"终于我的思绪渐渐复苏， 当我发现自己已不再是原来模样； 首先我感到这海绿色的胡须开始生长， 这两鬓也获得了这宽大的殊荣； 我长长的发绺在波浪中飘拂， 我宽阔的肩膀划开柔软的深海； 我鱼形的尾巴，我蔚蓝的双臂， 每一部分都已神圣地改变，我都看在眼里。\" -Ovid, _Metamorphoses_, XIII, 546-7. 8 A.D. trans. Garth, Dryden, et al.","“Lord, Lord! methought, what pain it was to drown! What dreadful noise of waters in mine ears! What ugly sights of death within mine eyes! Methought I saw a thousand fearful wrecks, Ten thousand men that fishes gnawed upon, Wedges of gold, great anchors, heaps of pearl, Inestimable stones, unvalued jewels, All scattered in the bottom of the sea: Some lay in dead men’s skulls; and in those holes Where eyes did once inhabit, there were crept, As ’t were in scorn of eyes, reflecting gems.” -William Shakespeare, _King Richard III_, I, iv. 1597":"\"主啊，主啊！我想，溺水是多么痛苦啊！ 耳中听到的是多么可怕的水声！ 眼前看到的是多么丑陋的死亡景象！ 我想我看见了上千艘可怕的沉船， 上万个被鱼啃食的人， 大块的金锭，巨大的铁锚，成堆的珍珠， 无价的宝石，无法估量的珠玉， 全都散落在海底： 有些躺在死人头骨里；而在那些 曾是眼睛栖居的窟窿中， 仿佛是对眼睛的嘲弄，嵌着反光的宝石。\" -William Shakespeare, _King Richard III_, I, iv. 1597","“Then up it raise the mermaiden, Wi the comb an glass in her hand: ‘Here's a health to you, my merrie young men, For you never will see dry land.’” -“Sir Patrick Spens”, Scottish folk song, version 58J in Francis James Child, _The English and Scottish Popular Ballads_. 1898.":"\"于是美人鱼从海中升起， 手中拿着梳子和镜子： '敬你们一杯，我快乐的年轻人们， 因为你们再也见不到陆地了。'\" -\"Sir Patrick Spens\", Scottish folk song, version 58J in Francis James Child, _The English and Scottish Popular Ballads_. 1898.","“Damn ye! Let Neptune strike ye dead, Winslow! HAAARK! Hark Triton, hark! Bellow, bid our father the Sea King rise from the depths full foul in his fury! Black waves teeming with salt-foam to smother this young mouth with pungent slime, to choke ye, engorging your organs ‘til ye turn blue and bloated with bilge and brine and can scream no more -- only when he, crowned in cockle shells with slitherin’ tentacled tail and steaming beard take up his fell be-finnéd arm, his coral-tine trident screeches banshee-like in the tempest and plunges right through yer gullet, bursting ye -- a bulging bladder no more, but a blasted bloody film now -- a nothing for the harpies and the souls of dead sailors to peck and claw and feed upon, only to be lapped up and swallowed by the infinite waters of the dread emperor himself -- forgotten to any man, to any time, forgotten to any god or devil, forgotten even to the sea, for any stuff or part of Winslow, even any scantling of your soul is Winslow no more, but is now itself the sea!” -Thomas Wake, _The Lighthouse_. 2019":"\"该死的！让尼普顿劈死你，温斯洛！听啊！听啊，特里同，听啊！咆哮吧，叫我们的父海王从深渊中升起，满怀着狂暴的愤怒！黑色的巨浪翻腾着盐沫，用辛辣的黏液窒息这张年轻的嘴，噎死你，塞满你的器官直到你发青浮肿，被舱底污水和盐水填满，再也不能尖叫——只等他头戴蛤壳冠，拖着黏滑蜿蜒的触手尾和冒着热气的胡须，举起他那可怕的生着鱼鳍的手臂，他那珊瑚齿的三叉戟在风暴中发出女妖般的尖啸，径直刺穿你的喉咙，将你爆开——不再是一团鼓胀的水泡，而是一层爆碎的血色薄膜——一滩虚无，供哈尔庇厄和死去水手的幽灵啄食、抓挠、吞食，最终被那可畏的帝王本人的无尽海水舔食吞咽——从此被所有人遗忘，被所有时间遗忘，被任何神祇或魔鬼遗忘，甚至被大海遗忘，因为温斯洛的任何部分、任何碎片，你灵魂的任何碎屑都不再是温斯洛，而是此刻已然成为大海！\" -Thomas Wake, _The Lighthouse_. 2019","<merfolk>":"<merfolk>","“Row'd on, in reach of an erected voice, The Sirens soon took note, without our noise, Tuned those sweet accents that made charms so strong, And these learn'd numbers made the Sirens' song: ‘Come here, thou worthy of a world of praise, That dost so high the Grecian glory raise, Ulysses! stay thy ship, and that song hear That none past ever but it bent his ear, But left him ravish'd, and instructed more By us, than any ever heard before. For we know all things whatsoever were In wide Troy labour'd; whatsoever there The Grecians and the Trojans both sustain'd By those high issues that the Gods ordain'd. And whatsoever all the earth can show T' inform a knowledge of desert, we know.’” -Homer, _The Odyssey_, XII, 268-82. trans. George Chapman, 1857.":"\"我们继续划行，进入那高扬歌声所及之处； 塞壬很快察觉了我们，我们却未发出声响。 她们调好甜美的音调，施下强烈魔力， 用这些精妙诗句唱起塞壬之歌： '来吧，尤利西斯，举世赞颂的英雄， 是你将希腊的荣耀高高托起！ 停下船来，听听这支歌吧； 从未有人经过此地而不侧耳倾听， 也无人不心醉神驰地离开， 从我们这里获知前所未闻的更多见识。 特洛伊广袤土地上发生的一切， 希腊人与特洛伊人依诸神旨意 在那里承受的一切，我们无不知晓。 凡大地所能展现、足以增长 人对世间功业的见识，我们尽皆知晓。'\" -Homer, _The Odyssey_, XII, 268-82. trans. George Chapman, 1857.","<war gargoyle>":"<war gargoyle>","“When within sight of their foe Berserks wrought themselves into such a state of frenzy, that they bit their shields and rushed forward to the attack, throwing away their arms of defence, reckless of every danger, sometimes having nothing but a club, which carried with it death and destruction.” -Paul Belloni Du Chaillu,_The Viking Age: the Early History, Manners, and Customs of the Ancestors of the English Speaking Nations_. 1889.":"\"当狂战士望见敌人时，便使自己陷入狂怒状态，甚至啃咬自己的盾牌，向前猛冲发动攻击，丢弃防御的武器，不顾一切危险，有时仅持一根大棒，却带来死亡与毁灭。\" -Paul Belloni Du Chaillu,_The Viking Age: the Early History, Manners, and Customs of the Ancestors of the English Speaking Nations_. 1889.","“I see Egypt and the Egyptians — I see the pyramids and obelisks; I look on chisel'd histories, songs, philosophies, cut in slabs of sand-stone, or on granite-blocks; I see at Memphis mummy-pits, containing mummies, embalm'd, swathed in linen cloth, lying there many centuries; I look on the fall'n Theban, the large-ball'd eyes, the side-drooping neck, the hands folded across the breast.” -Walt Whitman, “Salut au Monde”":"\"我看见埃及和埃及人——我看见金字塔和方尖碑； 我看见刻在沙石板、或花岗岩块上的 凿刻的历史、歌谣、哲思； 我在孟菲斯看见木乃伊坑，里面有木乃伊，涂抹了防腐香料， 裹着亚麻布，在那里躺了许多世纪； 我望着倒下的底比斯人，圆睁的眼球，歪斜的脖颈， 双手交叉在胸前。\" -Walt Whitman, \"Salut au Monde\"","“Amongst the deities and Asuras and celestial Rishis, O amiable lady, the Nagas are endued with great energy. Possessed of great speed, they are endued again with excellent fragrance. They deserve to be worshipped. They are capable of granting boons. Indeed, we too deserve to be followed by others in our train. I tell thee, O lady, that we are incapable of being seen by human beings.” -Mahābhārata, Santi Parva, Mokshadharma Parva, section CCCLX. ca. 500 B.C. trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.":"\"在天神、阿修罗和天仙之中，可爱的女士啊，纳迦被赋予了巨大的能量。他们拥有极快的速度，又被赋予了极佳的芬芳。他们值得被崇拜。他们能够赐予恩惠。确实，我们也值得被别人追随左右。我告诉你，女士啊，人类是无法看见我们的。\" -Mahābhārata, Santi Parva, Mokshadharma Parva, section CCCLX. ca. 500 B.C. trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.","<naga>":"<naga>","“Then there have also come nagas from Lake Nabhasa, Vesali, and Tacchaka. Kambalas, Assataras, Payagas, and their kin. And from the River Yamuna comes the prestigious naga, Dhatarattha. The great naga Eravanna: He, too, has come to the forest meeting.” -Mahasamaya Sutta, _Dīgha Nikāya_, 20. ca. 500 B.C. trans. Thanissaro Bhikkhu":"\"还有来自纳巴沙湖的 纳迦们， 维萨利，和塔克查卡。 坎巴拉斯，阿萨塔拉斯， 帕亚加斯，以及他们的亲族。 还有来自阎牟那河的 尊贵的纳迦，达塔拉特哈。 伟大的纳迦埃拉凡纳： 他，也来了， 来到这林中盛会。\" -Mahasamaya Sutta, _Dīgha Nikāya_, 20. ca. 500 B.C. trans. Thanissaro Bhikkhu","“Then the sallow oval between Ged's arms grew bright. It widened and spread, a rent in the darkness of the earth and night, a ripping open of the fabric of the world. Through it blazed a terrible brightness. And through that bright misshapen breach clambered something like a clot of black shadow, quick and hideous, and it leaped straight out at Ged's face.” -Ursula K. Le Guin, _A Wizard Of Earthsea_. 1968.":"\"然后，格得双臂之间那片灰黄的椭圆变得明亮起来。它扩大、延展，成了大地与黑夜的黑暗中一道裂口，撕裂了世界的织体。从中迸射出一道可怕的光芒。而通过那道明亮的、畸形的裂缝，有什么东西攀爬了出来，像一团黑色的阴影凝块，迅捷而丑恶，径直扑向格得的面孔。\" -Ursula K. Le Guin, _A Wizard Of Earthsea_. 1968.","“Even now the intensity of his dread power can be felt Weakening the body and saddening the heart Ultimately they will become empty, mindless spectres Stripped of will and soul Only their thirst for freedom Gives them hunger for vengeance...” -Rush, “The Necromancer”. 1975.":"\"即使此刻，他那可怖力量的强度仍能被感知到 削弱着身体，使心灵哀伤 最终他们将化为空洞的、无意识的幽灵 被剥夺了意志和灵魂 只有他们对自由的渴望 赋予他们复仇的饥渴……\" -Rush, \"The Necromancer\". 1975.","“Humans, eh? Think they’re lords of creation. Not like us cats. We _know_ we are. Ever see a cat feed a human? Case proven.” -Terry Pratchett, “The Amazing Maurice and His Educated Rodents”. 2001.":"\"人类，是吧？以为自己是万物之灵。不像我们猫。我们_知道_我们是。见过猫喂人吗？证毕。\" -Terry Pratchett, \"The Amazing Maurice and His Educated Rodents\". 2001.","“If thus mutation is influenced by natural selection, it implies, that any particular mutation must advance in a direction advantageous for the respective species, and, indeed, many examples of mutation known among fossil animals are apparently due to the advantage produced by the change. I must add here, however that probably not all mutations (in a palaeontological meaning) are due to natural selection, but that many do not imply an actual improvement.” -_Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society_, Volume XXV, no. 150. 1896.":"\"如果突变因此受自然选择的影响，这就意味着任何特定的突变必然朝着对相应物种有利的方向进展；而实际上，化石动物中已知的许多突变例子，显然都是由于这种变化带来的优势所致。然而，我必须在此补充说明，并非所有的突变（就古生物学的意义而言）都归因于自然选择，许多突变并不意味着实际的改良。\" -_Proceedings of the American Philosophical Society_, Volume XXV, no. 150. 1896.","“Each family or tribe has a wizard or conjuring doctor, whose office we could never clearly ascertain.” -Charles Darwin, _The Voyage of the Beagle_, ch. X. 1839.":"\"每个家族或部落都有一位巫师或行咒医者，其职能我们始终 未能确切查明。\" -查尔斯·达尔文，《小猎犬号航海记》，第十章。1839年。","“In their brief time together Slothrop forms the impression that this octopus is not in good mental health, though where's his basis for comparing? But there is a mad exhuberance, as with inanimate objects which fall off of tables when we are sensitive to noise and our own clumsiness and don't want them to fall, a sort of wham! ha-ha you hear that? here it is again, WHAM! in the cephalopod's every movement, which Slothrop is glad to get away from as he finally scales the crab like a discus, with all his strength, out to sea, and the octopus, with an eager splash and gurgle, strikes out in pursuit, and is presently gone.” -Thomas Pynchon, _Gravity's Rainbow_. 1973.":"\"在他们短暂的相处中，斯洛思罗普形成的印象是这只章鱼 精神健康状况不佳——尽管他有什么比较的依据呢？但这种 软体动物的每一个动作中都有一种疯狂的亢奋，就像当我们 对噪音和自己的笨拙格外敏感、不希望东西掉落时，那些 无生命的物体偏偏从桌上掉下来——一种'砰！哈哈你听到 了吗？又来了，砰！'的感觉——斯洛思罗普终于像掷铁饼 一样用尽全身力气把螃蟹抛向大海，得以脱身；而那只章鱼 则急切地溅起水花、咕噜作响，紧追不舍，随即消失不见。\" -托马斯·品钦，《万有引力之虹》。1973年。","“The little princess, asleep in her cradle, floated on the water, and at last she was cast up on the shore of a beautiful country, where, however, very few people dwelt since the ogre Ravagio and his wife Tourmentine had gone to live there-for they ate up everybody. Ogres are terrible people. When once they have tasted raw human flesh they will hardly eat anything else, and Tourmentine always knew how to make some body come their way, for she was half a fairy.” -Marie-Catherine Le Jumel de Barneville, Baronne d'Aulnoy, “'Orangier et l'Abeille”. 1697.":"\"小公主在摇篮中沉睡，漂浮在水面上，最终被冲上了一片 美丽国度的海岸。然而，那里几乎无人居住，因为食人魔 拉瓦乔和他的妻子图尔芒蒂娜搬到那里去了——他们把 所有人都吃掉了。食人魔是可怕的生物。一旦尝过生人肉， 他们几乎就不愿再吃别的东西了；而图尔芒蒂娜总有办法 让人送上门来，因为她有一半仙女的血液。\" -玛丽-卡特琳·勒朱梅尔·德·巴纳维尔，奥努瓦男爵夫人， 《橙子树与蜜蜂》。1697年。","“NO. Layers. Onions have layers. Ogres have layers. Onions have layers. You get it? We both have layers.” -Shrek. 2001.":"\"不。层次。洋葱有层次。食人魔也有层次。洋葱有层次。 懂了吗？我们都有层次。\" -史莱克。2001年。","“The little princess, asleep in her cradle, floated on the water, and at last she was cast up on the shore of a beautiful country, where, however, very few people dwelt since the ogre Ravagio and his wife Tourmentine had gone to live there-for they ate up everybody. Ogres are terrible people. When once they have tasted raw human flesh they will hardly eat anything else, and Tourmentine always knew how to make some body come their way, for she was half a fairy.” -Marie-Catherine Le Jumel de Barneville, Baronne d'Aulnoy, “'Orangier et l'Abeille”. 1697. “NO. Layers. Onions have layers. Ogres have layers. Onions have layers. You get it? We both have layers.” -Shrek. 2001.":"\"小公主在摇篮中沉睡，漂浮在水面上，最终被冲上了一片 美丽国度的海岸。然而，那里几乎无人居住，因为食人魔 拉瓦乔和他的妻子图尔芒蒂娜搬到那里去了——他们把 所有人都吃掉了。食人魔是可怕的生物。一旦尝过生人肉， 他们几乎就不愿再吃别的东西了；而图尔芒蒂娜总有办法 让人送上门来，因为她有一半仙女的血液。\" -玛丽-卡特琳·勒朱梅尔·德·巴纳维尔，奥努瓦男爵夫人， 《橙子树与蜜蜂》。1697年。 \"不。层次。洋葱有层次。食人魔也有层次。洋葱有层次。 懂了吗？我们都有层次。\" -史莱克。2001年。","<ogre>":"<ogre>","“Carbonic acid is one of the three materials which together form the starting point of vegetable growth; the others being water and nitric acid. This acid is formed of carbon and oxygen in the proportion of one part of the former to two of the latter chemically combined. It is a colorless gas, having an acid taste and smell; is soluble in water; weighs one-half more than air and can be poured from one vessel to another, as a liquid may be; 100 parts of water dissolve 106 parts of this gas, and it is from this source that the roots of plants derive the needed supplies of it.” -Henry Stuart, _The Culture of Farm Crops: A Manual of the Science of Agriculture, and a Hand-book of Practice for American Farmers_, ch X. 1887.":"\"碳酸是构成植物生长起点的三种材料之一，另外两种是水 和硝酸。这种酸由碳和氧按一比二的比例化合而成。它是 一种无色气体，具有酸味和酸臭；可溶于水；比空气重 一半，可以像液体一样从一个容器倒入另一个容器；一百 份水可溶解一百零六份这种气体，植物的根系正是由此 获得所需的供应。\" -亨利·斯图尔特，《农作物的栽培：农业科学手册与美国 农民实用指南》，第十章。1887年。","<oklob plant>":"<oklob plant>","“The popularity and longevity of the oni myth is no doubt partially based on the beings’ conventional demonic accoutrements, which have remained relatively constant through the ages: they are dreadful super-natural beings emerging from the abyss of Buddhist hell to terrify wicked mortals; their grotesque and savage demeanor and form instill instant fear; and the oni’s omnipresence in the socio-historical and cultural archive of Japan is directly attributable to the moral, social, and religious edification that stories about oni engender.” -Noriko T. Reider, _Japanese Demon Lore: Oni from Ancient Times to the Present_, ch. 1, 2010.":"\"鬼神话的流行与经久不衰，无疑部分基于这些生物一贯的 恶魔特征——这些特征历经岁月而相对恒定：它们是从佛教 地狱深渊中涌现的可怕超自然存在，来恐吓邪恶的凡人； 它们怪异而凶残的举止和外形令人瞬间生畏；而鬼在日本 社会历史与文化档案中的无所不在，则直接归因于鬼的故事 所产生的道德、社会和宗教教化作用。\" -诺里科·T·赖德，《日本恶魔传说：从古至今的鬼》， 第一章，2010年。","“As I looked at the living creatures, I saw a wheel on the ground beside each creature with its four faces. This was the appearance and structure of the wheels: They sparkled like chrysolite, and all four looked alike. Each appeared to be made like a wheel intersecting a wheel. As they moved, they would go in any one of the four directions the creatures faced; the wheels did not turn about as the creatures went. Their rims were high and awesome, and all four rims were full of eyes all around.” -Ezekiel 1:15-18 (New International Version)":"\"我观看活物的时候，见活物的脸旁，各有一轮在地上。 轮的形状和构造，好像苍翠的水苍玉。四轮都是一个样式， 形状和构造，好像轮中套轮。轮行走的时候，向四方都能 直行，并不掉转。至于轮辋，高而可畏；四个轮辋周围 满有眼睛。\" -以西结书 1:15-18（和合本）","“In Sparkill buried lies that man of mark Who brought the Obelisk to Central Park, Redoubtable Commander H.H. Gorringe, Whose name supplies the long-sought rhyme for ‘orange.’” -Arthur Guiterman, “Local Note”. 1934.":"\"斯帕基尔埋葬着那位显赫之人 他将方尖碑带到了中央公园， 可畏的指挥官H.H.戈林奇， 他的名字提供了苦苦寻觅的'orange'之韵脚。\" -阿瑟·吉特曼，《本地纪事》。1934年。","“X gon' give it to ya (what) Fuck waitin' for you to get it on your own, X gon' deliver to ya Knock knock, open up the door, it's real With the non-stop pop-pop from stainless steel [...] First we gonna rock, then we gonna roll Then we let it pop, go, let it go X gon' give it to ya, he gon' give it to ya X gon' give it to ya, he gon' give it to ya -DMX, “X Gon' Give It To Ya”. 2002":"\"X gon' give it to ya（啥） 才不等你自己搞定，X gon' deliver to ya 咚咚，开门，来真的了 不锈钢连发的啪啪声不停 ［……］ 先摇起来，再滚起来 然后让它炸开，走，放手干 X gon' give it to ya，他 gonna give it to ya X gon' give it to ya，他 gonna give it to ya\" -DMX，《X Gon' Give It To Ya》。2002年。","“There 's not the smallest orb which thou behold'st But in his motion like an angel sings, Still quiring to the young-eyed cherubins.” -William Shakespeare, _The Merchant of Venice_, V, i. 1597.":"\"你所看见的每一颗微小的天球， 在运转时无不发出天使般的歌声， 永远应和着明眸的天使们的合唱。\" -威廉·莎士比亚，《威尼斯商人》，第五幕第一场。1597年。","“Mean while the winged heralds by command Of Sovran power, with awful Ceremony And Trumpets sound throughout the Host proclaim A solemn Councel forthwith to be held At Pandaemonium, the high Capital Of Satan and his Peers...” -John Milton, _Paradise Lost_, Book I, 1667.":"\"与此同时，奉至上大能的谕令， 插翅使者们以威严的仪式 和响彻全军的号角之声宣告 即刻在撒旦及其群臣的巍峨都城—— 万魔殿——召开庄严会议……\" -约翰·弥尔顿，《失乐园》，第一卷，1667年。","“Who wondrous things concerning our welfare, And straunge phantomes doth lett us ofte foresee.” -Spenser, _The Faerie Queene_ II. xii. 47":"\"关于我们的福祉，有奇妙之事， 令我们时常预见那奇异的幻影。\" -斯宾塞，《仙后》第二卷第十二章第47节。","“Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven; And he overthrew those cities, and all the plain, and all the inhabitants of the cities, and that which grew upon the ground. But [Lot's] wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.” -KJV Bible, Genesis 19:24-26.":"\"当时，耶和华将硫磺与火，从天上耶和华那里，降与所多玛 和蛾摩拉，把那些城和全平原，并城里所有的居民，连地上 生长的都毁灭了。罗得的妻子在后边回头一看，就变成了一根 盐柱。\" -和合本圣经，创世记 19:24-26。","“Know thyself.” -Inscription in the pronaos of the Temple of Apollo at Delphi":"\"认识你自己。\" -德尔斐阿波罗神庙前殿铭文。","“The Polar Bear is an animal of tremendous strength and fierceness. Barentz, in his voyage in search of a north-east passage to China, had proofs of the ferocity of these animals, in the island of Nova Zembla, where they attacked his seamen, seizing them in their mouths; carrying them off with the utmost ease, and devouring them in the sight of their comrades. It is said that they will attack and attempt to board armed vessels, at a great distance from shore, and have sometimes been with much difficulty repelled.” -George Shaw, _General Zoology, or, Systematic Natural History_, vol. I, p. 2. 1800.":"\"北极熊是一种力量和凶猛都极为惊人的动物。巴伦支在寻找 通往中国的东北航道的航行中，在新地岛上亲历了这些动物 的残暴：它们袭击他的船员，用嘴叼住他们，轻而易举地将 他们拖走，在同伴的注视下将他们吞噬。据说它们会攻击并 试图登上远离海岸的武装船只，有时极难将其击退。\" -乔治·肖，《普通动物学，或称系统自然史》，第一卷， 第2页。1800年。","“A spell was cast and the sky turned red The angel's heart froze to ice In the gloomy sky black clouds were gathering The silence was broken by cries A spell was cast and the sky turned red The angel's heart froze to ice In the gloomy sky — The silence where dead angels lie":"\"咒语被施下，天空变红 天使的心冻结成冰 阴沉的天空聚集起黑云 寂静被哭喊打破 咒语被施下，天空变红 天使的心冻结成冰 在阴沉的天空下——死天使躺卧的寂静中","Touch the snow... Caress the lifeless sculptures Die!!!” -Dissection, “Where Dead Angels Lie”. 1996.":"触摸那雪……轻抚那无生命的雕塑 死！！！\" -Dissection，《死天使躺卧之处》。1996年。","“A spell was cast and the sky turned red The angel's heart froze to ice In the gloomy sky black clouds were gathering The silence was broken by cries A spell was cast and the sky turned red The angel's heart froze to ice In the gloomy sky — The silence where dead angels lie Touch the snow... Caress the lifeless sculptures Die!!!” -Dissection, “Where Dead Angels Lie”. 1996.":"\"咒语被施下，天空变红 天使的心冻结成冰 阴沉的天空聚集起黑云 寂静被哭喊打破 咒语被施下，天空变红 天使的心冻结成冰 在阴沉的天空下——死天使躺卧的寂静中 触摸那雪……轻抚那无生命的雕塑 死！！！\" -Dissection，《死天使躺卧之处》。1996年。","“If builders built buildings the way programmers wrote programs, then the first woodpecker that came along would destroy civilization.” -Gerald Weinberg, Weinberg's Second Law":"\"如果建筑师像程序员写程序那样盖楼，那么第一只啄木鸟 飞来就会毁灭整个文明。\" -杰拉尔德·温伯格，温伯格第二定律。","“I call upon Proteus, key-holding master of the sea, first-born, who showed the beginnings of all nature, changing matter into a great variety of forms. Honored by all, he is wise, and he knows what is now, what was before, and what will be in the future. He has all at his disposal, transformed far beyond all other immortals who dwell on snowy Olympos and fly through the air and over land and sea, for Physis was the first to place everything in Proteus. Father, attended by holy providence, visit the mystic initiates, and bring a good end to a life of industry and prosperity.” -_The Orphic Hymns_, XXV. trans. Apostolos N. Athanassakis and Benjamin M. Wolkow, 2013.":"\"我呼唤普罗透斯， 执掌钥匙的沧海之主， 首生之神，他揭示了 万物的起源， 将物质变换为 千姿百态。 受万有敬仰，他通晓智慧， 知道现在之事， 过去之事， 以及未来之事。 他掌管一切， 其变化远超 栖居于白雪皑皑的奥林匹斯、 翱翔于天空、 跨越大地与海洋的 所有不朽者， 因为菲西斯最先 将万物置于普罗透斯之中。 父神啊，在神圣天命的随侍下， 请降临于秘仪的信徒， 为勤劳富足的一生 带来善终。\" -《俄耳甫斯赞美诗》，第二十五首。 阿波斯托洛斯·N·阿萨纳萨基斯与本杰明·M·沃尔科夫英译，2013年。","“Vaisampayana said, 'Not far from the place where the Pandavas were asleep, a Rakshasa by name Hidimva dwelt on the Sala tree. Possessed of great energy and prowess, he was a cruel cannibal of visage that was grim in consequence of his sharp and long teeth. He was now hungry and longing for human flesh. Of long shanks and a large belly, his locks and beard were both red in hue. His shoulders were broad like the neck of a tree; his ears were like unto arrows, and his features were frightful.” -_Mahābhārata_, Adi Parva, Hidimva-vadha Parva, section CLIV. ca. 500 B.C. trans. Kisari Mohan Ganguli, 1883.":"\"毗舍波衍那说：'离般度族安睡之地不远，有一个名叫希丁巴的 罗刹栖居在娑罗树上。他力大无比，勇猛非凡，是个残忍的 食人者，因牙齿尖长而面目狰狞。此刻他饥肠辘辘，渴望 人肉。他腿长腹大，须发皆为赤红。双肩宽阔如树干；双耳 如箭簇，容貌可怖。'\" -《摩诃婆罗多》，初篇，希丁巴伏诛篇，第一百五十四章。 约公元前500年。基萨里·莫汉·甘古利英译，1883年。","“All our times have come. Here but now they're gone. Seasons don't fear the reaper, Nor do the wind, the sun or the rain. We can be like they are. Come on baby, don't fear the reaper.” -Buck Dharma, Blue Öyster Cult, “(Don't Fear) The Reaper”. 1976.":"\"我们的时光都到了。 方才还在，而今已逝。 四季不畏惧死神， 风、太阳和雨也一样。 我们可以像它们那样。 来吧宝贝，别畏惧死神。\" -巴克·达摩，Blue Öyster Cult，《（别畏惧）死神》。1976年。","“While the angels, all pallid and wan, Uprising, unveiling, affirm That the play is the tragedy, ‘Man’, And its hero, the Conqueror Worm.” -Edgar Allan Poe":"\"天使们，全都苍白而憔悴， 站起身来，揭开面纱，断言 这出戏是悲剧，名为'人'， 而主角则是那征服者蠕虫。\" -埃德加·爱伦·坡。","<mummy>":"<mummy>","“As for example: the Salamander made in fashion of a Lizard, marked with spots like to stars, never comes abroad and sheweth it selfe but in great showers; for in faire weather he is not seene. He is of so cold a complexion, that if hee do but touch the fire, hee wil quench it as presently, as if yce were put into it. The Salamander casteth up at the mouth a certaine venomous matter like unto milke, let it but once touch any bare part of a man or womans bodie, all the haire will fall off: and the part so touched will change the colour of the skin to the white morphew.” -Gaius Plinius Secundus, _Naturalis Historia_, Book X, ch. LXVII. 79 A.D. trans. Philemon Holland, 1601.":"\"例如：沙罗曼达形似蜥蜴，遍体斑点如星，从不外出， 只在暴雨中现身；因为晴朗天气里是见不到它的。其性 至寒，若触火，则火即灭，犹如投冰入火。沙罗曼达口中 吐出一种如奶的毒液，一旦触及男女身体任何裸露之处， 毛发尽落；被触之处肤色变为白斑。\" -盖乌斯·普林尼乌斯·塞昆杜斯，《自然史》，第十卷， 第六十七章。公元79年。菲莱蒙·霍兰德英译，1601年。","“Those poisonous fields, with rank luxuriance crown'd, Where the dark scorpion gathers death around” -Oliver Goldsmith, “The Deserted Village”, l. 351-2. 1770.":"\"那片毒野，被茂盛的杂草所覆盖， 黑暗的蝎子在那里聚集死亡。\" -奥利弗·戈德史密斯，《荒村》，第351-352行。1770年。","“In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the LORD sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.":"\"当乌西雅王崩的那年，我见主坐在高高的宝座上。他的衣裳 垂下，遮满圣殿。","Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.":"其上有撒拉弗侍立，各有六个翅膀：用两个翅膀遮脸，两个 翅膀遮脚，两个翅膀飞翔。","And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.” -KJV Bible, Isaiah 6:1-3.":"彼此呼喊说：圣哉！圣哉！圣哉！万军之耶和华，他的荣光 充满全地！\" -和合本圣经，以赛亚书 6:1-3。","“In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the LORD sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple. Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly. And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.” -KJV Bible, Isaiah 6:1-3.":"\"当乌西雅王崩的那年，我见主坐在高高的宝座上。他的衣裳 垂下，遮满圣殿。 其上有撒拉弗侍立，各有六个翅膀：用两个翅膀遮脸，两个 翅膀遮脚，两个翅膀飞翔。 彼此呼喊说：圣哉！圣哉！圣哉！万军之耶和华，他的荣光 充满全地！\" -和合本圣经，以赛亚书 6:1-3。","“Between the idea And the reality Between the motion And the act Falls the Shadow For thine is the Kingdom":"\"在观念 与现实之间 在行动 与动作之间 落下阴影 因为国度是你的","Between the conception And the creation Between the emotion And the response Falls the Shadow Life is very long” -T.S. Eliot, “The Hollow Men”. 1925.":"在概念 与创造之间 在情感 与回应之间 落下阴影 生命如此漫长\" -T.S.艾略特，《空心人》。1925年。","“Between the idea And the reality Between the motion And the act Falls the Shadow For thine is the Kingdom Between the conception And the creation Between the emotion And the response Falls the Shadow Life is very long” -T.S. Eliot, “The Hollow Men”. 1925.":"\"在观念 与现实之间 在行动 与动作之间 落下阴影 因为国度是你的 在概念 与创造之间 在情感 与回应之间 落下阴影 生命如此漫长\" -T.S.艾略特，《空心人》。1925年。","“As we grow old, we become aware that death is drawing near; his shadow falls across our path...” -Stefan Zweig, _Twenty-Four Hours in the Life of a Woman_. 1927.":"\"当我们渐渐老去，我们意识到死亡正在临近；他的影子落在 我们路途之上……\" -斯蒂芬·茨威格，《一个女人一生中的二十四小时》。1927年。","“Crux sacra sit mihi lux / Non draco sit mihi dux Vade retro satana / Numquam suade mihi vana Sunt mala quae libas / Ipse venena bibas [Let the Holy Cross be my light / Let not the dragon be my guide Step back Satan / Never tempt me with vain things What you offer me is evil / You drink the poison yourself.]” -Full text of initials on the Saint Benedict Medal, worn to ward off evil spirits. Inscription from 11-15th century, formally approved by Pope Benedict XIV in 18th century.":"\"愿圣十字架作我的光明 / 愿龙不作我的向导 撒旦退去吧 / 永勿以虚妄引诱我 你所献的是邪恶 / 你自饮那毒药吧。\" -圣本笃圣牌上的铭文全文，用以驱邪。铭文可追溯至11至 15世纪，18世纪由教宗本笃十四世正式批准。","“Yesterday, upon the stair, I met a man who wasn't there He wasn't there again today I wish, I wish he'd go away...” -Hughes Mearns ,_Antigonish_, 1-4. 1899.":"\"昨天，在楼梯上， 我遇见一个不在那里的人 今天他又不在那里 我希望，我希望他能走开……\" -休斯·默恩斯，《安蒂戈尼什》，第1-4行。1899年。","“There is unrest in the forest There is trouble with the trees For the maples want more sunlight And the oaks ignore their pleas” -Rush, \"The Trees\". 1978.":"\"森林里有骚动 树木间有纷争 因为枫树想要更多阳光 而橡树无视它们的恳求\" -Rush，《树》。1978年。","“And then th' old Sea-God crept From forth the deeps, and found his fat calves there, Survey'd, and number'd, and came never near The craft we used, but told us five for calves. His temples then dis-eased with sleep he salves; And in rush'd we, with an abhorred cry, Cast all our hands about him manfully; And then th' old Forger all his forms began: First was a lion with a mighty mane, Then next a dragon, a pied panther then, A vast boar next, and suddenly did strain All into water. Last he was a tree, Curl'd all at top, and shot up to the sky.” -Homer, _The Odyssey_, IV, 602-14. trans. George Chapman, 1857.":"\"于是那古老的海神从深处 爬出，找到了他的肥牛犊， 审视、清点，却从未接近 我们设下的计谋，只当那是五头牛犊。 他用睡眠舒缓了自己的额角； 我们高喊可怖的呼号，一拥而上， 奋力用双手从四面八方抱住他； 于是那古老的变形者开始施展他所有的形态： 首先是一头鬃毛雄壮的狮子， 接着是一条龙，然后是一头斑豹， 然后是一头巨野猪，又骤然化作 一片流水。最后他变成一棵树， 树冠卷曲，直冲云霄。\" -荷马，《奥德赛》，第四卷，602-614行。 乔治·查普曼英译，1857年。","“There is a silence where hath been no sound, There is a silence where no sound may be,— In the cold grave, under the deep, deep sea, Or in the wide desert where no life is found.” -Thomas Hood, “Silence”. Early 19th cent.":"\"有一种寂静，那里从未有过声响， 有一种寂静，那里不可能有声响，—— 在冰冷的坟墓中，在深深的、深深的海底， 或在没有生命的辽阔荒漠里。\" -托马斯·胡德，《寂静》。19世纪初。","“The simulacrum now hides, not the truth, but the fact that there is none, that is to say, the continuation of Nothingness.” -Jean Baudrillard, “Radical Thought”. 1994. trans. François Debrix, 1995.":"\"拟像如今遮蔽的不是真理，而是真理并不存在这一事实， 也就是说，是虚无的延续。\" -让·鲍德里亚，《激进思想》。1994年。 弗朗索瓦·德布里英译，1995年。","“I saw a mouth jeering. A smile of melted red iron ran over it. Its laugh was full of nails rattling. It was a child's dream of a mouth. A fist hit the mouth: knuckles of gun-metal driven by an electric wrist and shoulder. It was a child's dream of an arm. The fist hit the mouth over and over, again and again. The mouth bled melted iron, and laughed its laughter of nails rattling. And I saw the more the fist pounded the more the mouth laughed. The fist is pounding and pounding, and the mouth answering.” -Carl Sandburg, “Gargoyle”, _Cornhusker_. 1918.":"\"我看到一张嘴在嘲讽。熔化的红铁般的笑容从上面掠过。它 的笑声满是钉子叮当碰撞。那是孩子梦中才会出现的嘴。 一只拳头击中了那张嘴：由电动的腕和肩驱动的炮铜指节。 那是孩子梦中才会出现的手臂。 拳头一次又一次、一遍又一遍地击打着那张嘴。嘴里流出 熔化的铁血，发出钉子叮当碰撞的笑声。 而我看到，拳头捶打得越狠，那张嘴笑得越响。拳头不停地 捶打着，捶打着，嘴巴回应着。\" -卡尔·桑德堡，《滴水兽》，《玉米剥皮者》。1918年。","“Speak! speak! thou fearful guest! Who, with thy hollow breast Still in rude armor drest, Comest to daunt me! Wrapt not in Eastern balms, But with thy fleshless palms Stretched, as if asking alms, Why dost thou haunt me?” -Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “The Skeleton in Armor”. 1841.":"\"说吧！说吧！你这可怕的来客！ 你胸中空空， 却仍披着粗陋的战甲， 前来惊吓我！ 未曾裹以东方香膏， 却伸出你无肉的掌心， 仿佛在乞求施舍， 你为何萦绕我不散？\" -亨利·沃兹沃思·朗费罗，《披甲骷髅》。1841年。","“God save us from the skeleton Who sitteth at the feast!” -James Jeffrey Roche, _The Skeleton at the Feast_. 1890.":"\"愿上帝拯救我们脱离那 端坐于宴席上的骷髅！\" -詹姆斯·杰弗里·罗奇，《宴席上的骷髅》。1890年。","“Her own mother lived the latter years of her life in the horrible suspicion that electricity was dripping invisibly all over the house.” -James Thurber, _My Life and Hard Times_. 1934.":"\"她的亲生母亲在生命的最后几年里，一直怀着一种可怕的 猜疑：电正无形地从房子的每个角落滴漏下来。\" -詹姆斯·瑟伯，《我的人生与艰难岁月》。1934年。","“The very deep did rot: O Christ! That ever this should be! Yea, slimy things did crawl with legs Upon the slimy sea.” -Samuel Tayor Coleridge, “The Rime of the Ancient Mariner”. 1798.":"\"深渊本身腐烂了：哦基督！ 这竟会发生！ 是啊，黏滑的东西用腿爬行 在黏滑的海面上。\" -塞缪尔·泰勒·柯勒律治，《古舟子咏》。1798年。","“No — it wasn't that way at all. It was everywhere — a gelatin — a slime yet it had shapes, a thousand shapes of horror beyond all memory. There were eyes — and a blemish. It was the pit — the maelstrom — the ultimate abomination. Carter, it was the unnamable!” -H.P. Lovecraft, _The Unnamable_. 1925.":"\"不——根本不是那样。它无处不在——一种凝胶——一种黏液， 却有着形态，千种超出一切记忆的恐怖形态。那里有眼睛—— 还有一种污迹。那是深渊——大漩涡——终极的憎恶。 卡特，那是不可名状之物！\" -H.P.洛夫克拉夫特，《不可名状》。1925年。","“Why does the thin grey strand Floating up from the forgotten Cigarette between my fingers, Why does it trouble me?” -D.H. Lawrence, “Sorrow”. 1916.":"\"为什么那纤细的灰色丝缕， 从我指间被遗忘的 香烟中升起时， 为什么它令我心神不宁？\" -D.H.劳伦斯，《忧伤》。1916年。","“After a while they came to a village. ”Now then,“ said Snapping Turtle, ”in the morning at daylight, my friends, we will make on attack. I myself will first go to the place,“ the leader of the war party said to them.":"\"走了一阵，他们来到了一个村庄。'好吧，'鳄龟说， '朋友们，天亮时分，我们就发起进攻。我先去那个地方。' 战团的首领对他们说道。","”Good,“ said the other little one, ”thou art the one who sees to it what we shall do,“ they said to that Snapping Turtle. ”Now then,“ said Snapping Turtle, ”verily I am now going to tell you what I shall do.“ Thus he spoke. ”Now is the time I shall begin to walk toward this village. Verily at the time I shall kill the daughter of the chief will be when the light of day is breaking, and at the same instant the sky will glow with red in the direction whence the morrow comes. ‘Ho, there, our comrade has killed her!’ will thus be the thought in your hearts. Then is the time when you want to make a great noise, when you shall whoop all keep it up. Now is the time that you go to attack this village.“ Thus he spoke to those his young men.":"'好，'另一个小家伙说，'你是决定我们该做什么的人，' 他们对那只鳄龟说道。'好吧，'鳄龟说，'现在我要 告诉你们我该做什么。'他这样说道。'现在，我要开始 朝这个村子走了。等我杀死酋长的女儿时，天正好破晓， 与此同时，明日来临的方向天空会染红。'嗬，那边，我们 的同伴杀了她！'——你们心里要这样想。那时就是你们发出 巨大声响的时刻，你们要不停地呐喊。现在就是你们去攻打 这个村子的时候。'他如此对他那些年轻人说道。","”All right!“ said the other little fellows.” -“When Snapping Turtle went to War”, _Publications of the American Ethnological Society, Volume IX: Kickapoo Tales_. 1915. trans. Truman Michelson":"'好的！'其他小家伙们说道。\" -《鳄龟出征记》，《美国民族学学会出版物，第九卷： 基卡普故事集》。1915年。 杜鲁门·迈克尔逊英译。","“After a while they came to a village. ”Now then,“ said Snapping Turtle, ”in the morning at daylight, my friends, we will make on attack. I myself will first go to the place,“ the leader of the war party said to them. ”Good,“ said the other little one, ”thou art the one who sees to it what we shall do,“ they said to that Snapping Turtle. ”Now then,“ said Snapping Turtle, ”verily I am now going to tell you what I shall do.“ Thus he spoke. ”Now is the time I shall begin to walk toward this village. Verily at the time I shall kill the daughter of the chief will be when the light of day is breaking, and at the same instant the sky will glow with red in the direction whence the morrow comes. ‘Ho, there, our comrade has killed her!’ will thus be the thought in your hearts. Then is the time when you want to make a great noise, when you shall whoop all keep it up. Now is the time that you go to attack this village.“ Thus he spoke to those his young men. ”All right!“ said the other little fellows.” -“When Snapping Turtle went to War”, _Publications of the American Ethnological Society, Volume IX: Kickapoo Tales_. 1915. trans. Truman Michelson":"\"走了一阵，他们来到了一个村庄。'好吧，'鳄龟说， '朋友们，天亮时分，我们就发起进攻。我先去那个地方。' 战团的首领对他们说道。 '好，'另一个小家伙说，'你是决定我们该做什么的人，' 他们对那只鳄龟说道。'好吧，'鳄龟说，'现在我要 告诉你们我该做什么。'他这样说道。'现在，我要开始 朝这个村子走了。等我杀死酋长的女儿时，天正好破晓， 与此同时，明日来临的方向天空会染红。'嗬，那边，我们 的同伴杀了她！'——你们心里要这样想。那时就是你们发出 巨大声响的时刻，你们要不停地呐喊。现在就是你们去攻打 这个村子的时候。'他如此对他那些年轻人说道。 '好的！'其他小家伙们说道。\" -《鳄龟出征记》，《美国民族学学会出版物，第九卷： 基卡普故事集》。1915年。 杜鲁门·迈克尔逊英译。","“Negation is the mind's first freedom.” -E.M. Cioran, _The Temptation to Exist_. 1956.":"\"否定是心灵最初的自由。\" -E.M.齐奥朗，《存在的诱惑》。1956年。","“It was just a colour out of space—a frightful messenger from unformed realms of infinity beyond all Nature as we know it; from realms whose mere existence stuns the brain and numbs us with the black extra-cosmic gulfs it throws open before our frenzied eyes.” -H.P. Lovecraft, “The Colour out of Space”. 1927.":"\"那不过是来自外太空的一种颜色——一个来自我们认知的 自然之外、来自无尽彼岸的未成形领域的可怕信使；来自 那些仅凭其存在就足以令大脑昏眩、令我们在它向我们疯狂 的眼前拉开的漆黑宇宙外深渊面前麻木的领域。\" -H.P.洛夫克拉夫特，《星之彩》。1927年。","“In any composition, the solid narrates the anomalies generated by the void, or the infection of the void through the solid (where the void comes to the solid, it works as a convoluting plague, a coiling swirling epidemic rather than a nullifying process or a solid-annihilating agent); in a composition there is no pure solid but a defiled one, a diseased and deflowered solid. [...] The only way that the solid can initialize its architectonic and compositional activities (processes for survival, development, etc.) is by letting the void in. The dynamic traits of solid can only be actuated when solid is eaten, convoluted and messed up by the void. There is no other option for solid.” -Reza Negarestani, _Cyclonopedia: Complicity with Anonymous Materials_. 2008":"\"在任何组合中，固体叙述着由虚空生成的异常，或者说， 虚空对固体的感染（当虚空抵达固体时，它作用为一种缠绕 的瘟疫，一种盘卷翻腾的传染病，而非一种消除过程或固体 湮灭剂）；在组合中，没有纯粹的固体，只有被玷污的、 染病和被摧残的固体。 ［……］ 固体能够启动其构造和组合活动（生存、发展等过程）的 唯一方式，就是让虚空进入。固体的动态特征只有在被虚空 吞噬、缠绕和搅乱时才能被激活。固体别无选择。\" -雷扎·内加雷斯塔尼，《旋风学：与匿名物质的共谋》。2008年。","“On the hungry craving wind My Spectre follows thee behind.” -William Blake, “Broken Love”. ca. 1800.":"\"在饥饿贪婪的风中 我的幽灵紧随你身后。\" -威廉·布莱克，《破碎的爱》。约1800年。","“When you think Your toys have gone berserk It's an illusion You cannot shirk” -Siouxsie and the Banshees, “Spellbound”":"\"当你想 你的玩具发了疯 那是幻觉 你无法逃避\" -苏克西与女妖乐队，《Spellbound》。","“Oedipus speaks: 'Far from me is the crime and shame of cowardice, and my valour knows not dastard fears[...] The Sphinx, weaving her words in darkling measures, I fled not; I faced the bloody jaws of the fell prophetess and the ground white with scattered bones. And when from a lofty cliff, already hovering over her prey, she prepared her pinions and, lashing her tail like a savage lion, stirred up her threatening wrath, I asked her riddle. Thereupon came a sound of dread; her jaws crashed, and her talons, brooking no delay, eager for my vitals, tore at the rocks. The lot's intricate, guile-entangled words, the grim riddle of the winged beast, I solved.'” -Seneca, _Oedipus_, 1st cent. A.D. trans. Frank Justus Miller, 1917.":"\"俄狄浦斯说：'怯懦的罪恶与耻辱离我很远，我的勇气不 知畏惧为何物［……］斯芬克斯，用晦暗的韵律编织着谜语， 我并未逃遁；我直面那凶残女预言家的血盆大口和散落白骨 染白的土地。当她从高耸的悬崖上，已经在她猎物上方盘旋， 张开羽翼，像一头野蛮的狮子般甩动尾巴，激起她威胁的 怒火时，我问出了她的谜语。随即传来一阵恐怖的声音； 她的下颚嘎吱作响，她的利爪迫不及待，垂涎我的内脏， 撕扯着岩石。那命运之神错综复杂、诡计交织的言辞， 那有翼野兽的可怕谜语，我解开了。'\" -塞内加，《俄狄浦斯》，公元1世纪。 弗兰克·贾斯特斯·米勒英译，1917年。","\"My colleagues may have dismissed the sightings as blink frog egg casings, but today I shall prove that these creatures came from beyond the firmament. Let's begin the dissection.\" -Ardun Idrick, cryptozoologist, last words":"\"我的同事们或许将这些目击现象视作闪烁蛙的卵囊而予以 否定，但今天我将证明，这些生物来自天穹之外。让我们 开始解剖吧。\" -阿顿·伊德里克，隐生动物学家，临终遗言。","“Did you see that star go out? I seen it burn.":"\"你看见那颗星星熄灭了吗？ 我看见它燃烧。","That little star went out, your little eyes went out.":"那颗小星星熄灭了， 你的小眼睛熄灭了。","Our burnt little dreams are hid up where the stars get lit.” -Thee Silver Mt. Zion, “I Built Myself a Metal Bird”. 2010.":"我们烧焦的小梦想藏在 星星被点亮的地方。\" -银锡安山，Thee Silver Mt. Zion，《我为自己造了一只金属鸟》。2010年。","“Did you see that star go out? I seen it burn. That little star went out, your little eyes went out. Our burnt little dreams are hid up where the stars get lit.” -Thee Silver Mt. Zion, “I Built Myself a Metal Bird”. 2010.":"\"你看见那颗星星熄灭了吗？ 我看见它燃烧。 那颗小星星熄灭了， 你的小眼睛熄灭了。 我们烧焦的小梦想藏在 星星被点亮的地方。\" -银锡安山，Thee Silver Mt. Zion，《我为自己造了一只金属鸟》。2010年。","“I really believe what you say, answered the knight; for, I have been engaged with the giant, in the most obstinate and outrageous combat that I believe I shall ever fight in all the days of my life: with one backstroke, slam went his head to the ground; and discharged such a quantity of blood, that it ran like rills of water, along the field.” -Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra, _The Ingenious Gentleman Don Quixote of La Mancha_, IV, 10. 1605. trans. Carlos Fuentes, 1997.":"\"'我真的相信你说的话，'骑士答道；'因为，我刚刚与那个 巨人经历了一场我平生所经历的最为激烈、最为固执的战斗： 反手一击，砰的一声，他的头落到了地上；鲜血四溅，如同 溪水般流淌在田野上。'\" -米格尔·德·塞万提斯·萨维德拉，《拉曼查的奇情异想的 绅士堂吉诃德》，第四卷第十章。1605年。 卡洛斯·富恩特斯英译，1997年。","“Behold him setting in his western skies, The shadows lengthening as the vapours rise.” -John Dryden, “Absalom and Achitophel”, I, 268. 1681.":"\"看他正在西天沉落， 阴影随雾霭升腾而拉长。\" -约翰·德莱顿，《押沙龙与亚希多弗》，第一卷，268行。1681年。","“The sky is sad and beautiful, like a vast altar. The sun has drowned in its congealing blood.” -Charles Baudelaire, _Flowers of Evil_, 43: Evening Harmony. 1857. trans. Ruth White, 1969.":"\"天空悲戚而美丽，如同一座巨大的祭坛。 太阳已溺死在自己凝结的血中。\" -夏尔·波德莱尔，《恶之花》，第43首：黄昏的和声。1857年。 鲁思·怀特英译，1969年。","“Behold him setting in his western skies, The shadows lengthening as the vapours rise.” -John Dryden, “Absalom and Achitophel”, I, 268. 1681. “The sky is sad and beautiful, like a vast altar. The sun has drowned in its congealing blood.” -Charles Baudelaire, _Flowers of Evil_, 43: Evening Harmony. 1857. trans. Ruth White, 1969.":"\"看他正在西天沉落， 阴影随雾霭升腾而拉长。\" -约翰·德莱顿，《押沙龙与亚希多弗》，第一卷，268行。1681年。 \"天空悲戚而美丽，如同一座巨大的祭坛。 太阳已溺死在自己凝结的血中。\" -夏尔·波德莱尔，《恶之花》，第43首：黄昏的和声。1857年。 鲁思·怀特英译，1969年。","“Sweet is the swamp with its secrets, Until we meet a snake; 'T is then we sigh for houses, And our departure take":"\"沼泽带着它的秘密是甜美的， 直到我们遇见一条蛇； 那时我们便叹息着想念房屋， 于是拔腿而逃","At that enthralling gallop That only childhood knows. A snake is summer's treason, And guile is where it goes.” -Emily Dickinson, “A Snake”. ca. 1865.":"以那种只有童年才懂的 迷人的飞奔。 蛇是夏日的背叛， 狡诈随着它的行踪而至。\" -艾米莉·狄金森，《蛇》。约1865年。","“Sweet is the swamp with its secrets, Until we meet a snake; 'T is then we sigh for houses, And our departure take At that enthralling gallop That only childhood knows. A snake is summer's treason, And guile is where it goes.” -Emily Dickinson, “A Snake”. ca. 1865.":"\"沼泽带着它的秘密是甜美的， 直到我们遇见一条蛇； 那时我们便叹息着想念房屋， 于是拔腿而逃 以那种只有童年才懂的 迷人的飞奔。 蛇是夏日的背叛， 狡诈随着它的行踪而至。\" -艾米莉·狄金森，《蛇》。约1865年。","“The fool, as I think, at the chasm's brink, Prone by the swamp or the marsh's side, Did, even as I, in the end rejoice, Since the voice of death must be His true voice.” -Arthur Edward Waite, “At The End of Things”. 1906.":"\"那愚人，如我所想，在深渊边缘， 俯身在沼泽或泥淖之旁， 正如我一样，终将欢喜， 因为死亡之声必是祂真正的声音。\" -阿瑟·爱德华·韦特，《万物的终结》。1906年。","“A Bird came down the Walk — He did not know I saw — He bit an Angleworm in halves And ate the fellow, raw” -Emily Dickinson, “A Bird came down the Walk”. ca. 1865.":"\"一只鸟沿着小径走来—— 它不知道我看见—— 它把一条蚯蚓啄成两半 生吞了那家伙\" -艾米莉·狄金森，《一只鸟沿着小径走来》。约1865年。","“I can puff up my feathers, look real mean Be the old man that this here's scene I'm a struttin' preenin' bantam rooster looking for a fight.” -Andrew Bird's Bowl of Fire, “Cock o' the Walk”. 1998.":"\"我可以蓬起羽毛，看起来真凶 当那个老家伙，这里我说了算 我是只昂首阔步、梳理羽毛的矮脚公鸡，在找架打。\" -Andrew Bird's Bowl of Fire，《Cock o' the Walk》。1998年。","“Oozing and surging up out of that yawning trap-door in the Cyclopean crypt I had glimpsed such an unbelievable behemothic monstrosity that I could not doubt the power of its original to kill with its mere sight. Even now I cannot begin to suggest it with any words at my command. I might call it gigantic — tentacled — proboscidian — octopus-eyed — semi-amorphous — plastic — partly squamous and partly rugose — ugh!” -H.P. Lovecraft and Hazel Heald, “Out of the Aeons”, _Weird Tales_, 25, No. 4, pp. 478-96. April 1935.":"\"从那巨怪地窖中那个豁开的陷阱门里渗出翻涌而出的，是 一尊如此难以置信的巨兽般的怪物，我无法怀疑其原型仅凭 目视便足以杀人的力量。即使现在，我仍无法用我所能驾驭 的任何词语来形容它。我可以称它为巨大的——长触须的—— 长鼻的——章鱼眼的——半无定形的——可塑的——部分有鳞、 部分有皱的——呃！\" -H.P.洛夫克拉夫特与黑兹尔·希尔德，《自万古而出》， 《诡丽幻谭》，第25卷第4期，第478-96页。1935年4月。","“And on the other part the Titans eagerly strengthened their ranks, and both sides at one time showed the work of their hands and their might. The boundless sea rang terribly around, and the earth crashed loudly: wide Heaven was shaken and groaned, and high Olympus reeled from its foundation under the charge of the undying gods, and a heavy quaking reached dim Tartarus and the deep sound of their feet in the fearful onset and of their hard missiles. So, then, they launched their grievous shafts upon one another, and the cry of both armies as they shouted reached to starry heaven; and they met together with a great battle-cry.” -Hesiod, _Theogony_, 8th cent. B.C. trans. H.G. Evelyn-White, 1914.":"\"另一边，泰坦们也急切地加强阵势，双方同时展示着他们 双手的力量和威力。无边的海洋可怖地咆哮，大地轰然作响： 辽阔的天空颤抖呻吟，高耸的奥林匹斯山在永生众神的冲击 下从根基动摇，沉重的震撼直达幽暗的塔耳塔罗斯，还有 他们在那可怕的突袭和猛烈投石中沉重的脚步声。于是， 他们彼此投掷着致命的飞弹，两军呐喊的呼声直达星空； 他们以惊天动地的战吼交汇在一起。\" -赫西俄德，《神谱》，公元前8世纪。 H.G.伊夫林-怀特英译，1914年。","“But the Seneschal gathered the toadstool fly-bane.” -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, III. 1834. trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.":"\"但总督采了那毒蝇蕈。\" -亚当·密茨凯维奇，《塔杜施先生》，第三卷。1834年。 G.R.诺伊斯英译，1917年。","“Gentle socks pamper them by day, and shoes cobbled of leather fortify them, but my toes hardly notice. All they're interested in is turning out toenails—semitransparent, flexible sheets of a hornlike material, as defence against—whom?” -Jorge Luis Borges, “Toenails”. 1960. trans. Andrew Hurley, 1998.":"\"白天温柔的袜子宠爱它们，皮革缝制的鞋子加固它们， 但我的脚趾几乎浑然不觉。它们唯一感兴趣的，就是长出 脚趾甲——那种半透明、柔韧的角质薄片，作为一种防御 ——防御谁呢？\" -豪尔赫·路易斯·博尔赫斯，《脚趾甲》。1960年。 安德鲁·赫尔利英译，1998年。","“Thou art to me a delicious torment.” -Ralph Waldo Emerson, _Essays: First Series_, Essay VI: Friendship. 1841.":"\"你之于我，是一种甜蜜的折磨。\" -拉尔夫·沃尔多·爱默生，《随笔：第一辑》，第六篇：友谊。1841年。","“Snail, snail, slug-slow, To me thy four horns show; If thou dost not show me thy four, I will throw thee out of the door, For the crow in the gutter, To eat for bread and butter.” -Silesian rhyme. Quoted by S.W. Singer in _Notes and Queries_, no. 69. 1851.":"\"蜗牛，蜗牛，慢如鼻涕虫， 把你的四只角给我看； 你若是不给我看四只角， 我就把你扔出门外， 让沟里的乌鸦 拿你当面包和黄油吃。\" -西里西亚童谣。S.W.辛格引用于《笔记与查询》第69期。1851年。","“Things are only mannequins and even the great world-historical events are only costumes beneath which they exchange glances with nothingness, with the base and the banal.” -Walter Benjamin, _Protocols to the Experiments on Hashish, Opium and Mescaline 1927-1934_, “Protocol II: Highlights of the Second Hashish Impression”. 15 January 1928. trans. Scott J. Thompson, 1997.":"\"事物只是人体模型，即便是伟大的世界历史事件，也不过 是戏服，在它们下面人们与虚无、与卑贱和平庸交换着 眼神。\" -瓦尔特·本雅明，《大麻、鸦片和墨斯卡灵实验记录 1927-1934》，\"记录二：第二次大麻体验的亮点\"。 1928年1月15日。斯科特·J·汤普森英译，1997年。","Scully: “Where the hell did it come from?” Mulder: “I don’t know, but it looks like I’m going to have to tell Skinner that his suspect is a giant bloodsucking worm after all.” -_The X-Files_, “The Host”. 1994":"斯嘉丽：\"这他妈是从哪来的？\" 穆德：\"我不知道，但看来我得告诉斯金纳， 他的嫌疑人毕竟是一条巨型吸血蠕虫。\" -《X档案》，\"宿主\"。1994年。","“We were permitted to shriek in the tongue of dwarfs and demons” -Czesław Miłosz, “A Task”.":"\"我们被允许用侏儒与恶魔的语言尖叫\" -切斯瓦夫·米沃什，《一项任务》。","“Beauty is no quality in things themselves: It exists merely in the mind which contemplates them; and each mind perceives a different beauty. One person may even perceive deformity, where another is sensible of beauty; and every individual ought to acquiesce in his own sentiment, without pretending to regulate those of others.” -David Hume":"\"美并非事物本身的品质：它仅存在于观赏它的心灵之中； 而每个心灵感知到的美各不相同。一个人甚至可能感知到 丑陋，而另一个人却感受到美；每个人都应当默守自己的 感受，而无需假装去规范他人的感受。\" -大卫·休谟。","“The awful shadow of some unseen Power Floats, tho’ unseen, amongst us.” -Percy Bysshe Shelley, “Hymn to Intellectual Beauty”, I, 1-2. 1816.":"\"某种不可见力量的可怕阴影 虽不可见，却漂浮在我们中间。\" -珀西·比希·雪莱，《咏智性之美》，第一节第1-2行。1816年。","“Spell for causing a shabti to do work for a man in the realm of the dead: O shabti, allotted to me, if I be summoned or if I be detailed to do any work which has to be done in the realm of the dead, if indeed any obstacles are implanted for you therewith as a man at his duties, you shall detail yourself for me on every occasion of making arable the fields, of flooding the banks or of conveying sand from east to west; ‘Here I am’, you shall say. -Spell 6, _Book of the Dead_, from _Ancient Egyptian Book of the Dead: Journey through the afterlife_, edited by John H. Taylor. 2010":"\"驱使沙伯替为亡者在冥界劳作的咒语： 哦，分派给我的沙伯替，若我被召唤或指派去完成冥界中的 任何劳作，若有人像役使当差者一般给你设下任何阻碍， 你都应代我承担：开垦田地、灌溉河岸或将沙土从东运至西； 你当说：'我在此。'\" -第6号咒语，《亡灵书》，引自《古埃及亡灵书：穿越来世 之旅》，约翰·H·泰勒编。2010年。","• Scuze me. My friend Burt says you're a vampire hunter. 'zat so? — Uh yes. Yes it is. • Well you n'ain't gonna find one round here, mate. They ain't no vampires. — You don't believe in vampires? • 'course not! • But I do believe in con artists. And charletans who like to stir up trouble! • Dead people who get up at night and suck blood. How stupid do you think we are? • My place is haunted with 16 ghosts and they all say there n'ain't no vampires! -Rich Morris, Yet Another Fantasy Gamer Comic":"• 打扰一下。我朋友伯特说你是吸血鬼猎人。是吗？ — 嗯，是的。是的。 • 那你在这儿可找不着，哥们。这里没有吸血鬼。 — 你不信有吸血鬼？ • 当然不信！ • 但我信有骗子。还有喜欢煽风点火的江湖术士！ • 死人夜里爬起来吸人血。你把我们想得多蠢？ • 我的房子闹鬼，有十六个鬼，它们都说没有吸血鬼这回事！ -里奇·莫里斯，《Yet Another Fantasy Gamer Comic》。","“For something is amiss and out of place When mice with wings can wear a human face.” -Theodore Roethke, “The Bat”. 1938.":"\"有什么不对劲、不妥当 当长翅膀的老鼠能戴上一张人脸。\" -西奥多·罗特克，《蝙蝠》。1938年。","“I'm ugly, I'm ugly as sin, But beautiful's out, ugly's in. If you're ugly like me, you're in good company. There are millions of us who are ugly.” -_The Muppet Show_, “Ugly Song”. 1977":"\"我丑，我丑得不可饶恕， 但美已过时，丑正流行。 如果你像我一样丑，那你可不孤单。 我们丑人成千上万。\" -《大青蛙布偶秀》，\"丑之歌\"。1977年。","“The monstrous plant bud . . . had grown again with preternatural rapidity, from Falmer's head. A loathsome pale-green stem was mounting thickly, and had started to branch like antlers after attaining a height of six or seven inches.":"\"那怪异的植物蓓蕾……以超乎寻常的速度再次从法尔默的 头上长了出来。一根可憎的淡绿色茎干正粗壮地向上生长， 长到六七英寸高时开始像鹿角一样分叉。","More dreadful than this, if possible, similar growths had issued from the eyes; and their stems, climbing vertically across the forehead, had entirely displaced the eyeballs.” -Clark Ashton Smith, “The Seed from the Sepulcher”. 1933.":"比这更可怕的——如果还有可能的话——是从眼睛里长出了 类似的生长物；它们的茎干垂直攀过前额，完全取代了 眼球。\" -克拉克·阿什顿·史密斯，《坟墓之种》。1933年。","“The monstrous plant bud . . . had grown again with preternatural rapidity, from Falmer's head. A loathsome pale-green stem was mounting thickly, and had started to branch like antlers after attaining a height of six or seven inches. More dreadful than this, if possible, similar growths had issued from the eyes; and their stems, climbing vertically across the forehead, had entirely displaced the eyeballs.” -Clark Ashton Smith, “The Seed from the Sepulcher”. 1933.":"\"那怪异的植物蓓蕾……以超乎寻常的速度再次从法尔默的 头上长了出来。一根可憎的淡绿色茎干正粗壮地向上生长， 长到六七英寸高时开始像鹿角一样分叉。 比这更可怕的——如果还有可能的话——是从眼睛里长出了 类似的生长物；它们的茎干垂直攀过前额，完全取代了 眼球。\" -克拉克·阿什顿·史密斯，《坟墓之种》。1933年。","“Telimena, wearied with the prolonged wrangling, wanted to go out into the fresh air, but sought a partner. She took a little basket from the peg. “Gentlemen, I see that you wish to remain within doors,” she said, wrapping around her head a red cashmere shawl, “but I am going for mushrooms: follow me who will!” Under one arm she took the little daughter of the Chamberlain, with the other she raised her skirt up to her ankles. Thaddeus silently hastened after her—to seek mushrooms!” -Adam Mickiewicz, _Pan Tadeusz_, II. 1834. trans. G.R. Noyes, 1917.":"\"泰莉梅娜厌倦了这冗长的争吵，想去呼吸新鲜空气，却在 寻找同伴。她从挂钩上取下一个小篮子。'先生们，我看 你们打算待在屋里，'她说着，将一条红色开司米披巾裹在 头上，'但我要去采蘑菇：谁愿跟我来！'她一手挽起 内侍长的小女儿，另一只手提起裙子到脚踝。塔德乌什 默默地快步跟在她身后——去采蘑菇！\" -亚当·密茨凯维奇，《塔杜施先生》，第二卷。1834年。 G.R.诺伊斯英译，1917年。","“Their innumerable sculptures of demons and dragons assumed a lugubrious aspect. The restless light of the flame made them move to the eye. There were griffins which had the air of laughing, gargoyles which one fancied one heard yelping, salamanders which puffed at the fire, tarasques which sneezed in the smoke. And among the monsters thus roused from their sleep of stone by this flame, by this noise, there was one who walked about, and who was seen, from time to time, to pass across the glowing face of the pile, like a bat in front of a candle.” -Victor Hugo, _The Hunchback of Notre-Dame_, 10, ch. IV. 1831. trans. Isabel F. Hapgood":"\"无数恶魔与龙的雕塑呈现出阴郁的面貌。火焰躁动的光芒 使它们仿佛在眼前移动。有些狮鹫似乎在笑，有些滴水兽 仿佛在嚎叫，有些沙罗曼达朝着火焰喷气，有些塔拉斯各 在烟雾中打喷嚏。在这些被火焰和喧嚣从石头的沉睡中唤醒 的怪物中，有一个在走动，不时看见它穿过燃烧柴堆那发光 的表面，如同一只蝙蝠掠过烛光。\" -维克多·雨果，《巴黎圣母院》，第十卷第四章。1831年。 伊莎贝尔·F·哈普古德英译。","“Alas, poor Yorick! I knew him, Horatio, a fellow of infinite jest, of most excellent fancy. He hath bore me on his back a thousand times, and now how abhorr'd in my imagination it is! My gorge rises at it.” -William Shakespeare, _The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark_, V, 1. 1603":"\"唉，可怜的约里克！我认识他，霍拉旭，他是个妙趣无穷、 想象力极为卓越的家伙。他曾经把我驮在他背上一千次； 而今，我心中一想到此，就觉得多么可憎！我的胃都在 翻涌。\" -威廉·莎士比亚，《丹麦王子哈姆雷特的悲剧》，第五幕 第一场。1603年。","“Teacher: How does a dog smell? Student: I don't know. Teacher: Correct!” -Traditional Spanish joke.":"\"老师：狗怎么闻东西？ 学生：我不知道。 老师：答对了！\" -西班牙传统笑话。","“Oh, but you can't expect to wield supreme executive power just because some watery tart threw a sword at you.” -Monty Python and the Holy Grail, 1975.":"\"哦，你可不能仅仅因为某个水里的荡妇扔了把剑给你，就 指望掌握最高行政权力。\" -《巨蟒与圣杯》，1975年。","“Unhappie wight, borne to desastrous end, That doth his life in so long tendance spend!” -Edmund Spenser, “Mother Hubberds Tale”, _Complaints_. 1591.":"\"不幸的人啊，生来注定悲惨的结局， 以如此漫长的服侍虚度此生！\" -埃德蒙·斯宾塞，《哈伯德母亲的故事》，《怨诉集》。1591年。","<ribbon worm>":"<ribbon worm>","“God, though this life is but a wraith, Although we know not what we use, Although we grope with little faith, Give me the heart to fight—and lose.” -Louis Untermeyer, “Prayer”. 1919.":"\"上帝啊，纵然此生不过幻影， 纵使我们不知自己所为何用， 纵使我们摸索前行却信心微薄， 请赐我战斗——并失败——的心。\" -路易斯·翁特迈耶，《祈祷》。1919年。","“Stare into the sun Wherever you may roam Feel it calling you home Despite the mounting danger Stare into the sun Let its fire fill you Whatever doesn’t kill you Only makes you stranger” -The Sunbeams, “The Tug”. 2020":"\"凝视太阳 无论你走到哪里 感受它在呼唤你回家 尽管危险日益加剧 凝视太阳 让它的火焰充满你 杀不死你的 只会让你更怪异\" -The Sunbeams，《The Tug》。2020年。","“My complete answer to the late 19th century question 'what is electrodynamics trying to tell us' would simply be this:":"\"我对19世纪末那个问题'电动力学想告诉我们什么'的完整 回答，简单来说就是：","Fields in empty space have physical reality; the medium that supports them does not.":"虚空中的场具有物理实在性；支撑它们的介质则没有。","Having thus removed the mystery from electrodynamics, let me immediately do the same for quantum mechanics:":"在消除了电动力学的神秘之后，请允许我立即对量子力学 做同样的事：","Correlations have physical reality; that which they correlate does not.” -N. David Mermin, _What is quantum mechanics trying to tell us?_, 1998.":"关联具有物理实在性；被关联的事物则没有。\" -N.大卫·默明，《量子力学想告诉我们什么？》，1998年。","“My complete answer to the late 19th century question 'what is electrodynamics trying to tell us' would simply be this: Fields in empty space have physical reality; the medium that supports them does not. Having thus removed the mystery from electrodynamics, let me immediately do the same for quantum mechanics: Correlations have physical reality; that which they correlate does not.” -N. David Mermin, _What is quantum mechanics trying to tell us?_, 1998.":"\"我对19世纪末那个问题'电动力学想告诉我们什么'的完整 回答，简单来说就是： 虚空中的场具有物理实在性；支撑它们的介质则没有。 在消除了电动力学的神秘之后，请允许我立即对量子力学 做同样的事： 关联具有物理实在性；被关联的事物则没有。\" -N.大卫·默明，《量子力学想告诉我们什么？》，1998年。","“He fixed his eyes upon the door, which, slowly opening, disclosed a stranger of majestic form, but scowling features, who demanded sternly, why he was summoned? ‘I did not summon you,’ said the trembling student. ‘You did!’ said the stranger, advancing, angrily; ‘and the demons are not to be invoked in vain.’ The student could make no reply; and the demon, enraged that one of the uninitiated should have summoned him out of mere presumption, seized him by the throat and strangled him.":"\"他的眼睛紧盯着那扇门；门缓缓开启，显现出一个身形 威严却面容阴沉的陌生人，严厉地质问他为何被召唤。'我 没有召唤你，'那颤抖的学生说道。'你召唤了！'陌生人 愤怒地逼近，说道；'恶魔可不是白白就能召唤的。'学生 无言以对；那恶魔因一个未经入门者竟敢仅凭妄念便召唤他 而大怒，抓住学生的喉咙，将他勒死了。","When Agrippa returned, a few days afterwards, he found his house beset with devils. Some of them were sitting on the chimneypots, kicking up their legs in the air; while others were playing at leapfrog, on the very edge of the parapet. His study was so filled with them that he found it difficult to make his way to his desk.” -Charles Mackay, _Memoirs of Extraordinary Popular Delusions_, Vol. III, Part I. 1841.":"几天后，阿格里帕回来时，发现他的房子被群魔包围了。 有些恶魔坐在烟囱顶上，在空中踢着腿；还有些在女儿墙 边缘玩着跳背游戏。他的书房里挤满了恶魔，他几乎无法 走到书桌前。\" -查尔斯·麦凯，《异常流行幻象与群体疯狂回忆录》， 第三卷，第一部分。1841年。","“He fixed his eyes upon the door, which, slowly opening, disclosed a stranger of majestic form, but scowling features, who demanded sternly, why he was summoned? ‘I did not summon you,’ said the trembling student. ‘You did!’ said the stranger, advancing, angrily; ‘and the demons are not to be invoked in vain.’ The student could make no reply; and the demon, enraged that one of the uninitiated should have summoned him out of mere presumption, seized him by the throat and strangled him. When Agrippa returned, a few days afterwards, he found his house beset with devils. Some of them were sitting on the chimneypots, kicking up their legs in the air; while others were playing at leapfrog, on the very edge of the parapet. His study was so filled with them that he found it difficult to make his way to his desk.” -Charles Mackay, _Memoirs of Extraordinary Popular Delusions_, Vol. III, Part I. 1841.":"\"他的眼睛紧盯着那扇门；门缓缓开启，显现出一个身形 威严却面容阴沉的陌生人，严厉地质问他为何被召唤。'我 没有召唤你，'那颤抖的学生说道。'你召唤了！'陌生人 愤怒地逼近，说道；'恶魔可不是白白就能召唤的。'学生 无言以对；那恶魔因一个未经入门者竟敢仅凭妄念便召唤他 而大怒，抓住学生的喉咙，将他勒死了。 几天后，阿格里帕回来时，发现他的房子被群魔包围了。 有些恶魔坐在烟囱顶上，在空中踢着腿；还有些在女儿墙 边缘玩着跳背游戏。他的书房里挤满了恶魔，他几乎无法 走到书桌前。\" -查尔斯·麦凯，《异常流行幻象与群体疯狂回忆录》， 第三卷，第一部分。1841年。","“It seemed that while the zombie came from the grave, it was neither a ghost, nor yet a person who had been raised like Lazarus from the dead. The zombie, they say, is a soulless human corpse, still dead, but taken from the grave and endowed by sorcery with a mechanical semblance of life—it is a dead body which is made to walk and act and move as if it were alive. People who have the power to do this go to a fresh grave, dig up the body before it has had time to rot, galvanize it into movement, and then make of it a servant or slave, occasionally for the commission of some crime, more often simply as a drudge around the habitation or the farm, setting it dull heavy tasks, and beating it like a dumb beast if it slackens.” -William Seabrook, _The Magic Island_. 1929.":"\"看起来，丧尸虽然从坟墓中出来，却既不是鬼魂，也不是 像拉撒路那样从死里复活的人。据说，丧尸是一具没有灵魂 的人类尸体，仍是死的，只是被人从坟墓中挖出，通过巫术 赋予了一种机械的生命表象——它是一具被驱使着像活人一样 行走、行动和移动的死尸。拥有这种能力的人会去一座新坟， 在尸体还未腐烂之前将其挖出，用电流刺激其活动，然后将 它变成仆人或奴隶，偶尔用来犯下某些罪行，更多的时候 只是作为住所或农场周围的苦力，给它安排沉重乏味的劳作， 如果它懈怠，就像对待哑巴牲畜一样鞭打它。\" -威廉·西布鲁克，《魔幻岛》。1929年。","“They’re not afraid! No matter what we do, no matter how many we kill, they will never, ever be afraid!” -Max Brooks, _World War Z: An Oral History of the Zombie War_. 2006.":"\"它们不怕！无论我们做什么，无论我们杀多少，它们永远、 永远不会害怕！\" -马克斯·布鲁克斯，《僵尸世界大战：一部僵尸战争口述史》。2006年。","“It seemed that while the zombie came from the grave, it was neither a ghost, nor yet a person who had been raised like Lazarus from the dead. The zombie, they say, is a soulless human corpse, still dead, but taken from the grave and endowed by sorcery with a mechanical semblance of life—it is a dead body which is made to walk and act and move as if it were alive. People who have the power to do this go to a fresh grave, dig up the body before it has had time to rot, galvanize it into movement, and then make of it a servant or slave, occasionally for the commission of some crime, more often simply as a drudge around the habitation or the farm, setting it dull heavy tasks, and beating it like a dumb beast if it slackens.” -William Seabrook, _The Magic Island_. 1929. “They’re not afraid! No matter what we do, no matter how many we kill, they will never, ever be afraid!” -Max Brooks, _World War Z: An Oral History of the Zombie War_. 2006.":"\"看起来，丧尸虽然从坟墓中出来，却既不是鬼魂，也不是 像拉撒路那样从死里复活的人。据说，丧尸是一具没有灵魂 的人类尸体，仍是死的，只是被人从坟墓中挖出，通过巫术 赋予了一种机械的生命表象——它是一具被驱使着像活人一样 行走、行动和移动的死尸。拥有这种能力的人会去一座新坟， 在尸体还未腐烂之前将其挖出，用电流刺激其活动，然后将 它变成仆人或奴隶，偶尔用来犯下某些罪行，更多的时候 只是作为住所或农场周围的苦力，给它安排沉重乏味的劳作， 如果它懈怠，就像对待哑巴牲畜一样鞭打它。\" -威廉·西布鲁克，《魔幻岛》。1929年。 \"它们不怕！无论我们做什么，无论我们杀多少，它们永远、 永远不会害怕！\" -马克斯·布鲁克斯，《僵尸世界大战：一部僵尸战争口述史》。2006年。","The scales of an acid dragon. Although it does not provide its wearer with as much protection as the armour made from the scales of some larger dragons, it is somewhat lighter and less encumbering. It is also remarkably smooth, letting corrosive slime flow off it like water.":"一套酸龙鳞甲。尽管它不像一些由更大的龙的鳞片制成的护甲那样， 能为穿戴者提供更多的防护，但它却更轻便、妨碍也更少。 它也非常光滑，腐蚀性的黏液会像水那样从上面流走。","A charm crafted to call the attention of the gods to its wearer. This divine attention makes it easier to please your god, but your god will also take more notice of your transgressions. The amulet will drain some of your divine favour when removed.":"这条精致的项链旨在引起神对佩戴者的留意。 在神的注意下会更易取悦你的神，但神也会更容易察觉到你的冒犯。 当这条项链被取下时，神会减少对你的好感。","An amulet containing a protective spirit which will cause any damage taken to be divided between the wearer's reserves of health and magic.":"这条项链含有守护之灵， 它能让佩戴者的生命和法力储备分摊承受受到的任何伤害。","An amulet that increases the wearer's rate of magic regeneration. In order to function, it must first attune itself to the wearer's body with full reserves of magic.":"这条项链可以提升佩戴者的法力恢复速度。 佩戴期间法力全满时，它就会与身体完成同调，从而发挥作用。","An amulet with no special properties.":"这条项链没有特殊属性。","An amulet which improves its wearer's ability to shield against attacks. If no shield is worn, the force the amulet emits can serve as a weak shield on its own. Regardless, any ranged attacks the wearer blocks will be reflected back toward the attacker.":"这条项链可以提升佩戴者格挡攻击的能力。 如果没有装备盾牌，这条项链本身就相当于较弱的盾牌。 无论是否装备盾牌，佩戴者格挡的远程攻击都会被反射回攻击者。","An amulet that increases the wearer's rate of health regeneration. In order to function, it must first attune itself to the wearer's body at full health.":"这条项链可以增加佩戴者的生命值恢复速度。 佩戴期间生命值全满时，它就会与身体完成同调，从而发挥作用。","An amulet that allows the user to tumble and roll to evade the blows of their enemies, but only while moving and waiting. While taking other actions (including climbing stairs) the amulet conveys no benefits.":"这条项链，能让佩戴者以翻滚的方式躲避敌人的攻击， 但这只会在移动和等待时生效。在进行其他动作（包括爬楼梯）时， 这条项链并不会带来相应正面效果。","A large piece of thick skin covered in fur, cut from the corpse of an animal and worn as a primitive garment. It offers rudimentary protection against harm, but, having never been tanned, it carries a light stench of rotting flesh.":"一个从动物的尸体上切下的大块厚皮，上面还有毛，作为简陋的衣着。 它也能提供基础的保护以抵挡伤害。 由于没有鞣制过，这东西闻起来有一点腐肉的味道。","A large piece of machinery used for firing bolts, braced with steel and cranked with a windlass. It takes some time to load and fire.":"一架用于发射弩矢的巨大器械，以钢材加固，并用曲柄转动绞盘。 装填和发射都需要一些时间。","As clear and blue as a cloudless sky or a depthless sea, this gem holds its secrets locked within impenetrable depths.":"这颗宝石像万里无云的天空或深不可测的大海那样清澈湛蓝， 它那难以穿透的深处隐藏着不为人知的秘密。","A long pole with an enormous, cleaving blade on one end.":"一根长杆，一端装有巨大的劈砍斧刃。","Armour for the scaly midsections of nagas and armataurs.":"用于保护纳迦和甲马有鳞身体中段的护甲。","A large war axe with a formidable double-sided head.":"一把有着令人生畏的双面斧头的大型战斧。","A jagged cluster of blades, almost impossible to grasp without injury. Causes long, needle-thin blades to grow from the wearer's body, allowing them to perform rapid auxiliary melee attacks and even parry blows. Having so many fragments of metal inside one's body reduces the effectiveness of body armour, but Shapeshifting skill mitigates this effect as well as increases the damage dealt.":"锯齿状的一簇刀片，很难抓着它而不受伤。 它能令使用者身体长出长长的、针般薄的刀片，使其能够进行快速的辅助近战攻击， 甚至能格挡攻击。体内有如此多的金属碎片会降低身体护甲的效力， 但变形术技能可以减轻这种影响，并增加造成的伤害。","A primer on the elemental magics of Air. The great minotaur hero Vuxhurn, given a copy of this book while trapped atop the tower of a wizard with a particularly perverse sense of humour, used its pages to construct a rudimentary glider and soared to freedom.":"一本空气魔法的入门读物。 伟大的牛头人英雄乌克斯胡恩被困在一个有着特别过分的幽默感的巫师塔塔顶时， 得到了这本书的副本，他用这本书的书页搭建了一个简陋的滑翔机，飞向了自由。","A tome of arcane fury, greatly sought after by sorcerers. It allows the gifted and resourceful to conjure destruction with ease.":"一本关于奥术狂暴的巨著，深受术士追捧。有天赋和机敏的人能凭借它轻易唤起毁灭。","A book describing various magical arms and armours. It was written in the midst of a particularly bloody civil war, and the text is made substantially less helpful by its author's frequent digressions describing the crimes committed by the other side.":"一本描述各种魔法武器和盔甲的书。 它是在一场特别血腥的内战中写成的， 由于作者频繁地离题描述对方所犯下的罪行，文本在很大程度上不太有帮助。","An astonishingly vain and self-aggrandising work. The author claims credit for a wide swathe of weapon-augmenting magics, but seems to have misunderstood or misrepresented most of them. Only a few of the spells described in the book actually work.":"一部极其自负、自我膨胀的作品。作者声称这一系列武器增强魔法归功于他， 但从这本书来看，作者似乎不理解或误传了其中大部分内容。 这本书中描述的咒语中只有少数能起作用。","A book of spells focused on the summoning of beasts. Its pages nip at careless readers' fingers.":"一本专注于野兽召唤术的书。它的书页会夹住粗心读者的手指。","A book of spells used to set off powerful explosions. This edition's binder was careful to pad the cover, so that if its reader lacked sufficient caution, the book, at least, would survive.":"一本关于制造强大爆炸的魔法书。这一版本的装订工小心地给封面包着护垫， 这样即使读者不够小心，至少这本书能保留下来。","A book of works dedicated to the manipulation of blood, both that of the caster and of creatures with particularly unusual ichor flowing through their veins. Some claim it to have been composed by the vampire lord Jory, but it's unclear why he would deign to share his secrets with others.":"一本关于操控血液的书，包括施法者的和血管中流着不寻常灵液的生物的血液。 有些人声称它是由吸血鬼领主乔里创作的， 但不清楚他为什么要屈尊于与他人分享其秘密。","A book containing spells useful for theft, breaking and entering, and other miscellaneous larceny.":"这本书收录了多种关于偷盗、破坏、入室等各种行窃的实用法术。","An introductory text on the magical summoning of beasts and beings from other realms.":"这是一本关于以魔法召唤野兽和异界生物的入门读物。","A book containing a small selection of very basic magic spells, intended for beginners who wish to learn the rudiments of one of the featured magical schools.":"这本书面向想要学习某一特色魔法流派基本原理的初学者， 包含一些非常基础的魔法。","A book of spells that leave the caster's surroundings in a state of complete disarray. It's not clear why anyone would write such a thing, but it's here.":"一本能让施法者周围一片混乱的魔法书。 不清楚为什么会有人写这样的东西，但它就是在这里。","A book containing an introduction to the destructive magical arts of Conjurations.":"一本介绍咒法系破坏性法术的书。","A book describing the creation and use of magical entities best kept at arm's reach. Or, preferably, even farther.":"一本描述创造和利用魔法造物的书。这些魔法实体最好保持在一臂之外， 或者更远。","A manuscript containing dark spells of Necromancy. Each page is filled with grotesque art depicting scenes of disgusting decay.":"一个记载黑暗的死灵术咒语的手稿。 每一页都以怪诞的风格绘满了令人作呕的腐烂场景。","A spellbook containing spells known for having a particularly unpleasant effect on their victims. It's considered something of a faux pas in the wizarding community to be seen with this book in one's collection.":"一本包含能对受击者产生特别不愉快效果的咒语的魔法书。 在巫师界，如果有人看到有谁收藏了这本书，会认为这种行为有失体统。","A book of Necromancy, dictated by the god Kikubaaqudgha to an unfortunate apostle across the course of a nine-day fugue. The necromancer is said to have finished the dread work with their own life's blood... but of course this is just a copy, written in almost entirely normal ink.":"一本死灵之书，由奇库巴库哈神在九天的神游过程中传述给一个不幸的门徒。 据说，死灵法师是用他们的鲜血完成了这个可怕的工作…… 当然，这本书只是副本，几乎完全是用正常的墨水写成的。","A book of spells to bring others closer, or sometimes farther, depending on the user's whim.":"一本能依使用者意愿将他者拉近、或移得更远的法术书。","The somniloquent utterings of a famed mystic, using uniquely bizarre imagery and cryptic digressions to describe spells drawn from the mystic's visions.":"本书收录了一位秘术师在神游时的呓语， 以奇异的意象和迷离的旁逸描述着他眼中浮现的咒语。","A book containing advanced spells in the elemental school of Fire, stolen from the secret college of the djinn.":"这本窃于灯神的秘密学院的书，包含火焰魔法学派的高级咒语。","A book of magic spells.":"一本魔法书。","The standard text used in arcane academies by students of the elemental magic of Fire. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of insulated gloves.":"火焰魔法学徒在奥术学院使用的标准读本。建议读者戴上隔热手套。","A book of magic spells, often used as an introduction to the elemental magics of Ice. Its pages feel unusually brittle, as if they'd crumble at a touch.":"这本魔法书通常用作寒冰魔法的入门读物。它的页面异常地脆，仿佛一碰就碎了。","A book containing basic spells involving the element of Earth. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of gardening gloves.":"这本书收录了与大地元素有关的基础法术。建议读者戴上园艺手套。","A spellbook containing an assortment of powerful Hexes, which sparkles and shimmers as the pages are flipped.":"一本收录了各种强大诅咒系法术的魔法书，翻页时会闪闪发光。","A book of advanced magical spells using the element of Ice. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of warm gloves.":"一本关于运用冰元素的高级魔法书。建议读者戴上暖和的手套。","An ancient, metal-bound spellbook, covered in dark red blotches. Are they rust stains, or..?":"一本用金属装订的古老魔法书，上面有着深红色的斑点。它们是锈斑还是……？","A book that fairly crackles with arcane power.":"这本书上面的奥术能量在噼啪作响。","A spellbook containing a variety of simple but useful magical incantations. Many prominent spellcasters used this book to begin their arcane studies.":"这本魔法书中包含许多简单但实用的咒语。 许多著名的施法者都以这本书入门，开始他们的奥术研究。","A spellbook dedicated to the art of inflicting creative calamities on one's foes. Superstitious wizards claim that the book itself actually absorbs ill fortune and carry it around as a good-luck charm, but the effects of this seem subtle at best.":"这本魔法书致力于创造灾祸，施加到敌人头上。 迷信的巫师声称，这本书实际上是在吸收着厄运，并把它作为护身符随身携带， 但其效果充其量只能说是很微妙。","A macabre book containing basic Necromancy spells. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of gloves they don't mind disposing of afterward.":"这本可怕的书，包含着基础的死灵术。建议读者戴上用后不介意丢掉的手套。","A book containing a variety of fun spells guaranteed to liven up any wizarding party, as well as a number of toasts, jokes, and party games.":"这本书中，包含各种保证能使任何巫师聚会活跃起来的有趣魔法， 还有许多祝酒词、笑话和派对游戏。","A book of powerful and destructive magic spells, rumbling and shuddering with barely-contained energies.":"一本关于强大而具有破坏性的魔法的书，隆隆作响， 因勉强克制着其中的能量而颤动着。","A magical book, blasted and scoured by long exposure to the desert sun. Upon its badly-weathered pages lie the secrets to inflicting the desert's dangers upon the caster's foes.":"这本魔法书长期暴露在沙漠烈日下，已被炙烤侵蚀得破损褪色。 它那饱经风吹日晒的书页上，记载着让施法者的敌人遭受沙漠种种危险的奥秘。","A lazily written book.":"一本懒散地写下的书。","A basic spellbook on the magical field of Translocations. Many would-be mages have seen it disappear just as they needed it most.":"一本关于传送系魔法的初级魔法书。 许多即将成为法师的人在最需要它的时候，它却凭空消失了。","A book covered in glittering sequins. An impromptu lightshow bursts from every page, clearly reserving this book for only the tackiest of wizards.":"这本书上满是闪烁的亮片。每翻动一页就有一阵即兴的灯光秀， 显然它是最俗气的巫师留下的。","A heavy tome written with wildly flammable ink. Care must be taken even opening it, but the power of the spells described therein is undeniable. {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"Its desiccated pages smell faintly of sulphur.\" end }}":"一本厚重的巨著，书写这本书所用的墨水非常易燃， 即便只是打开它也必须要小心，但书中记录的咒语的威力却是毋庸置疑的。 {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"它干燥的书页散发着淡淡的硫磺味。\" end }}","A book containing a well-rounded collection of sphere-related spells. Its final pages begin to describe a spell titled 'Summon Orb of Zot', but sadly, the remainder of the book has been completely vaporised.":"这本书中包含着与球体相关的详尽的咒语。 它的最后几页写着一个名为“召唤佐特宝珠”的咒语， 但遗憾的是，这本书的剩余部分已经完全蒸发了。","A book written by the magician Lan Shi, who was preoccupied with the study and control of natural phenomena. Most of Shi's works have been lost, but those still remaining are treasured by wizards lucky (or unscrupulous) enough to get their hands on a copy.":"这本书由魔法师兰石编写，他致力于研究和控制自然现象。 石的大部分作品已经失传；残存的作品则被那些有幸（或不择手段） 得到副本的巫师珍藏。","A magical book of spells which allow some command over dragons and their aspects.":"一本写有控制龙和其他关于龙的咒语的魔法书。","A book holding lore ripped from distant and untamed lands, allowing their denizens to be called forth to serve the reader. {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"It smells distressingly musty.\" end }}":"这本书收录了从遥远蛮荒之地搜集来的知识， 可召唤那里的生物为读者效力。 {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"它有股难闻的霉味。\" end }}","A guide to drawing immense power from the depths of the earth. The original was written as a collaboration between the hill dwarves and the mountain dwarves, but its compilation was cut short when a massive wave of earthquakes plunged the hill dwarves' civilisation into ruin.":"一本讲解如何从大地深处汲取巨大力量的指南。 原著由丘陵矮人与山地矮人合著，但一场大地震使丘陵矮人文明覆灭， 编纂也因此中断。","A mundane book on hunting. Someone has gone through and covered the book in corrections and scathing criticisms, crossing out entire sections in favour of spells that accomplish the same task.":"一本关于狩猎的平淡无奇的书。 有人翻阅完这本书，所做的修正和严厉的批评涂满了整本书， 甚至还划掉了整个章节，换用了能完成相同任务的咒语。","A book written by a mad wizard, who had become convinced that the moon far above was composed, not of shining light, but of rock as solid as that beneath one's feet. Many of the pages have been mangled beyond recognition, seemingly shredded by a pair of powerful claws... but what would a troll be doing with a spellbook?":"这本书由一位疯狂的巫师所写，他深信天边的月亮不是由闪亮的光构成的， 而是像脚下那样坚硬的岩石构成的。 许多书页已被撕得面目全非，这似乎是被一对有力的爪子撕碎的…… 但巨魔拿着一本魔法书做什么？","A scholarly work, describing the senses used by living creatures to perceive the world around them. A handful of spells are included to demonstrate the principles being described.":"这部学术作品描述生物用来感知周围世界的各种感官。 它包含了一些咒语，以演示其所描述的原理。","A meticulous compendium of research notes, filled with formulae for decomposing and reconstituting all manner of substances. It was written by one of the legendary alchemists among the sludge elves, before that species mysteriously vanished from the world. The author appears to have had a strange obsession with becoming a butterfly, but even if their ultimate aim eluded them, many of the spells detailed therein are nonetheless quite practical.":"一份细致的研究笔记摘要，里面充满了分解和重组各种物质的公式。 它由污泥精灵中一位传奇炼金术士所写，在那个种族神秘地从世界上消失之前。 作者似乎对变成蝴蝶有一种奇怪的痴迷， 但即使他们的最终目标没能实现，书中详述的许多咒语仍然相当实用。","A frost-gripped tome describing icy spells, somewhat abridged. The Vaults are said to hold the full text, but the guardians of that place guard their treasures jealously.":"一部结满冰霜的巨著，上面描写着冰系魔法，有些删节。 据说宝库里藏有全文，但那里的守卫对他们的宝藏严加保护。","A book of advanced Translocations spells, written by a particularly misanthropic mage. After its completion, they were never seen again, which may or may not have been the point.":"一本高级传送系法术书，由一位特别蔑视世人的法师所写。 编写完成后，他们再也没出现过，这可能是也可能不是重点。","A book describing spells requiring very close proximity to their target. The author seems to have had a low opinion of their wizardly peers, and spends much of the text describing the hygiene and social etiquette needed to enter close proximity to other sentient beings.":"这本书描述着需要邻近目标才能施放的咒语。作者似乎对他的同辈巫师评价很低， 还花了大量篇幅描述了接近其他有意识的生物所需的卫生和社交礼仪。","An unholy book describing a variety of magical methods for the creation and command of undead servants.":"这本邪恶的书描述了多种以魔法创造并控制亡灵仆从的方法。","A book of magic spells for creating an assortment of clouds, vapours and mists. It is difficult to read, as the text is frequently interrupted by descriptions of unusually-shaped clouds the author spotted while writing.":"一本关于创造各种云雾和蒸汽的魔法书。 它很难阅读，因为文本经常被打断，作者常常插叙在写作时碰到的奇形怪状的云。","A book of spells used by rebels against an ancient and evil empire. The rebels were crushed, but this book was rediscovered years later, found by paladins of the crusade that finally destroyed the empire and slew its immortal twin sovereigns.":"一本被叛军用来对付一个古老、邪恶的帝国的魔法书。 叛军被击溃，但这本书却被圣战的骑士发现，得以重见天日， 最终帝国覆灭，不朽的孪生君主被杀死。","A book of spells written by the sorceress Ellawe, who sought to use her time productively while trapped inside by particularly harsh weather for over six months. A postscript details the bloody vengeance she took after discovering the weather mage responsible.":"这本魔法书由女术师埃拉薇撰写， 她因特别恶劣的天气而被困在室内六个多月，期间试图充分利用时间。 后记详细记载了她发现罪魁祸首是天气法师后所展开的血腥报复。","A curved, flat, throwing baton designed to return to its user.":"一个弯曲的、扁平的投掷短棒，其设计使它能回到使用者手上。","A box filled with the bizarre leftovers of a depraved wizard's magical experimentations. Opening it might set loose a friendly mutant beast: bizarre creatures, each with their own combination of traits. Increased skill with Evocations will allow stronger beasts to be released.":"这个盒子里满是堕落巫师的奇异实验残留。打开它会释放一只友好的变异兽： 每只奇异的生物都有自己的一套特质。魔力释放技能越强，释放出的野兽就越强。","There are six known traits: * Bat beasts fly and move very quickly, but erratically. * Fire beasts resist and breathe fire. * Ox beasts resist cold, are armoured with thick fur, and can knock back foes. * Shock beasts resist electricity and can transform into living lightning. * Sting beasts resist poison and have a reaching poison-tail attack. * Weird beasts can see invisible and attack with constricting tentacles.":"有六种已知的特质： ＊蝙蝠野兽能飞行且十分迅捷，但行动失序。 ＊火焰野兽能抵抗并喷吐火焰。 ＊公牛野兽耐寒，皮毛厚实，能击退敌人。 ＊电击野兽能抵抗电流并能变形成活体闪电。 ＊刺叮野兽能抵抗毒素，并以可隔格攻击的毒尾刺击敌人。 ＊诡秘野兽能看见隐形并用触手进行束缚攻击。","As far as anyone knows, all beasts have exactly two of these traits.":"众所周知，任何野兽都恰好具有二种特质。","A box filled with the bizarre leftovers of a depraved wizard's magical experimentations. Opening it might set loose a friendly mutant beast: bizarre creatures, each with their own combination of traits. Increased skill with Evocations will allow stronger beasts to be released. There are six known traits: * Bat beasts fly and move very quickly, but erratically. * Fire beasts resist and breathe fire. * Ox beasts resist cold, are armoured with thick fur, and can knock back foes. * Shock beasts resist electricity and can transform into living lightning. * Sting beasts resist poison and have a reaching poison-tail attack. * Weird beasts can see invisible and attack with constricting tentacles. As far as anyone knows, all beasts have exactly two of these traits.":"这个盒子里满是堕落巫师的奇异实验残留。打开它会释放一只友好的变异兽： 每只奇异的生物都有自己的一套特质。魔力释放技能越强，释放出的野兽就越强。 有六种已知的特质： ＊蝙蝠野兽能飞行且十分迅捷，但行动失序。 ＊火焰野兽能抵抗并喷吐火焰。 ＊公牛野兽耐寒，皮毛厚实，能击退敌人。 ＊电击野兽能抵抗电流并能变形成活体闪电。 ＊刺叮野兽能抵抗毒素，并以可隔格攻击的毒尾刺击敌人。 ＊诡秘野兽能看见隐形并用触手进行束缚攻击。 众所周知，任何野兽都恰好具有二种特质。","An axe with langets, spikes, a lengthed haft and a single-bladed crescent head.":"一把带有细金属条、尖刺和一个月牙状的刃的长柄斧子。","A small piece of wood and metal, to be strapped on one arm for defence.":"一小块木头和金属，通过绑在一只手臂上进行防御。","A suit of armour made entirely out of tiny metal rings.":"一件完全用小金属环制成的护甲。","A cloth cloak.":"一件布披风。","A heavy piece of wood. While clubs are rather primitive weapons, bashing someone's skull in with one remains a very popular and effective means of dispute resolution.":"一块沉重的木头。虽然棍棒是相当原始的武器， 但猛击某人的头颅仍是解决争端的一种十分流行且有效的方法。","A magical device that condenses ambient energy into various destructive clouds. When evoked these clouds form around hostile monsters near the user. The quantity and lethality of these clouds increases with Evocations skill. At low power it will create noxious fumes, and as power increases this gives way to roaring flames, freezing vapours, and poisonous gas. At the highest tiers of power storm clouds, acidic fog and clouds of excruciating misery become available.":"这件魔法装置能将周围的能量凝结成各种具有破坏性的云。 激活时，这些云会在使用者附近的敌对怪物周围形成。 云的数量和杀伤力会随魔力释放技能的提升而增加。 威力较低时，它会生成毒烟；随着威力提高，毒烟会让位于咆哮的烈焰、冰冻蒸汽和毒气。 威力处于最高几档时，还可生成风暴云、酸雾和带来极度痛苦的云雾。","A corpse. Useless and dead.":"一具尸体。没有用处、没有生命。","An incredibly heavy but extremely effective suit of crystalline armour.":"这件水晶护甲重得吓人，但防护效果也非常好。","A double-edged fighting knife with a sharp point.":"一把尖端锐利的双刃格斗短刀。","A thin piece of metal, typically coated in some harmful substance. When thrown it can deliver its toxins into the bloodstream of a living or demonic being.":"一个薄金属片，通常上面会涂有一些有害物质。 当投掷它时，会将其中的毒素传递到生物或恶魔的血液中。","A decaying skeleton.":"一具正在腐烂的骷髅。","A deck of magical cards, most of which hurl death and destruction at one's foes (or, if unlucky, at oneself).":"一副魔法卡牌， 其中的大部分牌会向你的敌人投射死亡和毁灭（或向你自己，如果倒霉的话）。","A deck of magical cards, mainly dealing with various forms of escape.":"一副魔法卡牌，主要用于多种形式的逃脱。","A deck of magical cards which wreak havoc on the user.":"一副魔法卡牌，向使用者带来灾难。","A deck of magical cards, depicting a range of weird and wonderful creatures.":"一副魔法卡牌，上面描绘了一系列怪异而不可思议的生物。","A terrible weapon, forged in the fires of Hell.":"一件可怕的武器，在地狱之火中锻造而成。","A terrible three-pronged weapon, moulded by fire and brimstone.":"一件可怕的有着三股叉的武器，由火和硫磺铸成。","A terrible weapon, woven in the depths of the inferno.":"一件可怕的武器，在炼狱深处编织而成。","A flail with long spikes and a heavy head.":"一把具有长刺和沉重头部的连枷。","A fearsome weapon with a forked, razor-sharp blade.":"一把刀刃分叉、极其锐利的可怕的武器。","An intricate carving, inlaid with dragon tooth and scale. {{ local desc = \"Transforms the wearer into a mighty\"":"一件精致的雕刻品，镶嵌着龙牙和龙鳞。{{ local desc = \"将使用者变为一条强大的\"","if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \" dragon. The wearer retains their innate colour, \" .. \"becomes resistant to poison, and their breath weapon's \" .. \"power and recharge rate are greatly increased.\" else desc = desc .. \" golden dragon. The wearer becomes resistant to fire, \" .. \"cold, and poison, and gains a powerful breath attack \" .. \"that inflicts all three types of damage at once, but \" .. \"only recharges as you gain XP.\" end return desc }}":"if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \"龙。使用者将保留其固有的颜色，获得毒抗，\" .. \"并且其吐息攻击的威力和充能速度将大幅提升。\" else desc = desc .. \"金龙。使用者将获得火抗、寒抗和毒抗，\" .. \"并获得一种强大的吐息攻击，能同时造成这三种类型的伤害，\" .. \"但只能通过获取经验值来充能。\" end return desc }}","An intricate carving, inlaid with dragon tooth and scale. {{ local desc = \"Transforms the wearer into a mighty\" if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \" dragon. The wearer retains their innate colour, \" .. \"becomes resistant to poison, and their breath weapon's \" .. \"power and recharge rate are greatly increased.\" else desc = desc .. \" golden dragon. The wearer becomes resistant to fire, \" .. \"cold, and poison, and gains a powerful breath attack \" .. \"that inflicts all three types of damage at once, but \" .. \"only recharges as you gain XP.\" end return desc }}":"一件精致的雕刻品，镶嵌着龙牙和龙鳞。{{ local desc = \"将使用者变为一条强大的\" if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \"龙。使用者将保留其固有的颜色，获得毒抗，\" .. \"并且其吐息攻击的威力和充能速度将大幅提升。\" else desc = desc .. \"金龙。使用者将获得火抗、寒抗和毒抗，\" .. \"并获得一种强大的吐息攻击，能同时造成这三种类型的伤害，\" .. \"但只能通过获取经验值来充能。\" end return desc }}","Deep within this gem, flowing leaves and swaying branches seem to lurk. And here, a bone picked clean - there, a predator's eyes, staring hungrily out..?":"在这颗宝石的深处，似乎暗藏着飘垂的树叶和摇曳的树枝。 而在这边，有一根剔得干干净净的骨头—— 那边，有一个捕食者的眼睛，在贪婪地盯着外面……？","A rotten eggplant which you can throw at the Crawl developers. It's a bug if you ever see this message.":"一个腐烂的茄子，你可以把它丢向Crawl的开发者。 如果你碰到它，说明遇到错误了。","A sacred blade from the forges of Heaven, inhabited by a good spirit. It is a favoured weapon of the Shining One's servants.":"一把在天堂中锻成的圣刃，其中寄居着一个善灵。 这件武器深受光辉者的信徒喜爱。","The opposite of a morningstar. A balanced mace with a long shaft and a metal head covered in lethal spikes.":"晨星锤的对应物。一把配重均衡的钉头锤，长柄，金属锤头上覆有致命的尖刺。","A book of magical spells, meticulously organised, dense, and almost entirely burnt black. Only a few pages are still legible, but the power within still blasts the reader with a furnace-like heat.":"一本魔法书，精心编排，密密麻麻，却几乎完全被烧成黑色。 只有几页仍清晰可辨，但其中的力量仍以火炉般的热浪扑向读者。","A fearsome weapon covered in dried blood and crude engravings of torture and death, bearing an enormous axehead.":"一件可怕的武器，上面有着凝固的血和关于酷刑与死亡的粗糙雕刻， 带有一个巨大的斧头。","A long single-edged sword with a slightly curved blade.":"一把长长的单刃剑，刀刃略微弯曲。","A collection of spells once used by the great swamp civilisations.":"伟大的沼泽文明使用过的法术合集。","A small figurine made of some strange material, shaped like a stepped pyramid. It is remarkably detailed – almost like a real, vast structure, shrunk somehow smaller than a human hand.":"一个由某种奇特物质制成的小雕像，形状像带有阶梯的金字形神塔。 它非常细致——比人手还小，却几乎像是以某种方式由真实、巨大的建筑缩放而来的。","The scales of a fire-breathing dragon. It provides great protection from fire, while rendering its wearer more susceptible to cold.":"吐息火焰之龙的鳞甲。 它能够提供极好的火抗，也致使它的穿戴者更易受到寒冷的影响。","A mace with a short chain connecting the head to the haft.":"一把用短链把锤头连在柄上的钉头锤。","A stone of unearthly beauty and almost immeasurable value outside the dungeon. Within its confines, it is utterly useless.":"一块来自地牢之外美丽绝伦、价值难以估量的石头。在它的范围内，它是完全无用的。","Zot hoards these gems jealously, and will spitefully smash them soon after an adventurer enters the branch of the Dungeon in which they rest. Still, a very quick-moving adventurer might seize one first and keep its precious shards. Zot cannot track gems outside their home branches, so with truly astonishing speed, it might be possible to abscond with one still intact... but such a feat is difficult to credit, and likely pointless besides.":"佐特小心翼翼地贮藏着这些宝石， 一旦冒险者进入存在宝石的地牢分支，佐特就会恶意地打碎相应宝石。 然而，一个行动极其迅速的冒险者有机会抓到一个宝石，并保留其珍贵的碎片。 佐特无法在存放宝石的原分支之外继续追踪它， 因此，如果有真正惊人的速度，是有可能带着一颗完好无损的宝石成功逃脱…… 然而这样的壮举简直是天方夜谭，而且可能毫无意义。","Once the Orb of Zot is taken, Zot will be unable to smash any gems.":"一旦佐特宝珠被拿走，佐特将无法打碎任何宝石。","A stone of unearthly beauty and almost immeasurable value outside the dungeon. Within its confines, it is utterly useless. Zot hoards these gems jealously, and will spitefully smash them soon after an adventurer enters the branch of the Dungeon in which they rest. Still, a very quick-moving adventurer might seize one first and keep its precious shards. Zot cannot track gems outside their home branches, so with truly astonishing speed, it might be possible to abscond with one still intact... but such a feat is difficult to credit, and likely pointless besides. Once the Orb of Zot is taken, Zot will be unable to smash any gems.":"一块来自地牢之外美丽绝伦、价值难以估量的石头。在它的范围内，它是完全无用的。 佐特小心翼翼地贮藏着这些宝石， 一旦冒险者进入存在宝石的地牢分支，佐特就会恶意地打碎相应宝石。 然而，一个行动极其迅速的冒险者有机会抓到一个宝石，并保留其珍贵的碎片。 佐特无法在存放宝石的原分支之外继续追踪它， 因此，如果有真正惊人的速度，是有可能带着一颗完好无损的宝石成功逃脱…… 然而这样的壮举简直是天方夜谭，而且可能毫无意义。 一旦佐特宝珠被拿走，佐特将无法打碎任何宝石。","A giant lump of wood.":"一块非常大的木头。","A giant lump of wood with sharp spikes at one end.":"一个巨型木棒，一端装有尖木刺。","A pole with a large, heavy blade on one end.":"杆子一端有着又大又重的刀刃。","The scales of a golden dragon. It is much heavier than most dragon scale armours, and grants its wearer resistance to poison, fire and cold.":"一套金龙鳞甲。它比大多数龙鳞甲重得多，但能给穿戴者提供毒抗、火抗、寒抗。","A pile of glittering gold coins.":"一堆闪闪发亮的金币。","A heavy stone icon, bearing the countenance of some long-forgotten king or god. Transforms the wearer into a slow, stone statue. The wearer's stone body is immune to poison and miasma, and gains resistance to electricity, negative energy, and torment. Shapeshifting skill increases armour granted.":"一个沉重的石符，上面有一个被遗忘已久的国王或是神明的头像。 它能将使用者变成一个缓慢的石像。 使用者的石质身躯免疫毒和瘴气，并获得对电、负能量和折磨的抗性。 提升变形术技能可以增加该形态赋予的护甲。","A book describing how the mighty among summoners can bend to their will the terrible things from betwixt the planes. Many have been the unwary souls, however, who have toyed with this tome and been driven mad by unimaginable eldritch horrors.":"这本书讲述强大的召唤者如何使位面夹缝中的可怖存在屈从于自己的意志。 然而，许多轻率摆弄此书的人都被难以想象的异界恐怖逼疯。","An enormous metal war club, of great cumbrousness.":"一根巨型金属战棍，非常笨重。","A sword with a very long, heavy blade and a long handle.":"一把有着长柄和很长的沉重剑刃的剑。","A collection of spells from great wizards throughout history. The author seems to have been extremely enthusiastic, and each wizard is described in voluminous, comprehensive detail.":"历史上伟大巫师的咒语集。作者似乎非常热情， 对每个巫师都有浩繁、全面的描述。","A collection of spells from great wizards throughout history. The author seems to have been quite tired of their project - the wizards' descriptions are terse and minimal, meeting the lowest requirement for completeness.":"历史上伟大巫师的咒语集。作者似乎对他们的项目已经厌倦了—— 对巫师的描述简明扼要，只是满足了对完整性的最低要求。","A polearm consisting of an axe blade topped with a spike, mounted on a long shaft.":"一把长柄武器，在长柄的顶端，有一个带刺的斧刃。","A blunt striking weapon, essentially equivalent to a mace.":"一把钝击武器，基本上相当于权杖。","A small axe.":"一把小斧头。","A machine that fires metal slugs via applied thaumaturgy. Some enchant their projectiles to fall forward instead of down, others bewitch the slugs with a fatal attraction to their targets. All are slow, loud, and blast out thick smoke with each shot.":"一个运用了奇术用于发射弹药的器械。 一些人为弹药附魔，使其向前而不是向下坠落； 另一些人为弹药附加了致命的朝向目标的引力。 所有手炮都缓慢、响亮，每次发射都会喷出浓烟。","A cloth hat.":"一顶布帽。","A piece of metal headgear.":"一个金属头盔。","The horn belonging to Geryon, guardian of the Vestibule of Hell. It has the power to call forth demonic beasts. With high Evocations skill, it will call greater numbers of beasts, with lower chances of those beasts being hostile.":"这个号角属于格律翁，他是地狱前庭的守卫者。它能够用来召唤恶魔野兽。 魔力释放技能越高，它就能召唤更多的野兽， 并且这些野兽是敌对的几率也会更低。","A piece of cloth and leather for launching stones, adequate for hunting small game like rabbits or goblins.":"一段用来发射石头的布料和皮革，能够猎捕小型猎物，诸如兔子和地精。","The scales of a cold-breathing dragon. It provides great protection from cold, while rendering its wearer more susceptible to fire.":"吐息寒冰之龙的鳞甲。 它能够提供极好的寒抗，也致使它的穿戴者更易受到火的影响。","Countless spirits swirl around this gem, shrouding it in a bone-deep chill. Unwelcome in the Good gods' afterlife, they find here a heaven of their own.":"无数灵体围绕着这颗宝石旋转，将它笼罩在彻骨的寒意中。 在善神转生之后，它们变得不受欢迎，但在这里找到了自己的天堂。","Sigils of fire burn deep within this gem, symbol of the eternal compact between naga and salamander. Their bond is that of the poison which scourges the impure and the flame which burns away impurity.":"这颗宝石的深处燃烧着火焰的印记，它象征着纳迦和火蜥蜴之间永恒的契约。 他们的结合是毒与火的结合，毒液责罚着腐化之物，火焰烧除着罪恶之物。","A lightweight spear, designed for throwing. It will pass through the targets it hits, potentially hitting all targets in its path until it reaches maximum range. {{ if you.race() == \"Kobold\" or you.race() == \"Spriggan\" then return \"Unfortunately, it is too long and awkward for you to use.\" end }}":"这根轻型矛是为投掷而设计的。 它将击穿目标，并有可能击中其路径中的所有目标，直到达到最大射程。 {{ if you.race() == \"Kobold\" or you.race() == \"Spriggan\" then return \"很遗憾，对于你来说它太长了，不方便使用。\" end }}","A piece of wood and metal, to be strapped on one arm for defence.":"一块木头和金属，通过绑在一只手臂上进行防御。","A very rare and extremely effective weapon, featuring a pole with half-moon blades at both ends.":"一把十分罕见而极为高效的武器，杆子的两端各有一个半月形的刃。","A very large and very heavy stone. {{ if you.race() == \"Ogre\" or you.race() == \"Troll\" then return \"\" else return \"Only large creatures are capable of throwing it.\" end }}":"一块沉重的巨石。{{ if you.race() == \"Ogre\" or you.race() == \"Troll\" then return \"\" else return \"只有大型生物才能投掷它。\" end }}","A suit made from layers of tanned animal hide. It provides basic protection with almost no hindrance to spellcasting or stealthy movement.":"这件护甲是用几层鞣过的动物皮做成的。 穿着它几乎不会对施法或潜行造成阻碍，不过它只能提供一点最基础的防护。","A rod that allows its wielder to fire unavoidable blasts of lightning. Consecutive evocations cause the discharge to be sustained, which increases the power level up to four times and allows the blast to be redirected to affect an area. The strength of the blast increases with Evocations skill and, for redirected blasts, decreases with the size of the affected area.":"这根杆子能让使用者射出无法闪避的闪电冲击。 连续激活将使其释出的能量增强，直至达到四倍的强度， 同时能够改变方向来攻击一整片区域。冲击的强度随魔力释放技能的提高而提高， 变换了方向的冲击会随受影响区域的扩大而减弱。","A sword with a long, slashing blade.":"一把长而凌厉的剑。","A long, strong bow made of yew.":"一张紫杉制成的长而坚固的弓。","A short club with a metal head.":"一根带金属头的短棒。","A valuable book which allows one to learn a certain skill faster.":"一本很有用的书，能让人更快地学习某种技能。","A loosely bound collection of the infamous Maxwell's schemes, diagrams and plans. Amidst messages written to and by his many minions, allies of convenience and hated rivals, a patient reader can discover spells of electrifying power.":"一本松散的装订集，收录着臭名昭著的麦克斯韦的草图、图表和计划。 在与他的众多下属、处得来的友人和讨厌的竞争对手的往来信息中， 耐心的读者可以发现电能的咒语。","A miniature, desiccated head of some ferocious and hopefully extinct creature. Transforms the wearer's midsection into a giant mouth, gnashing and ready to devour foes. This maw confers a powerful bite attack which scales additionally with the wearer's own strength and can devour slain creatures to temporariy increase one's regeneration. Unfortunately, it also confers such profound hunger that it can be difficult to pull oneself away from particularly appetising foes.":"某种凶猛而且但愿已经灭绝的生物的干缩头颅。 它能将使用者的腹部变成一个咬牙切齿、准备吞食敌人的大嘴。 这张大嘴能赋予强大的咬击，其伤害还会随使用者的力量进一步提升， 并且可以吞食被杀死的生物来暂时提升使用者的再生速度。 不幸的是，它也会带来极度的饥饿感，让人难以摆脱特别诱人的敌人。","The stoneborn brought forth this gem from the uttermost depths of the earth as a gift and a warning: beware Zot! That it lies now within Zot's power is a sure proof of the perversity of mortals and fate alike.":"石裔从大地的深处带来了这块宝石作为礼物和警告：当心佐特！ 而它现在掌握在佐特的手中，这无疑证实了凡人的堕落，一如它的命运。","Smooth as a spider's silk, white as the eyes of some crawling thing which has lived too long in the dark, this gem buzzes with a fearful potential. Still, to a certain eye, it possesses a strange allure...":"这颗宝石光滑得像蜘蛛丝，白得像久居黑暗的爬行动物的眼睛， 嗡嗡作响，充满了可怕的潜能。 尽管如此，在某种程度上，它具有一种奇怪的吸引力……","A mace with a head covered in short spikes.":"一把锤头覆有短刺的钉头锤。","Though it drips with mud and muck, still a peculiar dignity attaches itself to this gem. The people of the Swamp, who first carried this stone, struggled against insurmountable odds. They failed, but there is much to admire even in the ruin of their efforts.":"尽管这颗宝石滴着泥浆和淤泥，但它仍带着一种特殊的高贵气质。 最先拿起这块石头的沼泽居民曾与不可逾越的困难作了斗争。 他们失败了，但即使他们的努力付之东流，也有很多值得钦佩的地方。","An extremely rare book, powerful and sinister. Many foolhardy magicians have tried to study this tome, only to find themselves entangled within necromantic forces they could not hope to control.":"一本极为罕见的书，强大而邪恶。许多鲁莽的魔法师试图研究这本巨著， 却发现自己已陷入了他们无法控制的亡灵力量之中。","A sphere of crystal, carried in place of a shield. Magic scintillates within its interior.":"一个水晶球，可拿在装备盾牌的位置。魔法在里面闪烁着。","An invaluable artefact. Once you have escaped to the surface with it, your quest is complete.":"一个无价之宝。只要你能带着它逃到地面，你的任务就宣告完成。","A recurved bow, crudely crafted from troll-bone and warg hair. The cave orcs' use of archery, so unlike their surface-dwelling ancestors, shows the influence of their elvish allies.":"这把反曲弓是用巨魔的骨头和座狼的毛发粗糙地制作而成。 洞穴兽人与那些居住在地表的表亲不同，他们掌握着箭术， 这表明他们受到了精灵盟友的影响。","A pair of boots. They are worn on the feet, and cover all but the largest hooves and talons.":"一双靴子。它们要穿在脚上，一般是合身的，除非是最大的蹄子或爪子。","A pair of gloves. They are worn on the hands, and cover all but the largest claws.":"一双手套。它们要戴在手上，一般是合身的，除非是最大的爪子。","The nacreous scales of a pearl dragon. It grants its wearer resistance to negative energies.":"一套珍珠龙的珍珠质鳞甲。它赋予穿戴者对负能量的抗性。","A hand mirror which can create a reflection of a nearby creature, clouding in the process. The reflection's duration increases with Evocations skill and decreases with the willpower of the target. It is, invariably, slightly weaker than the creature it mirrors.":"这面手镜能创造附近生物的镜像，镜面也会在过程中变得浑浊。 镜像的持续时间随魔力释放技能的提升而增加，随目标的意志力越强而减少。 它总是比它所映射的生物稍弱些。","An enchanted vessel of elemental water. Removing the stopper unleashes a torrent of water, smashing the target and flooding the nearby area. If any creatures engulfed by the wave need air to breathe, they'll be unable to cast spells until they recover. The strength of the torrent and the duration of the flooding increase with Evocations skill.":"一个充满水元素的魔法容器。 取下塞子，小瓶会释出洪流，将对目标造成伤害，并淹没周围地区。 如果有需要呼吸空气的生物被波浪吞没，在恢复正常前，他们将无法施法。 洪流的威力和淹水持续时间会随魔力释放技能提升。","A full suit of solid metal plate: cuirass, pauldrons, vambraces, waist plate and greaves. It provides excellent protection.":"一整套实心金属板：胸甲、护肩、臂甲、腰甲和胫甲。它提供了出色的保护。","A strange substance, produced by ghost moths. Consuming it causes regeneration of health and magic, along with total befuddlement. The two effects are fundamentally linked – the regeneration ends the moment the confusion does.":"其中的奇怪物质，是由鬼蛾产生的。 饮用它，会恢复生命值和法力，但也会让人完全混乱。 这两个效果根本相连——混乱一结束，生命值与法力恢复也会立即停止。","A potion which can send one into an incoherent rage, granting them a great but temporary increase to their health, damage, and speed. In exchange, their mind is clouded by anger, only allowing them to move and attack in melee. The rage will wear off quickly if they do not attack monsters, and upon expiry, the imbiber will be fatigued, causing them to slow dramatically and rendering them unable to berserk again for a short duration.":"这瓶药水能让饮用者陷入一种失去理智的狂暴状态， 极大地但暂时地提升其生命值、伤害力和速度。 作为代价，他们的心智会被愤怒所蒙蔽，只能进行移动和近战攻击。 如果不攻击怪物，狂暴状态会迅速消退；状态结束后，饮用者将陷入疲惫， 行动大幅减缓，并在短时间内无法再次狂暴。","A potion which increases the power of the drinker's spells and halves their magic cost (rounding up).":"饮用这瓶药水会提高饮用者的法术威力，并且法力消耗减半（向上取整）。","A potion which ends most magical effects, good or bad, affecting one who drinks it. It also reduces magical contamination.":"这瓶药水对饮用它的人来说，能终结大多数或好或坏的魔法效果。 它也能减少魔法污染。","A potion which restores a small amount of health, and cures poison and confusion.":"这瓶药水能回复少量健康值，并治疗中毒和混乱。","A potion which uplifts both the body and mind of its drinkers, lifting them from the ground and increasing their Will to resist the world's temptations.":"这瓶药水能够提升饮用者的身心， 将他们从地面升起，并增强他们抵抗世间诱惑的意志力。","A truly wonderful and very rare drink, which grants experience when consumed.":"一瓶非常罕见的极佳饮品，饮用时能给予经验。","An enchanted beverage which speeds the actions of anyone who drinks it.":"这种魔力饮料，能加快饮用者的行动速度。","A magical healing elixir which causes wounds to close and heal almost instantly.":"一个神奇的疗伤灵药，能使伤口立刻愈合。","A potion which confers invisibility on one who consumes it.":"这瓶药水能让饮用者隐形。","A potion which transforms the imbiber into an animated tree with sap for blood and branches capable of holding weapons. Such a tree has minimal evasion but increased health and natural armour, and is resistant to poison, and immune to torment and drowning. However, it is rooted in place while the transformation lasts, and cannot teleport.":"这瓶药水能临时将饮用者变为会动的树，其枝干能持握武器。 变成树会更难闪避，但生命值和自身防护得到增强，有了毒抗，并免疫折磨和溺水。 然而，当处于这种形态时，会扎根原地，无法传送。","A valuable potion which grants an infusion of magical energy.":"这是瓶很有用的药水，它能注入魔力。","A potion which greatly increases the power of the drinker's melee attacks.":"这瓶药水能大幅提升饮用者近战攻击的威力。","A potion which mutates the drinker, removing several mutations then granting a few random mutations, which are likely (but not guaranteed) to be beneficial.":"这瓶药水会使饮用者发生突变：先移除数个突变，再赋予数个随机突变； 后者很可能有益，但并无保证。","A potion which grants temporary resistance to a variety of harmful effects: fire, cold, electricity, poison, and acid.":"这瓶药水能暂时地赋予饮用者对一些有害效果的抗性：火、寒、电、毒和酸。","A potion which makes the drinker attract enemies, translocating them quickly closer for the duration of the effect. The effect is surprisingly subtle, and unwary victims may sleep through it entirely.":"这瓶药水能让饮用者引来敌人，在效果持续时间能迅速将敌人拉到更近的地方。 其效果十分微妙，不警觉的、受影响的怪物可能仍在沉睡。","Shining with every colour of the rainbow and a few others besides, some consider this gem 'a bit tacky'. Preposterous!":"这颗宝石闪耀着彩虹色和其他几种颜色，但一些人认为这颗宝石“有点俗气”。真是荒唐！","A mysterious item resembling a rune of some kind. Once evoked, it will make the user glow blue and add a reverb to all sound... and there may be other effects as well.":"一个看上去像是某种符文的神秘物品。 激活它会导致使用者身上发出蓝光并能给所有声音加入混响……也许还有其他效果。","A sturdy wooden pole, meant for fighting.":"一根结实的用于战斗的木棍。","The scales of a quicksilver dragon. Although it does not provide its wearer with as much protection as the scales of some heavier dragons, it is somewhat lighter and less encumbering. The armour repels both attacks on the wearer's willpower and magical modification of itself - it cannot be enchanted.":"一套水银龙鳞甲。尽管它不像一些更重的龙的鳞甲那样， 能为穿戴者提供更多的防护，但它却更轻便、妨碍也更少。 这套盔甲会抵抗对穿戴者意志力的攻击， 但也会抵抗针对自身的魔法改造——它不能被附魔。","A dagger with an uncanny enchantment upon it, allowing it to strike twice for every blow its wielder makes. It takes great skill to use to its full potential.":"这把带有不可思议的魔力的匕首，能让使用者一次发动双重攻击。 但需要高超的技巧才能发挥其全部潜力。","A slender, sharply pointed sword, with an uncommonly elegant design.":"一把纤细、尖锐的剑，有着非凡的优雅设计。","A light leather suit reinforced with a covering of metal rings. It is protective in combat, but slightly uncomfortable due to the added weight.":"一件覆有金属环的轻质皮革护甲。它在战斗中能提供防护， 但因重量的增加而略有妨碍。","A ring that increases the dexterity of its wearer.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者的敏捷。","A ring that makes its wearer more capable of avoiding attacks.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者躲避攻击的能力。","A ring that grants its wearer flight.":"这枚戒指能赋予佩戴者飞行的能力。","A ring that increases the intelligence of its wearer.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者的智力。","A ring that protects its wearer from the effects of acid and corrosion.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵抗酸和腐蚀。","A ring that increases its wearer's reserves of magical power for so long as it is worn.":"这枚戒指能增加佩戴者的法力储备。","A ring that protects its wearer from poison.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵抗毒。","A ring that protects its wearer from the effects of negative energy.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵抗负能量。","A ring that protects its wearer from most sources of damage.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵挡大多数种类的伤害。","A ring that protects its wearer from cold.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵抗寒冷。","A ring that protects its wearer from fire.":"这枚戒指能帮助佩戴者抵抗火焰。","A ring that increases its wearer's willpower, protecting against certain magical effects.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者的意志力，以抵御某些魔法。","A ring that allows its wearer to see invisible things.":"这枚戒指能让佩戴者看见隐形的东西。","A ring that increases the wearer's accuracy and damage with ranged weapons and melee attacks.":"这枚戒指会增加佩戴者使用远程武器和近战的命中率和攻击力。","A ring that increases the strength of its wearer.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者的力量。","A ring that increases the success rate of its wearer's magical spells.":"这枚戒指能提升佩戴者施法的成功率。","A large, loose-fitting, wide-sleeved outer garment made of light cloth. It offers little protection against physical harm, but does not hinder evasion or spellcasting.":"一件有着宽袖的宽松大件外套，由轻质布料制成。 它几乎无法防备物理伤害，但不会妨碍闪避或施法。","A charm which allows entry into the Realm of Zot.":"这个神符是打开佐特领域大门的钥匙。","A woven silk bag. Opening it will cover the area with webs, spiders, and other skittering things. Evocations skill increases spider quality, quantity and webbing.":"一个用丝绸织成的袋子。打开它，蛛网、蜘蛛和其他爬虫会覆盖这片区域。 魔力释放技能会提高蜘蛛的质量与数量，并增加蛛网覆盖。","A blessed weapon, woven by the saints in Heaven and hated by the unholy. It is a favoured weapon of the Shining One's servants.":"这是一把神圣的武器，由天堂的圣徒所编织，并被邪恶者憎恨。 这件武器深受光辉者的信徒喜爱。","They who smote down Death herself and buried themselves in a Tomb of their own making were not shy of their ambitions. Fain to seize upon baubles and overweening proud, their Lord journeyed into their eternal unrest with this gem upon their breast.":"一些人击败了死神，把自己埋在自己建造的坟墓里，而且并不耻于自己的野心。 他们的主出于对小玩意儿的喜好和自负，把这颗宝石戴在胸前， 进入了他们永恒的动荡之中。","A leather suit covered with metal plates attached to each other in overlapping rows to provide full protection, but at the cost of reduced freedom of movement.":"一套皮革护甲，表面覆盖着相互重叠成排的金属片，能提供充分防护， 但代价是会对行动造成不便。","A length of stylish fabric. At its creation, enchantments were woven into it, and as such it cannot accept further enchantment.":"一段时髦的织物。在制作它时，已经织入了魔法，因此它不能继续附魔。","A long sword with a wide, curved blade.":"一把具有弯曲阔刃的长剑。","A wonderful scroll which causes the creation of a valuable item, with the reader choosing from a small selection. The items offered will often be a good match for the reader's skills; and if nothing recommends itself, the reader can always choose a heap of gold.":"这张奇妙的卷轴，可以让读者选择要创建的物品类型， 从而凭空创造出一件珍贵的物品。所提供的物品通常与读者的技能非常匹配； 如果它推荐的东西没什么有用的，读者总是可以选择要一大堆金子。","A scroll that allows its reader to selectively erase one spell from memory to recapture the magical energy bound up with it.":"这张卷轴能让读者选择遗忘一个法术， 从而释放被该法术占用的记忆容量。","A scroll that allows its reader to teleport a short distance, with precise control.":"这张卷轴能够让读者进行一次精确的短距离传送。","A scroll that imbues a weapon with a random brand. Any existing brand will be replaced with a different one, and any brand forbidden by your current god will not be chosen. Artefacts cannot be branded in this way.":"这张卷轴能给武器加上一个随机的铭印。 任何已有的铭印会被一个不同的替代，且不会加上你当前的神所抵触的铭印。 神器无法以这种方式获得铭印。","Melee weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy, venom or protection brand (or with the special brand exclusive to the category of weapon being branded), and rarely with the draining, electrocution, spectral, vampiric or chaos brand.":"近战武器通常会获得火焰、冰冻、重击、淬毒或防护铭印， （或该类武器专属的特殊铭印），但很少会被印上汲取、电击、幽魂、吸血或混沌铭印。","Ranged weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy or draining brand, and rarely with the electrocution or chaos brand.":"远程武器通常会获得火焰、冰冻、重击或汲取铭印， 但很少会获得电击或混沌铭印。","A scroll that imbues a weapon with a random brand. Any existing brand will be replaced with a different one, and any brand forbidden by your current god will not be chosen. Artefacts cannot be branded in this way. Melee weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy, venom or protection brand (or with the special brand exclusive to the category of weapon being branded), and rarely with the draining, electrocution, spectral, vampiric or chaos brand. Ranged weapons will commonly be branded with the flaming, freezing, heavy or draining brand, and rarely with the electrocution or chaos brand.":"这张卷轴能给武器加上一个随机的铭印。 任何已有的铭印会被一个不同的替代，且不会加上你当前的神所抵触的铭印。 神器无法以这种方式获得铭印。 近战武器通常会获得火焰、冰冻、重击、淬毒或防护铭印， （或该类武器专属的特殊铭印），但很少会被印上汲取、电击、幽魂、吸血或混沌铭印。 远程武器通常会获得火焰、冰冻、重击或汲取铭印， 但很少会获得电击或混沌铭印。","A scroll that surrounds its user with a flight of beautiful butterflies, blowing back other creatures nearby with the flapping of their wings.":"这张卷轴，能让使用者周围环绕着一群美丽的蝴蝶， 蝴蝶扇动翅膀，将附近其他生物吹退。","A scroll that places an enchantment on a piece of armour chosen by the reader. Body armour and bardings can be enchanted up to the same value as their base armour rating. Bucklers, kite shields and tower shields can be enchanted up to +3, +5 or +8 respectively, and other armour can be enchanted up to +2. Magical artefacts cannot be enchanted at all.":"这张卷轴，能让读者选择一件防具进行附魔。 铠甲和马铠可以附魔至与其自身护甲等级相同的值。 小圆盾、鸢盾和塔盾分别可以附魔至＋3、＋5或＋8，其他防具可以附魔至＋2。 神器无法继续附魔。","A scroll that places an enchantment on a weapon chosen by the reader, increasing both accuracy and damage. Weapons can be enchanted up to +9. Magical artefacts cannot be enchanted at all.":"这张卷轴，能让读者选择一件武器进行附魔，同时提升命中和伤害。 武器最多能附魔至＋9。神器无法继续附魔。","A scroll that causes great fear in nearby foes, causing them to flee until attacked, cornered, or enough time has passed. Non-living, undead and plant monsters cannot be feared, and berserk or frenzied monsters are also immune.":"这张卷轴能极大地震慑附近的敌人，使他们逃跑， 除非他们受到攻击、走投无路或是已经过去了足够长的时间。 没有生命的、亡灵和植物类怪物不会吓到，狂暴或疯狂的怪物也对此免疫。","A scroll that surrounds the reader with a dense cloud of fog, which can block vision temporarily. The fog takes a short time to fully spill out.":"这张卷轴能在读者身边生成一层浓雾，暂时阻挡视线。 浓雾需要短暂时间才能完全扩散开来。","A useful magic scroll which identifies the properties of any unknown object.":"这张有用的魔法卷轴，可以鉴定任何未知物品的属性。","A scroll that fills the creatures around the reader with an unstable and powerful inner flame. This fire is released any time the victims are hit, and explosively released upon their death. Giant creatures cause bigger explosions.":"卷轴令读者周围的生物充满强大而不稳定的内焰。 受害者每次被击中时都会释放火焰，死亡时则爆炸性释放； 巨型生物能造成更大的爆炸。","A prank scroll that creates a loud noise when read.":"这个卷轴在阅读时会恶作剧般地制造大量噪音。","A scroll that fills the air with poison, covering every unoccupied space in sight with toxic fumes.":"这张卷轴能用于弥漫毒气，视线中每一个空置的空间都会被毒烟填充。","A scroll that reveals its reader's surroundings. The layout of the current floor is fully mapped, and everything within a moderate radius, including both visible and invisible monsters, is momentarily shown.":"这张卷轴能显现读者的周围环境。它会展现出当前楼层的所有布局， 并立刻揭示出一定范围内的所有东西，包括可见和隐形的怪物。","A scroll that eliminates all sound near the reader. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible in the reader's vicinity.":"这张卷轴可以消除读者周围的所有声音。 这使读者附近无法阅读卷轴、施放法术、调用神圣能力或喊叫。","Certain monsters have innate magical or special abilities which will still be usable while silenced.":"某些怪物具有与生俱来的魔法或特殊能力，即使被沉默也能使用。","The effect starts out with a large radius, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the reader, before it times out.":"起始的生效范围较大，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者，直到完全失效。","A scroll that eliminates all sound near the reader. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible in the reader's vicinity. Certain monsters have innate magical or special abilities which will still be usable while silenced. The effect starts out with a large radius, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the reader, before it times out.":"这张卷轴可以消除读者周围的所有声音。 这使读者附近无法阅读卷轴、施放法术、调用神圣能力或喊叫。 某些怪物具有与生俱来的魔法或特殊能力，即使被沉默也能使用。 起始的生效范围较大，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者，直到完全失效。","A scroll that calls forth several allied creatures woven from shadow into the shapes of those beings found within the reader's immediate vicinity.":"这个卷轴能召唤出几个作为友方的阴影生物， 他们会以当前读者附近的生物为模样塑造形象。","A scroll that translocates the reader to a random position after a short delay. Reading this scroll while waiting for a teleportation will instead cancel it.":"这张卷轴能在一小段时间之后，将读者传送到一个随机的位置。 在等待传送时再阅读这种卷轴，会取消其效果。","A scroll that calls on the powers of darkness to inflict great pain on any nearby creature — including the reader! This halves the resilience of all living creatures and cuts down all holy creature resilence by about a third, although it is never directly fatal.":"此卷轴将召来黑暗能量，给附近所有生物以极大的痛楚——甚至包括读者！ 它会使所有活物的生命值减半，并使所有神圣生物的生命值减少约三分之一， 但不会直接致死。","A scroll that briefly halves the willpower of the reader and any nearby beings, rendering them vulnerable to many magical effects. The scroll cannot affect those fully immune to such effects.":"这张卷轴会将读者和周围的任何生物的意志力暂时减半， 使其易受许多魔法效果的影响。完全免疫这些效果的不受此卷轴影响。","A farm implement, usually only used by untrained mobs in combat. In practice, it's quite similar to a halberd.":"这只是一个农具，通常只有没受过训练的家伙才会在战斗中使用它。 在使用时，它很像戟。","A jade snake coiled around a fossilised egg. Transforms the wearer into an amphisbaena - a legendary two-headed serpent. It is capable of wearing two pieces of headgear at once and its powerful coils can wind around foes and crush them to death, but its cold blood leaves it succeptible to being slowed by cold attacks.":"一条玉蛇盘绕在一颗化石蛋的周围。 它能将使用者变成双头蛇——一种传说中的双头巨蛇。 它能同时佩戴两件头部装备，其强大的蛇身可以缠绕敌人并将其挤压至死， 但它的冷血使其容易被寒冷攻击减速。","Many are the treasures of the Ironbound Order, but none older nor more precious than this steel-shining gem. The Vaults were first forged to hold it, and none who gazed within its depths could fault the choice.":"铁缚会有很多珍宝，但没有比这颗发出钢铁光泽的宝石更古老、更珍贵的了。 宝库最初就是为了保存它而锻造的，任何人只要凝视它的深处，就不会做出错误的选择。","Unearthly energies gently flow along the surface of this gem, guided by the archmage who first built the Elven Halls. Countless generations of elves flocked to learn from her, but her foremost pursuit was always the perfection of this piece of art.":"在最初建造精灵殿堂的大法师的引导下，超凡的能量沿着这颗宝石的表面缓缓流淌。 无数代精灵纷纷向她学习，但她的最高追求却始终是使这件艺术品臻于完美。","A curved piece of wood and string, for shooting arrows.":"一段弯曲的木头和绳子，用于射箭。","A personal stabbing weapon with a short grip.":"一件个人用的短柄刺杀武器。","Swirls of dark smoke seem to lurk in the depths of this gem. Countless dark deeds were done in the Dungeon even before Zot seized and remade it, and their dreadful residue now taints every hint of beauty trapped within its confines.":"这块宝石的深处似乎潜藏着一股黑烟。 甚至在佐特占领、改造地牢之前，就已经有无数的黑暗在地牢上演， 现在那些可怕的残留物玷污了困于地牢范围内每一个美丽的事物。","A hunting weapon consisting of a wooden shaft with a pointed metal head fastened on one end.":"一把用于狩猎的武器，由木杆和固定在一端的金属尖头组成。","A staff that increases the power of air spells cast by its wielder, and insulates them from electricity. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Air Magic, they can shock those struck by it, dealing electrical damage which bypasses half of defenders' armour.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展空气魔法的威力，并能使其与电绝缘。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和空气魔法，就能用其电击受击者， 所造成的电击伤害会无视防御者一半的护甲。","A staff that increases the power of alchemy spells cast by its wielder, and protects them from the effects of poison. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Alchemy, they can envenom those struck by it.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展炼金术法术的威力，并保护其免受毒素影响。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和炼金术，就能用它使受击者中毒。","A staff that increases the power of ice spells cast by its wielder, and protects them from the effects of cold. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Ice Magic, they can freeze those struck by it.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展寒冰魔法的威力，并能帮助其抵御寒冷的影响。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和寒冰魔法，就能用其冰冻受击者。","A staff that increases the power of conjurations cast by its wielder. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Conjurations, they can blast those they strike with pure energy.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展咒法系法术的威力。 若使用者精通魔力释放技能和咒法系，就能以纯粹能量轰击受击者。","A staff that increases the power of necromantic spells cast by its wielder, and protects them from negative energy. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Necromancy, they can inflict great pain on those living souls they strike, dealing negative energy damage which bypasses armour.":"这根法杖能增强使用者所施展的死灵法术的威力，并帮助其抵御负能量的影响。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和死灵术，就能使被自己击中的活物承受巨大痛楚， 并对其造成无视护甲的负能量伤害。","A staff that increases the power of earth spells cast by its wielder. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Earth magic, they can fracture the ground beneath those struck by it, dealing substantial damage - though much less to creatures which fly.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展大地魔法的威力。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和大地魔法， 就能破碎受击者脚下的地面，造成巨大伤害——尽管对飞行生物的伤害要小得多。","A staff that increases the power of fire spells cast by its wielder, and protects them from the effects of fire. If the wielder is skilled in Evocations and Fire Magic, they can burn those struck by it.":"这根法杖能增强使用者施展火焰魔法的威力，并能帮助其抵御火焰的影响。 如果使用者精通魔力释放技能和火焰魔法，就能用其烧灼受击者。","Odd lights twinkle within the depths of this gem. From what strange stuff is it made, and from what distant land did it travel?":"这颗宝石的深处闪烁着奇异的光芒。 它是用什么奇怪的物质制成的？它是从哪个遥远的地方流传过来的？","The scales of a steam-breathing dragon. Unlike the scales of some larger dragons, it does not provide its wearer with much protection (beyond a resistance to scalding steam), but it is extremely light and supple.":"吐息蒸汽之龙的鳞甲。 它为穿戴者提供的防护不如那些更大的龙的鳞甲（除了对灼热蒸汽的抵抗力）， 但它却十分柔软、轻盈。","A small chunk of dense but otherwise unremarkable natural mineral. It can be thrown to cause minor damage.":"一小块致密而常见的天然矿物。投掷它可以造成少量伤害。","The scales of a great umbral dragon. It is heavier than most dragon scale armours, but its encumbrance does not penalise the wearer's stealth. It also grants additional stealth to the wearer.":"巨大的暗影龙的鳞甲。它比大多数龙鳞甲重，但其负重不会妨碍穿戴者潜行， 并会额外提升穿戴者的潜行能力。","The scales of a lightning-breathing dragon. It is heavier than most dragon scale armours, and gives its wearer resistance to electrical discharges.":"吐息闪电之龙的鳞甲。它比大多数龙鳞甲重，并赋予穿戴者电抗。","Lightning trapped, impossibly, in a bottle. Lets the wearer walk through the air as a raging, lightning-filled tempest. The wearer's melee attacks are electrified and strike all adjacent foes. The wearer also flies, gains immunity to poison, miasma, petrification, constriction, and sticky flame, and also resists electricity. They can launch themselves as a lightning bolt, blasting through everything in their way.":"闪电不可思议地被捕获在一个瓶子里。 它能让使用者在空中穿行，如同一股狂暴的、充满闪电的风暴。 使用者的近战攻击将带有电属性，会打击到所有相邻的敌人。 使用者还能够飞行，免疫毒、瘴气、石化、束缚和粘性火焰，并有了电抗。 他们可以像闪电箭一样发射自己，炸开挡路的一切。","The scales of a swamp dragon. It confers resistance to poison on its wearer.":"一套沼泽龙鳞甲。它能赋予穿戴者对毒的抗性。","A grey-black vessel, infused with dark power through a sickening ritual. Transforms the wearer into an undying offence against life itself.":"一个灰黑色的容器，以令人不安的仪式向其注入了黑暗的力量。 它能将使用者变成对生命本身永不消亡的亵渎之物。","Foes struck by wearer's melee weapons or hands are weakened, slowed, and drained. The wearer can also heal themself by tormenting living foes nearby; Shapeshifting skill increases the amount healed. Further, the wearer resists cold, has enhanced willpower, and is immune to poison, miasma, negative energy, and torment.":"被使用者用近战武器或手击中的敌人会被虚弱、减速、衰竭。 使用者还可以通过折磨附近的活物敌人来治疗自己；提升变形术技能能增加治愈量。 此外，使用者将能抵抗寒冷，意志力会增强，并免疫毒、瘴气、负能量和折磨。","The wearer also gains some of the more dubious benefits of having an undead body. They are vulnerable to holy damage and Dispel Undead, and cannot consume potions.":"使用者还能从这副亡灵身躯中获得一些颇为可疑的好处。 然而，他们易受神圣攻击和驱散亡灵的伤害，且无法服用药水。","A grey-black vessel, infused with dark power through a sickening ritual. Transforms the wearer into an undying offence against life itself. Foes struck by wearer's melee weapons or hands are weakened, slowed, and drained. The wearer can also heal themself by tormenting living foes nearby; Shapeshifting skill increases the amount healed. Further, the wearer resists cold, has enhanced willpower, and is immune to poison, miasma, negative energy, and torment. The wearer also gains some of the more dubious benefits of having an undead body. They are vulnerable to holy damage and Dispel Undead, and cannot consume potions.":"一个灰黑色的容器，以令人不安的仪式向其注入了黑暗的力量。 它能将使用者变成对生命本身永不消亡的亵渎之物。 被使用者用近战武器或手击中的敌人会被虚弱、减速、衰竭。 使用者还可以通过折磨附近的活物敌人来治疗自己；提升变形术技能能增加治愈量。 此外，使用者将能抵抗寒冷，意志力会增强，并免疫毒、瘴气、负能量和折磨。 使用者还能从这副亡灵身躯中获得一些颇为可疑的好处。 然而，他们易受神圣攻击和驱散亡灵的伤害，且无法服用药水。","A compilation of children's stories about great adventures, always ending with the traveller returning to the place they started. The love infused into its pages by countless generations has granted it power, allowing a skilled mage to transport others by reciting specific passages.":"这本汇编收录着关于伟大冒险的儿童故事， 这些故事总会以旅行者回到他们开始的地方为结束。无数代人向其中注入了爱， 赋予了它力量，使得熟练的法师可以通过吟诵特定的段落传送他人。","A mesh of ropes knotted together with weights around the edge, used to entangle and entrap targets. Struggling victims can eventually destroy the net and break free, if they live long enough.":"一个在边缘打结了重物的绳网，用来缠住和诱捕猎物。 挣扎着的受害者最终能摧毁网并获得自由，如果他们能活到那么久的话。","A large piece of wood and metal, to be strapped on one arm for defence.":"一大块木头和金属，通过绑在一只手臂上进行防御。","A set of dormant, magnetic earth elementals in the form of tiny, very heavy pebbles. When released, the elementals are drawn magnetically to the center of nearby monsters, where they literally explode with rage at their rest being disturbed. Tremorstones usually land slightly off-target, and the user is always at risk of being hit. However, armour is extremely effective at repelling the lightweight fragments of rock from a tremorstone's explosion, so a well-armoured wielder has little to fear. Evocations skill increases the number of explosions.":"一组休眠的、有磁性的土元素，外形是微小的、非常重的鹅卵石。 当释放时，元素会被磁力吸引到附近怪物的中心， 在那里，它们会因在休眠时被扰动而愤怒地爆炸。 震颤石通常会稍微偏离目标，并且使用者总有被击中的风险。 然而，护甲在抵挡震颤石的爆炸中所迸发的轻质岩石碎片非常有效， 所以一个护甲精良的使用者没什么好担心的。提升魔力释放技能能增加爆炸次数。","A fishing spear improved with a longer shaft and a three-pronged metal head.":"一把经过改进的鱼叉，有了更长的杆和三叉的金属头。","A magical book written by a numerologically obsessed wizard. Everything from sentence length to overall organization is structured. It's unclear whether the author thought this was helpful.":"这本魔法书，由痴迷于数字命理学的巫师所写。 从句子长度到整体组织，都是结构化的。 目前尚不清楚作者是否认为这是有用的。","A crossbow with three strings arranged in series to provide exceptional power, initially designed as a siege weapon and then scaled down. It takes a considerable amount of time to load and fire.":"一把将三根弦串联排列、因而威力非凡的弩，最初被设计为攻城武器， 后来缩小了规模。装填和发射都需要一些时间。","A formidable weapon created by a master craftsman. The blade of the sword forks into three great razor-sharp edges.":"一把由大师级工匠打造的强大武器。这把剑的刀刃分叉成三个锋利的刀口。","A blessed trident moulded by cleansing flame, with three points symbolising the combined might of the three holy gods. It is a favoured weapon of the Shining One's servants.":"一把在净化之焰中铸就的三叉戟，三个尖端象征三位善神合在一起的力量。 这件武器深受光辉者的信徒喜爱。","The stiff and knobbly skin of a troll. It magically regenerates its wearer's flesh, once attuned to the wearer's body at full health.":"巨魔坚硬而多节的外皮。它能神奇地恢复穿戴者的身体健康， 但需要在生命值已满后穿戴，才能与身体相协调从而发挥作用。","A collection of spells that assault everything in sight of the caster, unrestrained by petty limitations like 'needing a clear shot' or 'concern about collateral damage'.":"一本法术合集，收录着能攻击施法者视线范围内一切东西的咒语， 不受诸如“需要明确的射击”或“担心附带伤害”等琐碎原则的局限。","A magical device which throws bolts of corrosive acid.":"一支可以射出腐蚀性酸液的魔法道具。","A magical device which causes a creature to become fiercely, but briefly, loyal to the user.":"这支魔法道具能使一个生物短暂但极其忠诚于使用者。","A magical device which drills tunnels through unworked rock.":"一支能在未开凿岩石中钻出通道的魔法道具。","A magical device which throws little puffs of flame.":"一支能喷射出一些火焰的魔法道具。","A magical device which creates a loud explosion of ice shards, bypassing half of victims' resistance to cold.":"这支魔法道具，能造成轰鸣作响的碎冰爆炸，这能穿透受击者的一半寒抗。","A magical device which fires a ray of searing light, injuring and blinding those struck. Only living, undead, demonic and angelic monsters can be blinded, and tougher monsters will recover their vision more quickly.":"这支魔法道具，能发射灼热的光线，使被击中的怪物受伤和失明。 只有活物、亡灵、恶魔和天使类怪物才能失明。并且更强的怪物会更快地恢复视力。","A magical device which launches a psychic attack on a target creature. If it overcomes their willpower, it 'blows their mind' in a violently literal fashion, dealing damage that bypasses their armour entirely. It is useless against mindless creatures.":"一支能对目标生物发动心灵攻击的魔法道具。 若攻击压倒目标的意志力，就会猛烈地“轰爆其心智”——这绝非比喻，而是字面意义上的轰爆—— 并造成完全无视护甲的伤害；对无心智生物无效。","A magical device which can render a creature immobile, incapable of moving any of its limbs.":"这支魔法道具，能使生物无法移动，且无法移动任何肢体。","A magical device which causes a creature to be transmogrified into another form. It is especially effective against shape-changing creatures.":"这支魔法道具能将目标生物变形成另一种形态。它对拥有变形能力的怪物特别有效。","A magical device which fires a beam of destructive energy, dispelling enchantments on creatures struck.":"这支魔法道具，能发射一束破坏性能量，驱散被击中的生物身上的魔力。","A magical device which fires a magical seed, entangling its target and adjacent foes in quick-growing tree roots. Those entangled will be immobilised and take damage over time until they escape or the roots wither away. The roots will only sprout from solid ground.":"这件神奇的道具，能够发射一颗魔法种子， 将目标和相邻的敌人缠绕在快速生长的树根中。 那些被缠绕的怪物会被固定，并随着时间的推移受到伤害， 直到他们逃脱或根系枯萎。根系只会从坚实的土地中发芽。","A military axe with a long haft and a single-bladed head.":"一把长柄、单刃的军用斧。","A long plaited strip of leather. Originally developed for use in disagreements with cattle, this simple weapon is now widely used to settle differences between all sorts of creatures.":"一条长长的编织皮条。这种简易武器最初用于解决与牲畜的分歧， 如今广泛用于解决各种生物之间的分歧。","An introductory book for the magic arts of poison. Readers are recommended to wear a pair of very thick, non-absorbent gloves.":"一本介绍毒素魔法的书。建议读者戴上非常厚实、没有吸收性的手套。","An amulet which allows the wearer to extract small amounts of magical energy from any potion they drink and also enhances the power of their alchemy spells. The magic restoration effect requires the amulet to attune itself to the wearer's body while their reserves of magic are full.":"一条允许佩戴者从他们饮用的任何药水中提取少量法力的项链， 还能增强其炼金术法术的威力。法力恢复效果需要项链在法力储备 已满时与佩戴者的身体相协调。","An amulet which causes magic contamination and negative status effects upon the wearer to expire twice as quickly with time.":"一条使佩戴者身上的魔法污染和负面状态效果随时间流逝速度翻倍的项链。","An amulet which improves its wearer's skill with Shapeshifting.":"一条提升佩戴者变形术技能的项链。","A book of schematics and spells to construct a variety of elaborate mechanisms. The obvious safety hazards involved with many of them are relegated to a single footnote on page 157, but to an enterprising adventurer, that might be considered an upside.":"一本关于构建各种精巧机械装置的图纸与法术的书。 其中涉及的许多明显安全隐患被归入第157页的一个单独脚注中， 但对应变的冒险者来说，这或许算是优点。","An illustrated guide to shaping ice into both practical and artistic forms. An entire chapter is devoted to tables of mineral impurities and their effect on colour and melting point.":"一本关于将冰塑造成实用和艺术形态的图文指南。 一整章专门介绍矿物杂质的表格及其对颜色和熔点的影响。","An eclectic spellbook, mingled with rambling philosophical anecdotes about the twin nature of every action. Even by the end, it remains unclear whether the author considered there to be some spiritual purity to spells which incorporate offence and defence into a single motion, or if they just lived a life extremely pressed for time.":"一本折衷的法术书，夹杂着关于每个行为双重本质的散漫哲学轶事。 即使读到末尾，仍不清楚作者是认为将攻击和防御融入一个动作的法术 具有某种精神上的纯粹，还是他们只是过着极其匆忙的生活。","A concise catalogue of afflictions, both magical and mundane, often described with a disquieting degree of cheerfulness. Most of them operate on timescales too slow to be useful to an adventurer, but a few sound remarkably efficacious.":"一本关于各种魔法和世俗疾病的简明目录，描述时常常带着令人不安的 愉悦感。大多数疾病的发作时间太慢，对冒险者无用，但有几个听起来 出奇地有效。","A tome of advanced Forgecraft magic. Its pages are regularly inlaid with technical figures made from elaborate metal filigree, perhaps as an illustration of the author's own skill with the art described herein.":"一本高级锻造术魔法的大部头。书页中定期镶嵌着由精致金属丝制成的技术图表， 也许是作者对本书所述技艺的自身技能的展示。","A spellbook that seems to leap open at the slightest touch. Its writing flits from description of one spell to another, giving enough information to truly understand only a few of them, though all seem to relate to movement in some way.":"一本似乎轻轻一触就会弹开的法术书。其内容从对一个法术的描述 跳到另一个，只提供足够的信息来真正理解其中的几个， 尽管所有法术似乎都以某种方式与移动相关。","A book of spells that purports to make their caster as resilient as a stone fortress. Its cover is fashioned from thick, magically-reinforced steel, making the book unreasonably heavy for no obvious benefit.":"一本声称能使其施法者像石头堡垒一样坚韧的法术书。 其封面由厚实的魔法强化钢制成，使这本书异常沉重，却毫无明显用途。","A heavy tome of necromantic spells. Those who touch it frequently report a palpable sense of unease, as if something unwholesome were buried between its very pages. {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"Its vellum smells faintly of dirt and decay.\" end }}":"一本厚重的死灵术法术书。触碰它的人常常报告一种明显的莫名不安感， 仿佛有某种不洁之物埋藏在书页之间。 {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"它的羊皮纸隐约散发出泥土和腐朽的气味。\" end }}","A long-forbidden tome, describing spells for various unholy (or, at least, underhanded) creations. It would be unwise to bring such a book back to the surface world - better to read it and discard it in some well-hidden location.":"一本长期被禁的巨著，描述了各种不神圣（或至少是不光彩）的创造法术。 将这样一本书带回地面世界是不明智的——最好阅读后将其丢弃在 某个隐蔽的地方。","An exhaustive collection of research notes on the effects of electricity upon everything from sawdust to snozzcumbers, interspersed with spell formulae and usable technical schematics. The author's handwriting deteriorates shockingly in the middle of the chapter on spriggan electrophysiology, leading to much speculation about both their identity and their sense of self-preservation.":"一本关于电对从锯末到斯诺兹黄瓜等一切事物影响的详尽研究笔记汇编， 穿插着法术公式和可用的技术图解。作者在关于小精灵电生理学的章节中， 笔迹恶化得令人震惊，引发了关于其身份及其自我保护意识的诸多猜测。","An analytical treatise on siege warfare, written in a clear and readable manner. A majority of its chapters are concerned with logistics and the maintenance of supply lines, but several detail spells useful for breaching fortifications (and also other, softer, things).":"一本关于攻城战的分析性专论，以清晰易懂的方式撰写。 大部分章节涉及后勤和补给线维护，但有几章详述了用于突破防御工事 （以及其他更柔软之物）的法术。","A strange sea fossil, adorned with abalone and pearl. {{ local hands = you.hand() .. \"s\" return \"Causes the wearer's \" .. hands }} to transform into a pair of wriggling electric eels that sometimes discharge arcs of electricity through connected targets when used to strike enemies. When the wearer's health becomes dangerously low, they will discharge an even more violent voltage.":"一块奇异的海化石，装饰着鲍鱼壳和珍珠。 {{ local hand_names = { hand = \"手\", paw = \"爪\", tentacle = \"触手\", claw = \"爪\", grasper = \"机械手\", tendril = \"卷须\" } local hands = hand_names[you.hand()] or \"手\" return \"使佩戴者的\" .. hands }}变成一对扭动的电鳗，在攻击敌人时有概率通过相连的目标释放 电弧。当佩戴者的生命值降至危险水平时，它们将释放更强烈的电压。","A small glass bauble containing an ominously glowing substance. Crushing it will flood you with transmutational energy, leaving your physical form unstable at a fundamental level.":"一个装有令人不安发光物质的小玻璃球。捏碎它将使你充满变形能量， 使你的物理形态在基本层面上变得不稳定。","In this state of flux, your melee attacks are much weaker, but each strike will contaminate whatever you hit with transmutational energy - growing so intense upon the third strike that it will cause their body to twist and deform, inflicting significant damage. The lack of certainty in your physical form also makes you much harder to hit, though you glow in a way that hinders stealth.":"在这种变形状态下，你的近战攻击弱得多，但每次攻击会用变形能量污染 被击中的目标——第三次攻击时变得如此强烈，以至于会导致它们的身体 扭曲变形，造成显著伤害。物理形态的不确定性也使你更难被击中， 尽管你发光的方式会妨碍潜行。","The power contained in each bauble is finite, and once it is exhausted by spreading it to enemies, you will return to your previous form.":"每个小球中蕴含的力量是有限的，一旦通过传播给敌人而耗尽， 你将恢复之前的形态。","A small glass bauble containing an ominously glowing substance. Crushing it will flood you with transmutational energy, leaving your physical form unstable at a fundamental level. In this state of flux, your melee attacks are much weaker, but each strike will contaminate whatever you hit with transmutational energy - growing so intense upon the third strike that it will cause their body to twist and deform, inflicting significant damage. The lack of certainty in your physical form also makes you much harder to hit, though you glow in a way that hinders stealth. The power contained in each bauble is finite, and once it is exhausted by spreading it to enemies, you will return to your previous form.":"一个装有令人不安发光物质的小玻璃球。捏碎它将使你充满变形能量， 使你的物理形态在基本层面上变得不稳定。 在这种变形状态下，你的近战攻击弱得多，但每次攻击会用变形能量污染 被击中的目标——第三次攻击时变得如此强烈，以至于会导致它们的身体 扭曲变形，造成显著伤害。物理形态的不确定性也使你更难被击中， 尽管你发光的方式会妨碍潜行。 每个小球中蕴含的力量是有限的，一旦通过传播给敌人而耗尽， 你将恢复之前的形态。","A miniature battlement, carved from a piece of shell. Transforms the wearer into a heavily armoured crab, fusing whatever body armour they are wearing into the shell in the process. In this form, they are slow-moving, but well-defended and even capable of wielding a weapon in their large main claw. Despite all this bulk, they are well-adapted to the water. They can also breathe clouds of rust at the cost of their own HP, which corrode and weaken enemies.":"一个从贝壳碎片雕刻而成的微型城垛。将佩戴者变成一只重甲螃蟹， 在此过程中将其穿戴的身体护甲融入壳中。在此形态下，它们移动缓慢， 但防御良好，甚至能用其大螯持有武器。尽管如此笨重， 它们非常适应水中环境。它们还可以消耗自身生命值喷吐锈蚀云雾， 腐蚀并削弱敌人。","A copper and tungsten tambourine that vibrates excitedly in your hands, as if eager to be used.":"一面铜和钨制成的铃鼓，在你的手中兴奋地振动着，仿佛渴望被使用。","Just as music brings people together, shaking it with the proper rhythm will draw a large group of monsters into a narrow space and hold any hostile ones in place for a short time with inescapable waves of crushing gravity.":"正如音乐将人们聚到一起，以正确的节奏摇动它将把一大群怪物吸引到 一个狭窄的空间中，并用无法逃脱的碾压重力波将所有敌对目标 固定在原地一小段时间。","The area of effect and duration increases with Evocations skill.":"效果范围和持续时间随魔力释放技能提升。","A copper and tungsten tambourine that vibrates excitedly in your hands, as if eager to be used. Just as music brings people together, shaking it with the proper rhythm will draw a large group of monsters into a narrow space and hold any hostile ones in place for a short time with inescapable waves of crushing gravity. The area of effect and duration increases with Evocations skill.":"一面铜和钨制成的铃鼓，在你的手中兴奋地振动着，仿佛渴望被使用。 正如音乐将人们聚到一起，以正确的节奏摇动它将把一大群怪物吸引到 一个狭窄的空间中，并用无法逃脱的碾压重力波将所有敌对目标 固定在原地一小段时间。 效果范围和持续时间随魔力释放技能提升。","A practical introduction to Forgecraft, covering basic principles and their common applications.":"一本关于锻造术的实用入门书，涵盖了基本原理及其常见应用。","A preserved and decorated hive, still dripping with ambrosial nectar. Transforms the wearer into a living beehive, filled with the buzz of countless insects labouring inside them. The nectar produced within greatly increases the wearer's health and magic regeneration and if they become seriously injured, angry bees will swarm out to defend their hive.":"一个经过保存和装饰的蜂巢，仍然滴着神酒般的甘露。将佩戴者变成 一个活蜂巢，充满了无数在里面劳作的昆虫的嗡嗡声。内部产生的甘露 大大提高了佩戴者的生命值和魔力恢复速度，如果他们严重受伤， 愤怒的蜜蜂将蜂拥而出保卫蜂巢。","A small bottle filled with mystical ink. Transforms the wearer into a walking scroll whose body is tattooed with the knowledge of a hundred mages. Being an omnibus of magical techniques gives them increased skill with all spell schools, which improves with Shapeshifting skill, but the form's ability to channel such magic is limited, and it cannot cast spells above level 4.":"一个装满神秘墨水的小瓶子。将佩戴者变成一本行走的卷轴， 其身体上纹有百位法师的知识。作为魔法技艺的百科全书， 使他们在所有法术学派中获得更高的技能，这随变形术技能提升而增加， 但此形态引导此类魔法的能力有限，无法施放4级以上的法术。","Its attacks are also very weak, but have a chance of restoring 1 MP when they hit.":"其攻击也非常弱，但命中时有概率恢复1点魔力。","A small bottle filled with mystical ink. Transforms the wearer into a walking scroll whose body is tattooed with the knowledge of a hundred mages. Being an omnibus of magical techniques gives them increased skill with all spell schools, which improves with Shapeshifting skill, but the form's ability to channel such magic is limited, and it cannot cast spells above level 4. Its attacks are also very weak, but have a chance of restoring 1 MP when they hit.":"一个装满神秘墨水的小瓶子。将佩戴者变成一本行走的卷轴， 其身体上纹有百位法师的知识。作为魔法技艺的百科全书， 使他们在所有法术学派中获得更高的技能，这随变形术技能提升而增加， 但此形态引导此类魔法的能力有限，无法施放4级以上的法术。 其攻击也非常弱，但命中时有概率恢复1点魔力。","A painted eyepatch made from a scrap of wolf pelt. Transforms the wearer into a vicious werewolf, muscles surging with predatory instinct. Killing enemies with melee attacks in this form will give a stacking bonus to your damage and accuracy, and slaying enough of them in a row will cause you to unleash a vicious howl that makes any still alive cower in fear - and leaves them susceptible to a devastating leaping takedown.":"一块由狼皮碎片制成的涂色眼罩。将佩戴者变成一只凶猛的狼人， 肌肉涌动着掠食本能。在此形态下用近战攻击击杀敌人将为你提供 叠加的伤害和命中加成，连续击杀足够多的敌人将导致你释放出 凶猛的嚎叫，使任何还活着的敌人因恐惧而畏缩—— 并使它们容易被毁灭性的跳跃扑杀攻击。","A fossilised jellyfish polyp, inscribed with sigils. Causes a mane of long stinging tendrils to sprout from the wearer's head which lash out at nearby enemies whenever the wearer attacks, poisoning them. When they feel their host's life is in danger, they can even turn these poisoned foes to stone.":"一块刻有符印的水母螅体化石。使佩戴者头部生出长长的 螫刺触须鬃毛，每当佩戴者攻击时向附近敌人挥击，使其中毒。 当它们感到宿主生命垂危时，甚至可以将这些中毒的敌人变成石头。","While purporting itself to be the personal account of a famous naturalist, it becomes clear upon reading that this book was compiled from multiple unrelated sources, including notes from a stagehand of a travelling magical circus. The travelogue may be fictitious, but some of the spell diagrams carefully transcribed in the margins seem quite real.":"虽然自称是一位著名博物学家的个人记述，但阅读后很快发现这本书 是从多个不相关的来源汇编的，包括一个巡回魔法马戏团舞台助手的笔记。 旅行记录可能是虚构的，但页边仔细抄录的一些法术图示似乎非常真实。","A brief text on magic, perhaps excerpted from some larger work. It contains knowledge of one spell.":"一篇关于魔法的简短文本，或许是从某部更大的著作中摘录的。 它包含一个法术的知识。","A long polearm with sharp protrusions on either side of the spearhead.":"一把长柄武器，矛头两侧有锋利的突出物。","A potent alcohol, distilled in some dubious corner of the dungeon. Drinking it reduces the imbiber's accuracy, evasion, and spellcasting success for a while.":"一种在地牢某个可疑角落蒸馏的烈酒。饮用后会在一定时间内降低饮用者 的命中率、闪避和施法成功率。","An ever-changing fragment of something primordial; its substance seems to undulate between flesh and bone and perhaps even metal. A sufficiently skilled shapeshifter can stabilise it into a useable - if unpredictable - form.":"一块不断变化的原始物质碎片；其物质似乎在血肉、骨骼甚至金属之间波动。 足够熟练的变形者可以将其稳定成可用的——尽管不可预测的——形态。","(If your Shapeshifting skill is at least 6, attempting to put this on will transform it into a random one of: Rimehorn, Scarab, Medusa, or Spore talismans.)":"（如果你的变形术技能至少为6，尝试戴上它将使其随机变成以下之一： 霜角、圣甲虫、美杜莎或孢子护符。）","An ever-changing fragment of something primordial; its substance seems to undulate between flesh and bone and perhaps even metal. A sufficiently skilled shapeshifter can stabilise it into a useable - if unpredictable - form. (If your Shapeshifting skill is at least 6, attempting to put this on will transform it into a random one of: Rimehorn, Scarab, Medusa, or Spore talismans.)":"一块不断变化的原始物质碎片；其物质似乎在血肉、骨骼甚至金属之间波动。 足够熟练的变形者可以将其稳定成可用的——尽管不可预测的——形态。 （如果你的变形术技能至少为6，尝试戴上它将使其随机变成以下之一： 霜角、圣甲虫、美杜莎或孢子护符。）","A spiny trinket reminiscent of a cactus. Causes sharp quills to grow all over the wearer's body which may cause injury to anyone unwise enough to attack them in melee.":"一个像仙人掌般的多刺饰品。使尖锐的刺生长遍布佩戴者的全身， 可能伤害任何愚蠢到用近战攻击他们的人。","An intricate puzzlebox containing an unknowable prize. Transforms the wearer into a riddle-loving sphinx. In this form, they are {{ if you.race() == \"Felid\" then return \"normally capable of wearing a cloak and barding (though your\" .. \" own diminutive size would prevent this)\" else return \"capable of wearing a cloak and barding\" end }}, and their melee attacks cause powerful winds to strike their foe which do increased damage for every open space next to them. They are also masterful enchanters, casting Hex spells much more easily and ignoring a portion of their foe's Willpower.":"一个内含未知奖品的精巧谜盒。将佩戴者变成一只爱好谜语的斯芬克斯。 在此形态下，他们{{ if you.race() == \"Felid\" then return \"通常能够穿戴披风和马铠（尽管你自身的微小体型会阻止这一点）\" else return \"能够穿戴披风和马铠\" end }}，其近战攻击会引起强风打击敌人，相邻每多一格空地，伤害就越高。 他们还是高超的惑控师，更容易施放诅咒系法术， 并忽略敌人一部分的意志力。","Alas, their love of riddles is so compulsive that even the most hardened adventurer will be unable to resist posing them to new foes they encounter, no matter how unwise this may be.":"唉，他们对谜语的热爱如此强烈，以至于即使是最坚毅的冒险者也无法 抗拒向遇到的新敌人提出谜语，无论这可能多么不明智。","An intricate puzzlebox containing an unknowable prize. Transforms the wearer into a riddle-loving sphinx. In this form, they are {{ if you.race() == \"Felid\" then return \"normally capable of wearing a cloak and barding (though your\" .. \" own diminutive size would prevent this)\" else return \"capable of wearing a cloak and barding\" end }}, and their melee attacks cause powerful winds to strike their foe which do increased damage for every open space next to them. They are also masterful enchanters, casting Hex spells much more easily and ignoring a portion of their foe's Willpower. Alas, their love of riddles is so compulsive that even the most hardened adventurer will be unable to resist posing them to new foes they encounter, no matter how unwise this may be.":"一个内含未知奖品的精巧谜盒。将佩戴者变成一只爱好谜语的斯芬克斯。 在此形态下，他们{{ if you.race() == \"Felid\" then return \"通常能够穿戴披风和马铠（尽管你自身的微小体型会阻止这一点）\" else return \"能够穿戴披风和马铠\" end }}，其近战攻击会引起强风打击敌人，相邻每多一格空地，伤害就越高。 他们还是高超的惑控师，更容易施放诅咒系法术， 并忽略敌人一部分的意志力。 唉，他们对谜语的热爱如此强烈，以至于即使是最坚毅的冒险者也无法 抗拒向遇到的新敌人提出谜语，无论这可能多么不明智。","A crude ornament carved from the horn of a rare arctic beast - so cold to the touch that ice still clings to it. Transforms the wearer into a rime yak, a hardy ungulate that is highly resistant to cold and whose breath is so frigid that it freezes the walls around itself as it fights. Being so attuned to arctic temperatures also makes it easier for the wearer to cast Ice magic.":"一件由稀有极地野兽的角雕刻而成的粗糙饰品——触感如此寒冷，冰仍然附着 在上面。将佩戴者变成一头霜角牦牛，一种高度抵抗寒冷的坚韧有蹄动物， 其呼吸如此冰冷，以至于在战斗中会冻结周围的墙壁。对极地温度的如此适应 也使佩戴者更容易施放寒冰魔法。","A vial of roiling blood that pulses with the beat of an unseen heart. Transforms the wearer into a fearsome vampire - a creature that straddles the border between life and undeath. They can drink the lifeblood of the living to heal themselves, and even turn those they slay stealthily into vampiric thralls, but do not heal in the presence of monsters. At great effort, they may scatter into a swarm of bats - either to flee or to assail their enemies.":"一瓶翻涌的鲜血，随着一颗无形心脏的搏动而脉动。将佩戴者变成一个 可怕的吸血鬼——一种跨越生命与亡灵界限的生物。它们可以吸取活物的 生命之血来治愈自己，甚至可以将那些潜行击杀的生物变成吸血仆从， 但在有怪物时不会自然恢复。在巨大努力下，它们可以散开成一群蝙蝠—— 要么逃跑，要么攻击敌人。","A small golden cameo of a beetle. Transforms the wearer into a sun scarab, a fiery insect that carries around a mote of searing heat and light outside itself, like a tiny sun.":"一个甲虫形状的小金浮雕。将佩戴者变成一只太阳圣甲虫， 一种携带着灼热与光明的火虫，在其身外像一颗微型太阳。","This solar ember burns adjacent enemies whenever the scarab attacks, and can be healed by swapping with it. In addition, the scarab's own mandibles can reduce enemies' fire resistance and Fire spells are easier for the wearer to cast.":"当圣甲虫攻击时，这颗太阳余烬会灼烧相邻的敌人， 与其交换位置可以治愈圣甲虫。此外，圣甲虫自身的下颚可以降低 敌人的火焰抗性，佩戴者也更容易施放火焰法术。","A small golden cameo of a beetle. Transforms the wearer into a sun scarab, a fiery insect that carries around a mote of searing heat and light outside itself, like a tiny sun. This solar ember burns adjacent enemies whenever the scarab attacks, and can be healed by swapping with it. In addition, the scarab's own mandibles can reduce enemies' fire resistance and Fire spells are easier for the wearer to cast.":"一个甲虫形状的小金浮雕。将佩戴者变成一只太阳圣甲虫， 一种携带着灼热与光明的火虫，在其身外像一颗微型太阳。 当圣甲虫攻击时，这颗太阳余烬会灼烧相邻的敌人， 与其交换位置可以治愈圣甲虫。此外，圣甲虫自身的下颚可以降低 敌人的火焰抗性，佩戴者也更容易施放火焰法术。","A coupon good for one item of any price from any store in the dungeon, to be used automatically when you would make a purchase that exceeds your funds. How generous! No refunds. One coupon per purchase per customer. Offer limited by availability. Void if defaced or otherwise altered. Valid only within the dungeon of Zot and its subsidiary branches. Additional purchase not required.":"一张可在任何地牢商店兑换任意价格物品的优惠券，当你进行超出资金 的购买时自动使用。多么慷慨！概不退款。每笔交易每客户限用一张。 优惠受库存限制。如有涂改或以其他方式篡改则无效。 仅限佐特地牢及其附属分支有效。无需额外购买。","A strange charm made from shed arachnid exoskeletons bound together with silk. Transforms the wearer into an agile jumping spider who can move swiftly towards foes and inflict grievous damage on any it catches unaware. It cannot be ensnared by webs, but its attacks can ensnare its enemies in them. It can also leap briskly away from many dangers.":"一件由蜕下的蛛形纲外骨骼用蜘蛛丝捆扎成的奇异护符。将佩戴者变成 一只敏捷的跳蛛，能迅速向敌人移动，并对任何被其发现的毫无防备者 造成重创。它不会被网困住，但其攻击可以将敌人困入网中。 它也可以迅速跳离许多危险。","A small charm made from a still-living mushroom. Transforms one of the wearer's arms and parts of their lower body into a vibrant mass of multicoloured fungus. Melee attacks in this form may release spores that weaken their target, as well as cause mushrooms to sprout on the ground behind them which will release their own bursts of dazing spores if allowed to grow. Shapeshifting skill increases the durability of these mushrooms as well as their damage.":"一件由仍活着的蘑菇制成的小护符。将佩戴者的一只手臂和部分下半身变成 一团充满活力的彩色真菌。在此形态下的近战攻击可能释放出削弱目标的孢子， 并导致蘑菇在它们身后的地面上生长，如果允许其生长，会释放出自身的 致眩孢子爆发。变形术技能提高这些蘑菇的耐久度和伤害。","An analytical volume discussing methods and materials with which to construct a dizzying array of traps - from those intended to safeguard a pantry from ants to ones which would please even the most sadistic dungeon architect.":"一本分析性的著作，讨论构建令人眼花缭乱的各种陷阱的方法和材料—— 从旨在保护储藏室免受蚂蚁侵害的陷阱，到连最虐待狂的地牢建筑师 都会满意的陷阱。","A magical device which creates a brief but violent rift in space, damaging everything caught in its wake and sometimes blinking them a short distance away.":"一个魔法装置，在空间中制造出短暂但猛烈的裂隙，对波及范围内的一切 造成伤害，有时会将它们闪烁到短距离外。","A small amphora from which pours a seemingly unending quantity of water. Transforms the wearer's flesh into elemental water, allowing them to move flexibly and reach to attack from a great distance. From time to time, they can even cause the water around them to rise up and drown their enemies.":"一个似乎能涌出无尽之水的小型双耳瓶。将佩戴者的肉体变成元素之水， 使其能够灵活移动并从很远的距离攻击。 偶尔，它们甚至可以让周围的水升起并淹死敌人。","The malleability of this water even allows them to retain the benefits of their physical mutations, but cold attacks can freeze it solid and fire may cause it to erupt with steam.":"这种水的可塑性甚至允许它们保留物理变异的好处，但寒冷攻击可以将水 冻结成固体，火焰可能导致其爆发出蒸汽。","A small amphora from which pours a seemingly unending quantity of water. Transforms the wearer's flesh into elemental water, allowing them to move flexibly and reach to attack from a great distance. From time to time, they can even cause the water around them to rise up and drown their enemies. The malleability of this water even allows them to retain the benefits of their physical mutations, but cold attacks can freeze it solid and fire may cause it to erupt with steam.":"一个似乎能涌出无尽之水的小型双耳瓶。将佩戴者的肉体变成元素之水， 使其能够灵活移动并从很远的距离攻击。 偶尔，它们甚至可以让周围的水升起并淹死敌人。 这种水的可塑性甚至允许它们保留物理变异的好处，但寒冷攻击可以将水 冻结成固体，火焰可能导致其爆发出蒸汽。","Once the primary guardian serpent of a legendary treasure hoard, she was disgraced after thieves looted it while she slept. She seeks to make up for her failure by protecting the only treasure the villains overlooked, a single precious talisman.":"她曾是一个传奇宝库的守卫巨蛇， 却因盗贼趁她熟睡时洗劫宝库而蒙羞。 她试图通过保护唯一一件被恶人忽视的宝藏——一枚珍贵护符，来弥补自己的过失。","Amaemon always knew he was different, but it was still a horrific surprise when his demonic heritage manifested. As his body twisted, Amaemon was forced to flee far from the surface. The passage of time has only left him more obsessed with what he has lost - consumed by poison both physical and spiritual.":"亚麦蒙一直知道自己与众不同，但恶魔血统显现时，仍令他惊骇万分。 随着身体扭曲，亚麦蒙被迫逃到远离地表之处。 时间的流逝只会让他更加沉迷于失去的东西——被肉体和精神上的毒药所吞噬。","Once a hero among the titans, Antaeus grew jealous of the titan queen. In single combat he challenged and slew her, and for this crime he was exiled and descended into the Hells. Finding the inhabitants of that place no match for his might, Antaeus tore from its substance a fourth Hell, Cocytus, a realm born of frozen spite.":"安泰俄斯曾经是泰坦中的英雄，但他嫉妒泰坦女王。 在一次战斗中，他发起挑战并杀死了她，因此随后被流放到了地狱。 安泰俄斯发现栖息在那个地方的生灵无法与他匹敌， 于是他从其实质上撕开了第四层地狱——悲叹河，一个由冰冻和怨恨而生的领域。","Once a talented human weaver, Arachne was transformed into a monstrous half-spider by a jealous rival's curse. Driven out of her village, she found sanctuary for a time among the jorogumo before a bitter feud forced her to flee once more.":"阿拉克涅曾是一位才华横溢的人类织工，却被嫉妒的对手诅咒， 变成了可怖的半蜘蛛怪物。被逐出村庄后，她一度在络新妇中找到庇护， 但一场激烈争斗又迫使她逃亡。","Now she wanders other corners of the dungeon with a small retinue of loyal students in tow, seeking a new domain in which they can spin their peerless tapestries in peace.":"如今，她带着一小群忠诚学生游荡在地牢的其他角落， 寻找一片能让众人安静织造无双锦绣的新领地。","Once a talented human weaver, Arachne was transformed into a monstrous half-spider by a jealous rival's curse. Driven out of her village, she found sanctuary for a time among the jorogumo before a bitter feud forced her to flee once more. Now she wanders other corners of the dungeon with a small retinue of loyal students in tow, seeking a new domain in which they can spin their peerless tapestries in peace.":"阿拉克涅曾是一位才华横溢的人类织工，却被嫉妒的对手诅咒， 变成了可怖的半蜘蛛怪物。被逐出村庄后，她一度在络新妇中找到庇护， 但一场激烈争斗又迫使她逃亡。 如今，她带着一小群忠诚学生游荡在地牢的其他角落， 寻找一片能让众人安静织造无双锦绣的新领地。","Greatest and most cunning of the Lords of Hell, Asmodeus was born when the twin fires of greed and treachery first sparked to life within a mortal's heart. His hideous body is perpetually wreathed in flame.":"作为最伟大、最狡猾的地狱领主， 阿斯摩蒂斯诞生于贪婪和背叛的双生之火第一次在凡人的心中燃起之时。 他那狰狞的身躯永远被火焰包围着。","Once a king infamous for waging bloodthirsty campaigns, Asterion was exiled to the depths of the dungeon for his crimes. Here he lurks in his tattered finery, dreaming of a new kingdom. In his lust for power, the minotaur king turned to the worship of Makhleb, and Makhleb has rewarded him with horrifying destructive might.":"阿斯忒里翁曾经是一个国王，因发动了残酷的战争而臭名昭著， 后来因为他的罪行被流放地牢的地底。 他穿着破旧的华服潜伏在这里，梦想建立新的王国。 这个牛头人王出于对力量的渴望，转而皈依马科列布， 而马科列布也赐予他骇人的毁灭性力量。","A powerful, belligerent efreet. (Is there any other kind?)":"一个强大而好战的伊弗利特。（难道还有不好战的吗？）","A weary draconian with foreign and watery scales. She has come to the Dungeon in hopes of resurrecting her mortal husband; a noble cause, for a being once known for quarrelling with saints and flooding unfortunate temples. If pressed to her limits, she will reveal her true form, the mere sight of which struck her husband dead. Adventurers may wish they were so lucky!":"一个疲惫的龙人，长有异样的似水的鳞片。 她来到地牢是为了一项崇高的事情，希望能找到复活她的凡人夫君的方法， 但她也因与和尚斗法而淹没不幸的佛寺而闻名。 如果把她逼得走投无路，她会展现出自己的真实形态， 她的丈夫仅仅只是看到就被吓死了。冒险者可能会希望他们也能这么幸运！","An ancient and powerful lich. Like all true liches, Boris is immortal, and will regenerate his desiccated skeletal remains even if completely disintegrated. The same cannot be said for his many victims over his many centuries, from which he collects and channels their dying woes and regrets.":"一个强大的远古巫妖。和所有真正的巫妖一样， 鲍里斯是不朽的，即使被完全解离得只剩骨灰也能复生。 但对于几个世纪里他的那些受害者而言却并非如此， 在这些岁月中，他收集、引导着受害者临终的痛苦和遗憾。","A violent and wrathful demon, Cerebov appears as a giant humanoid covered in shining golden armour and wielding a huge twisted sword.":"塞雷波夫是一个残暴易怒的恶魔。 他有一个巨大的人形身躯，身穿黄金铠甲，手持一把扭曲的巨剑。","Chuck the stone giant loves rocks, the bigger the better! Over the years, he has managed to amass quite the collection, including some rare, enchanted ones.":"石巨人查克喜欢石头——越大的越好！ 多年来，查克已经收集了大量的石头，其中包括几块附有魔法的稀有货。","A withered old gnoll with a long silver beard, wielding a quarterstaff and wearing a cloak. He looks like a figure from mythology! Wait, is his beard held on to his ears with hooks?":"一个干瘪的老豺狼人，长着银色的胡须，手持铁头木棒，穿着披风。 他看起来真像是神话故事里的角色！等等，他的胡子是用钩子挂在他的耳朵上的吗？","Greatest and most ruthless of the Lords of Hell, Dispater was born when first an iron sword drank mortal blood. They despise mortal vanities, the pursuit of ‘reason’ and ‘beauty’ - the only art they enjoy is the art of war.":"作为最伟大、最残忍的地狱领主，迪斯帕特诞生于第一把铁剑饮用凡人的鲜血之时。 他鄙视凡人的虚荣心和对所谓“理性”、“美”的追求—— 他唯一喜欢的艺术是战争艺术。","The Pits of Slime used to be a thriving civilisation, and Dissolution was the prophet of their god. When the city was overtaken by its current residents, only Dissolution survived, for they alone turned faithfully to the Slime God. Dissolution became a tremendous mass of acidic ooze, yet retained their intelligence. They are filled with hatred for anything that can hold a form.":"黏液坑洞曾经是一座繁荣的都市，而分解者则是居民们所信仰的神的先知。 当这座城市被现在的居民占领的时候，只有分解者活了下来， 因为他们选择转而忠于黏液神。 分解者已经变成了一大团酸性软泥，但他依然保留着他的心智。 他们极度憎恨一切有固定形态的东西。","{{ local descript = \"An adventurer just like you, trying to find the Orb.\"":"{{ local descript = \"一个和你一样在寻找宝珠的冒险者。\"","if you.race() ~= \"Merfolk\" and you.race() ~= \"Octopode\" then descript = descript .. \" Unlike you, and d\" else descript = descript .. \" D\" end":"if you.race() ~= \"Merfolk\" and you.race() ~= \"Octopode\" then descript = descript .. \"但不像你，尽管\" else descript = descript .. \"尽管\" end","descript = descript .. \"espite his hatred of it, he takes to water \" .. \"like a fowl.\"":"descript = descript .. \"他厌恶这个，却如鱼得水\" .. \"。\"","return descript }}":"return descript }}","{{ local descript = \"An adventurer just like you, trying to find the Orb.\" if you.race() ~= \"Merfolk\" and you.race() ~= \"Octopode\" then descript = descript .. \" Unlike you, and d\" else descript = descript .. \" D\" end descript = descript .. \"espite his hatred of it, he takes to water \" .. \"like a fowl.\" return descript }}":"{{ local descript = \"一个和你一样在寻找宝珠的冒险者。\" if you.race() ~= \"Merfolk\" and you.race() ~= \"Octopode\" then descript = descript .. \"但不像你，尽管\" else descript = descript .. \"尽管\" end descript = descript .. \"他厌恶这个，却如鱼得水\" .. \"。\" return descript }}","A beautiful but vain deep elf with an aptitude for magic and little else. His skills are the perfect complement of his twin sister Duvessa's fighting prowess. In search of more powerful spells, he journeys to the surface with his sister.":"一个美丽但高傲的地底精灵，有着魔法天赋，但除此之外，就没什么了。 他的技能是对他的双胞胎妹妹多维莎的格斗技能的完美补充。 为寻求更强大的魔法，他和他的妹妹一起前往地表。","A plain-looking deep elven fighter who is technically brilliant in many forms of combat, but over-confident because of it. She is complemented by the magical skills of her twin brother, Dowan. She journeys to the surface to challenge its greatest champions.":"一个外表普通的地底精灵战士， 她在多种形式的战斗中，技巧都非常精湛，但也因此过于自信。 她的双胞胎哥哥多万的法术技能对她起到了补充作用。 她前往地表以挑战最强大的斗士。","A jealous sibling of Sigmund (indeed, the youngest of nine brothers). He has none of Sigmund's skills in magic, but makes up for it with his skills in fighting and a canny head for money. He is eager to prove his superiority by killing hapless adventurers with his expensive flail and quick wit.":"西格蒙德的一个好嫉妒的弟弟（他是九个兄弟中最小的一个）。 他不像西格蒙德那样会施法，但他的格斗技能和精明的头脑弥补了这方面的不足。 他急着想要靠他的昂贵的连枷和诡计来杀死几个倒霉的冒险者， 以此来证明他的实力。","First and most fearful of her kind, the Enchantress rules over the spriggans of the dungeon. She wears an opalescent outfit made of dragon skin that shimmers with many colours.":"妖术女王是同族中最早出现、也最令人胆寒的一位，统领地牢中的小精灵。 她常穿着龙皮制成的乳白色外衣，闪烁着各色光芒。","Greatest and most inexorable of the Lords of Hell, Ereshkigal was born when first a mortal breathed her last. Noiselessly she laughs at lives cut short and loved ones separated by untimely death, enwreathed in the silence of the grave.":"作为最伟大、最无情的地狱领主，埃列什基伽勒诞生于第一个凡人咽气之时。 她无声地嘲笑戛然而止的生命，以及因夭亡而分离的爱侣， 周身萦绕着坟墓般的寂静。","A wild-tempered adventuress. She's quite prideful for an octopode, and brandishes their venomous capacity and camouflage talents with cruel force.":"一个性格狂野的女冒险者。 她为自己是章鱼而自豪，并以残暴的力量炫耀其毒性和伪装能力。","An especially cunning ogre-mage.":"一个特别狡猾的食人魔法师。","An apprentice summoner with a flowing moustache. He has funny ideas about honour.":"一个留着飘逸胡子的见习召唤师。他对荣誉有着有趣的想法。","A cold-hearted elven sorcerer, draped in robes of high office. They whisper grimly to themself as they stalk the dungeon, trailing ice crystals through the air behind them.":"一位冷血的精灵术师，身穿高级长袍。 他漫游地牢，时而阴冷地自言自语，身后的空气结为冰晶。","A stout warrior who once bested a powerful lord of Pandemonium in combat, gaining control over the demon's realm and thanes. The battle left her with a deep facial scar, one that she carries as a badge of honour rather than a symbol of shame.":"这位健壮的战士曾在战斗中击败一位强大的万魔殿领主， 从而掌控了那恶魔的领地与封臣。 那场战斗在她脸上留下了一道深深的疤痕； 在她眼里，那不是羞耻的印记，反而是荣耀的象征。","A svelte fighter-mage with a gold-rimmed monocle, a keen sense of tradition, and the blood of the gods running through his veins. He's here looking for a worthy opponent, but he's yet to find one.":"一个身材苗条的战斗法师，戴着金边单片眼镜，有着强烈的传统观念， 血脉中流淌着众神的血。他正在寻找一个值得重视的对手，但还没有找到一个。","A voracious and surprisingly intelligent slug, devoted to eating everything and everyone he comes across, with a pointed hat perched rakishly atop his head. He acquired the hat the same way he acquired his intelligence and his knowledge of spells: by consuming their former owner, a powerful wizard.":"一条贪婪且出奇聪明的蛞蝓，它会吃掉它遇到的所有人和物， 头上放荡地顶着一个尖帽子。他获得帽子与获得智慧和法术知识的方式相同： 吃掉帽子的前主人——一个强大的巫师。","A huge, three-headed, winged arch-demon, guardian of the four Hells. Legends say that his silver horn can summon terrible beasts to aid him in battle.":"一个巨大的三头有翼大恶魔，是四个地狱的守卫者。 传说他的银色号角可以召唤可怕的野兽来助他战斗。","A shadowy figure clothed in profound darkness.":"一个被深邃黑暗笼罩中的身影。","An inefficient shadow imp previously employed as a torturer in one of the lower circles of Hell. She has a tendency to complain and make inane statements.":"一个无能的暗影小恶魔。她以前在地狱低层做拷问者工作。 她总喜欢滔滔不绝地抱怨和讲废话。","A tough-looking gnoll, wearing the pelt of one of his former war dogs.":"一个外表凶狠的豺狼人，身上穿着他以前的一条战犬的毛皮。","A brutally twisted undead gnoll in the eternal service of Ereshkigal, lord of Tartarus. Legend has it that he sold his soul to return his most beloved hunting dog to life. Whether that hound is a member of his current pack, none can say.":"一个残忍扭曲的豺狼人亡灵，永远为塔尔塔鲁斯的领主埃列什基伽勒服务。 传说他出卖了自己的灵魂，为了让他最心爱的猎犬得以复活。 这只猎狗是否属于他现在的群落，谁也说不准。","A middle-aged bounty hunter, anxious to retire after one final job. He hopes to settle down somewhere and live a quiet life with his family, using the money from his final bounty: you.":"一位中年的赏金赏金猎人，急着要干完最后一票生意后退休。 他希望找个地方安顿下来，与他的家人过上平静的生活， 凭借他最后的赏金：你的命。","While a mortal cannot turn into a demon aside from divine intervention, this is what happened to Ignacio after Makhleb saw his love for his job and smiled upon him. He is now slated to continue the joy of his life for all eternity.":"若是没有神明的介入，凡人是不可能变为恶魔的。 当马科列布看到伊格纳西欧对他的工作的热爱并对他微笑后， 伊格纳西奥身上就发生了这样的事情。现在他将永远继续他一生的乐趣了。","Although his new form includes a number of large razor-sharp blades growing from his demonic appendages, he kept his favourite axe and is eager to let you test its edge.":"尽管他的新形态有着从恶魔附肢长出的大量锋利的刀片， 但他还是保留了他最喜欢的斧头，并想用你来测试它的锋利程度。","While a mortal cannot turn into a demon aside from divine intervention, this is what happened to Ignacio after Makhleb saw his love for his job and smiled upon him. He is now slated to continue the joy of his life for all eternity. Although his new form includes a number of large razor-sharp blades growing from his demonic appendages, he kept his favourite axe and is eager to let you test its edge.":"若是没有神明的介入，凡人是不可能变为恶魔的。 当马科列布看到伊格纳西欧对他的工作的热爱并对他微笑后， 伊格纳西奥身上就发生了这样的事情。现在他将永远继续他一生的乐趣了。 尽管他的新形态有着从恶魔附肢长出的大量锋利的刀片， 但他还是保留了他最喜欢的斧头，并想用你来测试它的锋利程度。","A small and shrewd goblin inventor, wearing blue rags coated in soot. She claims dominion over this level of the dungeon; trespassers will find themselves on the business end of a homemade wand.":"一个小而精明的地精发明家，穿着沾满煤烟的蓝色破布。 她自称是这层地牢的统治者；入侵者会在她自制的魔杖那里迎来终结。","A deadly merfolk water-witch, who uses her dominion over the tides to draw unwitting adventurers to their deaths.":"一个致命的人鱼水系女巫，驾驭潮水将毫无戒心的冒险者引向死亡。","Jeremiah was a peaceful dreamer, prone to impromptu naps. They slipped into slumber while gazing into a magical orb, and dreamed of an old and hateful power binding them into service. Now Jeremiah stumbles through the dungeon, searching for the precious dreamshard that will restore their master’s power, unsure whether they wake or slumber still. Their dreams leak into reality in the form of a constant stream of butterflies.":"耶利米是一个爱好和平的神游者，时常随兴打盹。 他们凝视着一个神秘的水晶球进入睡眠， 梦到有一种古老而可恨的力量把他们束缚在侍奉上。 现在耶利米跌跌撞撞地穿过地牢，寻找珍贵的、能恢复主人力量的梦碎片， 但不确定他们是醒着还是在沉睡。他们的梦以源源不断的蝴蝶流的形式渗入现实。","An evil apprentice sorceress. She entered the dungeon hoping to find a quiet, secluded place where she could study the darker arts without being disturbed.":"一个邪恶的见习女术师。她来地牢是想找到一个安静、与世隔绝的地方， 这样就可以不受干扰地学习更黑暗的技艺了。","A dwarven magician, particularly well-attuned to the dungeon around him. He wields powerful earth magic in combat.":"一位矮人魔法师，与周围的地牢环境格外契合。 他在战斗中使用强力的大地魔法。","Once a simple village peasant, Jory found himself transformed in undeath into a powerful creature. Through the countless centuries unlived since then, he has honed his skills in combat and magic, and amassed great wealth and many possessions.":"乔里曾是一位普通的乡下农民，有一天发现自己化身成了强大不死怪物。 此后那些他未曾真正活过的漫长世纪里，他不断磨炼战斗与魔法技艺， 也积累了巨量财富与宝物。","Looks like a mercenary in a stupid-looking hat.":"看起来像一个戴着愚蠢帽子的雇佣兵。","A fearsome necromancer who followed her craft beyond the limits of flesh and life. Her pursuit of demonic knowledge left her body ruined, but the powers she gained allowed her to rebuild her missing limbs from glittering ice.":"一个可怕的死灵法师，追寻着她的技艺，超越了肉体和生命的界限。 她对恶魔知识的追求摧毁了她的身体， 但她获得的力量使她能够从闪闪发光的冰上重筑失去的四肢。","A formidable necromancer, committed to her craft even after it left her aged, decaying, and half-undead herself.":"一位令人敬畏的死灵法师， 即使在她年老、腐朽、半死不活的情况下仍致力于她的技艺。","An incredibly powerful emperor on the way to godhood. He died quite some time ago, but he sees no reason why that should stop him.":"这位非常强大的皇帝，要成为神。 很早之前他就去世了，但他认为没有任何理由能阻止他。","A master of transformation and treachery. Beware, or you may be the next swine to join her herd!":"一个变化无常、背信弃义的大师。小心点，不然你会变成她身边的一头猪！","A huge beast, mightiest of hydras, infamous in myth and legend. It flows through the water faster than a human can run, swatting aside trees as though they were matchsticks. Its many heads slaver and gnash constantly as it hunts for prey to slake its bottomless appetite.":"这头身形庞大的野兽，是多头蛇中的最强者，在传说和神话中臭名昭著。 它在水中游动的速度比人类跑得快，游动时会将树拍到一边，仿佛它们是火柴杆。 它的许多头在不断地淌着口水、磨着牙，想要捕获猎物，以满足其无尽的食欲。","An ogre emissary of the Ironbound Order, sent to find and stop intruders before they enter the Vaults. Fiercely charismatic, he's rallied a small army of his kin, overawing them with the long-range lightning array he wears on his back. (The large coin purse he took from the Vaults is also quite persuasive.)":"一个铁缚会的食人魔使者，被派去追踪并阻止入侵者进入宝库。 他极具个人魅力，召集了一小群由同族组成的军队， 并凭借其背上的远程闪电阵震慑住了他们。 （他从宝库里拿走的一大笔钱也很有说服力。）","Stoic and inscrutable, Lom Lobon is an ancient demon infamous for their mastery of magic. Rumoured to be the most learned being in the halls of Pandemonium, they are at times sought out by mortal wizards who offer their souls in exchange for the secrets of the arcane. Lacking the terrible wrath present in most demons, Lom Lobon's single eye instead hides a cold, impartial cruelty.":"洛姆·洛邦是一个以精通魔法而臭名昭著的古老恶魔，他坚忍而高深莫测。 据传他是万魔殿中最博学的存在，有时凡人巫师会寻找到他， 要用自己的灵魂交换其奥术秘密。 洛姆·洛邦的独眼没有大多数恶魔身上那种可怕的愤怒， 反而隐现着一种冷酷、无差别的残忍。","A mighty sorceress, clad from head to toe in heavy armour. Once an adventurer looking for the fabled Orb of Zot, she was cast into the Abyss and got hopelessly lost there. Toyed with by some greater power, she was stuck on the hostile plane for nearly a decade. When she finally emerged from the Abyss, Louise had become powerful indeed, but had also gone fully insane. She now wanders the halls of the dungeon, seeking other adventurers to share her fate.":"一个强大的女术师，用重甲全副武装。 她曾经是一个寻找传说中的佐特宝珠的冒险者，但却在途中被打入无尽深渊。 她被某个强大的存在玩弄着，被困在那个充满敌意的位面中长达十年之久。 在最终逃离深渊的时候，路易丝变得极为强大，但也完全失去了理智。 现在她徘徊在地牢之中，想让其他冒险者也承受与她一样的命运。","This tall and powerful demon is Mara, Lord of Illusions, mighty among dreamers. He is capable of creating intricately detailed illusions, so real that they are almost as deadly as the creatures they impersonate.":"这个高大而强大的恶魔名叫玛拉，是幻象领主、梦者中的强者。 他能制造结构精巧的幻象，真实得几乎与所模仿的生物同样致命。","In a distant time, Maggie was apprenticed to the dreaded Hell Knights - but she grew impatient. In search of a shortcut to fame and fortune (and somewhat short on imagination), she entered the Dungeon and set out to slay a dragon. Now having slain one, Maggie sees no reason to stop.":"在遥远的岁月里，玛吉是可怕的地狱骑士的学徒——但她变得不耐烦了。 为了寻找成名和发财的捷径（有点缺乏想象力）， 她进入了地牢，并着手杀死了一条龙。 现在已经杀了一个，玛吉觉得没有理由停下来。","A lithe spellcaster in service to the powers of Hell; it is her duty to ensure that the inhabitants of the Dungeon never forget their place. She personally slew the ancient dragon from whose hide her strange armour is crafted.":"一个服侍于地狱力量的灵巧的施法者； 她的职责是确保地牢居民永远不会忘记自己的地位。 她亲手杀死了一条古老的龙，她那奇怪的盔甲是用它的皮制作的。","A sly, conniving thief. A self-proclaimed legend, he was one of the most skilled and crafty of the thieves and rogues lured by the Orb. The magical parasitic vines that have claimed his body still wish to continue his life's work, with a back-up plan of both a vicious magic-drinking maw and potent wands.":"一个狡猾、搞阴谋的盗贼。 他自称是一位传奇人物，是被宝珠吸引而来的小偷和流氓中最熟练、最狡诈的一个。 而占据了他身体的魔力寄生藤蔓仍然希望继续其一生的工作， 并拥有一个邪恶的吸取魔力的胃和强大的魔杖以备不时之需。","A fair and noble ruler of an ancient and mighty kingdom, mummified after an early death. His faithful priests subsequently infused him with great and powerful magic, seeking to grant him eternal life. Now he is forgotten and reduced to mouldering bandages and dry, brittle bones.":"他是强盛的古国中的一位公正而崇高的统治者，英年早逝后被做成了木乃伊。 他忠实的祭司们随后为他注入了强大的魔法，试图让他永生。 现在他已经被遗忘了，只剩腐烂的布条和干燥、脆弱的骸骨。","There was once a human priest named Mennas. He travelled far and wide as a missionary of Zin, often venturing even into Orcish lands. He beseeched the orcs to abandon their false tribes and return to the peoples of their birth; only Zin's light could truly cleanse the weight of sin that had twisted their bodies.":"曾经有位名叫门纳斯的人类祭司。他作为辛的传教士四处远行，甚至经常深入兽人领地。 他恳求兽人抛弃虚假的部族，回归自己出生的族群；唯有辛之光才能真正洗净 令其身体扭曲的沉重罪孽。","By all accounts the orcs were not happy with Mennas. Eventually, a group of them demanded he recant his words and when Mennas remained silent, they cut out his tongue.":"无论何种记载，兽人都显然对此不满。最后，一群兽人要求他收回这些话； 门纳斯始终沉默，于是它们割掉了他的舌头。","Whether or not this angel is that same Mennas is something of a mystery, as he seems to have difficulty speaking.":"这个天使是否就是那位门纳斯仍是谜团，因为他似乎难以开口说话。","There was once a human priest named Mennas. He travelled far and wide as a missionary of Zin, often venturing even into Orcish lands. He beseeched the orcs to abandon their false tribes and return to the peoples of their birth; only Zin's light could truly cleanse the weight of sin that had twisted their bodies. By all accounts the orcs were not happy with Mennas. Eventually, a group of them demanded he recant his words and when Mennas remained silent, they cut out his tongue. Whether or not this angel is that same Mennas is something of a mystery, as he seems to have difficulty speaking.":"曾经有位名叫门纳斯的人类祭司。他作为辛的传教士四处远行，甚至经常深入兽人领地。 他恳求兽人抛弃虚假的部族，回归自己出生的族群；唯有辛之光才能真正洗净 令其身体扭曲的沉重罪孽。 无论何种记载，兽人都显然对此不满。最后，一群兽人要求他收回这些话； 门纳斯始终沉默，于是它们割掉了他的舌头。 这个天使是否就是那位门纳斯仍是谜团，因为他似乎难以开口说话。","A demon prince once possessed a hunger for power that was exceptional even by the standards of his kind. He betrayed his realm to Lugonu, and his reward was to become this twisted mass of corruption, now known only as Mlioglotl.":"这位恶魔王子曾经对力量有一种渴望，即使以他的同类标准来衡量， 这种渴望也是超乎寻常的。他把自己的王国出卖给了卢格努， 而回报就是变为这个如今被称为姆利奥格洛特尔的扭曲的腐化团。","A weirdly glowing figure, dancing through the twisted air of Pandemonium.":"一个散发着诡异光芒的身影，在万魔殿扭曲的空气中舞动。","A demonic skull rolling along the ground.":"一个恶魔般的头骨在地上滚动。","A fast-moving magical cat. Once a powerful wizard's familiar, Natasha was abandoned after her master was consumed by the very necromantic forces he sought to control. Now she patrols the dungeon, taking a bloody vengeance with spell and claw upon any adventurer who crosses her path.":"一只移动迅速、有魔力的猫。娜塔莎曾是一个强大的巫师的伙伴， 但在她的主人被他试图控制的死灵力量吞噬后，她被遗弃了。 现在她在地牢里巡游，用法术和利爪对任何经过她的路线的冒险者进行血腥的报复。","This cat doesn't have nine lives, but just one death isn't going to be enough to put her down for good.":"这只猫没有九条命，但仅仅一死也不足以让她安息。","A fast-moving magical cat. Once a powerful wizard's familiar, Natasha was abandoned after her master was consumed by the very necromantic forces he sought to control. Now she patrols the dungeon, taking a bloody vengeance with spell and claw upon any adventurer who crosses her path. This cat doesn't have nine lives, but just one death isn't going to be enough to put her down for good.":"一只移动迅速、有魔力的猫。娜塔莎曾是一个强大的巫师的伙伴， 但在她的主人被他试图控制的死灵力量吞噬后，她被遗弃了。 现在她在地牢里巡游，用法术和利爪对任何经过她的路线的冒险者进行血腥的报复。 这只猫没有九条命，但仅仅一死也不足以让她安息。","A highly intelligent elephant who travelled as part of a circus. One dark night, she slipped out of her chain and disappeared into Pandemonium, never to be seen again.":"一头非常聪明的大象，曾随一个马戏团巡游。 有一天晚上，她挣脱了锁链，然后踏入了万魔殿，从那以后就再也没有人见过她。","A shrewd and wizened orc who has devoted her life to chronicling the bloody history of her people. She claims to know the names and deeds of every last orc who lost their life in their great exodus into the Dungeon, and even if this is a lie, she nonetheless seems to be on a first-name basis with many of them.":"一位精明而衰老的兽人，毕生致力于记录族人的血腥历史。 她声称知道每一个在兽人大举迁入地牢时丧命者的姓名与事迹； 即便这是谎言，她似乎仍与其中许多人熟识到能直呼其名。","More than any other orc still breathing, she knows the blood and sacrifice it took to make this place a refuge for her kind. She will not brook it being intruded upon by anyone - least of all you.":"她比任何仍在呼吸的兽人都更清楚，为使此地成为族人的避难所曾付出多少鲜血与牺牲。 她绝不容许任何人闯入——尤其是你。","A shrewd and wizened orc who has devoted her life to chronicling the bloody history of her people. She claims to know the names and deeds of every last orc who lost their life in their great exodus into the Dungeon, and even if this is a lie, she nonetheless seems to be on a first-name basis with many of them. More than any other orc still breathing, she knows the blood and sacrifice it took to make this place a refuge for her kind. She will not brook it being intruded upon by anyone - least of all you.":"一位精明而衰老的兽人，毕生致力于记录族人的血腥历史。 她声称知道每一个在兽人大举迁入地牢时丧命者的姓名与事迹； 即便这是谎言，她似乎仍与其中许多人熟识到能直呼其名。 她比任何仍在呼吸的兽人都更清楚，为使此地成为族人的避难所曾付出多少鲜血与牺牲。 她绝不容许任何人闯入——尤其是你。","A centaur warrior, skilled at warfare and deceit. They slew a mighty hydra, and now its deadly blood drips, still-fuming, from their arrows.":"一个半人马战士，擅长作战和诈术。 他曾杀死过一只强大的多头蛇，现在它的致命血液从箭上滴落，仍在冒烟。","A brilliant scientist obsessed with electricity. In his attempts to perfect his electric golem, he was involved in a terrible accident, and now phases in and out of reality.":"一个对电异常狂热的天才科学家。他在尝试改进他的电魔像时卷入一场可怕的事故， 因此现在时不时地进入或脱离现实。","A relaxed water cultist with a healthy tan and a soothing voice. He doesn't really care if it is you or he who dies — “both” would probably be the best option.":"一个从容的水教徒，有着健康的棕褐色皮肤和舒缓的声音。 他并不在乎是你死还是他死——也许“同归于尽”才是最好的选择。","An unusually weak troll.":"一个异常虚弱的巨魔。","An unusually strong troll, his thick frame scarred by many against-the-odds victories. He has been wounded so many times that his body has adapted, and now heals almost instantly. His necklace of troll claws is a memento of those who underestimated him.":"一个异常强壮的巨魔，他壮硕的身躯上有许多恶战后留下的伤痕。 他受过很多次伤，身体已经适应了，现在伤口几乎能瞬间愈合。 他的巨魔爪项链会是那些低估他的人的纪念。","A wise kobold would fear the forces of Hell, and certainly would not set up a highly lucrative transdimensional trade in damned souls. But Pikel is better known for his whip than his wisdom, mercilessly tormenting his piteous charges as he ferries them to their buyers.":"一个聪明的狗头人会畏惧地狱的力量，绝不会进行暴利、跨维度的该死的灵魂贸易。 但皮克尔更为人所知的是他的鞭子，而不是他的智慧， 当他把他的可怜的奴隶运送给他们的买家时，他无情地折磨着他们。","A cyclops shepherd, he is very protective of his charges, whom he watches with an undying fervor through his single massive eye. Nevertheless, he won't hesitate to use them as projectiles in a pinch; after all, the best defence is a good offence.":"这个独眼巨人牧羊人，非常爱惜自己的牲畜， 他用那只透露着永恒热情的巨大的眼睛注视着它们。 尽管如此，在紧要关头，他还是会毫不犹豫地将它们用作弹丸； 毕竟，最好的防守就是好的进攻。","A frog of unusual size, with a tiny crown perched incongruously atop his head.":"一只个头不同寻常的青蛙，头上戴着个小王冠，显得很不协调。","A mountain hobgoblin, recently come in search of the legendary Orb. Not foolhardy or reckless enough to delve into the depths of the Dungeon alone, Robin has built a small army of minions. Potential competitors will quickly find a stream of screaming goblins flying toward them!":"罗宾是一个山地大地精，最近也前来寻找传奇的宝珠。 但他并没有莽撞地独自进入地牢深处，而是组建了由随从组成的小型队伍。 可能有竞争对手很快会发现有一股尖叫的地精向他们飞来！","A strikingly realistic sapphire statue of a famous earth mage who disappeared after a catastrophic mishap with a magical talisman.":"一尊格外逼真蓝宝石雕像，其形象是一位著名的土系法师， 她在一次灾难性的事故后带着一个有魔力的符咒失踪了。","Rippling muscles, glistening pecs, incredible glutes - Rupert is the peak of physical perfection. Even so, his roars seem louder than even his fantastic form can explain. Perhaps he holds some talisman that lends supernatural force to his bellows?":"起伏的肌肉、闪亮的胸肌、巨大的臀肌——鲁珀特达到了完美肉体的巅峰。 即便如此，他的咆哮似乎比以他那种奇异体形所能吼出的还要响亮。 也许，正是他持有的某个符咒，给他的吼叫带来了超自然的力量？","A mighty warlord. Some orcs even say they are the Chosen One of Beogh.":"一位强大的将军。有些兽人甚至说他就是被比欧弗选中的人。","The elder of a pair of brothers who came for the Orb. No one knows what Sigmund saw in the dungeon to drive him mad, but his shrewd magical tactics and wicked scythe now leave little time for his victims to wonder. Despite his reputation as a vicious murderer, his grandiose and dramatic ways have earned him the admiration of many denizens of the dungeon.":"他是为宝珠而来的一对兄弟中的哥哥。 没人知道西格蒙德在地牢里看到了什么因而发疯， 但他狡猾的魔法战术和厉害的镰刀现在可没有留给让他的受害者好奇的时间。 尽管他有恶毒的凶手的名声，但他浮夸而戏剧化的手法赢得了许多地牢居民的赞叹。","A particularly corpulent troll with a short temper and a sizable gut. Uninterested in the Orb, Snorg delights in the endless parade of adventurers – that is, easy meals — it attracts.":"一个特别肥胖的巨魔，他的脾气很坏，肚子很大。斯诺格对宝珠并不感兴趣， 而是喜欢冒险者的无休止的行进——也就是说，小菜——吸引了他。","Queen of the tengu, with legendary skill in swordsmanship, tactics, and magic. Storytellers claim she once trapped a raging tempest in a bottle and kept it as a talisman.":"天狗女王，其剑术、谋略和魔法出神入化。 讲故事的人说，她曾把一场强烈的风暴捕获在一个瓶子里，并把它当作符咒保存着。","A graceful kobold assassin. Admire her graceful pirouettes, thrill at her daring leaps! But watch out for her knives!":"一位优雅的狗头人刺客。欣赏她优雅的旋转吧，因她那大胆的跳跃而震颤吧！ 但要小心她的刀！","A veteran of a war against the armataurs' elephant-riders. He has recently retired to make a new home in the dungeon.":"一个暴力杀手。他杀人的原因不仅是为了钱，也是为了获取愉悦感。 泰伦斯之前在一次行动中失败了，因此不得不藏起来。 他头上还有悬赏呢——他可不能让任何看见他的人活着走出地牢！","The earthly avatar of Tiamat, deity of dragonkind, here incarnated as a mighty draconian warrior. Her scales seem to shimmer and change colour as you watch.":"提亚马特的现世化身，龙族的神，在这里具现为强大的龙人战士。 当你观察她时，她的鳞片似乎会闪耀并变幻颜色。","A coarse and lanky orc. Urug lost her eye in a fight with a harpy, and has sworn to slay every last one of them. Unfortunately, the vision in her remaining eye is not very good, and she has mistaken you for one. {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"She smells terrible.\" end }}":"一个身形粗犷、瘦长的兽人。 乌鲁格在与鸟妖的战斗中失去了一只眼睛，因此发誓要把世上的鸟妖全部杀光。 不幸的是，由于她剩下的一只眼视力不太好，她把你当成了鸟妖。 {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"她很难闻。\" end }}","An elite marksnaga who leads a skilled team of sharpshooters. She is particularly skilled in translocation magic.":"一个领导着神射手团队的精英射手纳迦。她特别擅长移位魔法。","One of the Stoneborn, formed untold aeons ago with supreme command over rock. Her people shelter deep within the living earth, so whatever has forced Vv into the oppressive openness of the Dungeon must be dire indeed. But whatever it is, she's not talking...":"数万年前形成的石裔之一，拥有对岩石的至高的控制力。 她的人民躲避在充满活力的大地深处， 因此迫使芙芙进入压抑、空旷的地牢的东西一定是很可怕的。 但不管是什么，她都不说话……","An ancient and mighty dragon.":"一条强大的古龙。","A master weaponsmith, her flesh melding into steel so smoothly that it's hard to tell where one ends and the other begins. She entered the Dungeon to search for the secrets of an ancient, long-suppressed cult, said to have exalted metal over flesh. The price of knowledge was her humanity - a price she paid eagerly.":"一位武器锻造大师，她的身体与钢铁融为一体， 以至于很难分清哪块是肉，哪块是钢铁。 她进入地牢是为了探寻一个古老的、长期被压制的邪教的秘密， 据说这个邪教推崇金属胜于肉体。知识的代价是她的人性——这是她热切付出的代价。","A huge, red-glowing, three-headed dragon, shrouded in damnation. It is possessed by the very essence of Gehenna and its eternal fire.":"一条巨大的、发出红光的三头龙，被笼罩在诅咒之中。 它被欣嫩谷的实质及其永恒之火所缠绕。","A massive white three-headed dragon, covered with shards of gleaming ice, wholly possessed by the nightmarish cold of Cocytus.":"一条巨大的白色三头龙，覆有锃亮的冰块碎片， 完全被悲叹河那噩梦般的寒冷所附着。","A towering three-headed beast with an army's worth of swords for teeth. Each of its scales is a shield with a razored edge.":"一个极高大的三头野兽，有着军队的利剑一般的牙齿。 它的每个鳞片都是边缘锋利的盾牌。","Seemingly three pairs of lurid magenta eyes hanging in the darkness, the outline of a vast, sinuous dragon is just barely perceptible behind. Its malice is palpable.":"黑暗中似乎悬着三双可怕的洋红色眼睛，后面一条蜿蜒的巨龙轮廓隐约可见。 其恶意昭然若揭。","A small dragon with brilliant yellow scales, its mouth dripping with corrosive slime.":"一条具有亮黄色鳞甲的小型龙，嘴上滴着腐蚀性的黏液。","A common dungeon snake, a species of troglodytic reptile commonly found in subterranean spaces.":"一条普通的地牢蛇，它是一种在地下常见的穴居爬行类动物。","A spirit drawn from the elemental plane of air. It exists in this world as a lightning-spitting spirit, stunning foes with its crackling bursts.":"一个来自气元素位面的灵体，以喷吐闪电的形态存在于此世， 用噼啪作响的爆裂击晕敌人。","An aggressive crocodilian with great crunching jaws full of sharp teeth.":"一条攻击性很强的鳄鱼，有着巨大、嘎吱作声的嘴，上面长满了锋利的牙齿。","A particularly large and nasty snapping turtle. Like its smaller relative, it can reach out and bite from afar.":"一只格外巨大而凶猛的巨鳄龟。和它较小的亲缘物种一样，它也能从远处伸过来咬。","A very large snake that moves with startling swiftness. It kills not by poison but by constricting its prey.":"一条非常大的蛇，移动速度惊人。它不是通过毒液而是通过束缚猎物进行猎杀。","A humanoid construct of insubstantial memory, floating through the air. Though perhaps somewhat changed in shape and bearing few discernable features, still they seem somehow to resemble a warrior from the distantly remembered past. The memory and the memorialist fight in concert, each able to fire past the other.":"一个由虚幻记忆构成的人形造物，浮在空中。尽管外形有所改变， 也没有多少明显特征，但它似乎仍像一位来自遥远往昔的战士。 记忆和追忆者并肩战斗，双方的射弹都能穿越彼此。","An unfathomably ancient skeleton. It has hundreds of golden sigils etched onto its bones, and pulses with terrible, unholy power.":"一具不可名状的远古骷髅。 它的骨头上刻有数百个金色印记，脉动着可怕的邪恶力量。","A lich who, having existed for countless centuries, has grown almost unimaginably powerful through the study of dark magic.":"一个存在了无数个世纪的巫妖，通过研究黑魔法，强大得难以想象。","A nexus of sentient cancer and disease, borne aloft perhaps by malice alone. Its nature inflicts withering illness on all living beings in its presence.":"一个有意识的疾病与肿瘤的结合物，也许它只是因恶意而生成。 它会本能地让出现在它面前的所有生物感染致命的疾病。","A divine warrior of the Shining One. It is a towering winged figure of unnatural beauty surrounded by an aura of brilliant white light.":"光辉者的一名圣战士。它长着高耸的翅膀，美得不像是这个世间的东西， 周身环绕着光彩夺目的白色光环。","A curious quadraped, resembling a cross between an armadillo and a yaktaur.":"一种奇特的四足生物，像是犰狳和牦牛人的混合体。","The sweat and toil of the armourer working leather and steel infuses an intention into their creation, a unique spark within every cuirass, pauldron and vambrace. A skilled forgewright can manifest these intentions in physical form, allowing their armour to protect its wearer in a more aggressive fashion than armour customarily does.":"军械士加工皮革与钢铁时付出的汗水和辛劳，会为造物注入意念， 在每件胸甲、护肩和臂甲中留下独特火花。技艺高超的铸甲师能让这些 意念具现，使防具以远比通常更具攻击性的方式保护穿戴者。","A placid, sacred bull of Elyvilon. Its status as an exalted envoy of the Healer lets its very presence double the health of its allies.":"艾利维隆的一头平静而神圣的公牛。身为治疗者的崇高使者， 它仅凭自身存在便能使盟友的生命值翻倍。","An opalescent crab with jet black eyes, and chaotic mists effusing from its mandibles. Rumours claim that this species is waiting for the end of time.":"一只泛着蛋白石光泽的螃蟹，长着黑玉般的眼睛，混沌迷雾从口器中涌出。 传言称，这个物种在等待着时间的终结。","A wizard fond of spectacle and destruction. They scorn the cowardice of other magicians, who hide from their foes rather than simply blasting them out of existence.":"一个喜欢精彩场面和破坏的巫师。 他们蔑视那些躲着敌人、而不是随手将其炸飞的懦弱的魔法师。","The divided and churning remains of a protean progenitor, striving desperately for form. Whatever they become, the last of their progenitor's power ensure it will be stronger and swifter than any such creature found elsewhere in the dungeon.":"一个变形之祖的分裂、搅动的遗骸，竭力变化着形态。无论它们变成什么， 它们祖先的最后力量将确保它比任何在地牢其他地方碰到的那种生物更强、更快。","An extremely cold blob of bright blue cytoplasm, forming bits of frost in the air around it.":"一团极冷的亮蓝色细胞质，它周围的空气都结成了冰霜。","A swift sphere of coruscating electrical energy. It will explode at the slightest disturbance.":"一个迅捷、发光的电能球体。即使是最轻微的扰动也会使它爆炸。","A small snake that can augment its bite by constricting small creatures.":"一条小蛇，它可以通过束缚小型动物来增加它的咬合力。","A lumpy reddish fungus covered in knobbly rhizome growths, growing well in the dank underground dungeon. When it senses a threat, the ballistomycete may release a deadly floating spore that explodes on its victims.":"一种块状淡红色真菌，覆有多节的根瘤，在阴湿的地牢中生长良好。 当孢子炮菌察觉到威胁时，可能会释放飘浮着的致命孢子，在受害者身上爆炸。","A fast, gas-filled floating spore released by a ballistomycete when it senses a threat. After seeking out its foe, the spore will explode, damaging anything caught in the blast and further confusing living creatures.":"一枚快速飘浮、充满气体的孢子，由受到威胁的孢子炮菌释放。 找到敌人后，它会爆炸，伤害范围内的一切，并使其中的活物更加混乱。","A huge and very powerful demon, wreathed in fire and shadows.":"一个巨大且强力的恶魔，身体被环绕在火焰与阴影之中。","An amphibious humanoid with a very ugly attitude.":"一个脾气极其恶劣的两栖人形生物。","A crested lizard of middling size with a terrible petrifying gaze.":"一个中等大小、有羽冠的蜥蜴，有着可怕的石化凝视。","A large grey bat that, despite being herbivorous, is quite aggressive. It is myopic and uses echolocation to navigate.":"一只大型灰色蝙蝠，虽然是食草动物，但攻击性却很强。 它的视力很差，要靠回声来定位。","A humanoid construct of insubstantial memory, floating through the air. Though perhaps somewhat changed in shape and bearing few discernable features, still it seems somehow to resemble a warrior from the distantly remembered past, skilled with both conjurations and melee combat.":"一个由虚幻记忆构成的人形造物，浮在空中。 尽管外形会发生变化，也没什么明显可辨的特征， 但它仍像一位来自记忆深处、遥远往昔的战士，擅长咒法系法术和近战。","A small globe of destructive energy. Each time its creator casts an offensive spell, it will launch a magical barrage at the most injured nearby foe it can reach.":"一个魔法能量小球。 每当它的创造者施放攻击性法术时，它便会向其能够攻击到的附近伤势最重的敌人发射一轮魔法弹幕。","A sacred, self-created sunbird, representative of rebirth. It has ascended past the cycles of life and death, and calls upon aspects of both, rising forth from death in a burst of unholy flame.":"一只神圣的、能自生的太阳鸟，象征着重生。 它已超脱了生死的轮回，望着生死的两边。它会从一团邪恶的火焰中复活。","A small black bear. Like all ursines, it will become enraged if badly hurt.":"一头小型黑熊。和所有其他熊类一样，它会在受重伤时会变得狂暴。","A muscular black-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and powerful wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有黑色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和有力的翅膀。","An astonishingly fast tropical snake whose bite bears a deadly venom.":"一条快得惊人的热带蛇，咬伤带有致命毒液。","The exposed elemental core of a blazeheart golem. Far too unstable to remain without its shell, it is in the process of violently exploding.":"焰心魔像暴露的元素核心。如果脱离外壳，它会变得非常不稳定，将造成剧烈爆炸。","A volatile elemental spark encased in a shell of slag iron. If destroyed while its fires still blaze, the exposed core will violently detonate a moment later.":"它的渣铁外壳包裹着不稳定的元素火花。 如果它在其火焰仍在燃烧时被摧毁，暴露的核心将在片刻后剧烈爆炸。","A species of frog that possesses the ability to blink at will. It can blink itself close to its intended prey, or blink away to escape harm. It is commonly found in packs.":"一种能自行闪现的大型蛙。 它既可以通过闪现来接近猎物，也可以利用闪现来逃脱伤害。这种蛙经常成群行动。","A greater demon formed from wistful snow and bitter lightning.":"一个由怅惘之雪与苦涩闪电构成的高阶恶魔。","A decaying undead corpse. When it reaches a victim (or if it's destroyed first), the gases trapped inside it are released and create a large, violent concussive blast.":"一具腐烂的亡灵尸体。当它靠近受害者（或者如果它在此之前就被摧毁）时， 里面的气体被释放，并产生巨大、猛烈的冲击波。","A block of ice shaped like a statue, but worked by no living hands.":"一块形如雕像的冰块，但并非出自活人之手。","An undead figure preserved by the brackish waters of a bog, and reanimated by some unknown magic.":"一个亡灵生物，被沼泽的咸水所保存，并被某种未知的魔法复活。","A malevolent and dangerous little sprite. The shadowy illusions it summons may not be real, but are deadly all the same.":"一个邪恶又危险的小妖精。它能够召唤阴影幻象，虽然并非真实，但同样致命。","An unassuming beetle filled with an incredible amount of hypergolic fluid. The sticky spray it fires is capable of igniting predators and unwary adventurers alike, though more experienced ones know to keep moving if they wish to avoid a fiery grave.":"一只不起眼的甲虫，它的体内充满了大量的自燃液体。 它喷出的粘性喷雾能点燃捕食者和粗心的冒险者， 而更有经验的人知道，如果想要逃离这个火焰坟墓，最好继续前进。","A mighty undead abomination, pieced together from the broken bones of many dragons by powerful necromantic magic. The collective despair of such desecrated dragons gives this horror its own undying breath weapon, in billowing clouds of excruciating misery.":"这个强大的亡灵怪物，在强大的死灵术作用下由许多龙的断骨拼接而成。 这些遭亵渎巨龙的集体绝望，赋予了这怪物永不消逝的吐息武器， 喷涌出令人痛不欲生的苦难云雾。","A gnoll witch possessed by a spirit of spite which flashes out from behind their eyes. Its strange chants and ululations send other gnolls into a wild frenzy.":"一个被怨灵附身的豺狼人女巫，怨灵在其眼后闪现。 它那奇怪的吟唱和呼喊能让其他豺狼人陷入疯狂。","A mass of fast-rolling stone, crushing everything in its path.":"一个快速滚动的石头，碾碎沿途的一切。","A grey beetle with an almost impenetrable rocky carapace. When at some distance from its foe, a boulder beetle is capable of rolling at high speed, attempting to crash into its target for heavy damage.":"一个灰色甲虫，有着几乎无法穿透的岩石外壳。 当与敌人有一定距离时，巨砾甲虫会高速滚动，试图撞向目标以造成严重伤害。","The soul of a living, holy, or demonic creature, captured by a dark sacrifice to Yredelemnul. The bound soul will follow its captor through stairs and come when recalled from a different level.":"一个活物、神圣生物或恶魔生物的灵魂，被献给伊莱德莱姆努尔的 黑暗祭仪所俘获。缚魂会跟随捕获者穿过楼梯，也能从其他楼层被召回。","A slimy fluorescent worm with a greatly distended head. This creature feeds on others' intellect as it squirms through unworldly grime.":"一条黏滑的荧光蠕虫，长有极度膨胀的头部。 这个生物在超凡的尘垢中蠕动，以他人的智力为食。","A tangled cluster of thorny briars, sharp enough to pierce thick hide and armour. Although stationary, its branches are possessed with a will of their own. They move to allow magic and missiles fired by those friendly to this plant to pass through unaffected.":"一丛缠绕的带刺荆棘，锋利得足以刺穿厚皮和护甲。 它尽管静止不动，但却有着自己的意志。 他们会进行摆动，让那些对这种植物友好的人所发射的魔法和飞弹不受影响地穿过。","A huge and powerful demon wreathed in damnation, with great scaly wings. It is one of the most fearsome denizens of any of the Hells.":"一个巨大且强力的恶魔，身体被环绕在天谴之中，还长有巨大的鳞翼。 这是地狱中最可怕的物种之一。","A giant spider swollen with eggs. Its innumerable offspring are always at its call.":"一只鼓满卵的巨型蜘蛛。它的无数孩子会永远听从其召唤。","A masked priest in the service of Kikubaaqudgha, well-versed in choral rituals to both rouse the dead and send them to eternal rest.":"一位服侍奇库巴库哈的蒙面祭司，精通唤醒死者和使其永远安息的合唱仪式。","A woody plant. It looks dry enough to be easily set on fire, and its foliage is not very dense, permitting both magic and missiles to pass through unaffected. However, it is firmly rooted, and requires significant effort to destroy.":"一株木本植物。它看起来并不潮湿，可以轻易被火点燃，它的枝叶也并不茂密， 魔法和飞弹也能不受影响地穿过。但它的根基却非常扎实，破坏它可得费一番力气。","An unusually aggressive amphibian that pursues its prey with rapid hops. Its croak is loud and distinctive, but unlike its smaller counterparts above ground, the dungeon bullfrog is as large as it sounds.":"一个攻击性极强的两栖动物，快速跳跃，追捕猎物。它的叫声响亮而独特， 但与地面上较小的近亲不同，地牢牛蛙的体形和叫声一样夸张。","A flesh-eating beast that uses its limbs and tail interchangeably. It moves with alarming speed, but must pause to reorganise itself after each attack. Its distinctive screams carry far and wide.":"一个食肉动物，交替使用肢体和尾巴。它能以惊人的速度移动， 但每次攻击后都必须停下来重新调整自己。它独特的尖叫声能传得很远很远。","A large, brightly coloured butterfly with beautifully patterned wings, fluttering incongruously through the darkness of the cave.":"一只亮丽的大蝴蝶，翅膀上有着漂亮的图案， 它飞舞的身影在这黑暗的洞窟中显得很不协调。","A green-skinned, spiny colossus, with a hearty barrel chest and a thirst for battle. Any foe that strikes it in melee will be lucky to live to regret it.":"一个绿色皮肤、多刺的巨人，有着健壮的桶状胸脯，对战斗充满了渴望。 任何在近战中攻击他的敌人都会庆幸还能活着后悔。","A maniacal demon, brimming with accursed power. Its gleeful laughter rarely ceases, even in the heat of battle.":"这个恶魔奇丑无比，狂暴而有着传奇般的力量， 它会先使敌人失去行动能力，然后再将他们轰杀至渣。","A hideous toad whose thick, warty hide is covered in poison glands. Unlike its smaller above-ground relatives, this dungeon-dweller is the size of a wolf.":"一个丑陋的蟾蜍，其厚而多疣的皮上长满了毒腺。 与地面上较小的亲缘物种不同，这只地牢物种有狼那么大。","A sluggish black buffalo, its hide encrusted with dull scales. It carries its hog-like head just above the ground, protected by a stiff mane of bristles. Its fearsome breath turns flesh into stone.":"一头行动迟缓的黑色野牛，它的皮上覆有一层暗色的鳞片。 它那像猪一样的头刚刚高出地面，被坚硬的鬃毛保护着。 它那可怕的吐息会把肉体变成石头。","A swift, nightmarish bird whose razor-sharp metallic feathers drip with corrosive acid.":"一只迅捷而噩梦般的鸟，剃刀般锋利的金属羽毛滴着腐蚀性酸液。","A hybrid with the torso of a human atop the body of a horse. It is highly skilled in archery.":"一个混种生物，在马的身体上有着人的躯干。其箭术很高超。","A muscular centaur, veteran of numerous battles, armed with well-made weapons and able to use them skilfully.":"一个肌肉发达的半人马，身经百战，装备着精良的武器，能够熟练地使用它们。","A small, wilful minor demon. Its wings, far larger than its scrawny body, were made to soar, and it lands only rarely and with the greatest reluctance.":"一个矮小、任性的低阶恶魔。它的翅膀比它那瘦骨嶙峋的身体要大得多， 生来就是为了飞翔。它也很少、很不情愿着陆。","A being of pure chaos, its form is constantly shifting, growing and then losing eyes, mouths, claws and tentacles. It corrupts everything it touches.":"一个由纯粹的混沌构成的存在，其形态在不断变化， 眼睛、嘴巴、爪子和触手不断在它的身体上长出来，随后又会消失。 被它碰到的东西都会遭到腐蚀。","A throne-bearer of the gods, whose head is beset by four faces: one of a man, one of an ox, one of a lion, one of an eagle. It is one of the angelic beings who stand before the good gods, singing eternal hymns of praise to their glory and greatness.":"神的敕谕信使，他的头被四张脸环绕着：人的、牛的、狮的和鹰的。 他是站在善神一边的天使，为神的荣耀和伟大歌颂永恒的赞美诗。","A formless mass of ancient fire, bound by heat and malevolence. It longs to unleash itself as a wild fire storm, yet must first patiently burn towards its victims with implaceable inevitability.":"一团无形的远古火焰，被高温和邪恶束缚着。 再轻微的干扰也会破坏将其连接在一起的纽带，并引发一场火焰风暴。 它渴望释放，但在被观察时似乎不愿移动。","A small, ugly minor demon. Its fanged maw seems locked in a permanent malign grin, and its horns protrude obscenely from its scaly pate.":"一个矮小、丑陋的低阶恶魔。它那长满尖牙的嘴似乎永远保持着一副恶意的咧嘴笑， 它的角从有鳞的脑袋里可憎地突出来。","A crocodilian with powerful jaws.":"一条有着强力嘴巴的鳄鱼。","A spiny, long snouted rodent grown out of pure living crystal. It is immune to most forms of magic and hurls both crystallising shots and painful barbs.":"一个由纯净的活性水晶生成的多刺、长鼻啮齿动物。 它对大多数形式的魔法免疫，并且会投掷水晶箭和令人疼痛的倒钩。","An intricate animated statue made of heavily ensorcelled crystal that is immune to most forms of magic. The spells which created it are so powerful that even flesh may start to crystallise around any fragments that become embedded in it - leaving its foes brittle and vulnerable.":"一个结构精巧的活动雕像，由被重重魔法强化的水晶制成， 对大多数魔法免疫。创造它的法术强大到甚至被其碎片嵌入的血肉， 也会在碎片周围开始结晶，使敌人变得脆弱易伤。","A small spider with rudimentary healing abilities. Though not undead, it packs a nasty vampiric bite.":"一个有着基础治疗能力的小蜘蛛。虽然不是亡灵，但它会造成吸血鬼那样的咬伤。","A charred skull floating in the air and rotating slowly. Mystic symbols are carved into its blackened surface.":"一个烧焦的头骨，浮在空中慢慢旋转着。神秘的符号刻在它焦黑的表面上。","A disembodied toe, hanging in the air and radiating an intense field of negative energy.":"一个脱离躯体的脚趾浮在空中，在周围形成了一个致密的负能量场。","A giant with one eye in the centre of its forehead. Despite its lack of binocular vision, it is able to throw boulders with fearsome accuracy.":"这个巨人的额头正中长着一只眼睛。 虽然独眼巨人只有一只眼视物，但他投出的石块命中率却很高。","A towering winged figure radiating an aura of brilliant golden light. It is a divine agent of the Shining One.":"一个高大而长有双翼的身影，散发着璀璨金光。 它是光辉者的神圣使者。","A small invertebrate. It hunts prey considerably larger than itself by firing chitinous darts, using a concealed air bladder to launch them with remarkable range and power.":"一个小型无脊椎生物。 它能通过隐藏的气囊射出有着惊人射程和威力的壳质飞镖来猎杀比它大得多的生物。","A noxious and deadly fungus suffused with negative energy. While parasitic in life, undeath has granted it the ability to absorb its nutrients directly from the life force of others.":"一个有毒的致命真菌，充满了负能量。 它生前是寄生菌，而不死形态使它能够直接从他人的生命力中汲取养分。","A dreadful undead cob of maize. Look, this one was probably a mistake. We're sorry.":"一块可怕的亡灵玉米棒。瞧，这可能是个错误。我们很抱歉。","A dark and baleful minor dragon. It breathes a lethally potent miasma from its pestilential maw.":"一条邪恶的黑色亚龙。它能从它的瘟疫之胃中喷吐出一团致命的瘴气。","A warrior-priest of Yredelemnul, chanting fearful supplications to its dark god.":"一个伊莱德莱姆努尔的战斗祭司，向黑暗之神吟诵着可怕的祈求。","A hideous swarming undead insect, exuding death and decay and feeding on the life energies of those unfortunate enough to encounter it.":"一个成群涌现的可怕的亡灵昆虫，散布着死亡和腐化， 以它所遇到的不幸生物的生命能量为食。","A larger and beefier relative of the common dungeon yak. Its little red eyes gleam with hunger for living flesh.":"这头牦牛比常见的亲缘物种地牢牦牛更大、更强。 它红色的双眼闪烁着，仿佛在诉说对鲜肉的渴望。","A deep elf who exults in conjured mayhem and destruction. It is widely hated and feared, both for the power and for the precision of its destructive magics.":"一个以唤起伤害和破坏为乐的地底精灵。 其毁灭魔法强大而精准，许多人对他又恨又怕。","An experienced deep elf fighter with a penchant for ranged combat.":"一个经验丰富的地底精灵战士，喜欢远程战斗。","A champion of the deep elves, who scorns magic and is devoted to the study of the sword. It wields two weapons with astonishing dexterity and speed.":"地底精灵的勇士之一，他蔑视魔法，毕生致力于剑术。 他能以难以置信的敏捷和速度持两把武器作战。","A deep elf surrounded by a shimmering aura of negative energy, as a result of its practice of necromancy and life-sapping magic.":"一个地底精灵，被闪烁的负能量光环所环绕， 这是他练习死灵术和衰竭生命力的魔法的结果。","A deep elf who is marked heavily by long years of contact with unnatural demonic forces and the creatures of the Abyss.":"一个地底精灵，长期接触非自然的恶魔力量和深渊中的生物。","A deep elf commanding the primal forces of the universe. It is renowned for its ability to pin down even the most elusive foes with powerful, unavoidable magic.":"一个支配宇宙原始力量的地底精灵。即使再难以捉摸的敌人， 他也能用强大的、不可回避的魔法进行牵制和锁定，他也因此而闻名。","An exalted servant of the ancient dark god of the deep elves, basking in hellish death magic.":"地底精灵的远古黑暗之神的一个显赫的仆从，沉浸在地狱般的死亡魔法中。","A battle-hardened deep elf fighter.":"一个身经百战的地底精灵战士。","A deep elf archer who has devoted a lifetime to the mastery of archery, dismissing magic as a frivolous distraction.":"一个地底精灵射手，毕生致力于精通箭术，将魔法视为一种无聊的消遣。","A deep elf learned in the ways of fiery magic. It is capable of casting a wide array of scorching spells.":"一个地底精灵，掌握了火系魔法。它可以施放各种灼热法术。","A mighty spellcaster who draws power from the very Hells, and possesses lethal arcane abilities.":"一个强大的施法者，他从地狱中汲取力量，并有着致命的奥术能力。","An elf with a singular focus on the magic of the air, leaving little time to study anything else.":"一个专注于空气魔法的精灵，几乎没有时间学习其他东西。","A stooped troll with dark skin. It often travels in packs.":"一个驼背的黑皮巨魔。他们经常成群出没。","A particularly intelligent deep troll. It uses its magic to tunnel through the earth and ambush foes.":"一个极其聪明的深渊巨魔。它会用魔法在大地中挖掘通道，伏击敌人。","A deep troll blessed with divine power to strengthen and hasten its kin.":"一个蒙受神力祝福的深渊巨魔，能够强化并加速同类。","A human-like figure with an aura of power betraying its divine ancestry.":"这个人形生物身上的能量气息，揭示着他背叛了他的神圣先祖。","A hellish insectoid creature, fueled by some infernal power that constantly regrows its chitinous segments. Nothing short of a lethal blow will stop it for long.":"一个地狱的昆虫类生物，由某种地狱般的力量刺激着，不断代谢着它的壳节。 除非是致命的一击，否则没有什么能长久地阻挡它。","A half-mortal, half-demonic creature, with its hellish heritage asserting itself through a certain devilish cast to its features.":"一个半人半魔的生物，能从身上一些恶魔的特征看出他有来自地狱的血统。","A half-mortal, half-demonic creature, radiating an intense heat. It weaves powerful and unpredictable spells of devastation.":"一个半人半魔的生物，散发着强烈的热量。他编织着强大而不可预测的毁灭咒语。","A half-mortal, half-demonic creature, oozing with dark energies. It twists space around itself, and can corrupt weapons, armour and even the very flesh of its opponents.":"一个半人半魔的生物，散发着黑暗能量。 他扭曲了自身周围的空间，可以腐蚀武器、盔甲甚至对方的血肉。","A half-mortal, half-demonic creature, covered in icy blue scales. Its devotion to the deities of death grants it great insight into the vulnerabilities and applications of mortal souls.":"一个半人半魔的生物，身上覆盖着冰蓝色的鳞片。 它对死亡诸神的虔诚信仰，使它深谙凡人灵魂的弱点与用途。","A half-mortal, half-demonic creature, now more beast than whatever species it is descended from. It is devoted to martial combat, disrupting the magic of its foes as it feasts off of endless conflict.":"一个半人半魔的生物，如今比它出身的任何族类都更像野兽。 它一心投入武斗，在无休止的冲突中汲取力量，并扰乱敌人的魔法。","A towering obelisk surrounded by a powerful storm.":"一个高耸的方尖塔，被强大的风暴所环绕。","A huge pachyderm, wilder and fiercer than normal elephants, with a very thick hide, powerful legs, and a memory to die for.":"一种巨大的厚皮动物，比普通大象更加狂野和凶猛， 有着厚实的皮、有力的腿，还有可以铭记到死的记忆力。","An elemental spirit formed from smokeless fire.":"一个由无烟火形成的元素之灵。","A demon lapdog of the queen of Tartarus, bound to hunt her enemies. The first time a foe hears its howl, it will echo in their mind, calling nightmarish creatures to hunt them. Those who survive have the small consolation of being inoculated against that particular hound's howl.":"塔尔塔罗斯的一条恶魔宠物狗，准备追猎她的敌人。 当敌人第一次听到它的嚎叫时，嚎叫会在他们的脑海中回响， 呼唤噩梦般的生物来猎杀他们。 那些幸存者有一个小小的安慰，那就是接种了抵御这种特殊猎犬嚎叫疫苗。","A brown-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings. It is yet to develop the distinct colouring and powerful breath attack of its mature form.":"一个长有棕色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。 他还尚未发育出成熟形态的独特色彩和强大的吐息攻击。","A draconian that uses powerful conjurations to destroy anyone who dares to stand in its way.":"一个龙人，他会使用强大魔法消灭任何胆敢阻挡他的敌人。","A draconian protected by thick scales, skilful weapon use, and complementary magic.":"一个身上长有厚鳞片的龙人，擅长使用武器和辅助性的魔法。","A draconian who has eschewed the study of weaponry and magic in order to train in the art of unarmed combat. Its scaly fists, well-thewed legs, and mighty tail rain down blows upon its opponents.":"一个龙人，为了专心修炼徒手格斗技艺，而放弃了学习武器和魔法。 他那覆有鳞片的拳头、肌肉发达的腿、有力的尾巴，如雨点般密集地砸向敌人。","A cunning draconian who has mastered the inner secrets of the element of fire. Its scales are sooty from years of magical pyrotechnics.":"一个狡猾的龙人，掌握着火元素的独特奥秘。 他的鳞片因多年的魔法烟火的施放而被熏黑。","A draconian master of the warp, who can translocate both itself and anyone else to any place, either on this world or outside of it.":"一个精通空间扭曲的龙人， 他有能力将自己或是其他任何人传送到任何一个地方，包括这个世界之外。","A draconian deriving its thunderous powers and draconic allies from the worship of Qazlal.":"这个龙人从对卡兹拉尔的崇拜中获得雷霆般的力量和龙族盟友的协助。","A lich who has made terrible pacts with demonic forces to augment its dark magic.":"一个巫妖，为了增强其黑暗魔法，与恶魔力量签订了可怕的契约。","A drowsy, fluffy ovine whose coat sparkles with motes of dream dust. It gathers in herds and fills the air with dream dust, overwhelming its victims and putting them to sleep.":"一只睡意朦胧、毛绒绒的绵羊，毛上闪耀着梦尘。 它们成群聚在一起，让空气中充满了梦尘。梦尘覆盖在受害者身上，使之陷入沉睡。","A cold and hollow apparition of the drowned dead, chained by some lingering attachment to the depths in which it perished. It rushes to embrace the living, sharing the last moments of its watery fate with whatever it touches.":"一个冰冷、空洞的溺死者的亡灵，被某种挥之不去的情感束缚在它死去的深渊中。 它冲过去抱住生者， 要让接触到的任何人也品尝到它生命的最后一刻淹在水里的滋味。","A spirit of nature, bound to the forest in which it resides. It is capable of calling upon the trees to defend against incursions.":"一个自然之灵，与栖息的森林紧密相连。她能够召唤树木以抵御入侵。","A member of a short, sturdy mountain-dwelling folk.":"一个矮小结实的山地居民。","A spirit drawn from the elemental plane of earth. It exists in this world as a sinuous stream of silt and stone, capable of smoothly flowing through solid rock.":"一个来自地元素位面的灵体，以蜿蜒流动的泥沙与岩石存在于此世， 能够平滑地穿行于坚固岩层。","An imposing, muscular figure engulfed in a cloud of searing flame.":"一个威严而强壮的生物，全身被一团灼热的火焰裹挟着。","An ancient skeletal apparition, sheathed in a cloud of mist. Its form glows white-hot with debilitating energy.":"一个远古的骷髅幻影，隐没于一团云雾之中。 它的身体发出白热的光，散发着衰弱能量。","An immense, squamous appendage of some unseen creature, dripping with ichor and tipped with a single, terrible-looking claw.":"这条巨大、多鳞的肢体属于某个看不见的生物，败液从上面滴落， 在肢体的末端还长有一个骇人的爪子。","A part of an immense, squamous appendage. It thrashes and pulsates like no other living thing.":"某条巨大、多鳞的肢体的一部分。你从未见过其他活物像它这样抽打、悸动。","An animated figure made completely of electricity, created in some demented wizard's experiment.":"一个完全由电形成的造物，它是在某个疯狂巫师的实验中被创造出来的。","A type of fish capable of generating a powerful electric field.":"一种能产生强大电场的鱼。","Spirits of marshes and bogs. From the cypresses and willows of the fens stems the power of these fierce protective spirits. With the boughs and branches they flow, emerging from trees near their foes to strike.":"湿地和沼泽之灵。沼地的柏树和柳树孕育出这些凶猛的守护之灵。 随枝条摆动，他们从敌人附近的树上冒出来进行攻击。","A swirling conflux of elemental water streaming from the elemental plane into this one, with powerful spirits and mighty floods flowing from it.":"一股元素水漩流，从元素位面流到这个位面，倾泻着强大的灵体和洪流。","A large, thick-hided pachyderm. It crushes its foes and then thrashes them with its trunk.":"一个巨大的厚皮动物。它会踩扁它的敌人，然后再用鼻子进行抽打。","An elf, a member of an ancient fey race.":"一个精灵——一个古代精类种族中的一员。","A giant scorpion with a massive barb on its tail dripping deadly venom. It is one of the largest arachnids known.":"一只巨大的蝎子，尾巴上有一个巨大的倒刺，滴着致命的毒液。 它是已知的最大的蛛形纲动物之一。","A glob of grey sludge that has somehow developed a rudimentary awareness and limited motility. It periodically draws heat from its surroundings to sustain itself, freezing enemies unfortunate enough to be adjacent at the time.":"一团灰色污泥，不知何故已具备了初步的意识，有着有限的运动能力。 它周期性地从周围吸取热量，以维持自身的生存，同时冰冻附近不幸的敌人。","A gaunt humanoid with flaking, pale chitin. Its spindly limbs are capable of startlingly quick movement and end in razor-sharp talons.":"一个瘦削的人形怪物，有一身苍白、蜕皮的甲壳。 其瘦长的四肢的行动极为迅速，并长有锋利的爪子。","A two-headed giant, stronger than most, and able to land devastating blows left and right with its two huge weapons.":"一个长有双头的巨人，比大多数巨人都要强壮， 能够用两支巨型武器左右开弓，发动毁灭性的打击。","A horribly powerful and swift demon, its shape obscured by a cloud of swirling scythe-like blades.":"一个极其强大、敏捷的恶魔，一团旋转的镰刀形的刀刃遮蔽了其身形。","A huge eyeball, encased in a levitating globe of incandescent energy.":"一个巨型眼球，被裹在一个飘浮、炽热的能量球之中。","A hybrid with the torso of a human atop the forelegs of a goat. It is fabled for its ability to play with the minds of those who intrude into its domain.":"一个混种生物，在山羊的前腿上有着人的躯干。 传说中，他能够玩弄闯入其领地的生物的心灵。","A feline creature that has been granted sentience by magical means. It uses the gift of speech to demand milk, treats and catnip.":"这只猫科动物被魔法赋予了心智。它会利用它的语言能力索要牛奶、零食和猫薄荷。","Followers of the ancient swamp ways, these witches rise above the muck and mire on a pair of stilt-like chicken legs. They are masters of pain and poison.":"这些女巫践行着古代的沼泽道路，她们踩着一双高跷状的鸡腿越过淤泥和泥沼。 她们是痛楚和毒药大师。","A bat whose leathery body burns with a hot flame.":"这只蝙蝠的毛皮上燃烧着一团炽热的火焰。","A variety of crab prized for its brilliantly jewelled shell. The rarity of the shells is only enhanced by its almost supernatural ability to wade through molten lava and expel massive quantities of flames.":"这种螃蟹因其璀璨的镶有宝石的外壳而备受珍视。 它的壳更为珍奇之处在于它那几近超自然的力量，它可以穿过熔岩，喷出大量火焰。","A great reptilian beast with powerful claws on its limbs, covered in thick red scales and with two huge bat-like wings. Little trails of smoke spill from its toothy maw.":"一条巨大的爬行类野兽，四肢上有强力的爪子，覆盖着厚厚的红色鳞片， 长有两只巨大的蝠翼形翅膀。它那长满利牙的口中冒出几缕烟雾。","A spirit drawn from the elemental plane of fire, which exists in this world as a brilliant column of raging flames.":"一个来自火元素位面的灵体，它以一柱熊熊的火焰的形态存在于这个世界上。","A giant with obsidian skin and a wild mane of glowing red hair, holding aloft a fiery sword. Fire giants believe that they are destined to unite and burn the entire world to cinders.":"一个巨人，有着黑曜石皮肤和狂野、浓密的炽红色头发，高举着一把燃烧着的剑。 火巨人相信他们终将联合起来，要把整个世界烧成灰烬。","A swirling cloud of flame. After striking a foe, it disintegrates.":"一团旋转的火焰云。击中敌人后，它会解体。","A hideous floating undead creature, the anguished spirit of a tortured victim, with torn skin hanging from an emaciated body. It restlessly stalks the dungeon, inflicting the anguish it felt in life upon those still living.":"一个丑陋、飘浮着的亡灵。 它是饱受折磨的受害者的苦痛灵魂，瘦骨嶙峋的身体上垂着撕裂的皮肤。 它不安地游荡于地牢，把生前承受的痛苦强加给仍然活着的人。","A lizard with a giant and colourful fringe folded around its neck. It flares its impressive frill at its victims while hissing angrily.":"一只蜥蜴，脖子上有着巨大、五颜六色的褶边。 它一边愤怒地嘶叫，一边向敌人展示它那令人印象深刻的褶边。","A sentient ant that walks upright and is competent at digging.":"一个有意识的蚂蚁，能够直立行走，善于挖掘。","A gelatinous assemblage of tentacles and venom, leaving a glistening trail as it slides along. Surely such a mockery of life could not be natural..?":"一团触手和毒液的凝胶状混合物，在滑动时会留下闪闪发光的痕迹。 当然，这种玩笑般的生命可能并非来自自然……？","A thin wisp of flaming swamp gas. It will burn the first hostile thing it touches and then dissipate.":"一缕稀薄的燃烧着的沼气。它会烧掉任何冒险靠太近的东西，无论是朋友还是敌人。","An incorporeal skeletal form surrounded by a cloud of freezing air, likely the remains of some unfortunate adventurer. It now floats slowly through the dungeon, seeking to share its fate with others.":"这个虚体的骷髅周身环绕着一团冷气。可能是某个不幸冒险者的遗骸。 现在它在地牢中缓慢飘动，想让别人也遭到和它一样的命运。","A giant with blue skin and hair like ice and snow. Its eyes are as bleak as winter skies. It marches grimly into battle with a great, frosty axe and howling blasts of cold.":"一个巨人，有着蓝色皮肤，长有冰雪般的头发。他的眼睛像冬季的天空一样阴郁。 他带着一把冰霜巨斧，裹挟着呼啸的寒流，冷酷地投入战斗。","A slender prism of unstable, soft gold that crackles with barely-contained destructive energy. Any blow which cracks its fragile surface is likely to result in a violent explosion.":"一个由不稳定的柔软金质构成的细长棱镜，难以遏制的破坏能量在其中噼啪作响。 任何能在它那脆弱的表面上产生裂纹的打击，都很有可能产生猛烈的爆炸。","A lumpy grey fungus, growing well in the dank underground dungeon.":"一种块状的灰色真菌，在潮湿的地牢里生长良好。","A granite statue of a hideous winged monster, somehow brought to life.":"一个可怕的有翼怪物的花岗岩雕像，不知怎么活过来了。","A crab twisted by proximity to negative energy. Apparitions of the dead swirl around it, only barely visible.":"一只因接近负能量而扭曲的螃蟹。周围盘旋着几乎看不见的鬼魂。","A vile interdimensional predator that feeds on the life force of living beings. It resembles an enormous, spiny moth.":"一只穿梭在次元间的邪恶捕食者，以活物的生命力为食。 它看起来像是一只巨大的、长刺的飞蛾。","A decayed cadaver, reanimated and accursed with a terrible hunger. It desires nothing but to feed on the flesh of the living, and will fell its victims with its vicious claws.":"一具活过来的腐烂的尸体，被极度的饥饿所诅咒。 它只想以活人的肉为食，并会用其恶毒的爪子击倒受害者。","A floating eyeball formed from living glass. Only the divine Jiyva could form such a curious servitor.":"一个由活性玻璃形成的浮眼。只有吉瓦的神力才能造出如此奇异的侍从。","A huge pulsating brain, floating just off the floor and glowing with mutagenic energies. It radiates a constant psychic influence upon nearby allies, using its vast intellect to empower their spellcasting abilities.":"一个巨大的脉动大脑，悬浮在地面上方，散发着诱变能量。 它持续以精神力量影响附近盟友，凭借庞大智力强化它们的施法能力。","A shapeshifter which has lost control over its transformations, and is constantly changing form.":"这个变形者已经失去了对变形的控制能力，在不断地变换形态。","A taller and better-equipped relative of goblins, and ally of orcs. It is somewhat doglike in appearance.":"地精和兽人的一个身材更高、装备更好的近亲，外貌有点像狗。","A commander of a pack of gnolls. Scars on its stout body give evidence of how it earned its rank.":"一群豺狼人的首领。他壮硕的身躯上满是伤痕，这足以证明他是怎么赢得今天的地位的。","A short, impatient and unfriendly humanoid. Goblins first appeared only a few years ago, but are now remarkably numerous. Sadly, no number of raucous goblin parties will put them in a welcoming mood toward adventurers.":"一个矮小、急躁、不友好的人形生物。地精在几年前才开始出现，但现在数量惊人。 遗憾的是，没有几个喧闹的地精派对能让冒险者觉得自己受到了欢迎。","A great winged dragon covered in shining golden scales. Legends say that its blood runs both hot and cold, and is venomous to boot.":"一条有翼巨龙，身上覆盖着闪耀的金鳞。传说它的血滚烫而又寒冷，并有着毒性。","A tiny and shimmering floating eye, swift as the wind and glistening like gold. It has a peculiarly hypnotic look.":"一个微小、发出微光的浮眼。它和风一样迅捷，并会像金子一样闪闪发光。 它的外表很特别，似乎能将人催眠。","A frog of exceptional size, for a frog. It lashes its prey with its tongue from a distance to coat them in its acidic stomach juices.":"对于蛙来说，它的体形极其巨大。 它从远处用舌头抽打猎物，把酸性胃液涂满它们全身。","A levitating ball, covered in malignant eyes and humming with eldritch energies. Many is the adventurer ripped limb from limb by its dreadful eyeteeth.":"一个飘浮的球，上面满是恶毒的眼睛，怪异的能量在嗡嗡作响。 许多冒险者被它那可怕的眼牙肢解了。","A bloated form covered in oozing sores and exhaling clouds of lethal poison.":"这团肿胀的东西上面满是渗出的疮，它不断排放出致命的毒云。","A muscular green-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有绿色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A muscular grey-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有灰色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","An ancient warrior, embalmed and cursed to walk in undeath for eternity.":"一个远古的战士，其尸体被防腐处理，被诅咒永远以死者之躯行走在世上。","A rare and distinct member of scaly society, light and swift like a snake, yet also intelligent like a naga. It is said that a guardian serpent would rather die in battle than leave anything to an intruder.":"它是有鳞生物中稀有而独特成员，既像蛇一样轻快，又有与纳迦一样的智力。 据说，守护蛇宁可战死，也不会给入侵者留下任何东西。","An ancient undead sorcerer, exhumed by the living divines Sheza and Sargol and forced to labour night and day to anchor them to the world. Even after the fall of the divine twins, it works to resurrect its fallen masters.":"一个古代的亡灵术师，被还在世的神西泽和萨格尔发掘出来， 被迫昼夜不停工作让他们弥留在世上。 即使在这对神倒下后，它仍在努力复活它那陨落的主人。","A bird-like creature with a human face that roams the coasts endlessly, feared for its sharp claws and harrying strikes.":"一个长有人脸的鸟状生物，无休止地在海岸上飞荡，要当心她的利爪和扑打。","A ravenous brute of a demon - as much animal as person. Born from the residue of mortal depravity, it gorges itself on malice and magic alike.":"一头贪得无厌的恶魔蛮兽，半似野兽，半似人形。 它由凡人的堕落残渣孕育而生，以恶意与魔力为食。","An extremely large and aggressive swine, bred in Hell, whose breath burns its foes to ash.":"一头在地狱中被养大、攻击性极强的巨型猪，其吐息能将敌人烧成灰烬。","A huge black dog with glowing red eyes, and smoke pouring from its fanged mouth.":"这条黑色的大狗长着炽红色眼睛，它那长满利齿的口中不断有烟雾喷出。","A heavily armoured warrior, in league with the powers of Hell, and usually accompanied by other unsavoury beings of its ilk.":"一名身着重甲的战士，与地狱力量结盟，经常与其他令人作呕的家伙集群行动。","A unusually large rat. Its weird, knobbly orange skin glows with the infernal energies that spawned it.":"一只特别大的老鼠。它那怪异的、长满疙瘩的橙色表皮散发着孕育它的地狱能量。","A towering monolith constructed and possessed by demonic forces. A thousand eyes leer through slits in its jagged, spiked armour.":"一块巨大的雕像，由恶魔力量构造和控制。 千只眼睛透过它那凹凸不平、长满尖刺的铠甲的缝隙窥视着。","An abhorrent pachyderm, descendant of demons, burning from within with the fires of Hell.":"一头令人憎恶的厚皮动物，它是恶魔的后裔，体内燃烧着地狱之火。","A hateful demon, desirous to see all life destroyed by its damnation.":"一个可恶的恶魔，渴望用它的诅咒毁灭所有见到的生命。","A hideous skeletal demon. It swoops through the air on powerful wings of ancient withered skin, taking sadistic joy from harrying those who would try to flee its grasp.":"一个丑陋的骷髅恶魔。它用强大的、表皮老而干瘪的翅膀在空中掠过， 从袭扰那些试图逃离它掌控的人中获得虐待狂的快乐。","A humanoid construct of insubstantial memory, floating through the air. Though perhaps somewhat changed in shape and bearing few discernable features, still it seems somehow to resemble a warrior from the distantly remembered past, ready with debilitating spells and deadly knifework.":"一个由虚幻记忆构成的人形造物，浮在空中。 尽管外形会发生变化，也没什么明显可辨的特征， 但它仍像一位来自记忆深处、遥远往昔的战士，准备着衰弱法术和致命的刀法。","A large creature with the hindquarters of a horse and the wings, head and talons of a great eagle. As popular heraldric creatures, some fortresses may keep them as symbols and defenders alike, where they in turn launch intruders into the waiting blades of their masters.":"一种大型生物，后半身如马，翅膀、头颅和利爪则如巨鹰。 它们是常见的纹章形象，有些堡垒也会将其作为象征与守卫饲养； 它们会把入侵者掷向主人守候着的刀锋。","A larger and even ruder goblin. Hobgoblins are perfectly capable of wielding weapons, but most prefer to beat their opponents to death with their bare hands.":"一个体形更大，甚至更粗暴的地精。 大地精完全有能力持握武器，但大多数更喜欢徒手把他们的敌人打死。","A large even-toed ungulate. Like human beings, it is omnivorous, intelligent, and nearly hairless.":"一头大型偶蹄类动物。像人类一样，杂食、聪明，而且几乎不长毛。","A rare celestial version of a usually filthy animal, said to be an angelic being who succumbed to hostile magic.":"在通常肮脏的动物之中罕见地出现了一个神圣品种， 据说，它是被敌对魔法击败的天使变成的。","A fearsome hunting dog, lithe and alert.":"一条骇人的猎狗，灵巧而又机警。","An aggressively territorial primate, known for the astonishing variety and volume of noise it can produce.":"一个领地意识极强、好斗的灵长类动物，以叫声种类繁多、音量惊人而闻名。","A great and nightmarish lacertilian beast. It has many heads, and the potential to grow many more!":"一头噩梦般的巨型蜥蜴类怪兽。它有很多个头，而且可能还会长出更多！","Hitting it with any bladed weapon bigger than a short blade risks lopping a head off and causing two more to grow in its place. Very large claws, such as trolls', are long enough to do the same. Only a weapon branded with flame will cauterise the wound and prevent more heads from growing.":"用任何比短刃更大的有刃武器击打它，有可能会砍掉一个头部， 但却会导致其位置上长出另外两个头。 用巨大的爪子进行攻击，比如巨魔的爪子，也会因足够长，导致产生同样的情况。 只有用带有火焰印记的武器才能灼烧伤口并防止长出更多的头。","A great and nightmarish lacertilian beast. It has many heads, and the potential to grow many more! Hitting it with any bladed weapon bigger than a short blade risks lopping a head off and causing two more to grow in its place. Very large claws, such as trolls', are long enough to do the same. Only a weapon branded with flame will cauterise the wound and prevent more heads from growing.":"一头噩梦般的巨型蜥蜴类怪兽。它有很多个头，而且可能还会长出更多！ 用任何比短刃更大的有刃武器击打它，有可能会砍掉一个头部， 但却会导致其位置上长出另外两个头。 用巨大的爪子进行攻击，比如巨魔的爪子，也会因足够长，导致产生同样的情况。 只有用带有火焰印记的武器才能灼烧伤口并防止长出更多的头。","A terrible creature, formed of snow and crystalline ice. Its feet leave puddles of icy water on the floor.":"一个由雪和冰晶构成的可怕生物。它所踏及的地面上会留下一滩冰水坑。","A man-sized demon covered in glittering ice.":"一个人类大小的恶魔，身上覆盖着闪光的寒冰。","A white, frost-coated dragon. Snowflakes trickle from its nostrils.":"一条满身冰霜的白龙。雪花从它的鼻孔上落下。","A huge frigid demon covered in frost and wreathed in freezing air. It is one of the most terrible denizens of the many Hells.":"一个巨大而寒冷的魔鬼，身上覆满冰霜，被冰冷的空气环绕着。 这是地狱中最可怕的魔物之一。","An imposing idol of some nameless arctic god, carved in glistening deep blue ice. Freezing vapours swirl about it, and a chill pervades the air.":"某个无名的极地神祗的壮观神像，用发光的深蓝色冰雕刻而成。 冰汽在它身边盘旋，空气中弥漫着寒意。","An emaciated warrior-mage, bound to guard long-coveted treasures. It calls forth deadly frost from its surrounds, freezing foes that are next to walls.":"一个憔悴的战斗法师，致力于守护渴望已久的宝藏。 他会从周围召唤出致命的冰霜，冻结靠近墙边的敌人。","A green lizard with strong jaws and sharp teeth, prized for its flesh.":"这条绿色蜥蜴长有强壮的颚和尖锐的牙齿，它的肉价值很高。","A warrior initiated in the mysteries of a dying cult, dedicated to serve thrones long-fallen. Its blows strip away magical defences, leaving its foes vulnerable to even the simplest hexes.":"一个在没落的邪教的奥秘中得到启蒙的战士，致力于服侍失落已久的王座。 他的攻击会剥去魔法防御，让他的敌人哪怕面对最简单的法术也会显得脆弱。","A mystical canine, frequently bound into the service of wizards and sorcerers. Its eyes flicker with remarkable intelligence, but its bite is no less sharp than its wilder cousins.":"一只神秘的犬科动物，经常为巫师和术师服务。 它的眼睛闪烁着非凡的智慧，它的咬伤也不比它更狂野的表亲逊色。","They are difficult to truly kill - when gravely wounded, they instead return to spiritual form to lick their wounds until ready to be summoned again.":"它们很难被真正杀死—— 当受到重伤时，它们会回到灵体形态舔舐伤口，直到准备好再次响应召唤。","A mystical canine, frequently bound into the service of wizards and sorcerers. Its eyes flicker with remarkable intelligence, but its bite is no less sharp than its wilder cousins. They are difficult to truly kill - when gravely wounded, they instead return to spiritual form to lick their wounds until ready to be summoned again.":"一只神秘的犬科动物，经常为巫师和术师服务。 它的眼睛闪烁着非凡的智慧，它的咬伤也不比它更狂野的表亲逊色。 它们很难被真正杀死—— 当受到重伤时，它们会回到灵体形态舔舐伤口，直到准备好再次响应召唤。","A very heavy, slow and apparently flightless dragon. It is named for its scales, which are so tough they might be iron. Small flakes of metal trail from its nostrils.":"这条龙非常沉重、迟缓，而且似乎不会飞。 它因其鳞片而得名，鳞片坚韧得像铁一样。铁屑从它的鼻孔中飞出。","A rare and powerful spirit from the elemental plane of earth, it exists in this world by inhabiting a hulking mass of iron.":"一个来自土元素位面的罕见而强大灵体， 凭借占据着一个巨大的铁块而存在于这个世界上。","A huge, rusting monolith, larger than any other species of giant. It packs an incredible punch.":"一个生锈的巨像，比其他任何各类的巨人都要大。他有着惊人的冲击力。","A large, ponderous and very solid statue of metal, given the power of locomotion through some esoteric means.":"一尊巨大、笨重而且极其坚固的金属雕像，某种深奥的法术赐予了它行动能力。","An ugly, twisted little minor demon with metal skin.":"一个丑陋、扭曲的低阶恶魔，长有钢铁皮肤。","A great troll, mighty of limb and plated with thick scales that resemble lightly rusted iron, especially in their hardness.":"一个强大的巨魔，四肢强壮，身上厚重的鳞片不仅看起来像生锈的铁， 而且硬度也和铁差不多。","A brutish figure, hastily armoured in scraps of leather and metal to combat a fearsome intruder. On its back is an antique, arcane 'lightning rod', which calls down thunder on distant foes, although it cannot hit nearby targets.":"一个粗野的生物，匆忙披上皮革和金属碎片，以抵抗可怕的入侵者。 他的背上有一根古老、神秘的“引雷针”，可以向远处的敌人发出雷霆， 尽管它无法击中附近的目标。","A guardian mage clad in pattern-etched armour. It can recite words of power to summon distant allies and imbue them with unnatural might.":"一个身穿有着刻蚀图案盔甲的守卫法师。 他可以吟诵强大的咒语来召唤附近的盟友，并给他们灌输异常的力量。","A towering, muscular figure, capable of safeguarding its allies by selflessly accepting a portion of the injuries inflicted upon them.":"一个高耸、肌肉发达的人，会无私地抗下友方受到的部分伤害来保护他们。","A small canine scavenger. Packs of jackals roam the underworld, searching for carrion to devour.":"一个小型的犬科食腐动物。成群结队的豺狼游荡在地下世界中寻找腐肉来果腹。","A pulsating mass of acidic protoplasm.":"一团悸动的酸性原生质。","A vampiric thrall bound into servitude by esoteric rituals. Though its rigid limbs give it an awkward gait, it moves with surprising speed, leaping upon its victims and leeching away their life essence with its vicious claws.":"被神秘的仪式束缚为吸血的奴隶。尽管其僵硬的四肢使它步态笨拙， 但却有着惊人速度，它扑向受害者，用恶毒的爪子吸取他们的生命精华。","A spider spirit that takes the appearance of a human. It weaves deadly magics to incapacitate and kill its prey.":"一个化身为人类的蜘蛛精。她编织着致命的法术，使猎物丧失行动能力并进行捕杀。","A gigantic humanoid with thick iron plates welded to its skin. It moves with alarming speed and deals incredible damage with its immense fists, but must rest between blows.":"一个巨大的人形怪，皮上烙着厚铁板，却移速极快。他能以惊人的速度移动， 用巨大的拳头造成难以置信的伤害，但必须在打击之间进行休整。","A spider which weaves webs between its front legs and leaps at its prey, ensnaring them. The speed with which it leaps is almost supernatural.":"这只蜘蛛会在它的两条前腿间织网，然后扑向猎物，将其捕捉。 它跳跃的速度几乎是超自然的。","A giant bee, bearing a deadly barb which can sting repeatedly.":"一只巨型的蜂，长着致命的倒刺，可以反复刺叮。","A comical figure full of life and laughter. It looks very happy to see you... but is there a slightly malicious cast to its features? Is that red face paint or something altogether less pleasant?":"一个满是活力和欢笑的丑角。他见到你似乎非常开心…… 不过，他的脸上似乎透露出些微恶意？ 那块红色的东西真的只是脸上的涂料吗，还是其他什么令人不快的东西？","A humanoid construct of insubstantial memory, floating through the air. Though perhaps somewhat changed in shape and bearing few discernable features, still it seems somehow to resemble a warrior from the distantly remembered past, well equipped with arms and armour both.":"一个由虚幻记忆构成的人形造物，浮在空中。 尽管外形会发生变化，也没什么明显可辨的特征， 但它仍像一位来自记忆深处、遥远往昔的战士，装备着精良的武器和盔甲。","A small, greyish creature with the look and temperament of a feral dog. No one knows for sure where kobolds come from, but ancient demon-gods, evil spirits, and meddling wizards have all been suggested as culprits.":"一个灰色的小型动物，其外表和性格都很像疯狗。 没人确切知道狗头人到底是从哪来的， 不过远古的魔神、邪灵和不安分的巫师都经常被指控为元凶。","A kobold that is bigger and tougher than the ordinary kobold, with a penchant for underhanded tactics.":"这个狗头人比普通的狗头人更大、更强壮，并且喜欢卑鄙的战术。","A kobold, ready with multiple armaments to defend itself from the many dangers of the depths. The blastmote-packed cannon on its shoulder bears its maker's mark, and is fiercely loyal; it will fire for none other.":"一个狗头人，准备了多种武器来保护自己免受深处的许多危险。 扛在其肩上的装着爆炸粉尘的火铳带有制造商的标记，而且非常忠诚： 其他人无法用它开火。","A kobold in league with demonic powers, able to call forth beings from the depths of Hell.":"一个与恶魔力量结盟的狗头人，能召唤来自地狱深处的生物。","An enormous monitor lizard more than capable of preying on large animals.":"一条超巨型的蜥蜴，能够捕食大型动物。","A gargantuan sea monster, capable of devouring entire ships. Its many tentacles reach towards the shore and crush any who draw near.":"一只巨大的海怪，能吞噬整艘船。它的许多触手伸向岸边，会把任何靠近的人击碎。","A hideous conglomeration of mangled body parts, possessed and altered in ways that challenge sanity. Each varies in speed, strength, or resilience by the nature of whatever unfortunates were used to make it.":"一团骇人的残缺肢体，被附身并扭曲成挑战理智的形态。 其速度、力量或坚韧各不相同，取决于制造它时用了哪些不幸者的躯体。","A blazing swift skull that cackles with the bleak malice of the dead. Fond of swarming, its laughter grows more spiteful and powerful for each nearby member of its own kind.":"一个燃烧的、迅捷的头骨，带着死者冷酷的恶意咯咯地笑着。 它喜欢成群结队，一旦附近有同类成员，笑声将变得更恶毒、更强大。","A burning red snake which dwells in pools of lava. It spits gobs of molten rock at passers-by.":"一条火红色的蛇，栖息在岩浆池之中。它会向路过的人喷射一团熔岩。","An accursed soul magically bound to hellish servitude for the highest bidder. If its master is slain, it will be freed, departing this realm with gratitude.":"一个被诅咒的灵魂，被魔法束缚在地狱般的奴役之下，会为最高出价者而战。 如果它的主人被杀，它将得到自由，带着感激离开这个世界。","A powerful wizard who has learned to cheat death itself, now existing as a skeletal, desiccated corpse kept intact by a mighty exercise of dark magic.":"有些强大的巫师甚至能骗过死亡本身， 而现在它只剩一具骷髅、干燥的尸体，通过强大的黑暗魔法维系着存在。","A buzzing contraption made from a coil and a rod. It irregularly zaps electricity at the most distant enemy in its range.":"一个用线圈和金属杆制成、嗡嗡作响的装置。 它会不定时向射程内最远的敌人释放电流。","A small serpentine dragon with a pair of strong forelimbs. Its thick scales give off an eerie red glow.":"一条小型蛇形龙，长有一对强壮的前肢。它坚厚的鳞片发出诡异的红光。","A spell, waiting to cast itself at the first foe that enters its range. Once it does, it'll dissipate into the ether.":"这个法术，在等待着时机，向第一个进入其射程的敌人施放。 一旦发生，它便会消散到以太中。","The echo of an unmourned soul. Though the memories of its living self are long-faded, it is drawn to the moment of death by some lingering instinct. It seizes upon the passage of other souls, losing the last vestiges of its being in the memories of another's life.":"一个无人哀悼的灵魂的回音。尽管它自己生前的记忆已经褪去很久了， 但还是被某种弥留的本能拉到了死亡的那一刻。 它攫住其他灵魂离去的时刻，并在另一段人生的记忆中耗尽自身最后的残痕。","A formless mass of negative energy, bound to bring terrible torment once the forces holding it together dissolve. The alien presence of intruders to the Abyss is sure to unravel it, yet it seems perversely drawn toward them; still, it seems somehow reluctant to move while being observed.":"一个无定形的负能量团，一旦维系它的力量消失，势必带来可怕的折磨。 闯入者对深渊而言格格不入的存在必定会令它瓦解，它却反常地被他们吸引。 不过，在被观察的时候，它似乎不太想移动。","A violet-scaled serpent with faintly glowing eyes. It thirsts for magic as well as flesh, and its bite can drink dry the magical reservoirs of even a powerful mage in no time.":"一条长有紫色鳞片和微微发光的眼睛的巨蛇。它对魔法的渴望如同对肉的渴望一样， 哪怕是一个强大的法师被它咬一口，魔力库也会瞬间被吸干。","A hideous cross-breed, bearing the features of a human and a lion, with great bat-like wings. Its tail bristles with spikes that can be loosed at potential prey.":"一个狰狞的混种动物：它身上既有人的特征也有狮子的特征， 还长着一对巨大的蝠翼形翅膀。它的尾巴上长满的尖刺，会射向潜在的猎物。","The wandering shade of a long-dead soul who died for a forgotten cause. Though their memories have turned to mist, something deep within still compels them to serve and sacrifice - no matter the cost.":"一个早已死去、为某个被遗忘的事业而献身的灵魂的游荡阴影。 尽管它们的记忆已经变得模糊，但内心深处的某种东西仍然驱使它们去服侍和牺牲—— 无论付出什么代价。","A nymphal hybrid, with a winged torso of a human atop the stinging abdomen of a bee. The meliai serve under many roles: priestesses of nature, nurses to the divine, and warrior-champions for their hives.":"一个仙女的混种，上方是带有翅膀的人类躯体，下方是长有蜂刺的腹部。 墨利埃肩负多重职责：自然的祭司、神圣的看护者和蜂巢的战士。","A hybrid with the torso of a human and the tail of a fish. It is capable of dwelling both in water and on land, and fiercely defends its domain.":"一个人身鱼尾的混种生物。他能在水中和陆地上栖居，并会激烈地捍卫其领地。","A slender merfolk mystic with unusually webby hands. Its form shifts and glistens as if seen through ocean spray.":"一个纤细的人鱼秘术师，有着不同寻常的蹼状手。 他的形态变幻、发光，仿佛是透过海浪所看到的。","A beguiling merfolk whose voice mesmerises listeners. It carries no weapon, but its song summons drowned souls to defend the sea against intruders.":"一个迷人的人鱼，她的声音令听众陶醉其中。 她虽然没有持任何武器，但她的歌声能召唤溺魂，抵抗入侵者，保卫海洋。","A powerfully muscled merfolk warrior, bearing a deadly weapon.":"一个肌肉强健的人鱼战士，手持一把致命武器。","A fearsome merfolk champion with a piercing gaze and a large bundle of javelins.":"一名令人畏惧的人鱼勇士，目光锐利，还携有一大捆标枪。","A beguiling merfolk whose voice can mesmerise listeners.":"一个迷人的人鱼，她的声音会迷住听众。","A large muscular human with the head of a bull. It makes its home in a gauntlet where it awaits worthy challengers.":"一个高大、壮硕的人形生物，长着一颗牛头。他居住在竞技场，等待值得较量的挑战者。","A hideous molten stone statue come to life, with flames licking across its body.":"一个可怕的熔岩雕像活了过来，火舌缠绕着它的身体。","A moth known for its ability to inspire rage by touching its foes, or merely gazing at its friends. For some inexplicable reason, it was eradicated from the surface centuries ago.":"一种飞蛾，以其通过触碰它的敌人或仅仅凝视它的友方就能激发狂暴的能力而闻名。 由于某些莫名其妙的原因，几个世纪前它就从地表消失了。","An undead figure covered in bandages and embalming fluids, compelled to walk by an ancient curse. It radiates a malign aura.":"一个裹着绷带和防腐液的亡灵，被古老的诅咒驱使着行走。它散发出邪恶的气息。","An ancient servant of a long forgotten god, embalmed and cursed to walk in undeath for all eternity.":"一位早已被遗忘的神明的远古仆人，经防腐处理后受诅咒， 永远以不死之身行走。","A bizarre creature, twisted and warped by overexposure to magical radiation. Each has a different set of traits.":"一个奇异的生物，由于过度暴露于魔力辐射而扭曲变形。每个都有不同的特征。","A hybrid that is human from the waist up; below is a scaly, muscular snakelike tail. Its mouth drips with venomous saliva.":"一个人和蛇的混种，他的腰部以上是人类，下面却是一条健壮的、长着鳞片的蛇尾。 他的嘴边滴着毒性唾液。","A naga that has trained in the use of magic, trailed by an eldritch nimbus. It is especially skilled in spells dealing with poison and venom.":"这个纳迦进行过施法训练，所到之处都会留下神秘的灵气。 他特别擅长施放和毒有关的法术。","An esoteric mystic draped in talismans. It venerates poison as a sacred gift and means of spiritual purification.":"一个高深莫测的秘术师，佩戴着护身符。他将毒药尊崇为神圣的礼物和净化精神的手段。","A naga with exceptionally keen eyesight, adept in the use of ranged weaponry and simple magics which allows it to snipe at targets across nearly any obstruction.":"一个视力极其敏锐的纳迦，善于使用远程武器和简单魔法， 使得他几乎可以跨越任何阻碍狙击目标。","A fearsome naga warrior clad in sturdy armour and wielding a mighty weapon.":"一个令人敬畏的纳迦战士，身穿坚甲，手拿利器。","A magnificent example of the naga. It is an expert at both martial and magical arts.":"一个在纳迦中受到尊崇的模范。他精通武术和魔法。","A malign force from the space between planes. It is hostile to the magic forces that removed it from its home. These horrors are often the result of mistaken summoning spells and have slain many aspiring wizards.":"一个来自位面之间的邪恶力量。它对把它带离家园的魔法力量充满敌意。 这个恐怖通常是召唤魔法出错的结果，并杀死了许多有抱负的巫师。","An ancient stone creature that has lived among these frozen caves since before Antaeus rent Cocytus into being. It tolerates its new neighbors begrudgingly, preferring the company of its petrified enemies. Veins of ice permeate its frozen stone flesh.":"一个古老的石质生物，早在安泰俄斯撕裂出悲叹河之前便生活在这些冰冻洞穴中。 它勉强容忍新邻居，却更喜欢与自己石化的敌人为伍。 冰脉在它那冰冻的石肉中流通着。","An evil wizard who is devoted to the practice of death magic, the mastery of unholy energies, and the raising of corpses into a parody of life.":"这个邪恶的巫师毕生钻研死亡魔法的奥秘， 掌握邪恶的能量，以及给予尸体虚假的生命。","A vile undead creation of the most unholy necromancy, made from the decaying corpses of humanoid creatures. It exists to spread disease and decay.":"一个被最邪恶的死灵法术创造出来的亡灵造物，其身体由人形生物的腐尸拼凑而成。 它的存在的就是为了散布疾病与腐化。","A weirdly shaped demon, pulsing and shifting with mutagenic energies, its belly distended with the devoured brains of its victims.":"一个奇形怪状的恶魔。它的身体受变异能量的影响，不断搏动变化着， 它的肚子因吞食太多受害者的脑子而发胀。","A beautiful statue of an unknown creature, jet-black like a tear in reality. Its eyes glow with an otherworldly, malignant radiance.":"一尊美丽的未知生物的雕像，黑玉般晶莹的色泽像是现实中的泪珠。 它的眼睛闪烁着超乎寻常的邪恶光芒。","A wizard fond of illusion and treachery. They scorn the crudeness of other magicians, who hurl wild conjurations toward their foes rather than cunningly exploiting their greatest weaknesses.":"一个喜欢幻象和背叛的巫师。 他们蔑视那些向敌人疯狂施展魔法、而不是巧妙利用其最大的弱点的粗鲁的魔法师。","A more intelligent cousin of the mighty kraken, capable of using tools and spells. It is fully amphibious, but most of its species choose to stay beneath the waves and serve their King.":"强大的海怪的一个近亲，但比海怪更聪明，能够使用工具和魔法。 它是完全两栖的，但它们大多数物种还是选择留在波涛之下，服侍它们的王。","A large, ugly, and fat creature, distantly related to goblins. It is tremendously strong, and likes fighting alongside its orc friends.":"一个高大、丑陋而肥胖的生物，是地精的远亲。 它力大无穷，喜欢和兽人朋友并肩作战。","A rare breed of ogre, skilled in the use of magic. It usually becomes a chieftain among its kin.":"一个罕见的食人魔，擅长使用魔法。他通常是一群食人魔的酋长。","A very dangerous plant which fends off predators by spraying corrosive vitriol at them. Even experienced adventurers give oklob plants a wide berth.":"这株危险的植物能靠喷吐腐蚀性强酸来击退捕食者。 即使是经验丰富的冒险者，也会尽量远离奥克罗布植物。","A young oklob plant. It is more fragile than the mature specimen, but the acid it sprays is just as deadly.":"一株奥克罗布植物幼苗。它比成熟植株更脆弱，但喷出的酸同样致命。","A large, rowdy, and drink-loving creature. When they're not busy with their duties serving any number of gods, oni mostly love a good fight.":"一个体形巨大、吵闹、爱喝酒的生物。 当鬼不忙于侍奉神明的职责时，他们通常会喜欢痛快地打上一架。","A creature from the heavenly realms. It consists of a wheel within a wheel, and both of these are covered in eyes; strange flames of holy fire flicker all over it. To be seen by its countless eyes is to be highlighted and branded as both dissident and quarry for its allies to hunt down.":"一个来自天国的生物。 它由轮中套轮构成，两个轮上都布满眼睛，周身闪烁着奇异圣火。 被它无数只眼睛看见，就会被标记为异端与猎物，供它的盟友追猎。","An intricately carved idol of some nameless godling, hewn of translucent orange crystal. Its lifeless eyes seem to glitter uncannily with a wicked intelligence. It is capable of unleashing a powerful psychic assault upon the minds of any who approach it.":"某个无名神祗的神像，用透明橙色水晶细致地雕刻而成。 它那无生命的眼睛似乎闪烁着邪恶的智慧。 它会对任何接近它的人的心灵发动强大的精神攻击。","An amber-coloured demon with a barbed tail not unlike that of a scorpion.":"一个琥珀色的恶魔，尾巴上的倒刺，与蝎子无异。","A huge, glowing, four-limbed purple creature with heightened senses, created by the Orb itself. It guards the Orb with enormous punctiliousness and violence, and its death will alert any Boundless Tesseracts on the level to begin creating reinforcements.":"一个巨大、发光的紫色四肢生物，有着特别敏锐的知觉，被宝珠自身所创造。 它一丝不苟而又凶暴地守护着宝珠；它一旦死亡，就会惊动本层所有 无界超立方体，使其开始制造援军。","Unless the Orb has already been disturbed, it will refuse to abandon its duty by leaving the floor.":"除非宝珠已经受到惊扰，否则它绝不会离开本层、擅离职守。","A huge, glowing, four-limbed purple creature with heightened senses, created by the Orb itself. It guards the Orb with enormous punctiliousness and violence, and its death will alert any Boundless Tesseracts on the level to begin creating reinforcements. Unless the Orb has already been disturbed, it will refuse to abandon its duty by leaving the floor.":"一个巨大、发光的紫色四肢生物，有着特别敏锐的知觉，被宝珠自身所创造。 它一丝不苟而又凶暴地守护着宝珠；它一旦死亡，就会惊动本层所有 无界超立方体，使其开始制造援军。 除非宝珠已经受到惊扰，否则它绝不会离开本层、擅离职守。","A conjured globe of pure magic that homes onto a designated target, albeit with massive inertia. A smart and agile person may move out of its path, causing it to miss its target. It cannot be avoided by Dodging skill, and is able to make sharp turns to hit adjacent targets.":"一个变出的纯魔法球，能够锁定指定目标，尽管具有巨大的惯性。 一个聪明而敏捷的人可能会选择偏离它的路径，会让它错过目标。 但仅凭闪避技能无法避免它，并且它能够急转弯以击中相邻目标。","A globe of raw primordial fire, capable of impressive pyrotechnics and of twisting the very flesh of creatures who come into its ken.":"一个由最原始的火焰构成的球体，能够发出壮观的烟火， 并能扭曲进入其视野的生物的肉体。","An eerily glowing spider with strands of pure energy emerging from its spinnerets. It seems to want to keep its distance.":"一只发着奇异光芒的蜘蛛，纯粹的魔法能量从它的喷丝头上涌出。 它似乎在竭力和你保持距离。","A subterranean tribe whose forebearers were once scattered across every corner of the surface world. Eons of persecution have taught them the necessity of violence and the importance of having your brethren at your side.":"一个丑陋的地下生物，被认为是人类、猪或是鸭嘴兽的远亲。 兽人喜欢成群聚在一起，制造骚乱。","An exalted servant of the orc god Beogh and a master of many foul rites, to whose aid Beogh will even send beings from the netherworld.":"这名兽人是兽人之神比欧弗的高级仆从之一，主管多种污秽仪式， 比欧弗甚至会派遣地狱生物来支援他。","A heavily armoured orc, covered in scars from many past battles. It commands its brethren in battle, rousing them to greater, more violent efforts with bloodcurdling shouts.":"一个重甲兽人，身上布满过去战斗留下的疤痕。 他在战斗中指挥着他的兄弟，用恐怖的吼声激发他们投入更大、更暴力的力量。","A servant of Beogh, the ancient god of the orcs. Beogh rewards its devoted prayers by striking down its enemies.":"这个兽人侍奉比欧弗——古老、残忍的兽人之神。 通过打击敌人，比欧弗会回报其虔诚的祈祷。","An exceptionally competent orcish wizard, in league with hellish and chthonic forces and motivated by the purest imaginable strain of malevolence.":"一名法术造诣高深的兽人术士，与地狱和黑暗力量为盟，被世间最纯粹的恶意所驱使。","A supreme commander of an orc host, skilled at both melee and ranged combat.":"兽人大军的最高指挥官，擅长近战和远程战斗。","An experienced, armoured and well-armed orc soldier, able to command a small mob of its fellows.":"一名装备精良、战斗经验丰富的兽人士兵。他是一个小型战团的首领。","An orc who has gained proficiency in the occult arts, using them for martial purposes.":"一个精通神秘技艺的兽人，会将其用于战斗。","A muscular humanoid with pale scales, a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有苍白色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A formidable demon lord inhabiting the endless halls of Pandemonium. Each one is different, with its own set of strengths and weaknesses.":"这个可怕的恶魔领主居住在万魔殿无尽的厅堂中。 每位万魔殿领主都是独一无二的存在，拥有不同的能力和弱点。","A four-legged humanoid construct, tasked with recapturing escaped prisoners and punishing heretics. Long after the fall of the empire it once served, it continues to enforce imperial law, knowing no jurisdiction.":"一个有着四条腿的人形造物，其任务是抓捕逃犯和惩罚异教徒。 它曾服务过的帝国已经覆灭很久了， 它却仍不知疆界地执行着帝国法律。","A dragon consecrated to the holy divine powers. Its breath is blessed fire, and its claws sear its victims with divine wrath.":"一条侍奉于神圣力量的龙。它的吐息是神圣的火，利爪会带着神怒灼伤受害者。","A hideous translucent green spirit of a warrior fallen in battle but recalled to this plane by unholy magic. The blade it wields is ethereal, rendering those it strikes weak-willed and vulnerable to dark magic.":"一个可怕的、幽绿色的战败战士的灵魂，被邪恶魔法召回到这个层面。 它所持的利刃虚无缥缈，会削弱被击中者的意志，使其更易受黑暗魔法影响。","A nearly-transparent undead spirit, suspected by some sages to be a degenerate form of ghost, with no memories of its former life. It rarely stays in one place for long.":"一个几乎全身透明的亡灵幽魂，有些贤者怀疑它是一种退化的鬼魂， 因为它完全没有生前的记忆。它很少会在一个地方停留很长时间。","A royal ant returned to unlife through strange, probably horrifying means. It binds the souls of its allies when slain, allowing them to fight on after death as simulacra.":"一只皇家蚂蚁通过奇怪的，可能是可怕的方式恢复了生命。 当盟友被杀时，它会缚住他们的灵魂，让他们在死后作为拟像继续战斗。","A pillar of salt shaped like a statue, but worked by no living hands.":"一根像是雕像的盐柱，但并非由手工打造。","A plant that has adapted to grow in the unpleasant dungeon environment, somehow thriving even underground in the absence of the sun.":"一株已经适应在恶劣的地牢环境中生长的植物， 不知何故在没有太阳的地下也能茁壮成长。","The apparition of an unfortunate adventurer, retaining many of the skills and abilities the adventurer had in life. It is condemned to haunt this particular level of the dungeons, lashing out violently at the next adventurer to cross its path.":"这是某个不幸冒险者的鬼魂，它依然保有着许多生前拥有的技能和能力。 它被诅咒，徘徊在这一层地牢，向碰见它的下一个冒险者发起猛烈的攻击。","A bear covered in glistening white fur, habituated to cold conditions. Like all ursines, it will become enraged if badly hurt.":"这头熊身上披着发光的白色皮毛，能在寒冷环境中生存。 和所有其他熊类一样，它会在受重伤时会变得狂暴。","A blasphemous being that was once an angel of the Shining One. It now stands as unliving proof that not even the holiest of beings are beyond Yredelemnul's grasp.":"这个渎神之物曾经是光辉者的天使之一。然而，现在它的存在只能证明一件事： 即使是世间最圣洁的存在也无法逃出伊莱德莱姆努尔的魔掌。","A ravenous and incredibly buggy monster. Please report its existence to the DevTeam.":"一个贪婪、令人难以置信的臭虫怪物。请向开发者团队报告它的存在。","A gargantuan humanoid of fractured shape from the aeons when the seas were but primordial soup. The many shapeshifters of the dungeon once sloughed off from these unfathomably ancient beings, and when they themselves finally cease, even their remains will give birth one last time to furious monsters.":"一个巨大的、身形破碎的人形生物，当海洋还是原始汤的洪荒时代，他就已经出现了。 地牢中许多变形者就是从这些深不可测的古代生物身上脱落的， 当这些远古生物最终终结时，他们的遗体甚至还会在这最后一次生成愤怒的怪物。","A starved spirit whose mouth is a pit of rot, emitting vile fumes. Its putrid maw cannot eat the food it finds, so it moans with rage and desparate hunger.":"一个饥饿的灵魂，它的嘴是个腐烂的坑，散发着恶臭。 它那腐烂的嘴无法吃它找到的食物，愤怒地呻吟着，绝望地饿着。","A muscular purple-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有紫色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A ruler of a swarm of bees, even larger and more dangerous than its many offspring.":"一个蜂群的统治者，她比她的后代更大、更危险。","A long and sinuous dragon, seemingly more neck and tail than anything else. Its skin shines like molten mercury, magical energies arc from its pointed snout, and it moves with terrifying swiftness.":"一条长而蜷曲着的龙，看起来几乎完全是颈和尾巴。 它的皮肤像熔铸的水银一样发着光，口鼻喷射着魔法能量，而且它的动作迅捷得吓人。","A mercurial spirit drawn from the elemental plane of earth. It exists in this world by inhabiting a shimmering body of liquid metal.":"一个来自土元素位面的灵体。 它凭借占据着一个闪闪发光的液态金属体而存在于这个世界上。","A pesky little marsupial that is a bit like a rat, but not quite.":"这个烦人的小型有袋动物外形有点像老鼠，但只是有点像而已。","A giant cockroach that has been exposed to high amounts of mutagenic energy. It is horrifyingly mutated, but this has only made it stronger.":"一个暴露于大量诱变能量的巨型蟑螂。 它发生了可怕的变异，但这只会让它变得更强大。","A bedraggled priest, once-fine robes now lined with salt and dust. Forsaken by the gods, it now relies on constructs to protect itself.":"一个邋遢的祭司，曾经华丽的长袍现已沾满了盐和灰尘。 他被诸神抛弃，现在依赖造物保护自己。","A maneater demon, bestial and misshapen, in search of hidden power and knowledge. It is an expert in the art of illusion, and is exceptionally intelligent and cruel.":"一个畸形而兽性的食人恶魔，追寻隐秘的力量与知识。 它精通幻术，极其聪明而残忍。","A dirty rodent that has grown large and aggressive in the dungeon environment.":"这个肮脏的啮齿动物在地牢的环境下长得又大又凶猛。","A profoundly unnatural hound, crackling with electricity. It travels in packs, and covers great distances by bursting into living lightning.":"一条很反常的猎犬，身上的电流噼啪作响。 它们成群行动，并能以爆出活体闪电的方式行进很远的距离。","A haunting form wielding a giant scythe, ceaselessly harvesting the souls of the living.":"一具骷髅挥舞着一把巨大的镰刀，不断收割生者的灵魂。","A larger cousin of the common imp, with a fiendish grin and two short wings sprouting from its shoulders. It favours tridents and loves to skewer its victims with painful barbs.":"常见的小恶魔的一个体形更大的近亲，咧着邪恶的笑容，肩上生有两个短小的翅膀。 它喜欢三叉戟，爱用令人痛苦的倒刺串起它的受害者。","A muscular red-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有红色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A buzzing hornet with a vicious stinger dripping with paralytic poison.":"一只嗡嗡作响的大黄蜂身上有一根毒刺，上面滴着麻痹性毒液。","A vicious black spider with a splash of red on its swollen abdomen. Its mandibles drip with lethal poison.":"一只凶狠的黑色蜘蛛，它肿胀的腹部上有一大块红斑。 致命毒液正从它的虫颚上滴落下来。","The skeletal remains of someone who died unmourned and forgotten. It burns with an unquenchable hunger to be remembered.":"一个缠绕着幽冷蓝色火焰的骷髅，跨在今生和来世之间。 弥留的亡者的回响在鬼火中摇曳着。","A giant annelid, glistening with slime, with unusually large teeth. It expels fragments of its own innards to ensnare unsuspecting prey.":"一条巨大的环节动物，身上的黏液闪烁着，牙齿大得出奇。 它排出自己内脏的碎片来诱捕毫无戒心的猎物。","A small but dangerous dragon. Its breath is visible even on the warmest days.":"一个小而危险的龙。即使在最炎热的天气里，也能看到它的吐息。","A rodent with hair of a most peculiar green colour, and a powerful bite. It tends to form great swarms with its kin.":"一个长有奇异绿毛的啮齿动物，咬合力很强。它往往和它的同类成群生活。","An oozing avalanche, scouring the ground beneath it as it rumbles forward. It consumes only the metal and bone from its victims, using them to reinforce itself even further.":"一个涌出的山崩，它隆隆前进时冲刷着下方的地面。 它只吞食受害者的金属和骨头，用它们来进一步增强自身。","A particularly rich and golden gelatinous thing. Smaller jellies swim and pulse just below its surface, ready to burst forth at the slightest touch.":"一个特别浓郁的金色凝胶状物质。 更小的果冻怪在它的表面下游动、搏动，只要稍加触碰就会喷涌而出。","An ancient pharaoh, embalmed and cursed to undeath, now capable of great and terrifying feats of magic.":"一位古代法老，被防腐并诅咒为不死之人，现在能够完成伟大而可怕的魔法技艺。","A hideous humanoid figure with rust-spotted metal skin, spreading corrosion and decay to all it touches.":"一个丑陋的人形人物，有着锈迹斑斑的金属皮肤， 要把腐蚀和腐烂蔓延到所有接触到的地方。","A red, flaming half-human half-snake creature with a legendary affinity for fire.":"一个红色的、燃烧的半人半蛇的生物，传说和火的关系很密切。","A member of the salamander's scholarly caste, possessed of lesser size and strength, but wise in the ways of magic.":"沙罗曼蛇学者阶层的一员，体形和力量较弱，却深谙魔法之道。","An intimidating volcano lord. It commands the magma of its realm as an extension of its body, and the majesty of its gaze can weaken even the proudest challenger.":"一个令人生畏的火山领主。他能控制自己领域内的岩浆，仿佛是身体的延伸。 再骄傲的挑战者也会因他那威严的目光而畏缩。","A small, human-shaped agglomeration of salt. It was created by the last fugitive loyalists of the fallen eastern empire, forced in desperation to construct golems from local resources to defend themselves.":"一个小型的人形盐块。它是由最后一批忠于没落的东方帝国的逃亡者创建的， 他们在绝望中被迫用当地资源建造魔像来保护自己。","A more intelligent relative of the faun, often found in their company, and far more unforgiving of — and dangerous to — interlopers.":"牧神的一种更聪明的近亲，常与牧神为伍； 它对闯入者更为无情，也远为危险。","A loathsome arachnid, armed to the teeth. Its body is covered in a thick carapace, its tail is tipped by a venomous sting, and its forelimbs are equipped with a pair of sharp grasping claws.":"一只讨厌的蛛形纲动物，武装到了牙齿。 它的躯体上覆着一层厚厚的甲壳，尾巴末端有一根毒刺，前肢上还长有一对利爪。","A brightly coloured snake, very comfortable in the water. It has a highly potent venomous bite.":"一条颜色鲜艳的蛇，水性很好。它的咬伤有很强的毒性。","An animated corpse alight with terrible fire. The flames are fueled by its regenerating flesh, which bubbles and melts as it grows.":"一具会动的尸体，燃烧着可怕的火焰。 火焰以其不断再生的血肉为燃料；血肉生长时会起泡、熔化。","A six-winged servant of the good gods, of the highest rank of the angelic hosts. Its eyes burn with divine fire.":"一个善神的仆人，生有六翼，是最高级别的天使。他的眼睛燃烧着圣焰。","A member of an order of monks who abandoned their former faith. It now serves a minor god of wind and whispers, who allows it to calm the air and, when in great need, to break the stillness with divine thunder.":"一个放弃原先信仰的僧侣。 现在他侍奉掌管风和低语的低阶的神，这使得他能让空气平静下来， 或是非常需要的时候，用神圣的雷声打破寂静。","A skulking apparition that disguises itself as a harmless shadow. Attuned to the dim light of the dungeon, it can slip in and out of sight at will, moving swiftly from one pool of shade to the next before striking unerringly at the blind spots of those who cannot see it.":"一个潜行的幽影，伪装成无害的影子。它与地牢的昏暗光线相契， 能随意隐现，从一片阴影飞快移至另一片，再精准袭向看不见它的敌人的盲区。","A mysterious demonic figure, difficult to distinguish from the darkness around it. It weaves the shadows into powerful minions.":"一个神秘的恶魔身影，很难与周围的黑暗区分。它把阴影编织成强大的仆从。","A great umbral dragon, radiating evil and death. Its breath reeks of the grave.":"一条巨大的暗影龙，散发着邪恶和死亡。它的吐息弥漫着坟墓的气味。","A shadowy minor demon, with an affinity for the necromantic arts.":"一个影状的低阶恶魔，精于死灵术。","A mist-wreathed skeletal shadow, hanging in mid-air. It drains away the life force of living beings.":"烟雾缭绕的骸骨之影，在半空中游荡。它以活物的生命力为食。","A gnarled mangrove, possessed of sapience and a cantankerous disposition. Its roots run deep through the water and soil of its marshy home and can make footing very difficult for those who provoke its ire. Marsh fauna are often found nesting within its branches, and may not take kindly to being disturbed.":"一片长有节瘤的红树林，智慧而性情乖戾。 它的根深深扎入水和它的沼泽家园中，这使得激怒它的人很难站稳脚根。 沼泽动物常在它的枝上筑巢，他们被打扰了可不是善茬。","A disturbing creature with the power to change its form. It is very rarely observed alive in its natural state.":"这个诡异的怪物拥有变换自己形态的能力。它原本形态的存在很少被观察到。","An incredibly fast-moving bird, known for impaling its prey on shards of ice before tearing them to pieces. It has acclimated to the desolate wastes of Cocytus, and is enveloped with an accursed chill.":"一只移动速度极快的鸟，以先用冰片刺穿猎物、再将其撕碎而闻名。 它已适应悲叹河那荒凉的废墟，被严酷的寒意裹挟着。","A strangely deformed floating eyeball, pulsating with flesh-twisting energy.":"一个诡异变形了的浮眼，悸动着扭曲血肉的能量。","A sinuous serpent whose body crackles with volatile electricity. Its electric shroud can discharge when struck, inflicting a painful shock on any nearby foes.":"一条蜿蜒的巨蛇，身上不稳定的电流噼啪作响。 它的电罩被攻击时会放电，对附近的敌人造成痛苦的电击。","A terrible spirit which brings an unearthly silence to the area around it, making it impossible to recite the magical incantations involved with casting spells or reading scrolls.":"这个可怕的幽魂给周围区域带来超乎寻常的寂静， 身处结界中的时候无法吟诵魔法咒语，也就不能施放魔法或是阅读卷轴。","An icy replica of a monster, animated by heretical magics.":"一个怪物的冰制复制品，由异端魔法所激活。","A small vile creature that moves in bursts, stopping then darting with lightning speed. It sprays sparks as it goes.":"这个邪恶的小东西会突然停下，然后又以闪电般的速度突进。它边走边迸出电火花。","A vicious and heavily armed humanoid skeleton, animated by unholy power.":"一具被不洁之力复活的人形骷髅，性情凶暴，装备精良。","A skeleton compelled to unlife by the exercise of necromancy.":"一具被死灵法术复活的骷髅。","A strange aerial creature formed of fleshy clouds and electric feathers. It commands the faint wind currents of the Dungeon with every strike, which will buffet its victims in dramatic correlation to the amount of open air around said prey.":"一种奇异的空中生物，由血肉般的云团与带电羽毛构成。 它每次攻击都会驱使地牢中微弱的气流；猎物周围越空旷， 遭受的狂风冲击就越猛烈。","Skysharks cut through the air with a thoughtless ease. Just a taste of blood gives them an enraged strength, and further morsels drive them into a frenzy.":"天鲨自在地划过天空。 哪怕只有一丝血也能激起它们愤怒的力量，要是有更多的鲜血会使其陷入疯狂。","A surprisingly ambulatory mushroom. It wafts its spores over prey to send them into a deep sleep, making it simple for the fungus to kill and devour them. It can take months for its mycelia to fully infiltrate and digest victims.":"一个令人惊奇的会走动的蘑菇。它能将孢子飘散到猎物身上， 使猎物进入深度睡眠，这样真菌就能轻易杀死并吞噬它们。 菌丝可能需要数月时间才能完全侵入并消化受害者。","An icky glob of slime that slithers along the ground. It can merge with other slime creatures to become dramatically more dangerous, and is especially likely to do so in confined spaces.":"一团黏稠的软泥在地上蠕动着。 它可以与其他史莱姆生物融合，会变得更加危险，尤其是在密闭空间中。","A hideous mass of body parts. Each varies in speed, strength, or resilience by the nature of whatever unfortunates were used to make it.":"一团骇人的残肢。其速度、力量或坚韧各不相同， 取决于制造它时用了哪些不幸者的躯体。","An infernal demon that manifests itself as a writhing cloud of smoke. Having considerable pyrokinetic powers, it can very effectively attack its enemies from afar.":"这个地狱恶魔化身为一团翻腾的烟雾。 它拥有强大的火焰异能，可以在远处给予它的敌人巨大打击。","A swift and sinuous vine brought alive by a dryad's magic. It can quickly bind and entangle the dryad's foes, dragging them back to the forest from which it surges.":"一条被树精魔法赋予生命的迅捷藤蔓。 它能迅速束缚、缠绕树精的敌人，将他们拖回自己涌出的森林。","Part of a swift and sinuous vine brought alive by a dryad's magic. It can quickly bind and entangle the dryad's foes, dragging them back to the forest from which it surges.":"一段被树精魔法赋予生命的迅捷藤蔓。 它能迅速束缚、缠绕树精的敌人，将他们拖回自己涌出的森林。","A belligerent testudine with an armoured carapace. Its neck is surprisingly extensible and can reach out and bite from afar.":"一只长着坚硬甲壳的凶猛乌龟。它的脖子有惊人的延展性，可以从远处伸过来咬。","A demon that manifests as a malignantly shifting shadow gliding through the air. It radiates an intense aura of negative force.":"这个恶魔看起来就像是一团恶意翻腾的阴影，在空气中滑过。 它散发着强烈的负能量力场。","A profoundly unnatural insect covered in vaguely metallic plates. Its stinger crackles with electricity, capable of delivering a powerful shock to unwary victims, and is capable of closing the distance with them at shockingly lethal speed.":"一个完全非自然的昆虫，身上像是覆盖着金属板。它的毒刺噼啪带着电， 能给那些不小心的受害者强大的电击，它也能以惊人的致命速度拉近与他们的距离。","A malevolent rift in reality, dissolving all terrain it passes by into swirling vortices.":"现实空间中的一个狂暴的裂口，能把它经过的所有地形溶解成旋涡。","A crazily shifting twist in the fabric of reality.":"一个在现实空间中的螺旋，疯狂地移动、变化着。","A hideous glowing apparition.":"一个可怕的发着光的幽灵。","A spirit drawn from a weapon — it never strikes on its own. Damage done to it will be partially mirrored onto the caster.":"一个从武器中汲取的灵魂——它永远不会自行攻击。 对它造成的损伤会部分反馈到施法者身上。","A magical construct forged around a spark of its creator's own arcane power, allowing it to wield some of their destructive magics directly.":"一个魔法造物，铸入了咒法师的魔法， 并与外层位面召唤而来原始元素面的智慧相融合。 它那被锻造的魔法赋予它使用其创造者的一些破坏性法术的能力。","A small humanoid, resembling a human or elf except for the size. It moves at a great speed, and loves playing dirty tricks on people.":"一个小型人形生物，除了体形小了点之外和人类或精灵没什么区别。 他能快速移动，喜欢对人们搞点恶作剧。","A magically adept spriggan blessed with the secrets of the winds.":"一个擅长魔法的小精灵，蒙受风之奥秘的祝福。","A relatively mighty spriggan that plunges recklessly into combat.":"这个相对强壮的小精灵会不顾一切地冲入战斗。","An elite, well-equipped spriggan warrior, renowned for its unbelievable agility and its prowess with advanced weaponry.":"一名装备精良的小精灵精锐战士，以不可思议的敏捷和高超武艺闻名。","A spriggan whose connection with the birds and the beasts is exceptionally strong. If it dies, its sacrifice will heal and temporarily strengthen nearby animals.":"这个小精灵和飞鸟、野兽有着特别密切的联系。 如果它死了，它的牺牲会治愈并暂时增强附近的动物。","A spriggan that has tamed a hornet as its mount, and is tasked with protecting the spriggan fens and cairns from intruders.":"一个以驯服的大黄蜂为坐骑的小精灵， 负责保护小精灵的沼泽与石冢不受入侵者侵扰。","A mass of stellar detritus that glows with the sickly putrescence of a dying star, forever shrieking soundlessly in a voice beyond mortal grasp. Its form undulates constantly, dividing spontaneously and then withdrawing when threatened. When divided, its deafening chorus of screams can overwhelm the minds of even the bravest warriors, leaving them stunned and helpless.":"一团星星的碎片，散发着垂死星星的病态腐化的光芒，永远无声地尖叫着， 发出凡人无法理解的声音。其形态常常在波动，自发地分裂，受到威胁时又缩回去。 当分裂时，它那震耳欲聋的齐声尖叫能压垮哪怕最勇敢的战士的理智， 使他们陷入眩晕、无力反抗。","A mass of lashing vines and tentacles growing out of the husk of a dead star. Space itself runs through the xylem and phloem of its branches, which appear to be in many places at once.":"从死星的外壳中长出的一团藤蔓和触须。 空间贯通着它的分支的木质部和韧皮部，它们似乎同时存在于许多地方。","The writhing appendage of a tentacled starspawn, capable of grasping nearly any prey and dragging it back to be devoured. Any damage dealt to it hurts the whole creature.":"触手星之后裔扭动的附肢，几乎能捕获任何猎物，并把它们拖回去吞食。 对它造成的任何伤害都能伤及整体。","A sinuous length of an extended starspawn tentacle. Any damage dealt to it hurts the whole creature.":"触手星之后裔伸出的一段蜿蜒触手。对它造成的任何伤害都能伤及整体。","A piece of sculpted granite with glowing red eyes. Although it is rooted to its base, it can still move parts of itself.":"一块雕刻了的花岗岩，有着发光的红眼。 尽管它固定于底座，但身体的一部分仍能活动。","A relatively small grey dragon, with a resilient-looking scaly hide and steam pouring from its mouth.":"一条相对较小的灰色龙，身上的鳞皮看起来很坚韧，口中不时喷出蒸汽。","A large worm covered with hard, spiky metal plates. Despite the apparent heaviness of its outer armour, it is rather fast.":"一条覆有硬而多刺的金属板的大蠕虫。尽管它的外甲看起来很重，但速度相当快。","A mortal who made an unholy pact in life, now chained to tend the fires of hell in undeath as payment.":"一个凡人在生前订立了邪恶的契约，现在被束缚在亡灵身上照料地狱之火作为报酬。","A gigantic humanoid with grey skin almost as hard as rock. It carries several boulders, and is perfectly capable of flinging them a great distance.":"一个巨大的人形生物，他的灰色表皮几乎和石头一样硬。 他携带着好几块巨石，而且完全有能力将巨石抛出很远。","A powerful dragon with a hide of thick matte scales almost like blue rubber, and enormous scaly wings crackling with sparks.":"一条非常强大的龙，它身上厚厚的、粗糙的鳞甲简直像是蓝色橡胶， 巨大无比的鳞翼，上面不时迸出电火花。","A strange mechanical contraption, all hisses and pops. Shadows seem to dance across its reflective surface.":"一个奇怪的机械装置，发出嘶嘶和砰砰声。 阴影似乎在其反射面上跃动着。","A demonic figure shining with the heat and fury of a fallen star.":"一个恶魔，身体散发着陨星的炽热和愤怒。","A moth of transcendent beauty, coated in pyrophoric scales. Tiny cinders dance and twirl in its wake and whenever it beats its wings, they ignite in such spectacular displays of incandescence that one could almost forget how far away the sun is from this place.":"一只美丽绝伦的飞蛾，身上覆盖着易自燃的鳞片。 微小的余烬在它的尾迹上飞舞盘旋，每当它扇动翅膀， 余烬就会燃烧出炽热的壮观景象，以至于人们几乎会忘记太阳离这里有多远。","A slimy dragon, its gnarly hide covered in swamp muck. Noxious gases dribble from its snout.":"这条大型龙的身上满是黏液，它粗糙的表皮包裹在沼泽的污泥之中。 它的鼻孔不时喷出毒气。","A small and slimy dragon, covered in swamp muck and giving off a terrible stench.":"这条小龙浑身上下都是黏液和污泥，散发着可怕的恶臭。","A large slimy worm, adept at traversing swamps and marshes.":"一条满身黏液的蠕虫，擅长在沼泽的污泥中穿行。","A small but greatly-feared spider. Its touch alone causes victims to break into a frenzied dance.":"一只体形小却令人无比恐惧的蜘蛛。只需触碰，它就能让受害者陷入狂舞。","Before even the oldest of ancient liches mastered life and death, a group of titans attempted to pull themselves free of mortality through brute strength. They almost succeeded before rot dragged them to Ereshkigal. A glimmer of their former beauty remains, alluring despite the stench.":"在最早的远古巫妖掌握生死之前，就曾有一群泰坦试图通过蛮力摆脱死亡。 在腐烂将他们拖到埃列什基伽勒那里之前，他们几乎要成功了。 尽管留有恶臭，但仍保留着他们昔日美丽的微光。","A humanoid figure with the head and talons of a bird. Its ferociously combative nature belies its fragile appearance.":"一个人形生物，却长着鸟的头和爪子。他看似脆弱，其实十分好战。","A tengu with a talent for the destructive magical arts.":"一个擅长破坏性魔法的天狗。","An elite, ferocious tengu highly skilled with both steel and spells.":"一个凶恶的天狗精英，擅长兵器和法术。","A particularly bloodthirsty tengu who has opted to hone its skill in airborne fighting and weaponry instead of spellcasting.":"一个极其嗜血的天狗，他选择磨炼自己的空中格斗和武器技能，而非施法。","The mighty tentacle of a kraken. Any damage dealt to it hurts the whole creature.":"这条健壮的触手是某个海怪的身体的一部分。对它造成的任何伤害都能伤及整体。","A part of the mighty tentacle of a kraken. Any damage dealt to it hurts the whole creature.":"某个海怪的健壮的触手的一部分。对它造成的任何伤害都能伤及整体。","A writhing mass of tentacles, all covered in putrid mucus.":"一团翻腾蠕动的触手，上面粘满了腐臭的黏液。","A lumbering maw shrouded in a mass of sinuous tentacles. On spotting prey, its tentacles lunge outward, dragging victims directly to its waiting gullet.":"一个迟缓的胃被大量弯曲的触手包裹着。 一旦发现猎物，它的触手就会向外冲去，把受害者直接拖入等待着的食管之中。","A seething mass of yellow flesh. It thrashes erratically, staggering foes beneath the weight of its impacts.":"一团翻滚的黄色肉团。它不规律地扭动着，在其冲撞的力量下，敌人摇摇晃晃。","A huge, bolt-hurling, lightning-limned humanoid. It is unusually large and powerful, even among giants.":"一个巨大的人形生物，能投掷闪电束，身形被闪电所勾勒。 即使在巨人之中，他也是最大、最强的。","A predatory marsh plant, possessed of motility and a rudimentary intelligence. It ensnares its prey with protrusions of spiny brambles and then skewers the trapped creatures with its razor-sharp thorns.":"一种食肉的沼泽植物，有行动力和一定智力。 它会伸出荆棘捕捉猎物，然后用锋利的刺刺穿被困的生物。","A short-lived species of fungus typically found on or around decaying organic matter.":"这个短命的真菌通常只在腐烂的有机物附近出现。","A huge animated statue made entirely from toenail clippings. Some people just have too much time on their hands.":"这尊巨大的会动的雕像完全由剪下的脚趾甲制成。某些人真是闲得没事做啊。","A malign devil covered in all manner of claws, spines, and cruel hooks. It is able to inflict torturous agony on those foolish enough to gaze upon it.":"这个凶悍的恶魔身上全是爪子、骨刺、倒钩之类的东西。 它能让蠢到敢于直视它的人体验极端的痛苦。","A ponderous gastropod with a rock-hard shell. It is said to be in some way connected with the god Cheibriados; its very presence slows the movements of unwary adventurers, leaving them easy prey for its terrifying, ever-gnashing radulae.":"一个缓慢的腹足类动物，有着石头般坚硬的外壳。 据说它与切布理亚多有某种联系。它仅凭存在就能拖慢毫无戒心的冒险者， 让他们轻易落入那骇人而不停研磨的齿舌。","A mannequin used for battle practice.":"一个用于战斗训练的人偶。","A huge and physically powerful humanoid creature. Short on intelligence but long on brawn, its thick knobbly hide heals rapidly from most wounds.":"一个体形巨大、身体强壮的人形生物。 他头脑简单，但肌肉发达，而且他那结节状的厚皮能迅速愈合大多数伤口。","A whirling vortex of frost.":"一个冰霜旋涡。","A huge ogre with two heads on top of its bloated body. It is capable of holding a weapon in each giant hand.":"一个肥胖的食人魔，顶上长着两个脑袋。他的两只巨手能各持一件武器。","An exceptionally aggressive blood-sucking annelid that thrives in swamps and marshlands.":"一个极具攻击性的吸血的环节动物，它们在沼泽和湿地中兴旺地繁衍。","A horrific fallen divinity, possessing jaws of gnashing stone and a necklace of starry organs. It spreads disease and despair, and patiently awaits the end of days when it will devour the sun.":"一个令人畏惧的堕落神灵，长着咬合不休的石颌，项链上串着星光闪烁的器官。 它散布着疾病和绝望，耐心等待着末日降临，那时它会吞噬太阳。","A chattering and shrieking minor demon. They delight in sneaking past and backstabbing their prey.":"这个低阶恶魔总爱发出啁啾声和尖啸声。他们喜欢溜过猎物，然后对其发动背刺。","An ugly thing. According to legend, it is the otherworldly spawn of a wizard's breeding experiment. Yuck.":"这是一只丑陋之物。传说，这种恐怖的变异生物是某个巫师的杂交实验的超自然产物。 呕。","A creature rarely seen by anyone; those few who have seen one would rather they hadn't. It moves erratically.":"这个生物很少被看到，那些看到过的少数人宁愿自己没看到过。它的运动没有规律。","A funerary stone figurine kept in tombs to serve the deceased as they pass through the afterlife. It is inscribed with spells to protect the interred for eternity.":"一尊置于墓中的陪葬石像，在死者穿行来世时侍奉他们。 像上刻有法术，永远保护墓中之人。","A human cursed with vampirism, drifting in a state between life and undeath, perpetually hungry for the blood of the living.":"一个受到吸血鬼化诅咒的人类，游走在生与死之间，永远渴望着生者的鲜血。","A large black bat with vicious fangs that feeds on blood. It is the preferred form for vampires in disguise.":"一只大型黑蝙蝠，长着獠牙，以血为食。吸血鬼喜欢伪装成这个形态。","A powerful vampire noble who complements its combat prowess with dark magic.":"一个强大的吸血鬼贵族，用黑魔法完善他的战斗技能。","A sorcerer who, by accident or design, has been afflicted with the curse of the vampire. Regardless, through undeath, it has finally mastered the art of dark magic.":"不管是自愿的还是被迫的，这名术士是受到了吸血的诅咒。 但不管怎么说，在不死之力的帮助下，这名法师终于完全掌握了黑暗魔法的奥秘。","A mosquito that has fed upon tainted blood and been transformed into a revolting and pestilent undead insect, seeking to drain its victims to the last drop.":"这只蚊子以受污染的血液为食，变成了一只令人作呕、散播疾病的亡灵昆虫。 它的目的是将它的猎物吸干——一滴不留。","A heavily armed and armoured guardian of the Vaults.":"宝库的卫兵之一，武器、盔甲装备精良。","A vigilant scout, quick to alert its fellows to the presence of intruders. It marks such intruders with powerful magic, making them unable to hide from pursuit no matter where they flee.":"一个警惕的侦察员，能迅速提醒同伴出现了入侵者。 他会用强大的魔法标记入侵者，使其无论逃到哪里都无法躲过追捕。","A veteran commander, able to seal nearby doorways and staircases to prevent intruders from either trespassing further or escaping alive.":"一名经验丰富的指挥官，能封锁附近的门廊和楼梯， 以免入侵者继续侵入或逃之夭夭。","A very ugly thing. According to legend, it is the otherworldly spawn of a wizard's breeding experiment. Double yuck!":"这是一只极丑之物。 传说，这种恐怖的变异生物是某个巫师的杂交实验的超自然产物。呕，呕！","A bizarre symbiotic creature, made up of a carnivorous vine magically combined with a humanoid.":"一个奇异的共生生物，由食肉藤蔓与人形生物神奇地结合而成。","The viscous detritus of a thousand failed spells, surging forward with unnerving speed. Its very substance is a hole in the fabric of magic; enchantments find no purchase there and even momentary contact with it can leave one's spells greatly diminished.":"上千次失败法术留下的黏稠残渣，以令人不安的速度向前涌动。 它本身就是魔法织构上的空洞：附魔无法在其上立足，哪怕只是短暂接触， 也会让人的法术大幅衰弱。","A spellbook that has gone too long without being read. It overflows with magic, forming thick armour from its binding, legs from its pages, and periodically erupting in flurries of free-floating, self-casting spells.":"一本很久没有读过的魔法书。它充满魔力，它的封皮形成了厚厚的盔甲， 书页长出了腿，并周期性地爆出自由飘浮的自行施放的法术。","It is coated with impossibly ancient dust.":"它被一层不可思议的古老灰尘覆盖着。","A spellbook that has gone too long without being read. It overflows with magic, forming thick armour from its binding, legs from its pages, and periodically erupting in flurries of free-floating, self-casting spells. It is coated with impossibly ancient dust.":"一本很久没有读过的魔法书。它充满魔力，它的封皮形成了厚厚的盔甲， 书页长出了腿，并周期性地爆出自由飘浮的自行施放的法术。 它被一层不可思议的古老灰尘覆盖着。","It is encrusted with long, sharp, deadly-looking crystals.":"它镶嵌着长而锋利的致命水晶。","A spellbook that has gone too long without being read. It overflows with magic, forming thick armour from its binding, legs from its pages, and periodically erupting in flurries of free-floating, self-casting spells. It is encrusted with long, sharp, deadly-looking crystals.":"一本很久没有读过的魔法书。它充满魔力，它的封皮形成了厚厚的盔甲， 书页长出了腿，并周期性地爆出自由飘浮的自行施放的法术。 它镶嵌着长而锋利的致命水晶。","Its cover bears the icon of a long-forgotten god, still fully possessed of wrath.":"它的封面上有一个被遗忘已久的神像，仍然充满着愤怒。","A spellbook that has gone too long without being read. It overflows with magic, forming thick armour from its binding, legs from its pages, and periodically erupting in flurries of free-floating, self-casting spells. Its cover bears the icon of a long-forgotten god, still fully possessed of wrath.":"一本很久没有读过的魔法书。它充满魔力，它的封皮形成了厚厚的盔甲， 书页长出了腿，并周期性地爆出自由飘浮的自行施放的法术。 它的封面上有一个被遗忘已久的神像，仍然充满着愤怒。","It glistens with a thick layer of unmelting ice.":"它那层未融化的坚冰在闪烁着。","A spellbook that has gone too long without being read. It overflows with magic, forming thick armour from its binding, legs from its pages, and periodically erupting in flurries of free-floating, self-casting spells. It glistens with a thick layer of unmelting ice.":"一本很久没有读过的魔法书。它充满魔力，它的封皮形成了厚厚的盔甲， 书页长出了腿，并周期性地爆出自由飘浮的自行施放的法术。 它那层未融化的坚冰在闪烁着。","A large, fleshy mushroom that wanders slowly around the dungeon. It is both innately curious and incredibly shy, pursuing the objects of its curiosity only when out of sight. Noxious spores drift around its cap.":"一个在地牢中慢慢游走的大型肉质蘑菇。它有与生俱来的好奇心，而且又非常害羞， 只有在没有人看着的时候才会去追寻引起它好奇心的东西。 它的菌帽旁有毒性孢子在飘动。","A particularly evil-looking wolf, usually found in the company of orcs.":"一条面目格外狰狞的狼，通常和兽人一起出现。","A rare type of gargoyle, constructed from a solid steel statue and imbued with vicious strength, speed, and weaponised breath.":"一个罕见的石像鬼，由坚固的钢铁雕像幻化而成， 浸入了邪恶的力量、速度和能造成伤害的吐息。","A spirit drawn from the elemental plane of water. It exists on this world as part of a body of water and can engulf other beings in its form, depriving them of breath and voice.":"一个来自水元素位面的灵体。它作为水体的一部分存在于这个世界上， 在这个形态下可以吞没其他生物，让他们无法呼吸、发出声音。","A largish venomous brown snake. It usually lives near water, and is an able swimmer.":"一条体形较大的棕色毒蛇。它通常生活在水边，擅长游泳。","A capricious nature spirit, deeply bonded with the waters in which it lives. Wherever they flow, so may it, and ponds and rivers surge and leap at its whim.":"一个反复无常自然之灵，与她所栖息的水域紧密相连。 它们流到哪里，她就会到哪里，池塘和河流也会因为她的兴起而汹涌澎湃。","An undead skull kept aloft by unholy clouds of collective misery, which slowly drift out in its wake. It mourns without end for the living, the dead, and its own former life all alike.":"一个被聚集的邪恶愁云托起的亡灵头骨，云层在它的身后慢慢飘出。 它为生者、死者和它自己的前世无休止地哀悼着。","A gaunt spirit of frozen hunger, so ravenous it will consume friend and foe alike. According to legend, if one cuts off its legs, it will feast upon its own marrow. It stalks those lost wandering in the cold and hunts with the force of blizzards.":"一个冰冷饥饿、枯槁的灵魂，如此贪婪，以至于无论敌人还是朋友，它都要吞噬。 传说，如果砍掉它的腿，它甚至会朵颐自己的骨髓。 在寒冷的地方它会跟踪那些徘徊着的迷路的人，并会用暴风雪的力量进行猎杀。","A muscular white-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有白色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A small and mischievous minor demon covered in frost.":"一个小而调皮的低阶恶魔，浑身都是冰霜。","An ancient warrior, kept in a state of perpetual undeath by its desire to die with honour in battle.":"一位古代战士，怀着在战斗中光荣地死去的执念而永远保持着不死状态。","A green-glowing gaseous entity, flickering and pulsing irregularly as it hovers through the air. Travelers have been known to confuse these for distant lanterns - a mistake rarely made twice.":"一个绿色发光的气态实体，悬在空中，时时不规则地闪烁、悸动。 众所周知，旅行者会将这些与远方的灯笼相混淆——这种错误很少有机会犯两次。","A small but powerful dragon, particularly adept amongst its kin at manipulating the currents of air that surround it. It can exhale powerful blasts of wind.":"一条小而强大的龙，在它的同类中它尤为善于操控周围的气流。它能呼出强烈的风。","A strong wild canine, with sharp teeth and a healthy appetite.":"一条强壮的犬科动物，拥有尖利的牙齿和旺盛的食欲。","A hairy fast-moving hunting spider with vicious mandibles, the size of a wolf. It roams the dungeon in search of prey, which it kills with its deadly venom.":"一个多毛的、行动快速的猎蛛，有凶恶的下颚，体形像狼那么大。 它在地牢中漫游以寻找猎物，并用致命的毒液将其杀死。","A cloud of thick fog, with faint, feeble claws constantly reaching out and then fading back into the fog. When threatened, it calls forth creatures banished to the void between realities, using them to defend itself.":"一团浓雾，虚弱无力的爪子不停地伸出来，然后又消退在雾中。 当受到威胁时，它会召唤被放逐到现实和虚空之间的生物，利用它们来保护自己。","A cloud of black mist surrounding an insubstantial skeletal form. Its eyes burn bright with unholy malevolence and hunger for life essence, on which it feeds.":"一团黑色的薄雾裹挟着一具虚无的骷髅。 它的眼中闪烁着不洁的恶意，以及对吞食生命精华的渴望。","A conflux of unearthly light and energy, awash in unnatural colours and strange forms no normal being was meant to perceive. It fills all those in its presence with the disorder of the Abyss.":"一个诡异的光线和能量的聚合物，充斥着不自然的色彩和奇怪的形态， 这些景象本不该被任何正常生物目睹。它让所有在场者染上深渊的紊乱。","A dragon-like creature with a long, sharply pointed tail. Although smaller and less formidable than true dragons, it is nonetheless a foe to be reckoned with.":"这条类龙生物长有一条长长的尖尾巴。虽然双足飞龙体形比真龙小， 而且也没有真龙那么可怕，但它仍然是一个不容小觑的敌人。","A common dungeon yak, covered in shaggy yak hair and bearing a nasty pair of yak horns.":"一头普通的地牢牦牛，身上长满蓬松的牛毛，头上长着一对尖锐的牛角。","A hybrid with the torso of a robust human atop the body of a yak. It excels in ranged combat, and is also a formidable foe in close quarters.":"一个混种生物，在牦牛的身体上有着人的躯干。 他不但擅长远程战斗，近战方面也是个强大的敌人。","An exceptionally strong and brutish yaktaur, able to order its weaker brethren around to do its bidding.":"一个异常强壮、野蛮的牦牛人马，能够让他较弱的兄弟服从他的命令。","A muscular yellow-scaled humanoid with a reptilian tail and small wings.":"一个肌肉发达、长有黄色鳞片的人形生物，有着爬行动物的尾巴和小翅膀。","A winged demon covered in shiny metallic scales. It has a legion of minor demons under its command.":"一个有翼的恶魔，身上覆有闪耀的金属鳞片。它指挥着一个低阶恶魔军团。","A corpse raised to undeath by necromancy.":"一具被死灵法术复活的尸体。","The remains of a monster that existed in an older version, but has since been removed.":"旧版中怪物的残骸，但已经被移除。","A hostile monster whose presence has been detected.":"一个敌对怪物，其存在已被察觉。","A trivially weak monster whose presence has been revealed by the power of Ashenzari.":"一个微不足道的弱小怪物，其存在已被艾申扎利的力量所揭示。","A weak monster whose presence has been revealed by the power of Ashenzari.":"一个弱小怪物，其存在已被艾申扎利的力量所揭示。","A somewhat dangerous monster whose presence has been revealed by the power of Ashenzari.":"一个有一定危险性的怪物，其存在已被艾申扎利的力量所揭示。","A very dangerous monster whose presence has been revealed by the power of Ashenzari.":"一个非常危险的怪物，其存在已被艾申扎利的力量所揭示。","A friendly monster whose presence has been {{ if you.god() == \"Ashenzari\" then return \"revealed by the power of Ashenzari\" else return \"detected\" end }}.":"一个友好的怪物，其存在已被{{ if you.god() == \"Ashenzari\" then return \"艾申扎利的力量所揭示\" else return \"察觉\" end }}。","A powerful warrior-mage who instructs aspiring students in physical, magical, and anti-magical combat.":"一位强大的战斗法师，指导有抱负的学生进行物理、魔法和反魔法战斗。","A mighty spellcaster wreathed in arcane energies, muttering profane incantations.":"一位强大的施法者，全身被包裹在奥术能量中，呢喃着肮脏、亵渎的咒语。","A statue made of a fine glassy orange crystal. It depicts a mystic known as Wucad Mu, who mastered the matters of the mind, and is imbued with Wucad Mu's powers of mental combat.":"一个由精细的橙色玻璃水晶制成的雕像。 它所刻画的是一位掌握了心灵奥秘的的秘术师——乌卡德·穆， 而这尊雕像也充满了乌卡德·穆的精神战斗能力。","A bizarre breed of intelligent troll, glowing with mysterious power from beyond this world which shields it from damage except at close range.":"一种奇异而聪慧的巨魔，闪耀着来自异界的神秘力量； 这股力量能抵挡伤害，只有近距离攻击可以穿透。","<zot statue>":"<zot statue>","A delicate statue of a tengu gliding through the air. It looks quite insubstantial.":"一尊精美的雕像，雕的是一个在空中滑翔的天狗。它看起来虚无缥缈。","An unfathomably expensive skeleton. It has countless sigils engraved into its bones, and pulses with a ghostly presence.":"一具贵得不可理喻的骷髅。它的骨头上刻有无数的印记，脉动着幽灵的存在。","A statue of a beautiful elven archer, sculpted in finest marble. It holds a bow aloft, and appears to be magically animated, letting it use the bow to riddle intruders with arrows.":"一个美丽的精灵射手雕像，由最好的大理石雕刻而成。 它高举着弓，似乎有了魔力，能用弓箭把入侵者射得满是窟窿。","An undead figure preserved by the brackish waters of a bog. It has begun to decay heavily, and looks fragile.":"这个亡灵生物的身体被沼泽的咸水保存起来。 它已经腐朽得很严重了，看起来很脆弱。","A wild-eyed wizard whose tongue has been cut out, frantically mumbling and waving its arms but unable to cast a single spell.":"一个怒目而视的巫师。 他的舌头已被割下，疯狂地咕哝着，挥舞着手臂，但就是连一个法术也施展不了。","A statue that has been imbued with flame, allowing it to make use of simple fire-based conjurations.":"看起来，这尊雕像被灌入了火焰魔法，赋予它使用一些简单的火焰咒法的能力。","A terrifying creation that appears to have been constructed from the body parts of every monstrous creature imaginable, with writhing tentacles sprouting from its form.":"一个可怕的造物，由各种所能想像到的各种怪物的身体部件拼凑而成， 扭曲的触手从它的身体中蠕动出来。","A statue able to harness the mightiest of pure conjurations ever devised by Iskenderun.":"由伊斯肯德伦设计的一个能够驾驭有史以来最强大的纯魔法的雕像。","A poor creature that looks hideously deformed.":"这个可怜的生物外表严重畸形。","A demonic mockery of a plant, covered with mysterious appendages and writhing tentacles. It appears to be harmless.":"一个恶魔般恶劣的植物，满是神秘的附肢和蠕动的触手。它似乎是无害的。","A terrible creature with demonic ancestry. Its presence is horrifying, but supernaturally compelling.":"有着恶魔血统的可怕生物。它的存在是令人畏惧的、超出寻常、难以抗拒的。","A dwarf who seems to be working as an ale quality tester, and is enjoying the job a little too much.":"这个矮人的工作是检验酒的质量。他似乎有点太享受他的工作了。","A plain statue of a dwarf wielding a pickaxe. It looks incredibly heavy.":"一尊普通的矮人雕像，雕像的手中拿着一把鹤嘴锄。它看起来重得要命。","An ornately worked statue of an orc holding a torch aloft, hewn from black basalt. The air around it shimmers.":"一尊华丽的兽人雕像，手中高举着一个用黑色的玄武岩雕成的火炬。 它周围的空气似乎微微发光。","An animated mound of misshapen flesh, sculpted over an iron skeleton.":"一团会动的畸形肉堆，在铁骨架上塑成。","A statue of a mage, with frost constantly forming across its surface.":"一尊法师雕像，其表面不断生成冰霜。","A bat with a spectral visage.":"一只有着幽灵般面孔的蝙蝠。","An enormous, bloated bat.":"一只膨胀的巨型蝙蝠。","A mighty spirit drawn from the elemental plane of air, surrounded by a deadly vortex of frost.":"一个来自气元素位面的强大灵体，周围环绕着致命的冰霜旋涡。","An undead creature in the shape of a bat, made of ice.":"一个蝙蝠形的亡灵生物，它的身体是由冰构成的。","A kobold that has been enchanted to explode in a blaze of fire.":"这个狗头人被附了魔法，在火焰中会爆炸。","A devoted follower of Lugonu, driven mad by years of living in the Abyss.":"一个卢格努的忠实追随者，被多年的深渊里的生活逼疯了。","A young merfolk that looks deeply ill, but is still capable of bespelling its audience.":"一个年轻的人鱼，看起来病得很重，却仍能用魔法迷惑听众。","A demented wizard commanding the primal forces of the universe.":"一个控制着宇宙原始力量的疯狂巫师。","A huge black bat.":"一个巨大的黑色蝙蝠。","A bat that, despite its name, is not any smaller than a megabat.":"虽然这只蝙蝠的名字里没有“大”字，但其实它并不比大蝙蝠要小。","A follower of Okawaru, granted the honour of spectating a duel to the death.":"一个奥卡瓦鲁的追随者，被赐予观看生死决斗的殊荣。","<oklob plant annihilator>":"<oklob plant annihilator>","An immature oklob plant that seems to be mumbling some orisons... er, what?!?":"这株幼年酸箭草似乎在咕哝某种咒语……呃，啥鬼？！","A metal golem crackling with magical energies. It must have been created by a truly devious wizard, or possibly someone who misheard what monsters could be found in the Realm of Zot.":"一尊金属魔像，身上的魔法能量噼啪作响。它一定是由一位非常狡猾的巫师创造的， 或者是有人听错了能在佐特领域发现哪些怪物。","A strange, glowing bat that flutters through more dimensions than the average bat.":"这只奇怪的发光蝙蝠似乎同时在多个次元中飞行着。","An otherworldly spider that can move short and medium distances by briefly shifting between the planes of reality, in order to better ensnare its prey.":"这只奇异的蜘蛛通过在多个现实位面中相位来快速进行中短距离移动， 以便更轻松地捕住它的猎物。","An immaculately sculpted porphyry statue of an archer poised to release a bolt, with a full quiver at the hip.":"一尊雕刻得很完美的斑岩雕像，其形象是一名正要放箭的弓箭手， 他的臀部有一个装满了的箭筒。","A bat that is well past its sell-by date.":"一个早已过了保质期的蝙蝠。","A young merfolk that looks quite sick, but still has the power to mesmerise its victims.":"一个年轻的人鱼，看起来病得不轻，却仍有迷惑受害者的力量。","A bat skeleton without the decency to lie unmoving like dead bats are supposed to.":"这只骷髅蝙蝠就是不肯像正常的死蝙蝠一样趴在地上一动不动。","A smooth statue of a beautiful merfolk bathing in a fountain, sculpted from creamy, faintly pinkish travertine. It glistens softly in the light.":"一尊光滑的在泉中沐浴的鱼人雕像，由奶油色、略带浅粉色的钙华雕刻而成。 它在光线下中柔和地闪耀着。","An old and unnaturally ugly human, wearing robes stained with what appears to be swamp ooze, cauldron soot and brew ingredients.":"一个年老而异常丑陋的人，所穿的长袍上沾染着沼泽淤泥、大锅的烟灰和酿造原料。","A plant whose life has been drained away, but with its physical form still intact. It looks like it died many {{ if you.branch() == \"Crypt\" or you.branch() == \"Tomb\" or you.branch() == \"Zot\" then return \"centuries\"; else return \"years\"; end }} ago.":"这株植物的生命力已被吸干，然而它的躯壳仍然完好。 看上去它已经死了好几{{ if you.branch() == \"Crypt\" or you.branch() == \"Tomb\" or you.branch() == \"Zot\" then return \"世纪\"; else return \"年\"; end}}了。","A giant annelid, glistening with slime, with unusually large teeth.":"一条巨大的环节动物，身上的黏液闪烁着，牙齿大得出奇。","A divine agent of Zin. It is a towering winged figure with an aura of brilliant white light. Its face is marked by a scowl, as if its zeal against any real or perceived vice overshadows its goodness.":"一个辛的圣使。其身上有高耸的翅膀，身体有着璀璨的白光。 他的脸上有种怒容，似乎他那对抗现实和察觉到的恶的热忱盖过了他的善意。","A profoundly disturbing statue, hewn from a single piece of dark gabbro scintillating with tiny crystals. It is impossible to tell whether it is intended to represent some creature or personage, or to be completely abstract.":"一尊令人深感不安的雕像，只用一块黑色辉长岩雕刻而成， 上面的小水晶块还闪着微光。很难说它是在表现某种动物或人物，还是完全抽象。","<anaconda>":"<anaconda>","<great orb of eyes>":"<great orb of eyes>","<naga warrior>":"<naga warrior>","<acid blob>":"<acid blob>","<vault guard>":"<vault guard>","One of the legions of abominations created by the sculptors of flesh. Its bloated hulk pulsates and throbs constantly with accursed fires. It looks as if it could explode into a torrent of viscera at any moment.":"由肉雕师制造的憎恶军团中的一员。它那肿胀的身躯随着诅咒的火焰不停悸动着。 它似乎随时都有可能爆成内脏的洪流。","One of the legions of abominations created by the sculptors of flesh. Its form is large and muscular. It moves swiftly and with impetuous fury, the sole thought within its being to rend you apart with great fervour. As it rages, it creates a cacophonous din.":"由肉雕师制造的憎恶军团中的一员。它的体形很壮硕。 它移动迅速而狂暴，唯一的念头就是激情地把你撕碎。 当它狂怒时，会发出刺耳的噪音。","One of the legions of abominations created by the sculptors of flesh. Each of its eight necks is distended and elongated, connected to a colossal body crumpled and dripping with ichor. Its many heads spew blood while writhing and convulsing in agony, as it brings torment to itself and anything else that beholds its foul visage.":"由肉雕师制造的憎恶军团中的一员。 它的八个脖子都被伸展拉长，与一个起皱的、滴着腐液的巨大身体相连。 它的许多头痛苦地翻滚、痉挛着，并吐出鲜血， 它给它自己和任何见到它那污秽容貌的人带来了痛苦。","One of the legions of abominations created by the sculptors of flesh. Ablaze with demonic frenzy, it gores and tramples with ferocity unmatched. Its skin is flayed, exposing the glistening tendons and sinew underneath, and the teeth inside its cavernous maw are stained with blood.":"由肉雕师制造的憎恶军团中的一员。 在恶魔的迷乱中狂暴着，无比残酷地杀戮、践踏着。它的皮肤被剥了， 露出发光的筋肉和下方的肌腱，它的硕大的胃里的牙齿沾满了血污。","An artisan of unlife, the sculptor appears as a grim skeletal form. It has six long arms ending in mangled hands with broken fingers, upon which it crawls like a spider. Its skull is abnormally large and full of holes. Its bones are reddened and fractured, inscribed with the unholy spells it weaves to assemble its puppets.":"这位雕工是亡灵的工匠，外形是阴冷的骨架。 它有六支长臂，末端是残缺的手掌和断了的手指，利用这些它像一只蜘蛛一样爬行。 它的头骨异常的大而且布满了洞。 它的骨头发红并断裂，上面刻有它用来装配傀儡的邪恶咒语。","The destroyers begin to descend upon you. They come in numbers and with wrath, maws gaping like abaddon, bottomless and abyssal. They bring your doom and will feast on your remains.":"毁灭者开始向你袭来。他们带着怒气成群降临， 胃裂开得像是像地狱、无止境得像是深渊。 他们会给你带来厄运，并在你的遗骸上饕餮。","The accursed are the ones who came before. They have come to ensure you share their fate.":"被诅咒者是先前亡故的人。他们想让你也陷入他们的命运。","A colossal mass of bones and skulls, a walking tomb. You hear shrieks and screams as it approaches, shattering off bones with each crushing step, reassembling itself in eternal unrest.":"大堆骨头和头骨，它简直是个行走的坟墓。当它接近时，你会听到尖叫和呼啸， 每个步伐都是毁灭性的，骨头在碎裂，同时又无休止地进行重组。","An affront to existence, a void in which there is only torment and damnation. Its unearthly form is torn and twisted, black and hollow. It is bereft of rational thought, knowing only hatred and the desire to desecrate your soul.":"一个对存在冒犯的虚无，徒留折磨和诅咒。它那怪异的形态被撕裂扭曲，漆黑空洞。 它失去了理智，只怀有仇恨和亵渎你灵魂的欲望。","A vast serpentine form with raw and diseased skin, seeping bile and pus, spouting venom and blight.":"一个巨大的蛇形生物，皮肤粗糙、病态，渗着胆汁和脓液，喷着毒液和枯萎病。","You see the unseen, you stare and they stare back. They whisper and laugh, they grin and cry, they leer at you with contempt and gaze at you in adoration. They are the observers, they are the judge of your worth and will decide your end.":"你看着看不见的，你凝视着他们，他们也凝视着你。 他们低语着，笑着，他们又笑又哭，他们轻蔑地睨视着你，崇敬地凝望着你。 他们是观察者，他们是你的价值的仲裁，并决定着你的结局。","A spectre, struggling to leave the mortal world it is incarcerated in. It drains life and unlife from all those it comes into contact with.":"一个鬼魂，挣扎着离开囚禁它的尘世。它从接触过的身上吸取生命和非生命。","One of the greatest servants of the Meatlord. It is muscular, agile and full of malevolence.":"血肉领主最强大的随从之一。它强健敏捷，充满了怨恨。","An emaciated figure brimming with damnation and plague. Its appearance signifies the end of days.":"一个消瘦的身形，充满了诅咒和瘟疫。它的出现意味着世界末日。","His glaive is alight with the flames of hell.":"他的大刀燃烧着地狱的火焰。","Those who enter will not escape.":"进入的人无法再逃脱。","His shield is emblazoned with images of infernal flames.":"他的盾上饰有地狱火的图案。","You behold the embodiment of filth, corruption and depravity: the Meatlord. His foul body is bloated to the extreme, leaking viscous fluid and the stench of death. His head is that of a boar with bulging eyes and tusks split in two, his snout flares and oozes as he snorts and squeals at the sight of you, and his mouth is a toothless rift which drools pools of blood and vomits forth disgusting remains. His neck is stretched and lops forward, its skin sagging downward. His immense gut writhes and distorts as the larvae within await their repugnant release. His legs are unrecognisable masses of flesh, covered in protrusions and throbbing boils. Your mind reels at the sight of this hideous form, and your senses begin to shut down in an attempt to preserve your sanity as you choke on the oppressive stench.":"你看到了污秽、腐化和堕落的化身，血肉领主。 他那肮脏的身体肿到了极致，流着粘液，散发着死亡的恶臭。 他的头是野猪，长有凸出的眼睛和两个獠牙， 他的猪嘴抽动着，淌着液体，一见到你就会喷着鼻息、发出尖叫。 他的嘴是个没有牙的裂口，流着血，吐着令人作呕的残渣。 脖子向前伸展、耷拉着，皮肤下垂着。他的脖子向前伸展、耷拉着，皮肤下垂着。 当体内的幼虫要恶心地释出时，他的肠道会蠕动、扭曲。 他的腿是一团无法辨认的肉，被突起、跳动着的脓包覆盖着。 当你看到这个丑恶的形体时，思维开始崩溃，感官开始停止， 以试图在令人窒息的压迫性的恶臭中留有一丝理智。","You hear the echoes of planets behind the deafening roar of stars as it approaches. It is the jaws of the abyss. It brings forth crawling chaos from within. It is the last sight you will ever see.":"当你接近时，你会听到恒星那震耳欲聋的轰鸣声和随后的行星的回音。 它是深渊的入口。它带来了从内向外蔓延的混乱。这将是你看到的最后的景象。","Once a gangly and bedraggled vampire with a strange obsession with colour, Blorkula was offered succour by a missionary of Beogh and became a portly and vigorous orc with a strange obsession with colour instead.":"曾经是一个瘦长而邋遢的吸血鬼，对颜色有着奇怪的痴迷， 布洛库拉被一位贝奥格传教士所救助，变成了一个圆胖而精力充沛的兽人， 仍然对颜色有着奇怪的痴迷。","He wields magic tinged with every hue of the rainbow, and has mastered the art of dividing his own form among its many colours to avoid killing blows - though even he must rest a while before doing so a second time.":"他运用染上彩虹每种色调的魔法，并精通将自己的形态分散到众多颜色中 以避免致命一击的艺术——尽管即使是他也必须在再次使用前稍作休息。","Once a gangly and bedraggled vampire with a strange obsession with colour, Blorkula was offered succour by a missionary of Beogh and became a portly and vigorous orc with a strange obsession with colour instead. He wields magic tinged with every hue of the rainbow, and has mastered the art of dividing his own form among its many colours to avoid killing blows - though even he must rest a while before doing so a second time.":"曾经是一个瘦长而邋遢的吸血鬼，对颜色有着奇怪的痴迷， 布洛库拉被一位贝奥格传教士所救助，变成了一个圆胖而精力充沛的兽人， 仍然对颜色有着奇怪的痴迷。 他运用染上彩虹每种色调的魔法，并精通将自己的形态分散到众多颜色中 以避免致命一击的艺术——尽管即使是他也必须在再次使用前稍作休息。","As a young woman, Cassandra bound herself in service to Ashenzari and was blessed and cursed in equal measure - granted the ability to foresee disasters, but only those she was powerless to prevent.":"年轻时，卡珊德拉将自己献身于阿申扎里的服务，被同等程度地祝福与诅咒—— 被赋予了预见灾难的能力，但仅限于那些她无力阻止的灾难。","Eventually driven from her homeland as a harbinger of the very plagues she'd spent a lifetime warning against, she has come to the dungeon in her final days in hope of averting one last catastrophe.":"最终，作为她毕生警告的瘟疫的预兆者被驱逐出故乡， 她在最后的日子里来到地牢，希望阻止最后一场大灾变。","As a young woman, Cassandra bound herself in service to Ashenzari and was blessed and cursed in equal measure - granted the ability to foresee disasters, but only those she was powerless to prevent. Eventually driven from her homeland as a harbinger of the very plagues she'd spent a lifetime warning against, she has come to the dungeon in her final days in hope of averting one last catastrophe.":"年轻时，卡珊德拉将自己献身于阿申扎里的服务，被同等程度地祝福与诅咒—— 被赋予了预见灾难的能力，但仅限于那些她无力阻止的灾难。 最终，作为她毕生警告的瘟疫的预兆者被驱逐出故乡， 她在最后的日子里来到地牢，希望阻止最后一场大灾变。","A time-lost revenant, risen not from the death of a single individual but of many - its bones fused together from the young and the elderly and different species altogether. Whether they were all the victims of a single massacre or a thousand souls discarded over a thousand years is impossible to say now; history does not remember them.":"一个迷失于时光中的归来者，不是从一个人的死亡中升起，而是从许多人—— 其骨骼融合了年轻人和老人以及完全不同的物种。他们究竟是单场大屠杀的受害者， 还是千年间被遗弃的一千个灵魂，如今已无法判断；历史不记得他们。","But one thing is clear: they will fight to change that until every last memory they have left burns away.":"但有一件事是明确的：他们将为此而战，直到他们留下的每一份记忆燃烧殆尽。","A time-lost revenant, risen not from the death of a single individual but of many - its bones fused together from the young and the elderly and different species altogether. Whether they were all the victims of a single massacre or a thousand souls discarded over a thousand years is impossible to say now; history does not remember them. But one thing is clear: they will fight to change that until every last memory they have left burns away.":"一个迷失于时光中的归来者，不是从一个人的死亡中升起，而是从许多人—— 其骨骼融合了年轻人和老人以及完全不同的物种。他们究竟是单场大屠杀的受害者， 还是千年间被遗弃的一千个灵魂，如今已无法判断；历史不记得他们。 但有一件事是明确的：他们将为此而战，直到他们留下的每一份记忆燃烧殆尽。","A former beekeeper's apprentice with an ambitious dream: to modernise the whole world's beekeeping industry with the smooth certainty of disease-proof metal. His methods may be questionable and his goals dubious, but his prototype's stinger still looks awfully sharp...":"一个前养蜂人学徒，怀有雄心勃勃的梦想：用防病金属的光滑确定性来现代化 全世界的养蜂业。他的方法可能有疑问，目标可能可疑， 但他原型机的螫针看起来仍然相当锋利……","A cantankerous dwarf wearing a stupid-looking hat. He eyes you sourly, as if deciding exactly how much offence he should take to the way you're staring at it.":"一个脾气暴躁的矮人，戴着一顶看起来很蠢的帽子。他酸溜溜地打量着你， 仿佛在决定他应该对你的注视方式感到多大程度的冒犯。","It has been centuries since outsiders were last allowed access to the cavernous libraries of the formicids, but their emissaries are still seen from time to time - surveying other lands for resources or scientific discoveries that might aid the colony.":"几个世纪以来，外人最后一次被允许进入蚁族洞穴般的图书馆已是许久以前， 但他们的使者仍时常出现——巡视其他土地寻找可能帮助殖民地的资源或科学发现。","This one's study of the magical fibres excreted by orb spiders has already led to an alchemical breakthrough, allowing them to shape fulminant prisms such that their explosions are directed at enemies alone. Alas, their enthusiasm to conduct a field test bodes poorly for your health.":"这位对圆蛛分泌的魔法纤维的研究已经导致了一项炼金术突破， 使他们能够塑造爆炸棱镜，使得爆炸只针对敌人。唉，他们进行现场测试的 热情对你的健康可不是好兆头。","It has been centuries since outsiders were last allowed access to the cavernous libraries of the formicids, but their emissaries are still seen from time to time - surveying other lands for resources or scientific discoveries that might aid the colony. This one's study of the magical fibres excreted by orb spiders has already led to an alchemical breakthrough, allowing them to shape fulminant prisms such that their explosions are directed at enemies alone. Alas, their enthusiasm to conduct a field test bodes poorly for your health.":"几个世纪以来，外人最后一次被允许进入蚁族洞穴般的图书馆已是许久以前， 但他们的使者仍时常出现——巡视其他土地寻找可能帮助殖民地的资源或科学发现。 这位对圆蛛分泌的魔法纤维的研究已经导致了一项炼金术突破， 使他们能够塑造爆炸棱镜，使得爆炸只针对敌人。唉，他们进行现场测试的 热情对你的健康可不是好兆头。","A self-styled monarch of a shambling black alder, half respected and half ridiculed by other fae. It backs up its aspirations to sovereignty with unearthly vile magic quite close to a touch of death.":"一棵自称君主的蹒跚黑桤木，在其他精类中半受尊敬半被嘲笑。 它用近乎死亡之触的超自然邪恶魔法来支持其统治野心。","A minor hairy maggot spirit, phasing in and out of this plane. Each regional variant inflicts different minor ailments: the ones found in the Dungeon cause one's magic to grow weak.":"一只小小的多毛蛆虫精魂，在这个位面中忽隐忽现。每个地区变种 会造成不同的轻微疾病：在地牢中发现的那些会导致人的魔力变弱。","A small metal sphere surrounding a core of dormant fire magic. When given the proper command, it will detonate in a blast of metal and flame that is only partially affected by fire resistance.":"一个小金属球体，包裹着一个休眠火焰魔法核心。当收到正确指令时， 它将引爆为一团金属与火焰的爆炸，火焰抗性只能部分减免其伤害。","An impossible shape that scintillates with unearthly colour. The power of Zot flows heavily through it, overlaying this reality with countless others where its domain remains pristine.":"一个以超自然色彩闪烁的不可能形状。佐特的力量沉重地流过它， 将此现实与无数其他其领域保持原始状态的现实叠加在一起。","Each tesseract is inextricably linked to the other, and destroying one will destroy both (and expel all the creatures they have beckoned to this reality, as well as dazing even those which they have not). But so long as they are allowed to exist, there will be no end to the forces which seek to keep you from the Orb.":"每个超立方体与另一个密不可分地相连，摧毁一个将同时摧毁两个 （并驱逐它们召唤到此现实的所有生物，以及晕眩那些未被召唤的）。 但只要有它们存在，试图阻止你获取宝珠的力量就将永无止境。","An impossible shape that scintillates with unearthly colour. The power of Zot flows heavily through it, overlaying this reality with countless others where its domain remains pristine. Each tesseract is inextricably linked to the other, and destroying one will destroy both (and expel all the creatures they have beckoned to this reality, as well as dazing even those which they have not). But so long as they are allowed to exist, there will be no end to the forces which seek to keep you from the Orb.":"一个以超自然色彩闪烁的不可能形状。佐特的力量沉重地流过它， 将此现实与无数其他其领域保持原始状态的现实叠加在一起。 每个超立方体与另一个密不可分地相连，摧毁一个将同时摧毁两个 （并驱逐它们召唤到此现实的所有生物，以及晕眩那些未被召唤的）。 但只要有它们存在，试图阻止你获取宝珠的力量就将永无止境。","A rapidly-growing mushroom whose life-cycle culminates in an explosive release of spores. These spores have a mild psychoactive effect and can sometimes daze creatures who breathe them in.":"一种快速生长的蘑菇，其生命周期以孢子的爆发性释放为高潮。 这些孢子具有轻微的致幻效果，有时会使吸入它们的生物晕眩。","A balloon-like sac of slime mold spores, suspended in a nutrient slurry to sustain them on their search for a new home. To the great misfortune of any adventurers in the vicinity, this slurry is also a highly potent acid.":"一个气球般的黏菌孢子囊，悬浮在营养液中以维持它们寻找新家的旅程。 对附近的任何冒险者来说极为不幸的是，这种营养液也是一种强效酸液。","Some sorcerers care little for unholy realms or undead forms, seeking power instead in the whims of cruel chaos. This ominous owl-winged head is all that remains of a former archmage: it delights in spreading misfortune and drinking blood in its new airborne form.":"有些术士毫不在意邪恶领域或亡灵形态，而是在残酷混沌的变幻莫测中 寻求力量。这只不祥的枭翅头颅是一位前大法师的全部残存： 它以散布不幸和在新飞行形态中饮血为乐。","A common dungeon pest that combines the worst features of a scavenging insect and a looming deadline.":"一种常见的地牢害虫，结合了食腐昆虫和临近截止日期的最糟特征。","Time flows strangely around it, rewinding any injuries inflicted upon it unless the source of them is near enough to be caught up in its timestream.":"时间在它周围奇异地流动，倒转对它造成的任何伤害， 除非伤害源足够近以至于被卷入它的时间流中。","A common dungeon pest that combines the worst features of a scavenging insect and a looming deadline. Time flows strangely around it, rewinding any injuries inflicted upon it unless the source of them is near enough to be caught up in its timestream.":"一种常见的地牢害虫，结合了食腐昆虫和临近截止日期的最糟特征。 时间在它周围奇异地流动，倒转对它造成的任何伤害， 除非伤害源足够近以至于被卷入它的时间流中。","A mechanical insect powered by an intricate array of gears and springs. It is vicious and resilient to damage, but its clockwork naturally winds down as it attacks, eventually leaving it unable to move until its creator winds it again.":"一只由精巧的齿轮和弹簧阵列驱动的机械昆虫。它凶猛且对伤害有韧性， 但随着攻击，其发条自然会松弛，最终使其无法移动， 直到其创造者再次为它上发条。","A wizened, headless corpse, animated not by conventional necromancy but by the mournful malice of dead stars. Its psychic eyes, floating disjointedly from its body's movements, relentlessly burrow through its victims' minds.":"一具干瘪的无头尸体，不是由传统的死灵术驱动，而是由死星的哀怨恶意 所驱动。它的心灵之眼与其身体的动作脱节地飘浮着， 无情地钻入受害者的心智。","An unfathomably massive pile of mystic pulsating protoplasm. The slightest threat will cause it to undergo rapid weaponised mitosis, rapidly overwhelming potential meals in a cytoplasmic tidal wave.":"一堆令人难以理解地巨大的神秘脉动原生质。最轻微的威胁都会导致它 进行快速武器化有丝分裂，在细胞质海啸中迅速淹没潜在的猎物。","A modern breakthrough in arcane experimentation, this mobile prison cell weaponises the living fragments of once-escaped ugly things, extending the reach of their tendrils to thrash multiple foes at once from a distance.":"奥术实验的一项现代突破，这个移动监狱牢房将曾经逃脱的丑陋之物的 活体碎片武器化，延伸其触须的范围以从远处同时鞭打多个敌人。","An enormous and unnervingly motile slime mold colony. It creeps along the crevices of the walls in search of nutrients and can spread itself to new locations by launching enormous sporangia.":"一个巨大且令人不安地活动的黏菌群落。它沿着墙壁的缝隙爬行寻找养分， 并可以通过发射巨大的孢子囊来扩散到新位置。","A serrated disc forged of razor-sharp material. It spins in place at high velocity, shredding through flesh and metal alike.":"一个由锋锐材料锻造的锯齿圆盘。它以高速原地旋转，撕碎血肉和金属。","A mechanical insect powered by an intricate array of gears and springs. It has run out of power and can only be rewound by its creator moving into it.":"一只由精巧的齿轮和弹簧阵列驱动的机械昆虫。它耗尽了能量， 只能由其创造者移动到它之中来重新上发条。","A territorial gnarl of driftwood and shattered bones. Its resentment of the living has slowly twisted its remains into a monstrous form, capable of brandishing weapons and spreading terrible curses.":"一团由浮木和碎骨组成的有领地意识的纠结物。它对生者的怨恨已慢慢将 其残骸扭曲成怪异的形态，能够挥舞武器并传播可怕的诅咒。","A conniving demon born from the nightmares of sleeping mages. It delights in coaxing the imagined fears of mortals into reality.":"一个从沉睡法师的噩梦中诞生的狡猾恶魔。它以将凡人想象中的恐惧 引诱到现实中为乐。","A churning mass of flowing blood that throbs to the beat of an absent heart.":"一团随着缺席心脏的搏动而脉动的奔流之血。","Does it wish to bury itself in your arteries because it recognises, on some primordial level, that this is where it belongs? Alas, all it is capable of in this fleeing moment of sentience is violence.":"它想将自己埋入你的动脉，是因为它在某个原始层面上认识到这是它 所属的地方吗？唉，在这短暂的感知时刻，它所能做的只有暴力。","A churning mass of flowing blood that throbs to the beat of an absent heart. Does it wish to bury itself in your arteries because it recognises, on some primordial level, that this is where it belongs? Alas, all it is capable of in this fleeing moment of sentience is violence.":"一团随着缺席心脏的搏动而脉动的奔流之血。 它想将自己埋入你的动脉，是因为它在某个原始层面上认识到这是它 所属的地方吗？唉，在这短暂的感知时刻，它所能做的只有暴力。","A hovering horror, rare and unnatural even amongst servitor eyes, radiating baleful energies. They monitor the flow of chaotic life and ever-present death for the divine Jiyva.":"一个悬浮的恐怖之物，即使在侍从之眼中也是稀有且不自然的， 辐射着恶毒的能量。它们为吉瓦监视着混沌生命和永恒死亡的流动。","A beneficent remnant of the countless mortal knights who serve the Shining One. Their hosts' role in the divine hierarchy is to guide and direct their legions in righteous moral warfare, though they may also call upon those mortals to defend themselves.":"侍奉光辉者的无数凡人骑士留下的仁善残影。 这些军势在神圣序列中的职责，是引导并指挥军团投入正义圣战； 必要时，它们也会召来那些凡人保护自己。","A roiling sphere of intense destructive energies, drawn from the fabric of the Hells themselves. It pursues a designated target inexorably, growing in size as it travels. If it collides with either a creature or wall, it will explode violently - though its creator is protected from the wild destruction unleashed as it does so.":"一个翻涌的强烈毁灭能量球体，汲取自地狱的构造本身。它不可阻挡地 追逐指定的目标，在行进中不断变大。如果它与生物或墙壁碰撞， 将猛烈爆炸——尽管其创造者在它释放的狂野毁灭中受到保护。","Goblin clans fractured over the advent of steel exoskeletons long ago, prompting an experimental arms race for goblin hegemony. Some volunteered to join forces with other species, an alliance that has enabled capturing and taming wyverns. From uptop their majestic dragon-like mounts, these goblins swiftly soar about and skewer those who intrude upon their allies' domain.":"地精氏族在许久以前因钢铁外骨骼的出现而分裂，引发了一场争夺地精 霸权的实验性军备竞赛。一些地精自愿与其他物种结盟， 这种联盟使得捕捉和驯服双足飞龙成为可能。从它们雄伟的龙形坐骑上， 这些地精迅速飞翔并用矛刺穿闯入其盟友领地的人。","A goblin newly converted to Nemelex Xobeh. It's still learning about all the cards and, thankfully, isn't inclined to use them against you.":"一个刚皈依奈默勒克斯·佐贝的地精。它仍在学习所有卡牌的知识， 而且幸好，它不太想用它们来对付你。","<master elementalist>":"<master elementalist>","A fearsome aged hybrid with a woman's head, a lion's body, and the wings of an eagle. It solemnly guards the temples and treasures of the Dungeon with a multitude of mind-clouding maledictions.":"一只可怕的年迈混血生物，拥有女人的头、狮子的身体和鹰的翅膀。 它用众多混淆心智的诅咒庄严地守护着地牢的神庙和宝藏。","An ordinary piece of armour, held in your haunting grip. It can attack nearby enemies, but must return to your side if you ever stray too far from it.":"一件普通的护甲，被你以附身之力掌控着。它可以攻击附近的敌人， 但如果你离它太远，必须回到你身边。","A terrifying weapon hewn from molten rock. It rains fiery destruction down upon its creators' enemies.":"一种由熔岩凿成的恐怖武器。它向其创造者的敌人们倾泻火焰毁灭。","An elegant siege weapon, magically sculpted from crystalline ice. As ephemeral as a summer snowstorm, every salvo it fires consumes a portion of itself until nothing is left behind but water.":"一种由水晶般寒冰魔法雕塑而成的优雅攻城武器。如夏日暴风雪般短暂， 每次齐射都会消耗自身的一部分，直到什么也不剩，只有水。","A cruel and unruly brute who growls in the language of the untamed. Its very presence provokes and overworks non-sapient, living beasts and slimes alike into a rapid fervour.":"一个用野性之语咆哮的残酷而无序的蛮人。它的存在本身就激发和过度驱使 非智慧的有生野兽和软泥进入快速狂热状态。","A well-armoured coglin whose talents with machinery have been harnessed by the Ironbound order to repair and augment the many constructs that help guard the Vaults.":"一个装备精良的齿轮地精，其机械天赋被铁缚团利用来修理和增强 帮助守卫宝库的众多构造体。","A skull-masked kobold, its body mutated by forbidden magics. It conducts vile experiments in the service of demonic powers, formulating ever more terrible monstrosities as vessels for devilish minds.":"一个戴着骷髅面具的狗头人，其身体被禁忌魔法变异。它为恶魔力量 进行邪恶实验，为魔鬼心智制造越来越可怕怪异的容器。","A wily kobold who has learned to weaponise every crack and crevice that lines the walls of its domain.":"一个狡猾的狗头人，学会了把领地墙壁上的每条裂纹和缝隙都化作武器。","The flame-wreathed skeleton of a carnivorous fish, darting through air as easily as it once parted water. It burns with a hunger it could not satisfy in life and is singularly driven by in death.":"一具被火焰缠绕的肉食鱼骷髅，如曾经分开水流般轻松地在空中穿梭。 它燃烧着生前无法满足、死后单一驱动的饥饿。","While a single one may be only a nuisance, the swarm is never far behind, and every bite it lands will summon more and more of them until every scrap of flesh on its prey has been devoured.":"虽然单独一只可能只是个小麻烦，但鱼群永远不会落后太远， 它每咬一口都会召唤越来越多的同伙，直到猎物身上的每一丝肉都被吞噬殆尽。","The flame-wreathed skeleton of a carnivorous fish, darting through air as easily as it once parted water. It burns with a hunger it could not satisfy in life and is singularly driven by in death. While a single one may be only a nuisance, the swarm is never far behind, and every bite it lands will summon more and more of them until every scrap of flesh on its prey has been devoured.":"一具被火焰缠绕的肉食鱼骷髅，如曾经分开水流般轻松地在空中穿梭。 它燃烧着生前无法满足、死后单一驱动的饥饿。 虽然单独一只可能只是个小麻烦，但鱼群永远不会落后太远， 它每咬一口都会召唤越来越多的同伙，直到猎物身上的每一丝肉都被吞噬殆尽。","A flying munitions factory, held aloft on jets of fiery exhaust and packed to the brim with explosives. It can rapidly fill an area with bomblets, and when commanded by its creator, will explode them all (and itself) to devastating effect.":"一个飞行弹药工厂，由火焰排气喷射维持在空中，装满了炸药。 它可以迅速用小型炸弹填满一片区域，当其创造者命令时， 将引爆所有炸弹（以及它自己），造成毁灭性效果。","A multihued mire of roiling flesh and fluctuating sludge, striving and failing for more coherence than any other slime. As a fresh carrier of the ruinous contagion that overtook the Slime Pits, it can impart unto others the same horrible fate. While it may not be a permanent transformation for you, the melding of weapons and armour, as well as the severe weakening of spells, may make it a lethal one regardless.":"一团多色的翻涌血肉和波动污泥，比其他任何软泥都更努力地争取着 连贯性——但始终失败。作为吞没软泥坑的毁灭性传染的新载体， 它可以向他人传递同样可怕的命运。虽然对你来说可能不是永久性的变形， 但武器和护甲的融合，以及法术的严重削弱，仍可能使其致命。","An enormous land tortoise whose shell is so thick and rock-encrusted that sleeping ones are frequently mistaken for geological formations. And like a mountain, its exterior is nearly impervious to any destructive force; only at close range can one properly aim for the narrow gaps between its plates to strike the tender flesh within.":"一只巨大的陆龟，其龟壳如此厚实且覆盖岩石，以至于睡着的个体常被 误认为是地质构造。像山一样，其外表几乎不受任何毁灭力量的影响； 只有在近距离才能正确瞄准甲板之间狭窄的缝隙，攻击内部的柔软血肉。","A slime mold colony in an early phase of its life cycle. Not yet mature enough to reproduce, it can still defend itself by firing globs of potent acid.":"一个处于生命周期早期阶段的黏菌群落。尚未成熟到可以繁殖， 但它仍然可以通过发射强效酸液球来保护自己。","An upright feliform trickster of an elderly demon, with a forked tail ablaze with a shimmering haze. It holds a deep disdain for mortal humanoids, a patronising pity for mortal cats, and enough mystic might to subjugate both.":"一只直立的猫形老年恶魔骗子，叉尾燃烧着闪烁的薄雾。 它对凡人两足生物怀有深深的蔑视，对凡人猫抱有傲慢的怜悯， 并拥有足够的魔法力量来征服两者。","A faceless stone bat unearthed from infernal chasms. Devilish beasts hunt in its wake.":"一只从地狱裂谷中出土的无面石蝠。邪魔野兽紧随其后出猎。","An infamous, dutiful retainer of Gehenna. These immense and indomitable oni weave their weapons through reality itself to reach and capture the innumerable damned souls owed to the hells upon their deaths.":"火焚地狱的一个臭名昭著、忠诚的侍从。这些巨大而不可征服的鬼 让武器穿透现实本身，触及并捕获无数在死后归地狱所有的受诅灵魂。","A globe of profound nothingness and the oblivion that awaits all things - flesh, souls, and even time itself. When the universe ends, only these will remain.":"一个深沉虚无和等待万物——血肉、灵魂甚至时间本身——之湮灭的球体。 当宇宙终结时，只有这些将会留存。","A globe of deepest cold, still lingering from a time before the stars lit the heavens. It can shroud the soul in a chill so intense that even the gods cannot reach it.":"一个极寒的球体，仍然逗留在星辰照亮天穹之前的时代。 它可以以一种如此强烈的寒意笼罩灵魂，以至于连神都无法触及。","An orcish wayfarer who has been touched by the hand of Beogh. Whether out of religious devotion or personal jealousy, they have come to bar your path.":"一位被贝奥格之手触碰过的兽人旅者。无论是出于宗教虔诚还是个人嫉妒， 他们来此阻挡你的去路。","Hold nothing back - for neither they nor their followers will do so.":"不要留手——因为他们和他们的追随者也不会。","Glory to Beogh!":"荣耀归于贝奥格！","An orcish wayfarer who has been touched by the hand of Beogh. Whether out of religious devotion or personal jealousy, they have come to bar your path. Hold nothing back - for neither they nor their followers will do so. Glory to Beogh!":"一位被贝奥格之手触碰过的兽人旅者。无论是出于宗教虔诚还是个人嫉妒， 他们来此阻挡你的去路。 不要留手——因为他们和他们的追随者也不会。 荣耀归于贝奥格！","A favoured child of Beogh, once not so unlike yourself.":"贝奥格的一个受宠之子，曾经与你不是那么不同。","Now that you have proven yourself to them, they will fight and die for both you and the cause. Shepherd them well.":"既然你已经向他们证明了自己，他们将为你和事业而战而死。 好好引导他们。","A favoured child of Beogh, once not so unlike yourself. Now that you have proven yourself to them, they will fight and die for both you and the cause. Shepherd them well.":"贝奥格的一个受宠之子，曾经与你不是那么不同。 既然你已经向他们证明了自己，他们将为你和事业而战而死。 好好引导他们。","A sizeable and statuesque flower, fossilised either by bitter grief or the cruel grace of divinity, standing in its own eternal vigil.":"一朵硕大如雕像的花，因苦涩悲恸或残酷神恩而石化，独自永恒守望。","An intricate mechanical beetle covered in reinforced metal plates that resemble a shield. It projects a kinetic barrier around its creator while adjacent to them, increasing their armour class.":"一只覆盖着类似盾牌的强化金属板的精巧机械甲虫。当与其创造者相邻时， 它在其周围投射一道动能屏障，提高其护甲等级。","It will never voluntarily leave its creator's side, and if forcibly seperated, will prioritise returning to them over any other concerns.":"它永远不会自愿离开创造者的身边，如果被强行分离， 将优先返回他们身边而非任何其他考量。","An intricate mechanical beetle covered in reinforced metal plates that resemble a shield. It projects a kinetic barrier around its creator while adjacent to them, increasing their armour class. It will never voluntarily leave its creator's side, and if forcibly seperated, will prioritise returning to them over any other concerns.":"一只覆盖着类似盾牌的强化金属板的精巧机械甲虫。当与其创造者相邻时， 它在其周围投射一道动能屏障，提高其护甲等级。 它永远不会自愿离开创造者的身边，如果被强行分离， 将优先返回他们身边而非任何其他考量。","A heavily ruptured stonework, surrounded by rubble.":"一堆严重破裂的石雕，周围散落着碎石。","A leftover mess of broken bones, inert grasping organs, and scattered skin. While some highly-specialised sorcerers might be capable of bringing it to life, it is otherwise harmless - the possible leftovers of some departed or absent-minded magus.":"一堆残余的碎骨、惰性的抓握器官和散落的皮肤。 虽然一些高度专业的术士可能能够将其赋予生命， 但除此之外它是无害的——可能是某位离开或心不在焉的法师的残留物。","A spire of strangely tenebrous ice, its brittle tendrils reaching skyward like the fingers of an outstretched hand. {{ if spells.memorised(\"rimeblight\") then return \"If only the dying breath of every soul could create such art.\" else return \"It might even be beautiful if you didn't know the gruesome \" .. \"way it formed.\" end }}":"一根奇异阴暗寒冰的尖塔，其脆弱的卷须像伸出的手指一样伸向天空。{{ if spells.memorised(\"rimeblight\") then return \"如果每个灵魂的临终之息都能创造这样的艺术该多好。\" else return \"如果你不知道它形成的可怕方式，它甚至可能是美丽的。\" end }}","A gleaming warrior, wrought from precious metals and the very pinnacle of forgecraft techniques. Its every motion flows with a deadly, fluid grace that belies its artifical nature.":"一个闪闪发光的战士，由贵金属和锻造术的巅峰技艺铸成。 其每个动作都流淌着致命的流畅优雅，与其人造本质形成对比。","A ghostly trickster that is fond of possessing small objects and making them fly noisily through the air.":"一个喜欢附身于小物体并使它们在空中嘈杂飞舞的幽灵骗子。","Many poltergeists are fiercely territorial over the domains they choose to haunt, but these have extended that protection even to the people who share their domain with them. Some say they must be the lingering souls of those who guarded the Vaults in life; others suggest the Ironbound Order simply recruited them in common cause. Whichever is true, their very presence shelters other creatures from missiles, causing sling and spell alike to veer off-course at the last moment.":"许多骚灵对它们选择附身的领域极其有领地意识，但这些甚至将 保护延伸到了与它们共享领域的人们。有人说它们必定是在生前守卫 宝库之人的徘徊灵魂；其他人则认为铁缚团只是在共同目标下招募了它们。 无论哪种是真实的，它们的存在本身就庇护其他生物免受投射物伤害， 使投石索和法术在最后一刻偏转方向。","A jet-black corvid with a nasty beak and a reputation for heralding bad luck. Most ornithologists consider this a baseless stereotype; the rest are still recovering from a series of staggeringly unlikely accidents.":"一只漆黑的鸦科鸟类，有着难看的喙和预示坏运气的声音。 大多数鸟类学家认为这是一种毫无根据的刻板印象； 其余的仍在从一系列令人震惊地不可能的意外事件中恢复。","A crackling weapon formed of condensed magical energy. It can cut through entire rows of adversaries whenever its creator lands a melee attack.":"一把由凝聚魔法能量形成的噼啪作响的武器。每当其创造者用近战攻击命中时， 它可以切割一整排的敌人。","A timeworn revenant whose flames dance with the silhouettes of long-forgotten atrocities. Cursed with a hunger they can never satisfy, they unleash these long-dead echoes to reenact violence upon any soul they deem worthy of adding to their eternal collection.":"一个历经沧桑的归来者，其火焰中舞动着久被遗忘的暴行的剪影。 被永远无法满足的饥渴所诅咒，它们释放这些早已死去的回响， 对任何它们认为值得加入其永恒收藏的灵魂重新演绎暴力。","A strange stone-scaled fish that swims through solid rock with the same ease that most fish do through water.":"一种奇特的石鳞鱼，以大多数鱼在水中游动的同样轻松在坚固岩石中游动。","A large and vivid bloom drifting placidly upon the surface of the water. The cradle of the lotus's petals shine with eternity and elegance - while it is entirely harmless, it would take immense effort to destroy it.":"一朵大而鲜艳的花朵，静静地漂流在水面上。莲花花瓣的摇篮闪耀着 永恒与优雅——虽然它完全无害，但需要巨大的努力才能摧毁它。","A deeply unfortunate soul mostly processed into crystal by some malevolent tear in reality. Ethereal reflections of its past and future suffering are cast upon nearby surfaces and foes.":"一个极其不幸的灵魂，被现实中某个恶毒裂隙大致处理成了水晶。 其过去和未来苦难的空灵反射被投射到附近的表面和敌人身上。","An irritable, bristling shrub. It fends off anything that might graze upon it by launching some of its innumerable toxic stinging hairs.":"一种易怒、多刺的灌木。它通过发射一些数不清的有毒刺毛来抵御 任何可能啃食它的东西。","A stubborn and fiercely territorial lizard with the strength of a mountain. Its thunderous footfalls herald violent tremors.":"一只固执而极具领地意识的蜥蜴，拥有山一般的力量。 其雷鸣般的脚步预示着猛烈的地震。","A lizard egg the size of a small boulder and nearly as hard. Perhaps as a defence mechanism, they hatch rapidly in the presence of predators and even a newborn can give all but the most ambitious of monsters a reason to consider an easier meal.":"一颗小巨石大小、几乎一样坚硬的蜥蜴蛋。也许作为一种防御机制， 它们在捕食者面前会迅速孵化，即使是新生儿也能给除了最有野心的 怪物之外的所有生物一个考虑更容易食物的理由。","A featureless silhouette of your own body, moving independently through the divine power of Dithmenos. No matter how many times it is struck down, it will reform itself, for a shadow is inextinguishable so long as whatever cast it remains.":"你自身身体的一个无特征剪影，通过迪瑟梅诺斯的神圣力量独立移动。 无论它被打倒多少次，它都会重塑自身；只要投下它的本体仍然存在， 暗影便永不消散。","A prism-like silhouette which wavers with barely-contained destructive energy. Any blow which disrupts its form will result in a violent blast of shadow.":"一个棱镜般的剪影，因几乎无法容纳的毁灭能量而摇曳。 任何破坏其形态的攻击都将导致一次猛烈的暗影爆炸。","A minor servant of living shadow whose form wavers perpetually on the edge of recognition - as if an unseen light were flickering behind something almost familiar.":"活影的一个小仆从，其形态永远在识别的边缘摇曳—— 仿佛一盏看不见的灯在某个几乎熟悉的东西后面闪烁。","The strength of its attacks increases in proportion with the power of the spell which summoned it.":"其攻击的强度与召唤它的法术威力成比例增加。","A minor servant of living shadow whose form wavers perpetually on the edge of recognition - as if an unseen light were flickering behind something almost familiar. The strength of its attacks increases in proportion with the power of the spell which summoned it.":"活影的一个小仆从，其形态永远在识别的边缘摇曳—— 仿佛一盏看不见的灯在某个几乎熟悉的东西后面闪烁。 其攻击的强度与召唤它的法术威力成比例增加。","A strangely static silhouette whose form suggests a large cannon. Though it uses no gunpowder, the depths of its bore flickers angrily with every shot, as if remembering the fiery light of its ignition.":"一个奇特静止的剪影，其形态暗示着一门大型火炮。虽然它不使用火药， 其炮膛深处随着每次射击而愤怒地闪烁，仿佛在回忆其点火的炽热光芒。","A glimmering spark of magical energy. It seeks out nearby enemies to expend itself upon, dealing damage and pushing them backwards.":"一颗闪烁的魔法能量火花。它寻找附近的敌人来消耗自己， 造成伤害并将它们向后推开。","It does not block its allies' line of fire.":"它不会阻挡盟友的射击线。","A glimmering spark of magical energy. It seeks out nearby enemies to expend itself upon, dealing damage and pushing them backwards. It does not block its allies' line of fire.":"一颗闪烁的魔法能量火花。它寻找附近的敌人来消耗自己， 造成伤害并将它们向后推开。 它不会阻挡盟友的射击线。","A quivering amalgam of viscous slime, its many pseudopods gnashing at the air like a throng of reptilian maws. It rapidly absorbs nearby slime creatures into itself, growing a new 'head' for each one and becoming even more resilient.":"一团颤动的黏稠软泥，其众多伪足像一群爬行动物的嘴一样在空中咬啮。 它迅速将附近的软泥生物吸收进自身，每个都长出一个新\"头\"并变得 更加坚韧。","Whether through convergent evolution or genetic memory, it also shares the hydra's most infamous trait: lopping off a head with a bladed weapon will just make it grow two more unless the wound is cauterised by a flaming weapon.":"无论是通过趋同进化还是遗传记忆，它也分享了多头蛇最臭名昭著的特征： 用利器砍掉一个头只会让它再长出两个，除非伤口被火焰武器烧灼。","When not stalking prey, its constituent slimes may separate from it again, perhaps to seek new food sources on their own.":"当不追踪猎物时，其组成的软泥可能再次与它分离， 也许是为了自己寻找新的食物来源。","A quivering amalgam of viscous slime, its many pseudopods gnashing at the air like a throng of reptilian maws. It rapidly absorbs nearby slime creatures into itself, growing a new 'head' for each one and becoming even more resilient. Whether through convergent evolution or genetic memory, it also shares the hydra's most infamous trait: lopping off a head with a bladed weapon will just make it grow two more unless the wound is cauterised by a flaming weapon. When not stalking prey, its constituent slimes may separate from it again, perhaps to seek new food sources on their own.":"一团颤动的黏稠软泥，其众多伪足像一群爬行动物的嘴一样在空中咬啮。 它迅速将附近的软泥生物吸收进自身，每个都长出一个新\"头\"并变得 更加坚韧。 无论是通过趋同进化还是遗传记忆，它也分享了多头蛇最臭名昭著的特征： 用利器砍掉一个头只会让它再长出两个，除非伤口被火焰武器烧灼。 当不追踪猎物时，其组成的软泥可能再次与它分离， 也许是为了自己寻找新的食物来源。","A mote of intense light and heat manifested by a sun scarab. It is linked to their essence and will never leave their side, being reconstituted time and time again whenever it is extinguished.":"由太阳圣甲虫显现的一粒强烈光与热。它与它们的本质相连， 永远不会离开它们身边，每当被熄灭时都被一次又一次地重新构造。","Some myths even claim that the sun which shines down upon the outside world was once carried around by such a scarab.":"有些神话甚至声称照耀外部世界的太阳曾经由这样一只圣甲虫携带。","A mote of intense light and heat manifested by a sun scarab. It is linked to their essence and will never leave their side, being reconstituted time and time again whenever it is extinguished. Some myths even claim that the sun which shines down upon the outside world was once carried around by such a scarab.":"由太阳圣甲虫显现的一粒强烈光与热。它与它们的本质相连， 永远不会离开它们身边，每当被熄灭时都被一次又一次地重新构造。 有些神话甚至声称照耀外部世界的太阳曾经由这样一只圣甲虫携带。","A tiny fragment of a living soul, splintered from the body in which it belongs. Too mindless to be fully controlled, it seeks nothing but to reunite with its greater self once more - unfortunately, this process tends to be more violent than the magic which created it.":"一个活着灵魂的微小碎片，从原本所属的身体中裂出。 它几乎没有心智，无法被完全控制，只求再次与完整的自己合一—— 不幸的是，这个过程往往比创造它的魔法更加暴力。","A wicked youthful hybrid with a woman's head, a lion's body, and the wings of an eagle. It gleefully wreaks havoc with both the violent turbulence of high winds and the frustration of bewildering magics.":"一只邪恶的年轻混种生物，长着女人的头、狮子的身体和鹰的翅膀。 它兴高采烈地以高空狂风的猛烈乱流和令人晕头转向的魔法大肆破坏。","A durable barricade made of ice reinforced with forgecraft magic. A lattice of precise hairline cracks are visible just beneath its surface which allow it to fracture into a barrage of razor-sharp projectiles whenever it sustains critical damage.":"一座由用锻造术魔法加固的冰制成的坚固路障。其表面下可见精确细微裂纹 的网格，使其在承受致命伤害时碎裂成一阵锋锐的投射物弹幕。","A spriggan that has mastered the culinary arts.":"一个掌握了烹饪艺术的树精。","A white gelatinous mound that pulses with a strange iridescence. Its body absorbs magical energy like a sponge, and when sufficiently injured, will unleash this energy as a flurry of shooting stars.":"一个白色的明胶状土丘，脉动着奇异的虹彩。其身体如海绵般吸收魔法能量， 当受到足够的伤害时，会将这些能量以一阵流星雨的形式释放出来。","A clashing tempest of boundless energy, channelling into capacitor jewels. Its whirls of fire and ice occasionally escape and ricochet wildly off of walls.":"一股由无尽能量构成的冲突风暴，汇聚入电容器宝石中。 其火焰与寒冰的漩涡偶尔溢出并疯狂地从墙壁上弹跳。","The Dungeon's vast repositories of the dead and the unholy realms thereafter both require regular restocking and reorganisation, far beyond the coordination of the restless dead. These corpse-collecting constructs burrow through the earth and command divisions of zombified hands to assist them in stealing away carrion, and may also violently create new corpses for such purposes.":"地牢中庞大的死者贮藏库以及其后的不神圣领域都需要定期的补充和重组， 远超不息亡灵的协调能力。这些收集尸体的构造体挖掘穿过大地， 指挥一队队尸手协助它们偷走腐肉，也可能为此目的暴力地制造新尸体。","A swirling tempest of souls and steel: knights and blacksmiths and weaponmasters, all bound to weapons they once held in life. To fight one is like fighting an entire army.":"一股灵魂与钢铁的旋转风暴：骑士、铁匠和武器大师， 全都被绑定在生前曾握持的武器上。与一个战斗就像与整个军队战斗。","A scornful scion to whom even other vampires bend the knee. Their command over blood magic allows them to feed upon the lifeforce of entire armies at once.":"一个令即使其他吸血鬼也跪拜的傲慢子嗣。他们对血魔法的掌控使他们能够 同时从整支军队的生命力中吸取养分。","A mobile and combat-capable alchemical manufactory that uses the friction of melee combat to brew a variety of useful potions. When it has built up enough heat to complete its synthesis, it will automatically dispense the finished potions to nearby allies and fall apart.":"一个可移动且具战斗能力的炼金制造厂，利用近战摩擦来酿造各种有用的药水。 当积累足够的热量完成合成时，它将自动向附近的盟友分配成品药水并解体。","A small and strangely serpentine fold in space and time. Scholars once theorised the Dungeon's easy access to manifold unholy realms is due to the tunneling of yet-undiscovered translocations dragons. Whether or not this is true, distant stars mottle this drake's endless lengths, and dimensions bend to its writhing whim.":"一个在空间和时间中小而奇特蛇形的折叠。学者们曾推测地牢对多样的 不神圣领域的轻易通达是由于尚未被发现的传送龙类的挖掘。 无论这是否真实，遥远的星辰点缀着这条龙兽无尽的长度，而维度则 屈从于它扭动的怪念。","A demon born of mortal envy, its flesh undulating with a sickening wetness whenever it moves. It is driven by a singular desire to reduce all beauty to a form as hideous as its own.":"一个由凡人嫉妒而生的恶魔，每当移动时其肉体令人作呕地湿润地波动。 它被一个单一的欲望所驱使：将所有美毁灭成如它自己一样丑陋的形态。","Reduces the remaining duration of any nearby hostile summoned creatures.":"缩短附近所有敌对召唤生物的剩余存续时间。","Hurls an explosive ball of corrosive acid.":"投掷一颗会爆炸的腐蚀酸液球。","Cuts the health of an adjacent creature in half. This damage is never directly lethal.":"让一个邻近生物的生命值减半。但永远不会直接杀死目标。","Cuts the health of a target creature in half. This damage is never directly lethal.":"让一个目标生物的生命值减半。但永远不会直接杀死目标。","Causes the air around a creature to twist itself into a whirling vortex of meteorological fury. It does more damage to targets surrounded by empty space.":"使目标生物周围的空气扭曲成一团狂暴的气旋。 如果目标周围空旷，它会造成更大的伤害。","Converts a small portion of the brain matter of those around you into alcohol, attempting to confuse all intelligent creatures within view (although poison-resistant creatures may resist the effects). The caster will experience vertigo briefly if they successfully make contact with other minds. It is frequently used as an icebreaker at wizard parties.":"将你周围怪物的大脑中的一小部分物质转化成酒精， 以此混乱视野中的所有智慧生物（但有毒抗的生物可能会抵抗这个效果）。 如果施法者成功与其他心灵接触，便会短暂眩晕。 在巫师们的宴会上，这道法术经常被用来打破冷场。","Afflicts nearby foes with supernatural anguish, causing all damage they deal to rebound on them for the duration of the effect. Strong-willed foes can resist the necromantic visions of pain and suffering, and mindless creatures are unaffected.":"用超自然的痛苦折磨附近的敌人， 使他们在效果持续期间发出的所有伤害会反弹到他们身上。 意志力强的敌人可以抵抗痛苦的死灵幻觉，而没有意识的生物则不受到影响。","Draws upon the memory of your worn armour to manifest an echo of it that fights alongside you. This echo moves slowly, but the power of its blows increases dramatically with the weight of the armour used to form it. It possesses all the defensive properties of the armour itself.":"汲取你所穿护甲的记忆，显现出一个与你并肩作战的回响。 回响移动缓慢，但攻击威力会随用于构成它的护甲重量大幅提高， 并拥有护甲本身的全部防御属性。","Spellpower increases its durability.":"法术威力会提高其耐久度。","Draws upon the memory of your worn armour to manifest an echo of it that fights alongside you. This echo moves slowly, but the power of its blows increases dramatically with the weight of the armour used to form it. It possesses all the defensive properties of the armour itself. Spellpower increases its durability.":"汲取你所穿护甲的记忆，显现出一个与你并肩作战的回响。 回响移动缓慢，但攻击威力会随用于构成它的护甲重量大幅提高， 并拥有护甲本身的全部防御属性。 法术威力会提高其耐久度。","For some time after casting this, living creatures killed by the caster will rise as zombies. The chance of reanimating a monster and the duration of the effect increase with spell power. Re-casting this spell will return zombies to dust, as will leaving the floor.":"施法后的一段时间内，被施法者杀死的活物会化作丧尸复起。 使怪物化作丧尸的概率和效果持续时间随法术威力提高。 重新施放此法术会使丧尸归于尘土，离开当前楼层也同样如此。","Causes the target's magic to leak into the air, as though they were hit by an antimagic weapon, and heals the caster for the amount of magic drained, with no direct line of fire required.":"使目标的魔力泄入空气，如同被反魔法武器击中，并按汲取的魔力量治疗施法者； 只需视线，无需直达射线即可生效。","Pulls the top item or group of similar items from a distant pile to the floor near the caster. With low power, items might not be moved all the way to the caster's position.":"把远处地上一堆物品中最顶端的一件物品或一组类似物品拉向施法者。 法术威力低的情况下，物品可能不会一直朝施法者移动。","Extremely powerful magical items, such as the Orb of Zot, may actively resist the pull of this spell.":"特别强大的魔法物品——例如佐特宝珠，可能会主动抵抗该法术的拉力。","Pulls the top item or group of similar items from a distant pile to the floor near the caster. With low power, items might not be moved all the way to the caster's position. Extremely powerful magical items, such as the Orb of Zot, may actively resist the pull of this spell.":"把远处地上一堆物品中最顶端的一件物品或一组类似物品拉向施法者。 法术威力低的情况下，物品可能不会一直朝施法者移动。 特别强大的魔法物品——例如佐特宝珠，可能会主动抵抗该法术的拉力。","Sends a wave of electricity through everything adjacent or near-adjacent to the caster. The electricity continues to arc through everything in a connected chain, though the caster themself is unaffected. The damage dealt bypasses half of defenders' armour.":"向与施法者相邻或近邻的一切传导电流。电流会沿相互连接的目标继续跳跃， 但施法者不受影响。造成的伤害有一半无视目标护甲。","Empowers the magic of nearby wizard allies of the caster, allowing them to cast their magic more powerfully and more often.":"施法者为附近的友方法师赋予魔力，让他们能够更有力、更频繁地施法。","Sings a powerfully haunting song. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the singer (and will sometimes be drawn closer involuntarily), while other creatures will become dazed outright.":"唱出一首极具魔力、萦绕心头的歌。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离歌者 （有时还会不由自主地被拉近），其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。","In addition, it may call forth drowned souls from any nearby bodies of deep water.":"此外，它可能从附近的任何深水中召来溺魂。","Leaving the caster's line of sight will end the movement-controlling effect.":"离开施法者视野会结束控制移动的效果。","Sings a powerfully haunting song. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the singer (and will sometimes be drawn closer involuntarily), while other creatures will become dazed outright. In addition, it may call forth drowned souls from any nearby bodies of deep water. Leaving the caster's line of sight will end the movement-controlling effect.":"唱出一首极具魔力、萦绕心头的歌。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离歌者 （有时还会不由自主地被拉近），其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。 此外，它可能从附近的任何深水中召来溺魂。 离开施法者视野会结束控制移动的效果。","Gives some limited motility to nearby trees, allowing them to sway their branches and shift their roots. Such enchanted trees will lash at any adjacent enemy.":"为附近的树赋予运动能力，它们得以甩动树枝，移动根茎。 这些被施加魔法的树将会猛击邻近的敌人。","Causes vines to grow from the ground. The vines will reach out and grab interlopers, dragging them towards any nearby trees.":"让藤蔓破土而出。藤蔓会伸向前抓住闯入者，把他们拖向任一附近的树。","Banishes a creature into the Abyss.":"将一个生物放逐到深渊。","Inspires nearby allies of the caster to fight more aggressively, increasing the strength of their blows.":"激励施法者附近的友方更积极地投入战斗，增加他们的打击力量。","<Berserk ability>":"<Berserk ability>","Causes a nearby ally to fly into a berserk rage. Going berserk temporarily increases health, speed, and damage dealt in melee.":"使附近的一个盟友陷入狂暴状态。狂暴会暂时提升生命值、速度和近战伤害。","Bestows an enchantment on other nearby living creatures that causes them to rise as simulacra after being slain.":"为附近其他活物施加魔法，使其被杀死后化为拟像。","Bestows a strong beacon upon a targeted creature. It announces the presence and location of the marked creature to everyone on the same level.":"在目标生物身上施加强力信标，将被标记者的存在和位置告知同层所有生物。","Blinks allies in sight of the caster away from a nearby enemy.":"将施法者视野内的友方从附近敌人那里闪送走。","Translocates a number of allies in the caster's sight to surround a targeted enemy.":"将施法者视野内的友军转移到目标敌人周围。","Translocates the caster to a location further away from a targeted enemy.":"将施法者转移到远离目标敌人的位置。","Translocates the caster a short distance towards a targeted enemy.":"将施法者向目标敌人转移一小段距离。","Translocates a targeted enemy a short distance towards the caster. It cannot be resisted by willpower.":"将目标敌人向施法者处转移一小段距离。意志力无法抗拒它。","Randomly translocates a targeted enemy a short distance. It cannot be resisted by willpower.":"随机地将目标敌人转移一小段距离。意志力无法抗拒它。","Translocates the caster to a location further away from a targeted enemy, but still within sight of the target.":"将施法者移到远离目标敌人的位置，但仍然在其视线范围内。","Randomly translocates the caster a short distance. After translocating in this way, the spell cannot be cast again for a short period of time depending on spell power.":"随机地将施法者转移一小段距离。 以这种方式移位后，短时间内无法再次施展该法术，其间隔时间取决于法术威力。","Transforms the caster into a lightning bolt, and translocates the caster to the bolt's destination.":"将施法者变为闪电箭，并将施法者转移到目的地。","Fires a penetrating bolt of frost.":"射出一道穿透性的寒冰箭。","Fires a bolt of grief and heartache that cuts its victims' willpower in half.":"射出一道悲伤和心痛之箭，使受害者的意志力减半。","Fires a penetrating bolt of negative energy which drains any living creature it strikes.":"射出一道穿透性的负能量箭，对击中的任何活物造成负能量伤害并使其衰竭。","Fires a penetrating bolt of flames.":"射出一道穿透性的烈火箭。","Fires a penetrating bolt of molten rock. Half of its damage bypasses fire resistance.":"射出一道穿透性的岩浆箭。它造成的一半伤害，火抗无法抵御。","Blasts an iron ball toward a target. The force of the blast often sends the caster staggering backwards.":"向一个目标轰击铁球。轰击的力量也常常会使施法者踉跄地向后退。","Instantly heals any and all wounds suffered by the caster, but also permanently damages their health, to a degree dependent on (and inversely related to) power.":"这道法术瞬间治愈施法者身上所有的创伤， 但同时会永久损失最大生命值，其程度与法术威力成反比。","It is powerful enough to cancel the effects of Death's Door, although doing so will briefly paralyse the caster. It has no effect on the undead.":"这道法术极为强大，足以将施法者从“死亡之门”里拉出来， 但这么做施法者会被暂时麻痹。它对亡灵无效。","Instantly heals any and all wounds suffered by the caster, but also permanently damages their health, to a degree dependent on (and inversely related to) power. It is powerful enough to cancel the effects of Death's Door, although doing so will briefly paralyse the caster. It has no effect on the undead.":"这道法术瞬间治愈施法者身上所有的创伤， 但同时会永久损失最大生命值，其程度与法术威力成反比。 这道法术极为强大，足以将施法者从“死亡之门”里拉出来， 但这么做施法者会被暂时麻痹。它对亡灵无效。","Calls forth hands from corpses interred beneath the dungeon floor long ago. Enemies caught in the area will be held in place and constricted until they break free.":"唤起地牢地层下被长久掩埋的尸体的手。 被抓住的敌人会被束缚在原地，直到他们挣脱。","Drains a small amount of a visible enemy's mind and a proportion of their magic, with no direct line of fire required. If the enemy has near-emptied magic reserves, they will take doubled damage.":"令视野中的一个敌人流失少量心智和一定比例的魔力，无需直射。 如果敌人的魔力储备几近耗尽，则会受到双倍伤害。","Unleashes a massive rolling boulder in a given compass direction. This boulder damages any creature it hits, rolling over those who perish beneath it and pushing any others helplessly backwards (along with anyone else unfortunate enough to be standing behind them).":"在给定的基本方向上释出一个硕大的滚动巨砾。 巨砾会伤害撞到的生物，从死者身上碾过，并将幸存者及其身后的其他生物 一并无助地向后推去。","Its size and reckless locomotion make it difficult to use in confined areas; if launched down narrow passages, it will rapidly abrade against the walls and fall apart. It will also crumble if it leaves the caster's sight or strikes a wall or otherwise unmoveable creature.":"巨砾庞大且横冲直撞，难以在狭窄区域使用；沿窄道发射时，它会迅速与墙壁 摩擦而解体。它离开施法者视线、撞上墙壁或其他无法推动的生物时也会碎裂。","Unleashes a massive rolling boulder in a given compass direction. This boulder damages any creature it hits, rolling over those who perish beneath it and pushing any others helplessly backwards (along with anyone else unfortunate enough to be standing behind them). Its size and reckless locomotion make it difficult to use in confined areas; if launched down narrow passages, it will rapidly abrade against the walls and fall apart. It will also crumble if it leaves the caster's sight or strikes a wall or otherwise unmoveable creature.":"在给定的基本方向上释出一个硕大的滚动巨砾。 巨砾会伤害撞到的生物，从死者身上碾过，并将幸存者及其身后的其他生物 一并无助地向后推去。 巨砾庞大且横冲直撞，难以在狭窄区域使用；沿窄道发射时，它会迅速与墙壁 摩擦而解体。它离开施法者视线、撞上墙壁或其他无法推动的生物时也会碎裂。","<Brothers in Arms ability>":"<Brothers in Arms ability>","Summons an inugami to the caster's aid. These mystical canines form a bond with their summoner, strengthening them in direct proportion with the caster's spellpower.":"召唤一个犬神来协助施法者。 这些神秘的犬科动物与它们的召唤者形成了一种纽带， 施法者的法术威力越强，它们就越强。","Recasting this spell while your familiar is nearby will imbue it with additional magic, mending some of its wounds, cleansing it of poison, and causing its next attack to strike more quickly and cleave adjacent foes.":"当你的魔宠在附近时，重施这个法术会给它注入额外的魔力， 愈合它的部分伤口、清除中毒，并使它的下一次攻击提前发动并横扫相邻敌人。","Summons an inugami to the caster's aid. These mystical canines form a bond with their summoner, strengthening them in direct proportion with the caster's spellpower. Recasting this spell while your familiar is nearby will imbue it with additional magic, mending some of its wounds, cleansing it of poison, and causing its next attack to strike more quickly and cleave adjacent foes.":"召唤一个犬神来协助施法者。 这些神秘的犬科动物与它们的召唤者形成了一种纽带， 施法者的法术威力越强，它们就越强。 当你的魔宠在附近时，重施这个法术会给它注入额外的魔力， 愈合它的部分伤口、清除中毒，并使它的下一次攻击提前发动并横扫相邻敌人。","Blasts a targeted enemy with damnation, with no direct line of fire required. These unholy forces harm the victim and anyone adjacent, and are not affected by any means of protection, such as armour or resistances. However, certain creatures, usually those able to invoke damnation themselves, are entirely unscathed by damnation.":"以天谴轰击指定敌人，无需直射。这股不洁力量会伤害目标及与其相邻的 所有生物，且不受护甲、抗性等任何防护手段影响。不过，某些生物 （通常是自身也能降下天谴的生物）完全不会受到天谴伤害。","Blasts a targeted enemy with lightning, with no direct line of fire required. The targeting magics need distance to function, so enemies that are adjacent or nearly adjacent cannot be struck by this.":"用闪电轰击敌人，无需直射。 目标性魔法需要有距离才能发挥作用，因此相邻或几乎相邻的敌人无法被击中。","Calls forth a minor demon from the pits of Hell, equipped with a spear with which to jab at the caster's enemies. The quality of the imp's weaponry rises with spell power.":"从地狱深处呼唤出一个低阶恶魔。它配备着一支长矛，可以戳刺施法者的敌人。 小恶魔的武器质量随法术威力的增强而提升。","Summons some necromantic spectres. These lost souls can enter the bodies of more powerful undead to bring them back from brink of demise, or turn dying living creatures into ghostly versions of themselves.":"召唤一些由死灵魔法形成的幽魂。这些遗魂可以进入更强大的亡灵体内， 将其从消亡边缘救回；也可以把垂死的活物变成对应的幽灵形态。","Calls upon the powers of chaos to empower nearby allies, granting them haste, might, doubled vigour, or improved resistances. The chaotic magic may occasionally backfire and cause allies to instead lose their willpower or be berserked, polymorphed, or filled with inner flame.":"召来混沌之力增强附近盟友，赋予其加速、强效、活力加倍或更高抗性。 这个混沌的魔法偶尔会适得其反， 导致友方失去意志力或变得狂暴、被变形或被内焰所充斥。","Allows the caster to affect the tidal phase of all water within a large distance. Soon after calling it, the waters on the whole level will reach high tide. Waters near the caster will reach even higher levels than they would normally.":"施法者能影响大范围内所有水域的潮汐状态。呼唤潮汐后不久，整层水域都会 进入高潮；施法者附近的水位还会涨得比通常更高。","Casts one of a number of minor spells, aimed at trying to bolster the caster's morale. They have no noticeable effect.":"施放一个初级魔法，意在提升施法者的士气。它没有明显的效果。","Causes fear in those near to the caster, causing those affected to be unable to approach the caster, and to sometimes fail to attack them in melee. Leaving the caster's line of sight will end the effect.":"这道法术让施法者附近的生物陷入恐惧之中，使它们无法接近施法者， 对施法者的近战攻击有可能失败。离开施法者的视野范围将结束效果。","Creates an arc of pure chaos, striking nearby creatures with unpredictable effects. The arc can touch upon the caster without harming them.":"创造一个纯混沌能量的弧，以不可预知的效果攻击周围的生物。 能量弧会触及施法者但不会伤害他。","Releases a massive electrical discharge that arcs to the creature nearest the caster and then outward from it. The further it travels, the less damage it does. Secondary arcs have limited range and do little damage to the caster. The spell bypasses half of defenders' armour and resistance to electricity.":"释放一股巨大的电流，先击中离施法者最近的生物，再从那里向外连锁。 它走得越远，造成的伤害就越小。次生电弧的范围有限，对施法者的伤害很小。 该法术造成的一半伤害同时无视护甲和电击抗性。","Causes an otherwise hostile creature to fight on the caster's side for a while. Adventurers, set on their quest for the ORB, instead suffer momentary confusion.":"使一个敌对生物为施法者战斗一段时间。 执意追寻宝珠的冒险者不会被魅惑，而只会短暂陷入混乱。","Exhales a large cloud of fumes filled with the very essence of chaos.":"呼出一大片充满纯粹混乱精能的云。","Exhales a focused blast of icy-cold air.":"呼出一股凝聚的冰寒之气。","Invokes a huge blast of divine fury centered on the user, severely damaging undead and demons and dealing damage to all other hostile creatures.":"激起以使用者为中心的巨大的神怒爆炸，会对亡灵和恶魔造成严重伤害， 并对所有其他敌对生物造成伤害。","Intensifies the natural venom of the target monster. Poisonous bites and spit become intense enough to slow and asphyxiate.":"强化目标怪物自身的毒液。叮咬和唾液的毒性变得更强，会造成减慢和窒息。","Induces a state of bewilderment and confusion in a creature's mind.":"使生物的头脑陷入迷惑和混乱。","Enchants the caster's dominant hand with magical energy. This energy is released when the caster touches a monster, and may induce a state of confusion in the monster. The caster's attacks do no damage while attempting to touch a monster in this way.":"这道法术能向施法者的惯用手注入魔法能量。当施法者触碰一个怪物时， 这些能量会被释放出来，可能会让目标怪物陷入混乱。 施法者以这种触碰怪物的方式进行的攻击不会造成伤害。","Induces a state of bewilderment and confusion in a creature's mind, with no direct line of fire required.":"使一个生物的心智陷入迷茫与混乱，只需视线，无需直达射线。","Creates a pack of ball lightnings, which seek out the nearest enemy before exploding in a huge blast of electricity. The damage dealt bypasses half of defenders' armour. Casters are advised to use caution; the lightning is not mindful of what it may hit.":"创造数个球状闪电，寻找到敌人后造成巨大的闪电爆炸。 防御者的防具无法抵御它造成的一半伤害。 施法者需要谨慎，因为闪电并不能判断它击中的是什么。","The magic which keeps ball lightnings cohesive has limited range, so they may dissipate harmlessly if allowed to drift too far away from their caster before exploding.":"让球状闪电保持凝聚的魔力的范围有限，如果在爆炸前离施法者太远， 它们可能会无害地消散。","Creates a pack of ball lightnings, which seek out the nearest enemy before exploding in a huge blast of electricity. The damage dealt bypasses half of defenders' armour. Casters are advised to use caution; the lightning is not mindful of what it may hit. The magic which keeps ball lightnings cohesive has limited range, so they may dissipate harmlessly if allowed to drift too far away from their caster before exploding.":"创造数个球状闪电，寻找到敌人后造成巨大的闪电爆炸。 防御者的防具无法抵御它造成的一半伤害。 施法者需要谨慎，因为闪电并不能判断它击中的是什么。 让球状闪电保持凝聚的魔力的范围有限，如果在爆炸前离施法者太远， 它们可能会无害地消散。","Creates several living, autonomous spells, which cast themselves at the first foe to enter their range. Once cast, they dissipate.":"创造几个活体自主法术；它们会在第一个敌人进入射程时自行施放， 随后消散。","Causes a halo of glowing light to surround and effectively outline a creature. This glow offsets the dark, musty atmosphere of the dungeon, and makes the affected creature appreciably easier to hit.":"这道法术创造出光晕以环绕生物，有效地勾勒出其轮廓。 这道光驱散了地牢中的黑暗和霉味，因此要击中目标生物就容易多了。","Fires a penetrating bolt of highly-corrosive acid.":"射出一道由强腐蚀性酸液构成的穿透箭。","Unleashes Abyssal energies in the immediate vicinity. This changes the appearance of the affected area and temporarily summons creatures from the Abyss. This cannot be used in the Abyss itself.":"在附近释放深渊的能量。这会改变受影响区域的外观，并暂时召唤出深渊中的生物。 它不能在深渊中释放。","Instills a corruption within all visible targets, temporarily mutating their bodies in an adverse fashion. It cannot affect artificial beings, and the undead will decompose if affected.":"向所有可见目标注入腐化，暂时对他们的身体造成有害的变异。 它不会影响人造物；亡灵若受到影响则会腐朽。","Calls forth freezing cold from the walls. Any enemies of the caster standing next to the walls will be frozen and will find their movements slowed. Cold resistance will reduce damage, but not prevent the freezing effect.":"激起墙壁中刺骨的寒意。任何站在墙边的施法者的敌人都会被冻结， 并会发现他们的移动速度变慢了。寒抗能削减其伤害，但无法抵御冰冻效果。","Curses a foe, halving their remaining health after each of the next two times that the caster strikes them in melee.":"诅咒一个敌人；施法者接下来两次以近战击中该敌人时， 每次都会使其剩余生命值减半。","Emits a wave of pernicious gloom which attempts to smother the light around nearby creatures. Any living, demonic or holy creature caught in the effect may briefly lose their eyesight and be left stumbling blindly. Willpower is useless against this spell, but stronger creatures may still shrug off its effects.":"释放一波有害阴霾，试图吞没附近生物周围的光亮。 任何被波及的活物、恶魔或神圣生物都可能短暂失明，盲目踉跄。 意志力无法抵抗此法术，但更强壮的生物仍可能摆脱效果。","Binds the souls of slain living, demonic and holy creatures, forcing their spectres to remain and fight for the caster for as long as the channel lasts.":"束缚被杀死的活物、恶魔和神圣生物的灵魂，迫使其幽魂留下， 并在引导持续期间为施法者而战。","Exhales the essence of the dying, creating clouds of noxious miasma.":"呼出死亡的实质，制造出有毒的瘴气。","Renders the caster nigh invulnerable to harm for a brief period, but brings them dangerously close to death in the process. So close, in fact, that the body believes itself to be dead — healing effects will do nothing.":"使施法者在短时间内几乎不受伤害，但也会让施法者危险地接近死亡。 事实上，如此接近，以至于身体认为自己已经死了——治疗效果将无济于事。","The caster will receive one warning shortly before the spell expires. After expiry, the spell cannot immediately be recast, but with high power the caster will be left further from death when the effect ends. It has no effect on those who are already undead.":"施法者将在法术结束前不久收到一个警告。结束后，无法立即重新施展该法术， 但在效果结束时，法术威力高的施法者将会更远离死亡。 它对已经成为亡灵的生物无效。","Renders the caster nigh invulnerable to harm for a brief period, but brings them dangerously close to death in the process. So close, in fact, that the body believes itself to be dead — healing effects will do nothing. The caster will receive one warning shortly before the spell expires. After expiry, the spell cannot immediately be recast, but with high power the caster will be left further from death when the effect ends. It has no effect on those who are already undead.":"使施法者在短时间内几乎不受伤害，但也会让施法者危险地接近死亡。 事实上，如此接近，以至于身体认为自己已经死了——治疗效果将无济于事。 施法者将在法术结束前不久收到一个警告。结束后，无法立即重新施展该法术， 但在效果结束时，法术威力高的施法者将会更远离死亡。 它对已经成为亡灵的生物无效。","Fires a ray which does massive damage (1500 hp) and always hits.":"射出一道能造成巨大伤害（1500 hp）的射线，而且百发百中。","Envelops the caster in a repulsion field, greatly increasing their evasion against all types of projectile - even while otherwise incapacitated.":"以排斥力场包裹施法者，大幅提高其对所有种类投射物的闪避能力—— 即使施法者因其他原因无法行动时也依然有效。","Digs a tunnel through unworked rock.":"从未成形的岩石中挖出一条通道。","Blocks any translocations attempted by the affected target, be they voluntary or not. This includes even some cross-plane effects, although notably not Banishment.":"阻止受影响目标尝试进行的任何移位，无论是否是主动的。 这甚至包括一些跨位面效果，但不包括放逐。","Weaves a link between the caster's weaponry and a chosen target. Whenever the caster fires or throws something at a *different* enemy, a matching projectile will be teleported at the target. Spellpower increases their accuracy.":"在施法者的武器和选定的目标之间建立连接。 每当施法者向*不同的*敌人投射东西时，对应的弹药就会传送到目标。 法术威力越强，命中率就越高。","Drives nearby creatures into an wild frenzy, causing them to mercilessly attack anything and everything nearby with great strength and speed.":"驱使附近的生物陷入疯狂，使它们以极大的力量和速度无情地攻击周围的一切。","Destabilises the space in a sphere around the caster for a while, causing anyone nearby to blink away from the caster. The chance of blinking depends on the distance from the caster, being nearly certain when directly adjacent.":"让施法者周围一个球形区域内的空间结构变得不稳定， 使周围生物从施法者那里被闪送走。闪送的概率取决于到施法者的距离， 当直接近身时，几乎一定会被闪送。","Harms an adjacent undead creature greatly by interfering with the forces binding it together.":"通过扰乱维系亡灵形体的力量，对相邻的亡灵造成极大伤害。","Harms an undead creature greatly by interfering with the forces binding it together.":"通过扰乱维系亡灵形体的力量，对一个亡灵造成极大伤害。","Teleports away any creatures within a short distance of the caster. Any creature with the Will to resist will still be irresistibly blinked a shorter distance, and any monster it affects at all has a separate Will-based chance of being confused by the warping of space.":"将施法者附近的所有生物传送到远处。 即使生物的意志足以抵抗，也仍会被不可抗拒地闪送一小段距离。 此外，任何受该法术影响的怪物都有一次独立的意志检定； 检定失败时，它会因空间扭曲而陷入混乱。","Unleashes a piercing howl that catches and echoes in victims' minds. While those echoes linger, nightmarish creatures will hear and track them to their source. It can only be used once by a given creature.":"发放出刺耳的嚎叫，在受害者的脑海中回荡。 当那些回声还在徘徊时，噩梦般的生物会听到并追踪它们的来源。 这个法术只能由特定的生物施放一次。","Issues a powerful call to a draconic realm, beckoning forth dragon after dragon to engage the summoner's enemies. The spell is taxing to maintain, and each new dragon which answers the call will further drain the summoner's magical reserves. After the call ends, it cannot be issued again for a short time. The duration of the call and the species of dragons called depend on spell power.":"向龙域发出强力呼唤，接连召来巨龙与施法者的敌人交战。 维持该法术代价高昂，每条响应呼唤的新龙都会进一步消耗施法者的魔力。 呼唤结束后，短时间内无法再次发出呼唤。呼唤的持续时间及应召龙的种类 取决于法术威力。","Drains the life force of any nearby enemies, healing the user depending on the damage dealt.":"汲取附近所有敌人的生命力，并按造成的伤害治疗使用者。","Causes the target's magic to leak into the air, as though they were hit by an antimagic weapon.":"使目标的魔力泄到空中，就像他们被反魔法武器击中一样。","Overwhelms the target with soporific dream dust, putting them to sleep with an enchanting visual display. Additional dream sheep will increase the strength and duration of this effect.":"用梦尘淹没目标，使他们入睡。另有梦羊时，会增加效果的强度和持续时间。","Recalls woodland creatures from elsewhere on the same level.":"召回同层其他地方的林地生物。","Throws a bolt of electricity at the target, with high accuracy.":"向目标射出一道有着很高精确度的闪电箭。","Overwhelms an enemy with malignant energies, irresistibly weakening their melee attacks and reducing the power of their spells. It will additionally daze and blind any foe that fails to resist the full force of the curse - even those without visual senses!":"用邪恶能量压倒敌人，不可抗拒地削弱其近战攻击并降低法术威力。 它还会使无法抵抗全部诅咒力量的敌人眩晕和失明， 即使目标没有视觉感官也不例外。","Shoots a stream of webbing at a creature, ensnaring the target in a sticky web.":"向生物射出一连串的网，使目标困于黏性的网中。","Lowers its target's metabolic rate, inducing hibernation. After awakening, the target will be unable to be put to sleep again for some time.":"降低目标的代谢率，诱导冬眠。目标苏醒后，将在一段时间内无法再次入睡。","Corrodes the target, with no direct line of fire required.":"腐蚀目标，无需直射法术。","Causes the caster to release a torrent of sludge that transforms nearby areas into a toxic bog. The sludge damages and poisons all monsters, even those resistant to poison. The bog cannot form on areas adjacent to multiple solid features, nor on areas that lack solid floor, like deep water or lava. The transformation is temporary and cannot be sustained out of the caster's sight. Spellpower will increase how long the bog lingers.":"施法者释放出一股污泥，将附近区域变成有毒的沼泽。 污泥会对所有怪物造成伤害、引起中毒，即使是那些抗毒的怪物。 沼泽不能在有多个坚固地形相邻的区域形成，也不能在缺少坚实地面的区域形成， 例如深水或熔岩。变化只是暂时的，且无法在施法者的视线外持续。 法术威力越强，沼泽的持续时间就越长。","Splits the earth to draw up a localised, short-lived volcano under the target.":"裂开地面，在目标下方生成一个局部的、短暂存在的火山。","Opens painful illusionary wounds on the target's body, which disappear after a short time or on the death of the caster. This cannot kill directly, and is ineffective against unnatural targets.":"撕开目标身上痛苦的幻象伤口，伤口会在施法者死亡后或短时间内消失。 它不能直接杀死对方，并对非自然目标无效。","Breathes a blast of fire at a targeted creature.":"向一个目标生物喷吐火焰气流。","Calls forth a mighty storm of roaring flame directly onto the target, dealing damage in a large area and leaving behind short-lived fire vortices. Half of its damage bypasses fire resistance.":"这道法术能在目标区域塑造出一团威力巨大的火焰风暴， 在造成火焰伤害的同时还会留下一些短暂存在的火旋涡。 它造成的一半伤害无视火焰抗性。","Hurls an explosive ball of fire.":"掷出一个爆炸性的火球。","Blasts the caster's surroundings with a wave of fire. If the caster maintains focus and supplies the spell with magical power (by waiting in place and not taking any other actions), more and larger flame waves will radiate outward.":"用一波火焰冲击施法者的周围。 如果施法者保持专注，并为法术提供魔力（通过原地等待而不采取任何其他行动）， 就会向外辐射更多更大的火焰波。","Conjures up a large cloud of roaring flames.":"生成一大团咆哮的火焰云。","Freezes the air around a target, causing significant harm and slowing the target's movement for a short time. Half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"冻结一个目标周围的空气，对目标造成重大伤害并减慢其移动速度。 它造成的一半伤害无法被寒冷抗性抵御。","Calls forth winds to increase the caster's movement speed for a short duration.":"召来风力，在短时间内提高施法者的移动速度。","Fires a shaft of concussive force. If the impact deals damage, it may knock the target back. If this knockback causes the target to hit a wall or another creature, both will take additional damage.":"发射一道震荡力。若命中造成伤害，可能会击退目标。 如果目标因此撞上墙壁或其他生物，二者都会受到额外伤害。","Summons some creatures from one of the Snake Pit, the Spider Nest, the Swamp, the Shoals, the Elven Halls, the Vaults, or the Crypt; the specific branch varies with the caster.":"从蛇穴、蜘蛛巢、沼泽、海滩、精灵殿堂、宝库或墓室之一召唤一些生物； 具体分支因施法者而异。","Conjures two balls of burning swamp gas adjacent to the caster. The balls will rapidly seek the nearest monster and burn them. They will dissipate harmlessly if unable to reach a target or if the caster swaps places with them.":"在施法者附近生成两个燃烧的沼气球。球会迅速寻找最近的怪物并灼烧它们。 如果不能到达目标或者施法者与它们互换位置，它们将会无害地消散。","Freezes an adjacent creature, dealing damage that bypasses any armour the target may have. This may temporarily slow cold-blooded creatures.":"冰冻一个相邻的目标，造成的伤害能无视目标可能拥有的任何护甲。 这可能会暂时减缓冷血动物的速度。","Conjures up a large cloud of lethally cold vapour.":"生成一大团致命的冰汽云。","Encases surrounding walls with ice for a short time. Foes that wander near the icy walls will be damaged, and this may temporarily slow cold-blooded creatures. Each victim is only ever affected by one icy wall at a time.":"用冰封住周围的墙壁一小段时间。在冰墙附近游荡的敌人会受到伤害， 并可能会暂时减缓冷血生物的速度。每个受害者一次只能受到一面冰墙的影响。","The ice will crack and fall away if the caster moves to a new position.":"如果施法者移动到新位置，冰会破裂、脱落。","Encases surrounding walls with ice for a short time. Foes that wander near the icy walls will be damaged, and this may temporarily slow cold-blooded creatures. Each victim is only ever affected by one icy wall at a time. The ice will crack and fall away if the caster moves to a new position.":"用冰封住周围的墙壁一小段时间。在冰墙附近游荡的敌人会受到伤害， 并可能会暂时减缓冷血生物的速度。每个受害者一次只能受到一面冰墙的影响。 如果施法者移动到新位置，冰会破裂、脱落。","Calls out to the lingering remnants of the long dead. While active, each non-summoned enemy the caster or their allies slays attracts more vengeful souls into the caster's weapon, temporarily enhancing their melee and ranged effectiveness. When this bonus reaches its maximum, every hit will unleash a glimmer of the dead's suffering, causing pain damage to each other foe adjacent to your target.":"呼唤那些早已逝去的弥留物。在激活状态下， 施法者及其盟友每杀死一个非召唤的敌人就会吸引更多复仇的灵魂进入施法者的武器， 暂时提高其近战和远程攻击力。当这个加成达到最大值时， 每次命中都会释出死者一丝痛苦，对与目标相邻的其他敌人造成痛楚伤害。","Recasting this spell will release your grip on the souls you've attracted, resetting any bonus you've accumulated, and the cacophonous wailing of the dead may attract unwanted attention even while you maintain it.":"重施这个法术会使你失去对吸引来的灵魂的控制，重置你积累的任何加成， 即使你要保持它，死者刺耳的哀嚎也会引起不必要的注意。","Calls out to the lingering remnants of the long dead. While active, each non-summoned enemy the caster or their allies slays attracts more vengeful souls into the caster's weapon, temporarily enhancing their melee and ranged effectiveness. When this bonus reaches its maximum, every hit will unleash a glimmer of the dead's suffering, causing pain damage to each other foe adjacent to your target. Recasting this spell will release your grip on the souls you've attracted, resetting any bonus you've accumulated, and the cacophonous wailing of the dead may attract unwanted attention even while you maintain it.":"呼唤那些早已逝去的弥留物。在激活状态下， 施法者及其盟友每杀死一个非召唤的敌人就会吸引更多复仇的灵魂进入施法者的武器， 暂时提高其近战和远程攻击力。当这个加成达到最大值时， 每次命中都会释出死者一丝痛苦，对与目标相邻的其他敌人造成痛楚伤害。 重施这个法术会使你失去对吸引来的灵魂的控制，重置你积累的任何加成， 即使你要保持它，死者刺耳的哀嚎也会引起不必要的注意。","Conjures a shining prism of an unstable soft gold alloy. This is useless as legal tender, however, as it will unfortunately violently explode with arcane force after a short duration. If destroyed prematurely, its blast will be much weaker.":"生成一个由不稳定软金合金制成的闪亮棱镜。可惜它不能充当法定货币， 因为短时间后便会以奥术力量猛烈爆炸；若提前摧毁，爆炸会弱得多。","A ritual chant that briefly rouses several nearby undead allies to move more swiftly and strike with greater might.":"这首仪礼歌可以短暂地唤起附近的几个亡灵盟友， 让他们更快地移动，并以更大的力量进行攻击。","Hurls an exploding ball of negative energy which drains any living creature it engulfs.":"掷出一颗爆炸性的负能量球，使其笼罩的所有活物陷入衰竭。","Uses an ally's motivating essence to create a blast of negative energy, draining any living creature it engulfs. The being used to fuel the spell, no matter whether living or construct, is consumed and unmade in the process.":"以一名友方的活力精华制造一股负能量，使其笼罩的所有活物陷入衰竭。 为法术提供燃料的友方，无论是活物还是造物，都会在此过程中被吞噬并彻底抹除。","Conjures forth a mighty blast of ice. Creatures within its cone-shaped area of effect take damage, with higher damage being dealt to those close to the caster. Those hit by the blast are encased in ice, slowing their movement, and those killed by the blast may be frozen into solid blocks of ice. Half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"召来一股强大的寒冰冲击。锥形范围内的生物会受到伤害， 越靠近施法者，所受伤害越高。被冲击命中的生物会被冰封，移动速度减慢； 被冲击杀死的生物则可能冻成坚实的冰块。 它造成的一半伤害无法被寒冷抗性抵御。","Calls giant grasping roots from deep underground that hold and constrict their victim. The roots will retreat if the victim breaks free or if the caller moves out of view.":"从地下深处召出巨大的抓握根须，抓住并挤压受害者。 若受害者挣脱，或召唤者移出其视野，根须便会退去。","Summons a major demon.":"召唤一个大恶魔。","Conjures a cannonade of hail, battering nearby creatures that fail to dodge. The eye of the storm is wide enough that monsters adjacent to the caster are unaffected. Due to the strong impact and cutting edges, half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"召来一阵冰雹，痛击附近未能躲避的生物。 风暴眼足够宽广，紧邻施法者的怪物不会受影响。 由于强烈的冲击和锋利边缘，它造成的一半伤害无法被寒冷抗性抵御。","Speeds the actions of a nearby ally.":"加速一个附近友方的行动。","Fires a long and flexible barbed mass. The ensnared victim will either be pulled adjacent to the caster or collide with anything blocking the way.":"发射一个长而灵活的带刺重物。 被它捕捉的受害者会被拉到施法者附近或与挡住去路的东西相撞。","Speeds the actions of the caster.":"加速施法者的行动。","Calls wraiths and ghosts to haunt the caster's target. They will only attack the creature they are haunting, and will dissipate quickly once their target dies. The number of spectres summoned increases with spell power.":"召唤幽灵和鬼魂，以困扰施法者的目标。他们只会攻击他们所缠扰的生物， 一旦目标死亡，它们会迅速消散。召唤出的幽灵数量随法术威力增强而增加。","Heals a nearby ally.":"治疗附近的一个盟友。","Summons demons of flame and damnation.":"召唤火焰与天谴恶魔。","Inspires nearby allies to quicken their movement.":"激励附近盟友加快移动。","<Hurl Damnation ability>":"<Hurl Damnation ability>","Conjures a focused blast of highly toxic sludge, poisoning the victim and drenching their surroundings. The sludge damages and poisons all monsters, even those resistant to poison.":"生成一道饱含剧毒的污泥，它会让受害者中毒并使其周围环境变湿。 污泥会对所有怪物造成伤害、引起中毒，即使是那些抗毒的怪物。","Exhales a large cloud of blessed flame, shining with the glory of the good gods. These flames are especially dangerous to undead and demonic creatures, and have no effect on holy creatures.":"呼出一团巨大的、闪耀着善神荣光的神圣火焰。 这些火焰对亡灵和恶魔生物特别致命，对神圣生物没有影响。","Traps an enemy in a ring of blessed flame. These flames are especially dangerous to undead and demonic creatures, and have no effect on holy creatures.":"用神圣的火焰圈住一个敌人。 这些火焰对亡灵和恶魔生物特别致命，对神圣生物没有影响。","Fires a large mass of ice, which explodes on impact. Half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"发射一大团冰块，在撞击时爆炸。 它造成的一半伤害无法被寒冷抗性抵御。","Converts all nearby poison into liquid flame, burning poisoned creatures from within. It also turns clouds of poison and mephitic gases into flame. The caster is not affected directly.":"将附近的所有毒素变成液态火焰，从内部灼烧中毒的生物。 它还会将毒云和迷乱烟雾变成火焰。施法者不会直接受到影响。","All foes in the caster's surroundings are engulfed in balls of fire. The caster and their allies are protected from the fire and will never be harmed by this spell.":"施法者周围的所有敌人都被火球吞噬。 施法者及其友方免受火焰伤害，永远不会被此法术伤害。","Calls forth a plague of scarabs, infesting affected creatures for a duration depending on power and causing death scarabs to grow and burst from them upon death.":"召唤甲虫瘟疫，它会在一定时间内根据法术威力侵染受影响的生物， 死亡甲虫会在那些生物死亡时滋生、爆发。","Binds the caster to nearby allies, reducing all damage they take by half in exchange for suffering half of the prevented damage themselves.":"将施法者与附近的盟友联结起来，使他们受到的所有伤害减半； 作为代价，施法者会承受被阻止伤害的一半。","Reflects damage taken for a short duration, hurting attackers whenever the caster takes any damage. After the duration wears off, the caster cannot cast this spell again for a short while.":"短时间内反射所受伤害；施法者每次受到伤害时，都会伤害攻击者。 持续时间结束后，施法者会有一小段时间无法再次施放此法术。","Releases a thick cloud of ink to obscure vision.":"释出浓厚的墨云，模糊视线。","Fills an enemy with an intense fire. This fire is released any time the target is hit, and explosively released upon death. The size of the explosion caused is dependent on the size of the target.":"向一个敌人体内灌入烈火。目标每次被击中时都会释放火焰， 死亡时更会猛烈爆炸；爆炸范围取决于目标体形。","Turns the caster invisible.":"使施法者隐形。","Turns a nearby ally invisible.":"使附近的一个友方隐形。","Hurls a large and heavy metal shot.":"掷出一个巨大而沉重的钢铁投射物。","Transmutes an ultra-thin layer of the caster's skin (or equivalent) directly into pure magical energy, blasting adjacent creatures. It may heavily deform its victims, weakening them and reducing their armour. The caster is not left entirely unaffected; some of the magic lingers, enough to leave them dangerously contaminated after a few castings.":"将施法者一层极薄的皮肤的（或类似物质）直接转为纯魔法能量，轰击相邻生物。 这可能会使目标严重变形、虚弱，并削弱其护甲。施法者并非完全不受影响； 身上仍残留着一些魔力，在几次施法后它们会对身体造成危险的污染。","Conjures a small globe of destructive energy. Each time its creator casts a offensive spell, the battlesphere will also fire an unerring volley of energy at the most injured nearby foe it can reach.":"召出一颗由破坏性能量构成的小型战斗法球。每当创造者施放攻击性法术， 战斗法球也会向它能触及的附近敌人中受伤最重者射出绝不会落空的能量齐射。","The battlesphere's creator can freely fire through its position without harming it.":"创造者的攻击可以自由穿过战斗法球的位置而不伤到它。","Conjures a small globe of destructive energy. Each time its creator casts a offensive spell, the battlesphere will also fire an unerring volley of energy at the most injured nearby foe it can reach. The battlesphere's creator can freely fire through its position without harming it.":"召出一颗由破坏性能量构成的小型战斗法球。每当创造者施放攻击性法术， 战斗法球也会向它能触及的附近敌人中受伤最重者射出绝不会落空的能量齐射。 创造者的攻击可以自由穿过战斗法球的位置而不伤到它。","Detonates a crackling sphere of destructive energy. The explosion will hit all nearby monsters with physical force, knocking them back if damage is done. Spellpower increases damage and knockback distance.":"引爆一颗劈啪作响的破坏性能量球。爆炸会以物理力量冲击附近所有怪物， 并击退受到伤害的目标。法术威力会提高伤害和击退距离。","Calls the attention of trickster spirits. While it holds, the spirits will follow up on the caster's attacks. If the spell overcomes victims' willpower, they will suffer minor damage and be drained by the sprites' playful malice.":"唤起顽劣之灵的留意。效果还在持续时，顽劣之灵会跟进施法者的攻击。 如果这个法术击垮了受害者的意志力， 他们将受到轻微伤害，并会被灵体顽皮的恶意衰竭。","Fae assistance is fickle, however; they cannot be beckoned unless a susceptible victim is visible, and will depart rapidly once no more remain. Calling on the fae also reduces the caster's own willpower for a time.":"然而，灵体的援助是反复无常的；除非看到了易受影响的受害者， 否则无法呼唤他们，而且一旦没有其他受害者，它们就会迅速消散。 呼唤灵体也会在一段时间内降低施法者自身的意志力。","Calls the attention of trickster spirits. While it holds, the spirits will follow up on the caster's attacks. If the spell overcomes victims' willpower, they will suffer minor damage and be drained by the sprites' playful malice. Fae assistance is fickle, however; they cannot be beckoned unless a susceptible victim is visible, and will depart rapidly once no more remain. Calling on the fae also reduces the caster's own willpower for a time.":"唤起顽劣之灵的留意。效果还在持续时，顽劣之灵会跟进施法者的攻击。 如果这个法术击垮了受害者的意志力， 他们将受到轻微伤害，并会被灵体顽皮的恶意衰竭。 然而，灵体的援助是反复无常的；除非看到了易受影响的受害者， 否则无法呼唤他们，而且一旦没有其他受害者，它们就会迅速消散。 呼唤灵体也会在一段时间内降低施法者自身的意志力。","Brings forth a cloud of volatile blastmotes around the caster. These explode on contact with open flame or with creatures - including any caster foolish enough to linger in them! The explosion is concussive, knocking adjacent creatures away. Damage done rises with the spell's power.":"在施法者周围生成一团不稳定的爆炸粉尘云。 这些物质在接触明火或生物时会爆炸——包括任何愚蠢到还在其中逗留的施法者！ 震荡爆炸会将相邻生物推开。所造成的伤害随法术威力增强而增加。","Liquefies the ground around the caster, making it difficult to move through. Any movement through liquefied ground will be slowed, and creatures stuck in the liquefied ground will be unable to fly. Attempts to attack the caster in melee may fail.":"这道法术让施法者身边的地面液化，使地面变得难以通行。 在液化地面的任何移动都将减慢，被困在液化地面上的生物将无法飞行。 近战攻击施法者的尝试可能会失败。","The effect starts out with a radius depending on power, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the caster, before it times out. Maintaining the connection to the ground slows the caster's movement, even if they are flying.":"起始的生效范围的半径取决于法术威力，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者， 直到完全失效。维持着与大地的连接会减慢施法者的移动速度，即使他们正在飞行。","Liquefies the ground around the caster, making it difficult to move through. Any movement through liquefied ground will be slowed, and creatures stuck in the liquefied ground will be unable to fly. Attempts to attack the caster in melee may fail. The effect starts out with a radius depending on power, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the caster, before it times out. Maintaining the connection to the ground slows the caster's movement, even if they are flying.":"这道法术让施法者身边的地面液化，使地面变得难以通行。 在液化地面的任何移动都将减慢，被困在液化地面上的生物将无法飞行。 近战攻击施法者的尝试可能会失败。 起始的生效范围的半径取决于法术威力，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者， 直到完全失效。维持着与大地的连接会减慢施法者的移动速度，即使他们正在飞行。","Fragments a wall or a suitably brittle visible monster into an explosion of deadly shrapnel. It can be used on monsters made of ice, bone, or any wall-like substance, as well as those turned to stone by petrification. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.":"将一堵墙或一个可见的易碎怪物炸成致命的碎片。 这适用于由冰、骨或任何壁状物质构成的怪物， 也可以用在那些被石化成石头的怪物。防具可以大大削弱其造成的伤害。","Targets made from rock, stone, ice or bone will cause a small explosion. Metal targets will cause a small but more damaging explosion, and targets made from crystal will cause a large and more damaging explosion.":"由岩石、冰或骨构成的目标会引起小爆炸。 金属目标会引起一个范围小却更具有破坏性的爆炸， 而水晶目标会引起一个范围大而更具有破坏性的爆炸。","Fragments a wall or a suitably brittle visible monster into an explosion of deadly shrapnel. It can be used on monsters made of ice, bone, or any wall-like substance, as well as those turned to stone by petrification. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour. Targets made from rock, stone, ice or bone will cause a small explosion. Metal targets will cause a small but more damaging explosion, and targets made from crystal will cause a large and more damaging explosion.":"将一堵墙或一个可见的易碎怪物炸成致命的碎片。 这适用于由冰、骨或任何壁状物质构成的怪物， 也可以用在那些被石化成石头的怪物。防具可以大大削弱其造成的伤害。 由岩石、冰或骨构成的目标会引起小爆炸。 金属目标会引起一个范围小却更具有破坏性的爆炸， 而水晶目标会引起一个范围大而更具有破坏性的爆炸。","Conjures two explosive magical effects in instant succession. The effects can be any mix of Fireball, Iceblast, and Ghostly Fireball.":"立刻连续产生两个爆炸魔法效果。效果会是火球、冰爆和鬼火球的任意组合。","Hurls a lethally sharp shard of crystal.":"掷出一枚致命而锋利的水晶碎片。","Beckons the target forward, attempting to place them adjacent to the caster.":"将目标引来，试图让他们靠近施法者。","Fires a mighty bolt of lightning. Its damage bypasses half of defenders' armour, and it can be bounced off walls to hit targets twice.":"发射一道强大的闪电箭。防御者的防具无法抵御它造成的一半伤害。 它可以从墙壁上弹回，击中目标两次。","Fires a small bolt of magical energy which never misses.":"这道法术射出一支小魔法射弹，该法术百发百中。","Shoots a random harmful beam or explosion at the targeted creature.":"向目标生物射出随机的有害射束或爆炸。","Heals a large amount of damage to the caster's body.":"治疗施法者身体所受的大量伤害。","Tears a gash in reality, creating a self-sustained but temporary portal to an unknown, tainted otherworld. It requires open space to succeed. After a short time, a powerful clawed tentacle will reach through the portal, remaining bound to the caster's will for a duration depending on power. With the portal's expiry, the tentacle will be severed and turn on the caster. The duration of the portal increases with spell power.":"这道法术能在现实世界中撕开一道裂口， 创造出一座能暂时自我维系、通往某个未知且污秽异界的传送门。 该法术需要开阔的空间才能成功。 片刻之后，一条强大的长有爪子的触手将穿过传送门， 在一段时间内会受施法者的意志所制约，其持续时间取决于法术威力。 随着传送门的失效，触手将被切断并转而攻击施法者。 传送门的持续时间随法术威力的增强而增加。","Drains life from an enemy, healing nearby allies in the process.":"吸取一个敌人的生命，同时治疗附近的盟友。","Bestows a mutation on a target. The mutation is almost always harmful. It cannot affect artificial beings, and the undead will decompose if affected.":"让一个目标发生一次变异。这种变异几乎总是有害的。 它不会影响人造物；亡灵若受到影响则会腐朽。","Warps space into paradoxical configurations to strike many visible foes with one melee attack. Power increases the number of foes attacked with one cast, though unarmed attacks strike only half as many targets at once, as additional care must be taken when warping one's own limbs.":"将空间扭曲成反常结构，以一次近战攻击同时打击多个可见敌人。 法术威力越高，单次施法攻击的敌人越多；徒手攻击一次只能打击一半数量， 因为扭曲自己的肢体需要格外谨慎。","The time taken for the attack is exactly the same as a normal melee attack. Attacks performed this way never miss, but the exact spot struck cannot be controlled precisely, making them unable to do extra damage against unsuspecting foes.":"攻击耗时与普通近战攻击完全相同。这类攻击绝不会落空， 但无法精确控制命中位置，因此不能对毫无戒备的敌人造成额外伤害。","Warps space into paradoxical configurations to strike many visible foes with one melee attack. Power increases the number of foes attacked with one cast, though unarmed attacks strike only half as many targets at once, as additional care must be taken when warping one's own limbs. The time taken for the attack is exactly the same as a normal melee attack. Attacks performed this way never miss, but the exact spot struck cannot be controlled precisely, making them unable to do extra damage against unsuspecting foes.":"将空间扭曲成反常结构，以一次近战攻击同时打击多个可见敌人。 法术威力越高，单次施法攻击的敌人越多；徒手攻击一次只能打击一半数量， 因为扭曲自己的肢体需要格外谨慎。 攻击耗时与普通近战攻击完全相同。这类攻击绝不会落空， 但无法精确控制命中位置，因此不能对毫无戒备的敌人造成额外伤害。","Weaves illusions of the caster. Such illusions have the same physical prowess as the original, and can cast the same spells.":"编织出施法者的幻象。这些幻象拥有与本体相同的物理战斗能力，也能施放相同的法术。","Conjures a stream of stolen suffering, leaving clouds of excruciating misery in its wake and around its targets. These clouds of negative energy will rapidly drain the living of small fractions of their maximum health.":"生成一股窃取的痛苦之流，它的尾迹和目标周围会留下郁积愁云。 这些负能量云会迅速使受害者流失与最大生命值成比例的生命值。","Conjures two balls of burning swamp gas adjacent to the caster. The balls will rapidly seek the nearest monster and burn them. Wizards attempted to copy this with the spell 'Foxfire', but their version is much less powerful.":"在施法者附近生成两个燃烧的沼气球。球会迅速寻找最近的怪物并灼烧它们。 巫师试着将其仿制为“狐火”，但他们的版本的威力要小得多。","Beckons forth the soul of a long-dead martyr to shield your allies for a time. This soul suffers a portion of the damage your allies would otherwise receive.":"召唤一个早已死去的殉道者的灵魂来保护你的盟友一段时间。 这个灵魂将分担你的盟友原本会受到的伤害。","If it is slain (again!), it will transform into a flayed ghost, inflicting illusory wounds on foes. Such wounds are fleeting, and will disappear when the ghost departs - unless you kill its victims first.":"如果它被杀（再次！），它将变成一个剥皮鬼，会对敌人造成虚幻的创伤。 这样的伤口转瞬即逝，当鬼魂离开时就会消退——除非你能先杀死它的受害者。","Beckons forth the soul of a long-dead martyr to shield your allies for a time. This soul suffers a portion of the damage your allies would otherwise receive. If it is slain (again!), it will transform into a flayed ghost, inflicting illusory wounds on foes. Such wounds are fleeting, and will disappear when the ghost departs - unless you kill its victims first.":"召唤一个早已死去的殉道者的灵魂来保护你的盟友一段时间。 这个灵魂将分担你的盟友原本会受到的伤害。 如果它被杀（再次！），它将变成一个剥皮鬼，会对敌人造成虚幻的创伤。 这样的伤口转瞬即逝，当鬼魂离开时就会消退——除非你能先杀死它的受害者。","Causes confusion in all who gaze upon the caster.":"让所有注视着施法者的人陷入混乱之中。","Gradually builds up electric charge in the caster, so long as they maintain focus (by waiting in place and not taking any other actions). When a threshold is reached, the charge couples with the nearest foe, vaporising them instantly. Higher spell power will allow the caster to accumulate charge more rapidly. The spell requires a visible target to begin accumulating charge, though a different foe may be targeted when the charge is released.":"只要施法者保持专注（原地等待且不采取任何其他行动），体内就会逐渐积累电荷。 达到阈值后，电荷会与最近的敌人耦合，立即将其蒸发。法术威力越高， 积累电荷的速度越快。开始积累电荷时需要一个可见目标，但释放电荷时 可能会选中另一个敌人。","Conjures a fragile flask that explodes into short-lived clouds of noxious fumes. These clouds may cause confusion in any creature not resistant to poison. Tougher, more experienced creatures are less likely to be affected.":"召出一个脆弱的瓶子，瓶子爆炸后形成一团短暂存在的有害烟雾。 烟雾可能使任何没有毒抗的生物陷入混乱。 越坚韧、经验等级越高的生物越不容易受影响。","Attempts to entrance all enemies in sight. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the caster, while other creatures will become dazed outright.":"尝试迷住视野内所有敌人。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离施法者， 其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。","Attempts to entrance all enemies in sight. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the caster, while other creatures will become dazed outright. Leaving the caster's line of sight will end the movement-controlling effect.":"尝试迷住视野内所有敌人。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离施法者， 其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。 离开施法者视野会结束控制移动的效果。","Lowers the metabolic rate of every creature in the caster's vicinity, slowing all those who are not resistant to cold. Cold-blooded creatures will be affected much more strongly, and tougher creatures will be slowed for a shorter time.":"降低施法者周围所有生物的新陈代谢速率，减慢所有没有寒抗的生物。 冷血生物将受到更强烈的影响，而更强壮的生物会在更短的时间内被减速。","Fires a burst of metal splinters. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.":"射出一连串金属碎片。防具可以大大削弱其造成的伤害。","Creates a large cloud of foul pestilence, poisoning and sometimes slowing any living creatures it touches.":"产生一大团恶臭的瘟疫云，使接触到的活物中毒，有时还会使其减速。","Significantly increases a nearby ally's damage dealt in melee.":"大幅提高一个附近友方造成的近战伤害。","Significantly increases the caster's damage in melee.":"大幅提高施法者造成的近战伤害。","Launches a psychic attack. If it overcomes the victim's willpower, it 'blows their mind' in a violently literal fashion, dealing damage that bypasses their armour entirely. It is useless against mindless creatures.":"发动心灵攻击。若突破受害者的意志力，便会以极其直白而猛烈的方式 “击爆其心智”，造成完全无视护甲的伤害。此法术对无心智生物无效。","Heals a small amount of damage to the caster's body.":"治疗施法者身体所受的少量伤害。","Summons a powerful exotic creature to the caster's aid: either a manticore, a lindwurm, or a sphinx marauder.":"召唤一个强大的异域生物援助施法者：蝎尾狮、林德虫或劫掠斯芬克斯。","Conjures an arrow of elemental mercury which deals direct poison damage to whatever it hits and may also weaken their melee attacks for a short while.":"召出一支由元素汞构成的箭矢，对命中的目标造成直接毒素伤害， 并可能短暂削弱其近战攻击。","The physical force of the arrow inflicts a small amount of damage even to those immune to poison, and the weakening effect can splash to adjacent targets and ignores poison resistance altogether.":"箭矢的冲击力即使对毒素免疫者也会造成少量伤害；削弱效果还可能溅射至相邻目标， 并完全无视毒素抗性。","Conjures an arrow of elemental mercury which deals direct poison damage to whatever it hits and may also weaken their melee attacks for a short while. The physical force of the arrow inflicts a small amount of damage even to those immune to poison, and the weakening effect can splash to adjacent targets and ignores poison resistance altogether.":"召出一支由元素汞构成的箭矢，对命中的目标造成直接毒素伤害， 并可能短暂削弱其近战攻击。 箭矢的冲击力即使对毒素免疫者也会造成少量伤害；削弱效果还可能溅射至相邻目标， 并完全无视毒素抗性。","Exhales a stream of forgotten grief, leaving clouds of excruciating misery in its wake but skipping past creatures that would be vulnerable to it. These clouds of negative energy will rapidly drain the living of small fractions of their maximum health.":"呼出一股被遗忘的悲伤之流，它的尾迹会留下郁积愁云， 但会跳过那些容易受到它影响的生物。 这些负能量云会迅速使受害者流失与最大生命值成比例的生命值。","Magically accelerates the decay of damaged living tissue, causing great clouds of miasma to billow forth from a targeted victim's wounds over several turns which may slow and heavily poison any living creature who stands in them. Air currents will prevent this pestilence from forming wherever the caster is standing, but they are not otherwise protected from its effects.":"以魔法加速受损活体组织的腐败，使大量瘴气在数回合内从目标的伤口中涌出。 任何站在其中的活物都可能被减速并身中剧毒。 气流会阻止瘴气在施法者站立处形成，但除此之外，施法者并不免疫其效果。","This spell may only be cast on a living creature who is at least heavily wounded, and channelling such necrotic energies will leave the caster's own health temporarily drained (though spellpower will reduce the intensity of this side-effect).":"此法术只能以至少已身受重伤的活物为目标。 引导这种死灵能量会暂时汲取施法者自身的生命， 但法术威力越高，这项副作用就越轻。","Magically accelerates the decay of damaged living tissue, causing great clouds of miasma to billow forth from a targeted victim's wounds over several turns which may slow and heavily poison any living creature who stands in them. Air currents will prevent this pestilence from forming wherever the caster is standing, but they are not otherwise protected from its effects. This spell may only be cast on a living creature who is at least heavily wounded, and channelling such necrotic energies will leave the caster's own health temporarily drained (though spellpower will reduce the intensity of this side-effect).":"以魔法加速受损活体组织的腐败，使大量瘴气在数回合内从目标的伤口中涌出。 任何站在其中的活物都可能被减速并身中剧毒。 气流会阻止瘴气在施法者站立处形成，但除此之外，施法者并不免疫其效果。 此法术只能以至少已身受重伤的活物为目标。 引导这种死灵能量会暂时汲取施法者自身的生命， 但法术威力越高，这项副作用就越轻。","Creates a large cloud of noxious fumes, which may cause confusion.":"产生大量有毒烟雾，这可能会引起混乱。","Causes the caster to radiate toxic energy, continuously inflicting poison on everything in line of sight for as long as the spell lasts.":"施法者放出毒能量，在法术持续期间不断毒害视线内的所有生物。","Conjures an orb made of pure destructive magic. Compared to most other projectiles, these orbs travel at a relatively slow pace. The orbs home onto their targets, yet because of their huge inertia, especially agile opponents may be able to outmanoeuvre them. The orbs need some time to stabilise, and a nascent orb will deal reduced damage.":"生成一个毁灭性的纯魔力球。比起其他的发射物，这种能量球的飞行速度相对较慢。 能量球会自动追踪目标，但因为它们的惯性太强， 因此特别敏捷的对手可能会躲开它们。 球体需要一段时间来稳定，新生的能量球无法发挥出全部的伤害潜力。","Residents of the dungeon are able to maintain the orb until it impacts a target, but when cast by you the orb will dissipate upon leaving your line of sight.":"地牢的居民可以在它撞到目标前一直维持着球体，但你在施放时， 球体在离开你的视线时就会消散。","Conjures an orb made of pure destructive magic. Compared to most other projectiles, these orbs travel at a relatively slow pace. The orbs home onto their targets, yet because of their huge inertia, especially agile opponents may be able to outmanoeuvre them. The orbs need some time to stabilise, and a nascent orb will deal reduced damage. Residents of the dungeon are able to maintain the orb until it impacts a target, but when cast by you the orb will dissipate upon leaving your line of sight.":"生成一个毁灭性的纯魔力球。比起其他的发射物，这种能量球的飞行速度相对较慢。 能量球会自动追踪目标，但因为它们的惯性太强， 因此特别敏捷的对手可能会躲开它们。 球体需要一段时间来稳定，新生的能量球无法发挥出全部的伤害潜力。 地牢的居民可以在它撞到目标前一直维持着球体，但你在施放时， 球体在离开你的视线时就会消散。","Hurls a crackling orb of electrical energy, creating a huge explosion on impact. Its damage bypasses half of defenders' armour.":"掷出噼啪作响的电能量球，在撞击时产生巨大爆炸。 防御者的防具无法抵御它造成的一半伤害。","Envelops the caster's body in a protective layer of thick ice, granting a substantial bonus to armour as long as they remain in their current location. The ice will crack and fall away if the caster moves to a new position. The spell decreases in effectiveness in heavier armour, granting a lower bonus the higher the encumbrance rating of the caster's armour.":"在施法者的身体上覆一层厚的冰，只要他们呆在现在的位置，就有大量的防御加成。 如果施法者移动到新位置，冰会破裂、脱落。 该法术对重甲效果变弱，施法者的护甲的负担等级越高，加成越低。","Turns the air bitterly cold, freezing all other creatures in line of sight. This is less effective against creatures packed tightly together - those adjacent to their allies will be partly insulated from the cold, taking less damage.":"使空气变得非常寒冷，冻结视线中的所有其他生物。 这对紧密聚在一起的生物效果较差—— 一些与其他生物相邻的生物会部分地隔绝于寒冷，受到的伤害较小。","Inflicts an extremely painful injury upon one living creature.":"让一个活物遭受极其痛苦的伤害。","Prevents a creature from taking any action for a short time.":"让一个生物短期无法做出任何行动。","Irresistibly prevents a creature from taking any action for a short time, requiring multiple charges but not line of fire.":"不可抵抗地使一个生物短时间无法采取任何行动。该凝视需要多次充能， 但只需视线，无需直达射线。","Opens two gateways (one always near the caster), which allow instantaneous transport to random other open gateways to any creature entering them. There is no limit to the number of gateways that can be open at one time. However, gateways close a short time after being opened, or immediately once entered.":"这道法术开启两扇传送门（其中一扇总是出现在施法者附近）； 任何走进传送门的生物都会被随机传送到另一个打开着的传送门。 同一时间可以打开的传送门数量并没有限制。 但是，传送门在打开后会短时间内关闭，或是一旦进入就立刻关闭。","Allows the caster to travel a short distance through an adjacent rock wall and emerge again on the other side. This spell takes an unusally long time to cast, during which the caster will be unable to act, but also gain increased armour from their attunement to the rock.":"施法者可以穿过相邻的岩墙行进一小段距离，然后重新出现在另一边。 施展此法术所需时间格外漫长；在此期间施法者无法行动， 但也会因与岩石调谐而获得更高护甲。","Petrifies a targeted creature and up to two other foes in a chain. Those which do not muster the Will to resist are briefly slowed, and then turned to stone. Until they return to flesh, they are unable to act, but also take half damage. The spell's power is lessened against secondary targets.":"石化一个目标生物和最多与之相连的两个生物。 那些意志力不足以抵抗该法术的生物会暂时变慢，然后变成石头。在他们恢复肉身前， 他们无法行动，但受到的伤害会减半。该法术对次级目标的威力会减弱。","Exhales calcifying dust, which petrifies anyone affected for longer than a brief moment.":"呼出一股钙化尘雾。任何受其影响超过片刻的生物都会被石化。","Creates a phantom copy of a creature. The copy will be somewhat fragile, but otherwise almost indistinguishable from the original.":"创造一个怪物的幻影复制体。复制体会较为脆弱，但除此之外几乎与原体无异。","Summons some of the greater threats from one of the Pits of Slime, the Elven Halls, the Vaults, the Crypt, the Tomb of Ancients, or the Realm of Zot; the specific branch varies with each cast of the spell.":"从黏液坑洞、精灵殿堂、宝库、墓室、远古坟冢或佐特领域之一 召唤强大威胁；每次施法选择的分支都可能不同。","Fires a penetrating beam of plasma at one of the caster's most distant foes. The ionised beam bypasses half of defenders' armour, and a second beam of fire follows in its wake.":"向施法者最远的一个敌人发射穿透性的等离子束。 电离束会无视目标一半的护甲，随后沿同一路径射出一道火焰束。","Fires a magical arrow coated with the most vile and noxious toxin. Even those resistant to poison will be poisoned by it, and a small portion of its direct damage bypasses poison resistance.":"射出一支裹着剧毒的魔法箭。即使具有毒素抗性的目标也会中毒； 该箭造成的少量直接伤害还会无视毒素抗性。","Conjures forth a great cloud of lethal gases.":"生成一大团致命的毒云。","Turns the air around the caster into a freezing vortex, doing tremendous damage to everyone caught in it that can only be half-mitigated by resistance to cold. Those affected will also be swept up into the air and tossed around. Only the eye of the storm is a safe place, and it follows the caster. The vortex is unable to follow the caster through long-distance translocations. The spell's effectiveness is greatly diminished in closed areas. After the vortex fades, it cannot be called forth again for a short time.":"将施法者周围的空气变成一个冰冻的旋涡，对卷入其中的生物造成巨大伤害， 寒冷抗性最多只能减免其中一半。受影响的生物还会被卷到空中并抛来抛去。 只有风暴眼是安全的，并且它还会跟随施法者。 但施法者进行长距离传送后，这个旋涡无法继续跟随。 在封闭区域，该法术的效果会大大降低。旋涡消散后，短时间内无法再次施展它。","Randomly alters the form of a creature. It is especially effective against shape-changing creatures.":"随机改变一个生物的外形。该法术对会变换形态的生物尤其有效。","Transforms the target into a pig. The target moves swiftly but cannot cast spells. The caster's demise will cause the transformation to end.":"将目标变为猪。目标的移动变得迅捷，但无法施法。施法者一死，变形就会结束。","Teleports a fired or thrown missile at a targeted enemy.":"向一个目标敌人传送一个投射的弹药。","Conjures a torrent of water that may knock back the target, and creates a pool of shallow water for a short duration.":"召出一股激流，可能将目标击退，并在短时间内形成一滩浅水。","Launches a glob of liquid fire that clings to a targeted creature, dealing armour-ignoring fire damage over multiple turns. The victim can put the fire out much more quickly by moving.":"向目标生物发射一团会附着其身的液态火焰，在数个回合内造成无视护甲的火焰伤害。 目标移动时能更快扑灭火焰。","If the target is insubstantial, the liquid fire will fail to stick.":"如果目标没有实体，液态火焰便无法附着。","Launches a glob of liquid fire that clings to a targeted creature, dealing armour-ignoring fire damage over multiple turns. The victim can put the fire out much more quickly by moving. If the target is insubstantial, the liquid fire will fail to stick.":"向目标生物发射一团会附着其身的液态火焰，在数个回合内造成无视护甲的火焰伤害。 目标移动时能更快扑灭火焰。 若目标没有实体，液态火焰便无法附着。","Draws searing flames from lava. Any enemies of the caster standing next to or above lava will be burned.":"从熔岩中引出灼热的火焰。任何站在熔岩旁边或上方的施法者的敌人都会被灼烧。","Calls a surge of power from the earth, striking an enemy within the caster's sight. The spell cascades through nearby constructs, growing in strength with each one standing near the target.":"召唤一股来自大地的力量，攻击施法者视线内的敌人。 法术将附近的造物串联起来，每有一个造物在目标附近就会增强力量。","Roll into a ball, granting the boulder beetle tremendous speed as well as double melee damage. The roll may only be performed when at distance from a foe, and the beetle will always unroll after an attempted roll attack.":"滚成一个球，给予巨砾甲虫巨大的速度以及双倍的近战攻击力。 只有在与敌人有一定距离时才能进行翻滚， 并且甲虫在进行滚动攻击后总会展开身体。","Blasts a target with high-velocity rock shards. Gathering the rock from ambient grit is slow, making this spell take one-and-a-half times as long to cast as most. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.":"将一些小碎石以极高的速度射向目标。因为从周围环境中获得岩石的速度很慢， 使得这个法术的施法时间多出大多数法术的一半。防具可以大大削弱其造成的伤害。","Taints a targeted creature's ability to cast spells. Casting a spell while afflicted with this condition causes the target to lose access to their magic, briefly preventing them from casting any further spells.":"腐化目标生物的施法能力。受此状态影响时施放法术， 会使目标暂时失去魔法，短时间内无法继续施法。","Scorches a random foe. Those injured by this have their resistance to fire burned away for a short time.":"灼烧一个随机敌人。受此伤害的会在短时间内失去火抗。","Forms icy simulacra of an adjacent living, demonic, or holy creature. These fragile doppelgangers will take shape over a short period of time, eventually gaining the ability to move and attack the caster's enemies.":"生成以相邻的活物、恶魔或神圣生物为原型的冰制拟像。 这些脆弱的替身将在短时间内成型，最终获得移动和攻击施法者敌人的能力。","The good gods frown on this spell, as it works blood and ichor into unnatural facsimiles.":"善神不喜欢这个法术，因为它能把血和灵液变成不自然的赝品。","You can maintain up to 5 simulacra simultaneously.":"你最多可以同时维系 5 个拟像。","Forms icy simulacra of an adjacent living, demonic, or holy creature. These fragile doppelgangers will take shape over a short period of time, eventually gaining the ability to move and attack the caster's enemies. The good gods frown on this spell, as it works blood and ichor into unnatural facsimiles. You can maintain up to 5 simulacra simultaneously.":"生成以相邻的活物、恶魔或神圣生物为原型的冰制拟像。 这些脆弱的替身将在短时间内成型，最终获得移动和攻击施法者敌人的能力。 善神不喜欢这个法术，因为它能把血和灵液变成不自然的赝品。 你最多可以同时维系 5 个拟像。","Imparts seals on nearby doors and stairs, preventing those not allied with the caster from traversing them.":"封印附近的门和楼梯，阻止不属于施法者盟友的生物通过。","Fires a continuous piercing ray of arcane energy from the caster's hands. So long as the caster maintains focus upon the spell and supplies it with magical power (by waiting in place and not taking any other actions), the ray will follow the caster's target if it should move.":"从施法者的手中射出一束持续的穿透性奥术能量射线。 如果施法者保持专注，并为法术提供魔力（通过原地等待而不采取任何其他行动）， 射线将会追踪施法者的目标。","Breathes a blast of fire at a targeted creature, leaving a cloud of flames at the endpoint.":"向一个目标生物喷吐火焰气流，在终点留下一团火焰云。","Violently collapses a nearby simulacrum into a large mass of ice, which explodes on impact. The ice affects even cold-resistant creatures somewhat, due to the strong impact and cutting edges.":"猛烈地将附近的一个拟像崩成大冰块，它会在轰然倒塌时爆炸。 由于强大的冲击和切削，它造成的一半伤害无视寒冰抗性。","Creates replicas of creatures native to the caster's current location, weaving them from shadows and threads of Abyssal matter.":"创造施法者当前地域原生生物的复制品，以暗影和深渊物质的丝线将其编织成形。","Fires a shard of hardened shadow at a single enemy.":"向单个敌人射出一枚硬化的暗影碎片。","Causes an enormous burst of concussive force around the caster, dealing severe damage to all nearby creatures. It is especially effective against those made from ice, bone, or any wall-like substance (such as rock, metal or crystal), as well as those turned to stone by petrification. It is less effective against flying, gelatinous and insubstantial creatures. It may also destroy nearby walls.":"这道法术让施法者身边爆发出一道巨大的冲击力，对附近所有生物造成严重伤害。 它对那些由冰、骨或任何壁状物质构成的怪物尤为有效， 以及在那些被石化成石头的怪物。它对飞行、凝胶状和非实体生物的效果较差。 它可能会摧毁周围墙壁。","Summons weapons from far and wide - a dagger newly forged, a sword long-rusted in a moldering tomb, an axe still steaming with the blood of its victim - animating them and sending them out to attack.":"从四面八方召唤武器——一把新锻造的匕首，一把在腐朽的坟墓中生锈已久的剑， 一把仍在蒸腾着受害者热血的斧头——激活它们并派它们出击。","Throws a bouncing bolt of electricity. It bypasses half of defenders' armour.":"发射一道会反弹的电击束；造成的伤害有一半无视目标护甲。","Creates two sigils nearby. Anyone who passes over them will be bound, able to act and dodge normally but unable to move away. When the effect wears off, their movement speed will rebound, giving them temporary swiftness. Swiftness from any source grants immunity to binding.":"在附近创造两个印记。任何经过它们的人都会被束缚，可以行动和闪避，但无法移动。 当效果消失时，移动速度会回升，暂时使他们变得迅捷。 从任何来源获取的迅捷属性都能免疫束缚。","Only one set of sigils can be maintained at a time, and they will expire prematurely if they leave your sight.":"一次只能维护一组印记，而且如果它们离开你的视线，就会提前失效。","Creates two sigils nearby. Anyone who passes over them will be bound, able to act and dodge normally but unable to move away. When the effect wears off, their movement speed will rebound, giving them temporary swiftness. Swiftness from any source grants immunity to binding. Only one set of sigils can be maintained at a time, and they will expire prematurely if they leave your sight.":"在附近创造两个印记。任何经过它们的人都会被束缚，可以行动和闪避，但无法移动。 当效果消失时，移动速度会回升，暂时使他们变得迅捷。 从任何来源获取的迅捷属性都能免疫束缚。 一次只能维护一组印记，而且如果它们离开你的视线，就会提前失效。","Eliminates all sound near the caster. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible in the caster's vicinity.":"消除施法者附近的所有声音。 这使得无法在施法者附近阅读卷轴、施放法术、祈求神力或喊叫。","The effect starts out with a radius depending on power, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the caster, before it times out.":"起始的生效范围的半径取决于法术威力，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者， 直到完全失效。","Eliminates all sound near the caster. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible in the caster's vicinity. Certain monsters have innate magical or special abilities which will still be usable while silenced. The effect starts out with a radius depending on power, which will then shrink, eventually covering only the caster, before it times out.":"消除施法者附近的所有声音。 这使得无法在施法者附近阅读卷轴、施放法术、祈求神力或喊叫。 某些怪物具有与生俱来的魔法或特殊能力，即使被沉默也能使用。 起始的生效范围的半径取决于法术威力，然后会缩小，最后只覆盖施法者， 直到完全失效。","Sings a haunting song that mesmerises nearby listeners. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the singer, while other creatures will become dazed outright.":"唱出萦绕心头的歌，迷住附近听众。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离歌者， 其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。","Sings a haunting song that mesmerises nearby listeners. Adventurers who fail to resist will become unable to move away from the singer, while other creatures will become dazed outright. Leaving the caster's line of sight will end the movement-controlling effect.":"唱出萦绕心头的歌，迷住附近听众。未能抵抗的冒险者会无法远离歌者， 其他生物则会直接陷入眩晕。 离开施法者视野会结束控制移动的效果。","Puts a targeted creature to sleep. Taking damage will typically wake the target, and loud sounds can potentially do so as well.":"使一个目标生物沉睡。对目标造成伤害会将其唤醒， 如果发出巨大响声，也可能会这样。","Slows the actions of a creature.":"减慢一个生物的行动。","Fires a sharp dart of hardened chitin.":"射出一个坚硬甲壳质的锋利飞镖。","Smites any targeted enemy within sight, with no direct line of fire required.":"惩击视线内的指定敌人，无需直射路径。","Extends large tentacles to attack nearby enemies.":"伸出巨大的触手攻击附近的敌人。","Creates a cloud of spectral mist, dealing minor damage to all creatures other than the undead. Dangerous but short-lived spectral undead creatures will coalesce from the mist over time.":"制造一团幽灵迷雾云，对亡灵以外的所有生物造成轻微伤害。 随时间的推移，危险但短暂存在的幽灵亡灵生物将从迷雾中聚合。","Constructs a metallic servant with a spark of the caster's own arcane knowledge at its core. This spark allows the servitor to unleash some of the destructive spells known to its creator, though the strongest and most volatile of magics cannot be imbued in this fashion. The strength of the servitor increases with spell power.":"构造一个金属仆从，以施法者自身奥术知识的火花为核心。 它能施放创造者掌握的部分破坏性法术，但无法灌注最强大、最不稳定的魔法。 仆从的力量随法术威力提高。","(While you know this spell, you may choose which of your eligible spells it will cast with the Imbue Servitor ability.)":"（掌握此法术时，可通过“灌注仆从”能力选择它施放的合格法术。）","Constructs a metallic servant with a spark of the caster's own arcane knowledge at its core. This spark allows the servitor to unleash some of the destructive spells known to its creator, though the strongest and most volatile of magics cannot be imbued in this fashion. The strength of the servitor increases with spell power. (While you know this spell, you may choose which of your eligible spells it will cast with the Imbue Servitor ability.)":"构造一个金属仆从，以施法者自身奥术知识的火花为核心。 它能施放创造者掌握的部分破坏性法术，但无法灌注最强大、最不稳定的魔法。 仆从的力量随法术威力提高。 （掌握此法术时，可通过“灌注仆从”能力选择它施放的合格法术。）","Spits acid at a targeted creature.":"向一个目标生物喷吐酸液。","Spits lava at a targeted creature. Half of its damage bypasses fire resistance.":"向一个目标生物喷吐岩浆；造成的伤害有一半无视火焰抗性。","<Spit Poison ability>":"<Spit Poison ability>","Fires a burst of wooden splinters. Its damage is strongly reduced by armour.":"射出一连串木头碎片。防具可以大大削弱其造成的伤害。","Releases a fast, gas-filled floating spore. After seeking out its foe, the spore will explode, damaging anything caught in the blast and further confusing living creatures.":"释放一个快速移动、充满气体的浮游孢子。找到敌人后，孢子会爆炸， 伤害爆炸范围内的一切，并额外使活物陷入混乱。","Releases penetrating bolts of fire from the caster in every direction.":"从施法者向各个方向射出穿透性的烈火束。","Releases electrical charges against those next to the caster. These may arc to other adjacent creatures, or back to the caster, before eventually grounding out. It deals reduced damage when arcing to the caster, and the damage dealt bypasses half of defenders' armour.":"向施法者身边的生物释放出几股电流。 这些电流会作弧形运动，攻击到周围生物，或返给施法者，直到最后接地被导开。 电弧返回施法者时造成的伤害较低；造成的伤害有一半无视目标护甲。","Throws a ball of hot steam towards a targeted creature.":"向一个目标生物投射蒸汽球。","Unleashes a short-ranged spray of incendiary goo that clings to an adjacent creature and deals armour-ignoring fire damage over several turns. If the victim is allowed to move, it will put out the fire prematurely.":"释放一股短程的粘性燃烧物质，它会附着在邻近的生物身上， 并在几个回合内造成无视护甲的火焰伤害。如果受害者能够移动，他会更快地将火扑灭。","Unleashes a short-ranged spray of incendiary goo that clings to an adjacent creature and deals armour-ignoring fire damage over several turns. If the victim is allowed to move, it will put out the fire prematurely. If the target is insubstantial, the liquid fire will fail to stick.":"释放一股短程的粘性燃烧物质，它会附着在邻近的生物身上， 并在几个回合内造成无视护甲的火焰伤害。如果受害者能够移动，他会更快地将火扑灭。 如果目标没有实体，液态火焰便无法附着。","Brings the air into unnatural stillness across a huge area, preventing anything short of a polar vortex from breaking the calm. The effect takes concentration to maintain, and only lasts a short time; if the caster is killed, clouds will begin to form again as normal.":"使空气在一大片区域内进入反常的静止状态， 防止除极地旋涡之外的任何事物破坏平静。 该效果需要集中注意力才能维持，且只能持续很短的时间； 如果施法者被杀死，则云会重新正常形成。","Conjures a jagged shard of crystallised toxins. The stinger's impact will always poison a susceptible target. Even resistant targets have a chance to be poisoned and immune monsters will still be damaged by the physical impact of the stinger.":"生成一个锯齿状的结晶毒素碎片。毒刺的冲击总是会让易感目标中毒。 即使是有毒抗的目标也有可能中毒，免疫毒的怪物也会受到毒刺的物理冲击。","Adds malice to hellish fires, binding it with flame into a creeping inferno.":"为地狱之火添加恶意，与火焰结合成蔓延的毁灭性的大火。","Fires a sharp spine of rock.":"射出一根尖锐的岩刺。","Greatly reduces the target's willpower, making them more vulnerable to a variety of magical effects.":"大大削弱目标的意志力，使其更容易受到各种魔法效果的影响。","Fires a weak electrical burst which, on impact, causes very brief paralysis. Willpower is of no use against this effect, but resistance to electricity can sometimes prevent it.":"发出微弱的电脉冲，撞击时会造成短暂的麻痹。 意志力对抵抗这种影响毫无用处，但电抗有时可以阻止它的影响。","Converts some of the caster's blood into magical energy. The process is painful but never directly lethal. The efficiency of the conversion increases with the spell's power.":"将施法者的部分血液转化为魔法能量。这个过程是痛苦的，但绝不会直接致命。 转换的效率随法术威力增强而增加。","Summons one or more air elementals.":"召唤一个或多个气元素。","Summons a warrior from a particularly prickly tribe. Foes that strike these giants in melee are in for a painful surprise! When cast at a higher power, older, more robust warriors will answer the call.":"召唤一名来自格外多刺部落的战士。近战攻击这名巨人的敌人将遭到痛苦反击！ 法术威力越高，响应召唤的战士越老练、强壮。","Opens a gate to the realm of Pandemonium and draws forth one of its inhabitants to serve the caster for a time.":"打开一扇通往万魔殿领域的大门，引出其中一位居民为施法者效劳一段时间。","Summons and binds a powerful dragon to perform the caster's bidding. At high power it may summon particularly deadly varieties of dragon, or multiple lesser dragons at once.":"召唤并束缚一条强大的龙来执行施法者的命令。 当法术威力很高时，便可以召唤特别致命的龙，或者同时召唤多个较弱的龙。","Summons multiple drakes and lindwurms.":"召唤多只幼龙和蛇龙。","Summons one or more earth elementals.":"召唤一个或多个地元素。","Summons multiple noble and monstrous emperor scorpions.":"召唤多只高贵而凶暴的帝王蝎。","Summons multiple Executioners to tear apart foes of the caster.":"召唤多个处刑人撕裂施法者的敌人。","Summons multiple floating eyeballs that may be able to vitrify, polymorph, confuse, mutate or disintegrate.":"召唤多个浮空眼球，它们可能会造成玻化、变形、混乱、变异或碎裂。","Summons one or more fire elementals.":"召唤一个或多个火元素。","Forcefully intersects a forested plane with this world. It requires open space to succeed. While the spell holds, a spirit of the forest will be called forth, and the trees of the forest will be awakened to deal damage to nearby enemies. Spell power increases the duration, size, and thickness of the intersected plane; as well as the strength of the spirit.":"强行将森林位面与这个世界相交。该法术需要开阔的空间才能成功。 当法术生效时，森林之灵会被召唤出来， 森林的树会被唤醒，并对附近的敌人造成伤害。 法术威力能增加位面相交的持续时间、大小和密集程度；灵体的力量也会更强。","Calls forth one of the greater demons of Pandemonium to serve the caster.":"召唤一名万魔殿的高等恶魔为施法者效劳。","Constructs a shell of slag iron around a volatile elemental spark. It is capable of raining down powerful blows on its creator's adversaries - so powerful that the golem itself is often damaged by their impact.":"在一颗不稳定的元素火花外锻造渣铁外壳。 它能像雨点般密集地对创造者的敌人造成打击—— 如此猛烈，以至于魔像本身经常被它们的冲击所损坏。","Only tenuously independent of its creator's magic, the flames within it will rapidly go dormant if the two ever leave each other's side. If its shell is destroyed while the golem is still active, its exposed core will violently detonate a moment later.":"它只能勉强独立于创造者的魔力， 每当两者离开彼此身边，它内部的火焰就会迅速休眠。 如果它的外壳在仍处于活动状态时被摧毁，暴露的核心将在片刻后剧烈爆炸。","It gains greater explosive damage at higher power.":"法术威力越高，它的爆炸伤害就越高。","Constructs a shell of slag iron around a volatile elemental spark. It is capable of raining down powerful blows on its creator's adversaries - so powerful that the golem itself is often damaged by their impact. Only tenuously independent of its creator's magic, the flames within it will rapidly go dormant if the two ever leave each other's side. If its shell is destroyed while the golem is still active, its exposed core will violently detonate a moment later. It gains greater explosive damage at higher power.":"在一颗不稳定的元素火花外锻造渣铁外壳。 它能像雨点般密集地对创造者的敌人造成打击—— 如此猛烈，以至于魔像本身经常被它们的冲击所损坏。 它只能勉强独立于创造者的魔力， 每当两者离开彼此身边，它内部的火焰就会迅速休眠。 如果它的外壳在仍处于活动状态时被摧毁，暴露的核心将在片刻后剧烈爆炸。 法术威力越高，它的爆炸伤害就越高。","Summons a deadly sin beast.":"召唤一只致命的罪孽兽。","Summons a Hell Sentinel, a nightmarish edifice of animated hate.":"召唤一尊地狱哨兵——一座由仇恨驱动的噩梦般建筑。","Calls forth divine warriors to aid the caster.":"召来神圣战士协助施法者。","Opens a gate to the Abyss and calls through two or more hideous abominations from that dreadful place. While powerful, brushing one's mind against the fabric of the Abyss in this manner invites Doom upon the caster and may eventually cost them greatly.":"打开一扇通往深渊的大门，并从那片可怖之地呼来两个或更多畸形的可憎之物。 它们虽强大，但以这种方式让心智触及深渊的本质会使施法者遭受厄运， 最终可能付出惨重代价。","Summons a many-headed hydra to fight alongside the caster for a short time. Spell power determines the number of heads.":"召唤一只多头蛇，在短时间内与施法者并肩战斗。 法术威力决定着头的数量。","Calls forth a beast of ice to serve the caster. The strength of the beast depends on spell power.":"召唤一只冰兽为施法者效劳。野兽的力量取决于法术威力。","Summons a temporary mirror image of an enemy. Such a copy has the same physical prowess as the original, and can cast the same spells.":"召唤一个暂时存在的敌人镜像。 该复制品拥有与本体相同的物理战斗能力，也能施放相同的法术。","Constructs an immobile lightning spire at a nearby location. This spire irregularly discharges bolts of electricity at the caster's foes, prioritizing whichever of them is most distant from it.":"在附近锻造一座无法移动的闪电尖塔。尖塔会不时向施法者的敌人释放电击， 并优先攻击离它最远的敌人。","Summons a violet-scaled serpent whose bite can swiftly drain the magical reserves of nearly any foe. At higher power, the antimagic properties of the viper's bite grow even stronger.":"召唤一条紫鳞魔力毒蛇，其咬击能够迅速削减几乎任何敌人的魔力储备。 法术威力越强，魔力毒蛇咬击的反魔法效果越强。","Summons between one and three minor (rank 5) demons.":"召唤一至三个次级（第 5 阶）恶魔。","Summons wandering mushrooms and deathcaps next to a targeted creature.":"在目标生物附近召唤游走蘑菇和死亡菌。","Calls forth a swarm of death scarabs.":"召唤出一群死亡圣甲虫。","Calls forth a swarm of venomous scorpions.":"召唤出一群毒蝎子。","Summons a rat, bat, or quokka to the caster's aid. Spell power increases the chance of summoning a quokka.":"召唤一只老鼠、蝙蝠或短尾矮袋鼠来协助施法者。 法术威力越强，越有可能召唤出短尾矮袋鼠。","Calls out to the lingering souls of orcs who died in earlier ages, and, for a brief moment, gives them purpose in battle once again. More anchored to their past lives than most spectrals, they wield polearms with living skill, and will encircle their quarry with cold efficiency.":"呼唤远古战死兽人的徘徊灵魂，让它们短暂重拾战斗使命。 这些先锋比多数幽灵更依恋生前，能以生者般的技巧挥舞长柄武器， 并冷酷高效地包围猎物。","Summons one or more spiders.":"召唤一个或多个蜘蛛。","Summons a tzitzimitl, a demon of disease and despair.":"召唤一个齐齐米特尔——传播疾病与绝望的恶魔。","Summons multiple ufetubi; small, annoying demons.":"召唤多个乌菲特布斯；它们是小而恼人的恶魔。","Summons multiple undead monsters, creating various ghosts, vampires, wraiths and other lesser undead.":"召唤多个亡灵怪物，包括各种鬼魂、吸血鬼、幽魂和其他低阶亡灵。","Summons multiple rats, spiders, worms, and frogs.":"召唤多只老鼠、蜘蛛、蠕虫和蛙。","Summons one or more water elementals.":"召唤一个或多个水元素。","Calls forth winds to greatly increase the caster's movement speed. After the effect ends, the caster's movements will be sluggish for a time.":"召唤风以极大地提高施法者的移动速度。效果结束后，施法者的动作会暂时变慢。","Calls on the powers of darkness to cause agonising injury to any living or holy thing in the caster's vicinity, cutting their health in half (partially resisted by negative energy resistance). This damage is never directly lethal.":"召唤黑暗力量，折磨施法者附近的活物和神圣生物，使其生命值减半； 负能量抗性可抵消部分效果。此伤害绝不会直接致命。","Attempts to teleport a targeted creature out of the caster's sight, after a short delay.":"尝试在短暂延迟后将目标生物传送出施法者的视野。","Throws a nearby ally at the monster's foe, doing minimal damage and landing the thrown monster nearby.":"将附近的一名盟友扔向施法怪物的敌人，只造成很少伤害，并让被扔出的怪物 落在目标附近。","Fires a volley of barbs at the target, skewering them and making movement painful.":"向目标射出一阵倒刺，将其刺穿，使其移动时遭受痛苦。","Throws a small puff of flame.":"抛出一小团火焰。","Throws a small puff of frost.":"抛出一小团冰霜。","Fires a shard of ice. Due to its strong impact and cutting edges, half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"射出一枚冰片。由于冲击强烈且边缘锋利，其一半伤害会无视寒冷抗性。","Throws a harmful yet strangely delicious pie that can inflict its victim with a number of irresistible and debilitating temporary effects. These include inducing vertigo, silence, fire vulnerability, fragility, blindness, or an aversion to drinking potions.":"扔出一块有害却出奇美味的派，可能使受击者遭受多种无法抵抗的临时 削弱效果，包括眩晕、沉默、火焰易伤、脆弱、失明或厌恶饮用药水。","Creates an arc of electricity.":"产生一道电弧。","<Trog's Hand ability>":"<Trog's Hand ability>","Conjures forth a fragment of the caster's essence and twists it into a fragment of death, painfully draining the victim. The caster, too, will find their health reduced, until they gain enough experience to recover.":"从施法者的精元中塑出一枚碎片，再将其扭曲为死亡碎片，痛苦地衰竭受击者。 施法者自身的生命值也会降低，直到获得足够的经验值后才会恢复。","Animates the weapon of a targeted foe, ripping it from their hands and causing it to attack them relentlessly. Once the target dies, the weapon will fall to the ground shortly thereafter.":"给一个目标敌人的武器注入生命，它会脱离敌人掌控，倒戈相向。 一旦目标死亡，武器很快就会落地。","Certain powerful named artefacts cannot be animated, and any properties that require skill in evocations will not be active.":"某些强大的有名字的神器不会被影响，任何需要魔力释放技能的属性都不会被激活。","Animates the weapon of a targeted foe, ripping it from their hands and causing it to attack them relentlessly. Once the target dies, the weapon will fall to the ground shortly thereafter. Certain powerful named artefacts cannot be animated, and any properties that require skill in evocations will not be active.":"给一个目标敌人的武器注入生命，它会脱离敌人掌控，倒戈相向。 一旦目标死亡，武器很快就会落地。 某些强大的有名字的神器不会被影响，任何需要魔力释放技能的属性都不会被激活。","Calls on the forces of nature to blast a small area with magma, ice, wind, or rubble.":"呼唤自然力量，用岩浆、冰、风或碎石轰击一小片区域。","Steals the life of an adjacent living creature and grants it to the caster.":"窃取邻近生物的生命并给予施法者。","Fires a penetrating bolt of poison.":"发射一道穿透性的毒箭。","Makes a targeted creature more vulnerable to poison.":"使一个目标生物更易受到毒害。","Blasts a target with energy borrowed from the caster's own future movement. For a short time afterward, the caster will be left immotile - unable to walk, fly around, slither, etc. Only motile creatures can cast this spell.":"施法者从自己的未来移动中借来能量轰击目标。 在之后的一小段时间内，施法者将无法动弹——不能行走、飞行、滑翔等。 只有能动的生物才能施放这个法术。","Sends the caster hurtling at a chosen nearby enemy, launching a high-accuracy melee attack on arrival. Additional electric damage will be dealt based on the length of the charge, the power of the spell, and the physical damage of the attack. The caster is wrapped in an envelope of twisted space, allowing them to safely pass through creatures, traps, and harmful terrain, and to displace creatures at their destination. The time taken by the spell is the greater of the time normally needed to cast a spell or that needed to launch one melee attack.":"让施法者冲向选定的一个附近敌人，在近身时发动高精度的近战攻击。 所造成的额外电击伤害取决于冲锋距离、法术威力和这次物理攻击的伤害。 施法者被包裹在扭曲的空间中，从而得以安全地穿过生物、陷阱和有害地形， 并置换在目的地的生物。 该法术所花费的时间是正常施展一个法术或发动一次近战攻击所需的时间中的较大者。","Renders a creature's body structure as brittle and fragile as glass, increasing the damage they take from all sources.":"使一个生物的身体结构变得像玻璃那样易碎而脆弱， 任何来源的攻击都会对其造成更多伤害。","Irresistibly renders a creature's body structure as brittle and fragile as glass, increasing the damage they take from all sources. It requires line of sight but not line of fire.":"不可抵抗地使一个生物的身体结构变得如玻璃般易碎，使其承受的所有伤害 增加。该法术只需视线，无需直达射线。","Launches a small hail of sharp thorns.":"射出一小束锋利的荆棘。","Causes brambles to rapidly grow nearby. They have almost no structural strength, but the wicked thorns they bear make their removal difficult. Such brambles are sparse enough that almost any missile can pass through unhindered.":"使附近荆棘迅速生长。它们几乎没有结构性力量， 但它们上面的恶刺使它们很难被清除。 这种荆棘是稀疏的，几乎任何飞弹都可以穿过它们。","Generates a loud noise, alerting nearby enemies.":"发出巨大的噪音，警示周围的敌人。","Causes the water around or under the target to violently swirl, dealing damage. It can affect targets standing in or flying above water.":"使目标周围或下方的水剧烈旋转，造成伤害。 它可以影响站在水中或在水上飞行的目标。","Irresistibly weakens a creature's melee attacks for a period of time, requiring line of sight but not line of fire.":"不可抵抗地使一个生物的近战攻击暂时变弱。该法术只需视线，无需直达射线。","Causes a strong gust of wind, pushing away creatures and clouds in a cone. If this causes a creature to collide with something, it will take damage.":"产生一股强风，在锥形区域内推开生物和云雾。 如果生物因此撞上其他东西，它会受到伤害。","Draws on the vitality of leaf and bark to heal a large amount of damage. Cannot be cast without a tree adjacent.":"利用树叶和树皮的生命力来治疗大量创伤。 如果没有相邻的树，则无法施放。","Recalls intelligent allies from elsewhere on the same level to the caster, after a short delay.":"在短时间延迟后，将同层的有智慧的友方召回到施法者那边。","If cast upon a creature already blessed (or cursed) with magical enchantments, those enchantments will be torn apart, transforming into a spray of destructive mutagenic radiation. The victim and anyone adjacent will be blasted and heavily deformed, weakening them and reducing their armour. Summoned creatures are particularly vulnerable, as the enchantments binding them to this plane will unravel and cause them to be dismissed immediately.":"如果施放在一个已经被魔法祝福（或诅咒）的生物身上，这些魔法将被撕碎， 转化为破坏性的诱变辐射。受害者和任何相邻生物都会被炸伤并严重变形， 变得虚弱且护甲降低。 被召唤的生物特别容易受到伤害， 因为将它们绑定在这个位面的魔法会瓦解，导致它们立刻消散。","Constructs a mobile and combat-capable alchemical manufactory. It uses the friction of melee combat to brew a variety of useful potions, venting clouds of their toxic byproducts at whatever it punches. When it has built up enough heat to complete its synthesis, it will automatically dispense the finished potions to nearby allies before falling apart.":"构建一个可移动且具战斗能力的炼金制造厂。它利用近战摩擦来酿造各种 有用的药水，在出拳时排放有毒副产品的云雾。当积累足够热量完成合成时， 它将在解体前自动向附近盟友分发成品药水。","Channels a surge of chaotic energy through each pile of flesh in the caster's sight, animating them into empowered large abominations and dealing chaos damage to any foes unfortunate enough to be standing next to them.":"引导一股混沌能量穿过施法者视野中的每个肉堆，将其激活为强化的大型憎恶， 并对不幸站在它们旁边的任何敌人造成混沌伤害。","Twists the air around a creature to both deal damage and attempt to pull them closer to the caster.":"扭曲一个生物周围的空气，造成伤害并试图将其拉向施法者。","Temporarily grants numerous nearby allies a magical weapon from within the armoury, so long as the souls holding it together remain intact.":"暂时授予众多附近盟友来自军械库的魔法武器，只要维系它们的灵魂保持完整。","Fires a barrage of conjured flesh, which will briefly remain as a pile on the ground at the end of its path.":"发射一道由魔法创造的血肉的穿透性弹幕，在其路径尽头地面上短暂地 留下一堆血肉。","Fires a ray of searing light, which may blind any living, demonic, or holy creature it strikes.":"发射一道灼热光芒的穿透射线，可能致盲击中的任何活着的、恶魔的 或神圣的生物。","<Caustic Breath ability>":"<Caustic Breath ability>","<Combustion Breath ability>":"<Combustion Breath ability>","Constructs a simple mechanical trap within an adjacent wall which repeatedly skewers random adjacent enemies. Protected by the wall itself, it is invulnerable to most forms of damage, but will fall apart if the caster leaves its vicinity.":"在相邻的墙壁内构建一个简单的机械陷阱，反复刺穿随机的相邻敌人。 受墙壁本身保护，它对大多数形式的伤害免疫，但如果施法者离开其附近 将会解体。","Calls forth shadows from the corners of nearby walls to strike at all of the caster's enemies standing adjacent to them.":"从附近墙角召来暗影，袭击所有紧邻这些墙角的施法者敌人。","Hurls a large and heavy shard of crystal. It may render a creature's body structure as brittle and fragile as shattered and unrefined crystal, increasing the damage they take from all sources.":"掷出一块巨大而沉重的水晶碎片。它可能令生物的身体结构变得如破碎的 粗制水晶般脆弱，使其受到的所有伤害增加。","Affixes a volatile catalyst to the caster's fists or melee weapon, causing each of their strikes to release a fiery explosion at its primary target. The caster and their allies are protected from the explosion's effects. The activity of the catalyst may be prolonged indefinitely as long as the caster continues to attack, but it rapidly loses potency when they take other actions. The base damage of the caster's weapon and the caster's spellpower each increase the explosion's damage.":"在施法者的拳头或近战武器上附着不稳定催化剂， 使每次攻击都在主要目标处引发火焰爆炸；施法者及其盟友不受爆炸伤害。 持续攻击可无限延长催化剂活性，采取其他行动则会使其迅速衰减。 武器基础伤害和法术威力都会提高爆炸伤害。","Forges up to four razor-sharp sawblades at fixed positions around the caster which shred any enemies adjacent to them over several turns.":"在施法者周围固定位置锻造至多四片锋利锯片， 在数回合内撕碎与其相邻的敌人。","Irresistibly weakens the power of an enemy's spells for a period of time.":"不可抵抗地暂时削弱一个敌人的法术威力。","Manifests the caster's faith as a spiritual weapon, which will fight and slay the caster's enemies under its own power. As it is a direct reflection of the caster's unique zeal, the weapon they receive from their god will be the same each time.":"将施法者的信仰显化为一件灵体武器，由其自行与敌人战斗并将其斩杀。 这件武器直接反映施法者独有的虔诚，因此每次从神祇处获得的武器都相同。","Attempts to forcibly change the allegiance of all nearby undead which are not already loyal to the caster. Adventurers, being famously headstrong, cannot be fully controlled by this spell. They will instead lash out randomly for the duration of its effect, attacking nearby friend and foe alike before regaining their wits. This spell can be broken prematurely by the death of its caster.":"试图强行改变附近所有尚未效忠施法者的亡灵之阵营。 意志坚定的冒险者无法被完全控制，只会在效果期间随机攻击附近敌友； 施法者死亡会使此法术提前解除。","Fires a bolt of accursed malice which inflicts Doom.":"发射一道由受诅恶意凝聚而成的箭，使目标遭受厄运。","Foretells a terrible future, inflicting Doom equal to half of what it would take for you to reach 100%. Upon the caster's death, a sliver of this fate will come to pass in the form of an ambush; several well-hidden enemies from the floor will seek out your position unerringly and all stairs will temporarily be sealed.":"预言可怕的未来，施加等于当前达到 100% 尚需量一半的厄运。 施法者死亡时，这一命运会有一小部分化为伏击实现：本层数个藏得很好的敌人会 准确无误地找到你的位置，所有楼梯也会暂时封闭。","Can only be cast a single time, but even slaying the messenger in their sleep will not avoid what fate has in store for you.":"此法术只能施放一次；即使在信使睡梦中杀死它，也无法逃过命运的安排。","Foretells a terrible future, inflicting Doom equal to half of what it would take for you to reach 100%. Upon the caster's death, a sliver of this fate will come to pass in the form of an ambush; several well-hidden enemies from the floor will seek out your position unerringly and all stairs will temporarily be sealed. Can only be cast a single time, but even slaying the messenger in their sleep will not avoid what fate has in store for you.":"预言可怕的未来，施加等于当前达到 100% 尚需量一半的厄运。 施法者死亡时，这一命运会有一小部分化为伏击实现：本层数个藏得很好的敌人会 准确无误地找到你的位置，所有楼梯也会暂时封闭。 此法术只能施放一次；即使在信使睡梦中杀死它，也无法逃过命运的安排。","Fills a living creature with negative energy, draining them for a fraction of their maximum health. This spell requires line of sight but not line of fire.":"以负能量充斥一个活物，使其按最大生命值的一定比例陷入衰竭。 该法术需要视线，但无需直达射线。","Summons a toothy crocodile to assault an adjacent enemy. The crocodile will appear beneath the caster in a surge of murky water and perform an empowered attack against the chosen target, dragging both it and the caster backward before allowing the latter to dismount safely behind it. It cannot be recast while the crocodile is still active.":"召唤一条利齿森森的鳄鱼袭击相邻敌人。鳄鱼会随一股浑浊水流从施法者脚下现身， 对选定目标发动强化攻击，并将目标和施法者一同向后拖拽， 随后让施法者在它身后安全下马。鳄鱼仍在场时无法再次施放此法术。","Fires a magical seed, entangling victims in quick-growing tree roots. Those entangled will be painfully constricted until they escape or the roots wither away. The roots will only sprout from solid ground.":"射出一颗魔法种子，以快速生长的树根缠绕目标。被缠绕者将遭受痛苦的挤压， 直至挣脱或树根枯萎。树根只能在坚实的地面上生长。","A single soul from within the armoury leaps out, striking with their weapon and then duelling independently for a short time before returning to the maelstrom once more.":"军械库中的一个灵魂闪跃而出，以武器发动攻击， 随后独立决斗片刻，再返回翻腾的灵魂之中。","Constructs a flying incendiary factory, packed to the brim with cluster bomblets which it can deploy both in melee and launch at range. While the monarch's bomblets have no attack of their own, they will pursue the caster's enemies until given the signal to explode.":"锻造一个塞满集束小炸弹的飞行燃烧武器工厂。它能在近战中部署小炸弹， 也能将其发射至远处。君主炸弹的小炸弹不会自行攻击，而会追赶施法者的敌人， 直至收到爆炸信号。","Recasting this spell while anything it has created is still active will detonate the monarch bomb and all bomblets, dealing a combination of fire and physical damage to everything adjacent to them besides the caster themselves.":"此法术创造的任何造物仍然存在时再次施法，会引爆君主炸弹及所有小炸弹， 对它们相邻的所有生物造成火焰与物理混合伤害，但施法者自身除外。","Constructs a flying incendiary factory, packed to the brim with cluster bomblets which it can deploy both in melee and launch at range. While the monarch's bomblets have no attack of their own, they will pursue the caster's enemies until given the signal to explode. Recasting this spell while anything it has created is still active will detonate the monarch bomb and all bomblets, dealing a combination of fire and physical damage to everything adjacent to them besides the caster themselves.":"锻造一个塞满集束小炸弹的飞行燃烧武器工厂。它能在近战中部署小炸弹， 也能将其发射至远处。君主炸弹的小炸弹不会自行攻击，而会追赶施法者的敌人， 直至收到爆炸信号。 此法术创造的任何造物仍然存在时再次施法，会引爆君主炸弹及所有小炸弹， 对它们相邻的所有生物造成火焰与物理混合伤害，但施法者自身除外。","Constructs a small mechanical guardian which bolsters its creator's armour class for as long as it remains adjacent to them.":"锻造一个小型机械守卫；只要与创造者相邻，它就会提高创造者的护甲。","While also capable of biting foes, the phalanx beetle will never voluntarily leave its creator's side, and if forcibly separated, will prioritise returning to them over any other concern.":"方阵甲虫也能啃咬敌人，但绝不会自愿离开创造者身边；若被强行分开， 它会优先回到创造者身边，不顾其他事务。","Spellpower increases the magnitude of the AC increase, as well as the beetle's own durability.":"法术威力会提高护甲加成幅度及甲虫自身的耐久度。","Constructs a small mechanical guardian which bolsters its creator's armour class for as long as it remains adjacent to them. While also capable of biting foes, the phalanx beetle will never voluntarily leave its creator's side, and if forcibly separated, will prioritise returning to them over any other concern. Spellpower increases the magnitude of the AC increase, as well as the beetle's own durability.":"锻造一个小型机械守卫；只要与创造者相邻，它就会提高创造者的护甲。 方阵甲虫也能啃咬敌人，但绝不会自愿离开创造者身边；若被强行分开， 它会优先回到创造者身边，不顾其他事务。 法术威力会提高护甲加成幅度及甲虫自身的耐久度。","Draws upon the caster's own physical integrity to create a kinetic shockwave that damages foes in a large area. The caster is locked in place for several turns as the shockwave starts to form, and the spell will be cancelled if they are displaced during that time, but they may otherwise perform other actions freely.":"汲取施法者自身的身体强度，制造一道对大范围敌人造成伤害的动能冲击波。 冲击波开始成形后的数回合内，施法者会被固定在原地；若在此期间被迫位移， 法术就会取消，但施法者仍可自由执行其他动作。","Spellpower causes the spell to complete more quickly, but the damage depends entirely upon the caster's AC.":"法术威力越高，法术完成得越快；造成的伤害则完全取决于施法者的护甲值。","Draws upon the caster's own physical integrity to create a kinetic shockwave that damages foes in a large area. The caster is locked in place for several turns as the shockwave starts to form, and the spell will be cancelled if they are displaced during that time, but they may otherwise perform other actions freely. Spellpower causes the spell to complete more quickly, but the damage depends entirely upon the caster's AC.":"汲取施法者自身的身体强度，制造一道对大范围敌人造成伤害的动能冲击波。 冲击波开始成形后的数回合内，施法者会被固定在原地；若在此期间被迫位移， 法术就会取消，但施法者仍可自由执行其他动作。 法术威力越高，法术完成得越快；造成的伤害则完全取决于施法者的护甲值。","Fires a penetrating bolt of frigid air that leaves clouds of lethally cold vapour in its wake.":"发射一道穿透性的严寒气流，在沿途留下致命的寒气云。","A magnum opus of reckless chemistry, this spell conjures up a surfeit of volatile reagents to rain down upon your enemies. For the next several turns, up to 3 random enemies in sight will be struck by an exploding beaker that inflicts either fire, cold, electric, or poison damage. If any of these explosions overlap each other, the resulting reaction will inflict even greater irresistible damage and sometimes apply a random deleterious status on whoever is caught in the blast.":"这部鲁莽化学的巅峰之作会创造大量易爆试剂，如雨般倾泻在敌人身上。 接下来的数回合中，视野内最多 3 个随机敌人会被爆炸烧杯击中， 受到火焰、寒冷、电击或毒素伤害。如果爆炸彼此重叠，反应会造成更高的 不可抵抗伤害，并有时给爆炸范围内的目标施加随机有害状态。","This spell costs a small amount of the caster's magical energy each turn to maintain, and while it will never aim an explosion where it could hurt the caster, the caster's allies (and anything else in the general vicinity) are not so fortunate.":"维持此法术每回合会消耗少量魔力。爆炸绝不会瞄准可能伤害施法者的位置， 但施法者的盟友及附近其他事物就没有这么幸运了。","A magnum opus of reckless chemistry, this spell conjures up a surfeit of volatile reagents to rain down upon your enemies. For the next several turns, up to 3 random enemies in sight will be struck by an exploding beaker that inflicts either fire, cold, electric, or poison damage. If any of these explosions overlap each other, the resulting reaction will inflict even greater irresistible damage and sometimes apply a random deleterious status on whoever is caught in the blast. This spell costs a small amount of the caster's magical energy each turn to maintain, and while it will never aim an explosion where it could hurt the caster, the caster's allies (and anything else in the general vicinity) are not so fortunate.":"这部鲁莽化学的巅峰之作会创造大量易爆试剂，如雨般倾泻在敌人身上。 接下来的数回合中，视野内最多 3 个随机敌人会被爆炸烧杯击中， 受到火焰、寒冷、电击或毒素伤害。如果爆炸彼此重叠，反应会造成更高的 不可抵抗伤害，并有时给爆炸范围内的目标施加随机有害状态。 维持此法术每回合会消耗少量魔力。爆炸绝不会瞄准可能伤害施法者的位置， 但施法者的盟友及附近其他事物就没有这么幸运了。","<Galvanic Breath ability>":"<Galvanic Breath ability>","Briefly reorients local gravity to be in a cardinal direction of the caster's choosing, causing all creatures in sight to tumble a short distance in that direction.":"短暂地将局部重力重新定向为施法者选择的某个基本方向，使视野内所有生物 向该方向翻滚一小段距离。","The caster is not immune to the gravitational effects of this spell, but will be cushioned so they take no collision damage. Other creatures are not so fortunate, and the abrupt impact will batter anything which was not already standing beside its new 'floor'.":"施法者不能免疫此法术的重力效应，但会受到缓冲而免受碰撞伤害。其他生物 则没有这般幸运——骤然的撞击会重创任何未贴近新的\"地面\"站立的生物。","It takes a short time for gravity to stabilise enough to recast this spell, though more powerful mages are able to do so more frequently.":"重力需要短暂时间才能稳定到足以重新施放此法术，不过更强大的法师能够 更频繁地使用它。","Briefly reorients local gravity to be in a cardinal direction of the caster's choosing, causing all creatures in sight to tumble a short distance in that direction. The caster is not immune to the gravitational effects of this spell, but will be cushioned so they take no collision damage. Other creatures are not so fortunate, and the abrupt impact will batter anything which was not already standing beside its new 'floor'. It takes a short time for gravity to stabilise enough to recast this spell, though more powerful mages are able to do so more frequently.":"短暂地将局部重力重新定向为施法者选择的某个基本方向，使视野内所有生物 向该方向翻滚一小段距离。 施法者不能免疫此法术的重力效应，但会受到缓冲而免受碰撞伤害。其他生物 则没有这般幸运——骤然的撞击会重创任何未贴近新的\"地面\"站立的生物。 重力需要短暂时间才能稳定到足以重新施放此法术，不过更强大的法师能够 更频繁地使用它。","<Glacial Breath ability>":"<Glacial Breath ability>","Calls forth the spite of the recently dead to skewer a targeted enemy with shards of bone. This spell never misses, and will pin its target in place for several turns, but casting it rapidly consumes the remnants of death that linger upon the caster.":"唤起新近死者的怨恨，以骨片刺穿指定敌人。此法术绝不会落空， 并会将目标固定在原地数回合，但每次施放都会迅速消耗施法者身上残留的死亡气息。","You can stockpile enough malice to cast this spell at most three times, and this can only be replenished by causing the death of a sufficient number of living beings.":"最多可积蓄足以施放三次的怨恨；只有造成足够多活物死亡才能补充。","Calls forth the spite of the recently dead to skewer a targeted enemy with shards of bone. This spell never misses, and will pin its target in place for several turns, but casting it rapidly consumes the remnants of death that linger upon the caster. You can stockpile enough malice to cast this spell at most three times, and this can only be replenished by causing the death of a sufficient number of living beings.":"唤起新近死者的怨恨，以骨片刺穿指定敌人。此法术绝不会落空， 并会将目标固定在原地数回合，但每次施放都会迅速消耗施法者身上残留的死亡气息。 最多可积蓄足以施放三次的怨恨；只有造成足够多活物死亡才能补充。","Shoots a stream of webbing at a creature, ensnaring them in a sticky web and scattering additional webs nearby that dissolve after a short length of time.":"向生物射出一连串的网，使目标困于黏性的网中，并在附近散布额外蛛网； 这些蛛网会在短时间后消散。","Splits apart the ground in front of the caster and sculpts a terrifying weapon out of molten rock. This mortar will move slowly along the lava-filled chasm, autonomously launching gouts of magma at the caster's enemies as it does so.":"劈开施法者前方的地面，以熔岩塑造出一门可怕的武器。 这门迫击炮会沿充满熔岩的裂隙缓慢移动，并自动向施法者的敌人发射岩浆。","When it reaches the end of its path, or is obstructed in its movement by another creature, it will sink back into the lava, and the chasm will seal itself shut shortly thereafter.":"迫击炮抵达路径终点或被其他生物挡住时，会沉回熔岩； 裂隙随后也会很快闭合。","Splits apart the ground in front of the caster and sculpts a terrifying weapon out of molten rock. This mortar will move slowly along the lava-filled chasm, autonomously launching gouts of magma at the caster's enemies as it does so. When it reaches the end of its path, or is obstructed in its movement by another creature, it will sink back into the lava, and the chasm will seal itself shut shortly thereafter.":"劈开施法者前方的地面，以熔岩塑造出一门可怕的武器。 这门迫击炮会沿充满熔岩的裂隙缓慢移动，并自动向施法者的敌人发射岩浆。 迫击炮抵达路径终点或被其他生物挡住时，会沉回熔岩； 裂隙随后也会很快闭合。","Fires a shard of ice that coats whatever it hits with a layer of brittle frost which slows their movement.":"发射一枚冰片，为命中的目标覆盖一层脆霜，使其移动减慢。","Each shot fired will deplete the cannon's remaining durability, but if it survives to fire 5 times, the final shot will fragment to hit all enemies around the primary target for additional damage.":"每次发射都会消耗火炮剩余耐久度；若火炮存续到发射 5 次， 最后一发会碎裂并额外伤害主要目标周围的所有敌人。","Fires a shard of ice that coats whatever it hits with a layer of brittle frost which slows their movement. Each shot fired will deplete the cannon's remaining durability, but if it survives to fire 5 times, the final shot will fragment to hit all enemies around the primary target for additional damage.":"发射一枚冰片，为命中的目标覆盖一层脆霜，使其移动减慢。 每次发射都会消耗火炮剩余耐久度；若火炮存续到发射 5 次， 最后一发会碎裂并额外伤害主要目标周围的所有敌人。","Sculpts a pair of icy cannons that assail the caster's enemies from long range. The frigid shards they fire rapidly coat their targets with a layer of brittle frost which slows their movement.":"塑造两座冰霜火炮，从远处攻击施法者的敌人。 它们发射的寒冷碎片会迅速在目标身上覆上一层脆霜，减慢其移动速度。","The cannons are short-lived and consume a part of themselves with every shard they fire, but if they survive to fire their final salvo without interference, it will be extra-powerful.":"这些火炮寿命短暂，每次发射碎片都会消耗自身的一部分； 如果未受干扰并存续到发射最终齐射，最后一轮攻击会格外强力。","Sculpts a pair of icy cannons that assail the caster's enemies from long range. The frigid shards they fire rapidly coat their targets with a layer of brittle frost which slows their movement. The cannons are short-lived and consume a part of themselves with every shard they fire, but if they survive to fire their final salvo without interference, it will be extra-powerful.":"塑造两座冰霜火炮，从远处攻击施法者的敌人。 它们发射的寒冷碎片会迅速在目标身上覆上一层脆霜，减慢其移动速度。 这些火炮寿命短暂，每次发射碎片都会消耗自身的一部分； 如果未受干扰并存续到发射最终齐射，最后一轮攻击会格外强力。","Hurls a gout of umbral torchlight which deals irresistible damage to living, demonic, and holy beings. The torchlight will also briefly empower any friendly undead caught in its blast and is harmless to those who worship Yredelemnul.":"<Hurl Torchlight ability>","Bends the weave of fate against a target, inflicting significant Doom. Cannot be used if there are any obstructions between the caster and their target.":"扭曲目标的命运之网，施加大量厄运。施法者与目标之间有任何阻碍时均无法使用。","Weaves a thin kinetic filament around the caster's melee weapon and launches the other end of it at a nearby enemy. If this grapnel successfully hits and does damage, it will become lodged in them, allowing the next melee attack the caster performs against them to strike with perfect accuracy and a small slaying bonus.":"以细薄的动能丝缠绕施法者的近战武器，并把另一端射向附近敌人。 若抓钩命中并造成伤害，便会嵌入目标，使施法者下一次对其发动的近战攻击 必定命中，并获得少量杀伤加成。","Violently fractures the landscape, causing rubble to fall upon several nearby enemies and also the ground behind them - obstructing their path to flee the caster.":"猛烈震裂地貌，使碎石砸向数名附近敌人及其身后的地面， 从而阻断它们逃离施法者的路线。","Fires a bomblet on a ballistic trajectory that ignores line of fire, dealing minor damage to a single target within range and deploying the bomblet near it. Cannot target enemies adjacent to the caster or those with no nearby room for the bomblet to land.":"沿无视火线的弹道发射一枚小型炸弹，对射程内的单个目标造成少量伤害， 并将炸弹部署在其附近。无法以紧邻施法者的敌人为目标； 若目标附近没有空间供炸弹落下，也无法以其为目标。","Constructs a mechanical bee and winds its clockwork mechanisms over several turns before unleashing it against a targeted foe. The bee is swift and powerful, but its clockwork quickly winds down as it attacks, eventually leaving it helpless and unable to move.":"制造一只机械蜜蜂，并用数回合上紧发条，再将其放出攻击指定敌人。 蜜蜂迅捷而强大，但攻击会很快耗尽发条，最终使其无助地停止移动。","The caster may repair and rewind a dormant bee by attempting to move into it, at the cost of 1 MP.":"施法者可尝试移入休眠蜜蜂所在位置，花费 1点法力修复并重新上紧发条。","Spellpower increases the number of attacks the bee may perform before going dormant.":"法术威力会增加蜜蜂休眠前可发动的攻击次数。","Constructs a mechanical bee and winds its clockwork mechanisms over several turns before unleashing it against a targeted foe. The bee is swift and powerful, but its clockwork quickly winds down as it attacks, eventually leaving it helpless and unable to move. The caster may repair and rewind a dormant bee by attempting to move into it, at the cost of 1 MP. Spellpower increases the number of attacks the bee may perform before going dormant.":"制造一只机械蜜蜂，并用数回合上紧发条，再将其放出攻击指定敌人。 蜜蜂迅捷而强大，但攻击会很快耗尽发条，最终使其无助地停止移动。 施法者可尝试移入休眠蜜蜂所在位置，花费 1点法力修复并重新上紧发条。 法术威力会增加蜜蜂休眠前可发动的攻击次数。","Launches a caustic sporangium which will pursue any intriguing sources of nutrients - such as yourself - and engulf them in a massive acidic explosion. Nascent plasmodia, capable of firing acid of their own, may take root on any walls this explosion touches - though none within 2 tiles of any other.":"发射一个腐蚀性孢子囊；它会追逐任何诱人的营养来源——例如你自己—— 并将其吞没在巨大酸液爆炸中。爆炸接触的墙壁上可能扎根初生原生质体， 它们能自行发射酸液，但任何一只原生质体的 2 格内都不会再生成另一只。","Fires penetrating bolts of molten rock at up to two different enemy targets. Half of its damage bypasses fire resistance.":"向至多两个不同敌人发射穿透性熔岩弹；造成的伤害有一半无视火焰抗性。","Envelops a target in a thin layer of magnetically charged metal fragments, then unleashes a powerful surge of electricity that arcs unerringly towards every visible target coated in these fragments - firing an additional beam at each target thus marked. Magnetised creatures are additionally unable to evade attacks and will be revealed if invisible. If they die while still coated, they will leave behind a short-lived cloud of electrified metal that will continue to serve as a lightning rod for this spell.":"以一层带磁电的金属碎片包裹目标，随后释放强大电流， 必定向所有可见且带有碎片的目标跳跃，并为每个标记者追加一道电束。 被磁化的生物无法闪避攻击，隐形时也会显形；若在碎片仍附着时死亡， 会留下短时带电金属云，继续充当此法术的引雷物。","Causes all allied monsters nearby to rapidly regenerate over a short period of time. This regeneration is proportional to each of those creature's maximum health.":"使附近所有友方怪物在短时间内快速再生。 每个目标的恢复量都与其自身最大生命值成正比。","Compresses an envelope of space around the caster and an adjacent enemy (or a contiguous line of enemies), then allows it to decompress abruptly, propelling everyone forward until the unfortunate being at the far end collides with something solid, inflicting damage on them proportional to the distance travelled.":"压缩包围施法者与相邻敌人（或连续一列敌人）的一片空间，随后令其骤然舒张， 将所有人向前推进，直至最远端的不幸生物撞上坚固物体。对该生物造成的伤害 与移动距离成正比。","Fires a bolt of dispelling energy at a targeted creature, possibly removing some of its enchantments.":"向目标生物发射一道驱散能量，可能移除其部分魔法效果。","<Mud Breath ability>":"<Mud Breath ability>","Causes mutagenic energy to accumulate in a target, eventually reaching levels high enough to cause harmful mutations or explosions of unstable magical energy. This spell requires line of sight but not line of fire.":"使目标体内积累变异能量，最终可能达到足以造成有害变异或不稳定魔法能量 爆炸的程度。该法术需要视线，但无需直达射线。","Manifests a magical hammer that repairs and temporarily augments the offensive capabilities of any nearby construct - be it golem or phalanx beetle or even dancing weapon. This process results in a flurry of sparks, slag, and concussive shockwaves that do considerable damage to any enemies adjacent to the targeted construct, but it cannot be recast upon the same object until the enhancement wears off.":"显现一把魔法锤，修复并暂时增强附近任意构装体的攻击能力—— 无论是魔像、方阵甲虫，甚至舞动武器。 这一过程会迸发大量火花、熔渣和冲击波，对目标构装体相邻的所有敌人 造成可观伤害；强化消退前，不能对同一目标再次施放此法术。","Manifests a magical hammer that repairs and temporarily augments the offensive capabilities of any construct that was created by the caster's own Forgecraft spells. This process results in a flurry of sparks, slag, and concussive shockwaves that do considerable damage to any enemies adjacent to the targeted construct, but it cannot be recast upon the same object until the enhancement wears off.":"显现一把魔法锤，修复并暂时增强由施法者自身锻造术创造的任意构装体的 攻击能力。这一过程会迸发大量火花、熔渣和冲击波，对目标构装体相邻的 所有敌人造成可观伤害；强化消退前，不能对同一目标再次施放此法术。","<Noxious Breath ability>":"<Noxious Breath ability>","<Nullifying Breath ability>":"<Nullifying Breath ability>","Isolates a target from the divine - temporarily reducing their piety in the eyes of whichever god they worship and denying them access to any divine abilities that piety would allow. Being repeatedly affected by this spell will reduce the one's effective piety further and further, but can never directly lead to excommunication. This effect will slowly wear off as the afflicted being gains experience, eventually restoring access to the full piety they once possessed.":"使目标暂时与神祇隔绝，降低其在所信奉神祇眼中的有效虔诚值， 并阻止使用依赖该虔诚值的神圣能力。重复受影响会进一步降低有效虔诚， 但绝不会直接导致逐出教派。目标获得经验时效果会逐渐消退， 最终恢复原有全部虔诚带来的能力。","Calls on the ancient cold lurking within the earth to emerge - violently. The force of its emergence blasts rock from the ceiling, smashing into the target with unavoidable force. The cold itself is brief but unbearably bitter, bypassing armour entirely as it freezes the target and their neighbours.":"唤醒潜藏于大地深处的古老严寒，使其猛烈喷涌而出。喷发的力量震落顶上的岩石， 以无法躲避的力量砸中目标。寒意本身虽转瞬即逝，却极其刺骨； 它会完全无视护甲，冻结目标及其邻近生物。","It will always attempt to blast the largest concentration of foes in sight, and never explodes next to the caster.":"法术总会尝试轰击视野内敌人最密集的位置，且绝不会在施法者身旁爆发。","Calls on the ancient cold lurking within the earth to emerge - violently. The force of its emergence blasts rock from the ceiling, smashing into the target with unavoidable force. The cold itself is brief but unbearably bitter, bypassing armour entirely as it freezes the target and their neighbours. It will always attempt to blast the largest concentration of foes in sight, and never explodes next to the caster.":"唤醒潜藏于大地深处的古老严寒，使其猛烈喷涌而出。喷发的力量震落顶上的岩石， 以无法躲避的力量砸中目标。寒意本身虽转瞬即逝，却极其刺骨； 它会完全无视护甲，冻结目标及其邻近生物。 法术总会尝试轰击视野内敌人最密集的位置，且绝不会在施法者身旁爆发。","Weaves and fires a phantom copy of the caster with great force. Such phantoms have the same martial and mystic prowess as the caster, and an impromptu night parade of illusions may overwhelm the caster's victims.":"编织出施法者的幻影复制体，并将其猛烈射出。这些幻影拥有与施法者相同的 武艺和神秘力量；临时组成的幻影夜行队足以压倒施法者的受害者。","Overlays part of an adjacent reality onto this one, causing random local monsters to appear elsewhere on the floor. The first time this is used, multiple monsters will arrive at once; afterward, they will appear at a slow, steady rate.":"将相邻现实的一部分叠加到此处，使随机的本地怪物出现在本层其他位置。 首次使用时会同时到来多个怪物；之后则会缓慢而稳定地出现。","After a considerable amount of time has passed, these monsters may even appear near the player.":"经过相当长时间后，这些怪物甚至可能出现在玩家附近。","Overlays part of an adjacent reality onto this one, causing random local monsters to appear elsewhere on the floor. The first time this is used, multiple monsters will arrive at once; afterward, they will appear at a slow, steady rate. After a considerable amount of time has passed, these monsters may even appear near the player.":"将相邻现实的一部分叠加到此处，使随机的本地怪物出现在本层其他位置。 首次使用时会同时到来多个怪物；之后则会缓慢而稳定地出现。 经过相当长时间后，这些怪物甚至可能出现在玩家附近。","Constructs a gleaming metal champion whose prowess rivals that of the greatest living warriors. It is resistant to all forms of magic and wields a perfect replica of any artefact melee weapon the caster chooses.":"构建一名闪亮的金属勇士，其战力足以媲美最伟大的在世战士。 它抵抗一切形式的魔法，并使用施法者所选任意神器近战武器的完美复制品。","It creates a damaging shockwave around itself when first deployed and slowly gains charge as it attacks enemies. When it has gained sufficient charge, the spell may be recast to overload the paragon, unleashing a flurry of attacks in a wide area which inflict increased damage, but destroying the paragon in the process.":"首次部署时，它会在周围产生伤害性冲击波，并在攻击敌人时缓慢积蓄能量。 能量充足后，可再次施法使典范过载，在广大区域内发动一连串伤害提高的攻击， 但会在过程中摧毁典范。","Due to the magical link it maintains with its creator, it will perform an extra attack whenever they do, and will sometimes even parry attacks directed at them, if they are close enough together.":"由于它与创造者维持魔法联系，只要双方距离足够近，创造者每次攻击时它都会额外攻击， 有时甚至会格挡指向创造者的攻击。","Constructs a gleaming metal champion whose prowess rivals that of the greatest living warriors. It is resistant to all forms of magic and wields a perfect replica of any artefact melee weapon the caster chooses. It creates a damaging shockwave around itself when first deployed and slowly gains charge as it attacks enemies. When it has gained sufficient charge, the spell may be recast to overload the paragon, unleashing a flurry of attacks in a wide area which inflict increased damage, but destroying the paragon in the process. Due to the magical link it maintains with its creator, it will perform an extra attack whenever they do, and will sometimes even parry attacks directed at them, if they are close enough together.":"构建一名闪亮的金属勇士，其战力足以媲美最伟大的在世战士。 它抵抗一切形式的魔法，并使用施法者所选任意神器近战武器的完美复制品。 首次部署时，它会在周围产生伤害性冲击波，并在攻击敌人时缓慢积蓄能量。 能量充足后，可再次施法使典范过载，在广大区域内发动一连串伤害提高的攻击， 但会在过程中摧毁典范。 由于它与创造者维持魔法联系，只要双方距离足够近，创造者每次攻击时它都会额外攻击， 有时甚至会格挡指向创造者的攻击。","Transmutes a small amount of the air around a target into toxic vapours, poisoning anyone unfortunate enough to breathe them in. The quantity of air affected is small and it will not persist beyond the turn in which it is cast. It cannot affect those with any resistance to poison.":"将目标周围的少量空气转化为有毒气体，使吸入者中毒。 受影响的气体只存在于施法当回合，且无法影响任何具有毒素抗性的生物。","Ignites a memory from the nimbus which surrounds Nobody, temporarily granting them the knowledge of a powerful spell and healing their injuries. This power is fleeting and will be extinguished after taking any significant amount of damage, but so long as any other memories remain, they cannot be put to rest for good.":"点燃环绕“无名者”的光环记忆，暂时赋予其一个强力法术的知识并治疗伤势。 这股力量十分短暂，承受任何显著伤害后便会熄灭； 但只要还有其他记忆残留，就无法让它们永久安息。","Unleashes a torrent of vampire bats, filling the air around a target.":"释放一股吸血蝙蝠洪流，填满目标周围的空气。","These vampires will gnaw on anything which isn't undead with a voracious hunger, and their bites will eventually even lull their victims to sleep, leaving them easy prey.":"这些吸血生物会贪婪啃咬一切非亡灵目标；其啃咬最终甚至会使受害者入睡， 令其成为轻易捕获的猎物。","Unleashes a torrent of vampire bats, filling the air around a target. These vampires will gnaw on anything which isn't undead with a voracious hunger, and their bites will eventually even lull their victims to sleep, leaving them easy prey.":"释放一股吸血蝙蝠洪流，填满目标周围的空气。 这些吸血生物会贪婪啃咬一切非亡灵目标；其啃咬最终甚至会使受害者入睡， 令其成为轻易捕获的猎物。","Fires a penetrating bolt of energetic flames that can bounce off walls to hit targets twice.":"发射一道充满能量的穿透火焰束，可从墙壁弹回并二次命中目标。","Fires a penetrating bolt of energetic cold that can bounce off walls to hit targets twice.":"发射一道穿透性的强力寒流，能从墙壁反弹并命中目标两次。","Causes another creature to rapidly regenerate over a short period of time. This regeneration is proportional to that creature's maximum health.":"使另一个生物在短时间内快速再生。恢复量与该生物的最大生命值成正比。","Condenses the caster's magical energy into the form of a violently crackling blade. Each time the caster successfully hits with a melee attack while the spell is active, this blade will rend a path back and forth through nearby foes, dealing irresistible damage.":"将施法者的魔法能量凝聚成一柄猛烈噼啪作响的利刃。法术生效期间， 每当施法者的近战攻击命中，这柄利刃便会在附近敌人之间来回撕开一条路径， 造成无法抵抗的伤害。","Casting this spell temporarily drains *all* of the caster's remaining magical power to constitute the blade, but this energy will be returned to them as soon as the blade ceases to exist. Each point of magical power sequestered this way slightly increases the damage the blade inflicts.":"施放此法术会暂时抽走施法者所有剩余法力以构成利刃；利刃消失时， 这些能量会立刻返还。以此方式封存的每一点法力都会略微提高利刃的伤害。","Condenses the caster's magical energy into the form of a violently crackling blade. Each time the caster successfully hits with a melee attack while the spell is active, this blade will rend a path back and forth through nearby foes, dealing irresistible damage. Casting this spell temporarily drains *all* of the caster's remaining magical power to constitute the blade, but this energy will be returned to them as soon as the blade ceases to exist. Each point of magical power sequestered this way slightly increases the damage the blade inflicts.":"将施法者的魔法能量凝聚成一柄猛烈噼啪作响的利刃。法术生效期间， 每当施法者的近战攻击命中，这柄利刃便会在附近敌人之间来回撕开一条路径， 造成无法抵抗的伤害。 施放此法术会暂时抽走施法者所有剩余法力以构成利刃；利刃消失时， 这些能量会立刻返还。以此方式封存的每一点法力都会略微提高利刃的伤害。","Afflicts a creature (and up to two others near it) with a magical plague that slowly freezes them from the inside out. Victims take AC-ignoring cold damage each turn, and as the disease progresses, shards of crystalline ice will start erupting violently from their body, damaging nearby enemies. When they finally succumb, the plague may spread to those around them.":"使一个生物（及其附近最多两个其他生物）感染魔法瘟疫，从内向外缓慢冻结。 受害者每回合受到无视护甲的寒冷伤害；随着疾病发展，水晶冰片会猛烈地从体内迸出， 伤害附近敌人。受害者最终倒下时，瘟疫可能传播给周围生物。","In living, holy, or demonic creatures, the disease is especially virulent, feeding off the necromantic energies released by its host's suffering. As they approach the point of death, it will accelerate rapidly, devouring the last vestiges of their body and leaving nothing behind but a twisted pillar of stygian ice.":"对活物、神圣或恶魔生物而言，此病尤其凶猛，会以宿主受苦时释放的死灵能量为食。 当宿主接近死亡时，疾病会迅速加剧，吞噬其身体最后的残余， 只留下一根扭曲的冥界冰柱。","Afflicts a creature (and up to two others near it) with a magical plague that slowly freezes them from the inside out. Victims take AC-ignoring cold damage each turn, and as the disease progresses, shards of crystalline ice will start erupting violently from their body, damaging nearby enemies. When they finally succumb, the plague may spread to those around them. In living, holy, or demonic creatures, the disease is especially virulent, feeding off the necromantic energies released by its host's suffering. As they approach the point of death, it will accelerate rapidly, devouring the last vestiges of their body and leaving nothing behind but a twisted pillar of stygian ice.":"使一个生物（及其附近最多两个其他生物）感染魔法瘟疫，从内向外缓慢冻结。 受害者每回合受到无视护甲的寒冷伤害；随着疾病发展，水晶冰片会猛烈地从体内迸出， 伤害附近敌人。受害者最终倒下时，瘟疫可能传播给周围生物。 对活物、神圣或恶魔生物而言，此病尤其凶猛，会以宿主受苦时释放的死灵能量为食。 当宿主接近死亡时，疾病会迅速加剧，吞噬其身体最后的残余， 只留下一根扭曲的冥界冰柱。","Stomps heavily upon the ground, sending out violent shockwaves that fracture the ground beneath multiple nearby enemies. Flying creatures take greatly reduced damage from this attack, but those on the ground may sometimes to lose their footing altogether, delaying their next action as they struggle to regain balance on the uneven terrain.":"重踏地面，发出猛烈震波，震裂多名附近敌人脚下的地面。 飞行生物受到的伤害大幅降低；地面生物则可能完全失去平衡， 在崎岖地面上重新站稳时延后下一次行动。","Fires a penetrating beam of shadow.":"发射一道穿透性的暗影能量束。","Pins several random nearby enemies to their own shadows, briefly preventing them from moving. At higher spellpower, it affects more enemies at once.":"将附近随机选中的数名敌人钉在各自的影子上，使其短时间无法移动。 法术威力越高，同时影响的敌人越多。","Forcefully steals a sliver from the shadows of all nearby enemies, causing damage which bypasses the victim's armour entirely.":"强行从附近所有敌人的影子中夺取一缕，造成完全无视目标护甲的伤害。","Conjures a shadowy prism which will unleash a violent blast of shadows after a short duration. If destroyed prematurely, this blast will be much weaker.":"创造一个暗影棱镜，短暂延迟后会释放猛烈的暗影爆炸。 若棱镜提前被摧毁，爆炸威力会大幅减弱。","Summons a servant of living shadow to harass and constrict the caster's enemies. The strength of its attacks is directly increased by spellpower.":"召唤一个活影仆从骚扰并缠住施法者的敌人。 它的攻击强度随法术威力直接提高。","Fires a small bullet of hardened shadow at a single enemy.":"向单个敌人射出一颗小型硬化暗影弹。","Calls down shadowy lightning upon up to half of all visible enemies, dealing irresistible damage to them.":"向可见敌人中的至多一半降下暗影闪电，造成无法抵抗的伤害。","Saps the energy from a line of enemies, slowing them for a short while. Spellpower increases the duration of this effect, but stronger creatures may shake off their lethargy more quickly.":"汲取一列敌人的活力，使其短时间减速。法术威力越高，效果持续越久， 但更强大的生物可能更快摆脱这种麻木。","Forms a stationary turret of solidified shadow that repeatedly fires upon the caster's enemies.":"用凝固的暗影形成一座固定炮塔，反复向施法者的敌人开火。","Hurls a ball of flickering shadows, which explodes in a small area.":"发射一颗暗影球，在击中时爆炸。","Spins in place, dealing grievous damage to adjacent enemies with its serrated body.":"原地旋转，以锯齿状躯体重创相邻敌人。","Inflicts the sign of ruin upon a group of enemies, condemning their bodies to inexorable decay and collapse. Whenever anything bearing this sign receives damage from a melee attack, they will suffer heavy draining and may additionally become either slow, weak, or blind.":"为一群敌人施加毁灭印记，使其躯体不可避免地衰败崩解。 带有印记者每次受到近战伤害时都会陷入严重衰竭， 并可能额外陷入缓慢、虚弱或失明之一。","Torments nearby living foes, cutting their health in half. This damage is never directly lethal. The pain inflicted then heals the user.":"折磨附近的活物敌人，使其生命值减半；此伤害绝不会直接致命。 造成的痛苦随后会治疗使用者。","Causes the air around a creature to twist itself into a whirling vortex of frigid meteorological fury, encasing the victim in ice and slowing their movement briefly. It does more damage to targets surrounded by empty space and half of its damage bypasses cold resistance.":"使目标周围空气扭曲成严寒气旋，以冰封住受害者并短暂减慢移动。 目标周围越空旷，受到的伤害越高；造成的伤害有一半无视寒冷抗性。","Breathes a penetrating and unstable bijection burst. If it hits, it may teleport victims after a short delay. For particularly interesting morsels of adventurers such as yourself, this teleport will translocate those victims towards the caster's allies and bring the caster along for the ride, if possible.":"吐出一道穿透性且不稳定的双射能量冲击。若命中，它可能会在短暂延迟后 传送受害者。对于像你这样格外可口的冒险者，这次传送会将受害者移向 施法者的盟友，并在可能的情况下捎上施法者同行。","Attempts to force a tiny fragment of a living, holy, or demonic being's soul to take leave of their body and manifest as a soul wisp. This wisp is nominally under the necromancer's control, but will focus its attacks foremost on the creature it was created from, instinctually trying to return to its proper home once more. The victim will be weakened until the wisp reverts to where it belongs.":"尝试迫使活物、神圣或恶魔生物的一小片灵魂离开身体，显现为灵魂之息。 它名义上受死灵法师控制，却会优先攻击自己的来源，凭本能试图回归原本归宿。 在灵魂之息归位前，受害者会陷入虚弱。","Wisps created from more powerful souls have more damaging attacks, but are always fragile.":"由更强灵魂创造的灵魂之息攻击伤害更高，但始终十分脆弱。","Attempts to force a tiny fragment of a living, holy, or demonic being's soul to take leave of their body and manifest as a soul wisp. This wisp is nominally under the necromancer's control, but will focus its attacks foremost on the creature it was created from, instinctually trying to return to its proper home once more. The victim will be weakened until the wisp reverts to where it belongs. Wisps created from more powerful souls have more damaging attacks, but are always fragile.":"尝试迫使活物、神圣或恶魔生物的一小片灵魂离开身体，显现为灵魂之息。 它名义上受死灵法师控制，却会优先攻击自己的来源，凭本能试图回归原本归宿。 在灵魂之息归位前，受害者会陷入虚弱。 由更强灵魂创造的灵魂之息攻击伤害更高，但始终十分脆弱。","Summons a pair of riddling sphinxes - one guardian and one marauder - to debilitate the caster's enemies with hexes and batter them with violent winds. Spell power increases the sphinxes' durability and the power of their spells.":"召唤一对善出谜题的斯芬克斯——一只守卫、一只劫掠者—— 以妖术削弱敌人并用狂风猛击。法术威力会提高其耐久与法术威力。","Constructs a frangible shell of reinforced ice in a half-circle around the caster, pushing creatures out of the way to make space for it, if possible.":"在施法者周围构筑一道半圆形的强化冰壳；如果空间允许， 它会将生物推开，为自身腾出位置。","This barricade is durable, and whenever a segment of it is destroyed, will fracture into a salvo of icy projectiles launched at whatever destroyed it.":"这道屏障十分坚固；每当一段冰壳被摧毁时，都会碎裂成一阵冰片， 向摧毁它的生物齐射。","If the caster strays too far away from their barrier, it will melt rapidly.":"如果施法者离屏障太远，冰壳会迅速融化。","Constructs a frangible shell of reinforced ice in a half-circle around the caster, pushing creatures out of the way to make space for it, if possible. This barricade is durable, and whenever a segment of it is destroyed, will fracture into a salvo of icy projectiles launched at whatever destroyed it. If the caster strays too far away from their barrier, it will melt rapidly.":"在施法者周围构筑一道半圆形的强化冰壳；如果空间允许， 它会将生物推开，为自身腾出位置。 这道屏障十分坚固；每当一段冰壳被摧毁时，都会碎裂成一阵冰片， 向摧毁它的生物齐射。 如果施法者离屏障太远，冰壳会迅速融化。","<Steam breath ability>":"<Steam Breath ability>","Casts forth sticks and transforms them into snakes. Stronger casters will always create stronger snakes.":"掷出棍棒并将其变成蛇；施法者越强，生成的蛇也必定越强。","Calls forth one of the mightiest and fastest mortal champions of the Shining One. In this Dungeon, spriggan defenders and deep elf blademasters will answer the call.":"召来光辉者麾下最强大、最迅捷的凡人冠军之一。 在这座地牢中，会响应召唤的是小精灵防御者和精灵剑圣。","Summons the egg of a brutish lizard, just on the verge of hatching. So long as there are foes nearby and the caster remains adjacent to the egg, it will hatch several turns after being summoned to wreak havoc upon its summoner's foes.":"召唤一颗即将孵化的地震龙蛋。只要附近有敌人且施法者始终与蛋相邻， 它便会在被召唤数回合后孵化，蹂躏召唤者的敌人。","Even as a juvenile, a seismosaurus is a force to be reckoned with. It is nearly as hardy as a mountain, and its footfalls are capable of creating violent seismic shockwaves. Each shockwave deals considerable damage to non-flying enemies, and may sometimes even cause them to lose their footing altogether.":"地震龙即使尚未成年也不容小觑。它坚韧得近乎山岳，脚步能产生猛烈的 地震冲击波。每道冲击波都会对不会飞的敌人造成大量伤害，有时甚至会 让它们彻底站立不稳。","Spell power increases the egg's durability and the strength of the seismosaur within, but not the time it takes to hatch.":"法术威力会提高蛋的耐久度和其中地震龙的力量，但不会缩短孵化时间。","Summons the egg of a brutish lizard, just on the verge of hatching. So long as there are foes nearby and the caster remains adjacent to the egg, it will hatch several turns after being summoned to wreak havoc upon its summoner's foes. Even as a juvenile, a seismosaurus is a force to be reckoned with. It is nearly as hardy as a mountain, and its footfalls are capable of creating violent seismic shockwaves. Each shockwave deals considerable damage to non-flying enemies, and may sometimes even cause them to lose their footing altogether. Spell power increases the egg's durability and the strength of the seismosaur within, but not the time it takes to hatch.":"召唤一颗即将孵化的地震龙蛋。只要附近有敌人且施法者始终与蛋相邻， 它便会在被召唤数回合后孵化，蹂躏召唤者的敌人。 地震龙即使尚未成年也不容小觑。它坚韧得近乎山岳，脚步能产生猛烈的 地震冲击波。每道冲击波都会对不会飞的敌人造成大量伤害，有时甚至会 让它们彻底站立不稳。 法术威力会提高蛋的耐久度和其中地震龙的力量，但不会缩短孵化时间。","Hurls a colossal bolas at the target, wrapping around even the largest of foes and binding them in place.":"向目标投掷一具巨型流星索；它甚至能缠住最庞大的敌人，将其束缚在原地。","Attempts to cloud the target's mind with thoughtless frustration, forcing them to spend several turns doing nothing but attacking nearby spaces (whether those spaces are empty or even contain their allies).":"以无谓的挫败感蒙蔽目标心智，迫使其数回合内只会攻击附近格子， 无论格子为空还是其中站着盟友。","Sends the caster hurtling at a chosen nearby enemy, launching a high-accuracy melee attack on arrival, with additional electrical damage based on spellpower. The caster is wrapped in an envelope of twisted space, allowing them to safely pass through creatures, traps, and harmful terrain, and to displace creatures at their destination.":"让施法者冲向选定的一个附近敌人，在近身时发动高精度的近战攻击， 并根据法术威力造成额外电击伤害。 施法者会被包裹在扭曲的空间中，因而能够安全穿过生物、陷阱和有害地形， 并置换目的地的生物。","Twists a creature's body with mutagenic corruption, doing a small amount of damage and inflicting a transient mutation. If the target is already suffering from multiple transient mutations, it will inflict Vitrify instead.":"以诱发变异的腐化力量扭曲一个生物的身体，造成少量伤害并施加一项短暂变异。 若目标已经受到多项短暂变异影响，则改为对其施加玻璃化。","Creates a brief but violent rift in space, damaging everything caught in its wake and sometimes blinking them a short distance away.":"短暂撕开一道猛烈的空间裂隙，伤害被卷入其中的一切， 并有时将它们短距离闪现到别处。","An ancient altar, stripped of all identifying characteristics by the passage of aeons. Praying at it will convert you to an unknown god, and the altar's deity will greatly appreciate conversion at so ancient a site of worship.":"一座古老的祭坛，时间冲刷掉了它的全部特征。 在那里祈祷，将会皈依一个未知的神。 祭坛的神灵会非常感念于你在这样古老的礼拜场所进行皈依。","An altar to the Shining One, made from the purest gold and almost blinding in its radiance.":"光辉者的祭坛，由最纯净的黄金制成，光辉几乎令人目眩。","A crystal altar which shattered to pieces when Ashenzari was cursed. There is still a great power remaining within it: a dark aura holds the shards in mid-explosion, suspended in time and space much like the god they herald.":"当艾申扎利被诅咒的时候，这座水晶祭坛也随之破碎。 这里依然残留着强大的力量： 黑色的光环将碎片定格在爆炸中期，悬停在时间和空间上，就像它们所昭示的神。","An altar to Beogh, unmistakably roughly hewn by orcish artisans.":"比欧弗的祭坛，做工粗糙，一眼就能看出是出自兽人工匠之手。","A timeless altar to Cheibriados the Contemplative.":"深思者切布理亚多的祭坛。","An altar to Dithmenos the Shadowed. It seems to absorb light from its surroundings.":"隐没者迪斯姆诺的祭坛。它似乎在吸收四周的光。","An altar to Elyvilon the Healer, made from purest white marble and topped by a sculpture of the Chalice of Purification.":"治愈者艾利维隆的祭坛，由纯白色大理石制成，顶端有净化之杯的雕像。","An altar to Fedhas Madash, covered in vibrant and colourful plant life.":"费德哈·莽动的祭坛，上面覆盖着生机盎然、色彩艳丽植物。","A glittering golden and bejewelled altar to Gozag Ym Sagoz the Greedy, gleaming brightly even in the dim dungeon light.":"贪婪者哥萨戈·亿·赛格斯的祭坛，金光闪闪、饰以珠宝， 即使在昏暗的地牢也熠熠生辉。","An altar to Hepliaklqana the Forgotten, shrouded in mist and difficult to make out clearly. Something about it seems terribly familiar, but it's impossible to say exactly why.":"遗忘者惠普利亚卡纳的祭坛，被笼罩在薄雾中，难以清晰辨认。 有些东西似曾相识，但很难说清原因。","An altar to Ignis, the Dying Flame. It's completely covered in candles of all shapes and sizes, but only one remains alight, its slender flame wavering in the slightest breeze.":"伊格尼斯——垂死之火的祭坛。祭坛完全被形状、大小各异的蜡烛覆盖，但只有一根仍在燃烧；它纤细的火焰在最轻微的风中摇曳。","A slimy, ever-shifting altar to Jiyva. You're not sure what it's made from, and you don't really want to know.":"吉瓦的祭坛，黏滑、在不断变形。 你不确定这祭坛到底是用什么材料制造的，而且你也不想知道。","An altar created from piles of ancient bones, dedicated to the terrible Demon-God Kikubaaqudgha.":"这座用远古骸骨堆积成的祭坛供奉的是恐怖的魔神——奇库巴库哈。","An altar to Lugonu the Unformed, possibly dedicated to some other power before it was irrevocably corrupted.":"无形之神卢格努的祭坛， 这祭坛也许曾供奉过别的神祗，但现在已经不可逆转地被腐化了。","An ever-burning altar to Makhleb the Destroyer. Strange, twisting shapes are visible in the flames.":"毁灭者马科列布的祭坛，上面永远燃烧着火焰。 透过火焰，可以隐约看到一些奇特而扭曲的形状。","An altar sparkling with a lightshow brighter than any gambling den's, to attract followers for Nemelex Xobeh.":"这座祭坛上的灯光秀比任何赌场都更加耀眼，以此为尼姆雷斯·索布吸引信徒。","An altar of iron and steel dedicated to the Warmaster Okawaru. Its edges are surprisingly sharp.":"一座供奉战争之主奥卡瓦鲁的钢铁祭坛。祭坛的边缘出奇地锋利。","An altar dedicated to Qazlal Stormbringer, surrounded by fierce winds, electrical discharges, puffs of fire and magma, and the occasional tremor.":"兴风者卡兹拉尔的祭坛， 被包裹在狂风、闪电、喷涌的烈火和岩浆之中，时而与之震颤。","An altar to Ru the Awakened in the shape of a pair of scales, with a heart in one scale and a pictogram representing power and enlightenment in the other.":"觉醒者入的祭坛， 其外形是个天平，一个托盘中放有心，而另一个托盘中的符号象征力量和觉悟。","An altar to Sif Muna the Loreminder, covered in intricate patterns and writings in long forgotten scripts. Atop a deep blue pedestal hovers a shimmering condensation of pure magic.":"学识之主西芙·穆娜的祭坛，上面布满了错综复杂的图案和久久被遗忘的文字。 在深蓝色的基座上，盘旋着纯净的魔法凝结的光芒。","An altar to Trog the Wrathful, crudely made by what seem to be the hands of giants and covered with bloodstains.":"狂怒者特洛格的祭坛，它做工粗糙，像是由巨人建造的，上面溅满了鲜血。","An altar to Uskayaw the Reveller. It appears to be hollow and covered in a hide, giving it a resonant surface. Carvings on the side depict grouped figures that could be dancing or loving or fighting.":"狂欢者乌斯卡亚的祭坛。它似乎中空，表面覆有兽皮，因而能够产生共鸣。侧面的雕刻描绘着成群的人影，可能在舞蹈、相爱或战斗。","An altar, ablaze in the lights of Iskenderun and promising great destructive powers to those who would follow Vehumet.":"这座祭坛闪耀在伊斯肯德伦之光中，好像在对来人许诺： 只要追随维胡梅特，他就会赐予你无比的毁灭之力。","A red and gold altar to the Wu Jian Council. Sharp slivers of steel drift through the quiet air surrounding it.":"无间门派的红金相间的祭坛。锋利的钢片在周围安静的空气中飘过。","An altar constantly shimmering in all visible colours, and probably some invisible ones, matching the whims of Xom the Unpredictable.":"这座祭坛不断闪现着各色光芒，甚至可能还有不可见光， 和这座祭坛所供奉的神祗无常之主佐姆一样，变幻莫测。","An altar to Yredelemnul the Dark, worked from columnar basalt.":"黑暗神伊莱德莱姆努尔的祭坛，由柱状玄武岩建成。","An altar to Zin the Law-Giver, made from silver as pristine as Zin's followers are expected to be, and glowing gently.":"定法者辛的祭坛，由银制成，与辛的追随者们所期望的一样纯净，柔和地发着光。","The floor.":"地面。","A pool of deep water. Only giant creatures can wade through this, and only those well-adapted to water can swim through it; for the rest, the only way through is to fly over.":"一个深水池。 只有巨型生物可以趟过去，水性好的则可以游；而其他的，就只能选择飞过去。","An intensely hot pool of molten rock, emitting clouds of sulphurous smoke. Nothing but the mythical salamander can cross this without flight.":"一个炽热的熔岩池，喷吐着硫磺烟云。 只有传说中的火蜥蜴才能不凭借飞行就能穿越它。","A pool of cloudy, waist-deep water. Those well-adapted to water can swim through it and attack normally. Non-swimmers must wade through the water slowly and will occasionally fail to attack in melee when wading through shallow water; although large creatures are able to keep their balance, move at a normal speed, and avoid fumbling.":"一个浑浊的水池，深及腰部。 水性好的可以游过水，并能正常攻击。 不会游泳的必须缓慢地涉水，在趟过浅水时，有时会在近战中失手； 但大型生物能够以正常速度移动，以保持平衡，避免摔倒。","A filthy pool of poisonous, waist-deep sludge. Wading or swimming through the sludge will damage and poison any creature, even those resistant to poison. Those well-adapted to water can swim through it and attack normally. Non-swimmers must wade through the water slowly and will occasionally fail to attack in melee when wading through shallow water; although large creatures are able to keep their balance, move at a normal speed, and avoid fumbling.":"一个肮脏、有毒的淤泥池，深及腰部。 在淤泥中涉水或游泳会让任何生物中毒受伤，甚至是那些有毒抗的生物。 水性好的可以游过它，并能正常攻击。 不会游泳的必须缓慢地涉水，在趟过浅水时，有时会在近战中失手； 但大型生物能够以正常速度移动，以保持平衡，避免摔倒。","An expanse of endless wind and waves, with not a lighthouse in sight. Anyone venturing across it would be lost beyond all hope in short order.":"前方只有无尽的风浪，在你视野可及之处都没有一座灯塔。 任何冒险要穿越它的人，很快都会失去一切希望。","A wall imbued with magic that makes it indestructible.":"这面墙被注入魔力，坚不可摧。","A wall made from the weird stuff which makes up Pandemonium. It seems to be like rock in most other aspects.":"这面墙由构筑万魔殿的奇特材料制成。在其他大多数方面，它似乎都和岩石一样。","A wall made from polished crystal and imbued with arcane magics. They prevent its easy destruction, and make it reflect heat and cold.":"这面墙由抛光水晶制成，充满了奥术魔力。 这使得墙难以被轻易破坏，并能反射热和冷。","A rock wall made from a mineral as translucent as good quality glass. Whether it is natural or magical, you cannot tell.":"这面岩墙由一种像优质玻璃那样透明的矿物制成。 你不确定它的这种性质是自然的还是被魔法改造的。","A harder obstacle than rock walls. Only the mightiest magic can shatter stone walls. It has been imbued with arcane magics which render it translucent.":"这是比岩墙更难对付的障碍。只有最强力的魔法才能打碎石墙。 这面墙壁被注入奥术魔法，因此变成了透明的。","A wall imbued with magic that not only makes it indestructible but also makes it translucent like glass.":"这面墙被注入魔力，不仅使它坚不可摧，还让它变得像玻璃一样半透明。","A harder obstacle than rock walls. Only the mightiest magic can shatter stone walls.":"这是比岩墙更难对付的障碍。只有最强力的魔法才能打碎石墙。","A rock wall coated with acidic green slime; just standing near it is enough to cause temporary corrosion.":"这面岩墙附着着亮绿色的黏液。它摸起来是酸性的；站在它附近就会被暂时腐蚀。","A wall of bluish-grey metal. As every dungeon electrician knows, it will ground even magical bolts of lightning.":"一面蓝灰色金属墙。地牢中的每个电工都知道，它甚至能让闪电箭接地。","A wall consisting of simple rock.":"这仅仅是一面岩墙。","A staircase leading further down.":"一个通往下层的楼梯。","A staircase leading back up.":"一个通往上层的楼梯。","A large tree. While in most places the dim light of the dungeon is not bright enough to sustain large plants, there are spots where, with the grace of Fedhas, trees as big as those on the surface can grow underground.":"一棵大树。在地牢的大多地方，昏暗的光线不足以维持大型植物的生长， 但有些地方，受到费德哈的关照，在地下生长的树木也长得和地表的一样大。","This tree is specially adapted for growing in swampy conditions. Its vines are too thick to see through.":"这种树特别适合在沼泽环境中生长。它的藤蔓很茂密，看不到对面。","A tree hideously warped by the demonic forces of chaos. Despite its bizarre appearance and occasional, unsettling movement, it seems harmless.":"一棵被混乱的恶魔力量扭曲的树。 尽管外形怪异，偶尔还会有令人不安的动作，但它似乎是无害的。","A shop that has been abandoned.":"这间商店已经被废弃了。","An idol of the orc god Beogh.":"一尊兽人之神比欧弗的塑像。","A rusted iron grate, brittle enough to be disrupted with a spell or a wand quite easily. It is too strong to be breakable by hand, however.":"一个生锈的铁门，可以用法术或法杖轻易破坏。但徒手还是不行。","A spring-loaded one-way escape hatch set in the dungeon floor, allowing the adventurer beset by adversaries to exchange the perils of this level for the perils of the next.":"地牢的地面上一个单向逃生口， 让被敌人围困的冒险者可以选择使用它逃离眼下的危险，面对下一层的危险。","A spring-loaded one-way escape hatch set in the ceiling.":"天花板上一个装有弹簧的单向逃生口。","A hole in the ground, leading to a dungeon level one or more floors deeper.":"地面上的一个洞，通往更深一层或多层的地牢。","A descending passage sealed tightly by a magical barricade. It is impossible to climb through it so long as the magic holds.":"一条下行的通道，被魔法路障牢固地封印着。只要魔力一直存在，就不可能穿过它。","An ascending passage sealed tightly by a magical barricade. It is impossible to climb through it so long as the magic holds.":"一条上行的通道，被魔法路障牢固地封印着。只要魔力一直存在，就不可能穿过它。","A stone archway that seems to lead to nowhere in particular.":"一个石拱门，看起来无法通往任何地方。","An unstable gateway that allows instantaneous travel to another nearby passage of Golubria, and will close behind anything passing through it.":"这个不稳定的传送门让你瞬间传送到附近的另一个格鲁布里亚的通道上， 只要有任何东西通过这个传送门，它就会立刻关闭。","A gash-like tear in reality that looks into some terrifying, starry otherworld. Thankfully, the magic that opened it also prevents its vacuum from consuming and swallowing everything in sight.":"现实空间中的一道伤口般的裂缝，揭示着某个可怕的、繁星点点的另一个世界。 幸运的是，打开这道裂缝的魔法同时也会阻止它将视线中的一切东西尽数吞没。","A stone statue whose features have long since withered away.":"一座石像，其形象早已被时间消磨。","A wall made of pure silver, formed by the power of Zin to temporarily imprison a monster within its confines.":"一面纯银制成的墙，由辛的力量生成，用来将一个怪物暂时囚禁起来。","A dried-up decorative fountain that has seen better days.":"一个干涸的喷泉，见证过美好的岁月。","A decorative fountain, flowing with clear water.":"一个装饰性喷泉，水流清澈。","A decorative fountain, spurting with foul-looking blood.":"一个装饰性喷泉，喷着看上去肮脏的血液。","A decorative fountain, flowing with brightly sparkling, faintly magic water.":"一个装饰性喷泉，流淌着闪烁、起泡的水。","An unearthly, glittering light, floating and twisting in midair. A Rune of Zot is surely nearby, its power overspilling to cause this spectacular sight.":"一道超自然、闪耀的光芒，在半空中飘浮、扭曲。 附近肯定有个佐特符文，它溢出的能量生成出这一壮观的景象。","A cursed staircase leading further down, imbued with magic to prevent any return back up the stairs. Adventurers taking this passage will need to find a return stairway somewhere else on the level where they arrive.":"一个被诅咒的通往下层的楼梯，注入着魔力，以阻止任何回返。 走这条通道的冒险者，到达所通往的楼层后，需要找到其他能够返回楼梯。","A cursed staircase leading up, imbued with magic to prevent any return back down the stairs. Adventurers taking this passage will need to find a return stairway somewhere else on the level where they arrive.":"一个被诅咒的通往上层的楼梯，注入着魔力，以阻止任何回返。 走这条通道的冒险者，到达所通往的楼层后，需要找到其他能够返回楼梯。","A gate leading back to the dungeon.":"一个返回地牢的大门。","A gate leading to yet another region of Pandemonium. There'll always be more.":"一个通往万魔殿另一片区域的大门。万魔殿无穷无尽。","A gate leading to the endless halls of Pandemonium.":"一个通往万魔殿无尽厅堂的单向大门。","A staircase leading to the Depths.":"一个通往地底的楼梯。","A gate leading to the Realm of Zot.":"一个通往佐特领域的大门。","A gate which allows a feat popularly thought to be impossible: escaping Hell alive.":"这道大门能让你做到一件通常被认为不可能的事：活着逃出地狱。","A gateway out of the Abyss, shimmering and shifting in the impermanent landscape.":"一个离开深渊的出口，在无常的景象中发光变幻。","A strangely calm gateway amid the roiling landscape of the Abyss. It leads further into the depths of the Abyss.":"一个出奇平静的入口，坐落在深渊那混沌的景象中。它通向深渊的更深处。","A portal leading to a ziggurat.":"一个通往金字塔的门户。","A gateway leading to Gehenna.":"一个通往欣嫩谷的入口。","A gateway leading back to the Vestibule of Hell.":"一个返回地狱前庭的出口。","A gateway leading to the Vestibule of Hell. Few would go there voluntarily.":"一个通往地狱前庭的入口。很少有人自愿前往那个地方。","A gateway leading to the Iron City of Dis.":"一个通往狄斯铁城的入口。","<A gateway leading out of Gehenna>":"<A gateway leading out of Gehenna>","A gateway leading to Tartarus.":"一个通往塔尔塔罗斯的入口。","A gateway leading to Cocytus.":"一个通往悲叹河的入口。","A passage leading to the Spider Nest.":"一个通往蜘蛛巢的通道。","A gateway leading to the Abyss.":"一个通往深渊的入口。","A passage leading back to the Lair of Beasts.":"一个返回兽穴的出口。","A gateway leading back to the dungeon via the madness of the Abyss.":"一个通过疯狂的深渊返回地牢的出口。","A staircase leading back up to the familiarity of the dungeon.":"一个返回你遇到过的地牢楼层的楼梯。","A staircase leading back up to the Lair of Beasts.":"一个返回兽穴的楼梯。","A staircase leading back to the Orcish Mines.":"一个返回兽人矿井的楼梯。","A staircase leading back to the Vaults.":"一个返回宝库的楼梯。","This staircase leads back out of the dungeon.":"这个楼梯，穿过它能离开地牢。","A staircase leading out of the dungeon. Climbing these stairs will end your quest, whether you carry the Orb with you or not.":"这个楼梯是离开地牢的出口。爬上这些楼梯会结束你的探索，无论是否携带宝珠。","This staircase leads back out of the dungeon. A staircase leading out of the dungeon. Climbing these stairs will end your quest, whether you carry the Orb with you or not.":"这个楼梯，穿过它能离开地牢。 这个楼梯是离开地牢的出口。爬上这些楼梯会结束你的探索，无论是否携带宝珠。","A staircase leading back to the Crypt.":"一个返回墓室的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Crypt.":"一个通往墓室的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Ecumenical Temple.":"一个通往众神庙的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Elven Halls.":"一个通往精灵殿堂的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Lair of Beasts.":"一个通往兽穴的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Orcish Mines.":"一个通往兽人矿井的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Shoals.":"一个通往海滩的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Slime Pits.":"一个通往黏液坑洞的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Snake Pit.":"一个通往蛇穴的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Swamp.":"一个通往沼泽的楼梯。","A staircase leading to the Tomb of the Ancients.":"一个通往坟冢的楼梯。","A gateway leading to the Vaults.":"一个通往宝库的入口。","A one-way portal to another place on this level. When using a transporter, adjacent allies and monsters will travel with you to the other side.":"一个通往同层的另一个地方的传送门。 当使用了这个传送门，旁边的盟友和怪物也会随你一起到达另一边。","The destination site of a transporter. As the portal is one-way, you cannot use this location to return back through the transporter.":"传送门的目的地。由于这个传送门是单向的，你无法通过此位置的传送门返回。","A closed wooden door. All monsters that can wield equipment, and some of them that can't, may open it again. If it is opened by a monster while it is aware of you, it has a chance of breaking.":"一扇关闭的木门。如果被怪物打开，它可能会破裂。","A disappointingly poorly maintained wooden door. It'd take nothing short of magic to get this properly closed again.":"一扇令人失望、维护不善的木门。要想恰当地关闭它，只有魔法能做到。","An open door made from magically translucent wood. If closed again, all monsters that can wield equipment, and some of them that can't, could open it again. If it is closed and reopened by a monster that is aware of you, it has a chance of breaking.":"这扇打开的门由神奇的半透明木材制成。如果被怪物重新打开，它可能会破裂。","A closed door made from magically translucent wood. All monsters that can wield equipment, and some of them that can't, may open it again. If it is opened by a monster while it is aware of you, it has a chance of breaking.":"这扇关闭的门由神奇的半透明木材制成。所有能使用装备的怪物及一些不能使用装备的怪物 都可能再次打开它。若怪物在察觉到你的情况下打开它，门有概率破裂。","<A broken door>":"<A broken door>","A door sealed tightly by arcane runes. It refuses to open for any creature not recognised by its magic.":"这扇门被奥术符文牢固地封印着。只有被这扇门上面的魔法承认的生物才能打开它。","A door, covered in runic writing. It looks like there is something special behind it — perhaps danger, perhaps treasure. You may break the runes by opening it like any other door, but creatures of the dungeon will not dare to try.":"这扇门上满是符文记号。 门的后面应该有什么特别的东西——可能是危险，也可能是宝藏。 像打开其他门那样就能破坏符文，但地牢里的生物可不敢尝试。","<An open door>":"<An open door>","<A closed door>":"<A closed door>","<A runed door>":"<A runed door>","<A sealed door>":"<A sealed door>","<An open translucent door>":"<An open translucent door>","<A closed translucent door>":"<A closed translucent door>","<A broken translucent door>":"<A broken translucent door>","Anyone stepping on this trap will translocate themselves and anyone else in view to a new location nearby. Hostile monsters may trigger this trap, but your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"任何踩上这个陷阱的人都会将自己和视野中的其他怪物转移到附近的新位置。 敌对的怪物可能会故意触发这个陷阱，而你的盟友会避免踩到它。","After triggering, it cannot be triggered again for several turns.":"触发后，它在数回合内无法再次触发。","Anyone stepping on this trap will translocate themselves and anyone else in view to a new location nearby. Hostile monsters may trigger this trap, but your allies will avoid stepping on it. After triggering, it cannot be triggered again for several turns.":"任何踩上这个陷阱的人都会将自己和视野中的其他怪物转移到附近的新位置。 敌对的怪物可能会故意触发这个陷阱，而你的盟友会避免踩到它。 触发后，它在数回合内无法再次触发。","A large concealed net launcher hanging from the dungeon's ceiling. Enchanted by the power of Zot, whenever an intelligent creature steps here - whether friend or foe - the net will land only on you.":"一个挂在地牢天花板上的巨大而隐蔽的网。 它被佐特注入魔力，每当有智慧生物来到这里——无论是敌是友——网只会落你身上。","A trigger of some sort. You cannot tell what kind of trap it is attached to. Its complicated detection system will trigger the trap even when someone flies over it.":"某种触发机关。你无法确定它所连接的陷阱的类型。 它有着复杂的探测系统，即便是飞过也会触发陷阱。","A magical trap which will displace anyone passing over it to a random place on the same dungeon level. It is worn with age, and will dissipate on use.":"这个魔力陷阱，任何经过它的人会被传送到这层地牢的一个随机地点。 它会被消磨，一旦被激活就会消散。","A magical trap which will displace anyone passing over it to a random place on the same dungeon level.":"这个魔力陷阱，任何经过它的人会被传送到这层地牢的一个随机地点。","A spider's web. The spider who left it must have been huge, as it seems to be made for trapping {{ return you.genus(true) }} rather than flies.":"一个蜘蛛网。留下这张网的蜘蛛肯定是个大家伙， 因为这似乎是用来诱捕{{ return crawl.t_(you.genus()) }}而不是苍蝇的。","A trap which inflicts dangerously unpredictable magical effects on those unlucky enough to step on it. You may find yourself petrified, contaminated with enormous amounts of wild magic, have mighty fiends summoned against you, or the like. Hostile monsters may trigger this trap themselves to invoke its effects against you, but your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"这个陷阱，会对那些不幸踩到陷阱的人造成危险、不可预知的魔法效果。 你可能会发现自己陷入深渊，被大量的野性魔法污染， 被召唤出的强大的恶魔来对付你，等等。 敌对的怪物可能会故意触发这个陷阱从而对你引起效果，而你的盟友会避免踩到它。","A portal leading to a gauntlet.":"一个通往竞技场的门户。","A portal leading to an ice cave. The archway is gradually melting away.":"一个通往冰窟的门户。拱门在渐渐融化。","A portal leading to a glacial chasm, far more dangerous than the icy caverns found in the shallower reaches of the Dungeon. The archway is gradually melting away.":"一个通往冰川裂缝的门户，比地牢浅层的冰窟危险得多。拱门在渐渐融化。","A staircase leading to an ossuary. Sand is continuously pouring onto it, gradually blocking the entrance.":"一个通往埋骨地的楼梯。沙子在不断倾泻，会逐渐封住入口。","A passage leading to a sewer. It is gradually rusting away.":"一个通往下水道的通道。它在逐渐锈蚀。","A portal leading to a treasure trove. This portal is unstable and will collapse after a single use.":"一个通往库藏的门户。这个门户一旦被使用过就会变得不稳定，并会崩溃。","A portal leading to the heart of a volcano. Rocks are falling from the roof and sides of the tunnel, filling the entry.":"一个通往火山的门户。岩石不断从隧道顶部和侧面落下，将会堵住入口。","A salt-encrusted arch, covered with carved entreaties to the good gods to contain the evils sealed therein. Whatever protections this arch once offered have finally succumbed to the ravages of time, and a bitter breeze pours forth from the distant land beyond.":"一个被盐渍的拱门，上面雕满了诸善神，以求掩盖其中的邪恶。 这座拱门曾提供的任何保护终都屈服于时间的摧残， 遥远的土地上倾泻着刺骨的微风。","A portal leading to a wizard's laboratory. It is fading away.":"一个通往巫师实验室的门户。它在逐渐消失。","An unstable passage in the volcanic rock, admitting a draft of cool air from beyond. It leads back to the place you came from. You will be unable to return here once you pass through it.":"一个火山岩体中不稳定的通道，外面的冷空气可以从中进入。 它导向你回到原来的地方。一旦你穿过它，就再也无法回来了。","A stone wall on the brink of collapsing from disrepair but somehow remaining standing, seemingly frozen in time.":"一面因年久失修而濒临坍塌的石墙，不知何故屹立不倒，仿佛凝固在时间里。","A statue with strange and alien features. Is it because the statue is worn and tarnished that it has become so unrecognisable? Or is it that the subject was something demonic and evil?":"这座雕塑看起来非常奇怪诡异。雕塑是因为磨损和失去光泽，就变得如此难以辨认？ 还是它的主题就是什么恶魔和邪恶的东西？","A wall covered with disturbing, horrifying images.":"这面墙上满是令人不安、恐怖图案。","The floor. It is rough and uneven in places.":"地面。有些地方粗糙不平。","A wall that looks strangely organic, but incredibly tough and durable.":"这面墙看起来像奇怪有机体，但却惊人地坚韧。","A strange membrane, thin enough to see through.":"这层奇怪的膜很薄，可以透过它看东西。","The floor. It pulses to an unknown beat.":"地面。它以未知的节奏搏动着。","A nameless grave.":"一个无名的墓碑。","<A crystal wall>":"<A crystal wall>","A wall made from low-grade crystal with an opalescent gleam.":"这面墙由次等水晶制成，有着乳白色的光芒。","A wall decorated with images of death and destruction.":"这面墙上装饰着死亡和破坏的图案。","The dry remains of a long-dead tree.":"一棵死去已久的树的干枯残骸。","The dry remains of a long-dead mangrove.":"一棵死去已久的红树的干枯残骸。","A base type statue for other statue flavours. If you see this, file a bug report.":"一座其他风格雕塑的基本款雕塑。如果你碰到这个，请提交错误报告。","Walls of brass and nickel, covered in a thin golden foil steadily peeling away in the constant, oppressive heat. Designs depict mortals dealing with devils, but the former rarely seem to come out ahead on the exchange.":"这面墙由黄铜和镍制成，上面覆盖着的一层薄薄金箔在持续的高温下不断脱落。 图案描绘着凡人与魔鬼在做交易，但前者似乎很少能在交易中占上风。","A stone wall coated in a thick layer of ice. Twisted faces glower beneath the surface, locked in perpetual grimaces of rage and betrayal.":"这面石墙上有一层厚厚的冰霜。 表层下有扭曲的脸在怒目而视，这张愤怒和背叛的怪相永远被定格着。","Earth locked within perpetual frost and cold. It seems ageless and changeless, as though it has existed in this state for an eternity.":"这片地面永远被凝结在冰霜和寒冷之中。 它似乎是永驻的、不变的，仿佛这种状态已存在了永恒的时光。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its malevolent cursed energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其恶毒的诅咒能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its extraplanar warp energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其界外能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its negative energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其负能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its venomous churning energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其搅动的有毒能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its ever-burning energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其不断燃烧的能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its chilling cold energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其冷酷的能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its seismic energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其地震的能量会无害地消散。","A strange but benign metal construct, analysing raw ambient magical energy. If destroyed and disrupted by sufficiently mighty magic, its crackling energy will harmlessly disperse.":"一个奇怪但坚固的金属结构，在收集和分析原始的环境魔法能量。 如果它被足够强大的魔法摧毁破坏，其爆裂的能量会无害地消散。","A strangely slime-free stone wall, with strange lights twinkling within its airy confines. Mystical runes are scattered across its surface, seemingly referring to a 'Royal Jelly'.":"一面奇怪的没有黏液的石墙，在它的流通区域，闪着奇异的光。 上面散布着的神秘符文，似乎在谈及一个“皇家胶冻”。","A crystal wall etched with murals depicting, in great and gruesome detail, exactly what will be done to anyone caught stealing from the Vaults.":"这面水晶墙上蚀刻着壁画， 以极其可怕的细节描绘着从宝库中盗窃被抓的人的悲惨下场。","A portal leading back to the place you came from. Its magic is holding the ice at bay, preventing it from blocking the gate. You will be unable to return here once you pass through it.":"这个门户导向你回到原来的地方。 其魔力将冰挡在海湾，阻止它堵塞大门。一旦你穿过它，就再也无法回来了。","A rock wall covered by a thick layer of frost and ice.":"这面岩墙上有一层厚厚的冰霜。","A pool of deep water, crusted with broken blocks of ice.":"一个深水池，表面冻结成了碎冰块。","A pool of shallow water, crusted with broken blocks of ice.":"一个浅水池，表面冻结成了碎冰块。","An ancient tree, long ago passed from biology into geology. While no longer wooden in a material sense, it retains the spiritual qualities of a tree.":"一棵古树，很久以前就从生物学转入地质学意义。 虽然它在物质意义上不再是木质的，但保留了树的精神品质。","This area is wreathed by an umbra, improving your stealth if you are attuned to the shadows, and decreasing the accuracy of attacks by those unattuned to the shadows.":"这个区域被本影环绕，如果你被阴影所遮蔽，你的潜行能力得到提升， 那些无法适应阴影的怪物的攻击精度会降低。","The ground here is liquefied, making movement slow and causing any attempts to attack in melee to sometimes fail.":"这片地面被液化，移动会被减缓，发出任何近战攻击都有可能失手。","This area is bathed in translocational energy, causing creatures to blink away from the originator of the energy with an increasing chance the closer they are to the caster.":"这个区域暴露在移位能量中， 能量的发出者那里的生物会被闪送，距离施法者越近，几率就越大。","This tree has been temporarily enchanted to grant it some limited motility, allowing it to lash out out at any adjacent enemies of the creature who awoke it.":"这棵树被暂时注入魔力，从而获得一些有限的活动能力， 它会猛烈攻击任何相邻的与唤醒它的生物为敌的怪物。","It is susceptible to bolts of lightning and to sufficiently intense sources of fire. The resulting blaze can flare up, spreading to areas nearby and igniting other trees.":"它容易受到闪电和足够强烈的火源的影响。 由此产生的大火可能会蔓延到附近区域，引燃其他树木。","It is susceptible to bolts of lightning and to sufficiently intense sources of fire. Mangroves do not burn as vigorously as normal trees, due to growing on swampy terrain, and leave behind shallow water after they smoulder.":"它容易受到闪电和足够强烈的火源的影响。 由于生长在沼泽地带，红树燃烧起来不像普通树木那样旺盛，在闷烧后会留下浅水。","It is susceptible to bolts of lightning and to sufficiently intense sources of fire. Burning this tree releases a cloud of pure chaos instead of flames.":"它容易受到闪电和足够强烈的火源的影响。 这棵树燃烧会释放出纯粹的混乱云而不是火焰云。","A delicate arrangement, smashed to pieces and consigned to slow starvation.":"一件精致的插花布置，被砸成碎片并被遗弃而缓慢枯萎。","A hoard of breadstuffs, baked and fried from minor divine gifts of flour and growth cultures, granted extended shelflife through sacred succour. You already carry as much food as you will ever need for this journey, but a light snack shouldn't hurt.":"一堆烘焙食品，由面粉和发酵培养物等小型神圣礼物烘焙和油炸而成， 通过神圣援助获得了延长的保质期。你已经携带了此行所需的所有食物， 但来点小零食应该无妨。","A pile of assorted fruit, ranging from common dungeon staples like chokos and snozzcumbers, to rarer treats such as apples and oranges. You already carry as much food as you will ever need for this journey, but the occasional nibble wouldn't hurt.":"一堆各式水果，从地牢常见的主食如苦瓜和斯诺兹黄瓜，到较稀有的 美味如苹果和橙子。你已经携带了此行所需的所有食物， 但偶尔吃点也无妨。","A stash of preserved meats of varied origins and preparations: strips of jerky, lumpy smoked sausages, and indeterminate protein rations. You already carry as much food as you will ever need for this journey, but this could offer the rare chance to try out yak...":"一批来自不同来源和制备方法的保存肉类：肉干条、块状熏香肠， 以及不确定的蛋白质口粮。你已经携带了此行所需的所有食物， 但这提供了一个难得的机会来尝尝牦牛肉……","A murky flag of dark conquest shimmering with vile energies, planted in the name of some grand despoiling crusade.":"一面黑暗征服的阴沉旗帜，闪烁着邪恶的能量， 以某场宏大的亵渎远征之名插在此处。","A base floor type for various decorations one can walk over. If you see this, file a bug report.":"用于各种可以走过的装饰物的基础地板类型。如果你看到这个，请报告程序错误。","A magical trap linked by divine cruelty to the stomachs of some unfathomable interdimensional predators. When you or a hostile monster steps on it, it has a high chance it will expel digestive acid onto you, corroding you. Your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"一个由神圣残酷与某些无法理解的跨维度捕食者的胃相连的魔法陷阱。 当你或敌对怪物踩到它时，它有很大概率向你喷出消化酸液，腐蚀你。 你的盟友会避免踩到它。","It is currently recharging and will become active again in a short while.":"它正在重新充能，将在短时间内再次激活。","A drum ensemble whose rhythm serves as peaceful recreation here in the depths of the earth.":"一套鼓组，其节奏在这地底深处作为和平的娱乐。","A bed of hardy wildflowers, thriving in this place despite everything.":"一片坚韧的野花，尽管一切困难仍在此地茁壮成长。","A decorative fountain, bubbling over with listless and unmoving eyes.":"一座装饰性喷泉，冒着呆滞不动的眼睛。","A wall that radiates a chill so intense it can damage enemies which stand next to it.":"一堵散发着如此强烈寒气的墙，可以伤害站在旁边的敌人。","A grooming brush laid to rest beside a pile of tangled, matted yak fur.":"一把梳理刷，安放在一堆纠结打结的牦牛毛旁边。","A small decorative plot of flowers penned in by cobblestone.":"一小块被鹅卵石围起来的装饰性花地。","A magical trap left behind by the ineffable, spectacular revues of chaos. When you or a hostile monster steps on it, up to three of the strongest monsters in sight will have their attacks temporarily interwoven with a touch of chaos. Your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"一个由不可言说的混沌之壮丽奇观遗留下的魔法陷阱。当你或敌对怪物踩到它时， 视野中最多三个最强怪物的攻击将暂时被混入一丝混沌。你的盟友会避免踩到它。","<A runed translucent door>":"<A runed translucent door>","A staircase leading up from the grand vaults containing the silver rune of Zot, whose wealth attracts the most powerful champions from across the Dungeon to its defence.":"一道从藏有佐特之银符文的宏大宝库向上走的金属楼梯， 其财富吸引了整个地牢中最强大的冠军来保卫它。","A mop and bucket, useful for keeping one's environs orderly and clean. Too bad you're here now.":"一把拖把和水桶，有助于保持周围环境的整洁。可惜你现在在这里了。","A coruscating spark gap of twin electrodes of impenetrably advanced technology. These are used to forge and power thaumaturgical constructs, though despite the constant crackling, this one is used up and unable to do much more than harmlessly dance with the joy of creating life.":"一个闪耀的火花间隙，由难以理解地先进的技术的双电极组成。 这些用于锻造和为奇术构造体供能，但尽管不断发出噼啪声， 这个已经耗尽，除了无害地舞动着创造生命的喜悦外无法做得更多。","A portal leading to one of many Necropolis repositories, where the freshly slain and deeply resentful are sealed away. This wandering rift will eventually move elsewhere to receive further dead.":"一道通往众多墓城贮藏库之一的传送门，那里封印着新近被杀和极度怨恨的死者。 这道游荡的裂隙最终会转移到其他地方接收更多死者。","A door, covered in runic writing, made from magically translucent wood. It has been created to seal away great danger or glorious treasure. You may break the runes by opening it like any other door, but creatures of the dungeon will not dare to try.":"一扇覆盖着符文文字的门，由魔法半透明木材制成。它被创造出来是为了封印 巨大的危险或辉煌的宝藏。你可以像打开任何其他门一样打开它来打破符文， 但地牢中的生物不敢尝试。","A mix of various alcoholic drinks with worn-down labels. Unfortunately, the preservative magic sealing each bottle makes it impossible to sample from them without smashing their bottles open.":"一组标签已磨损的各种酒精饮料。不幸的是，密封每个瓶子的保存魔法使得 不砸碎瓶子就无法品尝它们。","A stone staircase leading further down.":"一道通向更深处的石制楼梯。","{{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"It is slick with slippery slime, but that is no obstacle for one \" .. \"such as yourself who has embraced the way of all slime.\" else return \"It is slick with slippery slime which will make it impossible \" .. \"for you to climb back up again until the power ruling this place \" .. \"is destroyed (or you choose to join it). However, being coated in \" .. \"this slime will greatly increase your HP and MP regenaration for \" .. \"short while afterward.\" end }}":"{{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，但对于像你这样已接受万黏之道的人来说，\" .. \"这不是什么障碍。\" else return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，在统治此地的力量被摧毁（或你选择加入它）之前，\" .. \"你将无法再爬回来。然而，被这种黏液覆盖将在之后短时间内\" .. \"大大提高你的生命值和魔力恢复速度。\" end }}","A stone staircase leading further down. {{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"It is slick with slippery slime, but that is no obstacle for one \" .. \"such as yourself who has embraced the way of all slime.\" else return \"It is slick with slippery slime which will make it impossible \" .. \"for you to climb back up again until the power ruling this place \" .. \"is destroyed (or you choose to join it). However, being coated in \" .. \"this slime will greatly increase your HP and MP regenaration for \" .. \"short while afterward.\" end }}":"一道通向更深处的石制楼梯。 {{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，但对于像你这样已接受万黏之道的人来说，\" .. \"这不是什么障碍。\" else return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，在统治此地的力量被摧毁（或你选择加入它）之前，\" .. \"你将无法再爬回来。然而，被这种黏液覆盖将在之后短时间内\" .. \"大大提高你的生命值和魔力恢复速度。\" end }}","A stone staircase leading back up.":"一道往回向上的石制楼梯。","{{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"It is slick with slippery slime, but that is no obstacle for one \" .. \"such as yourself who has embraced the way of all slime.\" else return \"It is slick with slippery slime, making it impossible for you to \" .. \"climb until the power ruling this place is destroyed (or you choose \" .. \"to join it).\" end }}":"{{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，但对于像你这样已接受万黏之道的人来说，\" .. \"这不是什么障碍。\" else return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，在统治此地的力量被摧毁（或你选择加入它）之前，\" .. \"你无法攀爬。\" end }}","A stone staircase leading back up. {{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"It is slick with slippery slime, but that is no obstacle for one \" .. \"such as yourself who has embraced the way of all slime.\" else return \"It is slick with slippery slime, making it impossible for you to \" .. \"climb until the power ruling this place is destroyed (or you choose \" .. \"to join it).\" end }}":"一道往回向上的石制楼梯。 {{ if you.god() == \"Jiyva\" then return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，但对于像你这样已接受万黏之道的人来说，\" .. \"这不是什么障碍。\" else return \"它被滑溜的黏液覆盖着，在统治此地的力量被摧毁（或你选择加入它）之前，\" .. \"你无法攀爬。\" end }}","A magical contraption which skewers nearby monsters with sharp spikes. It will disintegrate after a short length of time or if the caster strays too far away from it.":"一个魔法装置，用锋利的尖刺刺穿附近的怪物。它会在短时间内瓦解， 或者如果施法者离它太远也会瓦解。","A statue of a terrifying globe of profound nothingness, said to dwell within the Realm of Zot.":"一座恐怖球体的雕像，据说它代表着深沉的虚无，居住在佐特之域中。","A statue of a terrifying globe of raw primordial fire, said to dwell within the Realm of Zot.":"一座恐怖球体的雕像，据说它代表着原始的火焰，居住在佐特之域中。","A statue of a terrifying globe of uttermost cold, said to dwell within the Realm of Zot.":"一座恐怖球体的雕像，据说它代表着极致的寒冷，居住在佐特之域中。","A magical trap built to bolster the armies of some conquering despot. When you or a hostile monster steps on it, your melee attacks will be weakened to make up to three of the most dangerous monsters in sight become stronger. Your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"一个为增强某个征服暴君的军队而建造的魔法陷阱。当你或敌对怪物踩到它时， 你的近战攻击将被削弱，使视野中最多三个最危险的怪物变得更强。 你的盟友会避免踩到它。","A wall made from orange crystal. It has a mind-boggling sheen.":"一堵由橙色水晶制成的墙。它有着令人费解的光泽。","A magical trap crafted by some avaricious master wizard. When you or a hostile monster steps on it, you will lose a percentage of your mp, while up to three of the strongest hostile spellcasters in sight will have their spells empowered. Your allies will avoid stepping on it.":"一个由某位贪婪的大师级巫师制作的魔法陷阱。当你或敌对怪物踩到它时， 你将失去一定比例的魔力，而视野中最多三个最强的敌对施法者的法术将被增强。 你的盟友会避免踩到它。","A raised pedestal upon which rests the fabled Orb of Zot. More ancient than even the dungeon itself, it cannot be destroyed or transformed by any means.":"一个高高升起的基座，上面放着传说中的佐特之球。它甚至比地牢本身还要古老， 无法以任何方式被摧毁或变形。","Bones are a common sight in the Dungeon, but skulls left impaled in a shrike's manner on display send a more deliberate message to trespassers: the pike has room for one more skull, and whoever set it up is happy to help relieve its owner of theirs.":"骸骨在地牢中是常见的景象，但以伯劳鸟的方式展示被刺穿的头骨 向侵入者传达了一个更刻意的信息：矛上还有空位再放一个头骨， 而设置它的人很乐意帮助其原主人把脑袋移过来。","An enchanted blade which loves nothing more than to sing to its owner, whether they want it to or not.":"这件被施了魔法的有刃武器最喜欢对它的主人唱歌， 至于主人想不想听它唱，它可管不着。","<Singing Sword>":"<Singing Sword>","A bloodstained axe that was the favourite weapon of the old god Trog, before it was lost. It induces a bloodthirsty berserker rage when used in battle, although mere mortals who wield it will find themselves temporarily overwhelmed by Trog's power.":"这把血迹斑斑的斧头在遗失之前，曾是古神特洛格最爱的武器。 当在战斗中使用它时，它会引发嗜血狂暴， 凡人哪怕只是装备它，暂时都会被特洛格的力量所压倒。","A large mace said to have appeared when Xom grew bored with the predictability of more ordinary instruments of chaos.":"据说，当佐姆厌倦了普通混沌工具那可预料的表现时，这把巨型钉头锤便出现了。","The glaive of Prune carries a terrible and insidious curse. Unless its wielder maintains firm self-control, they are doomed to undergo a horrifying (albeit temporary) transformation. This is normally trivial to resist, but incapacitated wielders are certain to succumb, finding themselves nightmarishly purple, squishy, and delicious. They can take comfort in learning that it's surprisingly hard to injure a giant prune.":"这把梅干大刀带有可怕而阴险的诅咒。 持有它的人除非有着坚定的自制力， 否则注定会经历一场可怕的（尽管只是暂时的）变形。 这通常很容易抵抗，但无能的持有者肯定会屈服，他们会发现自己变得湿软、美味， 颜色也变成梦魇般的紫色。 他们可以感到欣慰的是，弄伤一颗巨大的梅干却出人意料地难。","A staff which was once wielded by the great alchemist Olgreb.":"强大的炼金术士奥格雷布曾用过的一把法杖。","A sphere of flawless crystal, shaped by countless mantras. When one focuses upon it, the boundaries between 'self' and 'other' sometimes seem to blur. {{ if you.race() == \"Djinni\" then return \"It is utterly useless to Djinn.\" end }}":"一颗由无数咒语打磨而成的完美水晶球。当人们凝视它时， \"自我\"与\"他者\"之间的边界似乎有时会变得模糊。 {{ if you.race() == \"Djinni\" then return \"它对灯神完全无用。\" end }}","An ivory-like quick blade that looks like it could have been crafted from the tooth of some enormous predatory creature. It is lethally vampiric.":"一把形同象牙的快刃，看上去像是雕琢自某种巨型肉食动物的牙。它有着致命的吸血之力。","A scythe surrounded by an ominous aura of dread. It carries a terrible and ancient curse, which it busily inflicts on both the wielder and their enemies.":"一把被环绕在不祥的恐惧光环下的镰刀。 它带有一种可怕而古老的诅咒，还不断将诅咒施加给持有者和敌人。","An accursed bone sceptre, created by some unknown hellish power. When used in combat, it causes agonising pain in all those unfortunate enough to gaze upon it, save for the wielder.":"一把被诅咒的骨制节杖，由某种未知的地狱力量创造。 在战斗中使用时，它会给所有注视它的不幸者带来极度痛楚，除了持用者。","A twisted blade, covered in eerie flames. Its demonic power burns away at the very essence of those it is wielded against.":"一把扭曲的剑，周身被包裹在诡异的火焰中。它的恶魔力量会焚蚀敌人的本质。","An orb pulsing with unholy energies, granting the power to unleash damnation when held — although not without draining the wielder's vitality in the process. It carries with it some of the corrosive malice of the Iron City of Dis.":"这个涌动着邪恶能量的球体能赋予持有者释放天谴的能力， 但使用时也会汲取其生命力。它还带有几分狄斯铁城那腐蚀性的恶意。","A bright ruby sceptre, carrying some of the powers of the arch-fiend Asmodeus. It may call forth fiery demons from their infernal home to do the wielder's bidding.":"一把明亮的红宝石节杖，带有魔王阿斯摩蒂斯的某些力量。 持有者能凭借它召唤、号令来自地狱巢穴的火系恶魔。","An enchanted suit of armour created from the scales of a rare breed of dragon, now thought to be extinct. This prized relic is now one of the last proofs that the vividly coloured faerie dragons ever existed.":"这套魔力铠甲，由一种稀有品种的龙的鳞片制成，而这个物种现在被认为已经灭绝。 这件珍贵的遗物是色彩鲜艳的精灵龙曾经存在过的最后证据之一。","A blade forged in Hell by the sacrifice of countless tortured souls. It fills its wielder with the rage and suffering of those souls, and gorges itself further on drained life force every time it strikes, leaving behind a mess of blood and gore.":"通过献祭无数受难灵魂而在地狱锻造出的一把剑。 它让那些灵魂的愤怒和痛苦充斥着它的持有者， 每次命中还会大肆吞噬汲取的生命力，留下一片血肉狼藉。","A long and exceedingly sharp scythe, capable of eviscerating in a single blow. Its extraordinary speed is the work of a mad wizard, who spent years refining it before discarding it in a fit of rage.":"一把锋利的长镰刀，一击就能将内脏掏出。 它那非凡的速度是出自一个疯狂的巫师的杰作， 他花了数年时间改进它，却一怒之下将其丢弃。","The blade looses a low keen as it cuts through the air.":"刀刃划过空气，留下咻咻的声音。","A long and exceedingly sharp scythe, capable of eviscerating in a single blow. Its extraordinary speed is the work of a mad wizard, who spent years refining it before discarding it in a fit of rage. The blade looses a low keen as it cuts through the air.":"一把锋利的长镰刀，一击就能将内脏掏出。 它那非凡的速度是出自一个疯狂的巫师的杰作， 他花了数年时间改进它，却一怒之下将其丢弃。 刀刃划过空气，留下咻咻的声音。","A sling made of weird green leather, oozing corrosive slime. Originally the weapon of a notorious mischief-maker and general scamp, it's since fallen into less savoury hands.":"用奇怪的绿色皮革制成的投石索，渗出着腐蚀性的黏液。 它最初是臭名昭著的恶作剧制造者和小捣乱鬼的武器，后来落入令人不快的生物手中。","This bow was woven from the air itself by Eiolaiphi the air mage as a gift for one of the children of Uskayaw. The bow can be pulled with incredible speed, and it launches swift and true. It is also nearly indestructible, which is fortunate given that the original owner was ripped to pieces by jealous celebrants.":"这张弓由气法师埃奥莱菲将空气本身编织而成， 是送给乌斯卡亚某个孩子的礼物。它的弓弦拉动起来快得惊人， 射出的箭矢迅疾而精准。它也几乎坚不可摧——幸好如此， 因为原主人后来被嫉妒的欢庆者撕成了碎片。","A massive enchanted cudgel that augments the already considerable strength of anyone mighty enough to wield it.":"一根巨大被施入魔法的棍棒，会增强任何强大到能够挥舞它的人本就相当强大的力量。","A glaive commissioned several years ago by a wealthy queen fearful for the safety of her vast treasury. No foe, the smith promised, could defeat a guard wielding such a weapon!":"几年前，一位富有的女王委托制造一把大刀，她担心自己庞大的国库的安全。 铁匠保证，没有任何敌人能打败一个手持这把武器的卫兵！","It was stolen a few months later, along with the rest of the queen's treasury; the guard, it transpired, had been caught napping. Still, it should serve more than adequately in the hands of a waking user.":"几个月后，它和女王金库里的其他东西一起被盗；据透露，这名卫兵被发现在打盹。 不过，如果使用者保持清醒，它应该仍能大显身手。","A glaive commissioned several years ago by a wealthy queen fearful for the safety of her vast treasury. No foe, the smith promised, could defeat a guard wielding such a weapon! It was stolen a few months later, along with the rest of the queen's treasury; the guard, it transpired, had been caught napping. Still, it should serve more than adequately in the hands of a waking user.":"几年前，一位富有的女王委托制造一把大刀，她担心自己庞大的国库的安全。 铁匠保证，没有任何敌人能打败一个手持这把武器的卫兵！ 几个月后，它和女王金库里的其他东西一起被盗；据透露，这名卫兵被发现在打盹。 不过，如果使用者保持清醒，它应该仍能大显身手。","A sword made of one huge piece of crystal. Legend says it was the Shining One's gift to a worshipper. This blade is notorious for inducing bloodthirsty rage in both the wielder and all of their followers.":"这把剑由一大块巨型水晶制成。传言是光辉者赐予其信徒的。 这把剑因在持用者及其所有追随者中引起嗜血的狂暴而臭名昭著。","An unholy crossbow, forged in the fires of Gehenna. It imbues the bolts it fires with the raw power of its namesake. Thankfully, the blasts this weapon produces never harm the one firing.":"一把邪恶的弩，在欣嫩谷的火中锻造而成。它将天谴的原始力量注入弩箭。 值得庆幸的是，这把武器产生的爆炸不会对开火的人造成伤害。","A jewelled morningstar, glowing brightly with the light of the dawn. It illuminates the dungeon's recesses, revealing the machinations of those who would prefer to stay invisible.":"一把镶有宝石的晨星锤，在曙光下熠熠生辉。 它照亮了地牢的幽深处，令那些想要隐身的怪物的图谋无所遁形。","A trident stolen many years ago from the Octopus King's garden. Luckily, he seems to be in no hurry to get it back.":"一把多年前从章鱼王的花园中偷来的三叉戟。幸运的是，他似乎不急于寻回。","A beautiful mithril axe, probably lost by some dwarven hero.":"一把精致的秘银斧，这大概是某个矮人英雄遗落的武器吧。","A powerful staff which used to belong to the leader of the Guild of Five Elements. It is imbued with protective and offensive enhancements from all the elemental schools of magic.":"一支强大的法杖，曾经属于五行会的会长。 它注入了各种元素魔法流派的进攻和防御性增益。","The sacred weapon of Toth-Mos, first apostle of the god Ashenzari. It grants the wielder a fraction of Ashenzari's own vision, ensuring that every shot will land true.":"这是艾申扎利第一位使徒托斯莫斯的神圣武器。 它可以让持用者获得艾申扎利的一部分视野，保证例无虚发。","An enchanted lance deadly to all dragonkind. It grows more powerful every time it inflicts a killing blow on a strong dragon. The more powerful it grows, the harder it will be to find a worthy opponent.":"一把对所有龙类致命的魔法长枪。 每对一只强大的龙造成致命一击都使它的威力就会更强。 它的威力越强，与它相称的强敌越少。","A dainty little knife which was made by Spriggans, or for Spriggans, or possibly from Spriggans. Anyway, it's in some way associated with those fey folk.":"一把精致的小刀，可能由小精灵制作，可能为小精灵制作， 也可能是用小精灵制作的。总之，它多少与那些妖精般的小家伙有关。","A triple sword made of weird glowing metal. It irradiates those it strikes, causing a range of unpredictable effects — if they survive the impact of the blade itself, that is.":"一把由奇异发光金属制成的三刃剑。它会辐射被其击中的目标， 造成一系列无法预料的效果——前提是目标能从剑刃本身的冲击下活下来。","A weapon imbued with magic to disrupt and destroy the forces binding undead creatures together. Legends say that, long ago, a lich lord created many such weapons to ensure the loyalty of his undead servants. Sadly, this mace might be the last one left.":"一种充满魔力的武器，能够瓦解、摧毁将亡灵生物的身体缚在一起的力量。 传说，很久以前，一个巫妖领主制造了许多这样的武器，以确保其亡灵仆从的忠诚。 遗憾的是，这把巨型钉头锤可能是仅存的一把。","A double-ended whip made from the cured hides of black mambas, and enchanted with toxins ranging from ordinary venoms to asphyxiating curare.":"一种由黑曼巴蛇的皮制成的双端鞭，附有从普通的毒液到令人窒息的箭毒碱毒素。","An infamous weapon, once used by a vile pirate captain to slaughter countless innocents. He finally met his destiny when a kraken swallowed his ship, and the cutlass was thought to be lost with him.":"曾经有个邪恶的海盗船长用这件臭名昭著的武器杀了无数的无辜之人。 当一只克拉肯吞下他的船时，他终于碰到了自己的劫数， 而那把短弯刀曾被认为和他一样，不知所踪。","A longbow with the colour of dark rain clouds that fires arrows like lightning.":"一张阴暗的雨云色的长弓，能射出闪电般的箭。","A shield unearthed from the remains of a ruined city. It bears an inscription written in an ancient language. Scholars and wise men laboured for countless hours to decipher it, and in time, a translation was finally settled on:":"从城市废墟中出土的盾牌。上面有用古文书写的铭文。 学者和智者们花费了无数的时间来破译它，最终，译文敲定了：","\"With a shield like this, who needs to think?\"":"“有了这样的盾牌，谁需要思考？”","A shield unearthed from the remains of a ruined city. It bears an inscription written in an ancient language. Scholars and wise men laboured for countless hours to decipher it, and in time, a translation was finally settled on: \"With a shield like this, who needs to think?\"":"从城市废墟中出土的盾牌。上面有用古文书写的铭文。 学者和智者们花费了无数的时间来破译它，最终，译文敲定了： “有了这样的盾牌，谁需要思考？”","A variegated robe, woven with enchantments to enhance the wearer's physical and mental abilities. Its creators wove in strands of hair from a hundred different animals, each chosen for the unique strengths it could grant the robe's wearer.":"一件斑驳的长袍，织入了魔法，以增强穿着者的身心。 它的制造者用百种不同动物的毛发进行编织， 每种动物的毛发都能赋予穿着者独特的力量。","A pitch-black cloak which allows its wearer to excel in the arts of thievery. Even the clumsy will find their footsteps softer and the shouts of their adversaries less attention-getting.":"一件漆黑的披风，能让它的穿着者精通盗窃艺术。 即便是笨手笨脚的人也会发现自己的脚步声变轻了，而敌人的喊叫声也变得不那么引人注目了。","A large circlet of dull bronze, set with a dazzling array of gemstones. It was first worn by a prince of the Titans, who sought protection from the incessant warfare between his fellow princes. In practice, the main effect of the artefact was to unite his rivals against him.":"一顶暗色青铜铸成的巨大王冠，镶嵌着许多光彩夺目的宝石。 一位泰坦族的王子曾戴过它，希望它能在王位之争中保护自己。 实际上，这件神器的主要效果是让他的对手联合起来对抗他。","A fur hat once owned by Ukta, a powerful ogre shaman. It houses the spirit of an especially mighty bear, whose rages devastated the ogres until it was slain.":"这顶毛帽曾经是一位强大的食人魔萨满——乌克塔的所有物。 它里面寄宿着一头格外强大的熊之灵；在它被杀死前，其狂怒曾重创食人魔。","A splendid flowing robe of fur and silk whose lucky colour has faded.":"一件精美、顺滑的长袍，用毛皮和丝绸织成，其幸运的色彩已经褪去。","A soft hood, enchanted by members of the Assassin's Guild to allow the wearer to sense potential victims nearby, and to easily spot vulnerabilities after closing in on them.":"一种柔软的兜帽，被刺客公会成员施入魔法，可以让佩戴者感知附近潜在的猎物， 并在接近他们后，轻易发现其弱点。","A well-made golden hauberk that covers all of its wearer's body parts. It includes a chainmail coif, chausses and maille gauntlets.":"这套做工精良的黄金锁子甲能覆盖穿戴者的所有身体部位。 这套护甲中包含一顶锁子甲防护帽、一副腿甲，和一副链制手套。","The {{ if you.can_smell() then return \"smelly \" end }}skin of some strange animal, native to cold and distant lands. It radiates the chill of its native habitat.":"一件{{ if you.can_smell() then return \"难闻的\" end }}毛皮，源于某种在寒冷而遥远的地方生长的奇怪动物。它散发着原栖息地的寒意。","Most salamanders' bodies are consigned to the fiery depths from which they sprang. Rarely, though, salamanders instead preserve the skins of those that passed. The runes and decorations on this hide suggest it once belonged to a respected warrior or priest - perhaps even a king. The fiery spirit remains in the skin, granting its power to the wearer.":"大多数火蜥蜴的尸体都被送到他们生长的火海深处。 然而，偶尔也会有火蜥蜴保存死者的皮肤。这张皮上的符文和装饰表明， 它曾经属于一位受人尊敬的战士或祭司，甚至可能是一位国王。 炽热的灵魂留在皮肤中，赋予穿戴者力量。","A pair of thick steel gauntlets. They were Okawaru's reward for a mighty warlord. The owner is destined to die in battle, but what a death it will be!":"一双厚厚的钢手套。这是奥卡瓦鲁对伟大的将军的赏赐。 它的主人注定要死在战斗中，但那将是一场多么惨烈的死亡啊！","A bronze shield, looking almost exactly like a tortoise's shell. It was built by the adherents of an obscure minor faith, who imbued it with the power of their god. As the god is said to, this shield protects against sword and sling, frost and flame.":"一个青铜盾牌，看起来几乎和龟壳一模一样。 一个鲜为人知的小宗教的信徒们打造了它，将自己的神的力量注入其中。 据说他们的神祇也会如此，这面盾牌既能抵御刀剑和投石索，也能抵御严霜和烈焰。","A dull grey robe. It is enchanted to provide mages with immeasurable power, and more than a little overconfidence...":"一件暗灰色长袍。它为法师们带来了不可估量的力量，还有过分的自信……","A suit of armour created by the famous inventor Maxwell, providing unparalleled protective qualities at a very affordable price. His unorthodox materials left it with certain shortcomings, but he's yet to have anyone come back for a refund.":"由著名发明家麦克斯韦制造的一套铠甲，以非常实惠的价格提供无与伦比的防护性能。 他用的非正统材料给它带来了一定的缺陷，但还没有人回来退款。","The mask of the High Priest of ancient Erebora. In ancient times, the gods of the Ereborans ceased to answer their prayers, and in desperation, the people turned to the forbidden worship of dragons. Now, of their works, only this mask remains.":"古代埃雷博拉高级祭司的面具。昔日，埃雷博拉人的神灵不再回应他们的祈祷， 在绝望中，人们转而信奉遭禁的龙族。如今，他们的造物只剩下这副面具。","A long black robe made of strange glossy material. It shrouds its wearer in darkness, reducing the range of vision. According to legend, it was the gift of Rutra, a renowned demigoddess of the night, to one of her followers.":"一件黑色长袍，由奇特的光泽材料制成。它将佩戴者笼罩在黑暗中，缩短视野距离。 传说，这是著名的夜之半神鲁特拉送给一名追随者的礼物。","A suit of armour created from the enchanted scales of a once-mighty king of dragons. In his time, titans and lesser dragons struggled with him in vain — but as with all things, even he was eventually cast down and undone. Of his life and deeds, this is all that remains.":"一套盔甲，由曾经强大的龙王的带有魔法的鳞片制成。 在他的时代，泰坦和较小的龙与他搏斗是徒劳的——但就像所有的事情一样， 即使是他最终也被打倒和毁灭。这是所有留存下来的，关于他的一生和事迹。","A dirty hat. It bears signs of surviving many weird explosions, which suggests it may have means of protecting the head inside from the risks involved with alchemy experiments.":"一顶肮脏的帽子。它似乎经过许多次奇怪的爆炸，但还是幸存下来，由此来看， 这顶帽子应该能在碰到炼金实验事故时保护下面的脑袋不受伤害。","A pair of gloves made of white silk.":"一副用白色丝绸织成的手套。","A phosphorescent cloak, woven of pure light beams. The ripples of its folds as the wearer leaps and swerves in combat may dazzle those who gaze on it.":"一件发出磷光的披风，由纯粹的光束织成。 当穿戴者在战斗中跳跃和转向时，其褶皱的起伏，可能会让注视它的人眼花缭乱。","A cloak stitched from the hides of hundreds of hell rats by an enchantress with far too much time on her hands. Many more rats remain somehow concealed within it, and may scurry out to assist the wearer.":"有个女巫闲得无聊，用数百只地狱鼠的皮缝制出这件披风。 还有更多的老鼠不知怎的藏在里面，它们可能会窜出来帮助穿戴者。","A heavy bronze gong that can be worn as a shield. Locked away in a temple for many years, its bearer is shielded by decades of accumulated prayer.":"一个沉重的铜锣，可当盾牌用。 它被锁在寺庙里多年，它的持用者将承载着几十年积累的祈祷的庇佑。","A sky-blue amulet, suffused with enchantments that protect the wearer and make their Air spells more powerful. Its creator lacked just one thing: a steady hand.":"一条天蓝色的项链，充满了保护佩戴者的魔法，并能增强其气系法术。 它的创造者只缺一样东西：一双稳健的手。","A black ring that can make its wearer one with the shadows.":"一枚黑色的戒指，它能使佩戴者融入阴影。","A pendant made of purest jade. It grants its wearer immense willpower and mental fortitude.":"这个垂饰是用纯净的玉制成的。它能赋予佩戴者强大的意志力和毅力。","A necklace made of bloodstained human and animal teeth, and something that appears to be a piece of spine.":"一条串着沾血人牙和兽牙的项链，其中似乎还混着一截脊椎骨。","An unadorned malachite ring, half of an ancient pair. Its wearer is exceptionally difficult to catch.":"一枚朴实无华的孔雀石戒指，是一对古老戒指中的一只。佩戴了它，很难被追上。","A rough-hewn aquamarine ring, half of an ancient pair. Its wearer is exceptionally difficult to harm.":"一枚粗糙的海蓝宝石戒指，是一对古老戒指中的一只。佩戴了它，很难受到伤害。","An enchanted sapphire, inset into a ring. It aids the spellcasting of its wearer.":"这枚戒指，镶着一颗有魔力的蓝宝石。它能强化佩戴者的施法能力。","A brooch with an intricate inlaid design, providing a range of magical protections. Back in the good old days, every adventurer had one of these handy devices. That, and a pony.":"一个设计复杂的胸针，提供一系列魔法保护。 从前，所有的冒险者都会带一个这种称手的东西。还有一匹小马。","A robe of a material as nebulous and insubstantial as the clouds. It whips the air around it up into a furious storm as it ripples and swirls.":"这件长袍的材质像是云做的一样，模糊而虚幻。 当它泛起涟漪和漩涡时，它会将周围的空气搅成一场猛烈的风暴。","The favourite hat of the slug wizard Gastronok, stained with reddish slime and enchanted to aid in his arcane pondering. It has been specially enchanted to protect against the desiccating effects of salt.":"鼻涕虫巫师加斯特罗诺克最喜欢的帽子， 沾有的红色黏液和附着的魔力有助于他那神秘的思考。 它被特地施了魔法以防盐的干燥效果。","An axe with a powerful curse placed on it by one of the lords of Pandemonium, so that unsuspecting adventurers would unleash demons into this world. Beware, for it has ways of taking its wielder under its command...":"某位万魔殿领主在这把斧头上施加了强大的诅咒， 为的是让毫无戒心的冒险者将恶魔释放到这个世界。 务必当心，它自有办法将持用者置于其掌控之下……","An axe with a delicate blessing placed on it by one of the sacred Seraphim, so that worthy adventurers would rid this world of demons. Rejoice, for it has ways of bringing courage to its wielder in even the darkest places...":"这把斧头上有着神圣的炽天使的祝福，这样受赏识的冒险者就能斩除世上的恶魔。 欢欣吧，因为即使在最黑暗的地方，它也能给持用者带来勇气……","A set of armoured plates assembled to protect a creature with a long, scaly lower body. Faintly crackling with electricity, they supercharge their wearer's ability to cover distance.":"一套用来保护下半身长而有鳞的生物板甲。 它发出微弱的电荷爆裂声，让佩戴者风驰电掣。","A heavy barding made from pitch-black steel and inlaid with plates of black diamond. It once protected the steed of the Black Knight during their reign of terror. Those who wear it become partially undead, gaining some of the benefits without the unfortunate downsides, although the great weight of metal and stone slows the wearer somewhat.":"一件重装马铠，由乌黑的钢制成并嵌有黑色钻石板。 在黑骑士的恐怖统治期间，它曾保护过其坐骑。 穿戴者会部分转化为亡灵，获得其中一些益处，而不必承受所有恼人的弊端， 尽管金属和石头的巨大重量会让佩戴者变慢一些。","A jewelled amulet famed for its powers of resilience and recuperation. Its greatest notoriety came from its use by the dread necromancer Borgnjor, who relied upon it to maintain her slender hold on life. After her final demise, the amulet vanished from the pages of history.":"这条宝石项链以其强大的恢复能力而闻名。它恶名昭彰， 因为可怕的死灵法师博格尼尔使用过它，她依靠它来维持自己纤弱的生命。 在她最终去世后，这条项链也不知所踪。","An exquisitely crafted sword. Its blade is so sharp that it can cut through space itself.":"一把做工精致的剑。它的刀刃非常锋利，甚至可以切开空间。","A wooden cudgel, loaded with more than just lead.":"这根木棍，灌的可不仅仅是铅。","An opalescent cloak gleaming with the colours of all kinds of dragons. It imbues the wearer with draconic resistances, although somewhat unreliably.":"这件乳白色的披风上闪烁着各种龙的颜色。 它为穿戴者注入了龙的抗性，但效果不是很可靠。","One of the eight rings once worn by the Octopus King and now scattered across the land. Each has its own unique enchantment.":"章鱼王曾经戴过八枚戒指，现在散布在这片土地上，这是其中的一枚。 每个都有独特的魔力。","As you hold this axe your mind does not feel fully your own. Your body begins to exhibit strength far beyond its capabilities, and your movements become guided by Makhleb.":"手中拿着这柄斧子时，你感觉自己的心智似乎不再完全属于自己。 你的身体开始展现远超极限的力量，而马科列布似乎在指引着你的动作。","A suit of armour rumoured to have been created by enchanting the hide of a now-extinct species of troll. Whether the name rings true or is merely appropriated to add mystique is something of a mystery. The armour's innate powers of regeneration and magical protection, however, are hard to dispute.":"传说，这件甲胄是用一种已经灭绝了的巨魔的毛皮强化而成。 这名称究竟名副其实，还是仅为增添神秘感而借用，仍是一个谜。 这件甲胄可以提升穿着者的恢复速度和魔法抗性，倒是实实在在的。","An ugly dangling finger on a string. Everything about it reeks of malign influences... but it's hard to avoid thinking that it would look better with a ring on it.":"一根丑陋的手指挂在绳子上。 它的一切都散发着邪恶影响……但人们不禁会想，若给这根手指戴枚戒指，应该会更好看。","A large, iron-shod maul specialised for dealing massively powerful blows. Such power comes at a price: the maul's head is so heavy it takes a great length of time to lift it up for another swing.":"一柄硕大的包铁重锤，专为打出威力骇人的重击而制。 这种威力也有代价：锤头太重，要花很长时间才能再次抬起挥动。","A blade somehow crafted from pure electricity. It arcs wildly between the wielder and their foes as it strikes.":"这是一把用纯电制作的刀刃。 当它攻击时，它会在持用者和他们的敌人之间疯狂地释放电弧。","A weapon said to have once been used to keep unruly imprisoned wizards in line; it violently disrupts the flow of magic around it.":"一把据说曾用来管束不服管束的巫师囚犯的武器；它会剧烈扰乱周围的魔力流动。","A silver-bladed lajatang, once bestowed upon a favoured worshipper of Zin. It became the most prized weapon of the many priests of Zin. After their order was destroyed, it fell into disuse and vanished from history.":"一柄带银刃的双头杖，曾被赐予辛的一位受宠信徒。 它成了辛的众多祭司的最宝贵的武器。 他们的教团覆灭后，它便遭到弃用，从历史中消失了。","A huge mace imbued with potent fire magic. It fills those it strikes with an inner flame, and offers some protection against the resulting devastation.":"一把注入强大火焰魔力的巨型钉头锤。 它会使击中的目标充满内焰，也会保护持用者免受随后爆炸的部分伤害。","A suit of armour carved from transparent orange crystal. It provides remarkable protection for both mind and body. The wearer can even channel psychic energies through the crystal itself, enhancing their magical abilities. However, it's rather heavy...":"一套用透明的橙色水晶雕刻而成的护甲。可以为肉体和心灵提供卓越的保护能力。 穿戴者甚至可以通过水晶引导精神力量来增强魔法能力。但是相当重……","A staff inhabited by a mighty demon, tricked and trapped in this form long ago. To survive, she now offers great arcane power in a terrible bargain: in exchange for a tiny portion of the caster's life essence, taken every time its wielder casts a spell, she will redirect the life essence of creatures damaged by the spell to the caster.":"一个居住着强大的恶魔的法杖，很久之前她就被以这种形式欺骗和困住。 为了活命，她如今以一笔可怕的交易提供强大的奥术力量： 施法者每次施法时她会从中获取一小部分生命精华， 而她会将被法术伤害的生物的生命精华导向施法者。","Two quick blades joined by a chain. Swinging one compels the wielder to swing the other, as if they have minds of their own.":"两个由链条连接的快刃。 挥动一个会迫使持有者挥动另一个，仿佛它们有自己的想法一样。","A robe woven of living vines. The vines form a symbiotic relationship with their wearer, greatly increasing their regeneration, but preventing them from being healed by potions.":"一件用活的藤蔓编织而成的长袍。藤蔓与穿戴者形成了共生关系， 大幅增强穿戴者的恢复能力，但是无法再通过药水获得治疗。","A coat of armour said to have been forged for Queen Kryia in her old age. She continued to insist on leading her armies from the front even into her dotage, and as her aging body failed her, this coat helped to enhance the healing draughts that kept her alive.":"一副据说是为晚年的克里娅女王锻造的盔甲。 即使年事已高，她仍坚持亲临前线；随着身体日渐衰弱， 这件链甲衫增强了维系她生命的治疗药剂。","A massive axe that looks like it was carved from a glacier, or possibly calved from one. It leaves ice crystals in its wake as it swings through the air.":"一把巨大的斧头，像是在冰川上雕刻的，或是从冰川上崩裂下来的。 在空中挥舞它，会留下冰晶。","A handheld array of hexagonal mirrors, synthesised from a truly exotic substance and polished to a blinding sheen.":"一个手持的六边形镜子阵列，由真正的奇异物质制成，并经过抛光，发出眩目的光泽。","An amulet that can be activated to render its wearer invisible.":"一条可激活以使佩戴者隐形的项链。","A strange sword, one blade blistering hot and the other icy cold. When it hits its target the thermal gradient increases. What causes this effect is unknown but it is rumoured that otherworldly forces are involved.":"一把奇怪的剑，一个刃炽热，而另一个冰冷。当它击中目标时，热梯度会增大。 造成此效果的原因尚不清楚，但有传言说它与超自然的力量有关。","A small wrinkle in the very fabric of reality, magically bound to a shaft by some mad acolyte of Lugonu. Its attacks can warp through nearby space at the wielder's command.":"卢格努的某个疯狂侍僧以魔法将现实结构中的细小皱褶绑在一根柄上。 在持用者的支配下，它的攻击可以扭曲穿越附近的空间。","An orb encased in vividly coloured scales, wrought by a long-forgotten wizard. It was the mage Iskenderun's favourite playtoy.":"一个外面裹着艳丽鳞片的水晶球，由一个被遗忘已久的巫师制作。 这是法师伊斯肯德伦最喜欢的玩具。","A suit of armour borne of rotten flesh and bone and gristle, held intact by the will of a long-dead sorcerer. The dreadful energies within it call to the bodies of the recently dead, protecting the wearer with a cocoon of carrion.":"一套由腐肉、骨骼和软骨制成的护甲，一名死去已久的术士以意志维系着它的完整。 里面的可怕能量召唤着刚刚死去的人的尸体，用腐肉茧保护着穿戴者。","An enchanted pair of boots which grant the ability to take strides of incredible length, as long as the wearer is advancing bravely towards their foes.":"一双注入了魔法的靴子，只要穿着它勇敢地朝敌人前进，就可以迈出难以置信的步伐。","A pair of gloves designed to carefully control and channel the flow of magic, later misused and mangled by the lunatic murderer-mages of the Fifth Circle. Their influence leaves the wearer utterly unable to cast spells - the wearer's magic is redirected to far bloodier purposes.":"一副用来小心控制和引导魔法流动的手套， 后来却被第五环的疯狂杀人法师滥用并毁坏了。 它会让穿戴者完全无法施法——穿戴者的魔力被转而用于做更血腥的事情。","A dull dusty mixture trapped within a cracked crystal on a thin silver chain.":"在一条细银链上，暗淡的尘土被束缚在一颗破碎的水晶中。","A beautiful rainbow of colour and motion trapped within a delicate crystal on a thin silver chain. Listening carefully, one can hear the distant echo of a thousand dreams from all corners of reality, their melody giving a warm sense of safety.":"在一条细银链上，色彩和运动的虹光被束缚在一颗精致的水晶中。 仔细聆听，你可以听到来自现实各个角落的一千个梦想的遥远回声， 它们的旋律给人一种温暖的安全感。","A pair of long ultramarine gloves, worn by a famed experimental alchemist in an age long past. They channel the energy of discovery, empowering their wearer with the force created by a blind step from ignorance to certainty.":"很久以前由一位著名的实验炼金术士戴过的一副群青色长手套。 它引导发现的能量，当佩戴者盲目地从未知到确定的探索时，会赋予其力量。","A weapon that chops foes down as steadily and methodically as a forester cutting wood. The unchanging rhythm of its work has settled on it with the force of natural law, and no amount of force or skill can make it swing faster or slower.":"这把武器，能像伐木工砍伐树木一样有条不紊地砍倒敌人。 它的工作节奏一成不变，这是自然法则所决定的， 再强的力量或技能也无法使它挥动得更快或更慢。","Taken from a paladin of the Shining One by the common cutpurse who murdered her, Throatcutter was used for a long series of increasingly sordid deeds thereafter. Blood, murder and betrayal stain its history and blade both, and little trace now remains of the blade which once stood between danger and the innocent.":"一个普通的扒手谋杀了一位光辉者的圣骑士， 并从其手上夺走了割喉者，此后用它干了一系列越来越肮脏的事迹。 鲜血、谋杀和背叛玷污了它的历史和刀锋， 如今已几乎看不出，这把刀曾挺身挡在危险与无辜者之间。","A sacred relic of the Monks of St. Lee, followers of the renunciate archmage. Just as St. Lee sought to atone for the destruction his spells wrought by protecting others, so his staff protects its wielder.":"这是遁世大法师圣李的追随者——圣李修士会——所供奉的圣物。 正如圣李通过保护他人来弥补他的法术所造成的破坏一样， 他的法杖也保护着持用者。","A weapon to bring forth guilt from the guilty. It was first wielded by the archangel Lucriel, who, on seeing the suffering of the first mortals, led them as an army against the cruelty of the gods. The ragged survivors of Lucriel's army took this weapon with them into the wilderness, the sole remnant of an archangel's virtue.":"一把让罪人产生罪恶感的武器。它最先是由天使长卢克利尔使用， 他看到了第一批凡人的苦难，就率领他们对抗残酷的诸神。 卢克利尔大军中衣衫褴褛的幸存者带着这件武器进入荒野， 它也成了天使长美德唯一留存的见证。","A blue-steel amulet. Its creator, an exceedingly practical woman, designed it to provide powerful protection against mundane jabs, stabs and bites. It's worse than useless against fire and frost, but how often does anyone really need to worry about that?":"一条蓝色钢制项链。它的创造者是一位非常务实的女性， 设计它是为了有力抵御凡俗的戳刺、捅刺与撕咬。 但它面对火焰和严霜时非但无用，反而有害——可谁真的会经常担心这些呢？","These sturdy boots were created by an artificer who lived high up on a remote mountain peak, as protection against the mountain's near-constant avalanches, rockslides, and snowstorms. No force short of translocations magic will budge the wearer from their position.":"这双结实的靴子是由一位住在偏远山峰上的工匠设计的， 用来抵御山上几乎不间断的雪崩、山崩和暴风雪。 除位移术外，没有任何力量能令穿戴者挪动分毫。","This brutal weapon, long thought lost to history, combines the extended reach of a polearm with the cleaving sharpness of an axe. Ghosts of ancient warriors linger about it, draining fickle users.":"这把野蛮的武器，长期被遗忘在历史的长河中， 它兼具长柄武器的攻击范围和斧头的锋利。 古代战士的鬼魂徘徊在它周围，汲取三心二意者的生命力。","An ascetic once took a sacred vow, forswearing use of magical tools and ownership of everything but this pendant. Which god they made this vow to remains a point of bitter contention among the devout, but their pendant's power - and limitations - are irrefutable.":"一位苦行者曾许下神圣誓言，不再使用魔法工具，也不再拥有这枚垂饰以外的任何东西。 是向哪一位神许下这个誓言仍然是虔诚者之间激烈争论的焦点， 但这枚垂饰的力量——以及它的局限——都无可辩驳。","Crafted from the tanned, smooth hide of a Western Skyshark, these slippers are astonishingly comfortable. They lack the protective benefits of a good pair of boots, but they can get their wearers out of almost any bind.":"这双拖鞋是用西方天鲨的光滑的皮鞣制而成的，舒适得令人称奇。 它没有好靴子那样的保护作用，但它能让穿着者摆脱几乎所有束缚。","A plain iron lance, imbued with supernatural gravitas via the artifice of the mage Gell. It strikes with a force many times stronger than that imparted by the wielder.":"这根朴素的铁制骑枪经法师盖尔巧手改造，注入了超自然的重力。 它的打击力量比持用者所施加的力量强许多倍。","An ancient artefact of Okawaru, these woolen robes were lost when a former champion failed a duel. Its enchantments increase in power when the wearer emerges victorious from threatening combat, but resorting to the use of scrolls or potions for assistance causes them to fade away again.":"这件羊毛长袍是奥卡瓦鲁的一件古代神器，前冠军在决斗失败后遗落了它。 当穿戴者取得险胜时，其附着的魔力会增强，但求助于卷轴或药水会使它们再次消失。","A disc of crackling metal, created by a woman whose cunning artifice and crafty politics once united a continent. Most of her surviving inventions are closely guarded by various royals, ostensible proof of their claim to be her true successor, but this early prototype slipped through their fingers.":"这张噼啪作响的金属圆盘，由一位女人所造， 她曾运用狡猾的诡计和政治手腕，让一块大陆团结在了一起。 她的那些幸免于难的发明，大多被各个皇室成员严密保护着， 这些皇室成员都宣称自己才是她的真正继承人， 而这个早期的原型却从他们手中溜走了。","Hand cannons use magical dust to launch projectiles. The alchemists who craft them boast of their potency, but omit the smoke and noise blasted out with each shot. Filled with powdered blastmotes, Mule packs an especially powerful kick.":"手铳使用魔尘来发射弹药。 制造它们的炼金术士吹嘘了它们的威力，但略过了每次发射都会喷出烟和噪音。 『骡子』装满了爆尘粉末，踢起来尤其有劲。","This orb is the work of a master artificer, contracted to retrieve the orb, who valued their life more than their professional integrity. While this fake faithfully recreates the eerie glow and space-warping properties of the true orb, the power it grants is artificial and only accessible to skilled evokers.":"这个球体是一位大师级工匠的作品，他受雇取回宝珠，却更珍视自己的生命 而非职业道德。虽然这个赝品忠实地再现了真正宝珠的诡异光芒和空间扭曲特性， 但它所赋予的力量是人造的，只有精通魔力释放技能的人才能使用。","An extravagant crown of gold filigree and glittering jewels that even a king could feel immodest wearing. It grants its wearer a regal aura the match of any in heaven and also a great deal of unearned confidence.":"一顶由金丝和闪亮珠宝制成的奢华王冠，即便是国王戴上它也会感到不够谦逊。 它赋予佩戴者堪比天界中任何存在的王者气场，以及大量不应得的自信。","The handiwork of a mad mycologist who once attempted to overcome the genetic anxiety of wandering mushrooms by cultivating a species that could be easily transported without disturbing them. The result is as much a living organism as it is a piece of clothing, every linen fibre twined together with fungal mycelia that draw both nutrients and confidence from whoever wears it. And in exchange for such trifles as blood or peptides, the colony will instinctively lash out to defend its wearer from whatever they perceive as a threat.":"一位疯狂真菌学家的作品，他曾试图通过培育一种可以轻松携带而不打扰 它们的物种来克服徘徊蘑菇的遗传焦虑。结果既是一件衣物，也是一个活的 有机体，每根亚麻纤维都与真菌菌丝交织在一起，从佩戴者身上汲取营养 和信心。作为对这些微不足道的血液或肽类物质的交换，菌落会本能地 猛烈反击被它们视为威胁的任何东西来保护佩戴者。","It's like wearing a thousand tiny friends at once! And the humming they fill your mind with in the dark is actually quite lulling....":"这就像同时穿着上千个小小的朋友！它们在黑暗中充满你心灵的嗡嗡声 其实相当催人入睡……","(This item also occupies your helmet slot.)":"（这件物品也占据你的头盔槽位。）","The handiwork of a mad mycologist who once attempted to overcome the genetic anxiety of wandering mushrooms by cultivating a species that could be easily transported without disturbing them. The result is as much a living organism as it is a piece of clothing, every linen fibre twined together with fungal mycelia that draw both nutrients and confidence from whoever wears it. And in exchange for such trifles as blood or peptides, the colony will instinctively lash out to defend its wearer from whatever they perceive as a threat. It's like wearing a thousand tiny friends at once! And the humming they fill your mind with in the dark is actually quite lulling.... (This item also occupies your helmet slot.)":"一位疯狂真菌学家的作品，他曾试图通过培育一种可以轻松携带而不打扰 它们的物种来克服徘徊蘑菇的遗传焦虑。结果既是一件衣物，也是一个活的 有机体，每根亚麻纤维都与真菌菌丝交织在一起，从佩戴者身上汲取营养 和信心。作为对这些微不足道的血液或肽类物质的交换，菌落会本能地 猛烈反击被它们视为威胁的任何东西来保护佩戴者。 这就像同时穿着上千个小小的朋友！它们在黑暗中充满你心灵的嗡嗡声 其实相当催人入睡…… （这件物品也占据你的头盔槽位。）","A pair of suede gloves covered in a dizzying array of delicate sigils. While originally intended to aid in the crafting of magical devices, they are nonetheless useful for wringing every last drop of power out of someone else's work.":"一双覆盖着令人眼花缭乱的精致符文的麂皮手套。虽然最初旨在帮助制造 魔法装置，但它们同样有助于从他人的作品中榨出每一滴力量。","A gleaming breastplate with a slot in its centre for a holy symbol or bejewelled coat of arms. Those who hear commands given by its wearer feel filled with the power to carry them out, no matter the adversity.":"一件闪闪发光的胸甲，中央有一个槽位用于放置圣徽或珠宝纹章。 听到其佩戴者发出的命令的人会感到充满了执行命令的力量，无论面临多大困难。","A scarf that can be activated to render its wearer invisible.":"一条可激活以使佩戴者隐形的围巾。","The skull of a legendary necromancer, seemingly parted from the rest of its body. When held, it seems disinclined to explain the precise circumstances of its ending up in this state, but offers no objection to others siphoning what considerable necromantic power still remains in its ancient bones.":"一位传奇死灵法师的头骨，似乎与其身体的其余部分分离了。当被握持时， 它似乎不愿解释自己落得如此境地的确切情况，但对他人汲取其古老骨骼中 仍然存留的相当可观的死灵术力量并不反对。","If you get this description, it is a bug.":"如果你碰到这个描述，说明你遇到程序错误了。","Spits poison at a targeted creature.":"向一个目标生物喷吐毒液。","Breathes a blast of poison gas at a targeted creature.":"向一个目标生物喷吐一股毒气。","Blasts a targeted enemy with damnation. These unholy forces harm the victim and anyone adjacent, and are not affected by any means of protection, such as armour or resistances. However, certain creatures, usually those able to invoke damnation themselves, are entirely unscathed by damnation.":"用天谴轰击一个目标敌人。 这些邪恶的力量会伤害目标和任何相邻生物，且不受护甲、抗性等任何保护手段削弱。 但某些生物，通常是那些能够自己释放天谴的生物，完全不受天谴伤害。","Speaks a word of chaos, forcing enemies nearby to blink away from the user. Additionally, those affected may be slowed, ensnared, or terrified by the experience. Invoking a word of chaos is no easy feat and will drain the user's maximum health somewhat, and the ability then cannot be used again for a short time.":"念出混沌之语，迫使附近的敌人闪烁远离使用者。 此外，受影响的敌人还可能因此被减速、束缚或恐惧。念出混沌之语绝非易事， 会略微降低使用者的生命上限，并使此能力在短时间内无法再次使用。","Heals the user significantly, with a chance of permanently reducing the user's maximum magic capacity by one.":"显著恢复使用者的生命值，但有可能永久降低 1 点法力上限。","Allows making tunnels through soft rock and rusted grates. Activating the ability has no cost and simply prepares you to start digging; once active, moving into a wall will start tunnelling. Doing so makes some noise and drains the user's maximum health.":"使你能在松软岩石和生锈栅栏中挖出通道。激活此能力本身没有消耗， 只会让你做好挖掘准备；激活后，向墙壁移动就会开始打通通道。 挖掘会制造一些噪音，并降低使用者的生命上限。","Once active, activating the ability again or making any non-digging movement action will cancel the Dig status.":"激活后，再次激活此能力或进行任何非挖掘的移动动作都会取消挖掘状态。","Allows making tunnels through soft rock and rusted grates. Activating the ability has no cost and simply prepares you to start digging; once active, moving into a wall will start tunnelling. Doing so makes some noise and drains the user's maximum health. Once active, activating the ability again or making any non-digging movement action will cancel the Dig status.":"使你能在松软岩石和生锈栅栏中挖出通道。激活此能力本身没有消耗， 只会让你做好挖掘准备；激活后，向墙壁移动就会开始打通通道。 挖掘会制造一些噪音，并降低使用者的生命上限。 激活后，再次激活此能力或进行任何非挖掘的移动动作都会取消挖掘状态。","Sends you to a random position one to three floors down, as if you jumped into a shaft trap. It takes some time to dig the shaft.":"使你如同跳入竖井陷阱一般，落到下方一至三层的随机位置。挖掘竖井需要一些时间。","Randomly translocates the user a short distance. After translocating in this way, the ability cannot be activated again for a short period of time depending on Evocations skill.":"将使用者随机传送一小段距离。 以这种方式传送后，短时间内无法再次激活此能力；冷却时间取决于魔力释放技能。","Turns the user invisible for a short period of time.":"使使用者短暂隐形。","Reverts you to your normal form.":"恢复到正常形态。","Begins to transform you back into your native form. A short period of concentration is required.":"开始将你变回你的原生形态。这需要花一小段时间来集中精力。","Temporarily provides protection from poison, confusion, petrification, and sickness, as well as the effects of clouds of foul pestilence. Your strength, intelligence and dexterity are also temporarily increased by a degree dependent on Invocations skill.":"暂时提供保护，免受毒、混乱、石化和疾病，以及腐臭瘟疫云的影响。 你的力量、智力、敏捷会暂时增加，增加的幅度取决于祈神技能。","Temporarily imprisons a monster in walls of silver. The duration of the prison is increased by Invocations skill.":"创造出临时性的白银墙壁，将一个怪物困在其中。 监禁的持续时间随祈神技能的提升而增加。","Transforms the area around the user into a domain of unbreakable law for a short duration. So long as anyone stands within this sanctuary, no harm may be done to them by others, and they may do no harm to others in turn.":"将使用者周围的区域短暂转化为不可侵犯的法则领域。只要任何人停留于此庇护所中， 他人便无法对其造成伤害，而他们也无法对他人造成伤害。","Beings with hostile intent are unable to enter a sanctuary and those already nearby when it is created will be forced to flee.":"怀有敌意的生物无法进入庇护所，在创建时已在附近的则会被迫逃离。","Transforms the area around the user into a domain of unbreakable law for a short duration. So long as anyone stands within this sanctuary, no harm may be done to them by others, and they may do no harm to others in turn. Beings with hostile intent are unable to enter a sanctuary and those already nearby when it is created will be forced to flee.":"将使用者周围的区域短暂转化为不可侵犯的法则领域。只要任何人停留于此庇护所中， 他人便无法对其造成伤害，而他们也无法对他人造成伤害。 怀有敌意的生物无法进入庇护所，在创建时已在附近的则会被迫逃离。","Cures all your mutations — but only once.":"治愈你体内所有变异。仅能使用一次。","Invokes a huge blast of divine fury centered on the user, severely damaging undead and demons and dealing damage to all other hostile creatures. The power of the blast is increased by Invocations skill.":"激起以使用者为中心的巨大的神怒爆炸，会对亡灵和恶魔造成严重伤害， 并对所有其他敌对生物造成伤害。爆炸的力量随祈神技能的提升而增大。","Summons a powerful warrior against evil, either an angel or a daeva. The duration of their assistance is increased by Invocations skill, and glory in battle may lead the Shining One to bless them with an even longer stay.":"召唤一个强大的天使或德瓦来帮助你扫除邪恶。 他们的持续时间随祈神技能的提升而增加，战斗中的荣耀可能会让光辉者祝福他们， 从而能持续更长时间。","Permanently blesses a weapon of your choice with the holy wrath of the Shining One. Demon weapons will be converted into a more powerful sacred weapon. This blessing may only be used once, and it cannot be used on artefact weapons.":"选择一件武器，让光辉者的神怒永久祝福它。 恶魔武器将被转化为更强力的圣武器。这个祝福只能使用一次，且不可用于神器。","Bring forth those near death from Kikubaaqudgha's necropolis, providing ample fodder for all kinds of necromancy. Their number and quality is dependent on Necromancy skill.":"将那些濒死的生物从奇库巴库哈的墓地带出，为各种死灵法术提供充足的食材。 它们的数量和质量随死灵术技能的提升而提升。","Permanently bloodies a weapon of your choice with the essence of pain itself. This blessing cannot be used on artefact weapons. You must choose between this gift or that of knowledge of the most powerful necromantic spells, and either gift may only be received once.":"用永久的痛楚血浴一件武器。这个祝福无法用于神器。 你必须在这个礼物和最强大的死灵法术之间二选一，而且任何一个礼物只能收到一次。","Grants you knowledge of the most powerful and sinister Necromancy spells: Haunt, Borgnjor's Revivification, Infestation, and Death's Door. You must choose between this gift or that of branding a weapon with pain, and either gift may only be received once.":"赐予你最强大、最邪恶的死灵法术：作祟、博格尼尔的再生、侵扰和死亡之门。 你必须在这个礼物和痛楚武器印记之间二选一，而且任何一个礼物只能收到一次。","Attempts to bind the soul of a living, holy, or demonic being into your eternal service. If the targeted monster is slain before it leaves your sight, it will return as a bound soul, retaining the equipment, spells and abilities it had in life. Only beings who are relatively uninjured may be targeted, and the focus required to keep their soul from escaping will consume 1/3 of the user's current health - returning it only upon slaying them. The attempt will fail entirely if the targeted monster leaves your sight before the process is complete. The bound soul's health is influenced by the user's Invocations skill. It will follow its captor through stairs, and can be recalled from other levels. Only one soul can be bound at a time.":"试图将一个活物、神圣或恶魔生物的灵魂束缚为你的永恒奴仆。如果目标怪物在离开你 视线之前被杀死，它将作为缚魂返回，保留生前拥有的装备、法术和能力。 只能选择相对未受重伤的生物作为目标，维持其灵魂不逃脱所需的专注会消耗使用者 当前生命值的1/3——杀死目标后才会归还。若目标怪物在过程完成前离开你的视线， 尝试将彻底失败。 缚魂的生命值受使用者的祈神技能影响。它将跟随其捕获者穿过楼梯，并能从其他楼层 召回。一次只能束缚住一个灵魂。","Greatly increases your combat speed. The duration is increased by Invocations skill.":"大幅加快你的战斗速度。持续时间随祈神技能的提升而增加。","Enters you into single combat with a worthy foe. On success, you and the challenged foe will be transported to Okawaru's Arena to fight to the death, with no escape until you either emerge victorious or are slain.":"让你和一个值得重视的敌人进行一对一博斗。 成功使用这个能力，你和被挑战的敌人将被运送到奥卡瓦鲁的角斗场战斗至死， 除非你取得胜利或被杀，否则无法逃脱。","Half of your missing health will be restored as the duel begins, and upon victory, Okawaru will return your health and magical power to whatever they were before you issued the challenge - letting you shake off any damage taken during it in the blink of an eye.":"决斗开始时将恢复你一半的已损失生命值，获胜后， 奥卡瓦鲁会将你的生命和魔力恢复至发出挑战前的状态—— 让你转瞬之间摆脱决斗中所受的一切伤害。","Enters you into single combat with a worthy foe. On success, you and the challenged foe will be transported to Okawaru's Arena to fight to the death, with no escape until you either emerge victorious or are slain. Half of your missing health will be restored as the duel begins, and upon victory, Okawaru will return your health and magical power to whatever they were before you issued the challenge - letting you shake off any damage taken during it in the blink of an eye.":"让你和一个值得重视的敌人进行一对一博斗。 成功使用这个能力，你和被挑战的敌人将被运送到奥卡瓦鲁的角斗场战斗至死， 除非你取得胜利或被杀，否则无法逃脱。 决斗开始时将恢复你一半的已损失生命值，获胜后， 奥卡瓦鲁会将你的生命和魔力恢复至发出挑战前的状态—— 让你转瞬之间摆脱决斗中所受的一切伤害。","Acquires a weapon from a choice of four. This blessing may only be redeemed once.":"从四把武器中选取其中一把。这个福泽只能承蒙一次。","Acquires a piece of armour from a choice of four. This blessing may only be redeemed once.":"从四件防具中选取其中一件。这个福泽只能承蒙一次。","Dramatically increases the user's regeneration of magical power for a duration that increases with Invocations skill.":"显著提高使用者的魔力回复能力，持续时间随着法术施展技能的提升而增加。","Removes a known spell from memory, so as to free memory to learn others.":"忘记一道你记忆中的法术，以便腾出记忆空间来学新法术。","Casts any spell from your spell library with guaranteed success. You receive a bonus to spell power based on your Invocations skill that is worth 50% more than equivalent levels of training in the relevant skills of the spell itself.":"能以必定成功的方式施展法术库中的任何法术。你会获得基于祈神技能的法术威力加成， 其价值比在该法术相关技能上进行同等级训练高 50%。","Invokes a powerful regeneration ability which stacks with all other sources and is effective even on those who would not otherwise be able to regenerate. It also fortifies the user's willpower, protecting against many magical effects.":"唤起强大的恢复能力，并能与其他来源的恢复效果叠加， 即使对那些无法自行恢复的物种也生效。 它还会强化使用者的意志力，从而能抵御许多魔法效果。","Summons huge angry allies to wreak havoc.":"召唤庞大而愤怒的友军进行破坏。","Heals a creature other than yourself by a moderate amount, depending on Invocations skill. Using this ability on hostile monsters will try to turn them neutral. This works best on living creatures, with the undead and demons being progressively harder to pacify. Intelligent creatures are also more difficult to pacify.":"根据祈神技能，治疗好一个你以外的目标生物的一些创伤。 对敌对怪物使用此能力将尝试使其变为中立。 这对活的生物最有效，而亡灵和恶魔则更难以安抚。智慧生物也更难以安抚。","Ghosts of dead adventurers and demon lords are too wrathful to be pacified, mindless creatures are too unintelligent to be pacified, and no monster can be pacified while it is asleep.":"死去的冒险者的鬼魂和恶魔领主因太过愤怒而无法被安抚； 没有心智的生物太笨拙而无法被安抚；在沉睡的怪物也无法被安抚。","Whether the pacification succeeds or not, the invested piety and magic points are lost. If it does succeed, the monster is healed and you gain the monster's full experience value. Otherwise, the monster is unaffected and you gain nothing.":"不管安抚成功与否，付出的虔诚值和魔力都会失去。 如果成功，那么怪物会被治愈，并且你会获得怪物全部经验值。 否则，怪物不受到影响，你却一无所获。","Heals a creature other than yourself by a moderate amount, depending on Invocations skill. Using this ability on hostile monsters will try to turn them neutral. This works best on living creatures, with the undead and demons being progressively harder to pacify. Intelligent creatures are also more difficult to pacify. Ghosts of dead adventurers and demon lords are too wrathful to be pacified, mindless creatures are too unintelligent to be pacified, and no monster can be pacified while it is asleep. Whether the pacification succeeds or not, the invested piety and magic points are lost. If it does succeed, the monster is healed and you gain the monster's full experience value. Otherwise, the monster is unaffected and you gain nothing.":"根据祈神技能，治疗好一个你以外的目标生物的一些创伤。 对敌对怪物使用此能力将尝试使其变为中立。 这对活的生物最有效，而亡灵和恶魔则更难以安抚。智慧生物也更难以安抚。 死去的冒险者的鬼魂和恶魔领主因太过愤怒而无法被安抚； 没有心智的生物太笨拙而无法被安抚；在沉睡的怪物也无法被安抚。 不管安抚成功与否，付出的虔诚值和魔力都会失去。 如果成功，那么怪物会被治愈，并且你会获得怪物全部经验值。 否则，怪物不受到影响，你却一无所获。","Heals a moderate amount of health, depending on Invocations skill.":"根据祈神技能，治疗好一些创伤。","Greatly increases your maximum health and magic points, depending on Invocations skill. Your current health and magic points will also be increased proportionally.":"根据祈神技能，极大地提高你的最大生命和魔力值。 你当前的生命和魔力值也会成比例增加。","Attempts to banish a creature into the Abyss. If the attempt succeeds, you gain some piety and the creature's full experience value. Even creatures that resist are left malmutated and weakened by the brush with the Abyss. Invocations skill makes Banishment harder to resist.":"尝试将一只怪物放逐到深渊中。如果尝试成功， 你会获得一些虔诚值和怪物的全部经验值。即使是能够抵抗的生物， 也会因与深渊摩擦而招致有害变异并变得虚弱。祈神技能会让此能力更难被怪物抵抗。","Corrupts the current level by unleashing Abyssal energies on it. This will cause the area nearby to change appearance, and will gate in creatures from the Abyss bent on causing destruction. This will not work on levels already corrupted or in the Abyss itself. The size of the effect is increased by Invocations skill.":"释放深渊的能量，腐化当前所在的楼层。 这会导致该楼层的外貌剧变，并为深渊的怪物敞开大门，来进行破坏。 它无法作用于已遭到腐化的楼层和深渊本身。其效果随祈神技能的提升而增强。","Transports you to Lugonu's realm instantly. The effort of even using the ability will leave your health depleted.":"立刻将你传送到卢格努的领域中。即使只是使用该能力，也会耗竭你的生命值。","Permanently corrupts a melee weapon of your choice with a localised field of distortion. This blessing may only be used once, and it cannot be used on artefact weapons.":"用局部扭曲场永久腐化你所选择的一件近战武器。 这个祝福只能使用一次，且不可用于神器武器。","Draws three cards from any deck, and allows you to choose one to play, discarding the other two.":"从任意一副牌组中抽三张牌，选择一张进行游戏，然后弃掉另外两张。","Plays four cards from a deck in the time it normally takes to draw a single card.":"在通常抽一张牌的时间内，从一副牌中打出四张牌。","Draws five cards from your choice of decks, and allows you to sort them into any order. Subsequently, you can draw these cards in the order you chose. Re-using this ability will discard the current stack.":"从你选择的牌组中抽五张牌，并可以把它们排为任何次序。 随后，你可以按照你所选的次序抽取这些牌。 重新使用这个能力将丢弃当前的牌堆。","Grows a short-lived ballistomycete at the location you choose. A ballistomycete occasionally releases spores that quickly seek out foes and violently explode, damaging and confusing all living things caught in the blast.":"在你所选的一个位置长出短暂存活的孢子炮菌。孢子炮菌偶尔会释放孢子， 它会迅速发现敌人并剧烈爆炸，对被卷入爆炸的所有活物造成伤害和混乱。","Invocations skill increases the health and duration of the ballistomycete as well as the damage of its exploding spores.":"提升祈神技能可以提高孢子炮菌的生命值和存在时间，以及孢子爆炸的伤害。","Grows a short-lived ballistomycete at the location you choose. A ballistomycete occasionally releases spores that quickly seek out foes and violently explode, damaging and confusing all living things caught in the blast. Invocations skill increases the health and duration of the ballistomycete as well as the damage of its exploding spores.":"在你所选的一个位置长出短暂存活的孢子炮菌。孢子炮菌偶尔会释放孢子， 它会迅速发现敌人并剧烈爆炸，对被卷入爆炸的所有活物造成伤害和混乱。 提升祈神技能可以提高孢子炮菌的生命值和存在时间，以及孢子爆炸的伤害。","Permanently destroys a wall-like structure, growing a short-lived plant ally in its place. Even a tree will give its life to support the will of Fedhas, and only truly indestructible walls are immune to this power.":"永久破坏一个墙类结构，在其位置生出一个短期存活的友方植物。 即使是一棵树也要献出生命来支持费德哈的意志， 只有真正无法破坏的墙壁才能抵抗这种力量。","Grows a short-lived oklob plant at the location you choose. These dangerous plants spray corrosive vitriol at your foes.":"在你所选的一个位置长出短暂存活的酸箭草。 这些危险的植物会向你的敌人喷吐腐蚀性的酸。","Invocations skill increases the health and duration of the oklob as well as the frequency with which it sprays its acid.":"提升祈神技能可提高酸箭草的生命值和存在时间，以及其喷吐酸液的频率。","Grows a short-lived oklob plant at the location you choose. These dangerous plants spray corrosive vitriol at your foes. Invocations skill increases the health and duration of the oklob as well as the frequency with which it sprays its acid.":"在你所选的一个位置长出短暂存活的酸箭草。 这些危险的植物会向你的敌人喷吐腐蚀性的酸。 提升祈神技能可提高酸箭草的生命值和存在时间，以及其喷吐酸液的频率。","Warps the flow of time, causing monsters to skip forwards in time relative to you.":"扭曲时间流，导致周围的怪物相对于你跳跃到未来的时间。","Causes damage to everyone in sight who is moving faster than you, dealing more damage with greater differences in speed.":"对视线中每个移动速度比你快的造成伤害，速度差异越大，造成的伤害越大。","Removes you completely from the flow of time. Time will pass as it usually does, and monsters will wander away and sometimes even fall back to sleep. After some time has passed, you will return in the same state as the very second you departed. Invocations skill increases the likelihood that your absence will have been so long that alert monsters have fallen asleep again.":"将你从时间流中脱离出来。 周围的一切仍会照常活动：怪物会四处游荡，有时甚至会重新睡去。 过一段时间后，你将回到与离开时的相同的状态。 提升祈神技能可以增加怪物因你长时间离去而再度陷入沉睡的可能性。","Calls forth acidic ooze from the walls of the dungeon around you, damaging foes depending on the number of slimy walls they remain adjacent to.":"从你周围的地牢墙壁中召唤出酸性软泥，对敌人造成伤害， 伤害取决于与其相邻的黏性墙壁的数量。","Destroys a chosen cursed equipped item, relieving the wearer of the curse.":"摧毁一个选定的诅咒装备，解除佩戴者的诅咒。","Sends funds to a merchant to help them set up shop at your location. The cost of funding a shop increases with the number of shops funded.":"资助商人在你那里开店。 开店的成本会随以这种方式开设的商店的数量增加而增加。","Gives 3000 gold to Gozag to spread throughout the inhabitants of the current branch, only possible if the branch has intelligent inhabitants. Those monsters may then become uninterested in fighting you (with tougher inhabitants having an increasing chance of being bribed), and more rarely will join your ranks, though they will not leave their home branch. Enemies accepting a bribe will lower the remaining bribe fund; upon its exhaustion, bribed enemies will become indifferent if they have not become your allies.":"给哥萨戈3000金币，将其散布给当前分支的所有居住者，前提是该分支有智慧生物。 这些怪物可能会失去与你战斗的兴趣（越强大的生物被贿赂的几率越大）， 并有很小的几率会加入你的行列，尽管他们还是不会离开自己的分支。 接受贿赂的敌人会降低剩余的贿赂资金； 当其耗尽时，如果贿赂的敌人没能成为盟友，他们将变得冷漠。","Causes your elemental clouds to coalesce into friendly elementals. Your Invocations skill increases the maximum number of elementals that can be created with one use of the ability.":"使你的元素云合并成友好的元素。 提升祈神技能，可以增加使用此能力时一次生成的最大元素数量。","Blasts the entire area around you with powerful natural forces. Invocations skill increases both damage and area affected.":"用强大的自然力量轰炸你周围整片区域。提升祈神技能会增加伤害和受影响的范围。","Performs an incredibly fast leap to a targeted location, causing an explosion upon landing which damages all adjacent foes. The amount of damage done increases with your piety and experience level.":"以难以置信的速度跳到目标位置，着陆时引起爆炸，对所有相邻的敌人造成伤害。 造成的伤害会随你的虔诚值和经验等级的提高而增加。","Reveals Ru's truth to your enemies, dealing severe damage to all enemies in your line of sight. Affected creatures may be paralysed, slowed or have their magic drained. The damage dealt increases with your piety and experience level.":"向敌人昭示入的真言，对视线内所有敌人造成严重伤害。 受影响的生物可能会麻痹、减慢或流失其魔力。 造成的伤害会随你的虔诚值和经验等级的提高而增加。","Sacrifices purity of body or mind, causing a single mutation.":"舍弃身体或心灵的纯洁，造成一次变异。","Sacrifices the ability to use magical scrolls in combat unless badly injured.":"舍弃在战斗中使用魔法卷轴的能力，除非身受重伤。","Sacrifices the ability to drink potions in combat unless badly injured.":"舍弃在战斗中饮用药水的能力，除非身受重伤。","Sacrifices magical essence, causing a single mutation.":"舍弃魔法精华，引发一次变异。","Sacrifices physical health, causing a single mutation.":"舍弃身体健康，引发一次变异。","Sacrifices stealth, causing you to always be noticed by foes and preventing you from having any ranks in the Stealth skill.":"舍弃潜行，使你总能被敌人注意到，并让你的潜行技能无法达到任何等级。","Sacrifices forms, preventing you from voluntarily changing your form and from having any ranks in the Shapeshifting skill.":"舍弃形态，你无法自行改变形态，也无法在变身技能上达到任何等级。","Sacrifices the ability to evoke any magical items, and prevents you from having any ranks in the Evocations skill.":"舍弃激活魔法物品的能力，并让你的魔力释放技能无法达到任何等级。","This includes wands and other items which use Evocations skill - that is, it does *not* affect reaching weapons, talismans, and ziggurat figurines. This also renders magical staves much less effective in melee.":"这包括魔杖和其他需要用到魔力释放技能的物品—— 但这*不会*影响长柄武器、符咒和金字塔雕像。 这也使得法杖在近战时的效果大大降低。","Sacrifices the ability to evoke any magical items, and prevents you from having any ranks in the Evocations skill. This includes wands and other items which use Evocations skill - that is, it does *not* affect reaching weapons, talismans, and ziggurat figurines. This also renders magical staves much less effective in melee.":"舍弃激活魔法物品的能力，并让你的魔力释放技能无法达到任何等级。 这包括魔杖和其他需要用到魔力释放技能的物品—— 但这*不会*影响长柄武器、符咒和金字塔雕像。 这也使得法杖在近战时的效果大大降低。","Sacrifices love, causing all creatures to become hostile, even those created by you. Monsters that are spell residue and which do not act independently, such as orbs of destruction and spectral weapons, are the only things which can remain friendly.":"舍弃爱，使所有的生物变得敌对，甚至那些由你创造的。 只有法术残留物和不能独立行动的，比如毁灭球和幽灵武器，才能保持友好。","Sacrifices courage, causing you to become terrified of dangerous monsters. Such monsters fill you with horror, which reduces the power of your spells and your ability to hit and damage monsters in combat.":"舍弃勇气，会让你恐惧危险的怪物。 这些怪物会让你充满恐惧，这会削弱你的法术威力以及战斗中打击和伤害怪物的能力。","Sacrifices arcana, causing you to lose the ability to use certain schools of magic and preventing you from having any ranks in those skills.":"舍弃奥术，使你失去使用某些类型魔法的能力，并让你的这些技能无法达到任何等级。","Sacrifices nimbleness, preventing you from having any ranks in the Dodging skill. This sacrifice is worth more if you cannot train Armour.":"舍弃敏捷，使你无法在闪避技能上达到任何等级。 如果你无法训练护甲技能，这个舍弃会更有价值。","Sacrifices durability, preventing you from having any ranks in the Armour skill. This sacrifice is worth more if you cannot train Dodging.":"舍弃耐久，使你无法在护甲技能上达到任何等级。 如果你无法训练闪避技能，这个舍弃会更有价值。","Sacrifices a hand, causing you to lose the ability to use shields{{ if you.race() ~= \"Formicid\" then return \" and two-handed weapons\" end }}, and to be able to wear one fewer ring.":"舍弃一只手，使你不能使用盾牌{{ if you.race() ~= \"Formicid\" then return \"和双手武器\" end }}且可佩戴戒指数减一。","Sacrifices some of your past experiences, causing you to lose one level immediately and also to have the maximum level you can attain lowered by one.":"舍弃一些你的过去的经验，使你立刻降两个等级，你可达到的等级上限也会降一级。","Sacrifices your skills, causing you to have all of your skill aptitudes decreased by one. This will likely cause you to lose ranks in trained skills.":"牺牲你的技能，使你所有技能的资质降低 1。这很可能使已训练技能失去等级。","Sacrifices an eye, causing you to have a much harder time hitting targets.":"舍弃一只眼，使你更难命中目标。","Sacrifices your resistance to extreme temperatures, causing you to become vulnerable to heat and cold.":"舍弃你对极端温度的抵抗力，使你易受冷和热的伤害。","Rejects all offered sacrifices. Doing so means Ru will take more time evaluating your readiness for future sacrifices. Ru will not offer more sacrifices while there is an existing offer still extended.":"拒绝所有要求的舍弃。这意味着入将会花更多时间评估你对后面的舍弃所做的准备。 在现有的舍弃延期的情况下，入不会要求做出其他舍弃。","Each consecutive rejection increases the sacrifice timer significantly. Accepting a sacrifice will reset the timer to the standard length.":"每个连续的拒绝都会显著增加舍弃的计时。 接受舍弃会将计时重置到标准长度。","Rejects all offered sacrifices. Doing so means Ru will take more time evaluating your readiness for future sacrifices. Ru will not offer more sacrifices while there is an existing offer still extended. Each consecutive rejection increases the sacrifice timer significantly. Accepting a sacrifice will reset the timer to the standard length.":"拒绝所有要求的舍弃。这意味着入将会花更多时间评估你对后面的舍弃所做的准备。 在现有的舍弃延期的情况下，入不会要求做出其他舍弃。 每个连续的拒绝都会显著增加舍弃的计时。 接受舍弃会将计时重置到标准长度。","Passes through a contiguous line of creatures at superhuman speed, ending up in a new location. Any creatures passed through in this way will be confused briefly, with the duration of confusion increasing with Invocations skill.":"以超人的速度穿过连续的生物线，最终到一个新的位置。 穿过的任何生物都会被短暂地混乱，混乱持续时间随着祈神技能的提升而增加。","Merges with a target emotionally and physically, and then bursts forth from them, violently splitting them apart and killing them instantly. This ability becomes easier to use as the worshipper's piety and Invocations skill increase.":"在情感上和身体上与目标融合，然后从他们身上爆发，猛烈地将他们分开， 并立即杀死他们。当信徒的虔诚值和祈神技能提升时，这个技能变得更易使用。","More violent Uskayaw sects consider their members not to be true worshippers until they have performed this rite.":"更狂热的乌斯卡亚教派认为，其成员在完成这一仪式前不算真正的信徒。","Merges with a target emotionally and physically, and then bursts forth from them, violently splitting them apart and killing them instantly. This ability becomes easier to use as the worshipper's piety and Invocations skill increase. More violent Uskayaw sects consider their members not to be true worshippers until they have performed this rite.":"在情感上和身体上与目标融合，然后从他们身上爆发，猛烈地将他们分开， 并立即杀死他们。当信徒的虔诚值和祈神技能提升时，这个技能变得更易使用。 更狂热的乌斯卡亚教派认为，其成员在完成这一仪式前不算真正的信徒。","Renounces your faith. This will make you leave your god (and usually anger said god).":"与你信仰的神断绝关系。这会导致你不再信仰该神（通常来说，这会触怒该神）。","Swears fealty to Beogh, the god of cave orcs. This god demands that all non-believers must die, but new believers must be spared and accepted into the fold. Beware, for orcs who do not see you convert may still be hostile until you have built your reputation!":"向洞穴兽人之神——比欧弗宣誓效忠。 比欧弗要求杀死一切异教徒，但新信徒会被饶恕，并被接纳入教会。需要小心： 在你名声响亮起来之前，没有看见你皈依比欧弗的兽人可能还是会与你为敌！","All other gods hate Beogh, and do not take desertion lightly.":"所有其他神祇都厌恶比欧弗，不要轻易背叛。","Swears fealty to Beogh, the god of cave orcs. This god demands that all non-believers must die, but new believers must be spared and accepted into the fold. Beware, for orcs who do not see you convert may still be hostile until you have built your reputation! All other gods hate Beogh, and do not take desertion lightly.":"向洞穴兽人之神——比欧弗宣誓效忠。 比欧弗要求杀死一切异教徒，但新信徒会被饶恕，并被接纳入教会。需要小心： 在你名声响亮起来之前，没有看见你皈依比欧弗的兽人可能还是会与你为敌！ 所有其他神祇都厌恶比欧弗，不要轻易背叛。","Donates half of your gold to Zin, which will increase your piety over time. The overall increase is determined by the size of your donation.":"将你的一半黄金献给辛，你的虔诚值会随时间而增加。 所增的总量取决于你的捐献数额。","Recalls your ancestor from anywhere in the dungeon to your immediate surroundings.":"将你的先祖从地牢的任何地方召回到你的跟前。","Restores your ancestor to an idyllic vision of their best self. Their wounds are forgotten and a glow of perfection infuses them, giving them a short-lived but dramatic increase in strength, spellcasting, and armour. The quality of the healing and duration of the idealisation granted are both improved by the Invocations skill.":"使你的先祖复现自己心目中完美的愿景。 他们的创伤被忘却，无瑕的光芒注入他们，使其力量、施法能力和护甲短暂而急剧地增强。 祈神技能可以提高治愈效果和理想化持续时间。","Forces a targeted creature to pass through the realms of memory and exchange places with your ancestor.":"迫使一个目标生物穿过记忆领域，与你的祖先交换位置。","With great piety, those near the target will be drained to a degree depending on Invocations skill.":"有着大量虔诚值，那些靠近目标的会被衰竭，其程度取决于祈神技能。","Forces a targeted creature to pass through the realms of memory and exchange places with your ancestor. With great piety, those near the target will be drained to a degree depending on Invocations skill.":"迫使一个目标生物穿过记忆领域，与你的祖先交换位置。 有着大量虔诚值，那些靠近目标的会被衰竭，其程度取决于祈神技能。","Remembers your ancestor as a knight, a strong melee combatant with superior defences. This choice is permanent and cannot be undone.":"回想起你的先祖是个骑士，他是个有着出色近战和防御能力的战士。 此选择是永久的，不能撤消。","Remembers your ancestor as a battlemage, a warrior capable of relentless offence with both melee and conjurations. This choice is permanent and cannot be undone.":"回想你的先祖是个战斗法师，一个能够近战和使用魔法进行冷酷攻击的战士。 此选择是永久的，不能撤消。","Remembers your ancestor as a hexer, a cunning rogue capable of swift knifework and debilitating spellcasting. This choice is permanent and cannot be undone.":"回想起你的先祖是个妖术师，一个掌握熟练刀法和衰败魔法技能的狡猾的贼。 此选择是永久的，不能撤消。","Recalls who your ancestor preferred to be known as, correcting their name and gender.":"回忆你的先祖更喜欢被称为什么，并更正其姓名和性别。","Vaults off an adjacent wall towards enemies, striking all enemies adjacent to the landing spot and taking two turns to complete the motion.":"从相邻的墙壁跳起冲向敌人，对所有与着陆点相邻的敌人造成冲击， 这需要花两个回合完成动作。","Allows you to move at supernatural speeds, making any normal movements up to a distance of two tiles instant. Martial attacks performed under the effect of Serpent's Lash are more damaging and never miss.":"使你以超自然的速度移动，能瞬间移动到两格远的位置。 在蛇鞭的作用下，武术攻击具有更大的杀伤力且总能命中。","Invokes a storm of heavenly clouds. While the storm rages, your evasion and combat accuracy and damage are substantially increased, and striking enemies with martial attacks increases this bonus. The storm weakens over time and fades away once the bonus reaches zero. The heavenly clouds prevent invisibility, and obscure the vision of those outside the storm.":"引起一场天云风暴。当风暴肆虐时，你的闪避和战斗准确度和伤害会大幅增加， 而且通过武术攻击敌人时还会有加成。风暴会随着时间的推移而减弱， 一旦加成达到零就会消失。天云阻止了隐形，也模糊了风暴外的人的视线。","Armours yourself in fire, providing +7 AC and searing foes foolish enough to strike you in melee. The fire takes quite a long time to burn out.":"用火焰武装自己，提供7点防护并灼烧那些蠢到胆敢近战攻击你敌人。 火需要很长时间才能熄灭。","Conjures a swarm of animate flames all around you. These rapidly seek the nearest monsters, burning them. They will dissipate harmlessly if unable to reach a target or if you swap places with them.":"在你周围生成一群有生命的火焰。它们迅速寻找最近的怪物，灼烧它们。 如果没能碰到目标或与它们交换位置，它们将无害地消散。","Sends you floating upward and, after a short delay for Ignis to gather enough power, blasts you through the ceiling and into the level above. This ability may only be used once.":"你会向上飘浮，在伊格尼斯短暂延迟以收集足够的能量后， 会炸穿天花板，将你轰入上层。此能力只能使用一次。","Hops toward a chosen destination, landing somewhere nearby. After using this ability, you will be unable to hop again until you have spent some time not moving. (Other actions, such as casting spells and attacking, are fine.)":"朝选定的目的地跳跃，并落在附近的某处。 使用此能力后，必须有一段时间不移动，才能再次跳跃。 （施法、攻击等其他动作不受影响。）","Turns the user into living lightning and zaps them at the chosen monster, dealing electric damage to everything in their path and depositing the user at the bolt's end. After using this ability, you will be unable to use it again for a short time.":"将使用者化成一道活体闪电并击向选定的怪物， 对路径上的一切造成电击伤害，并将使用者送到闪电箭的终点。 使用此能力后，短时间内无法再次使用。","Torments nearby living foes, halving their health. The pain inflicted heals the user to an extent determined by Shapeshifting skill. After using this ability, you will be unable to use it again for a short time.":"折磨附近的活物敌人，使其生命值减半。 所造成的痛楚能治疗使用者，治愈量取决于变形术技能。 使用此能力后，短时间内无法再次使用它。","Calls on the power of Asmodeus to summon fiery demons of Hell. The demons summoned will remain friendly only for a limited time, eventually becoming hostile before vanishing. The success of the ability scales with the Evocations skill, and this ability is available only while wielding the Sceptre of Asmodeus.":"唤起阿斯蒙蒂斯的力量，召唤地狱的火系恶魔。 被召唤的恶魔只会在有限的时间内保持友好，在最终消失之前会变得敌对。 该能力的强度与魔力释放技能成正比，并且该能力仅在使用阿斯蒙蒂斯的节杖时可用。","Blasts a targeted enemy with damnation. These unholy forces harm the victim and anyone adjacent, and are not affected by any means of protection, such as armour or resistances. However, certain creatures, usually those able to invoke damnation themselves, are entirely unscathed by damnation. The power of this ability scales with the Evocations skill.":"用天谴轰击一个目标敌人。这些邪恶力量会伤害目标及其相邻生物， 且不受护甲、抗性等任何保护手段削弱。 但某些生物，通常是那些本身也能释放天谴的生物，完全不受天谴伤害。 此能力的威力随魔力释放技能提高。","Causes the caster to radiate toxic energy, continuously inflicting poison on everything in line of sight for as long as the aura lasts. The power of this ability scales with the Evocations skill, and this ability is available only while wielding the Staff of Olgreb.":"使施法者散发出剧毒能量，在光环持续期间不断使视线内的一切中毒。 此能力的威力随魔力释放技能提高，且只有持握奥尔格雷布之杖时才能使用。","Grabs hold of another creature's shadow and rapidly unleashes their spells and abilities as if they were your own, aimed at random enemies. Creatures they summon this way will belong to you, and many beneficial effects that they would apply to themselves will be applied to you instead. You are also fully protected from any damage they would cause.":"抓住另一个生物的影子，并快速释放它们的法术和能力，如同你自己的一般， 瞄准随机的敌人。它们以这种方式召唤的生物将属于你，许多它们本应施加于 自身的增益效果将转而施加于你。你也不会受到它们造成的任何伤害。","Can only be used on creatures with eligible spells that they could productively cast at the moment. The process also leaves the victim's shadow too dim to grasp a second time - once used successfully on a target, it may never be used on them again.":"只能对拥有在当前时刻可以有效施放的合适法术的生物使用。 这个过程还会使受害者的影子变得太暗而无法再次抓取—— 一旦对目标成功使用，就再也不能对其使用。","(Not all spells can be cast via this method; those which cannot will be marked with an exclamation mark when examined.)":"（并非所有法术都能通过这种方法施放；无法施放的法术在检视时 将以感叹号标记。）","Grabs hold of another creature's shadow and rapidly unleashes their spells and abilities as if they were your own, aimed at random enemies. Creatures they summon this way will belong to you, and many beneficial effects that they would apply to themselves will be applied to you instead. You are also fully protected from any damage they would cause. Can only be used on creatures with eligible spells that they could productively cast at the moment. The process also leaves the victim's shadow too dim to grasp a second time - once used successfully on a target, it may never be used on them again. (Not all spells can be cast via this method; those which cannot will be marked with an exclamation mark when examined.)":"抓住另一个生物的影子，并快速释放它们的法术和能力，如同你自己的一般， 瞄准随机的敌人。它们以这种方式召唤的生物将属于你，许多它们本应施加于 自身的增益效果将转而施加于你。你也不会受到它们造成的任何伤害。 只能对拥有在当前时刻可以有效施放的合适法术的生物使用。 这个过程还会使受害者的影子变得太暗而无法再次抓取—— 一旦对目标成功使用，就再也不能对其使用。 （并非所有法术都能通过这种方法施放；无法施放的法术在检视时 将以感叹号标记。）","Unleashes the full power of your predatory instincts to leap towards a terrified enemy and perform a vicious melee attack against them. This attack receives a damage multiplier based on your Shapeshifting skill. If it kills them, you will always perform a Howl afterward.":"释放你全部掠食本能的力量，向一个恐惧的敌人跳跃并对其发动凶猛的近战攻击。 此攻击根据你的变形术技能获得伤害倍率。如果击杀了目标，你将在之后 自动发动嚎叫。","Can only target an enemy who is afraid, and who has at least one occupiable tile adjacent to them.":"只能瞄准处于恐惧状态且至少有一个可占据的相邻格子的敌人。","Unleashes the full power of your predatory instincts to leap towards a terrified enemy and perform a vicious melee attack against them. This attack receives a damage multiplier based on your Shapeshifting skill. If it kills them, you will always perform a Howl afterward. Can only target an enemy who is afraid, and who has at least one occupiable tile adjacent to them.":"释放你全部掠食本能的力量，向一个恐惧的敌人跳跃并对其发动凶猛的近战攻击。 此攻击根据你的变形术技能获得伤害倍率。如果击杀了目标，你将在之后 自动发动嚎叫。 只能瞄准处于恐惧状态且至少有一个可占据的相邻格子的敌人。","Beseeches Beogh to grant you an army with which to wreak bloody retribution. The user will be immediately surrounded by orcish allies, with more of them arriving over time from all directions. The prayer lasts a considerable length of time, but will expire far more rapidly once there are no more foes in sight.":"恳求贝奥格赐予你一支军队来实施血腥复仇。使用者将立即被兽人盟友包围， 更多盟友将随时间从四面八方赶来。祈祷持续相当长的时间， 但一旦视野中不再有敌人，持续时间将大大缩短。","Usable only while you are standing over the corpse of one of your apostles, and at most once per death.":"只能在站在你的一位使徒的尸体上时使用，每次死亡最多使用一次。","Beseeches Beogh to grant you an army with which to wreak bloody retribution. The user will be immediately surrounded by orcish allies, with more of them arriving over time from all directions. The prayer lasts a considerable length of time, but will expire far more rapidly once there are no more foes in sight. Usable only while you are standing over the corpse of one of your apostles, and at most once per death.":"恳求贝奥格赐予你一支军队来实施血腥复仇。使用者将立即被兽人盟友包围， 更多盟友将随时间从四面八方赶来。祈祷持续相当长的时间， 但一旦视野中不再有敌人，持续时间将大大缩短。 只能在站在你的一位使徒的尸体上时使用，每次死亡最多使用一次。","Permanently carves an Infernal Mark into yourself, forever tainting body and soul in service of the Destroyer.":"在你的身上永久刻下一个地狱印记，永远玷污身体与灵魂，以侍奉毁灭者。","So long as you continue to worship Makhleb, this mark will grant you the following power:":"只要你继续崇拜马科列布，此印记将赋予你以下力量：","Permanently carves an Infernal Mark into yourself, forever tainting body and soul in service of the Destroyer. So long as you continue to worship Makhleb, this mark will grant you the following power:":"在你的身上永久刻下一个地狱印记，永远玷污身体与灵魂，以侍奉毁灭者。 只要你继续崇拜马科列布，此印记将赋予你以下力量：","Exhales a blast of oxidizing vapour that continuously corrodes and weakens the attacks of creatures which stand inside it. These clouds are long-lasting, but do only minimal damage.":"呼出一股氧化蒸汽，持续腐蚀和削弱站在其中的生物的攻击力。 这些云雾持续时间很长，但只造成极少伤害。","Fully manifests your poltergeist nature, making all the armour you are haunting fly out and attack independently of your other actions for a short while - boots and scarves and helmets assailing your foes from all directions while a gleeful din fills the air.":"完全展现你的骚灵本质，使你附身的所有护甲飞出并独立于你的其他动作 进行攻击，持续一小段时间——靴子、围巾和头盔从四面八方袭击敌人， 同时欢快的喧嚣声充满空气。","These items are still tethered to you and cannot be directed more than a short distance away, but you do not share any damage they suffer and can freely fire through them. Their attacks may inflict a variety of minor maladies on your foes - sometimes dazing, draining, or even confusing them.":"这些物品仍与你相连，无法被指挥到太远的地方， 但你不分担它们受到的伤害，也可以自由地穿过它们射击。 它们的攻击可能使敌人陷入各种轻微的负面状态——有时会使其眩晕、衰竭， 甚至混乱。","After using this ability, you must gain experience points before you can recover enough power to use it again.":"使用此能力后，你必须获得经验值才能恢复足够的力量再次使用。","Fully manifests your poltergeist nature, making all the armour you are haunting fly out and attack independently of your other actions for a short while - boots and scarves and helmets assailing your foes from all directions while a gleeful din fills the air. These items are still tethered to you and cannot be directed more than a short distance away, but you do not share any damage they suffer and can freely fire through them. Their attacks may inflict a variety of minor maladies on your foes - sometimes dazing, draining, or even confusing them. After using this ability, you must gain experience points before you can recover enough power to use it again.":"完全展现你的骚灵本质，使你附身的所有护甲飞出并独立于你的其他动作 进行攻击，持续一小段时间——靴子、围巾和头盔从四面八方袭击敌人， 同时欢快的喧嚣声充满空气。 这些物品仍与你相连，无法被指挥到太远的地方， 但你不分担它们受到的伤害，也可以自由地穿过它们射击。 它们的攻击可能使敌人陷入各种轻微的负面状态——有时会使其眩晕、衰竭， 甚至混乱。 使用此能力后，你必须获得经验值才能恢复足够的力量再次使用。","Breathes a spray of concentrated acid which leaves corrosive clouds on any unoccupied tiles it passes over and corrodes whatever it hits.":"喷出一股浓缩酸液，在其经过的任何未占据格子上留下腐蚀性云雾， 并腐蚀击中的一切。","Breathes a blast of volatile embers that explode violently around each creature they touch. It is harmless to its user.":"喷出一股挥发性余烬，在接触每个生物时猛烈爆炸。对其使用者无害。","Frees this apostle from your service, sending them out to do good in the world in Beogh's name.":"将这位使徒从你的服务中解放，派遣他们以贝奥格之名在世间行善。","Stokes your ghostly flames to a fever pitch, greatly enhancing your spellcasting at the cost of burning away all accumulated memories.":"将你的幽灵火焰煽至炽热，大大增强你的施法能力，代价是燃烧所有积累的记忆。","While in this state, your damage-dealing spells cost no MP, are unaffected by encumbrance, and you receive a bonus to their spell success and power (the latter of which increases with your experience level). Any spellclaw attack made while Enkindled inflicts bonus damage proportional to the level of spell cast, and heals you for a percentage of the damage dealt.":"在此状态下，你的伤害法术不消耗法力，不受负重影响，并且会获得施法成功率 和法术威力加成（后者随你的经验等级提升）。在燃魂状态下进行的任何法术爪攻击 会造成与所施放法术等级成比例的额外伤害，并为你恢复伤害量一定百分比的生命值。","Each spell you cast while Enkindled consumes a memory, and the state will end once you have no more left (or after a short period of time, regardless).":"你在燃魂状态下施放的每个法术会消耗一份记忆，当记忆耗尽后状态将结束 （或在一小段时间后无论如何都会结束）。","At your current experience level, you can hold enough memories to cast a maximum of {{return 3 + math.floor(you.xl() * 3 / 20);}} spells in a row this way.":"在你当前的经验等级下，你可以持有足够的记忆以此方式连续施放 最多 {{return 3 + math.floor(you.xl() * 3 / 20);}} 个法术。","Stokes your ghostly flames to a fever pitch, greatly enhancing your spellcasting at the cost of burning away all accumulated memories. While in this state, your damage-dealing spells cost no MP, are unaffected by encumbrance, and you receive a bonus to their spell success and power (the latter of which increases with your experience level). Any spellclaw attack made while Enkindled inflicts bonus damage proportional to the level of spell cast, and heals you for a percentage of the damage dealt. Each spell you cast while Enkindled consumes a memory, and the state will end once you have no more left (or after a short period of time, regardless). At your current experience level, you can hold enough memories to cast a maximum of {{return 3 + math.floor(you.xl() * 3 / 20);}} spells in a row this way.":"将你的幽灵火焰煽至炽热，大大增强你的施法能力，代价是燃烧所有积累的记忆。 在此状态下，你的伤害法术不消耗法力，不受负重影响，并且会获得施法成功率 和法术威力加成（后者随你的经验等级提升）。在燃魂状态下进行的任何法术爪攻击 会造成与所施放法术等级成比例的额外伤害，并为你恢复伤害量一定百分比的生命值。 你在燃魂状态下施放的每个法术会消耗一份记忆，当记忆耗尽后状态将结束 （或在一小段时间后无论如何都会结束）。 在你当前的经验等级下，你可以持有足够的记忆以此方式连续施放 最多 {{return 3 + math.floor(you.xl() * 3 / 20);}} 个法术。","Engulfs the user's surroundings in Yredelemnul's inexorable grip. So long as you remain within this profane sanctuary, all hostile creatures that share it with you will be bound in place, and their life force will be continuously drained to restore your own. Victims who are isolated from their allies will take damage at a greatly increased rate.":"将使用者的周围吞没在伊莱德莱姆努尔的不可抗拒的掌控中。只要你留在这个 亵渎的圣所内，与你共享它的所有敌对生物将被束缚在原地，它们的生命力 将被持续汲取以恢复你自己的生命。与盟友隔离的受害者将以大幅提高的速率 受到伤害。","The affected area will shrink over time, and a new one cannot be created until the old one has fully expired.":"受影响区域会随时间缩小，新的区域在旧的完全消失前无法创建。","Engulfs the user's surroundings in Yredelemnul's inexorable grip. So long as you remain within this profane sanctuary, all hostile creatures that share it with you will be bound in place, and their life force will be continuously drained to restore your own. Victims who are isolated from their allies will take damage at a greatly increased rate. The affected area will shrink over time, and a new one cannot be created until the old one has fully expired.":"将使用者的周围吞没在伊莱德莱姆努尔的不可抗拒的掌控中。只要你留在这个 亵渎的圣所内，与你共享它的所有敌对生物将被束缚在原地，它们的生命力 将被持续汲取以恢复你自己的生命。与盟友隔离的受害者将以大幅提高的速率 受到伤害。 受影响区域会随时间缩小，新的区域在旧的完全消失前无法创建。","Exhales a charged burst of electricity that will arc through a target and every other creature that is connected to it.":"呼出一股带电冲击，电弧会穿过目标及与其相连的所有其他生物。","Exhales a powerful wave of frost which encases anything it kills in a solid block of durable ice.":"呼出一股强大的冰霜之波，将被其杀死的任何目标封入坚固耐久的冰块。","Launches a roiling sphere of intense destructive force drawn from the {{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"endless fires of Gehenna.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"frigid wastes of Cocytus.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"wailing grief of Tartarus.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"ruthless spite of Dis.\" else return \"very Hells themselves.\" end }}":"发射一个翻涌的强烈毁灭力球体，汲取自{{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"无尽的火焚地狱之火。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"冰狱的极寒荒原。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"悲叹地狱的哀嚎悲痛。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"铁城的无情恶毒。\" else return \"地狱本身。\" end }}","This sphere gathers strength as it travels, and will attempt to home in on a designated target, though it moves and turns with considerable inertia. When it collides with a creature or other obstruction, it will detonate in a violent explosion of {{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"fire or lava\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"cold or ice\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"negative energy or devastation\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"acid or metal splinters\" else return \"hellish energy\" end }} whose radius depends on the distance travelled.":"此球体在行进中积聚力量，并会试图追踪指定的目标， 但移动和转向时具有相当大的惯性。当它与生物或其他障碍物碰撞时， 将引爆为一场由{{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"火焰或熔岩\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"寒冷或冰霜\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"负能量或毁灭\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"酸液或金属碎片\" else return \"地狱能量\" end }}构成的猛烈爆炸，其范围取决于行进距离。","You are protected from this explosion yourself.":"你不会受到此爆炸的伤害。","Launches a roiling sphere of intense destructive force drawn from the {{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"endless fires of Gehenna.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"frigid wastes of Cocytus.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"wailing grief of Tartarus.\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"ruthless spite of Dis.\" else return \"very Hells themselves.\" end }} This sphere gathers strength as it travels, and will attempt to home in on a designated target, though it moves and turns with considerable inertia. When it collides with a creature or other obstruction, it will detonate in a violent explosion of {{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"fire or lava\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"cold or ice\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"negative energy or devastation\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"acid or metal splinters\" else return \"hellish energy\" end }} whose radius depends on the distance travelled. You are protected from this explosion yourself.":"发射一个翻涌的强烈毁灭力球体，汲取自{{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"无尽的火焚地狱之火。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"冰狱的极寒荒原。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"悲叹地狱的哀嚎悲痛。\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"铁城的无情恶毒。\" else return \"地狱本身。\" end }} 此球体在行进中积聚力量，并会试图追踪指定的目标， 但移动和转向时具有相当大的惯性。当它与生物或其他障碍物碰撞时， 将引爆为一场由{{ if you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Gehenna destruction\") == 1 then return \"火焰或熔岩\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Cocytus destruction\") == 1 then return \"寒冷或冰霜\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Tartarus destruction\") == 1 then return \"负能量或毁灭\" elseif you.get_base_mutation_level(\"Dis destruction\") == 1 then return \"酸液或金属碎片\" else return \"地狱能量\" end }}构成的猛烈爆炸，其范围取决于行进距离。 你不会受到此爆炸的伤害。","Exhales a powerful blast of elemental devastation, which inflicts both fire and cold damage, and leaves clouds of poisonous vapour in its wake.":"呼出一股强大的元素毁灭之息，同时造成火焰和寒冷伤害， 并在其路径上留下毒气云。","Hurls a gout of umbral fire from the Black Torch, which deals irresistible damage to living, demonic, and holy beings. The torchlight will also briefly empower any of your undead servants caught in its blast, and is harmless to those who worship Yredelemnul. The damage is increased by Invocations skill.":"从黑火炬中掷出一股暗影之火，对活物、恶魔和神圣生物造成不可抵抗的伤害。 火炬之光还会短暂增强任何被其爆发击中的亡灵仆从，对崇拜伊莱德莱姆努尔的人 无害。伤害随祈神技能提升。","This ability can be used only while the torch is lit, and only a limited number of times on each floor. The number of uses available per floor increases with piety, and stoking the Black Torch's flames with a particularly remarkable soul by killing a unique named enemy will also provide an additional use.":"此能力只能在火炬点燃时使用，且每层使用次数有限。 每层可用次数随虔诚值增加，通过击杀一个独特命名敌人来用特别卓越的 灵魂煽旺黑火炬的火焰也会提供额外使用次数。","Hurls a gout of umbral fire from the Black Torch, which deals irresistible damage to living, demonic, and holy beings. The torchlight will also briefly empower any of your undead servants caught in its blast, and is harmless to those who worship Yredelemnul. The damage is increased by Invocations skill. This ability can be used only while the torch is lit, and only a limited number of times on each floor. The number of uses available per floor increases with piety, and stoking the Black Torch's flames with a particularly remarkable soul by killing a unique named enemy will also provide an additional use.":"从黑火炬中掷出一股暗影之火，对活物、恶魔和神圣生物造成不可抵抗的伤害。 火炬之光还会短暂增强任何被其爆发击中的亡灵仆从，对崇拜伊莱德莱姆努尔的人 无害。伤害随祈神技能提升。 此能力只能在火炬点燃时使用，且每层使用次数有限。 每层可用次数随虔诚值增加，通过击杀一个独特命名敌人来用特别卓越的 灵魂煽旺黑火炬的火焰也会提供额外使用次数。","Chooses one of the caster's destructive spells to grant to Spellspark Servitors they create in the future, replacing any spell granted to them previously. The caster must be capable of casting this spell themselves with a failure rate of no more than 20%.":"选择施法者的一个破坏性法术赋予其未来创造的法术火花仆从， 替换之前赋予它们的任何法术。施法者必须能够以不超过20%的失败率 自己施放此法术。","Note: imbuing a spell in this manner will take several turns and also dismiss your servitor if it is active.":"注意：以这种方式赋予法术将花费数回合，并且如果仆从处于活动状态， 也会将其解散。","Chooses one of the caster's destructive spells to grant to Spellspark Servitors they create in the future, replacing any spell granted to them previously. The caster must be capable of casting this spell themselves with a failure rate of no more than 20%. Note: imbuing a spell in this manner will take several turns and also dismiss your servitor if it is active.":"选择施法者的一个破坏性法术赋予其未来创造的法术火花仆从， 替换之前赋予它们的任何法术。施法者必须能够以不超过20%的失败率 自己施放此法术。 注意：以这种方式赋予法术将花费数回合，并且如果仆从处于活动状态， 也会将其解散。","Analyzes the structural composition of an artefact melee weapon in your inventory and imprints it upon your Platinum Paragon spell, allowing it to wield a functional replica of it whenever you create one.":"分析你物品栏中一件神器近战武器的结构组成，并将其烙印到你的 白金典范法术中，使你今后创造的白金典范都能使用该武器的功能性复制品。","Uses one's own body as a conduit to unleash an army of chaos upon the world. For a short while, lesser demons will continuously manifest near the user - provided there is something around for them to fight. While these demons may be individually short-lived, the legions of chaos as a whole are virtually inexhaustible.":"以自己的身体为媒介，向世界释放一支混沌军团。在短时间内， 较小的恶魔将持续在使用者附近显现——前提是周围有值得战斗的东西。 虽然这些恶魔个体可能存活时间不长，但混沌军团整体几乎是无穷无尽的。","Beckons a demon from the far reaches of Hell and binds it into service with your blood. At low Invocations skill, only lesser devils may be summoned, but major demons and even executioners may answer the call of those with high Invocations skill.":"从地狱的遥远角落召唤一个恶魔，并以你的血液将其绑定为仆从。 在低祈神技能时，只能召唤较小的恶魔，但高祈神技能者甚至可能召唤出 大恶魔和执行者。","Beware that the armies of chaos are prone to infighting, and sometimes a hostile demon may answer the ritual alongside your summoned servant.":"注意：混沌军团容易内斗，有时一个敌对的恶魔可能与你的召唤仆从 一同响应仪式。","Beckons a demon from the far reaches of Hell and binds it into service with your blood. At low Invocations skill, only lesser devils may be summoned, but major demons and even executioners may answer the call of those with high Invocations skill. Beware that the armies of chaos are prone to infighting, and sometimes a hostile demon may answer the ritual alongside your summoned servant.":"从地狱的遥远角落召唤一个恶魔，并以你的血液将其绑定为仆从。 在低祈神技能时，只能召唤较小的恶魔，但高祈神技能者甚至可能召唤出 大恶魔和执行者。 注意：混沌军团容易内斗，有时一个敌对的恶魔可能与你的召唤仆从 一同响应仪式。","Uses your peerless coglin ingenuity to invent and assemble a one-of-a-kind piece of equipment and permanently install it in yourself. Such inspiration does not strike twice, so choose wisely.":"运用你无与伦比的齿轮地精才智发明并组装一件独一无二的装备， 并将其永久安装在自己身上。这种灵感不会降临两次，所以请谨慎选择。","Leaps through the air in the blink of an eye. While it is impossible to control your destination, the movement is so abrupt and agile that no monster will be able to land a blow on you until you can act again, and many may lose track of your position entirely.":"瞬间跃过空中。虽然无法控制目的地，但移动如此突然和敏捷， 以至于在你能够再次行动之前没有怪物能击中你，许多怪物甚至可能完全 无法追踪你的位置。","You must spend a short while recovering between each use of this ability.":"每次使用此能力后，你需要短暂恢复。","Leaps through the air in the blink of an eye. While it is impossible to control your destination, the movement is so abrupt and agile that no monster will be able to land a blow on you until you can act again, and many may lose track of your position entirely. You must spend a short while recovering between each use of this ability.":"瞬间跃过空中。虽然无法控制目的地，但移动如此突然和敏捷， 以至于在你能够再次行动之前没有怪物能击中你，许多怪物甚至可能完全 无法追踪你的位置。 每次使用此能力后，你需要短暂恢复。","Raises the Black Torch aloft and calls upon Yredelemnul to light it aflame, marking the beginning of your attempt to conquer the current level of the dungeon. Yredelemnul only grants piety for kills made while the torch is lit.":"高举黑火炬并呼唤伊莱德莱姆努尔将其点燃，标志着你开始征服当前地牢楼层。 伊莱德莱姆努尔只会为火炬点燃时进行的击杀提供虔诚值。","Those who have earned some of Yredelemnul's favour will be gifted temporary undead servants to help begin their conquest, with stronger servants being provided to the experienced and especially pious.":"那些已经赢得伊莱德莱姆努尔一些好感的人将被赐予临时的亡灵仆从来帮助 开始他们的征服，经验丰富且特别虔诚的人将获得更强大的仆从。","Yredelemnul does not offer second chances - the torch will be extinguished when you leave the current floor, and it may only be lit once per floor, ever.":"伊莱德莱姆努尔不提供第二次机会——当你离开当前楼层时火炬将熄灭， 且每层只能点燃一次，永不再来。","Raises the Black Torch aloft and calls upon Yredelemnul to light it aflame, marking the beginning of your attempt to conquer the current level of the dungeon. Yredelemnul only grants piety for kills made while the torch is lit. Those who have earned some of Yredelemnul's favour will be gifted temporary undead servants to help begin their conquest, with stronger servants being provided to the experienced and especially pious. Yredelemnul does not offer second chances - the torch will be extinguished when you leave the current floor, and it may only be lit once per floor, ever.":"高举黑火炬并呼唤伊莱德莱姆努尔将其点燃，标志着你开始征服当前地牢楼层。 伊莱德莱姆努尔只会为火炬点燃时进行的击杀提供虔诚值。 那些已经赢得伊莱德莱姆努尔一些好感的人将被赐予临时的亡灵仆从来帮助 开始他们的征服，经验丰富且特别虔诚的人将获得更强大的仆从。 伊莱德莱姆努尔不提供第二次机会——当你离开当前楼层时火炬将熄灭， 且每层只能点燃一次，永不再来。","Spits an enormous ball of mud that knocks back whatever it hits and drenches the surrounding area in a mud slick which impedes enemy movement and causes them to sometimes fumble their attacks.":"喷出一大团泥球，击退被击中的一切，并用泥泞覆盖周围区域， 阻碍敌人移动并导致它们有时攻击失手。","Breathes a line of noxious vapour which can confuse anything standing in it which does not resist poison. At higher levels, the clouds can cover a larger area and last longer.":"喷吐出一道毒雾；站在其中且无法抵抗毒素的生物可能陷入混乱。 随着等级提高，云雾可以覆盖更大范围并持续更久。","Breathes a large blast of pure antimagic that dispels magical effects from every creature it hits and also significantly interferes with their ability to cast spells for a while. It is harmless to its user.":"喷出一大股纯净的反魔法能量，驱散击中的每个生物的魔法效果， 并在一段时间内显著干扰它们的施法能力。对其使用者无害。","Invokes a night from before the stars first burned in the sky, engulfing your surroundings in impenetrable darkness. The user's sight radius will be reduced to nothing, preventing enemies from tracking or aiming abilities at you, and slowly expand back to normal over the duration of the effect. Your stealth will also be increased.":"唤起星辰第一次在天空中燃烧之前的夜晚，用无法穿透的黑暗吞没你的周围。 使用者的视野半径将被减至零，阻止敌人追踪或瞄准你使用能力， 并在效果持续期间缓慢恢复至正常。你的潜行能力也会增加。","It cannot be invoked again until its effect has fully ended, as even the very first night of creation must eventually give way to day.":"直到其效果完全结束前无法再次使用， 因为即使是创世之初的第一个夜晚最终也必须让位于白昼。","Invocations skill increases the duration of the effect.":"祈神技能增加效果的持续时间。","Invokes a night from before the stars first burned in the sky, engulfing your surroundings in impenetrable darkness. The user's sight radius will be reduced to nothing, preventing enemies from tracking or aiming abilities at you, and slowly expand back to normal over the duration of the effect. Your stealth will also be increased. It cannot be invoked again until its effect has fully ended, as even the very first night of creation must eventually give way to day. Invocations skill increases the duration of the effect.":"唤起星辰第一次在天空中燃烧之前的夜晚，用无法穿透的黑暗吞没你的周围。 使用者的视野半径将被减至零，阻止敌人追踪或瞄准你使用能力， 并在效果持续期间缓慢恢复至正常。你的潜行能力也会增加。 直到其效果完全结束前无法再次使用， 因为即使是创世之初的第一个夜晚最终也必须让位于白昼。 祈神技能增加效果的持续时间。","Recalls your apostles from anywhere in the dungeon to your immediate surroundings.":"从地牢各处将你的使徒召唤到你的紧邻周围。","Anoints a defeated apostle, and welcomes them as a permanent follower. They will follow you between floors and into any peril, willingly giving their life for the cause and their kin.":"为一个被击败的使徒施洗，欢迎他们成为永久的追随者。他们将跟随你 穿梭于各楼层，进入任何险境，甘愿为事业和同胞献出生命。","If they die, Beogh will eventually revive them once you gain sufficient piety - this process can be greatly accelerated by satisfying Beogh with the slaying of all foes who may have contributed to their apostle's death.":"如果他们牺牲了，贝奥格最终会在你获得足够虔诚值后复活他们—— 这个过程可以通过满足贝奥格，杀死所有可能参与使徒死亡的敌人 来大大加速。","You can have at most 3 followers accompanying you at a time, though you may freely dismiss old ones to invite new ones.":"你最多可以同时有3位追随者陪伴，不过你可以自由解散旧者以邀请新者。","Anoints a defeated apostle, and welcomes them as a permanent follower. They will follow you between floors and into any peril, willingly giving their life for the cause and their kin. If they die, Beogh will eventually revive them once you gain sufficient piety - this process can be greatly accelerated by satisfying Beogh with the slaying of all foes who may have contributed to their apostle's death. You can have at most 3 followers accompanying you at a time, though you may freely dismiss old ones to invite new ones.":"为一个被击败的使徒施洗，欢迎他们成为永久的追随者。他们将跟随你 穿梭于各楼层，进入任何险境，甘愿为事业和同胞献出生命。 如果他们牺牲了，贝奥格最终会在你获得足够虔诚值后复活他们—— 这个过程可以通过满足贝奥格，杀死所有可能参与使徒死亡的敌人 来大大加速。 你最多可以同时有3位追随者陪伴，不过你可以自由解散旧者以邀请新者。","Breathes a powerful blast of steam, scalding a target and leaving sight-obscuring steam clouds in its wake.":"喷出一股强大的蒸汽，烫伤目标并在其路径上留下遮蔽视线的蒸汽云。","Invokes a blood pact with the Destroyer, temporarily granting you enormous power at a dangerous price.":"与毁灭者签订血之契约，暂时赋予你巨大的力量，但代价危险。","At the moment the pact is sealed, a massive explosion of damnation will surround you, and you will transform into a demonic avatar, granting you demonic resistances, invulnerable will, doubled healing from kills, and reducing all damage you take by 1/3. You will additionally gain a bonus to all outgoing damage proportional to how injured you were when you used this ability.":"在契约封存的那一刻，一场巨大的诅咒爆炸将包围你，你将变身为恶魔化身， 获得恶魔抗性、不可动摇的意志、击杀时双倍治疗效果，并将所有受到的 伤害减少1/3。你还会根据使用此能力时的受伤程度获得额外的输出伤害加成。","When your transformation expires, you will be dragged down into the Crucible of Flesh, and made to fight through waves of demons until Makhleb considers your debt paid.":"当你的变身结束时，你将被拖入血肉熔炉，被迫与一波波恶魔战斗， 直到马科列布认为你的债务已偿清。","Invokes a blood pact with the Destroyer, temporarily granting you enormous power at a dangerous price. At the moment the pact is sealed, a massive explosion of damnation will surround you, and you will transform into a demonic avatar, granting you demonic resistances, invulnerable will, doubled healing from kills, and reducing all damage you take by 1/3. You will additionally gain a bonus to all outgoing damage proportional to how injured you were when you used this ability. When your transformation expires, you will be dragged down into the Crucible of Flesh, and made to fight through waves of demons until Makhleb considers your debt paid.":"与毁灭者签订血之契约，暂时赋予你巨大的力量，但代价危险。 在契约封存的那一刻，一场巨大的诅咒爆炸将包围你，你将变身为恶魔化身， 获得恶魔抗性、不可动摇的意志、击杀时双倍治疗效果，并将所有受到的 伤害减少1/3。你还会根据使用此能力时的受伤程度获得额外的输出伤害加成。 当你的变身结束时，你将被拖入血肉熔炉，被迫与一波波恶魔战斗， 直到马科列布认为你的债务已偿清。","Turns all of the water near you into a surging tide that attempts to drown every enemy standing in or above it. Those who need air to breathe will also become Flooded, preventing them from casting spells affected by Silence for several turns and dealing minor asphyxiation damage.":"将你附近的所有水域变为汹涌的潮汐，试图淹死站在其中或上方的每个敌人。 需要呼吸空气的敌人也会陷入淹没状态，数回合内无法施放受沉默影响的法术， 并造成少量窒息伤害。","Turns all of the water near you into a surging tide that attempts to drown every enemy standing in or above it. Those who need air to breathe will also become Flooded, preventing them from casting spells affected by Silence for several turns and dealing minor asphyxiation damage. After using this ability, you must gain experience points before you can recover enough power to use it again.":"将你附近的所有水域变为汹涌的潮汐，试图淹死站在其中或上方的每个敌人。 需要呼吸空气的敌人也会陷入淹没状态，数回合内无法施放受沉默影响的法术， 并造成少量窒息伤害。 使用此能力后，你必须获得经验值才能恢复足够的力量再次使用。","Scatters your physical form into a swarm of vampire bats, melding your equipment but allowing you to move quickly and evasively. The number of bats that issue from your body is so immense that it even fills nearby spaces like a choking cloud, assailing enemies and gradually putting them to sleep.":"将你的物理形态散开成一群吸血蝙蝠，融合你的装备，并让你能快速移动、灵活闪避。 从你身体中涌出的蝙蝠数量如此巨大，甚至像窒息的云雾一样填满附近的空间， 攻击敌人并逐渐使其入睡。","After using this ability, you must gain experience points before you can recover enough power to use it again. (Shapeshifting skill will increase the rate at which this skill recharges.)":"使用此能力后，你必须获得经验值才能恢复足够的力量再次使用。 （变形术技能将提高此能力充能的速度。）","Scatters your physical form into a swarm of vampire bats, melding your equipment but allowing you to move quickly and evasively. The number of bats that issue from your body is so immense that it even fills nearby spaces like a choking cloud, assailing enemies and gradually putting them to sleep. After using this ability, you must gain experience points before you can recover enough power to use it again. (Shapeshifting skill will increase the rate at which this skill recharges.)":"将你的物理形态散开成一群吸血蝙蝠，融合你的装备，并让你能快速移动、灵活闪避。 从你身体中涌出的蝙蝠数量如此巨大，甚至像窒息的云雾一样填满附近的空间， 攻击敌人并逐渐使其入睡。 使用此能力后，你必须获得经验值才能恢复足够的力量再次使用。 （变形术技能将提高此能力充能的速度。）","All of your actions are 50% faster.":"你的所有行动加速50%。","You are invisible. Most enemies will be unable to see you and will suffer penalties to hit, though they may be able to guess at your general location. If the status is greyed out, it is active but ineffective for some reason (for example if you are glowing with magical contamination or standing in shallow water).":"你隐身了。 大多数敌人看不到你，其命中率会受到负面影响，尽管他们也能猜到你的大概位置。 随时间推移，这会造成魔法污染，如果你在出现此状况前已经被污染了， 这会有一定危险。如果这个状态是灰色的，表明它是生效的（包括造成了魔法污染）， 但仍会因一些原因而失效（比如你因为魔法污染而身体发光，或是站在浅水中）。","You are about to teleport. While waiting to teleport, attempting to apply the status again (such as by using a scroll of teleportation) will cancel the teleportation.":"你很快就会传送。在等待传送的时候，如果再次进行传送（比如读了一个传送卷轴）， 就会取消本次传送。","You are flying above the ground, and are able to cross water and lava or fight above shallow water without penalties. Most types of flight will time out – be careful what you are above when that happens!":"你俯瞰地面，飞翔在空中，可以飞过水域和熔岩，或在浅水上不受影响地战斗。 大多数飞行能力有时间限制，快到时间的时候，可得当心飞在什么上面！","You are unnaturally agile, and gain a bonus to your evasion.":"你敏捷超群，闪避也有所增强。","You are unnaturally smart, and gain a bonus to the power of your spells as well as halving their magic cost (rounding up).":"你聪明异常，法术的威力增强，同时其消耗的法力减半（四舍五入）。","You are unnaturally mighty, doing significantly more damage in physical combat.":"你异常强壮，物理攻击力大大增强。","You regenerate health at an unnaturally fast rate. This is only shown for temporary regeneration.":"你恢复生命的速度非常快。该状态只在临时性的加速恢复时显示。","Your health has stopped regenerating due to the presence of nearby monsters.":"因为附近的一些怪物，你无法恢复健康。","You regenerate health and magic at an unnaturally fast rate. This is only shown for temporary regeneration.":"你恢复生命和法力的速度非常快。该状态只在临时性的加速恢复时显示。","Your attacks deal no damage, but have a chance of confusing monsters that they hit.":"你的攻击不会造成伤害，但可能使怪物进入混乱状态。","Your willpower is much stronger, protecting against many magical effects.":"你的意志力变得更强，能抵御许多魔法效果。","You are hasted, deal increased damage in combat, and have increased health, but are unable to perform most actions other than moving and attacking in melee. The status will wear off very quickly unless you are attacking monsters, and when it expires you will be slowed and unable to berserk again for a short duration.":"你的速度、近战伤害和生命值都有所提升， 但除了移动和近战攻击，无法进行其他大多数动作。 除非你在攻击怪物，否则此状态很快会消失。 当狂暴结束后，使用者将被减速，短时间内无法再次狂暴。","You are recovering from your berserk rage, and are unable to berserk again for a short duration.":"你刚从狂暴状态恢复正常，短时间内无法再次狂暴。","You are filled with barbearic rage! You are hasted, deal grizzly damage, and have greatly increased health, but find it impawsible to do much other than move and maul foes. You'll bid furwell to this status very quickly unless you are attacking, and when it expires you will be slowed and unable to bearserk again for a short duration.":"你充满了熊熊怒火！ 你的速度变快，能造成灰熊般的重击，生命值得到大幅提升， 但除了移动和重击敌人外无法做其他事情。 除非你在攻击怪物，否则此状态很快会消失。 当熊暴结束后，使用者将被减速，并且短时间内无法再次熊暴。","You are poisoned and will continually lose health. While poisoned, your current health will be partially recoloured to display the eventual poison damage that will be dealt. Poison can be cured immediately by potions of curing.":"你中毒了，会持续失去生命值。 中毒时，你当前的生命值的一部分会重新着色，以显示最终将受到的毒害。 服用治疗药水可立刻解毒。","You are confused. You may stumble in a random direction when attempting to move or attack, and are unable to cast spells or use most items other than potions. Confusion can be cured immediately by potions of curing.":"你陷入混乱。 你在尝试移动或攻击时会撞向随机的方向，并且不能施法或使用大多道具，除了药水。 服用治疗药水可立刻解除混乱状态。","You are glowing with mutagenic radiation. This can inflict mutations over time (usually negative) or even cause you to suffer damage as the unstable magic explodes violently. In addition, your glow prevents invisibility and reduces your stealth. {{ local dmg = you.contam_max_damage(); if dmg > 0 then return \"\\nAn explosion at your current level of contamination could \" .. \"inflict up to \" .. dmg .. \" damage.\" end }}":"你散发着诱变辐射。它可能随时间造成变异（通常是负面变异）， 甚至会在不稳定魔法猛烈爆炸时对你造成伤害。此外，发光会阻止隐形并降低潜行。 {{ local dmg = you.contam_max_damage(); if dmg > 0 then return \"\\n以你当前的污染程度，一次爆炸最多可造成 \" .. dmg .. \" 点伤害。\" end }}","Your maximum health has been temporarily drained by negative energy. This status will not wear off by waiting, but will gradually expire as you gain experience.":"你的最大生命值暂时因负能量而流逝。 原地休息无法消除此状态，但它会随你提升经验而逐渐失效。","Indicates how many uses of your draconian breath weapon are available. If the indicator is dim, there are zero. Otherwise, the number of plusses indicate additional uses available.":"你在屏住呼吸，在状态结束前无法使用吐息能力。","You are exhausted, and are unable to activate divine powers that cause exhaustion until the status expires.":"你精疲力尽，在状态结束前无法使用导致疲惫的神圣能力。","All your actions take 50% longer.":"你的所有行动减慢50%。","You are paralysed, and completely unable to act.":"你被麻痹了，完全无法行动。","You are asleep, and completely unable to act. Taking damage will wake you.":"你睡着了，完全无法行动。受到伤害时会被唤醒。","You are held in a net or a spider web. You cannot move freely and will instead try to struggle free.":"你被困在网或蜘蛛网中。你无法自由移动，并试着挣脱。","You are being constricted by an enemy. Your evasion is impaired, and you will take damage over time. You are unable to move away from the enemy, although you can struggle to escape by attempting to do so, and will become increasingly more likely to succeed and break the constriction when doing so multiple times.":"你被敌人所束缚，会受到更多伤害。 你无法从敌人那里走开（或闪现）， 但你可以试着挣脱它，并且当你持续这么做时，将越来越有可能成功打破束缚。","You are mesmerised and cannot move away from the monster mesmerising you. The effect can be broken by killing or confusing the responsible monster or by breaking line of sight with them.":"你被迷住了，无法远离让你着迷的怪物。 要打破该效果，可以杀死该怪物、使其混乱，或打断其视线。","You are overcome with fear and cannot move towards the monster causing fear in you. The effect can be broken by killing or confusing the responsible monster or by breaking line of sight with them.":"你被恐惧所支配，无法移向让你心生恐惧的怪物。 要打破该效果，可以杀死该怪物、使其混乱，或打断其视线。","You are prevented from teleporting or blinking.":"你无法传送或闪现。","You cannot walk, fly around, slither, etc. You can still take other actions, and can still be moved via translocations or by being pushed, pulled, and so on.":"你无法行走、飞行、滑翔，等等。 但你仍能做其他动作，并能通过瞬移或被推拉的方式进行移动。","Your location is marked due to the effects of a trap or a spell, and monsters will hunt you down more precisely and will be able to detect you even if you are not in their vision.":"因踏入陷阱或被施法，你的位置被标示。 怪物能更准确地追杀你，即使你不在其视线中，他们也能找到你。","You are covered with sticky fire, which causes damage over a moderate duration. Moving will quell the fire much more rapidly, and entering water will extinguish it immediately.":"你身上附着粘性的火，在一段时间内会受到伤害。 进行移动能更快地灭火，如果进入水中能立即扑灭火焰。","<Fire status>":"<Fire status>","You are surrounded by light, greatly reducing your stealth and making you easier to hit.":"你周身发光，潜行被大幅削弱，你更容易被击中。","There are barbs embedded in your skin, and moving around will cause you to take damage. Remaining in place for a short time will allow you to remove the barbs without taking damage.":"有刺扎入你的皮肤，移动时会受到伤害。 在原地休息一阵子，可以排出这些刺而不会受到伤害。","You have been sickened, and your health will no longer regenerate.":"你患病了，无法恢复健康。","You are disoriented and dizzy, reducing your accuracy, evasion, and spellcasting success rate.":"你晕头转向，你的命中率、闪避和施法成功率均被削弱。","You are corroded, reducing your damage in physical combat and your armour by an amount depending on the severity of the corrosion.":"你被腐蚀了，你的物理攻击力和防护被削弱，削弱程度取决于腐蚀的严重程度。","You are covered in illusionary wounds, causing severe damage while the effect remains active. Destroying the source of the illusion will restore all health lost to the flaying.":"你身上有虚幻的伤口，它在生效时会造成严重伤害。 摧毁幻觉来源可以恢复剥皮损失的所有生命值。","Your melee attacks do 25% less damage.":"你近战攻击造成的伤害减少25%。","You are covered in ice, and your movement speed is reduced.":"你被冰封，移动速度降低。","Your magic is sapped. Casting a spell will cause you to lose access to your magic, briefly preventing you from casting any further spells.":"你的魔力衰竭了。施放一个法术后，你会失去魔法通道，暂时无法再施放任何法术。","You are channelling the dead, causing any living creatures killed in your vicinity to be raised as spectral servants.":"你正在引导死者，附近被杀死的生物，都会化为幽灵仆从。","You are divinely vitalised, providing protection from poison, confusion, petrification, and sickness, and increasing and sustaining your strength, intelligence and dexterity.":"你被赐予活力，保护你免受毒、混乱、石化和疾病的侵害， 并增加、维持了你的力量、智力和敏捷。","Your willpower is weaker, making you vulnerable to many magical effects.":"你的意志力变弱，容易受到许多魔法效果的影响。","You are petrified, and completely unable to act. You are very easy to hit, but all damage taken is substantially reduced.":"你被石化了，完全无法行动。你很容易被击中，但受到的伤害大大减少。","You are turning to stone. Your actions are slowed, all damage taken is slightly reduced, and you will soon be completely petrified (gaining the Stone status).":"你正在石化。 你的行动被减慢，会轻微减少所受的伤害，不久会完全石化（变为石状态）。","You are more resistant to fire, cold, electricity, poison and acid.":"你更能抵抗火、寒、电、毒和酸。","Your wielded weapon or your fists are coated in slime, and will turn the next living or corporeal undead monster you hit into a neutral slime.":"你挥舞的武器或拳头上裹着黏液， 下一个击中的活物或有形的亡灵生物会变成一个中立的黏液。","You are covering ground swiftly.":"你在迅捷地移动。","You are covering ground slowly.":"你在缓慢地移动。","You are temporarily invulnerable to harm, but are brought close to death in the process and cannot be affected by healing while the effect is active. After the spell expires, it cannot be immediately recast.":"你暂时不会受到伤害，但在这个过程中会濒临死亡，在此状态生效时也无法进行治疗。 法术失效后，不能立即重施。","You are still close to death's doorway, and cannot recast Death's Door for a short duration.":"你离死亡之门仍然很近，短时间内无法重施死亡之门。","QUAD DAMAGE!":"四倍伤害！","You are silenced. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, invoking divine abilities, or shouting impossible.":"你被沉默了。这使你无法阅读卷轴、施放法术、调用神圣能力或喊叫。","Your stealth is greatly increased.":"你的潜行大幅增强。","You are in the eye of a mighty ice storm. After the vortex fades, it cannot be called forth again for a short time.":"你处在一个强大的冰风暴的中心。旋涡消散后，短时间内无法再次施展它。","You are surrounded by unstable winds, and cannot recast Polar Vortex for a short duration.":"你被不稳定的云所环绕，短时间内无法重施极地旋涡。","You are liquefying the ground around you, slowing the movement of all creatures in the area.":"你正在液化周围地面，这片区域中所有生物的移动会减慢。","Your combat skills are temporarily increased.":"你的战斗技能暂时得到提升。","Your combat speed is greatly increased.":"你的战斗技能暂时得到提升。","You are duelling a foe in Okawaru's Arena, and will be returned whence you came if you are victorious.":"你在奥卡瓦鲁的角斗场与敌人决斗，获胜后，就能从那里回来。","You are destabilising space around yourself, causing nearby monsters to be randomly blinked away from you.":"你在打破周围环境的稳定，附近的怪物会随机地被闪送走。","Your weapon is temporarily enhanced by the souls of the damned, providing slaying bonuses that increase with every enemy killed. At the maximum bonus, foes adjacent to your attacks' targets suffer pain damage.":"你的武器暂时被诅咒的灵魂增强，每杀死一个敌人，你的杀戮加成就会提升。 加成达到最大，与你攻击目标相邻的敌人就会受到痛楚伤害。","You have lived beyond your means. You cannot spend gold again until you earn enough to cancel out your debt.":"你已经入不敷出了。在你取得足以抵消债务的钱前，你无法使用金币进行消费。","You are radiating toxic energy, and will continuously inflict poison on all nearby creatures.":"你散发着有毒的能量，会持续对周围所有生物造成毒害。","You are reciting Zin's laws to nearby monsters, with a range of effects depending on the target. After finishing a recitation, it cannot be repeated for a short time.":"你在向附近的怪物吟诵辛的律令，并会产生一系列因目标而异的影响。 吟诵结束后，短时间内无法再次使用它。","You have recently finished reciting Zin's laws, and cannot recite again for a short duration.":"你刚吟诵完辛的律令，短时间内无法再吟诵了。","You are more vulnerable to fire.":"你更容易被火伤害。","You are more vulnerable to poison.":"你更容易被毒伤害。","You have targeted an enemy with a dimensional bullseye, causing missiles fired or thrown at a different enemy to also be teleported at the target.":"你已经用次元靶心瞄准了一个敌人，这会使你向不同敌人投射的弹药会被传送到目标。","You are calling a forested plane into temporary existence, and awakening nearby trees to damage your foes.":"你在召唤暂时存在的森林位面，并会唤醒周围的树攻击你的敌人。","You are calling forth mighty dragons to attack your foes. Each dragon which answers the call will drain your magical energy. After the call ends, it cannot be issued again for a short time.":"你在召唤强大的龙来攻击你的敌人。每个响应你的召唤的龙将消耗你的能量。 召唤结束后，短时间内无法再次施展它。","You have recently called forth dragons, and cannot recast Dragon's Call for a short duration.":"你刚召唤过龙，短时间内无法再次施展龙的呼唤了。","You are unable to quaff potions.":"你无法饮用药水。","You are more resistant to fire.":"你对火的抗性有所提高。","You are more resistant to cold.":"你对寒的抗性有所提高。","You are more resistant to electricity.":"你对电的抗性有所提高。","You are terrified of nearby monsters, reducing your damage and accuracy in combat as well as the power of your spells.":"你害怕附近的怪物，你战斗中的攻击力、命中率和法术威力均被削弱。","You are unable to read scrolls.":"你无法阅读卷轴。","Your melee attacks cleave, hitting all adjacent targets.":"你近战时能够顺劈，可以击中所有邻近目标。","You are regenerating health and magic, but are also confused. Curing the confusion will also end the regeneration.":"你正在恢复生命和法力，但会陷入混乱。混乱被治愈时，恢复也会中止。","Your next use of an evokable device will have its power enhanced, at the cost of some of your magic.":"你下次使用可激活装置时，其力量会被增强，同时会消耗你的一些法力。","A terrifying howl is echoing in your mind, calling forth powerful creatures to attack you.":"可怕的嚎叫回荡在你的脑海，呼唤着强大的生物攻击你。","Your body is covered in congealed blood, serving as armour for as long as you remain seriously injured.":"你的身体被凝固的血覆盖，只要你仍身受重伤，它就会充当护甲。","You are unable to cast spells.":"你无法施放法术。","You are channelling magical energy.":"你正在引导魔法能量。","You have been transformed into a monstrous, furry were-beast. The ferocious energy pulsing through your limbs keeps you ready to kill.":"你变成了可怕的、毛茸茸的野兽。残暴的能量在你的肢体内脉动，让你时刻想要杀戮。 任何手套、披风、帽子和靴子都会被融合。","You are unstable at a fundamental level. You inflict dangerous levels of magical contamination on foes with each touch. Sufficient contamination causes a highly localised meltdown, dealing enormous damage.":"你在基面上是不稳定的。你每次触碰敌人，都能造成危险程度的魔法污染。 污染程度够高，能使局部高度熔融，造成巨大的破坏。","However, this instability makes you unable to use weapons, shields, or body armour. You also glow, reducing stealth and preventing invisibility, and you do less damage in melee, as your limbs sometimes destabilise mid-swing.":"然而，由于不稳定的形态，你无法使用武器、盾牌或铠甲。 你还发着光，会削弱潜行并导致无法隐身， 你的近战攻击力也会降低，这是因为你的肢体在挥动时有时会摇摆不定。","You are unstable at a fundamental level. You inflict dangerous levels of magical contamination on foes with each touch. Sufficient contamination causes a highly localised meltdown, dealing enormous damage. However, this instability makes you unable to use weapons, shields, or body armour. You also glow, reducing stealth and preventing invisibility, and you do less damage in melee, as your limbs sometimes destabilise mid-swing.":"你在基面上是不稳定的。你每次触碰敌人，都能造成危险程度的魔法污染。 污染程度够高，能使局部高度熔融，造成巨大的破坏。 然而，由于不稳定的形态，你无法使用武器、盾牌或铠甲。 你还发着光，会削弱潜行并导致无法隐身， 你的近战攻击力也会降低，这是因为你的肢体在挥动时有时会摇摆不定。","Multiple vicious blades are growing out of your body.":"多把凶恶的刀刃正从你的身体上长出。","You have been transformed into a giant, cold-blooded, poison-resistant serpent, ready to wind your coils around foes and crush them to death.":"你变成了一条抗毒的、决意将敌人缠绕、挤压至死的冷血巨蛇。 装备的武器和护甲都会被融合。","Your midsection has transformed into a giant mouth, gnashing and ready to devour foes. The mouth may devour slain creatures, healing you to an extent increased by your Shapeshifting skill and the power of the creature eaten. Skill also increases the damage done by the maw.":"你的腹部变成了一个咬牙切齿、准备吞食敌人的大嘴。 这张嘴巴可以吞食被杀死的生物并治疗你，你的变形术技能和被吞食的生物越强， 治疗程度也越强。提升技能也会增加胃部造成的伤害。 变形后，装备的护甲都会被融合。","You have been transformed into a slow but extremely robust stone statue. Your melee damage, both unarmed and with weapons, is substantially increased. Your stone body is immune to poison and miasma, and gains resistance to electricity, negative energy and torment.":"你变成了缓慢但极其坚固的石像。 你的近战攻击，无论是徒手还是使用武器，都大大增强了。 你的石质身躯免疫毒和瘴气，并获得对电、负能量和折磨的抗性。 装备的铠甲、手套和靴子都会被融合。","{{ local desc = \"You have been transformed into a mighty\" if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \" dragon\" if you.race() ~= \"Grey Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \", increasing the power of any innate breath attacks\" end if you.race() == \"Red Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \". You are highly resistant to fire and \" .. \"resistant to poison, but vulnerable to cold\" elseif you.race() == \"White Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \". You are highly resistant to cold and \" .. \"resistant to poison, but vulnerable to fire\" elseif you.race() == \"Green Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \" and retaining your innate colour\" else desc = desc .. \". You retain your innate colour, and are \" .. \"also resistant to poison\" end else desc = desc .. \", fire-breathing dragon. You are highly resistant \" .. \"to fire and resistant to poison, but vulnerable to \" .. \"cold\" end desc = desc .. \".\" return desc }} Your melee attacks deal incredible damage, and you are much more robust but less evasive.":"{{ local desc = \"你变成了强大的\" if you.race():find(\"Draconian\") then desc = desc .. \"龙\" if you.race() ~= \"Grey Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \"，任何固有的吐息攻击的威力增强了\" end if you.race() == \"Red Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \"。你对火和\" .. \"毒有很强的抗性，但易受寒的伤害\" elseif you.race() == \"White Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \"。你对寒和\" .. \"毒有很强的抗性，但易受火的伤害\" elseif you.race() == \"Green Draconian\" then desc = desc .. \"并保留着你先天的颜色\" else desc = desc .. \"。你保留了先天色彩\" .. \"并对毒有着抗性\" end else desc = desc .. \"，吐息火焰的龙。你能很好地抵抗\" .. \"火和毒，但易受\" .. \"寒的伤害\" end desc = desc .. \"。\" return desc }}你的近战攻击会造成难以置信的伤害，身体也变得更结实，但闪避受到削弱。 装备的武器和护甲都会被融合。","You have been transformed into a lightning-filled tempest. Your melee attacks are strengthened and electrified, and strike all adjacent foes. You gain flight, increased evasion, immunity to poison, miasma, petrification, and constriction, and resistance to electricity. You gain the ability to launch yourself at foes as a lightning bolt.":"你变成了闪着电的风暴。 你在近战中攻击力得到加强，并带有电属性，会打击到所有相邻的敌人。 你能够飞行，提升了闪避能力，免疫毒、瘴气、石化和束缚，并有了电抗。 你获得了如同闪电箭那样，向敌人投射自己的能力。 装备的武器和护甲都会被融合。","You have been transformed into an undying offence against life itself.":"你成为了对生命存在的永恒冒犯。","Foes struck by your hands or melee weapons are weakened, slowed, and drained, and you can heal yourself by tormenting living foes nearby. You also resist cold, have enhanced willpower, and are immune to poison, miasma, negative energy, and torment. Unfortunately, you are vulnerable to holy damage and Dispel Undead, and cannot consume potions.":"被你用近战武器或手击中的敌人会被虚弱、减速、衰竭， 你还可以通过折磨附近的活物敌人来治疗自己。 此外，你能抵抗寒冷，意志力会增强，并免疫毒、瘴气、负能量和折磨。 不幸的是，你易受神圣攻击和驱散亡灵的伤害，且无法服用药水。","You have been transformed into an undying offence against life itself. Foes struck by your hands or melee weapons are weakened, slowed, and drained, and you can heal yourself by tormenting living foes nearby. You also resist cold, have enhanced willpower, and are immune to poison, miasma, negative energy, and torment. Unfortunately, you are vulnerable to holy damage and Dispel Undead, and cannot consume potions.":"你成为了对生命存在的永恒冒犯。 被你用近战武器或手击中的敌人会被虚弱、减速、衰竭， 你还可以通过折磨附近的活物敌人来治疗自己。 此外，你能抵抗寒冷，意志力会增强，并免疫毒、瘴气、负能量和折磨。 不幸的是，你易受神圣攻击和驱散亡灵的伤害，且无法服用药水。","You have been transformed into a swift-moving bat, increasing your evasion but substantially weakening your melee attacks.":"你变成了行动迅捷的吸血蝠，闪避能力得到提升，但近战攻击力受到削弱。","Any equipped weapons, armour and rings are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"装备的武器、护甲和戒指都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","You have been transformed into a swift-moving bat, increasing your evasion but substantially weakening your melee attacks. Any equipped weapons, armour and rings are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"你变成了行动迅捷的吸血蝠，闪避能力得到提升，但近战攻击力受到削弱。 装备的武器、护甲和戒指都会被融合，且无法施展法术。{{ if you.race() ~= \"Vampire\" then return \"你的近战攻击效果\" .. \"在这种形态下取决于经验等级而不是\" .. \"徒手格斗技能。\" end }}","You have been transformed into a pig. You move quickly but are less effective in melee.":"你变成了猪。你移动很快，但近战受到削弱。","You have been transformed into a pig. You move quickly but are less effective in melee. Any equipped weapons, armour and rings are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"你变成了猪。你移动很快，但近战受到削弱。 装备的武器、护甲和戒指都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","{{ if you.race() == \"Octopode\" then return \"A vicious spike has grown from one of your tentacles, \" .. \"increasing the damage of your extra tentacle attacks.\" else return \"Monstrous horns or talons have grown from your body, \" .. \"granting a chance of making an extra attack in melee.\" end }}":"{{ if you.race() == \"Octopode\" then return \"你的一根触手上长出了邪恶的刺，\" .. \"增加了触手的攻击力。\" else return \"你的身体上长出异常的角或爪，\" .. \"从而有机会在近战中进行一次额外的攻击。\" end }}","You have been transformed into a tree and are rooted to the ground, unable to move or teleport. You have minimal evasion but increased health and natural armour, and are resistant to poison, and immune to torment and drowning.":"你变成了扎根于地面的树，无法移动或传送。 你更难闪避，但生命值和自身防护得到增强，有着毒抗，并免疫折磨和溺水。","Any equipped cloak, helmet, gloves, boots and body armour are melded.":"装备的披风、头盔、手套、靴子和铠甲都会被融合。","You have been transformed into a tree and are rooted to the ground, unable to move or teleport. You have minimal evasion but increased health and natural armour, and are resistant to poison, and immune to torment and drowning. Any equipped cloak, helmet, gloves, boots and body armour are melded.":"你变成了扎根于地面的树，无法移动或传送。 你更难闪避，但生命值和自身防护得到增强，有着毒抗，并免疫折磨和溺水。 装备的披风、头盔、手套、靴子和铠甲都会被融合。","You have been transformed into an insubstantial wisp of gas. You are highly evasive and are resistant to fire, cold, electricity and acid, and immune to poison, and negative energy.":"你变成无形的气体。你有着高闪避，并能抵抗火、寒、电和酸，并免疫毒和负能量。","Any equipped weapons, armour and jewellery are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"装备的武器、护甲和首饰都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","You have been transformed into an insubstantial wisp of gas. You are highly evasive and are resistant to fire, cold, electricity and acid, and immune to poison, and negative energy. Any equipped weapons, armour and jewellery are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"你变成无形的气体。你有着高闪避，并能抵抗火、寒、电和酸，并免疫毒和负能量。 装备的武器、护甲和首饰都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","You have been transformed into a sentient fungus. You are highly evasive and can release spores to cause confusion when attacking in melee, but are unable to move when hostile creatures are present. You are resistant to poison and immune to negative energy.":"你变成了有意识的真菌。 你有着高闪避，在近战攻击时可以释放孢子造成混乱，但当敌方生物出现时无法移动。 你有着毒抗，并免疫负能量。","Any equipped weapons and armour are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"装备的武器和护甲都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","You have been transformed into a sentient fungus. You are highly evasive and can release spores to cause confusion when attacking in melee, but are unable to move when hostile creatures are present. You are resistant to poison and immune to negative energy. Any equipped weapons and armour are melded, and you are unable to cast spells. The effectiveness of your melee attacks while in this form is based on experience level instead of on Unarmed Combat skill.":"你变成了有意识的真菌。 你有着高闪避，在近战攻击时可以释放孢子造成混乱，但当敌方生物出现时无法移动。 你有着毒抗，并免疫负能量。 装备的武器和护甲都会被融合，且无法施展法术。 在这种形态下你的近战效果取决于经验等级而不是徒手格斗技能。","You have been transformed into a swirling mass of dark shadows. You are permanently invisible and are immune to poison, draining, and torment. All incoming damage is halved, you bleed smoke on any incoming attack, and you have infinite willpower. However, your ability to deal damage in melee and with ranged attacks is halved, your spellcasting power is greatly hampered, and your maximum health is further drained when taking damage.":"你变成了旋涡状的暗影团。你将持续隐形，且免疫毒、衰竭和折磨的影响。 所有受到的伤害会减半，受到任何攻击都会使你流出烟，并且你将拥有无限的意志力。 但是，你的近战和远程的攻击力将减半，施法会受到极大的阻碍， 在受到伤害时，你的最大生命值会流失。","You are near (or perhaps holding) the Orb of Zot, whose energies disrupt translocation magic. Teleportation will take longer and scrolls of blinking may transport you a short distance away from your intended destination.":"你在靠近（或持有）佐特宝珠时，其能量会扰乱位移魔法。 传送需要花费更长时间，闪烁卷轴也可能把你传送到与预定目的地有一小段距离的位置。","Your legs are tired, and you are unable to hop. This status will only recover after you spend several turns not moving. (Other actions, such as attacking or casting spells, are fine.)":"你的腿酸了，无法进行跳跃。 你需要花几个回合停下来休整，才能从这个状态恢复过来。 （其他动作，比如攻击或施法，是可行的。）","You are currently channelling a ray of searing magical energy. Pressing <w>.</w> or <w>s</w> to wait in place will maintain and intensify the ray, at the cost of 1 MP per turn. Any other action, including recasting the spell, will end it.":"你正在引导灼热射线的魔法能量。 按<w>.</w>或<w>s</w>在原地等待，将保持并增强射线，每回合会消耗 1 点法力。 任何其他动作，包括重施这个法术，会打断它。","<Ray status>":"<Ray status>","You are moving at supernatural speed, causing movement actions to become instant. Any martial attacks made while moving in this way deal increased damage and never miss.":"你以超自然的速度移动，瞬间完成移动动作。 以这种方式移动时，任何武术攻击都会增强且总能命中。","You are surrounded by a storm of heavenly clouds. While the storm rages, your evasion and combat accuracy and damage are substantially increased, and striking enemies with martial attacks increases this bonus. The storm weakens over time and fades away once the bonus reaches zero. The heavenly clouds prevent invisibility, and obscure the vision of those outside the storm.":"你被天云风暴所围绕。 当风暴肆虐时，你的闪避、命中率和伤害都会大幅增强， 而且通过武术攻击敌人时还会有加成。 风暴会随着时间的推移而减弱，所给的加成达到零就会消失。 天云阻止了隐形，也模糊了风暴外的怪物的视线。","Your movement is slowed on this liquid ground.":"在液体地面上，你的移动速度变慢了。","You are full of blood, and regenerate health quickly.":"你充满了血液，很快能恢复健康。","You receive spellcasting and slaying bonuses that scale with your health.":"你获得与生命值成比例的施法和杀戮加成。","You can swear fealty to Beogh, the god of all orcs, through a nearby priest. To do so, use the Convert to Beogh ability in the ability menu.":"你可以通过附近的祭司，向洞穴兽人之神比欧弗宣誓效忠。 要这样做，请在<white>能力</white>菜单上按<white>Y</white>。","Your body is entirely devoid of blood, reducing your maximum health and preventing you from regenerating health when monsters are visible. You are immune to poison and negative energy, significantly resist cold, and resist torment.":"你的体内完全没有血液，最大生命值降低了，当你碰到怪物时还无法恢复健康。 你免疫毒和负能量，并有着很强的寒抗，还能抵抗折磨。","You are bribing the inhabitants of the current branch.":"你在贿赂当前分支的栖息者。","You are in a cloud.":"你位于云中。","The air is too still for clouds to form.":"这里的空气太过平静，无法形成云雾。","You are digging.":"你正在挖掘。","Your health and/or magic are being rapidly restored, as well as the health of your allies.":"你的健康和/或魔法，还有你盟友的健康正在快速恢复。","You are under both slowing and hasting effects.":"你同时受到减速和加速的效果。","You are currently flying over lava.":"你正在飞越岩浆。","You are recalling your allies.":"你在召回你的盟友。","{{ local verb = you.flying() and \"flying over\" or you.race() == \"Merfolk\" and \"swimming in\" or \"standing in\" local feat = view.feature_at(0, 0):gsub(\"_\", \" \")":"{{ local verb = you.flying() and \"飞越\" or you.race() == \"Merfolk\" and \"游在\" or \"站在\" local feat = view.feature_at(0, 0):gsub(\"_\", \" \")","if feat ~= \"deep water\" and feat ~= \"shallow water\" then feat = \"water\" verb = \"over\" end":"if feat ~= \"深水\" and feat ~= \"浅水\" then feat = \"水面\" verb = \"越过\" end","return \"You are currently \" .. verb .. \" \" .. feat .. \".\" }}":"return \"你正\" .. verb .. \"\" .. feat .. \"。\" }}","{{ local verb = you.flying() and \"flying over\" or you.race() == \"Merfolk\" and \"swimming in\" or \"standing in\" local feat = view.feature_at(0, 0):gsub(\"_\", \" \") if feat ~= \"deep water\" and feat ~= \"shallow water\" then feat = \"water\" verb = \"over\" end return \"You are currently \" .. verb .. \" \" .. feat .. \".\" }}":"{{ local verb = you.flying() and \"飞越\" or you.race() == \"Merfolk\" and \"游在\" or \"站在\" local feat = view.feature_at(0, 0):gsub(\"_\", \" \") if feat ~= \"深水\" and feat ~= \"浅水\" then feat = \"水面\" verb = \"越过\" end return \"你正\" .. verb .. \"\" .. feat .. \"。\" }}","Enemies are magically translocated toward you. (This won't wake them up.)":"敌人会魔法般地向你移来。（这不会让他们苏醒。）","You have spent too much time in one branch, allowing the malevolent power of Zot to notice you. If you spend the indicated number of turns in the branch without descending to a new floor, Zot will find you, causing permanent health damage.":"你在一个分支上逗留了太多时间，佐特的邪恶力量注意到了你。 如果你在这个分支上耗尽了指定的回合数，但没有下到新的楼层， 佐特将会发现你，并对你的健康造成永久性伤害。","If you spend the indicated number of turns in this branch without descending to a new floor, Zot will find you, causing permanent health damage.":"如果你在这个分支上耗尽了指定的回合数，但没有下到新的楼层， 佐特将会发现你，并对你的健康造成永久性伤害。","If you spend the indicated number of turns in this branch, its gem will be found and shattered by the power of Zot.":"如果你在这个分支上耗尽了指定的回合数，其中的宝石就会被佐特的力量发现并被粉碎。","The wrath of Ignis prevents you from resisting fire.":"伊格尼斯的愤怒让你无法抵御火。","You are unstable and cannot cast Blink or activate evoked blink abilities for a short period of time. Powerful sources of translocation magic such as scrolls of blinking ignore this limitation, as do external sources of blinking outside of your control.":"你不稳定，短时间内无法施放闪现魔法或激活闪现能力。 强大的易位来源，如闪现卷轴，则不受此限制， 就像那些不受你控制的、能诱发闪现的外因一样。","You are recovering from becoming lightning, and are unable to blinkbolt again for a short duration.":"你刚从闪电形态中恢复正常，短时间无法再次使用闪现箭。","You are currently channelling electrical charge. Pressing <w>.</w> or <w>s</w> to wait in place will maintain and continue this process until it discharges. Any other action, including recasting the spell, will dissipate the charge harmlessly.":"你正在引导电荷。按<w>.</w>或<w>s</w>在原地等待， 将保持并继续此进程，直到放电。 任何其他动作，包括重施这个法术，电荷会无害地消散。","<Charge- status>":"<Charge- status>","You are currently channelling waves of flames. Pressing <w>.</w> or <w>s</w> to wait in place will maintain and intensify the waves, at the cost of 1 MP per turn. Any other action, including recasting the spell, will end it.":"你正在引导火焰波。按<w>.</w>或<w>s</w>在原地等待， 将保持并增强火焰波，每回合会消耗 1 点法力。 任何其他动作，包括重施这个法术，会打断它。","<Wave status>":"<Wave status>","You are encasing nearby walls in ice. The ice will crack and fall away if you move to a new position.":"你正在冰封周围的墙。如果你移动到新位置，冰会破裂、脱落。","You are creating a toxic bog in the nearby area, and are immune to its effects. You cannot sustain this transformation in areas out of your line of sight.":"你在附近生成了一个有毒的沼泽，并免疫其影响。 一旦它在你的视线之外，你将无力维持这个变化。","You are in touch with a greater truth, increasing your resistance to effects which target your willpower. Tragically, this epiphany won't last.":"你接触到了更为宏大的真理，提升了对那些与意志力挂钩的效果的抵抗力。 不幸的是，这样的顿悟不会一直持续下去。","<Enlightened status>":"<Enlightened status>","The dead are hopping! Living creatures you kill may rise as zombified servants.":"死物在跳跃！你杀死的生物可能会复活，变为丧尸仆从。","You are peering down the stairs. You can freely return to the previous level, but once you take any action on this floor, all stairs leading back up will collapse.":"你顺着楼梯往下看。 你可以自由返回前一层，但一旦在此楼层上采取任何行动，所有返回的楼梯都将坍塌。","Your body is as fragile and brittle as glass, increasing the damage you take from all sources.":"你的身体像玻璃那样易碎而脆弱，任何来源的攻击都会对你造成更多伤害。","Acidic ooze creeps out of the walls around you. Each turn, foes are damaged depending on the number of slimy walls they remain adjacent to.":"酸性软泥从你周围的墙上渗出。 每回合敌人受到的伤害取决于与其相邻的黏性墙壁的数量。","You have summoned your canine familiar.":"你已经召唤了你的魔犬。","Your canine familiar is recovering from its injuries, and cannot be summoned again for a short time.":"你的魔犬正在从伤势中恢复，短时间内不能再次召唤它。","You have recently siphoned the essence of the living, and cannot do so again for a short time.":"你刚吸取过生者的精华，短时间内无法再次吸取它。","You are fatigued from recently speaking a word of chaos, and are unable to do so again for a short time.":"你刚刚念出过混乱之语，短时间内无法再次念诵它。","Jinxing spirits encircle you. When you attack foes, those who fail a Will check are jinxed, taking damage and becoming drained. The spirits depart quickly when no foes are in sight.":"厄灵环绕着你。当你攻击敌人时，那些意志力不够强的会被诅咒，受到伤害并变被衰竭。 当视线中没有敌人时，这些灵体会迅速消散。","You are hovering upward toward the ceiling. After a short delay, Ignis' power will blast you into the level above.":"你正朝着天花板向上飘浮。在短暂延迟之后，伊格尼斯的力量会把你轰入上层。","You are about to teleport towards hostile monsters, if possible. Before this happens, attempting to teleport again (such as by using a scroll of teleportation) will cancel this teleportation.":"如果可能的话，你即将向敌对怪物传送。在此发生之前，再次尝试传送 （如使用传送卷轴）将取消本次传送。","You have recently performed an infernal blood rite and must fully heal before being able to perform another.":"你最近进行了一场地狱血之仪式，必须完全治愈后才能再次进行。","You are catching your breath, and are unable to use your innate breath ability until the status expires.":"你正在喘气，在状态消失之前无法使用你的天生吐息能力。","You have not yet harvested enough death to cast Grave Claw again.":"你尚未收集足够的死亡来再次施放墓爪。","Gravity around you is still unstable, and you cannot cast Gell's Gavotte again until it settles back down.":"你周围的重力仍然不稳定，在它重新稳定之前无法再次施放盖尔之加沃特。","You are unable to cast Hellfire Mortar again until the effect of your last cast ends.":"在你上次施放的效果结束之前，无法再次施放地狱火迫击炮。","Your lithotoxin has recently activated and will not do so again until you fully heal.":"你的石毒素最近激活过，在完全治愈前不会再次激活。","Your orb of mesmerism has recently expended its energy. It will recharge after a short length of time (but cannot recharge on turns where you move).":"你的迷魂宝珠最近耗尽了能量。它将在短时间后重新充能 （但在你移动的回合中无法充能）。","Your orb of stardust has recently expended its energy. It will recharge once several turns pass while your MP is full and there are no enemies in sight.":"你的星尘之球最近耗尽了能量。它将在你的法力已满且视野中没有敌人 数回合后重新充能。","The insects that dwell within you have recently swarmed to your defence. This will not happen again until your health fully recovers.":"栖息在你体内的昆虫最近蜂拥而出为你防御。在你的生命值完全恢复之前， 这不会再次发生。","Your body is composed of elemental water that can reach to attack and drown enemies.":"你的身体由元素之水构成，可以延伸攻击和淹死敌人。","You are preparing to unleash a kinetic shockwave and cannot move until this is complete.":"你正在准备释放一道动能冲击波，在此完成之前不能移动。","<Blast status>":"<Blast status>","Your vision is badly impaired. All spells and attacks you perform (which do not automatically hit) have an increased chance to miss. This chance is much greater the further away you are from your target.":"你的视力严重受损。你进行的所有法术和攻击（自动命中的除外） 有更高的概率失误。你离目标越远，这个概率越高。","<Breath status>":"<Breath status>","You are noisily attacking with all of your armour. Every piece of armour you haunt currently moves of its own volition; any damage it takes will not affect you, you can freely fire through it, and its attacks may daze, drain, or confuse your enemies.":"你正在用所有的护甲嘈杂地攻击。你附身的每件护甲目前都自主移动； 它们受到的任何伤害不会影响你，你可以自由地穿过它们射击， 它们的攻击可能晕眩、削弱或困惑你的敌人。","You have an explosive catalyst readied. The catalyst will detonate, dealing fire damage to the primary target of each of your melee attacks and any enemy adjacent to them, with each hit. Attacking will extend the duration of the catalyst even if you miss.":"你已准备好一个爆炸催化剂。催化剂将在每次攻击时引爆，对你每次近战攻击的 主要目标及其相邻的任何敌人造成火焰伤害。即使你未命中，攻击也会延长 催化剂的持续时间。","You have been challenged by a chosen apostle of Beogh, who will know your location no matter where on the floor you are. Defeat them, and you may recruit them to join you. If you flee the floor, Beogh will punish you by temporarily depriving you of allies.":"你被贝奥格选中的一位使徒挑战了，无论你在楼层的何处他们都知道你的位置。 击败他们，你可以招募他们加入你。如果你逃离楼层， 贝奥格将通过暂时剥夺你的盟友来惩罚你。","You are a heavily-armoured crab with rusting breath.":"你是一只重甲螃蟹，拥有锈蚀吐息。","At least one of your strength, intelligence, or dexterity has fallen to 0 or below. You will act slowly until this situation is remedied.":"你的力量、智力或敏捷至少有一项降到了0或以下。 在此情况得到纠正之前，你的行动会变得缓慢。","Your Unleash Destruction is growing more powerful as you use it consecutively.":"你的释放毁灭能力在连续使用时正变得更加强大。","<Destr status>":"<Destr status>","Your evasion and slaying are increased. This stacks up to 3 times and will never expire so long as you continue to perform melee attacks.":"你的闪避和杀戮值提高了。此效果最多叠加3次， 只要你继续进行近战攻击就永不过期。","The power of all your spells is reduced by half.":"你所有法术的威力减半。","A malevolent fate is gathering around you. If your Doom reaches 100%, you will be afflicted by a random bane and your Doom will reset to 0. Banes have diverse negative effects that can significantly endanger your character for an extended period of time.":"一场恶毒的命运正在你周围聚集。如果你的厄运达到100%， 你将受到一个随机的灾祸，厄运将重置为0。灾祸有多种负面效果， 可能会在长时间内严重危及你的角色。","Both Doom and Banes are only cured by gaining experience, though Banes typically last much longer.":"厄运和灾祸都只能通过获得经验值来消除，但灾祸通常持续更久。","A malevolent fate is gathering around you. If your Doom reaches 100%, you will be afflicted by a random bane and your Doom will reset to 0. Banes have diverse negative effects that can significantly endanger your character for an extended period of time. Both Doom and Banes are only cured by gaining experience, though Banes typically last much longer.":"一场恶毒的命运正在你周围聚集。如果你的厄运达到100%， 你将受到一个随机的灾祸，厄运将重置为0。灾祸有多种负面效果， 可能会在长时间内严重危及你的角色。 厄运和灾祸都只能通过获得经验值来消除，但灾祸通常持续更久。","You are rapidly growing sleepy and may soon fall asleep completely.":"你正在迅速变困，可能很快就会完全睡着。","Your arms are a pair of electric eels.":"你的手臂是一对电鳗。","Your maw has just consumed a delicious meal, greatly increasing your regeneration until it finishes digesting it.":"你的吞噬之口刚刚享用了一顿美餐，在消化完成前大幅提高你的恢复速度。","You are burning accumulated memories for power. Each damage-dealing spell you cast will consume a memory. In exchange, their power and spell success are increased, encumbrance penalties are ignored, and your spellclaw attacks do bonus damage proportional to the spell level and heal you based on the damage dealt.":"你正在燃烧积累的记忆以换取力量。你施放的每个伤害法术将消耗一份记忆。 作为交换，它们的威力和法术成功率提高，负重惩罚被忽略， 你的法术爪攻击根据法术等级造成额外伤害，并根据造成的伤害治疗你。","A path out of the Crucible has opened. Find it and claim your freedom again. For a time.":"一条离开熔炉的道路已经打开。找到它，重新获得你的自由。暂时的。","You are sharing your body with an Executioner, giving you a powerful auxiliary attack that also triggers when you dodge attacks, as well as letting you rampage towards foes. This will expire quickly if you stop attacking.":"你正在与一个处刑人共享身体，赋予你强大的辅助攻击，在你闪避攻击时 也会触发，并让你可以向敌人狂暴冲锋。如果你停止攻击，这会迅速消失。","Your lungs are filled with liquid, preventing you from breathing properly. This makes reading scrolls, casting spells, and invoking divine abilities impossible. You will also take asphyxiation damage every turn.":"你的肺里充满了液体，无法正常呼吸。这使得阅读卷轴、施法和祈求 神赐能力变得不可能。你每回合还会受到窒息伤害。","You are hurling conjured alchemical reagents at nearby monsters.":"你正在向附近的怪物投掷魔法炼金试剂。","The power of Zot no longer hunts you, but this branch's gem still remains intact.":"佐特的力量不再追猎你，但这个分支的宝石仍然完好无损。","You are a living beehive, abuzz with busy insects.":"你是一个活着的蜂巢，充满了忙碌的昆虫嗡鸣。","You have been temporarily transformed into a jelly. You have several unusual resistances and extra health, but heavily weakened spells.":"你被暂时变成了一只果冻。你拥有数种不寻常的抗性和额外的生命值， 但法术威力大幅削弱。","Any equipped weapons and armour are melded. The effectiveness of your newly-acidic melee attacks while in this form is based on your experience level rather than Unarmed Combat skill.":"任何装备的武器和护甲都被融合了。在此形态下你新获得的酸性近战攻击的 效果取决于你的经验等级而非徒手格斗技能。","You have been temporarily transformed into a jelly. You have several unusual resistances and extra health, but heavily weakened spells. Any equipped weapons and armour are melded. The effectiveness of your newly-acidic melee attacks while in this form is based on your experience level rather than Unarmed Combat skill.":"你被暂时变成了一只果冻。你拥有数种不寻常的抗性和额外的生命值， 但法术威力大幅削弱。 任何装备的武器和护甲都被融合了。在此形态下你新获得的酸性近战攻击的 效果取决于你的经验等级而非徒手格斗技能。","You are beckoning the legions of chaos; short-lived demons will be periodically summoned near you.":"你正在召唤混沌军团；短命的恶魔将定期在你附近被召唤出来。","You have a mane of venomous tendrils for hair.":"你有一头毒液触须构成的鬃发。","This indicates how many spells you could cast from accumulated memories if you Enkindled now.":"这表示如果你现在燃魂，可以从积累的记忆中施放多少个法术。","You are channelling the deepest night, greatly reducing your sight range. It will gradually return to normal over time.":"你正在引导最深的黑夜，大幅缩短你的视野范围。它将随时间逐渐恢复正常。","You are covered in regenerative ooze from your recent trip down the stairs. For a brief time, your wounds will heal rapidly and your reserves of magic will recover quickly.":"你因最近的楼梯之旅而被再生的软泥覆盖。在短时间内，你的伤口将快速愈合， 法力储备也将快速恢复。","You are holding the Charlatan's Orb, whose energies disrupt translocation magic. Teleportation will take longer and scrolls of blinking may transport you a short distance away from your intended destination.":"你持有江湖术士之球，其能量干扰了传送魔法。传送将花费更长时间， 闪烁卷轴可能将你传送到离预定目的地一段距离的地方。","Your connection to the divine has been partially cut-off, temporarily reducing your effective piety. Gaining experience will eventually recover all piety that has been locked away this way.":"你与神的连接被部分切断，暂时降低你的有效虔诚值。 获得经验值最终将恢复所有被以此方式锁定的虔诚值。","Makhleb has come to collect on certain promises made to them. {{ if you.god() == \"Makhleb\" then return \"Fulfill your oath as their instrument by slaying the terrified \" .. \"mortals that have been gathered here, and they may grant you \" .. \"freedom once again.\" else return \"Fight and bleed and you may be granted freedom once again.\" end}}":"马科列布来清算你许下的某些承诺了。 {{ if you.god() == \"Makhleb\" then return \"作为他们的工具履行誓言，杀死聚集在这里的恐惧凡人，\" .. \"他们可能再次赐予你自由。\" else return \"战斗、流血，然后你可能会再次获得自由。\" end }}","Your claustrophobia has given you a slaying malus. This is dependent on the number of walls surrounding you.":"你的幽闭恐惧症给你带来了杀戮减值。这取决于你周围的墙壁数量。","You have invoked divine aid in avenging the death of a fallen apostle. Orcs will continuously rally to your side, though your prayer will end more rapidly when there are no more foes around to fight.":"你祈求了神助来为一位阵亡的使徒复仇。兽人将持续集结到你身边， 但当周围不再有敌人可战斗时，你的祈祷将更快结束。","Your platinum paragon is close enough to you to sometimes parry attacks directed at you.":"你的白金典范离你足够近，有时可以格挡指向你的攻击。","You have spiny quills growing out of your body which may damage melee attackers.":"你身上长出了带刺的刚毛，可能会伤害近战攻击者。","An orcish apostle is available to recruit as a permanent companion. (Use the Recruit Apostle ability)":"一位兽人使徒可以被招募为永久同伴。 （使用招募使徒能力）","Trog's Hand is simultaneously making you regenerate health at an unnaturally fast rate and strengthening your willpower to protect you against many magical effects.":"特洛格之手同时让你以异常快的速度恢复生命值，并增强你的意志力， 以保护你免受许多魔法效果的影响。","You're starting to limber up. Your weapon-based and unarmed attacks are closer to full strength, and will continue to grow more powerful with each swing.":"你开始热身了。你的武器和徒手攻击接近全力，并将随着每次挥舞 继续变得更加强大。","You're limbered up. Your weapon-based and unarmed attacks are at full strength, and will remain so as long as you keep swinging and for a short while afterward.":"你已经热身完毕。你的武器和徒手攻击处于全力状态，只要你继续挥舞 并在之后的一小段时间内将保持如此。","You're limbering up. Your weapon-based and unarmed attacks are close to full strength, and will continue to grow more powerful with each swing.":"你正在热身。你的武器和徒手攻击接近全力，并将随着每次挥舞 继续变得更加强大。","You are marked with the sign of ruin, causing any melee attacks which damage you to heavily drain and randomly slow, weaken, or blind you.":"你被刻上了毁灭之印，导致任何对你造成伤害的近战攻击都会严重削弱你， 并随机减速、虚弱或致盲你。","You are a sun scarab, with solar fire blazing beside you.":"你是一只太阳圣甲虫，太阳之火在你身旁燃烧。","You are a walking scroll, parchment crisp and full of magic.":"你是一本行走的卷轴，羊皮纸清脆而充满魔力。","Yredelemnul's grip is engulfing an area in life-stealing chains.":"伊雷德勒姆纳的掌控正在用生命窃取之链吞没一片区域。","You are protected by a divine shield. Enemies that strike it in melee will have their attacks completely blocked, and they may also be blinded by its light.":"你被一个神圣护盾保护着。用近战攻击击中它的敌人将使其攻击被完全格挡， 并且他们也可能被其光芒致盲。","You are covered by a thin shroud of slime that may deflect a melee attack. When it does, the shroud will break for a short time, though it will soon repair itself naturally.":"你被一层薄薄的软泥覆盖，可能会偏转一次近战攻击。当它这样做时， 这层覆盖会在短时间内破裂，但很快会自然修复。","You are an instrument of Makhleb's destructive will. Your power and defences are greatly enhanced, but you must endure the Crucible of Flesh once this effect ends.":"你是马科列布毁灭意志的工具。你的力量和防御大大增强， 但在此效果结束后你必须忍受血肉熔炉的考验。","The damage and accuracy of your attacks is temporarily increased.":"你攻击的伤害和命中率暂时提高了。","Your body is slowly being turned into slime. Even if a full transformation occurs, you have enough force of will to eventually revert back.":"你的身体正慢慢被变成软泥。即使发生了完全转化， 你也有足够的意志力最终恢复。","You are a cunning, riddle-loving sphinx, with the force of a windstorm in your paws.":"你是一只狡猾、热爱谜语的斯芬克斯，爪中蕴含着暴风的力量。","You are an agile jumping spider whose attacks can web enemies.":"你是一只敏捷的跳蛛，其攻击可以将敌人困入网中。","Your arm is a mass of multicoloured fungus.":"你的手臂是一团彩色真菌。","Your next attack will have increased accuracy, inflict three times its normal damage, and cleave at an increased range. This bonus is lost if you perform any action besides attacking.":"你的下一次攻击将有更高的命中率，造成三倍伤害，并以扩大的范围劈砍。 如果你进行攻击以外的任何操作，此加成将丢失。","You have transformed into a swarm of vampire bats, allowing you to move quickly and evasively. You may trail clouds of bats in your wake.":"你已变身成一群吸血蝙蝠，让你可以快速而隐秘地移动。 你可能在身后留下蝙蝠云。","A Boundless Tesseract is drawing in forces from a parallel reality. New monsters will steadily appear at random locations across the floor until either of the tesseracts is destroyed. If this is allowed to continue for a very long time, those monsters may sometimes appear near your location instead.":"一个无限超立方体正在从平行现实中拉入力量。新怪物将稳定地在地图上 随机位置出现，直到任一超立方体被摧毁。如果允许此情况持续非常长时间， 那些怪物有时可能改为在你附近出现。","You carry the Black Torch. If this indicator is dark, the torch is unlit; if it is bright, you have called upon Yredelemnul to light the torch. So long as the torch burns, you will gain piety for kills. With sufficient piety, you will be able to use its umbral fire to empower your undead servants and damage your enemies.":"你携带着黑火炬。如果此指示器是暗的，火炬未点燃；如果它是明亮的， 你已呼唤伊雷德勒姆纳点燃了火炬。只要火炬燃烧，击杀将获得虔诚值。 有足够的虔诚值时，你将能够使用其暗影之火来增强你的亡灵仆从并伤害敌人。","You have become untethered in space, blinking randomly each turn and suffering a small amount of damage each time you do so.":"你已在空间中失去锚定，每回合随机闪烁并在这样做时受到少量伤害。","You have recently announced your regal presence and it simply would not do to leave the floor again so soon afterward.":"你最近宣布了你的王者存在，在此之后这么快就再次离开楼层实在不妥。","You are a vampire - a creature that straddles the border between life and undeath. You can drink the lifeblood of the living to heal, and even turn those you slay stealthily into vampiric thralls, but do not heal in the presence of monsters.":"你是一个吸血鬼——一种跨越生命与亡灵界限的生物。你可以吸取活物的 生命之血来治愈自己，甚至可以将那些潜行击杀的生物变成吸血仆从， 但在有怪物时不会自然恢复。","One of your apostles has been killed, and you have not yet killed all foes who were involved in their death. If you do so, Beogh will resurrect them sooner.":"你的一位使徒被杀害了，你尚未杀死所有参与其死亡的敌人。 如果你这样做，贝奥格将更快地复活他们。","Your mind is clouded by frustration. For the next several turns, you will uncontrollably attack random adjacent creatures (whether friendly or enemy) or even empty space.":"你的头脑被沮丧所笼罩。在接下来的数回合中，你将无法控制地攻击 随机的相邻生物（无论是友好的还是敌对的），甚至是空白位置。","You are a vicious werewolf.":"你是一只凶猛的狼人。","You are winding up your clockwork bee. It cannot attack its target until it is fully wound up.":"你正在上紧你的发条蜜蜂。在完全上紧发条之前它无法攻击目标。","<Winding status>":"<Winding status>","You are a rime yak, fur encrusted with ice.":"你是一头霜角牦牛，毛皮上结满了冰。","Fighting skill increases your accuracy and damage in physical combat, and also increases your maximum health.":"格斗技能会提高你在物理战斗中的命中率和伤害，并提高你的生命上限。","Short Blades are more effective than any other weapon type at stabbing helpless foes.":"短刃类武器比其他种类的武器更适合刺杀无力反抗的敌人。","Being skilled with Short Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升短刃技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Short Blades increases your effectiveness with Long Blades, and vice versa.":"提升短刃技能能同时提升你的长刃技能，反之亦然。","Short Blades are more effective than any other weapon type at stabbing helpless foes. Being skilled with Short Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Short Blades increases your effectiveness with Long Blades, and vice versa.":"短刃类武器比其他种类的武器更适合刺杀无力反抗的敌人。 提升短刃技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升短刃技能能同时提升你的长刃技能，反之亦然。","Being skilled with Long Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升长刃技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Long Blades increases your effectiveness with Short Blades, and vice versa.":"提升长刃技能能同时提升你的短刃技能，反之亦然。","Being skilled with Long Blades will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Long Blades increases your effectiveness with Short Blades, and vice versa.":"提升长刃技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升长刃技能能同时提升你的短刃技能，反之亦然。","Axes cleave through multiple enemies with a single swing, hitting foes in an arc around the wielder.":"挥动斧类武器能同时劈砍周围一圈多个敌人。","Being skilled with Axes will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升斧类技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Axes increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and Polearms, and vice versa.":"提升斧类技能能同时提升你的锤与链枷技能和长柄武器技能，反之亦然。","Axes cleave through multiple enemies with a single swing, hitting foes in an arc around the wielder. Being skilled with Axes will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Axes increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and Polearms, and vice versa.":"挥动斧类武器能同时劈砍周围一圈多个敌人。 提升斧类技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升斧类技能能同时提升你的锤与链枷技能和长柄武器技能，反之亦然。","Being skilled with Maces & Flails will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升锤与链枷技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Maces & Flails increases your effectiveness with Axes and Staves, and vice versa.":"提升锤与链枷技能能同时提升你的斧类技能和杖类技能，反之亦然。","Being skilled with Maces & Flails will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Maces & Flails increases your effectiveness with Axes and Staves, and vice versa.":"提升锤与链枷技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升锤与链枷技能能同时提升你的斧类技能和杖类技能，反之亦然。","Polearms can be evoked with ‘v’ to attack enemies from two spaces away.":"装备长柄武器时可以使用“v”键攻击两格远的敌人。","Being skilled with Polearms will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升长柄武器技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Polearms increases your effectiveness with Axes and Staves, and vice versa.":"提升长柄武器技能能同时提升你的斧类技能和杖类技能，反之亦然。","Polearms can be evoked with ‘v’ to attack enemies from two spaces away. Being skilled with Polearms will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Polearms increases your effectiveness with Axes and Staves, and vice versa.":"装备长柄武器时可以使用“v”键攻击两格远的敌人。 提升长柄武器技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升长柄武器技能能同时提升你的斧类技能和杖类技能，反之亦然。","Staves require a relatively low amount of skill to be used most effectively, although they lack the high damage potential of some other weapon classes.":"不需要很高的技能等级就能精通杖类武器， 但是杖类武器的攻击力潜力没有其他种类的武器那么高。","Being skilled with Staves will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升杖类技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Being skilled with Staves increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and Polearms, and vice versa.":"提升杖类技能能同时提升你的锤与链枷技能和长柄武器技能，反之亦然。","Staves require a relatively low amount of skill to be used most effectively, although they lack the high damage potential of some other weapon classes. Being skilled with Staves will allow you to attack more quickly with all weapons of this type, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them. Being skilled with Staves increases your effectiveness with Maces & Flails and Polearms, and vice versa.":"不需要很高的技能等级就能精通杖类武器， 但是杖类武器的攻击力潜力没有其他种类的武器那么高。 提升杖类技能能提升你使用此类武器的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。 提升杖类技能能同时提升你的锤与链枷技能和长柄武器技能，反之亦然。","Being skilled with Ranged Weapons will let you attack more quickly with all bows, crossbows and slings, as well as increasing your accuracy and damage with them.":"提升远程武器技能能提升你使用所有弓、弩和投石索的攻击速度、命中率和攻击力。","Training Throwing will make thrown weapons (such as javelins) more accurate and damaging. It also makes certain magical darts more likely to have an effect.":"提升投掷技能能提高投掷类武器（如标枪）的命中率和伤害， 并让某些魔法飞镖更容易生效。","Armour skill multiplies the AC gained from wearing armour of all kinds, both from body armour and cloaks, gloves, etc. It also slightly lessens penalties to spellcasting and ranged weapon speed from heavy armour.":"护甲技能会成倍提高穿戴各种护甲（包括身体护甲、披风、手套等）所获得的护甲值， 并略微减轻重甲对施法和远程武器攻击速度的负面影响。","The Dodging skill will affect your chance of dodging an attack, be it melee, ranged or magical. Certain types of attack cannot be dodged, however, such as enchantments (which must be resisted with willpower) and explosions.":"闪避技能会影响你躲开敌人攻击（包括近战、远程和魔法攻击）的几率。 但也有一些攻击类型无法被闪避，例如附魔效果（只能用意志力抵抗）和爆炸。","By training Stealth, you can make it less likely that monsters will notice you if they are asleep or otherwise 